(13273,45,273,'heading',4,'13.3.3 Isomerism',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13274,45,274,'paragraph',NULL,'Alkenes show both structural isomerism and geometrical isomerism.','[{"s": "Alkenes show both structural isomerism and geometrical isomerism.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13275,45,275,'paragraph',NULL,'Structural isomerism : As in alkanes, ethene (C 2 H 4 ) and propene (C 3 H 6 ) can have only one structure but alkenes higher than propene have different structures. Alkenes possessing C4H8 as molecular formula can be written in the following three ways:','[{"s": "Structural isomerism :", "t": "text"}, {"s": "As in alkanes, ethene (C", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "4", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") and propene (C", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "6", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") can have only one structure but alkenes higher than propene have different structures. Alkenes possessing C4H8 as molecular formula can be written in the following three ways:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
