(13371,45,371,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/chemistry/images/Hydrocarbons-image17.png'),
(13372,45,372,'paragraph',NULL,'4. Addition of sulphuric acid : Cold concentrated sulphuric acid adds to alkenes in accordance with Markovnikov rule to form alkyl hydrogen sulphate by the electrophilic addition reaction.','[{"s": "4. Addition of sulphuric acid :", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Cold concentrated sulphuric acid adds to alkenes in accordance with Markovnikov rule to form alkyl hydrogen sulphate by the electrophilic addition reaction.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13373,45,373,'paragraph',NULL,'Hydrocarbons-image138.png (13.44)','[{"s": "Hydrocarbons-image138.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "(13.44)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13374,45,374,'paragraph',NULL,'Hydrocarbons-image195.png (13.45)','[{"s": "Hydrocarbons-image195.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "(13.45)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13375,45,375,'paragraph',NULL,'5. Addition of water : In the presence of a few drops of concentrated sulphuric acid alkenes react with water to form alcohols, in accordance with the Markovnikov rule. 2','[{"s": "5.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Addition of water :", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "In the presence of a few drops of concentrated sulphuric acid alkenes react with water to form alcohols, in accordance with the Markovnikov rule.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "2", "t": "hl"}]','marked','["130830", "131515"]',NULL),
(13376,45,376,'paragraph',NULL,'Hydrocarbons-image121.png (13.46)','[{"s": "Hydrocarbons-image121.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "(13.46)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13377,45,377,'paragraph',NULL,'6. Oxidation: Alkenes on reaction with cold, dilute, aqueous solution of potassium permanganate (Baeyer’s reagent) produce vicinal glycols . Decolorisation of KMnO4 solution is used as a test for unsaturation.','[{"s": "6. Oxidation:", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Alkenes on reaction with cold, dilute, aqueous solution of potassium permanganate (Baeyer’s reagent) produce vicinal glycols", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "Decolorisation of KMnO4 solution is used as a test for unsaturation.", "t": "hl"}]','marked','["131507"]',NULL),
(13378,45,378,'paragraph',NULL,'Hydrocarbons-image101.png (13.47)','[{"s": "Hydrocarbons-image101.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "(13.47)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13379,45,379,'paragraph',NULL,'Hydrocarbons-image174.png (13.48)','[{"s": "Hydrocarbons-image174.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "(13.48)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13380,45,380,'paragraph',NULL,'b) Acidic potassium permanganate or acidic potassium dichromate oxidises alkenes to ketones and/or acids depending upon the nature of the alkene and the experimental conditions','[{"s": "b) Acidic potassium permanganate or acidic potassium dichromate oxidises alkenes to ketones and/or acids depending upon the nature of the alkene and the experimental conditions", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13381,45,381,'paragraph',NULL,'Hydrocarbons-image77.png (13.49)','[{"s": "Hydrocarbons-image77.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "(13.49)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13382,45,382,'paragraph',NULL,'Hydrocarbons-image97.png (13.50)','[{"s": "Hydrocarbons-image97.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "(13.50)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13383,45,383,'paragraph',NULL,'7. Ozonolysis : Ozonolysis of alkenes involves the addition of ozone molecule to alkene to form ozonide, and then cleavage of the ozonide by Zn-H2O to smaller molecules. 3 This reaction is highly useful in detecting the position of the double bond in alkenes or other unsaturated compounds.','[{"s": "7.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Ozonolysis :", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "Ozonolysis of alkenes involves the addition of ozone molecule to alkene to form ozonide, and then cleavage of the ozonide by Zn-H2O to smaller molecules.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "3", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "This reaction is highly useful in detecting the position of the double bond in alkenes or other unsaturated compounds.", "t": "hl"}]','marked','["131516", "131517", "131518", "131519"]',NULL),
(13384,45,384,'paragraph',NULL,'Hydrocarbons-image110.png (13.51)','[{"s": "Hydrocarbons-image110.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "(13.51)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13385,45,385,'paragraph',NULL,'Hydrocarbons-image73.png (13.52)','[{"s": "Hydrocarbons-image73.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "(13.52)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13386,45,386,'paragraph',NULL,'8. Polymerisation: You are familiar with polythene bags and polythene sheets. Polythene is obtained by the combination of large number of ethene molecules at high temperature, high pressure and in the presence of a catalyst. The large molecules thus obtained are called polymers. This reaction is known as polymerisation. The simple compounds from which polymers are made are called monomers. Other alkenes also undergo polymerisation.','[{"s": "8. Polymerisation:", "t": "text"}, {"s": "You are familiar with polythene bags and polythene sheets. Polythene is obtained by the combination of large number of ethene molecules at high temperature, high pressure and in the presence of a catalyst. The large molecules thus obtained are called polymers. This reaction is known as polymerisation. The simple compounds from which polymers are made are called monomers. Other alkenes also undergo polymerisation.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13387,45,387,'paragraph',NULL,'Hydrocarbons-image105.png (13.53)','[{"s": "Hydrocarbons-image105.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "(13.53)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13388,45,388,'paragraph',NULL,'Hydrocarbons-image68.png (13.54)','[{"s": "Hydrocarbons-image68.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "(13.54)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13389,45,389,'paragraph',NULL,'Polymers are used for the manufacture of plastic bags, squeeze bottles, refrigerator dishes, toys, pipes, radio and T.V. cabinets etc. Polypropene is used for the manufacture of milk crates, plastic buckets and other moulded articles. Though these materials have now become common, excessive use of polythene and polypropylene is a matter of great concern for all of us.','[{"s": "Polymers are used for the manufacture of plastic bags, squeeze bottles, refrigerator dishes, toys, pipes, radio and T.V. cabinets etc. Polypropene is used for the manufacture of milk crates, plastic buckets and other moulded articles. Though these materials have now become common, excessive use of polythene and polypropylene is a matter of great concern for all of us.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13390,45,390,'heading',3,'13.4 ALKYNES',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13391,45,391,'paragraph',NULL,'Like alkenes, alkynes are also unsaturated hydrocarbons. They contain at least one triple bond between two carbon atoms. The number of hydrogen atoms is still less in alkynes as compared to alkenes or alkanes. Their general formula is C n H 2n–2.','[{"s": "Like alkenes, alkynes are also unsaturated hydrocarbons. They contain at least one triple bond between two carbon atoms. The number of hydrogen atoms is still less in alkynes as compared to alkenes or alkanes. Their general formula is C", "t": "text"}, {"s": "n", "t": "text"}, {"s": "H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2n–2.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13392,45,392,'paragraph',NULL,'The first stable member of alkyne series is ethyne which is popularly known as acetylene. Acetylene is used for arc welding purposes in the form of oxyacetylene flame obtained by mixing acetylene with oxygen gas. Alkynes are starting materials for a large number of organic compounds. Hence, it is interesting to study this class of organic compounds.','[{"s": "The first stable member of alkyne series is ethyne which is popularly known as acetylene. Acetylene is used for arc welding purposes in the form of oxyacetylene flame obtained by mixing acetylene with oxygen gas. Alkynes are starting materials for a large number of organic compounds. Hence, it is interesting to study this class of organic compounds.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13393,45,393,'heading',4,'13.4.1 Nomenclature and Isomerism',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13394,45,394,'paragraph',NULL,'In common system, alkynes are named as derivatives of acetylene. In IUPAC system, they are named as derivatives of the corresponding alkanes replacing ‘ane’ by the suffix ‘yne’. The position of the triple bond is indicated by the first triply bonded carbon. Common and IUPAC names of a few members of alkyne series are given in Table 13.2.','[{"s": "In common system, alkynes are named as derivatives of acetylene. In IUPAC system, they are named as derivatives of the corresponding alkanes replacing ‘ane’ by the suffix ‘yne’. The position of the triple bond is indicated by the first triply bonded carbon. Common and IUPAC names of a few members of alkyne series are given in Table 13.2.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13395,45,395,'paragraph',NULL,'You have already learnt that ethyne and propyne have got only one structure but there are two possible structures for butyne – (i) but-1-yne and (ii) but-2-yne. Since these two compounds differ in their structures due to the position of the triple bond, they are known as position isomers. In how many ways, you can construct the structure for the next homologue i.e., the next alkyne with molecular formula C5H8? Let us try to arrange five carbon atoms with a continuous chain and with a side chain. Following are the possible structures :','[{"s": "You have already learnt that ethyne and propyne have got only one structure but there are two possible structures for butyne – (i) but-1-yne and (ii) but-2-yne. Since these two compounds differ in their structures due to the position of the triple bond, they are known as position isomers. In how many ways, you can construct the structure for the next homologue i.e., the next alkyne with molecular formula C5H8? Let us try to arrange five carbon atoms with a continuous chain and with a side chain. Following are the possible structures :", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(13396,45,396,'image',NULL,'eq12',NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/chemistry/images/Hydrocarbons-image24.jpg'),
(13397,45,397,'paragraph',NULL,'Structures I and II are position isomers and structures I and III or II and III are chain isomers.','[{"s": "Structures I and II are position isomers and structures I and III or II and III are chain isomers.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
