(13436,45,436,'paragraph',NULL,'2. From vicinal dihalides : Vicinal dihalides on treatment with alcoholic potassium hydroxide undergo dehydrohalogenation. One molecule of hydrogen halide is eliminated to form alkenyl halide which on treatment with sodamide gives alkyne.','[{"s": "2.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "From vicinal dihalides :", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "Vicinal dihalides on treatment with alcoholic potassium hydroxide undergo dehydrohalogenation.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "One molecule of hydrogen halide is eliminated to form alkenyl halide which on treatment with sodamide gives alkyne.", "t": "text"}]','marked','["131505"]',NULL),
