(14758,46,107,'heading',4,'12.3.2 Three-Dimensional Representation of Organic Molecules',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(14759,46,108,'paragraph',NULL,'The three-dimensional (3-D) structure of organic molecules can be represented on paper by using certain conventions. For example, by using solid ( Organic_Chemistry_Some_Basic_Principles_and_Techniques-image55.png ) and dashed ( Organic_Chemistry_Some_Basic_Principles_and_Techniques-image44.png ) wedge formula, the 3-D image of a molecule from a two-dimensional picture can be perceived. In these formulas the solid-wedge is used to indicate a bond projecting out of the plane of paper, towards the observer. The dashed-wedge is used to depict the bond projecting out of the plane of the paper and away from the observer. Wedges are shown in such a way that the broad end of the wedge is towards the observer. The bonds lying in plane of the paper are depicted by using a normal line (—). 3-D representation of methane molecule on paper has been shown in Fig. 12.1.','[{"s": "The three-dimensional (3-D) structure of organic molecules can be represented on paper by using certain conventions. For example, by using solid (", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Organic_Chemistry_Some_Basic_Principles_and_Techniques-image55.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": ") and dashed (", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Organic_Chemistry_Some_Basic_Principles_and_Techniques-image44.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": ") wedge formula, the 3-D image of a molecule from a two-dimensional picture can be perceived. In these formulas the solid-wedge is used to indicate a bond projecting out of the plane of paper, towards the observer. The dashed-wedge is used to depict the bond projecting out of the plane of the paper and away from the observer. Wedges are shown in such a way that the broad end of the wedge is towards the observer. The bonds lying in plane of the paper are depicted by using a normal line (—). 3-D representation of methane molecule on paper has been shown in Fig. 12.1.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
