(15697,46,1046,'paragraph',NULL,'63 . Two liquids (A) and (B) can be separated by the method of fractional distillation. The boiling points of liquid (A) is less than boiling point of liquid (B). Which of the liquids do you expect to come out first in the distillate? Explain.','[{"s": "63", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Two liquids (A) and (B) can be separated by the method of fractional distillation.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "The boiling points of liquid (A) is less than boiling point of liquid (B). Which of the liquids do you expect to come out first in the distillate? Explain.", "t": "text"}]','marked','["121378"]',NULL),
(15698,46,1047,'paragraph',NULL,'64. You have a mixture of three liquids A, B and C. There is a large difference in the boiling points of A and rest of the two liquids i.e., B and C. Boiling point of liquids B and C are quite close. Liquid A boils at a higher temperature than B and C and boiling point B is lower than C. How will you separate the components of the mixture. Draw a diagram showing set up of the apparatus for the process.','[{"s": "64. You have a mixture of three liquids A, B and C. There is a large difference in the boiling points of A and rest of the two liquids i.e., B and C. Boiling point of liquids B and C are quite close. Liquid A boils at a higher temperature than B and C and boiling point B is lower than C. How will you separate the components of the mixture. Draw a diagram showing set up of the apparatus for the process.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
