(15808,47,107,'paragraph',NULL,'Amine salts are soluble in water but insoluble in organic solvents like ether. This reaction is the basis for the separation of amines from the non basic organic compounds insoluble in water.','[{"s": "Amine salts are soluble in water but insoluble in organic solvents like ether. This reaction is the basis for the separation of amines from the non basic organic compounds insoluble in water.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(15809,47,108,'paragraph',NULL,'The reaction of amines with mineral acids to form ammonium salts shows that these are basic in nature. Amines have an unshared pair of electrons on nitrogen atom due to which they behave as Lewis base. Basic character of amines can be better understood in terms of their K b and pk b values as explained below:','[{"s": "The reaction of amines with mineral acids to form ammonium salts shows that these are basic in nature. Amines have an unshared pair of electrons on nitrogen atom due to which they behave as", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Lewis base.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Basic character of amines can be better understood in terms of their", "t": "text"}, {"s": "K", "t": "text"}, {"s": "b", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and pk", "t": "text"}, {"s": "b", "t": "text"}, {"s": "values as explained below:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(15810,47,109,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/chemistry/images/Organic_Compounds_Containing_Nitrogen-image59.png'),
