(17813,50,168,'paragraph',NULL,'We therefore, conclude that in this reaction copper is reduced from +1 state to zero oxidation state and sulphur is oxidised from –2 state to +4 state. The above reaction is thus a redox reaction. Further, Cu 2 O helps sulphur in Cu 2 S to increase its oxidation number, therefore, Cu(I) is an oxidant; and sulphur of Cu 2 S helps copper both in Cu 2 S itself and Cu 2 O to decrease its oxidation number; therefore, sulphur of Cu 2 S is reductant.','[{"s": "We therefore, conclude that in this reaction copper is reduced from +1 state to zero oxidation state and sulphur is oxidised from –2 state to +4 state. The above reaction is thus a redox reaction. Further, Cu", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "O helps sulphur in Cu", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "S to increase its oxidation number, therefore, Cu(I) is an oxidant; and sulphur of Cu", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "S helps copper both in Cu", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "S itself and Cu", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "O to decrease its oxidation number; therefore, sulphur of Cu", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "S is reductant.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
