(17840,50,195,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) Metal displacement: A metal in a compound can be displaced by another metal in the uncombined state. We have already discussed about this class of the reactions under section 8.2.1. Metal displacement reactions find many applications in metallurgical processes in which pure metals are obtained from their compounds in ores. A few such examples are:','[{"s": "(a)", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Metal displacement:", "t": "text"}, {"s": "A metal in a compound can be displaced by another metal in the uncombined state. We have already discussed about this class of the reactions under section 8.2.1. Metal displacement reactions find many applications in metallurgical processes in which pure metals are obtained from their compounds in ores. A few such examples are:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
