(27771,68,478,'paragraph',NULL,'Example 4.10 An insect trapped in a circular groove of radius 12 cm moves along the groove steadily and completes 7 revolutions in 100 s. (a) What is the angular speed, and the linear speed of the motion? (b) Is the acceleration vector a constant vector ? What is its magnitude ?','[{"s": "Example 4.10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "An insect trapped in a circular groove of radius 12 cm moves along the groove steadily and completes 7 revolutions in 100 s. (a) What is the angular speed, and the linear speed of the motion? (b) Is the acceleration vector a constant vector ? What is its magnitude ?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(17926,50,281,'paragraph',NULL,'In reaction (a), the compound nitric oxide is formed by the combination of the elemental substances, nitrogen and oxygen; therefore, this is an example of combination redox reactions. The reaction (b) involves the breaking down of lead nitrate into three components; therefore, this is categorised under decomposition redox reaction. In reaction (c), hydrogen of water has been displaced by hydride ion into dihydrogen gas. Therefore, this may be called as displacement redox reaction. The reaction (d) involves disproportionation of NO2','[{"s": "In reaction (a), the compound nitric oxide is formed by the combination of the elemental substances, nitrogen and oxygen; therefore, this is an example of combination redox reactions. The reaction (b) involves the breaking down of lead nitrate into three components; therefore, this is categorised under decomposition redox reaction. In reaction (c), hydrogen of water has been displaced by hydride ion into dihydrogen gas. Therefore, this may be called as displacement redox reaction.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "The reaction (d) involves disproportionation of NO2", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "", "t": "br"}]','marked','["220836"]',NULL),
(17927,50,282,'paragraph',NULL,'The Paradox of Fractional Oxidation Number','[{"s": "The Paradox of Fractional Oxidation Number", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(17928,50,283,'paragraph',NULL,'Sometimes, we come across with certain compounds in which the oxidation number of a particular element in the compound is in fraction. Examples are:','[{"s": "Sometimes, we come across with certain compounds in which the oxidation number of a particular element in the compound is in fraction. Examples are:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(17929,50,284,'paragraph',NULL,'C 3 O 2 [where oxidation number of carbon is (4/3)],','[{"s": "C", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "O", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "[where oxidation number of carbon is (4/3)],", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
