(18264,51,143,'paragraph',NULL,'Vapour pressure of chloroform (CHCl 3 ) and dichloromethane (CH 2 Cl 2 ) at 298 K are 200 mm Hg and 415 mm Hg respectively. 2 (i) Calculate the vapour pressure of the solution prepared by mixing 25.5 g of CHCl 3 and 40 g of CH 2 Cl 2 at 298 K and, (ii) mole fractions of each component in vapour phase.','[{"s": "Vapour pressure of chloroform (CHCl", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "3", "t": "hl"}, {"s": ") and dichloromethane (CH", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "2", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "Cl", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "2", "t": "hl"}, {"s": ") at 298 K are 200 mm Hg and 415 mm Hg respectively.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "2", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "(i) Calculate the vapour pressure of the solution prepared by mixing 25.5 g of CHCl", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and 40 g of CH", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Cl", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "at 298 K and, (ii) mole fractions of each component in vapour phase.", "t": "text"}]','marked','["160915", "160916"]',NULL),
(18265,51,144,'paragraph',NULL,'Solution','[{"s": "Solution", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
