(18394,51,273,'paragraph',NULL,'Here the symbols R and M 1 stand for the gas constant and molar mass of the solvent, respectively and T f and T b denote the freezing point and the boiling point of the pure solvent respectively in kelvin. Further, ∆ fus H and ∆ vap H represent the enthalpies for the fusion and vapourisation of the solvent, respectively.','[{"s": "Here the symbols", "t": "text"}, {"s": "R", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and", "t": "text"}, {"s": "M", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "stand for the gas constant and molar mass of the solvent, respectively and", "t": "text"}, {"s": "T", "t": "text"}, {"s": "f", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and", "t": "text"}, {"s": "T", "t": "text"}, {"s": "b", "t": "text"}, {"s": "denote the freezing point and the boiling point of the pure solvent respectively in kelvin. Further, ∆", "t": "text"}, {"s": "fus", "t": "text"}, {"s": "H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and ∆", "t": "text"}, {"s": "vap", "t": "text"}, {"s": "H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "represent the enthalpies for the fusion and vapourisation of the solvent, respectively.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
