(19404,52,391,'paragraph',NULL,'But we have only 4.96×103 mol H 2 . Hence, dihydrogen is the limiting reagent in this case. So, NH 3 (g) would be formed only from that amount of available dihydrogen i.e., 4.96 × 103 mol','[{"s": "But we have only 4.96×103 mol H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". Hence, dihydrogen is the limiting reagent in this case. So, NH", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(g) would be formed only from that amount of available dihydrogen i.e., 4.96 × 103 mol", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
