(20041,53,216,'paragraph',NULL,'where m e is the mass of the electron and v is the velocity associated with the ejected electron. Lastly, a more intense beam of light consists of larger number of photons, consequently the number of electrons ejected is also larger as compared to that in an experiment in which a beam of weaker intensity of light is employed.','[{"s": "where m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "e", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is the mass of the electron and v is the velocity associated with the ejected electron. Lastly, a more intense beam of light consists of larger number of photons, consequently the number of electrons ejected is also larger as compared to that in an experiment in which a beam of weaker intensity of light is employed.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
