(20616,54,254,'paragraph',NULL,'The standard enthalpy change for the formation of one mole of a compound from its elements in their most stable states of aggregation (also known as reference states) is called Standard Molar Enthalpy of Formation. Its symbol is 2 gas and those of dioxygen, carbon and sulphur are O 2 gas, C graphite and S rhombic respectively. Some reactions with standard molar enthalpies of formation are as follows.','[{"s": "The standard enthalpy change for the formation of one mole of a compound from its elements in their most stable states of aggregation (also known as reference states) is called Standard Molar Enthalpy of Formation. Its symbol is", "t": "text"}, {"s": "", "t": "br"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "gas and those of dioxygen, carbon and sulphur are O", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "gas, C", "t": "text"}, {"s": "graphite", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and S", "t": "text"}, {"s": "rhombic", "t": "text"}, {"s": "respectively. Some reactions with standard molar enthalpies of formation are as follows.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
