(20764,54,402,'paragraph',NULL,'(e) Hess’s Law of Constant Heat Summation','[{"s": "(e) Hess’s Law of Constant Heat Summation", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(20765,54,403,'paragraph',NULL,'We know that enthalpy is a state function, therefore the change in enthalpy is independent of the path between initial state (reactants) and final state (products). In other words, enthalpy change for a reaction is the same whether it occurs in one step or in a series of steps. This may be stated as follows in the form of Hess’s Law.','[{"s": "We know that enthalpy is a state function, therefore the change in enthalpy is independent of the path between initial state (reactants) and final state (products). In other words, enthalpy change for a reaction is the same whether it occurs in one step or in a series of steps. This may be stated as follows in the form of Hess’s Law.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(20766,54,404,'paragraph',NULL,'If a reaction takes place in several steps then its standard reaction enthalpy is the sum of the standard enthalpies of the intermediate reactions into which the overall reaction may be divided at the same temperature.','[{"s": "If a reaction takes place in several steps then its standard reaction enthalpy is the sum of the standard enthalpies of the intermediate reactions into which the overall reaction may be divided at the same temperature.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(20767,54,405,'paragraph',NULL,'Let us understand the importance of this law with the help of an example.','[{"s": "Let us understand the importance of this law with the help of an example.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(20768,54,406,'paragraph',NULL,'Consider the enthalpy change for the reaction','[{"s": "Consider the enthalpy change for the reaction", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(20769,54,407,'paragraph',NULL,'C (graphite,s) + Thermodynamics-image10.png O 2 (g) → CO (g); ∆ r H ⊖ = ?','[{"s": "C (graphite,s) +", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Thermodynamics-image10.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "O", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(g) → CO (g); ∆", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "⊖", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= ?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(20770,54,408,'paragraph',NULL,'Although CO(g) is the major product, some CO 2 gas is always produced in this reaction. Therefore, we cannot measure enthalpy change for the above reaction directly. However, if we can find some other reactions involving related species, it is possible to calculate the enthalpy change for the above reaction.','[{"s": "Although CO(g) is the major product, some CO", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "gas is always produced in this reaction. Therefore, we cannot measure enthalpy change for the above reaction directly. However, if we can find some other reactions involving related species, it is possible to calculate the enthalpy change for the above reaction.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(20771,54,409,'paragraph',NULL,'Let us consider the following reactions:','[{"s": "Let us consider the following reactions:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
