(20788,54,426,'paragraph',NULL,'It is convenient to give name to enthalpies specifying the types of reactions.','[{"s": "It is convenient to give name to enthalpies specifying the types of reactions.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(20789,54,427,'paragraph',NULL,'Standard Enthalpy of Combustion (symbol : ∆ c H ⊖ )','[{"s": "Standard Enthalpy of Combustion (symbol : ∆", "t": "text"}, {"s": "c", "t": "text"}, {"s": "H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "⊖", "t": "text"}, {"s": ")", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(20790,54,428,'paragraph',NULL,'Combustion reactions are exothermic in nature. These are important in industry, rocketry, and other walks of life. Standard enthalpy of combustion is defined as the enthalpy change per mole (or per unit amount) of a substance, when it undergoes combustion and all the reactants and products being in their standard states at the specified temperature.','[{"s": "Combustion reactions are exothermic in nature. These are important in industry, rocketry, and other walks of life. Standard enthalpy of combustion is defined as the enthalpy change per mole (or per unit amount) of a substance, when it undergoes combustion and all the reactants and products being in their standard states at the specified temperature.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(20791,54,429,'paragraph',NULL,'Cooking gas in cylinders contains mostly butane (C 4 H 10 ). During complete combustion of one mole of butane, 2658 kJ of heat is released. We can write the thermochemical reactions for this as:','[{"s": "Cooking gas in cylinders contains mostly butane (C", "t": "text"}, {"s": "4", "t": "text"}, {"s": "H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "). During complete combustion of one mole of butane, 2658 kJ of heat is released. We can write the thermochemical reactions for this as:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
