(20797,54,435,'paragraph',NULL,'The combustion of one mole of benzene takes place at 298 K and 1 atm. After combustion, CO 2 (g) and H 2 O (1) are produced and 3267.0 kJ of heat is liberated. Calculate the standard enthalpy of formation, ∆ f H ⊖ of benzene. Standard enthalpies of formation of CO 2 (g) and Thermodynamics-image43.png are –393.5 kJ mol–1 and – 285.83 kJ mol–1 respectively.','[{"s": "The combustion of one mole of benzene takes place at 298 K and 1 atm.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "After combustion, CO", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(g) and H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "O (1) are produced and 3267.0 kJ of heat is liberated. Calculate the standard enthalpy of formation, ∆", "t": "text"}, {"s": "f", "t": "text"}, {"s": "H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "⊖", "t": "text"}, {"s": "of benzene. Standard enthalpies of formation of CO", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(g) and", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Thermodynamics-image43.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "are –393.5 kJ mol–1 and – 285.83 kJ mol–1 respectively.", "t": "text"}]','marked','["60920"]',NULL),
