(21199,55,169,'paragraph',NULL,'Figure 7.11','[{"s": "Figure 7.11", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(21201,55,171,'paragraph',NULL,'Solution As the iron rod is inserted, the magnetic field inside the coil magnetizes the iron increasing the magnetic field inside it. Hence, the inductance of the coil increases. Consequently, the inductive reactance of the coil increases. As a result, a larger fraction of the applied ac voltage appears across the inductor, leaving less voltage across the bulb. Therefore, the glow of the light bulb decreases.','[{"s": "Solution As the iron rod is inserted, the magnetic field inside the coil magnetizes the iron increasing the magnetic field inside it. Hence, the inductance of the coil increases. Consequently, the inductive reactance of the coil increases. As a result, a larger fraction of the applied ac voltage appears across the inductor, leaving less voltage across the bulb. Therefore, the glow of the light bulb decreases.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(21202,55,172,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Alternating_Current-image26.png'),
(21203,55,173,'paragraph',NULL,'One complete cycle of voltage/current. Note that the current leads the voltage.','[{"s": "One complete cycle of voltage/current. Note that the current leads the voltage.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(21204,55,174,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Alternating_Current-image156.png'),
(33784,78,345,'paragraph',NULL,'Similarly, the breadth b may be written as','[{"s": "Similarly, the breadth", "t": "text"}, {"s": "b", "t": "text"}, {"s": "may be written as", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(33785,78,346,'paragraph',NULL,'b = 10.1 ± 0.1 cm','[{"s": "b", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 10.1 ± 0.1 cm", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(33786,78,347,'paragraph',NULL,'= 10.1 cm ± 1 %','[{"s": "= 10.1 cm ± 1 %", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(21205,55,175,'paragraph',NULL,'0-1 The current i flows as shown and from the maximum at 0, reaches a zero value at 1. The plate A is charged to positive polarity while negative charge q builds up in B reaching a maximum at 1 until the current becomes zero. The voltage vc = q/C is in phase with q and reaches maximum value at 1. Current and voltage are both positive. So p = vci is positive.','[{"s": "0-1 The current i flows as shown and from the maximum at 0, reaches a zero value at 1. The plate A is charged to positive polarity while negative charge q builds up in B reaching a maximum at 1 until the current becomes zero. The voltage vc = q/C is in phase with q and reaches maximum value at 1. Current and voltage are both positive. So p = vci is positive.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(21206,55,176,'paragraph',NULL,'Energy is absorbed from THE SOURCE during this quarter cycle AS THE CAPACITOR IS CHARGED.','[{"s": "Energy is absorbed from THE SOURCE during this quarter cycle AS THE CAPACITOR IS CHARGED.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(21207,55,177,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Alternating_Current-image121.png'),
(21208,55,178,'paragraph',NULL,'1-2 The current i reverses its direction. The accumulated charge is depleted i.e., the capacitor is discharged during this quarter cycle.The voltage gets reduced but is still positive. The current is negative. Their product, the power is negative.','[{"s": "1-2 The current i reverses its direction. The accumulated charge is depleted i.e., the capacitor is discharged during this quarter cycle.The voltage gets reduced but is still positive. The current is negative. Their product, the power is negative.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(21209,55,179,'paragraph',NULL,'the Energy absorbed during THE 1/4 CYCLE 0-1 IS RETURNED DURING this QUARTER.','[{"s": "the Energy absorbed during THE 1/4 CYCLE 0-1 IS RETURNED DURING this QUARTER.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(21210,55,180,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Alternating_Current-image60.png'),
(21211,55,181,'paragraph',NULL,'2-3 As i continues to flow from A to B, the capacitor is charged to reversed polarity i.e., the plate B acquires positive and A acquires negative charge. Both the current and the voltage are negative. Their product p is positive. The capacitor ABSORBS ENERGY during this 1/4 cycle.','[{"s": "2-3 As i continues to flow from A to B, the capacitor is charged to reversed polarity i.e., the plate B acquires positive and A acquires negative charge. Both the current and the voltage are negative. Their product p is positive. The capacitor ABSORBS ENERGY during this 1/4 cycle.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(21212,55,182,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Alternating_Current-image90.png'),
(21213,55,183,'paragraph',NULL,'3-4 The current i reverses its direction at 3 and flows from B to A. The accumulated charge is depleted and the magnitude of the voltage vc is reduced. vc becomes zero at 4 when the capacitor is fully discharged. The power is negative.ENERGY ABSORBED DURING 2-3 IS RETURNED TO THE SOURCE. NET ENERGY ABSORBED IS ZERO.','[{"s": "3-4 The current i reverses its direction at 3 and flows from B to A. The accumulated charge is depleted and the magnitude of the voltage vc is reduced. vc becomes zero at 4 when the capacitor is fully discharged. The power is negative.ENERGY ABSORBED DURING 2-3 IS RETURNED TO THE SOURCE. NET ENERGY ABSORBED IS ZERO.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(21214,55,184,'paragraph',NULL,'Figure 7.10 Charging and discharging of a capacitor.','[{"s": "Figure 7.10 Charging and discharging of a capacitor.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
