(21235,55,205,'paragraph',NULL,'This relation is represented in Fig. 7.13(b). Since V C and V L are always along the same line and in opposite directions, they can be combined into a single phasor (V C + V L ) which has a magnitude |v Cm – v Lm .| Since V is represented as the hypotenuse of a right-triangle whose sides are V R and (V C + V L ), the pythagorean theorem gives:','[{"s": "This relation is represented in Fig. 7.13(b). Since V", "t": "text"}, {"s": "C", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and V", "t": "text"}, {"s": "L", "t": "text"}, {"s": "are always along the same line and in opposite directions, they can be combined into a single phasor (V", "t": "text"}, {"s": "C", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+ V", "t": "text"}, {"s": "L", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") which has a magnitude |v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Cm", "t": "text"}, {"s": "– v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Lm", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".| Since V is represented as the hypotenuse of a right-triangle whose sides are V", "t": "text"}, {"s": "R", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and (V", "t": "text"}, {"s": "C", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+ V", "t": "text"}, {"s": "L", "t": "text"}, {"s": "), the pythagorean theorem gives:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
