(22354,57,238,'paragraph',NULL,'These formulae for equivalent resistances can be used to find out currents and voltages in more complicated circuits. Consider for example, the circuit in Fig. (3.17), where there are three resistors R 1 , R 2 and R 3 2 and R 3 are in parallel and hence we can replace them by an equivalent Current_Electricity-image116.png between point B and C with','[{"s": "These formulae for equivalent resistances can be used to find out currents and voltages in more complicated circuits. Consider for example, the circuit in Fig. (3.17), where there are three resistors R", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", R", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and R", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "", "t": "br"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and R", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "are in parallel and hence we can replace them by an equivalent", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Current_Electricity-image116.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "between point B and C with", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
