(22398,57,282,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) The network is a simple series and parallel combination of resistors. First the two 4Ω resistors in parallel are equivalent to a resistor = [(4 × 4)/(4 + 4)] Ω = 2 Ω.','[{"s": "(a) The network is a simple series and parallel combination of resistors. First the two 4Ω resistors in parallel are equivalent to a resistor = [(4 × 4)/(4 + 4)] Ω = 2 Ω.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22399,57,283,'paragraph',NULL,'In the same way, the 12 Ω and 6 Ω resistors in parallel are equivalent to a resistor of [(12 × 6)/(12 + 6)] Ω= 4 Ω.','[{"s": "In the same way, the 12 Ω and 6 Ω resistors in parallel are equivalent to a resistor of [(12 × 6)/(12 + 6)] Ω= 4 Ω.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22400,57,284,'paragraph',NULL,'The equivalent resistance R of the network is obtained by combining these resistors (2 Ω and 4 Ω) with 1Ω in series, that is,','[{"s": "The equivalent resistance R of the network is obtained by combining these resistors (2 Ω and 4 Ω) with 1Ω in series, that is,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22401,57,285,'paragraph',NULL,'R = 2 Ω + 4 Ω + 1 Ω = 7 Ω.','[{"s": "R = 2 Ω + 4 Ω + 1 Ω = 7 Ω.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22402,57,286,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) The total current I in the circuit is','[{"s": "(b) The total current I in the circuit is", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22403,57,287,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Current_Electricity-image89.png'),
(22404,57,288,'paragraph',NULL,'Consider the resistors between A and B. If I 1 is the current in one of the 4 Ω resistors and I 2 the current in the other,','[{"s": "Consider the resistors between A and B. If I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is the current in one of the 4 Ω resistors and I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "the current in the other,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22405,57,289,'paragraph',NULL,'I 1 × 4 = I 2 × 4','[{"s": "I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "× 4 = I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "× 4", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22406,57,290,'paragraph',NULL,'that is, I1 = I2, which is otherwise obvious from the symmetry of the two arms. But I 1 +I 2 = I = 2 A. Thus,','[{"s": "that is, I1 = I2, which is otherwise obvious from the symmetry of the two arms. But I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= I = 2 A. Thus,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22407,57,291,'paragraph',NULL,'I 1 = I 2 = 1 A','[{"s": "I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 1 A", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22408,57,292,'paragraph',NULL,'that is, current in each 4 Ω resistor is 1 A. Current in 1 Ω resistor between B and C would be 2 A.','[{"s": "that is, current in each 4 Ω resistor is 1 A. Current in 1 Ω resistor between B and C would be 2 A.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22409,57,293,'paragraph',NULL,'Now, consider the resistances between C and D. If I 3 is the current in the 12 Ω resistor, and I 4 in the 6 Ωresistor,','[{"s": "Now, consider the resistances between C and D. If I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is the current in the 12 Ω resistor, and I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "4", "t": "text"}, {"s": "in the 6 Ωresistor,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22410,57,294,'paragraph',NULL,'I 3 × 12 =I 4 × 6, i.e., I 4 = 2I 3','[{"s": "I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "× 12 =I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "4", "t": "text"}, {"s": "× 6, i.e., I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "4", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 2I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22411,57,295,'paragraph',NULL,'But, I 3 + I 4 = I = 2 A','[{"s": "But, I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+ I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "4", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= I = 2 A", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22412,57,296,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Current_Electricity-image1.png'),
(22413,57,297,'paragraph',NULL,'that is, the current in the 12 Ω resistor is (2/3) A, while the current in the 6 Ω resistor is (4/3) A.','[{"s": "that is, the current in the 12 Ω resistor is (2/3) A, while the current in the 6 Ω resistor is (4/3) A.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22414,57,298,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) The voltage drop across AB is','[{"s": "(c) The voltage drop across AB is", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22415,57,299,'paragraph',NULL,'V AB = I 1 × 4 = 1 A × 4 Ω = 4 V,','[{"s": "V", "t": "text"}, {"s": "AB", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "× 4 = 1 A × 4 Ω = 4 V,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22416,57,300,'paragraph',NULL,'This can also be obtained by multiplying the total current between A and B by the equivalent resistance between A and B, that is,','[{"s": "This can also be obtained by multiplying the total current between A and B by the equivalent resistance between A and B, that is,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22417,57,301,'paragraph',NULL,'V AB = 2 A × 2 Ω = 4 V','[{"s": "V", "t": "text"}, {"s": "AB", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 2 A × 2 Ω = 4 V", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22418,57,302,'paragraph',NULL,'The voltage drop across BC is','[{"s": "The voltage drop across BC is", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22419,57,303,'paragraph',NULL,'V BC = 2 A × 1 Ω = 2 V','[{"s": "V", "t": "text"}, {"s": "BC", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 2 A × 1 Ω = 2 V", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22420,57,304,'paragraph',NULL,'Finally, the voltage drop across CD is','[{"s": "Finally, the voltage drop across CD is", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22421,57,305,'paragraph',NULL,'V CD = 12 Ω × I 3 = 12 Ω ×(2/3)A = 8 V.','[{"s": "V", "t": "text"}, {"s": "CD", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 12 Ω × I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 12 Ω ×(2/3)A = 8 V.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22422,57,306,'paragraph',NULL,'V CD = 2 A × 4 Ω = 8 V','[{"s": "V", "t": "text"}, {"s": "CD", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 2 A × 4 Ω = 8 V", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22423,57,307,'paragraph',NULL,'Note that the total voltage drop across AD is 4 V + 2 V + 8 V = 14 V. Thus, the terminal voltage of the battery is 14 V, while its emf is 16 V. The loss of the voltage (= 2 V) is accounted for by the internal resistance 1 Ω of the battery [2 A × 1 Ω = 2 V].','[{"s": "Note that the total voltage drop across AD is 4 V + 2 V + 8 V = 14 V. Thus, the terminal voltage of the battery is 14 V, while its emf is 16 V. The loss of the voltage (= 2 V) is accounted for by the internal resistance 1 Ω of the battery [2 A × 1 Ω = 2 V].", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22424,57,308,'heading',3,'3.12 CELLS IN SERIES AND IN PARALLEL',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
