(22436,57,320,'paragraph',NULL,'If we wish to replace the combination by a single cell between A and C of emf ε eq and internal resistance r eq , we would have','[{"s": "If we wish to replace the combination by a single cell between A and C of emf ε", "t": "text"}, {"s": "eq", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and internal resistance r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "eq", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", we would have", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22437,57,321,'paragraph',NULL,'V AC = ε eq – I r eq (3.63)','[{"s": "V", "t": "text"}, {"s": "AC", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= ε", "t": "text"}, {"s": "eq", "t": "text"}, {"s": "– I r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "eq", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(3.63)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22438,57,322,'paragraph',NULL,'Comparing the last two equations, we get','[{"s": "Comparing the last two equations, we get", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22439,57,323,'paragraph',NULL,'ε eq = ε 1 + ε 2 (3.64)','[{"s": "ε", "t": "text"}, {"s": "eq", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= ε", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+ ε", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(3.64)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22440,57,324,'paragraph',NULL,'and r eq = r 1 + r 2 (3.65)','[{"s": "and r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "eq", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(3.65)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22441,57,325,'paragraph',NULL,'In Fig.3.20, we had connected the negative electrode of the first to the positive electrode of the second. If instead we connect the two negatives, Eq. (3.61) would change to V BC = –ε 2 –I r 2 and we will get','[{"s": "In Fig.3.20, we had connected the negative electrode of the first to the positive electrode of the second. If instead we connect the two negatives, Eq. (3.61) would change to V", "t": "text"}, {"s": "BC", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= –ε", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and we will get", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22442,57,326,'paragraph',NULL,'ε eq = ε 1 – ε 2 (ε 1 > ε 2 ) (3.66)','[{"s": "ε", "t": "text"}, {"s": "eq", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= ε", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "– ε", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(ε", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "> ε", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") (3.66)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22444,57,328,'paragraph',NULL,'(i) The equivalent emf of a series combination of n cells is just the sum of their individual emf’s, and','[{"s": "(i) The equivalent emf of a series combination of n cells is just the sum of their individual emf’s, and", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27833,68,540,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Motion_in_a_Plane-image8.png'),
(22445,57,329,'paragraph',NULL,'(ii) The equivalent internal resistance of a series combination of n cells is just the sum of their internal resistances.','[{"s": "(ii) The equivalent internal resistance of a series combination of n cells is just the sum of their internal resistances.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22446,57,330,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Current_Electricity-image115.png'),
(22447,57,331,'paragraph',NULL,'Figure 3.21 Two cells in parallel. For connections across A and C, the combination can be replaced by one cell of emf ε eq and internal resistances req whose values are given in Eqs. (3.73) and (3.74).','[{"s": "Figure 3.21 Two cells in parallel. For connections across A and C, the combination can be replaced by one cell of emf ε", "t": "text"}, {"s": "eq", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and internal resistances req whose values are given in Eqs. (3.73) and (3.74).", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22448,57,332,'paragraph',NULL,'This is so, when the current leaves each cell from the positive electrode. If in the combination, the current leaves any cell from the negative electrode, the emf of the cell enters the expression for ε eq with a negative sign, as in Eq. (3.66).','[{"s": "This is so, when the current leaves each cell from the positive electrode. If in the combination, the current leaves any cell from the negative electrode, the emf of the cell enters the expression for ε", "t": "text"}, {"s": "eq", "t": "text"}, {"s": "with a negative sign, as in Eq. (3.66).", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22450,57,334,'paragraph',NULL,'I = I 1 + I 2 (3.67)','[{"s": "I = I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+ I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(3.67)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22451,57,335,'paragraph',NULL,'Let V (B 1 ) and V (B 2 ) be the potentials at B 1 and B 2 , respectively. Then, considering the first cell, the potential difference across its terminals is V (B 1 ) – V (B 2 ). Hence, from Eq. (3.57)','[{"s": "Let V (B", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") and V (B", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") be the potentials at B", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and B", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", respectively. Then, considering the first cell, the potential difference across its terminals is V (B", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") – V (B", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "). Hence, from Eq. (3.57)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22452,57,336,'paragraph',NULL,'Current_Electricity-image56.png (3.68)','[{"s": "Current_Electricity-image56.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "(3.68)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22453,57,337,'paragraph',NULL,'Points B 1 and B 2 are connected exactly similarly to the second cell. Hence considering the second cell, we also have','[{"s": "Points B", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and B", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "are connected exactly similarly to the second cell. Hence considering the second cell, we also have", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(22454,57,338,'paragraph',NULL,'Current_Electricity-image85.png (3.69)','[{"s": "Current_Electricity-image85.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "(3.69)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
