(23165,58,421,'paragraph',NULL,'Q. 25 Consider a thin target ( 10 −2 m square, 10 −3 m thickness) of sodium, which produces a photocurrent of 100 1A when a light of intensity 100 W/m 2 (λ=660 nm) falls on it, Find the probability that a photoelectron is produced when a photon strikes a sodium atom.','[{"s": "Q. 25 Consider a thin target (", "t": "text"}, {"s": "10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "−2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "m square, 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "−3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "m thickness) of sodium, which produces a photocurrent of 100 1A when a light of intensity 100", "t": "text"}, {"s": "W/m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(λ=660 nm)", "t": "text"}, {"s": "falls on it, Find the probability that a photoelectron is produced when a photon strikes a sodium atom.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
