(23326,59,148,'paragraph',NULL,'This expression is identical to the expression obtained by Method I and we get the same value of ε.','[{"s": "This expression is identical to the expression obtained by Method I and we get the same value of ε.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(23328,59,150,'paragraph',NULL,'A wheel with 10 metallic spokes each 0.5 m long is rotated with a speed of 120 rev/min in a plane normal to the horizontal component of earth’s magnetic field H E at a place. If H E = 0.4 G at the place, what is the induced emf between the axle and the rim of the wheel? Note that 1 G = 10 –4 T.','[{"s": "A wheel with 10 metallic spokes each 0.5 m long is rotated with a speed of 120 rev/min in a plane normal to the horizontal component of earth’s magnetic field H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "E", "t": "text"}, {"s": "at a place. If H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "E", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 0.4 G at the place, what is the induced emf between the axle and the rim of the wheel? Note that 1 G = 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–4", "t": "text"}, {"s": "T.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(23329,59,151,'paragraph',NULL,'Solution','[{"s": "Solution", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(23330,59,152,'paragraph',NULL,'Induced emf = (1/2) ω B R 2','[{"s": "Induced emf = (1/2) ω B R", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(23331,59,153,'paragraph',NULL,'= (1/2) × 4π × 0.4 × 10 –4 × (0.5) 2','[{"s": "= (1/2) × 4π × 0.4 × 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–4", "t": "text"}, {"s": "× (0.5)", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(23332,59,154,'paragraph',NULL,'= 6.28 × 10 –5 V','[{"s": "= 6.28 × 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–5", "t": "text"}, {"s": "V", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(23333,59,155,'paragraph',NULL,'The number of spokes is immaterial because the emf’s across the spokes are in parallel.','[{"s": "The number of spokes is immaterial because the emf’s across the spokes are in parallel.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(23334,59,156,'heading',3,'6.7 ENERGY CONSIDERATION: A QUANTITATIVE STUDY',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(23335,59,157,'paragraph',NULL,'In Section 6.5, we discussed qualitatively that Lenz’s law is consistent with the law of conservation of energy. Now we shall explore this aspect further with a concrete example.','[{"s": "In Section 6.5, we discussed qualitatively that Lenz’s law is consistent with the law of conservation of energy. Now we shall explore this aspect further with a concrete example.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(23336,59,158,'paragraph',NULL,'Let r be the resistance of movable arm PQ of the rectangular conductor shown in Fig. 6.10. We assume that the remaining arms QR, RS and SP have negligible resistances compared to r. Thus, the overall resistance of the rectangular loop is r and this does not change as PQ is moved. The current I in the loop is,','[{"s": "Let r be the resistance of movable arm PQ of the rectangular conductor shown in Fig. 6.10. We assume that the remaining arms QR, RS and SP have negligible resistances compared to r. Thus, the overall resistance of the rectangular loop is r and this does not change as PQ is moved. The current I in the loop is,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
