(23581,59,403,'paragraph',NULL,'Q 11. Let us assume that the loop in question number 4 is stationary or constant but the current source which is feeding the electromagnet which is producing the magnetic field is slowly decreased. It was having an initial value of 0.3 T and the rate of reducing the field is 0.02 T / sec. If the cut is joined to form the loop having a resistance of 1.6Ω. Calculate how much power is lost in the form of heat? What is the source of this power?','[{"s": "Q 11. Let us assume that the loop in question number 4 is stationary or constant but the current source which is feeding the electromagnet which is producing the magnetic field is slowly decreased. It was having an initial value of 0.3 T and the rate of reducing the field is 0.02 T / sec. If the cut is joined to form the loop having a resistance of 1.6Ω. Calculate how much power is lost in the form of heat? What is the source of this power?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
