(23622,59,444,'paragraph',NULL,'Q. 18. Consider a closed loop C in a magnetic field (figure). The flux passing through the loop is defined by choosing a surface whose edge coincides with the loop and using the formula ϕ=B 1 dA 1 , B 2 dA 2 ...... . Now, if we choose two different surfaces S 1 and S 2 having C as their edge, would we get the same answer for flux. Justify your answer.','[{"s": "Q. 18. Consider a closed loop C in a magnetic field (figure). The flux passing through the loop is defined by choosing a surface whose edge coincides with the loop and using the formula", "t": "text"}, {"s": "ϕ=B", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "dA", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", B", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "dA", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "...... . Now, if we choose two different surfaces", "t": "text"}, {"s": "S", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and S", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "having C as their edge, would we get the same answer for flux. Justify your answer.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
