(24203,61,215,'paragraph',NULL,'where r 12 is the distance between q 1 and q 2 . We have made use of Eqs. (2.27) and (2.22). By the superposition principle for fields, we add up the work done on q 2 against the two fields (E and that due to q1):','[{"s": "where r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "12", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is the distance between q", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and q", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". We have made use of Eqs. (2.27) and (2.22). By the superposition principle for fields, we add up the work done on q", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "against the two fields (E and that due to q1):", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24204,61,216,'paragraph',NULL,'Work done in bringing q 2 to r 2','[{"s": "Work done in bringing q", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "to r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24205,61,217,'paragraph',NULL,'Electrostatic_Potential_and_Capacitance-image30.png (2.28)','[{"s": "Electrostatic_Potential_and_Capacitance-image30.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "(2.28)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24206,61,218,'paragraph',NULL,'Thus,','[{"s": "Thus,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24207,61,219,'paragraph',NULL,'Potential energy of the system','[{"s": "Potential energy of the system", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24208,61,220,'paragraph',NULL,'= the total work done in assembling the configuration','[{"s": "= the total work done in assembling the configuration", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24209,61,221,'paragraph',NULL,'Electrostatic_Potential_and_Capacitance-image1.png (2.29)','[{"s": "Electrostatic_Potential_and_Capacitance-image1.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "(2.29)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24210,61,222,'paragraph',NULL,'Example 2.5','[{"s": "Example 2.5", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24211,61,223,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) Determine the electrostatic potential energy of a system consisting of two charges 7 µC and –2 µC (and with no external field) placed at (–9 cm, 0, 0) and (9 cm, 0, 0) respectively.','[{"s": "(a) Determine the electrostatic potential energy of a system consisting of two charges 7 µC and –2 µC (and with no external field) placed at (–9 cm, 0, 0) and (9 cm, 0, 0) respectively.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24212,61,224,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) How much work is required to separate the two charges infinitely away from each other?','[{"s": "(b) How much work is required to separate the two charges infinitely away from each other?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24213,61,225,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) Suppose that the same system of charges is now placed in an external electric field E = A (1/r 2 ); A = 9 × 10 5 C m –2 . What would the electrostatic energy of the configuration be?','[{"s": "(c) Suppose that the same system of charges is now placed in an external electric field E = A (1/r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "); A = 9 × 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "5", "t": "text"}, {"s": "C m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". What would the electrostatic energy of the configuration be?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24214,61,226,'paragraph',NULL,'Solution','[{"s": "Solution", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24215,61,227,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) Electrostatic_Potential_and_Capacitance-image2.png = –0.7 J.','[{"s": "(a)", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Electrostatic_Potential_and_Capacitance-image2.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "= –0.7 J.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24216,61,228,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) W = U 2 – U 1 = 0 – U = 0 – (–0.7) = 0.7 J.','[{"s": "(b) W = U", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "– U", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 0 – U = 0 – (–0.7) = 0.7 J.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24217,61,229,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) The mutual interaction energy of the two charges remains unchanged. In addition, there is the energy of interaction of the two charges with the external electric field. We find,','[{"s": "(c) The mutual interaction energy of the two charges remains unchanged. In addition, there is the energy of interaction of the two charges with the external electric field. We find,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24218,61,230,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Electrostatic_Potential_and_Capacitance-image3.png'),
(24219,61,231,'paragraph',NULL,'and the net electrostatic energy is','[{"s": "and the net electrostatic energy is", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24220,61,232,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Electrostatic_Potential_and_Capacitance-image4.png'),
