(24600,61,612,'paragraph',NULL,'Figure 2.34 shows a charge array known as an electric quadrupole. For a point on the axis of the quadrupole, obtain the dependence of potential on r for r/a >> 1, and contrast your results with that due to an electric dipole, and an electric monopole (i.e., a single charge).','[{"s": "Figure 2.34 shows a charge array known as an electric quadrupole. For a point on the axis of the quadrupole, obtain the dependence of potential on r for r/a >> 1, and contrast your results with that due to an electric dipole, and an electric monopole (i.e., a single charge).", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24601,61,613,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Electrostatic_Potential_and_Capacitance-image111.png'),
(24602,61,614,'paragraph',NULL,'Question 2.23:','[{"s": "Question 2.23:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24603,61,615,'paragraph',NULL,'An electrical technician requires a capacitance of 2 μ F in a circuit across a potential difference of 1 kV. A large number of 1 μ F capacitors are available to him each of which can withstand a potential difference of not more than 400 V. Suggest a possible arrangement that requires the minimum number of capacitors.','[{"s": "An electrical technician requires a capacitance of 2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "μ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "F in a circuit across a potential difference of 1 kV. A large number of 1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "μ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "F capacitors are available to him each of which can withstand a potential difference of not more than 400 V. Suggest a possible arrangement that requires the minimum number of capacitors.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24604,61,616,'paragraph',NULL,'Question 2.24:','[{"s": "Question 2.24:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24605,61,617,'paragraph',NULL,'What is the area of the plates of a 2 F parallel plate capacitor, given that the separation between the plates is 0.5 cm? [You will realize from your answer why ordinary capacitors are in the range of μ F or less. However, electrolytic capacitors do have a much larger capacitance (0.1 F) because of the very minute separation between the conductors.]','[{"s": "What is the area of the plates of a 2 F parallel plate capacitor, given that the separation between the plates is 0.5 cm? [You will realize from your answer why ordinary capacitors are in the range of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "μ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "F or less. However, electrolytic capacitors do have a much larger capacitance (0.1 F) because of the very minute separation between the conductors.]", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24606,61,618,'paragraph',NULL,'Question 2.25:','[{"s": "Question 2.25:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL);
