(24609,61,621,'paragraph',NULL,'Question 2.26:','[{"s": "Question 2.26:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24610,61,622,'paragraph',NULL,'The plates of a parallel plate capacitor have an area of 90 cm2 each and are separated by 2.5 mm. The capacitor is charged by connecting it to a 400 V supply.','[{"s": "The plates of a parallel plate capacitor have an area of 90 cm2 each and are separated by 2.5 mm. The capacitor is charged by connecting it to a 400 V supply.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24611,61,623,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) How much electrostatic energy is stored by the capacitor?','[{"s": "(a) How much electrostatic energy is stored by the capacitor?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24612,61,624,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) View this energy as stored in the electrostatic field between the plates, and obtain the energy per unit volume u. Hence arrive at a relation between u and the magnitude Of electric field E between the plates.','[{"s": "(b) View this energy as stored in the electrostatic field between the plates, and obtain the energy per unit volume u. Hence arrive at a relation between u and the magnitude Of electric field E between the plates.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24613,61,625,'paragraph',NULL,'Question 2.27:','[{"s": "Question 2.27:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24614,61,626,'paragraph',NULL,'A 4 VF capacitor is charged by a 200 V supply. It is then disconnected from the supply and is connected to another uncharged 2 pF capacitor. How much electrostatic energy Of the first capacitor is lost in the form Of heat and electromagnetic radiation?','[{"s": "A 4 VF capacitor is charged by a 200 V supply. It is then disconnected from the supply and is connected to another uncharged 2 pF capacitor. How much electrostatic energy Of the first capacitor is lost in the form Of heat and electromagnetic radiation?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24615,61,627,'paragraph',NULL,'Question 2.28:','[{"s": "Question 2.28:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24616,61,628,'paragraph',NULL,'Show that the force on each plate of a parallel plate capacitor has a magnitude equal to (1/2) QE, where Q is the charge on the capacitor, and E is the magnitude of the electric field between the plates. Explain the Origin Of the factor 1/2.','[{"s": "Show that the force on each plate of a parallel plate capacitor has a magnitude equal to (1/2) QE, where Q is the charge on the capacitor, and E is the magnitude of the electric field between the plates. Explain the Origin Of the factor 1/2.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24617,61,629,'paragraph',NULL,'Question 2.29:','[{"s": "Question 2.29:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24618,61,630,'paragraph',NULL,'A spherical capacitor consists of two concentric spherical conductors, held in position by suitable insulating supports (Fig. 2.36). Show that the capacitance of a spherical capacitor is given by C = 4πε 0 r 1 r 2 r/ 1 − r 2 Where r 1 and r 2 are the radii of outer and inner spheres, respectively.','[{"s": "A spherical capacitor consists of two concentric spherical conductors, held in position by suitable insulating supports (Fig. 2.36). Show that the capacitance of a spherical capacitor is given by C =", "t": "text"}, {"s": "4πε", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r/", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "− r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Where r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "are the radii of outer and inner spheres, respectively.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24619,61,631,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Electrostatic_Potential_and_Capacitance-image98.png'),
(24620,61,632,'paragraph',NULL,'Question 2.30:','[{"s": "Question 2.30:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24621,61,633,'paragraph',NULL,'A spherical capacitor has an inner sphere of radius 12 cm and an outer sphere of radius 13 cm. The outer sphere is earthed and the inner sphere is given a charge of 2.5 WC. The space between the concentric spheres is filled with a liquid of dielectric constant 32.','[{"s": "A spherical capacitor has an inner sphere of radius 12 cm and an outer sphere of radius 13 cm. The outer sphere is earthed and the inner sphere is given a charge of 2.5 WC. The space between the concentric spheres is filled with a liquid of dielectric constant 32.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24622,61,634,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) Determine the capacitance of the capacitor.','[{"s": "(a) Determine the capacitance of the capacitor.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24623,61,635,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) What is the potential of the inner sphere?','[{"s": "(b) What is the potential of the inner sphere?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24624,61,636,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) Compare the capacitance of this capacitor with that of an isolated sphere Of radius 12 cm. Explain why the latter is much smaller.','[{"s": "(c) Compare the capacitance of this capacitor with that of an isolated sphere Of radius 12 cm. Explain why the latter is much smaller.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24625,61,637,'heading',3,'ADDITIONAL EXERCISES',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24626,61,638,'paragraph',NULL,'Question 2.31: Answer carefully:','[{"s": "Question 2.31: Answer carefully:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24627,61,639,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) Two large conducting spheres carrying charges Q 1 and Q 2 are brought close to each other. Is the magnitude of the electrostatic force between them exactly given by Q 1 Q 2 /4 πε 0 r 2 , where r is the distance between their centers?','[{"s": "(a) Two large conducting spheres carrying charges Q", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and Q", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "are brought close to each other. Is the magnitude of the electrostatic force between them exactly given by Q", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Q", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "/4", "t": "text"}, {"s": "πε", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", where r is the distance between their centers?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24628,61,640,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) If Coulomb\'s law involved 1/r 3 dependence (instead of 1/r 2 ), would Gauss\'s law be still true?','[{"s": "(b) If Coulomb\'s law involved 1/r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "dependence (instead of 1/r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "), would Gauss\'s law be still true?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24629,61,641,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) A small test charge is released at rest at a point in an electrostatic field configuration. Will it travel along the field line passing through that point?','[{"s": "(c) A small test charge is released at rest at a point in an electrostatic field configuration. Will it travel along the field line passing through that point?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24630,61,642,'paragraph',NULL,'(d) What is the work done by the field of a nucleus in a complete circular orbit of the electron? What if the orbit is elliptical?','[{"s": "(d) What is the work done by the field of a nucleus in a complete circular orbit of the electron? What if the orbit is elliptical?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24631,61,643,'paragraph',NULL,'(e) We know that the electric field is discontinuous across the surface of a charged conductor. Is electric potential also discontinuous there?','[{"s": "(e) We know that the electric field is discontinuous across the surface of a charged conductor. Is electric potential also discontinuous there?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24632,61,644,'paragraph',NULL,'(f) What meaning would you give to the capacitance of a single conductor?','[{"s": "(f) What meaning would you give to the capacitance of a single conductor?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24633,61,645,'paragraph',NULL,'(g) Guess a possible reason why water has a much greater dielectric constant (80) than say, mica (6).','[{"s": "(g) Guess a possible reason why water has a much greater dielectric constant (80) than say, mica (6).", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
