(24661,61,673,'paragraph',NULL,'In this problem, the three parallel branches of circuit can be considered in parallel, combined with one another. Therefore, potential difference across each branch is same. The capacitor offers infinite resistance in DC circuit, therefore no current flows through capacitor and 108 resistance, leaving zero potential difference across 102 resistance. thus, potential difference across lower and middle branch of circuit is equal to the potential difference across capacitor of upper branch of circuit,','[{"s": "In this problem, the three parallel branches of circuit can be considered in parallel, combined with one another. Therefore, potential difference across each branch is same. The capacitor offers infinite resistance in DC circuit, therefore no current flows through capacitor and 108 resistance, leaving zero potential difference across 102 resistance. thus, potential difference across lower and middle branch of circuit is equal to the potential difference across capacitor of upper branch of circuit,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24662,61,674,'paragraph',NULL,'2. A positively charged particle is released from rest in a uniform electric field. The electric potential energy of the charge','[{"s": "2. A positively charged particle is released from rest in a uniform electric field. The electric potential energy of the charge", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24663,61,675,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) remains a constant because the electric field is uniform','[{"s": "(a) remains a constant because the electric field is uniform", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24664,61,676,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) increases because the charge moves along the electric field','[{"s": "(b) increases because the charge moves along the electric field", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
