(24742,61,754,'paragraph',NULL,'28. (a) In a quark model of elementary particles, a neutron is made of one up quarks [charge (2/3) e] and two down quarks [charges — (1/3) e]. Assume that they have a triangle configuration with side length of the order of 10° m. Calculate electrostatic potential energy of neutron and compare it with its mass 939 MeV.','[{"s": "28. (a) In a quark model of elementary particles, a neutron is made of one up quarks [charge (2/3) e] and two down quarks [charges — (1/3) e]. Assume that they have a triangle configuration with side length of the order of 10° m. Calculate electrostatic potential energy of neutron and compare it with its mass 939 MeV.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24743,61,755,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) Repeat above exercise for a proton which is made of two up and one down quark.','[{"s": "(b) Repeat above exercise for a proton which is made of two up and one down quark.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24744,61,756,'paragraph',NULL,'29. Two metal spheres, one of radius & and the other of radius 2R, both have same surface charge density o. They are brought in contact and separated. What will be new surface charge densities on them?','[{"s": "29. Two metal spheres, one of radius & and the other of radius 2R, both have same surface charge density o. They are brought in contact and separated.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "What will be new surface charge densities on them?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24745,61,757,'paragraph',NULL,'30. In the circuit shown in figure, initially K 1 is closed and K 2 is open. What are the charges on each capacitors? Then K 2 was opened and K 1 was closed (order is important), what will be the charge on each capacitor now? [C = 1yF]','[{"s": "30. In the circuit shown in figure, initially K", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is closed and K", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is open. What are the charges on each capacitors? Then K", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "was opened and K", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "was closed (order is important), what will be the charge on each capacitor now? [C = 1yF]", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
