(24809,62,59,'paragraph',NULL,'in agreement with a value of g ≅ 9.8 m s -2 and the value of a m from Eq. (8.3). These observations led Newton to propose the following Universal Law of Gravitation :','[{"s": "in agreement with a value of g ≅ 9.8 m s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "-2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and the value of a", "t": "text"}, {"s": "m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "from Eq. (8.3). These observations led Newton to propose the following Universal Law of Gravitation :", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24811,62,61,'paragraph',NULL,'The quotation is essentially from Newton’s famous treatise called ‘Mathematical Principles of Natural Philosophy’ (Principia for short).','[{"s": "The quotation is essentially from Newton’s famous treatise called ‘Mathematical Principles of Natural Philosophy’ (Principia for short).", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24812,62,62,'paragraph',NULL,'Stated Mathematically, Newton’s gravitation law reads : The force F on a point mass m 2 due to another point mass m 1 has the magnitude','[{"s": "Stated Mathematically, Newton’s gravitation law reads : The force", "t": "text"}, {"s": "F", "t": "text"}, {"s": "on a point mass m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "due to another point mass m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "has the magnitude", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24813,62,63,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Gravitation-image119.png'),
(24814,62,64,'paragraph',NULL,'(8.5)','[{"s": "(8.5)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24815,62,65,'paragraph',NULL,'Equation (8.5) can be expressed in vector form as','[{"s": "Equation (8.5) can be expressed in vector form as", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24816,62,66,'image',NULL,'Screen Shot 2019-06-05 at 5.46.54 PM',NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Gravitation-image120.png'),
(24818,62,68,'paragraph',NULL,'The gravitational force is attractive, i.e., the force F is along – r . The force on point mass m 1 due to m 2 is of course – F by Newton’s third law. Thus, the gravitational force F 12 on the body 1 due to 2 and F 21 on the body 2 due to 1 are related as F 12 = – F 21 .','[{"s": "The gravitational force is attractive, i.e., the force", "t": "text"}, {"s": "F", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is along –", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". The force on point mass m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "due to m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is of course –", "t": "text"}, {"s": "F", "t": "text"}, {"s": "by Newton’s third law. Thus, the gravitational force", "t": "text"}, {"s": "F", "t": "text"}, {"s": "12", "t": "text"}, {"s": "on the body 1 due to 2 and", "t": "text"}, {"s": "F", "t": "text"}, {"s": "21", "t": "text"}, {"s": "on the body 2 due to 1 are related as", "t": "text"}, {"s": "F", "t": "text"}, {"s": "12", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= – F", "t": "text"}, {"s": "21", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24819,62,69,'image',NULL,'Screen Shot 2019-06-05 at 5.48.41 PM',NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Gravitation-image122.png'),
(24820,62,70,'paragraph',NULL,'Fig. 8.3 Gravitational force on m 1 due to m 2 is along r where the vector r is (r 2 – r 1 ).','[{"s": "Fig. 8.3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Gravitational force on m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "due to m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is along r where the vector r is (r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "– r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ").", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24821,62,71,'paragraph',NULL,'Before we can apply Eq. (8.5) to objects under consideration, we have to be careful since the law refers to point masses whereas we deal with extended objects which have finite size. If we have a collection of point masses, the force on any one of them is the vector sum of the gravitational forces exerted by the other point masses as shown in Fig 8.4.','[{"s": "Before we can apply Eq. (8.5) to objects under consideration, we have to be careful since the law refers to", "t": "text"}, {"s": "point", "t": "text"}, {"s": "masses whereas we deal with extended objects which have finite size. If we have a collection of point masses, the force on any one of them is the vector sum of the gravitational forces exerted by the other point masses as shown in Fig 8.4.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24822,62,72,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Gravitation-image123.png'),
(24823,62,73,'paragraph',NULL,'Fig. 8.4 Gravitational force on point mass m 1 is the vector sum of the gravitational forces exerted by m 2 , m 3 and m 4 .','[{"s": "Fig. 8.4", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Gravitational force on point mass m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is the vector sum of the gravitational forces exerted by m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "4", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24824,62,74,'paragraph',NULL,'The total force on m 1 is','[{"s": "The total force on m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24825,62,75,'image',NULL,'Screen Shot 2019-06-05 at 5.55.32 PM',NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Gravitation-image124.png'),
(24826,62,76,'paragraph',NULL,'Example 8.2 Three equal masses of m kg each are fixed at the vertices of an equilateral triangle ABC.','[{"s": "Example 8.2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Three equal masses of m kg each are fixed at the vertices of an equilateral triangle ABC.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24827,62,77,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) What is the force acting on a mass 2m placed at the centroid G of the triangle?','[{"s": "(a) What is the force acting on a mass 2m placed at the centroid G of the triangle?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24828,62,78,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) What is the force if the mass at the vertex A is doubled ?','[{"s": "(b) What is the force if the mass at the vertex A is doubled ?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24829,62,79,'paragraph',NULL,'Take AG = BG = CG = 1 m (see Fig. 8.5)','[{"s": "Take AG = BG = CG = 1 m (see Fig. 8.5)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24830,62,80,'paragraph',NULL,'Answer (a) The angle between GC and the positive x-axis is 30° and so is the angle between GB and the negative x-axis. The individual forces in vector notation are','[{"s": "Answer", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(a) The angle between GC and the positive x-axis is 30° and so is the angle between GB and the negative x-axis. The individual forces in vector notation are", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
