(24971,62,221,'paragraph',NULL,'Equation (8.32) applies equally well to an object thrown from the surface of the moon with g replaced by the acceleration due to Moon’s gravity on its surface and r E replaced by the radius of the moon. Both are smaller than their values on earth and the escape speed for the moon turns out to be 2.3 km/s, about five times smaller. This is the reason that moon has no atmosphere. Gas molecules if formed on the surface of the moon having velocities larger than this will escape the gravitational pull of the moon.','[{"s": "Equation (8.32) applies equally well to an object thrown from the surface of the moon with g replaced by the acceleration due to Moon’s gravity on its surface and r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "E", "t": "text"}, {"s": "replaced by the radius of the moon. Both are smaller than their values on earth and the escape speed for the moon turns out to be 2.3 km/s, about five times smaller. This is the reason that moon has no atmosphere. Gas molecules if formed on the surface of the moon having velocities larger than this will escape the gravitational pull of the moon.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(24964,62,214,'paragraph',NULL,'If the object is thrown from the surface of the earth, h = 0, and we get','[{"s": "If the object is thrown from the surface of the earth, h = 0, and we get", "t": "hl"}]','marked',NULL,NULL),
