(25124,62,374,'heading',4,'Points to Ponder',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(25125,62,375,'paragraph',NULL,'1. In considering motion of an object under the gravitational influence of another object the following quantities are conserved:','[{"s": "1. In considering motion of an object under the gravitational influence of another object the following quantities are conserved:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(25126,62,376,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) Angular momentum','[{"s": "(a) Angular momentum", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(25127,62,377,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) Total mechanical energy','[{"s": "(b) Total mechanical energy", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(25128,62,378,'paragraph',NULL,'Linear momentum is not conserved','[{"s": "Linear momentum is", "t": "text"}, {"s": "not", "t": "text"}, {"s": "conserved", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(25129,62,379,'paragraph',NULL,'2. Angular momentum conservation leads to Kepler’s second law. However, it is not special to the inverse square law of gravitation. It holds for any central force.','[{"s": "2. Angular momentum conservation leads to Kepler’s second law. However, it is not special to the inverse square law of gravitation. It holds for any central force.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(25131,62,381,'paragraph',NULL,'4. An astronaut experiences weightlessness in a space satellite. This is not because the gravitational force is small at that location in space. It is because both the astronaut and the satellite are in “free fall” towards the Earth.','[{"s": "4. An astronaut experiences weightlessness in a space satellite. This is not because the gravitational force is small at that location in space. It is because both the astronaut and the satellite are in “free fall” towards the Earth.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(25132,62,382,'paragraph',NULL,'5. The gravitational potential energy associated with two particles separated by a distance r is given by','[{"s": "5. The gravitational potential energy associated with two particles separated by a distance r is given by", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(25133,62,383,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Gravitation-image100.png'),
(25134,62,384,'paragraph',NULL,'The constant can be given any value. The simplest choice is to take it to be zero. With this choice','[{"s": "The constant can be given any value. The simplest choice is to take it to be zero. With this choice", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(25135,62,385,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Gravitation-image108.png'),
(25136,62,386,'paragraph',NULL,'This choice implies that V → 0 as r → ∞. Choosing location of zero of the gravitational energy is the same as choosing the arbitrary constant in the potential energy. Note that the gravitational force is not altered by the choice of this constant.','[{"s": "This choice implies that V → 0 as r → ∞. Choosing location of zero of the gravitational energy is the same as choosing the arbitrary constant in the potential energy. Note that the gravitational force is not altered by the choice of this constant.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(25137,62,387,'paragraph',NULL,'6. The total mechanical energy of an object is the sum of its kinetic energy (which is always positive) and the potential energy. Relative to infinity (i.e. if we presume that the potential energy of the object at infinity is zero), the gravitational potential energy of an object is negative. The total energy of a satellite is negative.','[{"s": "6. The total mechanical energy of an object is the sum of its kinetic energy (which is always positive) and the potential energy. Relative to infinity (i.e. if we presume that the potential energy of the object at infinity is zero), the gravitational potential energy of an object is negative. The total energy of a satellite is negative.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(25138,62,388,'paragraph',NULL,'7. The commonly encountered expression m g h for the potential energy is actually an approximation to the difference in the gravitational potential energy discussed in the point 6, above.','[{"s": "7. The commonly encountered expression m g h for the potential energy is actually an approximation to the difference in the gravitational potential energy discussed in the point 6, above.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32247,75,913,'paragraph',NULL,'7.19 A hoop of radius 2 m weighs 100 kg. It rolls along a horizontal floor so that its centre of mass has a speed of 20 cm/s. How much work has to be done to stop it?','[{"s": "7.19", "t": "text"}, {"s": "A hoop of radius 2 m weighs 100 kg.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "It rolls along a horizontal floor so that its centre of mass has a speed of 20 cm/s. How much work has to be done to stop it?", "t": "text"}]','marked',NULL,NULL),
(25139,62,389,'paragraph',NULL,'8. Although the gravitational force between two particles is central, the force between two finite rigid bodies is not necessarily along the line joining their centre of mass. For a spherically symmetric body however the force on a particle external to the body is as if the mass is concentrated at the centre and this force is therefore central.','[{"s": "8. Although the gravitational force between two particles is central, the force between two finite rigid bodies is not necessarily along the line joining their centre of mass. For a spherically symmetric body however the force on a particle external to the body is as if the mass is concentrated at the centre and this force is therefore central.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(25140,62,390,'paragraph',NULL,'9. The gravitational force on a particle inside a spherical shell is zero. However, (unlike a metallic shell which shields electrical forces) the shell does not shield other bodies outside it from exerting gravitational forces on a particle inside. Gravitational shielding is not possible.','[{"s": "9. The gravitational force on a particle inside a spherical shell is zero. However, (unlike a metallic shell which shields electrical forces) the shell does not shield other bodies outside it from exerting gravitational forces on a particle inside. Gravitational shielding is not possible.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
