(25459,63,318,'paragraph',NULL,'[Hint: Assume the atoms to be ‘tightly packed’ in a solid or liquid phase, and use the known value of Avogadro’s number. You should, however, not take the actual numbers you obtain for various atomic sizes too literally. Because of the crudeness of the tight packing approximation, the results only indicate that atomic sizes are in the range of a few Å].','[{"s": "[Hint: Assume the atoms to be ‘tightly packed’ in a solid or liquid phase, and use the known value of Avogadro’s number. You should, however, not take the actual numbers you obtain for various atomic sizes too literally. Because of the crudeness of the tight packing approximation, the results only indicate that atomic sizes are in the range of a few Å].", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(25460,63,319,'paragraph',NULL,'Q. 1 A cubic vessel (with face horizontal + vertical) contains an ideal gas at NTP. the vessel is being carried by a rocket which is moving at a speed of 500 ms −1 in vertical direction. The pressure of the gas inside the vessel as observed by us on the ground','[{"s": "Q. 1 A cubic vessel (with face horizontal + vertical) contains an ideal gas at NTP. the vessel is being carried by a rocket which is moving at a speed of 500", "t": "text"}, {"s": "ms", "t": "text"}, {"s": "−1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "in vertical direction. The pressure of the gas inside the vessel as observed by us on the ground", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(25461,63,320,'paragraph',NULL,'1. remains the same because 500 m s −1 is very much smaller than V rms of the gas','[{"s": "1. remains the same because 500", "t": "text"}, {"s": "m s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "−1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is very much smaller than", "t": "text"}, {"s": "V", "t": "text"}, {"s": "rms", "t": "text"}, {"s": "of the gas", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(25462,63,321,'paragraph',NULL,'2. remains the same because motion of the vessel as whole does not affect the relative motion of the gas molecules and the walls','[{"s": "2. remains the same because motion of the vessel as whole does not affect the relative motion of the gas molecules and the walls", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(25463,63,322,'paragraph',NULL,'3. will increase by a factor equal to (v 2 rms+(500) 2 )/v 2 rms where V rms was the original mean square velocity of the gas','[{"s": "3. will increase by a factor equal to", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "rms+(500)", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ")/v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "rms", "t": "text"}, {"s": "where", "t": "text"}, {"s": "V", "t": "text"}, {"s": "rms", "t": "text"}, {"s": "was the original mean square velocity of the gas", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(25464,63,323,'paragraph',NULL,'4. will be different on the top wall and bottom wall of the vessel','[{"s": "4. will be different on the top wall and bottom wall of the vessel", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(25465,63,324,'paragraph',NULL,'Q. 2 mole of an ideal gas is contained in a cubical volume V, ABCDEFGH at 300K (figure). One face of the cube (EFGH) is made up of a material which totally absorbs any gas molecule incident on it. At any given time,','[{"s": "Q. 2 mole of an ideal gas is contained in a cubical volume V, ABCDEFGH at 300K (figure). One face of the cube (EFGH) is made up of a material which totally absorbs any gas molecule incident on it. At any given time,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
