(25556,63,415,'paragraph',NULL,'Q. 29 Ten small planes are flying at a speed of 150 km/h in total darkness in an air space that is 20×20×1.5 km 3 in volume. You are in one of the planes, flying at random within this space with no way of knowing where the other planes are. On the average about how long a time will elapse between near collision with your plane. Assume for this rough computation that a saftey region around the plane can be approximated by a sphere of radius 10 m.','[{"s": "Q. 29 Ten small planes are flying at a speed of 150 km/h in total darkness in an air space that is", "t": "text"}, {"s": "20×20×1.5 km", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "in volume. You are in one of the planes, flying at random within this space with no way of knowing where the other planes are. On the average about how long a time will elapse between near collision with your plane. Assume for this rough computation that a saftey region around the plane can be approximated by a sphere of radius 10 m.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
