(25786,64,226,'paragraph',NULL,'Answer The forces acting on a block of mass m at rest on an inclined plane are (i) the weight mg acting vertically downwards (ii) the normal force N of the plane on the block, and (iii) the static frictional force f s opposing the impending motion. In equilibrium, the resultant of these forces must be zero. Resolving the weight mg along the two directions shown, we have','[{"s": "Answer", "t": "text"}, {"s": "The forces acting on a block of mass", "t": "text"}, {"s": "m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "at rest on an inclined plane are (i) the weight mg acting vertically downwards (ii) the normal force", "t": "text"}, {"s": "N", "t": "text"}, {"s": "of the plane on the block, and (iii) the static frictional force", "t": "text"}, {"s": "f", "t": "text"}, {"s": "s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "opposing the impending motion. In equilibrium, the resultant of these forces must be zero. Resolving the weight", "t": "text"}, {"s": "mg", "t": "text"}, {"s": "along the two directions shown, we have", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
