(26376,65,438,'paragraph',NULL,'Q.4 Consider the two idealized systems (i) a parallel plate capacitor with large plates and small separation and (ii) a long solenoid of length L>>R, the radius of the cross-section. In (i) E is ideally treated as a constant between plates and zero outside. In (ii) the magnetic field is constant inside the solenoid and zero outside. These idealized assumptions, however, contradict fundamental laws as below','[{"s": "Q.4 Consider the two idealized systems (i) a parallel plate capacitor with large plates and small separation and (ii) a long solenoid of length L>>R, the radius of the cross-section. In (i) E is ideally treated as a constant between plates and zero outside. In (ii) the magnetic field is constant inside the solenoid and zero outside. These idealized assumptions, however, contradict fundamental laws as below", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
