(26418,65,480,'paragraph',NULL,'Q.17 Three identical bar magnets are riveted together at the center in the same plane as shown in the figure. This system is placed at rest in a slowly varying magnetic field. It is found that the system of magnets does not show any motion. The north-south poles of one magnet are shown in the figure. Determine the poles of the remaining two.','[{"s": "Q.17 Three identical bar magnets are riveted together at the center in the same plane as shown in the figure. This system is placed at rest in a slowly varying magnetic field. It is found that the system of magnets does not show any motion. The north-south poles of one magnet are shown in the figure. Determine the poles of the remaining two.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
