(26620,66,190,'paragraph',NULL,'Fig. 10.10 Torricelli’s law. The speed of efflux, v1, from the side of the container is given by the application of Bernoulli’s equation. If the container is open at the top to the atmosphere then .','[{"s": "Fig. 10.10 Torricelli’s law. The speed of efflux, v1, from the side of the container is given by the application of Bernoulli’s equation. If the container is open at the top to the atmosphere then .", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(26621,66,191,'paragraph',NULL,'If the cross-sectional area of the tank A2 is much larger than that of the hole (A2 >>A1), then we may take the fluid to be approximately at rest at the top, i.e., v2 = 0. Now, applying the Bernoulli equation at points 1 and 2 and noting that at the hole P1 = Pa, the atmospheric pressure, we have from Eq. (10.12)','[{"s": "If the cross-sectional area of the tank A2 is much larger than that of the hole (A2 >>A1), then we may take the fluid to be approximately at rest at the top, i.e., v2 = 0. Now, applying the Bernoulli equation at points 1 and 2 and noting that at the hole P1 = Pa, the atmospheric pressure, we have from Eq. (10.12)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
