(26919,66,489,'paragraph',NULL,'10.28 In Millikan’s oil drop experiment, what is the terminal speed of an uncharged drop of radius 2.0 × 10 –5 m and density 1.2 × 10 3 kg m –3 . Take the viscosity of air at the temperature of the experiment to be 1.8 × 10 –5 Pa s. How much is the viscous force on the drop at that speed? Neglect buoyancy of the drop due to air.','[{"s": "10.28", "t": "text"}, {"s": "In Millikan’s oil drop experiment, what is the terminal speed of an uncharged drop of radius 2.0 × 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–5", "t": "text"}, {"s": "m and density 1.2 × 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "kg m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–3", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". Take the viscosity of air at the temperature of the experiment to be 1.8 × 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–5", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Pa s. How much is the viscous force on the drop at that speed? Neglect buoyancy of the drop due to air.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(26920,66,490,'paragraph',NULL,'10.29 Mercury has an angle of contact equal to 140° with soda-lime glass. A narrow tube of radius 1.00 mm made of this glass is dipped in a trough containing mercury. By what amount does the mercury dip down in the tube relative to the liquid surface outside? The surface tension of mercury at the temperature of the experiment is 0.465 N m –1 . Density of mercury = 13.6 × 10 3 kg m –3 .','[{"s": "10.29", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Mercury has an angle of contact equal to 140° with soda-lime glass. A narrow tube of radius 1.00 mm made of this glass is dipped in a trough containing mercury. By what amount does the mercury dip down in the tube relative to the liquid surface outside? The surface tension of mercury at the temperature of the experiment is 0.465 N m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". Density of mercury = 13.6 × 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "kg m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–3", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(26921,66,491,'paragraph',NULL,'10.30 Two narrow bores of diameters 3.0 mm and 6.0 mm are joined together to form a U-tube open at both ends. If the U-tube contains water, what is the difference in its levels in the two limbs of the tube? The surface tension of water at the temperature of the experiment is 7.3 × 10 –2 N m –1 . Take the angle of contact to be zero and density of water to be 1.0 × 10 3 kg m –3 (g = 9.8 ms −2 ).','[{"s": "10.30", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Two narrow bores of diameters 3.0 mm and 6.0 mm are joined together to form a U-tube open at both ends. If the U-tube contains water, what is the difference in its levels in the two limbs of the tube? The surface tension of water at the temperature of the experiment is 7.3 × 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "N m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". Take the angle of contact to be zero and density of water to be 1.0 × 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "kg m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(g = 9.8", "t": "text"}, {"s": "ms", "t": "text"}, {"s": "−2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ").", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
