(26925,66,495,'paragraph',NULL,'where ρ 0 = 1.25 kg m –3 is the density at sea level and y 0 is a constant. This density variation is called the law of atmospheres. Obtain this law assuming that the temperature of the atmosphere remains a constant (isothermal conditions). Also, assume that the value of g remains constant.','[{"s": "where ρ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 1.25 kg m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is the density at sea level and", "t": "text"}, {"s": "y", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is a constant. This density variation is called the law of atmospheres. Obtain this law assuming that the temperature of the atmosphere remains a constant (isothermal conditions). Also, assume that the value of g remains constant.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(26926,66,496,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) A large He balloon of volume 1425 m 3 is used to lift a payload of 400 kg. Assume that the balloon maintains constant radius as it rises. How high does it rise?','[{"s": "(b) A large He balloon of volume 1425 m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is used to lift a payload of 400 kg. Assume that the balloon maintains constant radius as it rises. How high does it rise?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(26927,66,497,'paragraph',NULL,'[Take y 0 = 8000 m and ρ He = 0.18 kg m –3 ].','[{"s": "[Take y", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 8000 m and", "t": "text"}, {"s": "ρ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "He", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 0.18 kg m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "].", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
