(26996,66,566,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) Considering the pressure p to be proportional to the density, find the p at a height h if the pressure on the surface of the earth is p 0','[{"s": "(b) Considering the pressure p to be proportional to the density, find the p at a height h if the pressure on the surface of the earth is", "t": "text"}, {"s": "p", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(26997,66,567,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) If p 0 =1.03×10 5 Nm −2 ,ρ 0 =1.29 kg m −3 andg=9.8 ms −2, at what height will be pressure drop to (1/10) the value at the surface of the earth?','[{"s": "(c) If", "t": "text"}, {"s": "p", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": "=1.03×10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "5", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nm", "t": "text"}, {"s": "−2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ",ρ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": "=1.29 kg m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "−3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "andg=9.8 ms", "t": "text"}, {"s": "−2,", "t": "text"}, {"s": "at what height will be pressure drop to (1/10) the value at the surface of the earth?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(26998,66,568,'paragraph',NULL,'Q. 22 Surface tension is exhibited by liquids due to force of attraction between molecules of the liquid. The surface tension decreases wit! increase in temperature and vanishes at boiling point. Given that thi latent heat of vaporisation for water L v =540kcal kg −1 , the mechanical equivalent of heat J=4.2 J cal −1 , density of water ρ w =10 3 kg l −1, Avagardro’s number N A =6.0×10 26 k mole −1 and the molecular weigh: of water M A = 10 kg for 1 k mole.','[{"s": "Q. 22 Surface tension is exhibited by liquids due to force of attraction between molecules of the liquid. The surface tension decreases wit! increase in temperature and vanishes at boiling point. Given that thi latent heat of vaporisation for water", "t": "text"}, {"s": "L", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "=540kcal kg", "t": "text"}, {"s": "−1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", the mechanical equivalent of heat", "t": "text"}, {"s": "J=4.2 J cal", "t": "text"}, {"s": "−1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", density of water", "t": "text"}, {"s": "ρ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "w", "t": "text"}, {"s": "=10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "kg l", "t": "text"}, {"s": "−1,", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Avagardro’s number", "t": "text"}, {"s": "N", "t": "text"}, {"s": "A", "t": "text"}, {"s": "=6.0×10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "26", "t": "text"}, {"s": "k mole", "t": "text"}, {"s": "−1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and the molecular weigh: of water", "t": "text"}, {"s": "M", "t": "text"}, {"s": "A", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 10 kg for 1 k mole.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
