(27482,68,189,'paragraph',NULL,'Equation (4.24a) gives the magnitude of the resultant and Eqs. (4.24e) and (4.24f) its direction. Equation (4.24a) is known as the Law of cosines and Eq. (4.24d) as the Law of sines .','[{"s": "Equation (4.24a) gives the magnitude of the resultant and Eqs. (4.24e) and (4.24f) its direction. Equation (4.24a) is known as the", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Law of cosines", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and Eq. (4.24d) as the", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Law of sines", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27483,68,190,'paragraph',NULL,'Example 4.3 A motorboat is racing towards north at 25 km/h and the water current in that region is 10 km/h in the direction of 60° east of south. Find the resultant velocity of the boat.','[{"s": "Example 4.3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "A motorboat is racing towards north at 25 km/h and the water current in that region is 10 km/h in the direction of 60° east of south. Find the resultant velocity of the boat.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27484,68,191,'paragraph',NULL,'Answer The vector v b representing the velocity of the motorboat and the vector v c representing the water current are shown in Fig. 4.11 in directions specified by the problem. Using the parallelogram method of addition, the resultant R is obtained in the direction shown in the figure.','[{"s": "Answer", "t": "text"}, {"s": "The vector", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "b", "t": "text"}, {"s": "representing the velocity of the motorboat and the vector", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "c", "t": "text"}, {"s": "representing the water current are shown in Fig. 4.11 in directions specified by the problem. Using the parallelogram method of addition, the resultant", "t": "text"}, {"s": "R", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is obtained in the direction shown in the figure.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
