(27626,68,333,'paragraph',NULL,'The concept of relative velocity, introduced in section 3.7 for motion along a straight line, can be easily extended to include motion in a plane or in three dimensions. Suppose that two objects A and B are moving with velocities v A and v B (each with respect to some common frame of reference, say ground','[{"s": "The concept of relative velocity, introduced in section 3.7 for motion along a straight line, can be easily extended to include motion in a plane or in three dimensions. Suppose that two objects A and B are moving with velocities", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "A", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "B", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(each with respect to some common frame of reference, say ground", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27628,68,335,'paragraph',NULL,'v AB = v A – v B (4.35a)','[{"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "AB", "t": "text"}, {"s": "=", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "A", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "B", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(4.35a)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27629,68,336,'paragraph',NULL,'and similarly, the velocity of object B relative to that of A is :','[{"s": "and similarly, the velocity of object B relative to that of A is :", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
