(27635,68,342,'paragraph',NULL,'Example 4.6 Rain is falling vertically with a speed of 35 m s –1 . A woman rides a bicycle with a speed of 12 m s –1 in east to west direction. What is the direction in which she should hold her umbrella ?','[{"s": "Example 4.6", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Rain is falling vertically with a speed of 35 m s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". A woman rides a bicycle with a speed of 12 m s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "in east to west direction. What is the direction in which she should hold her umbrella ?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27636,68,343,'paragraph',NULL,'Answer In Fig. 4.16 v r represents the velocity of rain and v b , the velocity of the bicycle, the woman is riding. Both these velocities are with respect to the ground. Since the woman is riding a bicycle, the velocity of rain as experienced by','[{"s": "Answer", "t": "text"}, {"s": "In Fig. 4.16", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "represents the velocity of rain and", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "b", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", the velocity of the bicycle, the woman is riding. Both these velocities are with respect to the ground. Since the woman is riding a bicycle, the velocity of rain as experienced by", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27637,68,344,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Motion_in_a_Plane-image120.png'),
(27638,68,345,'paragraph',NULL,'Fig. 4.16','[{"s": "Fig. 4.16", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27639,68,346,'paragraph',NULL,'her is the velocity of rain relative to the velocity of the bicycle she is riding. That is v rb = v r – v b','[{"s": "her is the velocity of rain relative to the velocity of the bicycle she is riding. That is", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "rb", "t": "text"}, {"s": "=", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "b", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27640,68,347,'paragraph',NULL,'This relative velocity vector as shown in Fig. 4.16 makes an angle θ with the vertical. It is given by','[{"s": "This relative velocity vector as shown in Fig. 4.16 makes an angle θ with the vertical. It is given by", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27641,68,348,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Motion_in_a_Plane-image165.png'),
(27642,68,349,'paragraph',NULL,'Or,','[{"s": "Or,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27643,68,350,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Motion_in_a_Plane-image164.png'),
(27644,68,351,'paragraph',NULL,'Therefore, the woman should hold her umbrella at an angle of about 19° with the vertical towards the west.','[{"s": "Therefore, the woman should hold her umbrella at an angle of about 19° with the vertical towards the west.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27645,68,352,'paragraph',NULL,'Note carefully the difference between this Example and the Example 4.1. In Example 4.1, the boy experiences the resultant (vector sum) of two velocities while in this example, the woman experiences the velocity of rain relative to the bicycle (the vector difference of the two velocities).','[{"s": "Note carefully the difference between this Example and the Example 4.1. In Example 4.1, the boy experiences the resultant (vector sum) of two velocities while in this example, the woman experiences the velocity of rain relative to the bicycle (the vector difference of the two velocities).", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27646,68,353,'heading',2,'4.10 PROJECTILE MOTION',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27647,68,354,'paragraph',NULL,'As an application of the ideas developed in the previous sections, we consider the motion of a projectile. An object that is in flight after being thrown or projected is called a projectile . Such a projectile might be a football, a cricket ball, a baseball or any other object. The motion of a projectile may be thought of as the result of two separate, simultaneously occurring components of motions. One component is along a horizontal direction without any acceleration and the other along the vertical direction with constant acceleration due to the force of gravity. It was Galileo who first stated this independency of the horizontal and the vertical components of projectile motion in his Dialogue on the great world systems (1632).','[{"s": "As an application of the ideas developed in the previous sections, we consider the motion of a projectile. An object that is in flight after being thrown or projected is called a", "t": "text"}, {"s": "projectile", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". Such a projectile might be a football, a cricket ball, a baseball or any other object. The motion of a projectile may be thought of as the result of two separate, simultaneously occurring components of motions. One component is along a horizontal direction without any acceleration and the other along the vertical direction with constant acceleration due to the force of gravity. It was Galileo who first stated this independency of the horizontal and the vertical components of projectile motion in his", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Dialogue on the great world systems", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(1632).", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27648,68,355,'paragraph',NULL,'In our discussion, we shall assume that the air resistance has negligible effect on the motion of the projectile. Suppose that the projectile is launched with velocity v o that makes an angle θ o with the x-axis as shown in Fig. 4.17.','[{"s": "In our discussion, we shall assume that the air resistance has negligible effect on the motion of the projectile. Suppose that the projectile is launched with velocity", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "that makes an angle θ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "with the x-axis as shown in Fig. 4.17.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27650,68,357,'paragraph',NULL,'a = -g ĵ','[{"s": "a = -g ĵ", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27651,68,358,'paragraph',NULL,'Or, a x = 0, a y = – g (4.36)','[{"s": "Or, a", "t": "text"}, {"s": "x", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 0, a", "t": "text"}, {"s": "y", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= – g (4.36)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27652,68,359,'paragraph',NULL,'The components of initial velocity v o are :','[{"s": "The components of initial velocity", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "are :", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27653,68,360,'paragraph',NULL,'v ox = v o cos θ o','[{"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "ox", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "cos θ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27654,68,361,'paragraph',NULL,'v oy = v o sin θ o (4.37)','[{"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "oy", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "sin θ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(4.37)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27655,68,362,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Motion_in_a_Plane-image149.png'),
(27656,68,363,'paragraph',NULL,'Fig 4.17 Motion of an object projected with velocity v o at angle θ 0 .','[{"s": "Fig 4.17", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Motion of an object projected with velocity v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "at angle θ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27657,68,364,'paragraph',NULL,'If we take the initial position to be the origin of the reference frame as shown in Fig. 4.17, we have :','[{"s": "If we take the initial position to be the origin of the reference frame as shown in Fig. 4.17, we have :", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27658,68,365,'paragraph',NULL,'x o = 0, y o = 0','[{"s": "x", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 0, y", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 0", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27659,68,366,'paragraph',NULL,'Then, Eq.(4.34b) becomes :','[{"s": "Then, Eq.(4.34b) becomes :", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27660,68,367,'paragraph',NULL,'x = v ox t = (v o cos θ o ) t and y = (v o sin θ o ) t – ( ½ )g t 2 (4.38)','[{"s": "x = v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "ox", "t": "text"}, {"s": "t = (v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "cos θ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") t and y = (v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "sin θ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") t – ( ½ )g t", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(4.38)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27662,68,369,'paragraph',NULL,'v x = v ox = v o cos θ o','[{"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "x", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "ox", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "cos θ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27663,68,370,'paragraph',NULL,'v y = v o sin θ o – g t (4.39)','[{"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "y", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "sin θ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "– g t (4.39)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27665,68,372,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Motion_in_a_Plane-image146.png'),
(27666,68,373,'paragraph',NULL,'Equation of path of a projectile','[{"s": "Equation of path of a projectile", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27667,68,374,'paragraph',NULL,'What is the shape of the path followed by the projectile? This can be seen by eliminating the time between the expressions for x and y as given in Eq. (4.38). We obtain:','[{"s": "What is the shape of the path followed by the projectile? This can be seen by eliminating the time between the expressions for x and y as given in Eq. (4.38). We obtain:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27668,68,375,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Motion_in_a_Plane-image155.png'),
(27669,68,376,'paragraph',NULL,'(4.40)','[{"s": "(4.40)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27670,68,377,'paragraph',NULL,'Now, since g, θ o and v o are constants, Eq. (4.40) is of the form y = a x + b x 2 , in which a and b are constants. This is the equation of a parabola, i.e. the path of the projectile is a parabola (Fig. 4.18).','[{"s": "Now, since g, θ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "are constants, Eq. (4.40) is of the form y = a x + b x", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", in which a and b are constants. This is the equation of a parabola, i.e. the path of the projectile is a parabola (Fig. 4.18).", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27671,68,378,'image',NULL,'C4.20',NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Motion_in_a_Plane-image152.png'),
(27672,68,379,'paragraph',NULL,'Fig. 4.18 The path of a projectile is a parabola.','[{"s": "Fig. 4.18", "t": "text"}, {"s": "The path of a projectile is a parabola.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27673,68,380,'paragraph',NULL,'Time of maximum height','[{"s": "Time of maximum height", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27674,68,381,'paragraph',NULL,'How much time does the projectile take to reach the maximum height ? Let this time be denoted by t m . Since at this point, v y = 0, we have from Eq. (4.39):','[{"s": "How much time does the projectile take to reach the maximum height ? Let this time be denoted by t", "t": "text"}, {"s": "m", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". Since at this point, v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "y", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 0, we have from Eq. (4.39):", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27675,68,382,'paragraph',NULL,'v y = v o sinθ o – g t m = 0','[{"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "y", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "sinθ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "– g t", "t": "text"}, {"s": "m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 0", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27676,68,383,'paragraph',NULL,'Or, t m = v o sinθ o /g (4.41a)','[{"s": "Or, t", "t": "text"}, {"s": "m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "sinθ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "/g (4.41a)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27677,68,384,'paragraph',NULL,'The total time T f during which the projectile is in flight can be obtained by putting y = 0 in Eq. (4.38). We get :','[{"s": "The total time T", "t": "text"}, {"s": "f", "t": "text"}, {"s": "during which the projectile is in flight can be obtained by putting y = 0 in Eq. (4.38). We get :", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27678,68,385,'paragraph',NULL,'T f = 2 (v o sin θ o )/g (4.41b)','[{"s": "T", "t": "text"}, {"s": "f", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 2 (v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "sin θ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": ")/g (4.41b)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27679,68,386,'paragraph',NULL,'T f is known as the time of flight of the projectile. We note that T f = 2 t m , which is expected because of the symmetry of the parabolic path.','[{"s": "T", "t": "text"}, {"s": "f", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is known as the", "t": "text"}, {"s": "time of flight", "t": "text"}, {"s": "of the projectile. We note that T", "t": "text"}, {"s": "f", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 2 t", "t": "text"}, {"s": "m", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", which is expected because of the symmetry of the parabolic path.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27680,68,387,'paragraph',NULL,'Maximum height of a projectile','[{"s": "Maximum height of a projectile", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27681,68,388,'paragraph',NULL,'The maximum height h m m in Eq. (4.38) :','[{"s": "The maximum height h", "t": "text"}, {"s": "m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "", "t": "br"}, {"s": "m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "in Eq. (4.38) :", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27682,68,389,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Motion_in_a_Plane-image141.png'),
(27683,68,390,'paragraph',NULL,'Or,','[{"s": "Or,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27684,68,391,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Motion_in_a_Plane-image139.png'),
(27685,68,392,'paragraph',NULL,'(4.42)','[{"s": "(4.42)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27686,68,393,'paragraph',NULL,'Horizontal range of a projectile','[{"s": "Horizontal range of a projectile", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27688,68,395,'paragraph',NULL,'R = (v o cos θ o ) (T f )','[{"s": "R = (v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "cos θ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") (T", "t": "text"}, {"s": "f", "t": "text"}, {"s": ")", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27689,68,396,'paragraph',NULL,'=(v o cos θ o ) (2 v o sin θ o )/g','[{"s": "=(v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "cos θ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") (2 v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "sin θ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": ")/g", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27690,68,397,'paragraph',NULL,'Or,','[{"s": "Or,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27691,68,398,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Motion_in_a_Plane-image144.png'),
(27692,68,399,'paragraph',NULL,'(4.43a)','[{"s": "(4.43a)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27693,68,400,'paragraph',NULL,'Equation (4.43a) shows that for a given projection velocity v o , R is maximum when sin 2θ 0 is maximum, i.e., when θ 0 = 45 0 .','[{"s": "Equation (4.43a) shows that for a given projection velocity v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", R is maximum when sin 2θ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is maximum, i.e., when θ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 45", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27695,68,402,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Motion_in_a_Plane-image142.png'),
(27696,68,403,'paragraph',NULL,'(4.43b)','[{"s": "(4.43b)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27698,68,405,'paragraph',NULL,'Answer For a projectile launched with velocity v o at an angle θ o , the range is given by','[{"s": "Answer", "t": "text"}, {"s": "For a projectile launched with velocity", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "at an angle θ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", the range is given by", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27699,68,406,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Motion_in_a_Plane-image95.png'),
(27700,68,407,'paragraph',NULL,'Now, for angles, (45° + α) and ( 45° – α), 2θ o is (90° + 2α) and ( 90° – 2α) , respectively. The values of sin (90° + 2α) and sin (90° – 2α) are the same, equal to that of cos 2α. Therefore, ranges are equal for elevations which exceed or fall short of 45° by equal amounts α.','[{"s": "Now, for angles, (45° + α) and ( 45°", "t": "text"}, {"s": "– α), 2θ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is (90° + 2α) and ( 90° – 2α) , respectively. The values of sin (90° + 2α) and sin (90° – 2α) are the same, equal to that of cos 2α. Therefore, ranges are equal for elevations which exceed or fall short of 45° by equal amounts α.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27701,68,408,'paragraph',NULL,'Example 4.8 A hiker stands on the edge of a cliff 490 m above the ground and throws a stone horizontally with an initial speed of 15 m s -1 . Neglecting air resistance, find the time taken by the stone to reach the ground, and the speed with which it hits the ground. (Take g = 9.8 m s -2 ).','[{"s": "Example 4.8", "t": "text"}, {"s": "A hiker stands on the edge of a cliff 490 m above the ground and throws a stone horizontally with an initial speed of 15 m s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "-1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". Neglecting air resistance, find the time taken by the stone to reach the ground, and the speed with which it hits the ground. (Take g = 9.8 m s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "-2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ").", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27702,68,409,'paragraph',NULL,'Answer We choose the origin of the x-,and y-axis at the edge of the cliff and t = 0 s at the instant the stone is thrown. Choose the positive direction of x-axis to be along the initial velocity and the positive direction of y-axis to be the vertically upward direction. The x-, and y- components of the motion can be treated independently. The equations of motion are :','[{"s": "Answer", "t": "text"}, {"s": "We choose the origin of the x-,and y-axis at the edge of the cliff and t = 0 s at the instant the stone is thrown. Choose the positive direction of x-axis to be along the initial velocity and the positive direction of y-axis to be the vertically upward direction. The x-, and y- components of the motion can be treated independently. The equations of motion are :", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27703,68,410,'paragraph',NULL,'x (t) = x o + v ox t','[{"s": "x (t) = x", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+ v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "ox", "t": "text"}, {"s": "t", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27704,68,411,'paragraph',NULL,'y (t) = y o + v oy t +(1/2) a y t 2','[{"s": "y (t) = y", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+ v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "oy", "t": "text"}, {"s": "t +(1/2) a", "t": "text"}, {"s": "y", "t": "text"}, {"s": "t", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27694,68,401,'paragraph',NULL,'The maximum horizontal range is, therefore,','[{"s": "The maximum horizontal range is, therefore,", "t": "hl"}]','marked','["2000034029", "2000107308"]',NULL),
(27705,68,412,'paragraph',NULL,'Here, x o = y o = 0, v oy = 0, a y = –g = –9.8 m s -2 ,','[{"s": "Here, x", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= y", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 0, v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "oy", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 0, a", "t": "text"}, {"s": "y", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= –g = –9.8 m s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "-2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ",", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27706,68,413,'paragraph',NULL,'v ox = 15 m s -1 .','[{"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "ox", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 15 m s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "-1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27707,68,414,'paragraph',NULL,'The stone hits the ground when y(t) = – 490 m.','[{"s": "The stone hits the ground when y(t) = – 490 m.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27708,68,415,'paragraph',NULL,'– 490 m = –(1/2)(9.8) t 2 .','[{"s": "– 490 m = –(1/2)(9.8) t", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27709,68,416,'paragraph',NULL,'This gives t =10 s.','[{"s": "This gives t =10 s.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27710,68,417,'paragraph',NULL,'The velocity components are v x = v ox and v y = v oy – g t','[{"s": "The velocity components are v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "x", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "ox", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "y", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "oy", "t": "text"}, {"s": "– g t", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27711,68,418,'paragraph',NULL,'so that when the stone hits the ground :','[{"s": "so that when the stone hits the ground :", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27712,68,419,'paragraph',NULL,'v ox = 15 m s –1','[{"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "ox", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 15 m s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–1", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27713,68,420,'paragraph',NULL,'v oy = 0 – 9.8 × 10 = – 98 m s –1','[{"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "oy", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 0 – 9.8 × 10 = – 98 m s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–1", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(27714,68,421,'paragraph',NULL,'Therefore, the speed of the stone is','[{"s": "Therefore, the speed of the stone is", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
