(28012,69,155,'paragraph',NULL,'connecting five quantities v 0 , v, a, t and x . These are kinematic equations of rectilinear motion for constant acceleration.','[{"s": "connecting five quantities", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", v, a, t", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and", "t": "text"}, {"s": "x", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". These are kinematic equations of rectilinear motion for constant acceleration.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28013,69,156,'paragraph',NULL,'The set of Eq. (3.11a) were obtained by assuming that at t = 0, the position of the particle, x is 0. We can obtain a more general equation if we take the position coordinate at t = 0 as non-zero, say x 0 . Then Eqs. (3.11a) are modified (replacing x by x – x 0 ) to :','[{"s": "The set of Eq. (3.11a) were obtained by assuming that at", "t": "text"}, {"s": "t", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 0, the position of the particle,", "t": "text"}, {"s": "x", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is 0. We can obtain a more general equation if we take the position coordinate at", "t": "text"}, {"s": "t", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 0 as non-zero, say", "t": "text"}, {"s": "x", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". Then Eqs. (3.11a) are modified (replacing", "t": "text"}, {"s": "x", "t": "text"}, {"s": "by", "t": "text"}, {"s": "x", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–", "t": "text"}, {"s": "x", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") to :", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
