(28057,69,200,'paragraph',NULL,'FIRST METHOD : In the first method, we split the path in two parts : the upward motion (A to B) and the downward motion (B to C) and calculate the corresponding time taken t 1 and t 2 . Since the velocity at B is zero, we have :','[{"s": "FIRST METHOD", "t": "text"}, {"s": ": In the first method, we split the path in two parts : the upward motion (A to B) and the downward motion (B to C) and calculate the corresponding time taken", "t": "text"}, {"s": "t", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and", "t": "text"}, {"s": "t", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". Since the velocity at B is zero, we have :", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
