(28355,70,175,'paragraph',NULL,'Figure 4.11 Magnetic field on the axis of a current carrying circular loop of radius R. Shown are the magnetic field dB (due to a line element dl ) and its components along and perpendicular to the axis.','[{"s": "Figure 4.11 Magnetic field on the axis of a current carrying circular loop of radius R. Shown are the magnetic field dB (due to a line element dl ) and its components along and perpendicular to the axis.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28356,70,176,'paragraph',NULL,'Moving_Charges_and_Magnetism-image88.png (4.12)','[{"s": "Moving_Charges_and_Magnetism-image88.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "(4.12)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28357,70,177,'paragraph',NULL,'Now r 2 = x 2 + R 2 . Further, any element of the loop will be perpendicular to the displacement vector from the element to the axial point. For example, the element dl in Fig. 4.11 is in the y-z plane, whereas, the displacement vector r from dl to the axial point P is in the x-y plane. Hence |dl × r|=r dl. Thus,','[{"s": "Now r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= x", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+ R", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". Further, any element of the loop will be perpendicular to the displacement vector from the element to the axial point. For example, the element dl in Fig. 4.11 is in the y-z plane, whereas, the displacement vector r from dl to the axial point P is in the x-y plane. Hence |dl × r|=r dl. Thus,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
