(28770,70,590,'paragraph',NULL,'4.25 A circular coil of 20 turns and radius 10 cm is placed in a uniform magnetic field of 0.10 T normal to the plane of the coil. If the current in the coil is 5.0 A, what is the','[{"s": "4.25 A circular coil of 20 turns and radius 10 cm is placed in a uniform magnetic field of 0.10 T normal to the plane of the coil. If the current in the coil is 5.0 A, what is the", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28771,70,591,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) total torque on the coil,','[{"s": "(a) total torque on the coil,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28772,70,592,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) total force on the coil,','[{"s": "(b) total force on the coil,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28773,70,593,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) average force on each electron in the coil due to the magnetic field?','[{"s": "(c) average force on each electron in the coil due to the magnetic field?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28774,70,594,'paragraph',NULL,'(The coil is made of copper wire of cross-sectional area 10 –5 m 2 29 m –3 .)','[{"s": "(The coil is made of copper wire of cross-sectional area 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–5", "t": "text"}, {"s": "m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "", "t": "br"}, {"s": "29", "t": "text"}, {"s": "m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–3", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28775,70,595,'paragraph',NULL,'4.26 A solenoid 60 cm long and of radius 4.0 cm has 3 layers of windings of 300 turns each. A 2.0 cm long wire of mass 2.5 g lies inside the solenoid (near its centre) normal to its axis; both the wire and the axis of the solenoid are in the horizontal plane. The wire is connected through two leads parallel to the axis of the solenoid to an external battery which supplies a current of 6.0 A in the wire. What value of current (with appropriate sense of circulation) in the windings of the solenoid can support the weight of the wire? g = 9.8 ms –2 .','[{"s": "4.26 A solenoid 60 cm long and of radius 4.0 cm has 3 layers of windings of 300 turns each. A 2.0 cm long wire of mass 2.5 g lies inside the solenoid (near its centre) normal to its axis; both the wire and the axis of the solenoid are in the horizontal plane. The wire is connected through two leads parallel to the axis of the solenoid to an external battery which supplies a current of 6.0 A in the wire. What value of current (with appropriate sense of circulation) in the windings of the solenoid can support the weight of the wire? g = 9.8 ms", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28776,70,596,'paragraph',NULL,'4.27 A galvanometer coil has a resistance of 12 Ω and the metre shows full scale deflection for a current of 3 mA. How will you convert the metre into a voltmeter of range 0 to 18 V?','[{"s": "4.27 A galvanometer coil has a resistance of 12 Ω and the metre shows full scale deflection for a current of 3 mA. How will you convert the metre into a voltmeter of range 0 to 18 V?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28778,70,598,'heading',4,'EXEMPLAR QUESTIONS',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28779,70,599,'paragraph',NULL,'4.1 Two charged particles traverse identical helical paths in a completely opposite sense in a uniform magnetic field B = B 0 k^ .','[{"s": "4.1 Two charged particles traverse identical helical paths in a completely opposite sense in a uniform magnetic field B =", "t": "text"}, {"s": "B", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": "k^", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28780,70,600,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) They have equal z-components of momenta.','[{"s": "(a) They have equal z-components of momenta.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28781,70,601,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) They must have equal charges.','[{"s": "(b) They must have equal charges.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28782,70,602,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) They necessarily represent a particle-antiparticle pair.','[{"s": "(c) They necessarily represent a particle-antiparticle pair.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28783,70,603,'paragraph',NULL,'(d) The charge to mass ratio satisfy: ( e/m ) 1 +( e/m ) 2 =0','[{"s": "(d) The charge to mass ratio satisfy:", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(", "t": "text"}, {"s": "e/m", "t": "text"}, {"s": ")", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+(", "t": "text"}, {"s": "e/m", "t": "text"}, {"s": ")", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "=0", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28784,70,604,'paragraph',NULL,'4.2 Biot-Savart law indicates that the moving electrons (velocity v) produce a magnetic field B such that','[{"s": "4.2 Biot-Savart law indicates that the moving electrons (velocity v) produce a magnetic field B such that", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28785,70,605,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) B ⊥ v.','[{"s": "(a) B ⊥ v.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28786,70,606,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) B || v.','[{"s": "(b) B || v.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28787,70,607,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) it obeys inverse cube law.','[{"s": "(c) it obeys inverse cube law.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28788,70,608,'paragraph',NULL,'(d) it is along the line joining the electron and point of observation.','[{"s": "(d) it is along the line joining the electron and point of observation.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28789,70,609,'paragraph',NULL,'4.3 A current-carrying circular loop of radius R is placed in the x-y plane with center at the origin. Half of the loop with x > 0 is now bent so that it now lies in the y-z plane.','[{"s": "4.3 A current-carrying circular loop of radius R is placed in the x-y plane with center at the origin. Half of the loop with x > 0 is now bent so that it now lies in the y-z plane.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28790,70,610,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) The magnitude of the magnetic moment now diminishes.','[{"s": "(a) The magnitude of the magnetic moment now diminishes.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28791,70,611,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) The magnetic moment does not change.','[{"s": "(b) The magnetic moment does not change.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28792,70,612,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) The magnitude of B at (0.0.z), z >>R increases.','[{"s": "(c) The magnitude of B at (0.0.z), z >>R increases.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28793,70,613,'paragraph',NULL,'(d) The magnitude of B at (0.0.z), z >>R is unchanged.','[{"s": "(d) The magnitude of B at (0.0.z), z >>R is unchanged.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28794,70,614,'paragraph',NULL,'4.4 An electron is projected with uniform velocity along the axis of a current-carrying long solenoid. Which of the following is true?','[{"s": "4.4 An electron is projected with uniform velocity along the axis of a current-carrying long solenoid. Which of the following is true?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28795,70,615,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) The electron will be accelerated along the axis.','[{"s": "(a) The electron will be accelerated along the axis.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28796,70,616,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) The electron path will be circular about the axis.','[{"s": "(b) The electron path will be circular about the axis.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28797,70,617,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) The electron will experience a force at 45° to the axis and hence execute a helical path.','[{"s": "(c) The electron will experience a force at 45° to the axis and hence execute a helical path.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28798,70,618,'paragraph',NULL,'(d) The electron will continue to move with uniform velocity along the axis of the solenoid.','[{"s": "(d) The electron will continue to move with uniform velocity along the axis of the solenoid.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28799,70,619,'paragraph',NULL,'4.5 In a cyclotron, a charged particle','[{"s": "4.5 In a cyclotron, a charged particle", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28800,70,620,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) undergoes acceleration all the time.','[{"s": "(a) undergoes acceleration all the time.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28801,70,621,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) speeds up between the dees because of the magnetic field.','[{"s": "(b) speeds up between the dees because of the magnetic field.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28802,70,622,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) speeds up in a dee.','[{"s": "(c) speeds up in a dee.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28803,70,623,'paragraph',NULL,'(d) slows down within a dee and speeds up between dees.','[{"s": "(d) slows down within a dee and speeds up between dees.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28804,70,624,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) MB','[{"s": "(a) MB", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28805,70,625,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) √3 MB/2','[{"s": "(b) √3 MB/2", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28806,70,626,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) MB/2','[{"s": "(c) MB/2", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28807,70,627,'paragraph',NULL,'(d) zero','[{"s": "(d) zero", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28808,70,628,'paragraph',NULL,'4.7 The gyro-magnetic ratio of an electron in an H-atom, according to the Bohr model, is','[{"s": "4.7 The gyro-magnetic ratio of an electron in an H-atom, according to the Bohr model, is", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28809,70,629,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) independent of which orbit it is in.','[{"s": "(a) independent of which orbit it is in.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28810,70,630,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) negative.','[{"s": "(b) negative.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28811,70,631,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) positive.','[{"s": "(c) positive.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28812,70,632,'paragraph',NULL,'(d) increases with the quantum number n.','[{"s": "(d) increases with the quantum number n.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28813,70,633,'paragraph',NULL,'4.8 Consider a wire carrying a steady current, I placed in a uniform magnetic field B perpendicular to its length. Consider the charges inside the wire. It is known that magnetic forces do no work. This implies that,','[{"s": "4.8 Consider a wire carrying a steady current, I placed in a uniform magnetic field B perpendicular to its length. Consider the charges inside the wire. It is known that magnetic forces do no work. This implies that,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28814,70,634,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) the motion of charges inside the conductor is unaffected by B since they do not absorb energy.','[{"s": "(a) the motion of charges inside the conductor is unaffected by B since they do not absorb energy.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28815,70,635,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) some charges inside the wire move to the surface as a result of B.','[{"s": "(b) some charges inside the wire move to the surface as a result of B.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28816,70,636,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) if the wire moves under the influence of B, no work is done by the force.','[{"s": "(c) if the wire moves under the influence of B, no work is done by the force.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28817,70,637,'paragraph',NULL,'(d) if the wire moves under the influence of B, no work is done by the magnetic force on the ions assumed fixed within the wire.','[{"s": "(d) if the wire moves under the influence of B, no work is done by the magnetic force on the ions assumed fixed within the wire.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28818,70,638,'heading',4,'EXEMPLAR QUESTIONS',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28819,70,639,'paragraph',NULL,'4.9 Two identical current carrying coaxial loops, carry current I in an opposite sense. A simple amperian loop passes through both of them once. Calling the loop as C,','[{"s": "4.9 Two identical current carrying coaxial loops, carry current I in an opposite sense. A simple amperian loop passes through both of them once. Calling the loop as C,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28820,70,640,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) ∮B.d1=∓2μ 0 I .','[{"s": "(a)", "t": "text"}, {"s": "∮B.d1=∓2μ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": "I", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28821,70,641,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) the value of ∮B.dl is independent of the sense of C.','[{"s": "(b) the value of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "∮B.dl", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is independent of the sense of C.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28822,70,642,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) there may be a point on C where B and dl are perpendiculars.','[{"s": "(c) there may be a point on C where B and dl are perpendiculars.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28823,70,643,'paragraph',NULL,'(d) B vanishes everywhere on C.','[{"s": "(d) B vanishes everywhere on C.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28824,70,644,'paragraph',NULL,'4.10 A cubical region of space is filled with some uniform electric and magnetic fields. An electron enters the cube across one of its faces with velocity v and a positron enters via the opposite face with velocity - v. At this instant,','[{"s": "4.10 A cubical region of space is filled with some uniform electric and magnetic fields. An electron enters the cube across one of its faces with velocity v and a positron enters via the opposite face with velocity - v. At this instant,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28825,70,645,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) the electric forces on both the particles cause identical accelerations.','[{"s": "(a) the electric forces on both the particles cause identical accelerations.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28826,70,646,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) the magnetic forces on both the particles cause equal accelerations.','[{"s": "(b) the magnetic forces on both the particles cause equal accelerations.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28827,70,647,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) both particles gain or loose energy at the same rate.','[{"s": "(c) both particles gain or loose energy at the same rate.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28828,70,648,'paragraph',NULL,'(d) the motion of the center of mass (CM) is determined by B alone.','[{"s": "(d) the motion of the center of mass (CM) is determined by B alone.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28829,70,649,'paragraph',NULL,'4.11 A charged particle would continue to move with a constant velocity in a region wherein,','[{"s": "4.11 A charged particle would continue to move with a constant velocity in a region wherein,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28830,70,650,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) E = 0, B ≠ 0.','[{"s": "(a) E = 0, B ≠ 0.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28831,70,651,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) E ≠ 0, B ≠ 0.','[{"s": "(b) E ≠ 0, B ≠ 0.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28832,70,652,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) E ≠ 0, B ≠ 0.','[{"s": "(c) E ≠ 0, B ≠ 0.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28833,70,653,'paragraph',NULL,'(d) E = 0, B = 0.','[{"s": "(d) E = 0, B = 0.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28834,70,654,'paragraph',NULL,'4.12 Verify that the cyclotron frequency ω = eB/m has the correct dimensions of [T] -1 .','[{"s": "4.12 Verify that the cyclotron frequency ω = eB/m has the correct dimensions of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "[T]", "t": "text"}, {"s": "-1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28835,70,655,'paragraph',NULL,'4.13 Show that a force that does no work must be a velocity-dependent force.','[{"s": "4.13 Show that a force that does no work must be a velocity-dependent force.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28836,70,656,'paragraph',NULL,'4.14 The magnetic force depends on v which depends on the inertial frame of reference. Does then the magnetic force differ from inertial frame to frame? Is it reasonable that the net acceleration has a different value in different frames of reference?','[{"s": "4.14 The magnetic force depends on v which depends on the inertial frame of reference. Does then the magnetic force differ from inertial frame to frame? Is it reasonable that the net acceleration has a different value in different frames of reference?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
