(28843,70,663,'paragraph',NULL,'4.19 An electron enters with a velocity v = v0i into a cubical region (faces parallel to coordinate planes) in which there are uniform electric and magnetic fields. The orbit of the electron is found to spiral down inside the cube in a plane parallel to the x-y plane. Suggest a configuration of fields E and B that can lead to it.','[{"s": "4.19 An electron enters with a velocity v = v0i into a cubical region (faces parallel to coordinate planes) in which there are uniform electric and magnetic fields. The orbit of the electron is found to spiral down inside the cube in a plane parallel to the x-y plane. Suggest a configuration of fields E and B that can lead to it.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
