(28845,70,665,'paragraph',NULL,'4.21 A multirange voltmeter can be constructed by using a galvanometer circuit as shown in Fig. 4.2. We want to construct a voltmeter that can measure 2V, 20V, and 200V using a galvanometer of resistance 10Ω and that produces maximum deflection for a current of 1 mA. Find R 1 , R 2 , and R 3 that have to be used.','[{"s": "4.21 A multirange voltmeter can be constructed by using a galvanometer circuit as shown in Fig. 4.2. We want to construct a voltmeter that can measure 2V, 20V, and 200V using a galvanometer of resistance 10Ω and that produces maximum deflection for a current of 1 mA. Find", "t": "text"}, {"s": "R", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", R", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", and R", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "that have to be used.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
