(28992,71,125,'paragraph',NULL,'N ( t ) = N 0 e −λ t (13.14)','[{"s": "N", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(", "t": "text"}, {"s": "t", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") =", "t": "text"}, {"s": "N", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": "e", "t": "text"}, {"s": "−λ t", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(13.14)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28993,71,126,'paragraph',NULL,'Note, for example, the light bulbs follow no such exponential decay law. If we test 1000 bulbs for their life (time span before they burn out or fuse), we expect that they will ‘decay’ (that is, burn out) at more or less the same time. The decay of radionuclides follows quite a different law, the law of radioactive decay represented by Eq. (13.14).','[{"s": "Note, for example, the light bulbs follow no such exponential decay law. If we test 1000 bulbs for their life (time span before they burn out or fuse), we expect that they will ‘decay’ (that is, burn out) at more or less the same time. The decay of radionuclides follows quite a different law, the", "t": "text"}, {"s": "law of radioactive decay", "t": "text"}, {"s": "represented by Eq. (13.14).", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(28994,71,127,'paragraph',NULL,'The total decay rate R of a sample is the number of nuclei disintegrating per unit time. Suppose in a time interval dt, the decay count measured is ∆ N . Then d N = – ∆ N .','[{"s": "The total decay rate", "t": "text"}, {"s": "R", "t": "text"}, {"s": "of a sample is the number of nuclei disintegrating per unit time. Suppose in a time interval dt, the decay count measured is ∆", "t": "text"}, {"s": "N", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". Then d", "t": "text"}, {"s": "N", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= – ∆", "t": "text"}, {"s": "N", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29015,71,148,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Nuclei-image73.png'),
(29016,71,149,'paragraph',NULL,'One can show by performing this integral that','[{"s": "One can show by performing this integral that", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29017,71,150,'paragraph',NULL,'τ = 1/λ','[{"s": "τ = 1/λ", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29018,71,151,'paragraph',NULL,'We summarise these results with the following:','[{"s": "We summarise these results with the following:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29019,71,152,'paragraph',NULL,'T 1/2 = Nuclei-image102.png = τ ln 2 (13.18)','[{"s": "T", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1/2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "=", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image102.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "= τ ln 2 (13.18)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29020,71,153,'paragraph',NULL,'Radioactive elements (e.g., tritium, plutonium) which are short-lived i.e., have half-lives much less than the age of the universe (~15 billion years) have obviously decayed long ago and are not found in nature. They can, however, be produced artificially in nuclear reactions.','[{"s": "Radioactive elements (e.g., tritium, plutonium) which are short-lived i.e., have half-lives much less than the age of the universe (~15 billion years) have obviously decayed long ago and are not found in nature. They can, however, be produced artificially in nuclear reactions.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29021,71,154,'paragraph',NULL,'Example 13.4 The half-life of Nuclei-image5.png undergoing α-decay is 4.5 × 10 9 years. What is the activity of 1g sample of Nuclei-image49.png ?','[{"s": "Example 13.4", "t": "text"}, {"s": "The half-life of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image5.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "undergoing α-decay is 4.5 × 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "9", "t": "text"}, {"s": "years. What is the activity of 1g sample of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image49.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29022,71,155,'paragraph',NULL,'Solution','[{"s": "Solution", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29023,71,156,'paragraph',NULL,'T 1/2 = 4.5 × 10 9 y','[{"s": "T", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1/2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 4.5 × 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "9", "t": "text"}, {"s": "y", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29024,71,157,'paragraph',NULL,'= 4.5 × 10 9 y x 3.16 x 10 7 s/y','[{"s": "= 4.5 × 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "9", "t": "text"}, {"s": "y x 3.16 x 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "7", "t": "text"}, {"s": "s/y", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29025,71,158,'paragraph',NULL,'= 1.42 × 10 17 s','[{"s": "= 1.42 × 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "17", "t": "text"}, {"s": "s", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29026,71,159,'paragraph',NULL,'One k mol of any isotope contains Avogadro’s number of atoms, and so 1g of Nuclei-image13.png contains','[{"s": "One k mol of any isotope contains Avogadro’s number of atoms, and so 1g of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image13.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "contains", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29027,71,160,'paragraph',NULL,'Nuclei-image16.png × 6.025 × 10 26 atoms/kmol','[{"s": "Nuclei-image16.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "× 6.025 × 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "26", "t": "text"}, {"s": "atoms/kmol", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29028,71,161,'paragraph',NULL,'= 25.3 × 10 20 atoms.','[{"s": "= 25.3 × 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "20", "t": "text"}, {"s": "atoms.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
