(29226,71,359,'paragraph',NULL,'13.8 The normal activity of living carbon-containing matter is found to be about 15 decays per minute for every gram of carbon. This activity arises from the small proportion of radioactive Nuclei-image72.png present with the stable carbon isotope Nuclei-image58.png . When the organism is dead, its interaction with the atmosphere (which maintains the above equilibrium activity) ceases and its activity begins to drop. From the known half-life (5730 years) of Nuclei-image55.png , and the measured activity, the age of the specimen can be approximately estimated. This is the principle of Nuclei-image55.png dating used in archaeology. Suppose a specimen from Mohenjodaro gives an activity of 9 decays per minute per gram of carbon. Estimate the approximate age of the Indus-Valley civilisation.','[{"s": "13.8", "t": "text"}, {"s": "The normal activity of living carbon-containing matter is found to be about 15 decays per minute for every gram of carbon. This activity arises from the small proportion of radioactive", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image72.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "present with the stable carbon isotope", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image58.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": ". When the organism is dead, its interaction with the atmosphere (which maintains the above equilibrium activity) ceases and its activity begins to drop. From the known half-life (5730 years) of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image55.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": ", and the measured activity, the age of the specimen can be approximately estimated. This is the principle of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image55.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "dating used in archaeology. Suppose a specimen from Mohenjodaro gives an activity of 9 decays per minute per gram of carbon. Estimate the approximate age of the Indus-Valley civilisation.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
