(29251,71,384,'paragraph',NULL,'13.16 Suppose, we think of the fission of a Nuclei-image22.png nucleus into two equal fragments, Nuclei-image105.png . Is the fission energetically possible? Argue by working out Q of the process. Given m ( Nuclei-image22.png Nuclei-image105.png ) = 27.98191 u.','[{"s": "13.16", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Suppose, we think of the fission of a", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image22.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "nucleus into two equal fragments,", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image105.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": ". Is the fission energetically possible? Argue by working out Q of the process. Given m (", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image22.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "", "t": "br"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image105.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": ") = 27.98191 u.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29252,71,385,'paragraph',NULL,'13.17 The fission properties of Nuclei-image86.png are very similar to those of Nuclei-image8.png . The average energy released per fission is 180 MeV. How much energy, in MeV, is released if all the atoms in 1 kg of pure Nuclei-image86.png undergo fission?','[{"s": "13.17", "t": "text"}, {"s": "The fission properties of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image86.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "are very similar to those of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image8.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": ". The average energy released per fission is 180 MeV. How much energy, in MeV, is released if all the atoms in 1 kg of pure", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image86.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "undergo fission?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29253,71,386,'paragraph',NULL,'13.18 A 1000 MW fission reactor consumes half of its fuel in 5.00 y. How much Nuclei-image8.png did it contain initially? Assume that the reactor operates 80% of the time, that all the energy generated arises from the fission of Nuclei-image8.png and that this nuclide is consumed only by the fission process.','[{"s": "13.18", "t": "text"}, {"s": "A 1000 MW fission reactor consumes half of its fuel in 5.00 y. How much", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image8.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "did it contain initially? Assume that the reactor operates 80% of the time, that all the energy generated arises from the fission of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image8.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "and that this nuclide is consumed only by the fission process.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
