(29262,71,395,'paragraph',NULL,'13.23 In a periodic table the average atomic mass of magnesium is given as 24.312 u. The average value is based on their relative natural abundance on earth. The three isotopes and their masses are Nuclei-image123.png (23.98504u) , Nuclei-image138.png (24.98584u) and Nuclei-image29.png (25.98259u). The natural abundance of Nuclei-image139.png is 78.99% by mass. Calculate the abundances of other two isotopes.','[{"s": "13.23", "t": "text"}, {"s": "In a periodic table the average atomic mass of magnesium is given as 24.312 u. The average value is based on their relative natural abundance on earth. The three isotopes and their masses are", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image123.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "(23.98504u)", "t": "text"}, {"s": ",", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image138.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "(24.98584u) and", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image29.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "(25.98259u). The natural abundance of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image139.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "is 78.99% by mass. Calculate the abundances of other two isotopes.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
