(29268,71,401,'paragraph',NULL,'13.25 A source contains two phosphorous radio nuclides Nuclei-image79.png (T 1/2 = 14.3d) and Nuclei-image39.png (T 1/2 = 25.3d). Initially, 10% of the decays come from Nuclei-image39.png . How long one must wait until 90% do so?','[{"s": "13.25", "t": "text"}, {"s": "A source contains two phosphorous radio nuclides", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image79.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "(T", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1/2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 14.3d) and", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image39.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "(T", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1/2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 25.3d). Initially, 10% of the decays come from", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image39.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": ". How long one must wait until 90% do so?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29269,71,402,'paragraph',NULL,'13.26 Under certain circumstances, a nucleus can decay by emitting a particle more massive than an α-particle. Consider the following decay processes:','[{"s": "13.26", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Under certain circumstances, a nucleus can decay by emitting a particle more massive than an α-particle. Consider the following decay processes:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
