(29273,71,406,'paragraph',NULL,'13.27 Consider the fission of Nuclei-image57.png by fast neutrons. In one fission event, no neutrons are emitted and the final end products, after the beta decay of the primary fragments, are Nuclei-image98.png and Nuclei-image30.png . Calculate Q for this fission process. The relevant atomic and particle masses are','[{"s": "13.27", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Consider the fission of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image57.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "by fast neutrons. In one fission event, no neutrons are emitted and the final end products, after the beta decay of the primary fragments, are", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image98.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "and", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Nuclei-image30.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Calculate Q for this fission process. The relevant atomic and particle masses are", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
