(29357,71,490,'paragraph',NULL,'18. A piece of wood from the ruins of an ancient building was found to have a 14 C activity of 12 distintegrations per minute per gram of its carbon content. The 14 C activity of the living wood is 16 disintegrations per minute per gram. How long ago did the tree, from which the wooden sample came, die? Given half-life of 14 C is 5760 yr.','[{"s": "18. A piece of wood from the ruins of an ancient building was found to have a", "t": "text"}, {"s": "14", "t": "text"}, {"s": "C activity of 12 distintegrations per minute per gram of its carbon content. The", "t": "text"}, {"s": "14", "t": "text"}, {"s": "C activity of the living wood is 16 disintegrations per minute per gram. How long ago did the tree, from which the wooden sample came, die? Given half-life of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "14", "t": "text"}, {"s": "C is 5760 yr.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29358,71,491,'paragraph',NULL,'19. Are the nucleons fundamental particles, or do they consist of still smaller parts? One way to find out is to probe a nucleon just as Rutherford probed an atom. What should be the kinetic energy of an electron for it to be able to probe a nucleon? Assume the diameter of a nucleon to be approximately 10 -15 m.','[{"s": "19. Are the nucleons fundamental particles, or do they consist of still smaller parts? One way to find out is to probe a nucleon just as Rutherford probed an atom. What should be the kinetic energy of an electron for it to be able to probe a nucleon? Assume the diameter of a nucleon to be approximately 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "-15", "t": "text"}, {"s": "m.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29359,71,492,'paragraph',NULL,'20. A nuclide 1 is said to be the mirror isobar of nuclide 2 if Z 1 = N 2 and Z 2 = N 1 . (a) What nuclide is a mirror isobar of 11 23 Na ? (b) Which nuclide out of the two mirror isobars have greater binding energy and why?','[{"s": "20. A nuclide 1 is said to be the mirror isobar of nuclide 2 if Z", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= N", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and Z", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= N", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". (a) What nuclide is a mirror isobar of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "11", "t": "text"}, {"s": "23", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Na", "t": "text"}, {"s": "? (b) Which nuclide out of the two mirror isobars have greater binding energy and why?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
