(29362,71,495,'paragraph',NULL,'Assume that we start with 1000 38 S nuclei at time t = 0. The number of 38 Cl is of count zero at t = 0 and will again be zero at t = ∞ . At what value of t, would the numebr of counts be a maximum?','[{"s": "Assume that we start with 1000", "t": "text"}, {"s": "38", "t": "text"}, {"s": "S", "t": "text"}, {"s": "nuclei at time t = 0. The number of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "38", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Cl", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is of count zero at t = 0 and will again be zero at t =", "t": "text"}, {"s": "∞", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". At what value of t, would the numebr of counts be a maximum?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29363,71,496,'paragraph',NULL,'22. Deuteron is a bound satate of a neutron and a proton with a binding energy B = 2.2 MeV. A γ -ray of energy E is aimed at a deuteron nucleus to try to break it into a (neutron + proton) such that the n and p move in the direction of the incident γ -ray. If E = B, show that this cannot happen. Hence, calculate how much bigger than B must E be for such a process to happen.','[{"s": "22. Deuteron is a bound satate of a neutron and a proton with a binding energy B = 2.2 MeV. A", "t": "text"}, {"s": "γ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "-ray of energy E is aimed at a deuteron nucleus to try to break it into a (neutron + proton) such that the n and p move in the direction of the incident", "t": "text"}, {"s": "γ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "-ray. If E = B, show that this cannot happen. Hence, calculate how much bigger than B must E be for such a process to happen.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
