(29462,72,70,'paragraph',NULL,'(i) sin ωt + cos ωt','[{"s": "(i) sin ωt + cos ωt", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29463,72,71,'paragraph',NULL,'(ii) sin ωt + cos 2 ωt + sin 4 ωt','[{"s": "(ii) sin ωt + cos 2 ωt + sin 4 ωt", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29464,72,72,'paragraph',NULL,'(iii) e – ωt','[{"s": "(iii) e", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–", "t": "text"}, {"s": "ωt", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29465,72,73,'paragraph',NULL,'(iv) log (ωt)','[{"s": "(iv) log (ωt)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29466,72,74,'paragraph',NULL,'Answer','[{"s": "Answer", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29467,72,75,'paragraph',NULL,'(i) sin ωt + cos ωt is a periodic function, it can also be written as Oscillations-image23.png','[{"s": "(i) sin ωt + cos ωt is a periodic function, it can also be written as", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Oscillations-image23.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29468,72,76,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Oscillations-image96.png'),
(29469,72,77,'paragraph',NULL,'The periodic time of the function is 2π/ω.','[{"s": "The periodic time of the function is 2π/ω.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29470,72,78,'paragraph',NULL,'(ii) This is an example of a periodic motion. It can be noted that each term represents a periodic function with a different angular frequency. Since period is the least interval of time after which a function repeats its value, sin ωt has a period T 0 = 2π/ω ; cos 2 ωt has a period π/ω =T 0 /2; and sin 4 ωt has a period 2π/4ω = T 0 /4. The period of the first term is a multiple of the periods of the last two terms. Therefore, the smallest interval of time after which the sum of the three terms repeats is T 0 , and thus, the sum is a periodic function with a period 2π/ω.','[{"s": "(ii) This is an example of a periodic motion. It can be noted that each term represents a periodic function with a different angular frequency. Since period is the least interval of time after which a function repeats its value, sin ωt has a period T", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 2π/ω ; cos 2 ωt has a period π/ω =T", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": "/2; and sin 4 ωt has a period 2π/4ω = T", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": "/4. The period of the first term is a multiple of the periods of the last two terms. Therefore, the smallest interval of time after which the sum of the three terms repeats is T", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", and thus, the sum is a periodic function with a period 2π/ω.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29471,72,79,'paragraph',NULL,'(iii) The function e –ωt is not periodic, it decreases monotonically with increasing time and tends to zero as t → ∞ and thus, never repeats its value.','[{"s": "(iii) The function e", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–ωt", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is not periodic, it decreases monotonically with increasing time and tends to zero as t →", "t": "text"}, {"s": "∞", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and thus, never repeats its value.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29472,72,80,'paragraph',NULL,'∞ , log(ωt) diverges to ∞ . It, therefore, cannot represent any kind of physical displacement.','[{"s": "", "t": "br"}, {"s": "∞", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", log(ωt) diverges to", "t": "text"}, {"s": "∞", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". It, therefore, cannot represent any kind of physical displacement.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29473,72,81,'heading',4,'14.3 Simple harmonic motion',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29474,72,82,'paragraph',NULL,'Consider a particle oscillating back and forth about the origin of an x-axis between the limits +A and –A as shown in Fig. 14.3. This oscillatory motion is said to be simple harmonic if the displacement x of the particle from the origin varies with time as :','[{"s": "Consider a particle oscillating back and forth about the origin of an x-axis between the limits +A and –A as shown in Fig. 14.3. This oscillatory motion is said to be simple harmonic if the displacement x of the particle from the origin varies with time as :", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29475,72,83,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Oscillations-image115.png'),
(29476,72,84,'paragraph',NULL,'Fig. 14.3 A particle vibrating back and forth about the origin of x-axis, between the limits +A and –A.','[{"s": "Fig. 14.3 A particle vibrating back and forth about the origin of x-axis, between the limits +A and –A.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29477,72,85,'paragraph',NULL,'x (t) = A cos (ω t + φ) (14.4)','[{"s": "x (t) = A cos (ω t + φ) (14.4)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29478,72,86,'paragraph',NULL,'where A, ω and φ are constants.','[{"s": "where A, ω and φ are constants.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
