(29754,72,362,'paragraph',NULL,'In this function, the cosine function has a period 2π/ω′ but the function x(t) is not strictly periodic because of the factor e –b t/2m which decreases continuously with time. However, if the decrease is small in one time period T, the motion represented by Eq. (14.33) is approximately periodic.','[{"s": "In this function, the cosine function has a period 2π/ω′ but the function x(t) is not strictly periodic because of the factor e", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–b t/2m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "which decreases continuously with time. However, if the decrease is small in one time period T, the motion represented by Eq. (14.33) is approximately periodic.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29755,72,363,'paragraph',NULL,'The solution, Eq. (14.33),can be graphically represented as shown in Fig. 14.20. We can regard it as a cosine function whose amplitude,which is','[{"s": "The solution, Eq. (14.33),can be graphically represented as shown in Fig. 14.20. We can regard it as a cosine function whose amplitude,which is", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29756,72,364,'paragraph',NULL,'Ae –b t/2m , gradually decreases with time.','[{"s": "Ae", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–b t/2m", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", gradually decreases with time.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29757,72,365,'paragraph',NULL,'Now the mechanical energy of the undamped oscillator is 1/2 kA 2 . For a damped oscillator, the amplitude is not constant but depends on time. For small damping, we may use the same expression but regard the amplitude as A e –bt/2m.','[{"s": "Now the mechanical energy of the undamped oscillator is 1/2 kA", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". For a damped oscillator, the amplitude is not constant but depends on time. For small damping, we may use the same expression but regard the amplitude as A e", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–bt/2m.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
