(29916,72,524,'paragraph',NULL,'14.14 The piston in the cylinder head of a locomotive has a stroke (twice the amplitude) of 1.0 m. If the piston moves with simple harmonic motion with an angular frequency of 200 rad/min, what is its maximum speed?','[{"s": "14.14", "t": "text"}, {"s": "The piston in the cylinder head of a locomotive has a stroke (twice the amplitude) of 1.0 m. If the piston moves with simple harmonic motion with an angular frequency of 200 rad/min, what is its maximum speed?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29917,72,525,'paragraph',NULL,'14.15 The acceleration due to gravity on the surface of the moon is 1.7 m s –2 . What is the time period of a simple pendulum on the surface of the moon if its time period on the surface of the earth is 3.5 s ? (g on the surface of the earth is 9.8 m s –2 )','[{"s": "14.15", "t": "text"}, {"s": "The acceleration due to gravity on the surface of the moon is 1.7 m s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". What is the time period of a simple pendulum on the surface of the moon if its time period on the surface of the earth is 3.5 s ? (g on the surface of the earth is 9.8 m s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ")", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29919,72,527,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) Time period of a particle in SHM depends on the force constant k and mass m of the particle: Oscillations-image46.png','[{"s": "(a) Time period of a particle in SHM depends on the force constant k and mass m of the particle:", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Oscillations-image46.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29920,72,528,'paragraph',NULL,'A simple pendulum executes SHM approximately. Why then is the time period of a pendulum independent of the mass of the pendulum?','[{"s": "A simple pendulum executes SHM approximately. Why then is the time period of a pendulum independent of the mass of the pendulum?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29921,72,529,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) The motion of a simple pendulum is approximately simple harmonic for small-angle oscillations. For larger angles of oscillation, a more involved analysis shows that T is greater than Oscillations-image80.png','[{"s": "(b) The motion of a simple pendulum is approximately simple harmonic for small-angle oscillations. For larger angles of oscillation, a more involved analysis shows that T is greater than", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Oscillations-image80.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29922,72,530,'paragraph',NULL,'. Think of a qualitative argument to appreciate this result.','[{"s": ". Think of a qualitative argument to appreciate this result.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29923,72,531,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) A man with a wristwatch on his hand falls from the top of a tower. Does the watch give correct time during the free fall?','[{"s": "(c) A man with a wristwatch on his hand falls from the top of a tower. Does the watch give correct time during the free fall?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29924,72,532,'paragraph',NULL,'(d) What is the frequency of oscillation of a simple pendulum mounted in a cabin that is freely falling under gravity?','[{"s": "(d) What is the frequency of oscillation of a simple pendulum mounted in a cabin that is freely falling under gravity?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29925,72,533,'paragraph',NULL,'14.17 A simple pendulum of length l and having a bob of mass M is suspended in a car. The car is moving on a circular track of radius R with a uniform speed v. If the pendulum makes small oscillations in a radial direction about its equilibrium position, what will be its time period?','[{"s": "14.17", "t": "text"}, {"s": "A simple pendulum of length l and having a bob of mass M is suspended in a car. The car is moving on a circular track of radius R with a uniform speed v. If the pendulum makes small oscillations in a radial direction about its equilibrium position, what will be its time period?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29927,72,535,'paragraph',NULL,'The cork is depressed slightly and then released. Show that the cork oscillates up and down simple harmonically with a period','[{"s": "The cork is depressed slightly and then released. Show that the cork oscillates up and down simple harmonically with a period", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29928,72,536,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Oscillations-image108.png'),
(29929,72,537,'paragraph',NULL,'where ρ is the density of cork. (Ignore damping due to viscosity of the liquid).','[{"s": "where ρ is the density of cork. (Ignore damping due to viscosity of the liquid).", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29930,72,538,'paragraph',NULL,'14.19 One end of a U-tube containing mercury is connected to a suction pump and the other end to the atmosphere. A small pressure difference is maintained between the two columns. Show that, when the suction pump is removed, the column of mercury in the U-tube executes simple harmonic motion.','[{"s": "14.19", "t": "text"}, {"s": "One end of a U-tube containing mercury is connected to a suction pump and the other end to the atmosphere. A small pressure difference is maintained between the two columns. Show that, when the suction pump is removed, the column of mercury in the U-tube executes simple harmonic motion.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29931,72,539,'paragraph',NULL,'Additional Exercises','[{"s": "Additional Exercises", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(29932,72,540,'paragraph',NULL,'14.20 An air chamber of volume V has a neck area of cross-section \'a\' into which a ball of mass \'m\' just fits and can move up and down without any friction (Fig.14.27). Show that when the ball is pressed down a little and released, it executes SHM. Obtain an expression for the time period of oscillations assuming pressure-volume variations of air to be isothermal [see Fig. 14.27].','[{"s": "14.20", "t": "text"}, {"s": "An air chamber of volume V has a neck area of cross-section \'a\' into which a ball of mass \'m\' just fits and can move up and down without any friction (Fig.14.27). Show that when the ball is pressed down a little and released, it executes SHM. Obtain an expression for the time period of oscillations assuming pressure-volume variations of air to be isothermal [see Fig. 14.27].", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
