(30219,73,277,'paragraph',NULL,'Example 9.8 (i) If f = 0.5 m for a glass lens, what is the power of the lens? (ii) The radii of curvature of the faces of a double convex lens are 10 cm and 15 cm. Its focal length is 12 cm. What is the refractive index of glass? (iii) A convex lens has 20 cm focal length in air. What is focal length in water? (Refractive index of air-water = 1.33, refractive index for air-glass = 1.5.)','[{"s": "Example 9.8", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(i) If f = 0.5 m for a glass lens, what is the power of the lens? (ii) The radii of curvature of the faces of a double convex lens are 10 cm and 15 cm. Its focal length is 12 cm. What is the refractive index of glass? (iii) A convex lens has 20 cm focal length in air. What is focal length in water? (Refractive index of air-water = 1.33, refractive index for air-glass = 1.5.)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30220,73,278,'paragraph',NULL,'Solution','[{"s": "Solution", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30221,73,279,'paragraph',NULL,'(i) Power = +2 dioptre.','[{"s": "(i) Power = +2 dioptre.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30222,73,280,'paragraph',NULL,'(ii) Here, we have f = +12 cm, R 1 = +10 cm, R 2 = –15 cm.','[{"s": "(ii) Here, we have f = +12 cm, R", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= +10 cm, R", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= –15 cm.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30223,73,281,'paragraph',NULL,'Refractive index of air is taken as unity.','[{"s": "Refractive index of air is taken as unity.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30225,73,283,'paragraph',NULL,'Substituting the values, we have','[{"s": "Substituting the values, we have", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
