(30615,73,673,'paragraph',NULL,'9.29 The mixture a pure liquid and a solution in a long vertical column (i.e., horizontal dimensions<< vertical dimensions) produces diffusion of solute particles and hence a refractive index gradient along the vertical dimension. A ray of light entering the column at right angles to the vertical is deviated from its original path. Find the deviation in travelling a horizontal distance d<<h, the height of the column.','[{"s": "9.29", "t": "text"}, {"s": "The mixture a pure liquid and a solution in a long vertical column (i.e., horizontal dimensions<< vertical dimensions) produces diffusion of solute particles and hence a refractive index gradient along the vertical dimension. A ray of light entering the column at right angles to the vertical is deviated from its original path. Find the deviation in travelling a horizontal distance d<<h, the height of the column.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(30616,73,674,'paragraph',NULL,'9.30 n(r)=1+2 GM/rc 2 where r is the distance of the point of consideration from the centre of the mass of the massive body, G is the universal gravitational constant, M the mass of the body and c the speed of light in vacuum. Considering a spherical object find the deviation of the ray from the original path as it grazes the object .','[{"s": "9.30", "t": "text"}, {"s": "", "t": "br"}, {"s": "n(r)=1+2 GM/rc", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "", "t": "br"}, {"s": "where r is the distance of the point of consideration from the centre of the mass of the massive body, G is the universal gravitational constant, M the mass of the body and c the speed of light in vacuum. Considering a spherical object find the deviation of the ray from the original path as it grazes the object", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
