(31046,74,424,'paragraph',NULL,'(iv) NAND Gate','[{"s": "(iv) NAND Gate", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(31047,74,425,'paragraph',NULL,'This is an AND gate followed by a NOT gate. 7 If inputs A and B are both ‘1’, the output Y is not ‘1’. The gate gets its name from this NOT AND behaviour. Figure 14.33 shows the symbol and truth table of NAND gate.','[{"s": "This is an AND gate followed by a NOT gate.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "7", "t": "text"}, {"s": "If inputs A", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and", "t": "text"}, {"s": "B are both ‘1’, the output Y is", "t": "text"}, {"s": "not", "t": "text"}, {"s": "‘1’. The gate gets its name from this NOT AND behaviour. Figure 14.33 shows the symbol and truth table of NAND gate.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(31048,74,426,'paragraph',NULL,'NAND gates are also called Universal Gates since by using these gates you can realise other basic gates like OR, AND and NOT (Exercises 14.12 and 14.13). 2','[{"s": "NAND gates are also called", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Universal Gates", "t": "text"}, {"s": "since by using these gates you can realise other basic gates like OR, AND and NOT (Exercises 14.12 and 14.13).", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
