(31694,75,360,'paragraph',NULL,'Thus, the time rate of change of the angular momentum of a particle is equal to the torque acting on it. This is the rotational analogue of the equation F = d p /dt, which expresses Newton’s second law for the translational motion of a single particle.','[{"s": "Thus, the time rate of change of the angular momentum of a particle is equal to the torque acting on it. This is the rotational analogue of the equation", "t": "text"}, {"s": "F", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= d", "t": "text"}, {"s": "p", "t": "text"}, {"s": "/dt, which expresses Newton’s second law for the translational motion of a single particle.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(31695,75,361,'paragraph',NULL,'Torque and angular momentum for a system of particles','[{"s": "Torque and angular momentum for a system of particles", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(31696,75,362,'paragraph',NULL,'To get the total angular momentum of a system of particles about a given point we need to add vectorially the angular momenta of individual particles. Thus, for a system of n particles,','[{"s": "To get the total angular momentum of a system of particles about a given point we need to add vectorially the angular momenta of individual particles. Thus, for a system of n particles,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
