(32086,75,752,'paragraph',NULL,'(d) The answers are the same, i.e. the kinetic energy gained by the wheel = work done by the force. There is no loss of energy due to friction.','[{"s": "(d) The answers are the same, i.e. the kinetic energy gained by the wheel = work done by the force. There is no loss of energy due to friction.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32087,75,753,'heading',2,'7.13 ANGULAR MOMENTUM IN CASE OF ROTATION ABOUT A FIXED AXIS',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32089,75,755,'paragraph',NULL,'We now wish to study the angular momentum in the special case of rotation about a fixed axis. The general expression for the total angular momentum of the system of n particles is','[{"s": "We now wish to study the angular momentum in the special case of rotation about a fixed axis. The general expression for the total angular momentum of the system of n particles is", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32090,75,756,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Systems_Of_Particles-image164.png'),
(32091,75,757,'paragraph',NULL,'(7.25b)','[{"s": "(7.25b)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32092,75,758,'paragraph',NULL,'We first consider the angular momentum of a typical particle of the rotating rigid body. We then sum up the contributions of individual particles to get L of the whole body.','[{"s": "We first consider the angular momentum of a typical particle of the rotating rigid body. We then sum up the contributions of individual particles to get", "t": "text"}, {"s": "L", "t": "text"}, {"s": "of the whole body.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32093,75,759,'paragraph',NULL,'For a typical particle l = r × p . As seen in the last section r = OP = OC + CP [Fig. 7.17(b)]. With p = m v ,','[{"s": "For a typical particle", "t": "text"}, {"s": "l", "t": "text"}, {"s": "=", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "×", "t": "text"}, {"s": "p", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". As seen in the last section", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "=", "t": "text"}, {"s": "OP", "t": "text"}, {"s": "=", "t": "text"}, {"s": "OC", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+", "t": "text"}, {"s": "CP", "t": "text"}, {"s": "[Fig. 7.17(b)]. With", "t": "text"}, {"s": "p", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": ",", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32094,75,760,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Systems_Of_Particles-image151.png'),
(32095,75,761,'paragraph',NULL,'The magnitude of the linear velocity v of the particle at P is given by v = ωr ⊥ where r ⊥ is the length of CP or the perpendicular distance of P from the axis of rotation. Further, v is tangential at P to the circle which the particle describes. Using the right-hand rule one can check that CP × v is parallel to the fixed axis. The unit vector along the fixed axis (chosen as the z-axis) is Systems_Of_Particles-image15.png . Hence','[{"s": "The magnitude of the linear velocity", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "of the particle at P is given by v = ωr", "t": "text"}, {"s": "⊥", "t": "text"}, {"s": "where r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "⊥", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is the length of CP or the perpendicular distance of P from the axis of rotation. Further,", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is tangential at P to the circle which the particle describes. Using the right-hand rule one can check that", "t": "text"}, {"s": "CP", "t": "text"}, {"s": "×", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is parallel to the fixed axis. The unit vector along the fixed axis (chosen as the z-axis) is", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Systems_Of_Particles-image15.png", "t": "img", "alt": "Screen Shot 2019-06-09 at 6.54.12 PM"}, {"s": ". Hence", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32096,75,762,'image',NULL,'Screen Shot 2019-06-09 at 6.54.49 PM',NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Systems_Of_Particles-image91.png'),
(32097,75,763,'paragraph',NULL,'Similarly, we can check that OC × v is perpendicular to the fixed axis. Let us denote the part of l along the fixed axis (i.e. the z-axis) by l z , then','[{"s": "Similarly, we can check that", "t": "text"}, {"s": "OC", "t": "text"}, {"s": "×", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is perpendicular to the fixed axis. Let us denote the part of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "l", "t": "text"}, {"s": "along the fixed axis (i.e. the z-axis) by", "t": "text"}, {"s": "l", "t": "text"}, {"s": "z", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", then", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32098,75,764,'image',NULL,'Screen Shot 2019-06-09 at 6.55.21 PM',NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Systems_Of_Particles-image47.png'),
(32099,75,765,'paragraph',NULL,'and Systems_Of_Particles-image200.png','[{"s": "and", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Systems_Of_Particles-image200.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32100,75,766,'paragraph',NULL,'We note that l z is parallel to the fixed axis, but l is not. In general, for a particle, the angular momentum l is not along the axis of rotation, i.e. for a particle, l and ω are not necessarily parallel. Compare this with the corresponding fact in translation. For a particle, p and v are always parallel to each other.','[{"s": "We note that", "t": "text"}, {"s": "l", "t": "text"}, {"s": "z", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is parallel to the fixed axis, but", "t": "text"}, {"s": "l", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is not. In general, for a particle, the angular momentum", "t": "text"}, {"s": "l", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is not along the axis of rotation, i.e. for a particle,", "t": "text"}, {"s": "l", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and ω are not necessarily parallel. Compare this with the corresponding fact in translation. For a particle,", "t": "text"}, {"s": "p", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "are always parallel to each other.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32101,75,767,'paragraph',NULL,'For computing the total angular momentum of the whole rigid body, we add up the contribution of each particle of the body.','[{"s": "For computing the total angular momentum of the whole rigid body, we add up the contribution of each particle of the body.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32102,75,768,'paragraph',NULL,'Thus Systems_Of_Particles-image226.png','[{"s": "Thus", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Systems_Of_Particles-image226.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32103,75,769,'paragraph',NULL,'We denote by Systems_Of_Particles-image139.png and L Z the components of L respectively perpendicular to the z-axis and along the z-axis;','[{"s": "We denote by", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Systems_Of_Particles-image139.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "and L", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Z", "t": "text"}, {"s": "the components of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "L", "t": "text"}, {"s": "respectively perpendicular to the z-axis and along the z-axis;", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32104,75,770,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Systems_Of_Particles-image57.png'),
(32105,75,771,'paragraph',NULL,'(7.44a)','[{"s": "(7.44a)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32106,75,772,'paragraph',NULL,'where m i and v i are respectively the mass and the velocity of the i th particle and C i is the centre of the circle described by the particle;','[{"s": "where m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "i", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "i", "t": "text"}, {"s": "are respectively the mass and the velocity of the i", "t": "text"}, {"s": "th", "t": "text"}, {"s": "particle and C", "t": "text"}, {"s": "i", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is the centre of the circle described by the particle;", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32107,75,773,'image',NULL,'Screen Shot 2019-06-09 at 6.56.52 PM',NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Systems_Of_Particles-image308.png'),
(32108,75,774,'paragraph',NULL,'(7.44b)','[{"s": "(7.44b)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32109,75,775,'paragraph',NULL,'The last step follows since the perpendicular distance of the i th particle from the axis is r i ; and by definition the moment of inertia of the body about the axis of rotation is Systems_Of_Particles-image70.png .','[{"s": "The last step follows since the perpendicular distance of the i", "t": "text"}, {"s": "th", "t": "text"}, {"s": "particle from the axis is r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "i", "t": "text"}, {"s": "; and by definition the moment of inertia of the body about the axis of rotation is", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Systems_Of_Particles-image70.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32110,75,776,'paragraph',NULL,'Note Systems_Of_Particles-image108.png','[{"s": "Note", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Systems_Of_Particles-image108.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32111,75,777,'paragraph',NULL,'(7.44c)','[{"s": "(7.44c)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32112,75,778,'paragraph',NULL,'The rigid bodies which we have mainly considered in this chapter are symmetric about the axis of rotation, i.e. the axis of rotation is one of their symmetry axes. For such bodies, for a given OC i , for every particle which has a velocity v i , there is another particle of velocity – v i located diametrically opposite on the circle with centre C i described by the particle. Together such pairs will contribute zero to Systems_Of_Particles-image139.png and as a result for symmetric bodies Systems_Of_Particles-image139.png is zero, and hence','[{"s": "The rigid bodies which we have mainly considered in this chapter are symmetric about the axis of rotation, i.e. the axis of rotation is one of their symmetry axes. For such bodies, for a given", "t": "text"}, {"s": "OC", "t": "text"}, {"s": "i", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", for every particle which has a velocity", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "i", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", there is another particle of velocity –", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "i", "t": "text"}, {"s": "located diametrically opposite on the circle with centre C", "t": "text"}, {"s": "i", "t": "text"}, {"s": "described by the particle. Together such pairs will contribute zero to", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Systems_Of_Particles-image139.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "and as a result for symmetric bodies", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Systems_Of_Particles-image139.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "is zero, and hence", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32113,75,779,'image',NULL,'Screen Shot 2019-06-09 at 6.57.58 PM',NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Systems_Of_Particles-image53.png'),
(32114,75,780,'paragraph',NULL,'(7.44d)','[{"s": "(7.44d)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32115,75,781,'paragraph',NULL,'For bodies, which are not symmetric about the axis of rotation, L is not equal to L z and hence L does not lie along the axis of rotation.','[{"s": "For bodies, which are not symmetric about the axis of rotation,", "t": "text"}, {"s": "L", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is not equal to", "t": "text"}, {"s": "L", "t": "text"}, {"s": "z", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and hence", "t": "text"}, {"s": "L", "t": "text"}, {"s": "does not lie along the axis of rotation.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32116,75,782,'paragraph',NULL,'Referring to Table 7.1, can you tell in which cases L = L z will not apply?','[{"s": "Referring to Table 7.1, can you tell in which cases", "t": "text"}, {"s": "L", "t": "text"}, {"s": "=", "t": "text"}, {"s": "L", "t": "text"}, {"s": "z", "t": "text"}, {"s": "will not apply?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32117,75,783,'paragraph',NULL,'Let us differentiate Eq. (7.44b). Since Systems_Of_Particles-image15.png is a fixed (constant) vector, we get','[{"s": "Let us differentiate Eq. (7.44b). Since", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Systems_Of_Particles-image15.png", "t": "img", "alt": "Screen Shot 2019-06-09 at 6.54.12 PM"}, {"s": "is a fixed (constant) vector, we get", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32118,75,784,'image',NULL,'Screen Shot 2019-06-09 at 6.59.13 PM',NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Systems_Of_Particles-image2.png'),
(32119,75,785,'paragraph',NULL,'Now, Eq. (7.28b) states','[{"s": "Now, Eq. (7.28b) states", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32120,75,786,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Systems_Of_Particles-image246.png'),
(32121,75,787,'paragraph',NULL,'As we have seen in the last section, only those components of the external torques which are along the axis of rotation, need to be taken into account, when we discuss rotation about a fixed axis. This means we can take Systems_Of_Particles-image137.png . Since Systems_Of_Particles-image108.png and the direction of L z (vector Systems_Of_Particles-image15.png ) is fixed, it follows that for rotation about a fixed axis,','[{"s": "As we have seen in the last section, only those components of the external torques which are along the axis of rotation, need to be taken into account, when we discuss rotation about a fixed axis. This means we can take", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Systems_Of_Particles-image137.png", "t": "img", "alt": "Screen Shot 2019-06-09 at 7.00.11 PM"}, {"s": ". Since", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Systems_Of_Particles-image108.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "and the direction of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "L", "t": "text"}, {"s": "z", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(vector", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Systems_Of_Particles-image15.png", "t": "img", "alt": "Screen Shot 2019-06-09 at 6.54.12 PM"}, {"s": ") is fixed, it follows that for rotation about a fixed axis,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32122,75,788,'image',NULL,'Screen Shot 2019-06-09 at 7.00.53 PM',NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Systems_Of_Particles-image307.png'),
(32123,75,789,'paragraph',NULL,'(7.45a)','[{"s": "(7.45a)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
