(32285,75,951,'paragraph',NULL,'7.23 A man stands on a rotating platform, with his arms stretched horizontally holding a 5 kg weight in each hand. The angular speed of the platform is 30 revolutions per minute. The man then brings his arms close to his body with the distance of each weight from the axis changing from 90cm to 20cm. The moment of inertia of the man together with the platform may be taken to be constant and equal to 7.6 kg m 2 . (a) What is his new angular speed? (Neglect friction.)','[{"s": "7.23", "t": "text"}, {"s": "A man stands on a rotating platform, with his arms stretched horizontally holding a 5 kg weight in each hand. The angular speed of the platform is 30 revolutions per minute. The man then brings his arms close to his body with the distance of each weight from the axis changing from 90cm to 20cm. The moment of inertia of the man together with the platform may be taken to be constant and equal to 7.6 kg m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". (a) What is his new angular speed? (Neglect friction.)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32286,75,952,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) Is kinetic energy conserved in the process? If not, from where does the change come about?','[{"s": "(b) Is kinetic energy conserved in the process? If not, from where does the change come about?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32287,75,953,'paragraph',NULL,'7.24 A bullet of mass 10 g and speed 500 m/s is fired into a door and gets embedded exactly at the centre of the door. The door is 1.0 m wide and weighs 12 kg. It is hinged at one end and rotates about a vertical axis practically without friction. Find the angular speed of the door just after the bullet embeds into it.','[{"s": "7.24", "t": "text"}, {"s": "A bullet of mass 10 g and speed 500 m/s is fired into a door and gets embedded exactly at the centre of the door. The door is 1.0 m wide and weighs 12 kg. It is hinged at one end and rotates about a vertical axis practically without friction. Find the angular speed of the door just after the bullet embeds into it.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32288,75,954,'paragraph',NULL,'(Hint: The moment of inertia of the door about the vertical axis at one end is ML 2 /3.)','[{"s": "(Hint: The moment of inertia of the door about the vertical axis at one end is ML", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "/3.)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32289,75,955,'paragraph',NULL,'7.25 Two discs of moments of inertia I 1 and I 2 about their respective axes (normal to the disc and passing through the centre), and rotating with angular speeds ω 1 and ω 2 are brought into contact face to face with their axes of rotation coincident. (a) What is the angular speed of the two-disc system? (b) Show that the kinetic energy of the combined system is less than the sum of the initial kinetic energies of the two discs. How do you account for this loss in energy? Take ω 1 ≠ ω 2 .','[{"s": "7.25", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Two discs of moments of inertia I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "about their respective axes (normal to the disc and passing through the centre), and rotating with angular speeds ω", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and ω", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "are brought into contact face to face with their axes of rotation coincident. (a) What is the angular speed of the two-disc system? (b) Show that the kinetic energy of the combined system is less than the sum of the initial kinetic energies of the two discs. How do you account for this loss in energy? Take ω", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "≠ ω", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32290,75,956,'paragraph',NULL,'7.26 (a) Prove the theorem of perpendicular axes.','[{"s": "7.26", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(a) Prove the theorem of perpendicular axes.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
