(32335,75,1001,'paragraph',NULL,'Question 7. 1. Give the location of the center of mass of an (i) sphere, (ii) cylinder, (iii) ring, and (iv) cube, each of uniform mass density. Does the center of mass of a body necessarily lie inside the body?','[{"s": "Question 7. 1. Give the location of the center of mass of an (i) sphere, (ii) cylinder, (iii) ring, and (iv) cube, each of uniform mass density. Does the center of mass of a body necessarily lie inside the body?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32336,75,1002,'paragraph',NULL,'Question 7. 2. In the HCl molecule, the separation between the nuclei of the two atoms is about 1.27 ( 1 A 0 = 10 -10 m) Find the approximate location of the CM of the molecule, given that a chlorine atom is about 35.5 times as massive as a hydrogen atom and nearly all the mass of an atom is concentrated in its nucleus.','[{"s": "Question 7. 2. In the HCl molecule, the separation between the nuclei of the two atoms is about 1.27", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1 A", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "-10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "m)", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Find the approximate location of the CM of the molecule, given that a chlorine atom is about 35.5 times as massive as a hydrogen atom and nearly all the mass of an atom is concentrated in its nucleus.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32337,75,1003,'paragraph',NULL,'Question 7. 3. A child sits stationary at one end of a long trolley moving uniformly with a speed V on a smooth horizontal floor. If the child gets up and runs about on the trolley in any manner, what is the speed of the CM of the (trolley + child) system?','[{"s": "Question 7. 3. A child sits stationary at one end of a long trolley moving uniformly with a speed V on a smooth horizontal floor. If the child gets up and runs about on the trolley in any manner, what is the speed of the CM of the (trolley + child) system?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32338,75,1004,'paragraph',NULL,'Question 7. 4. Show that the area of the triangle contained between the vectors a⇀ and b⇀ is one half of the magnitude of a⇀ × b⇀ .','[{"s": "Question 7. 4. Show that the area of the triangle contained between the vectors", "t": "text"}, {"s": "a⇀ and b⇀", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is one half of the magnitude of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "a⇀ × b⇀", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(32339,75,1005,'paragraph',NULL,'Question 7. 5. Show that a→.b→ x c→ is equal in magnitude to the volume of the parallelepiped formed on the three vectors, a→, b→ and c⇀','[{"s": "Question 7. 5. Show that", "t": "text"}, {"s": "a→.b→ x c→", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is equal in magnitude to the volume of the parallelepiped formed on the three vectors,", "t": "text"}, {"s": "a→, b→ and c⇀", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
