(32365,75,1031,'paragraph',NULL,'Question 7. 27. Prove the result that the velocity v of translation of a rolling body (like a ring, disc, cylinder, or sphere) at the bottom of an inclined plane of a height h is given by,v 2 =2gh/(1+k 2 /R 2 ) using dynamical consideration (i.e., by consideration of forces and torques). Note k is the radius of gyration of the body about its symmetry axis, and R is the radius of the body. The body starts from rest at the top of the plane.','[{"s": "Question 7. 27. Prove the result that the velocity v of translation of a rolling body (like a ring, disc, cylinder, or sphere) at the bottom of an inclined plane of a height h is given by,v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "=2gh/(1+k", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "/R", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") using dynamical consideration (i.e., by consideration of forces and torques). Note k is the radius of gyration of the body about its symmetry axis, and R is the radius of the body. The body starts from rest at the top of the plane.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
