(33416,77,395,'paragraph',NULL,'Q. 20 In a refrigerator one removes heat from a lower temperature and deposits to the surroundings at a higher temperature. In this process, mechanical work has to be done, which is provided by an electric motor. If the motor is of 1kW power and heat transferred from —3°C to 27°C, find the heat taken out of the refrigerator per second assuming its efficiency is 50%of a perfect engine.','[{"s": "Q. 20 In a refrigerator one removes heat from a lower temperature and deposits to the surroundings at a higher temperature. In this process, mechanical work has to be done, which is provided by an electric motor. If the motor is of 1kW power and heat transferred from —3°C to 27°C, find the heat taken out of the refrigerator per second assuming its efficiency is 50%of a perfect engine.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
