(33849,78,410,'paragraph',NULL,'Example 2.16 The SI unit of energy is J = kg m 2 s –2 ; that of speed v is m s –1 and of acceleration a is m s –2 . Which of the formulae for kinetic energy (K) given below can you rule out on the basis of dimensional arguments (m stands for the mass of the body) :','[{"s": "Example 2.16", "t": "text"}, {"s": "The SI unit of energy is J = kg m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "; that of speed v is m s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and of acceleration a is m s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". Which of the formulae for kinetic energy (K) given below can you rule out on the basis of dimensional arguments (m stands for the mass of the body) :", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(33850,78,411,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) K = m 2 v 3','[{"s": "(a) K = m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
