(34006,78,567,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) 3.0 m s –2 = .... km h –2','[{"s": "(c) 3.0 m s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= .... km h", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–2", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34007,78,568,'paragraph',NULL,'(d) G = 6.67 × 10 –11 N m 2 (kg) –2 = .... (cm) 3 s –2 g –1 .','[{"s": "(d) G = 6.67 × 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–11", "t": "text"}, {"s": "N m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(kg)", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= .... (cm)", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "g", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34008,78,569,'paragraph',NULL,'2.3 A calorie is a unit of heat (energy in transit) and it equals about 4.2 J where 1 J = 1 kgm 2 s –2 . Suppose we employ a system of units in which the unit of mass equals α kg, the unit of length equals β m, the unit of time is γ sec. Show that a calorie has a magnitude of 4.2 α –1 β –2 γ 2 in terms of the new units.','[{"s": "2.3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "A calorie is a unit of heat (energy in transit) and it equals about 4.2 J where 1 J = 1 kgm", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". Suppose we employ a system of units in which the unit of mass equals α kg, the unit of length equals β m, the unit of time is γ sec. Show that a calorie has a magnitude of 4.2 α", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "β", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "γ", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "in terms of the new units.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34009,78,570,'paragraph',NULL,'2.4 Explain this statement clearly :','[{"s": "2.4", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Explain this statement clearly :", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34010,78,571,'paragraph',NULL,'“To call a dimensional quantity ‘large’ or ‘small’ is meaningless without specifying a standard for comparison”. In view of this, reframe the following statements wherever necessary :','[{"s": "“To call a dimensional quantity ‘large’ or ‘small’ is meaningless without specifying a standard for comparison”. In view of this, reframe the following statements wherever necessary :", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34011,78,572,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) Atoms are very small objects','[{"s": "(a) Atoms are very small objects", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34012,78,573,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) a jet plane moves with great speed','[{"s": "(b) a jet plane moves with great speed", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34013,78,574,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) the mass of Jupiter is very large','[{"s": "(c) the mass of Jupiter is very large", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34014,78,575,'paragraph',NULL,'(d) the air inside this room contains a large number of molecules','[{"s": "(d) the air inside this room contains a large number of molecules", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34015,78,576,'paragraph',NULL,'(e) a proton is much more massive than an electron','[{"s": "(e) a proton is much more massive than an electron", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34016,78,577,'paragraph',NULL,'(f) the speed of sound is much smaller than the speed of light.','[{"s": "(f) the speed of sound is much smaller than the speed of light.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34017,78,578,'paragraph',NULL,'2.5 A new unit of length is chosen such that the speed of light in a vacuum is unity. What is the distance between the Sun and the Earth in terms of the new unit if light takes 8 min and 20 s to cover this distance?','[{"s": "2.5", "t": "text"}, {"s": "A new unit of length is chosen such that the speed of light in a vacuum is unity. What is the distance between the Sun and the Earth in terms of the new unit if light takes 8 min and 20 s to cover this distance?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34018,78,579,'paragraph',NULL,'2.6 Which of the following is the most precise device for measuring length?','[{"s": "2.6", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Which of the following is the most precise device for measuring length?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34019,78,580,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) A vernier callipers with 20 divisions on the sliding scale.','[{"s": "(a) A vernier callipers with 20 divisions on the sliding scale.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34020,78,581,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) A screw gauge of pitch 1 mm and 100 divisions on the circular scale','[{"s": "(b) A screw gauge of pitch 1 mm and 100 divisions on the circular scale", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34021,78,582,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) An optical instrument that can measure the length to within a wavelength of light.','[{"s": "(c) An optical instrument that can measure the length to within a wavelength of light.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34022,78,583,'paragraph',NULL,'(d) Both (a) and (b)','[{"s": "(d) Both (a) and (b)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34023,78,584,'paragraph',NULL,'2.7 A student measures the thickness of a human hair by looking at it through a microscope of magnification 100. He makes 20 observations and finds that the average width of the hair in the field of view of the microscope is 3.5 mm. What is the estimate of the thickness of the hair?','[{"s": "2.7", "t": "text"}, {"s": "A student measures the thickness of a human hair by looking at it through a microscope of magnification 100. He makes 20 observations and finds that the average width of the hair in the field of view of the microscope is 3.5 mm. What is the estimate of the thickness of the hair?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34024,78,585,'paragraph',NULL,'2.8 Answer the following :','[{"s": "2.8", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Answer the following :", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34025,78,586,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) You are given a thread and a meter scale. How will you estimate the diameter of the thread?','[{"s": "(a) You are given a thread and a meter scale. How will you estimate the diameter of the thread?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34026,78,587,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) A screw gauge has a pitch of 1.0 mm and 200 divisions on the circular scale. Do you think it is possible to increase the accuracy of the screw gauge arbitrarily by increasing the number of divisions on the circular scale?','[{"s": "(b) A screw gauge has a pitch of 1.0 mm and 200 divisions on the circular scale. Do you think it is possible to increase the accuracy of the screw gauge arbitrarily by increasing the number of divisions on the circular scale?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34027,78,588,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) The mean diameter of a thin brass rod is to be measured by vernier callipers. Why is a set of 100 measurements of the diameter expected to yield a more reliable estimate than a set of 5 measurements only?','[{"s": "(c) The mean diameter of a thin brass rod is to be measured by vernier callipers. Why is a set of 100 measurements of the diameter expected to yield a more reliable estimate than a set of 5 measurements only?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34028,78,589,'paragraph',NULL,'2.9 The photograph of a house occupies an area of 1.75 cm 2 on a 35 mm slide. The slide is projected onto a screen, and the area of the house on the screen is 1.55 m 2 . What is the linear magnification of the projector-screen arrangement?','[{"s": "2.9", "t": "text"}, {"s": "The photograph of a house occupies an area of 1.75 cm", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "on a 35 mm slide. The slide is projected onto a screen, and the area of the house on the screen is 1.55 m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". What is the linear magnification of the projector-screen arrangement?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34029,78,590,'paragraph',NULL,'2.10 State the number of significant figures in the following :','[{"s": "2.10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "State the number of significant figures in the following :", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
