(34554,79,474,'paragraph',NULL,'Q. 22 The optical properties of a medium are governed by the relative permittivity ( ε r ) and relative permeability ( u r ) . The refractive index is defined as √u r ε r =n . For ordinary material, ε r >0 and u r >0 and 4, > 0 and the positive sign is taken for the square root.','[{"s": "Q. 22 The optical properties of a medium are governed by the relative permittivity (", "t": "text"}, {"s": "ε", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") and relative permeability (", "t": "text"}, {"s": "u", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") . The refractive index is defined as", "t": "text"}, {"s": "√u", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "ε", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "=n", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". For ordinary material,", "t": "text"}, {"s": "ε", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r", "t": "text"}, {"s": ">0 and u", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r", "t": "text"}, {"s": ">0", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and 4, > 0 and the positive sign is taken for the square root.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34555,79,475,'paragraph',NULL,'In 1964, a Russian scientist V. Veselago postulated the existence of material with ε r <0 and u r <0. Since, then such metamaterials have been produced in the laboratories and their optical properties studied, For such materials √u r ε r .','[{"s": "In 1964, a Russian scientist V. Veselago postulated the existence of material with", "t": "text"}, {"s": "ε", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "<0 and", "t": "text"}, {"s": "u", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "<0. Since, then such metamaterials have been produced in the laboratories and their optical properties studied, For such materials", "t": "text"}, {"s": "√u", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "ε", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}, {"s": "", "t": "br"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34556,79,476,'paragraph',NULL,'(i) According to the description above show that if rays of light enter such a medium from air (refractive index = 1) at an angle 8 in 2nd quadrant, then the refracted beam is in the 3rd quadrant.','[{"s": "(i) According to the description above show that if rays of light enter such a medium from air (refractive index = 1) at an angle 8 in 2nd quadrant, then the refracted beam is in the 3rd quadrant.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34557,79,477,'paragraph',NULL,'(ii) Prove that Snell\'s law holds for such a medium.','[{"s": "(ii) Prove that Snell\'s law holds for such a medium.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34558,79,478,'paragraph',NULL,'Q. 23 To ensure almost 100% transmissivity, photographic lenses are often coated with a thin layer of dielectric material. The refractive index of this material is intermediated between that of air and glass (which makes the optical element of the lens). A typically used dielectric film is MgF 2 (n = 1.38). What should the thickness of the film be so that at the centre of the visible spectrum (5500 ∘ A ) there is maximum transmission.','[{"s": "Q. 23 To ensure almost 100% transmissivity, photographic lenses are often coated with a thin layer of dielectric material. The refractive index of this material is intermediated between that of air and glass (which makes the optical element of the lens). A typically used dielectric film is MgF", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(n = 1.38). What should the thickness of the film be so that at the centre of the visible spectrum (5500", "t": "text"}, {"s": "∘", "t": "text"}, {"s": "A", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") there is maximum transmission.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
