(34771,80,204,'paragraph',NULL,'This modification of Newton’s formula is referred to as the Laplace correction. For air γ = 7/5. Now using Eq. (15.24) to estimate the speed of sound in air at STP, we get a value 331.3 m s –1 , which agrees with the measured speed.','[{"s": "This modification of Newton’s formula is referred to as the Laplace correction. For air γ = 7/5. Now using Eq. (15.24) to estimate the speed of sound in air at STP, we get a value 331.3 m s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", which agrees with the measured speed.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34772,80,205,'heading',4,'15.5 The principle of superposition of waves',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34770,80,203,'paragraph',NULL,'v = √ γP/ρ (15.24)','[{"s": "v =", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "√", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "γP/ρ", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "(15.24)", "t": "hl"}]','marked','["2000040450", "2000109211"]',NULL),
(34773,80,206,'paragraph',NULL,'According to this principle, each pulse moves as if others are not present. The constituents of the medium, therefore, suffer displacments due to both and since the displacements can be positive and negative, the net displacement is an algebraic sum of the two. Fig. 15.9 gives graphs of the wave shape at different times. Note the dramatic effect in the graph (c); the displacements due to the two pulses have exactly cancelled each other and there is zero displacement throughout.','[{"s": "According to this principle, each pulse moves as if others are not present. The constituents of the medium, therefore, suffer displacments due to both and since the displacements can be positive and negative, the net displacement is an algebraic sum of the two. Fig. 15.9 gives graphs of the wave shape at different times. Note the dramatic effect in the graph (c); the displacements due to the two pulses have exactly cancelled each other and there is zero displacement throughout.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34774,80,207,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/physics/images/Waves-image109.png'),
(34775,80,208,'paragraph',NULL,'Fig. 15.9 Two pulses having equal and opposite displacements moving in opposite directions. The overlapping pulses add up to zero displacement in curve (c).','[{"s": "Fig. 15.9 Two pulses having equal and opposite displacements moving in opposite directions. The overlapping pulses add up to zero displacement in curve (c).", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34776,80,209,'paragraph',NULL,'To put the principle of superposition mathematically, let y 1 (x,t) and y 2 (x,t) be the displacements due to two wave disturbances in the medium. If the waves arrive in a region simultaneously, and therefore, overlap, the net displacement y (x,t) is given by','[{"s": "To put the principle of superposition mathematically, let y", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(x,t) and y", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(x,t) be the displacements due to two wave disturbances in the medium. If the waves arrive in a region simultaneously, and therefore, overlap, the net displacement y (x,t) is given by", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34777,80,210,'paragraph',NULL,'y (x, t) = y 1 (x, t) + y 2 (x, t) (15.25)','[{"s": "y (x, t) = y", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(x, t) + y", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(x, t) (15.25)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34778,80,211,'paragraph',NULL,'If we have two or more waves moving in the medium the resultant waveform is the sum of wave functions of individual waves. That is, if the wave functions of the moving waves are','[{"s": "If we have two or more waves moving in the medium the resultant waveform is the sum of wave functions of individual waves. That is, if the wave functions of the moving waves are", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34779,80,212,'paragraph',NULL,'y 1 = f 1 (x–vt),','[{"s": "y", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= f", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(x–vt),", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34780,80,213,'paragraph',NULL,'y 2 = f 2 (x–vt),','[{"s": "y", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= f", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(x–vt),", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34781,80,214,'paragraph',NULL,'..........','[{"s": "..........", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34782,80,215,'paragraph',NULL,'..........','[{"s": "..........", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34783,80,216,'paragraph',NULL,'y n = f n (x–vt)','[{"s": "y", "t": "text"}, {"s": "n", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= f", "t": "text"}, {"s": "n", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(x–vt)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34784,80,217,'paragraph',NULL,'then the wave function describing the disturbance in the medium is','[{"s": "then the wave function describing the disturbance in the medium is", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34785,80,218,'paragraph',NULL,'y = f 1 (x – vt)+ f 2 (x – vt)+ ...+ f n (x – vt)','[{"s": "y = f", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(x – vt)+ f", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(x – vt)+ ...+ f", "t": "text"}, {"s": "n", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(x – vt)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34786,80,219,'paragraph',NULL,'Waves-image63.png (15.26)','[{"s": "Waves-image63.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "(15.26)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34787,80,220,'paragraph',NULL,'The principle of superposition is basic to the phenomenon of interference.','[{"s": "The principle of superposition is basic to the phenomenon of interference.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34789,80,222,'paragraph',NULL,'y 1 (x, t) = a sin (kx – ωt) (15.27)','[{"s": "y", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(x, t) = a sin (kx – ωt) (15.27)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34790,80,223,'paragraph',NULL,'and y 2 (x, t) = a sin (kx – ωt + φ ) (15.28)','[{"s": "and y", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(x, t) = a sin (kx – ωt + φ ) (15.28)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34792,80,225,'paragraph',NULL,'y (x, t) = a sin (kx – ωt) + a sin (kx – ωt + φ) (15.29)','[{"s": "y (x, t) = a sin (kx – ωt) + a sin (kx – ωt + φ) (15.29)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
