(34870,80,303,'paragraph',NULL,'The systems above, strings and air columns, can also undergo forced oscillations (Chapter 14). If the external frequency is close to one of the natural frequencies, the system shows resonance.','[{"s": "The systems above, strings and air columns, can also undergo forced oscillations (Chapter 14). If the external frequency is close to one of the natural frequencies, the system shows resonance.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(34871,80,304,'paragraph',NULL,'Normal modes of a circular membrane rigidly clamped to the circumference as in a tabla are determined by the boundary condition that no point on the circumference of the membrane vibrates. Estimation of the frequencies of normal modes of this system is more complex. This problem involves wave propagation in two dimensions. However, the underlying physics is the same.','[{"s": "Normal modes of a circular membrane rigidly clamped to the circumference as in a tabla are determined by the boundary condition that no point on the circumference of the membrane vibrates. Estimation of the frequencies of normal modes of this system is more complex. This problem involves wave propagation in two dimensions. However, the underlying physics is the same.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
