(35440,81,203,'paragraph',NULL,'which means that K + V, the sum of the kinetic and potential energies of the body is a constant. Over the whole path, x i to x f , this means that','[{"s": "which means that K + V, the sum of the kinetic and potential energies of the body is a constant. Over the whole path, x", "t": "text"}, {"s": "i", "t": "text"}, {"s": "to x", "t": "text"}, {"s": "f", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", this means that", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(35441,81,204,'paragraph',NULL,'K i + V(x i ) = K f + V(x f ) (6.11)','[{"s": "K", "t": "text"}, {"s": "i", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+ V(x", "t": "text"}, {"s": "i", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") = K", "t": "text"}, {"s": "f", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+ V(x", "t": "text"}, {"s": "f", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") (6.11)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(35442,81,205,'paragraph',NULL,'The quantity K +V(x), is called the total mechanical energy of the system. Individually the kinetic energy K and the potential energy V(x) may vary from point to point, but the sum is a constant. The aptness of the term ‘conservative force’ is now clear.','[{"s": "The quantity K +V(x), is called the total mechanical energy of the system. Individually the kinetic energy K and the potential energy V(x) may vary from point to point, but the sum is a constant. The aptness of the term ‘conservative force’ is now clear.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(35443,81,206,'paragraph',NULL,'Let us consider some of the definitions of a conservative force.','[{"s": "Let us consider some of the definitions of a conservative force.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(35444,81,207,'paragraph',NULL,'W = K f – K i = V (x i ) – V(x f )','[{"s": "W = K", "t": "text"}, {"s": "f", "t": "text"}, {"s": "– K", "t": "text"}, {"s": "i", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= V (x", "t": "text"}, {"s": "i", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") – V(x", "t": "text"}, {"s": "f", "t": "text"}, {"s": ")", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(35445,81,208,'paragraph',NULL,'which depends on the end points.','[{"s": "which depends on the end points.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(35446,81,209,'paragraph',NULL,'Thus, the principle of conservation of total mechanical energy can be stated as','[{"s": "Thus, the principle of conservation of total mechanical energy can be stated as", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(35448,81,211,'paragraph',NULL,'The above discussion can be made more concrete by considering the example of the gravitational force once again and that of the spring force in the next section. Fig. 6.5 depicts a ball of mass m being dropped from a cliff of height H.','[{"s": "The above discussion can be made more concrete by considering the example of the gravitational force once again and that of the spring force in the next section. Fig. 6.5 depicts a ball of mass m being dropped from a cliff of height H.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
