(35511,81,274,'paragraph',NULL,'Fig. 6.7 Illustration of the spring force with a block attached to the free end of the spring. (a) The spring force Fs is zero when the displacement x from the equilibrium position is zero. (b) For the stretched spring x > 0 and Fs < 0 (c) For the compressed spring x < 0 and Fs > 0.(d) The plot of Fs versus x. The area of the shaded triangle represents the work done by the spring force. Due to the opposing signs of Fs and x, this work done is negative,','[{"s": "Fig. 6.7", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Illustration of the spring force with a block attached to the free end of the spring. (a) The spring force Fs is zero when the displacement x from the equilibrium position is zero. (b) For the stretched spring x > 0 and Fs < 0 (c) For the compressed spring x < 0 and Fs > 0.(d) The plot of Fs versus x. The area of the shaded triangle represents the work done by the spring force. Due to the opposing signs of Fs and x, this work done is negative,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
