(27756,68,463,'paragraph',NULL,'Now, if the distance travelled by the object during the time ∆t is ∆s, i.e. PP′ is ∆s, then :','[{"s": "Now, if the distance travelled by the object during the time ∆t is ∆s, i.e.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "PP′ is ∆s, then :", "t": "text"}]','marked','["2000107276"]',NULL),
(2064,20,195,'paragraph',NULL,'In prokaryotes, control of the rate of transcriptional initiation is the predominant site for control of gene expression. In a transcription unit, the activity of RNA polymerase at a given promoter is in turn regulated by interaction with accessory proteins, which affect its ability to recognise start sites. These regulatory proteins can act both positively (activators) and negatively (repressors). The accessibility of promoter regions of prokaryotic DNA is in many cases regulated by the interaction of proteins with sequences termed operators . The operator region is adjacent to the promoter elements in most operons and in most cases the sequences of the operator bind a repressor protein. Each operon has its specific operator and specific repressor. For example, lac operator is present only in the lac operon and it interacts specifically with lac repressor only.','[{"s": "In prokaryotes, control of the rate of transcriptional initiation is the predominant site for control of gene expression.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "In a transcription unit, the activity of RNA polymerase at a given promoter is in turn regulated by interaction with accessory proteins, which affect its ability to recognise start sites. These regulatory proteins can act both positively (activators) and negatively (repressors).", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "The accessibility of promoter regions of prokaryotic DNA is in many cases regulated by the interaction of proteins with sequences termed", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "operators", "t": "hl"}, {"s": ".", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "The operator region is adjacent to the promoter elements in most operons and in most cases the sequences of the operator bind a repressor protein. Each operon has its specific operator and specific repressor. For example, lac operator is present only in the lac operon and it interacts specifically with lac repressor only.", "t": "text"}]','marked',NULL,NULL),
