(23810,60,158,'paragraph',NULL,'It covers wavelengths ranging from about 4 × 10 –7 m (400 nm) down to 6 × 10 –10 m (0.6 nm). Ultraviolet (uv) radiation is produced by special lamps and very hot bodies. The sun is an important source of ultraviolet light. But fortunately, most of it is absorbed in the ozone layer in the atmosphere at an altitude of about 40 – 50 km. uv light in large quantities has harmful effects on humans. Exposure to UV radiation induces the production of more melanin, causing tanning of the skin. UV radiation is absorbed by ordinary glass. Hence, one cannot get tanned or sunburn through glass windows.','[{"s": "It covers wavelengths ranging from about 4 × 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–7", "t": "text"}, {"s": "m (400 nm) down to 6 × 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "m (0.6 nm). Ultraviolet (uv) radiation is produced by special lamps and very hot bodies. The sun is an important source of ultraviolet light.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "But fortunately, most of it is absorbed in the ozone layer in the atmosphere at an altitude of about 40 – 50 km.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "uv light in large quantities has harmful effects on humans. Exposure to UV radiation induces the production of more melanin, causing tanning of the skin. UV radiation is absorbed by ordinary glass. Hence, one cannot get tanned or sunburn through glass windows.", "t": "text"}]','marked',NULL,NULL),
(3283,28,23,'paragraph',NULL,'Another effective and popular method is the use of Intra Uterine Devices (IUDs). These devices are inserted by doctors or expert nurses in the uterus through vagina. These Intra Uterine Devices are presently available as the non-medicated IUDs (e.g., Lippes loop), copper releasing IUDs (CuT, Cu7, Multiload 375) and the hormone releasing IUDs (Progestasert, LNG-20) (Figure 4.2). IUDs increase phagocytosis of sperms within the uterus and the Cu ions released suppress sperm motility and the fertilising capacity of sperms. The hormone releasing IUDs, in addition, make the uterus unsuitable for implantation and the cervix hostile to the sperms. IUDs are ideal contraceptives for the females who want to delay pregnancy and/or space children. It is one of most widely accepted methods of contraception in India.','[{"s": "Another effective and popular method is the use of", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "Intra Uterine Devices (IUDs).", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "These devices are inserted by doctors or expert nurses in the uterus through vagina. These Intra Uterine Devices are presently available as the non-medicated IUDs (e.g., Lippes loop), copper releasing IUDs (CuT, Cu7, Multiload 375) and the hormone releasing IUDs (Progestasert, LNG-20) (Figure 4.2).", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "IUDs increase phagocytosis of sperms within the uterus and the Cu ions released suppress sperm motility and the fertilising capacity of sperms. The hormone releasing IUDs, in addition, make the uterus unsuitable for implantation and the cervix hostile to the sperms.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "IUDs are ideal contraceptives for the females who want to delay pregnancy and/or space children. It is one of most widely accepted methods of contraception in India.", "t": "hl"}]','marked','["261120", "261126", "261127", "261128", "261135", "261140"]',NULL),
(30003,73,61,'paragraph',NULL,'The size of the image relative to the size of the object is another important quantity to consider. We define linear magnification ( m ) as the ratio of the height of the image ( h ′) to the height of the object ( h ):','[{"s": "The size of the image relative to the size of the object is another important quantity to consider.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "We define linear", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "magnification", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "(", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "m", "t": "hl"}, {"s": ") as the ratio of the height of the image (", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "h", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "′) to the height of the object (", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "h", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "):", "t": "hl"}]','marked',NULL,NULL),
(2009,20,140,'paragraph',NULL,'(ii) The second complexity is that the primary transcripts contain both the exons and the introns and are non-functional. Hence, it is subjected to a process called splicing where the introns are removed and exons are joined in a defined order. hnRNA undergoes additional processing called as capping and tailing. In capping an unusual nucleotide (methyl guanosine triphosphate) is added to the 5\'-end of hnRNA. In tailing, adenylate residues (200-300) are added at 3\'-end in a template independent manner. It is the fully processed hnRNA, now called mRNA, that is transported out of the nucleus for translation (Figure 6.11).','[{"s": "(ii) The second complexity is that the primary transcripts contain both the exons and the introns and are non-functional.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Hence, it is subjected to a process called", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "splicing", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "where the introns are removed and exons are joined in a defined order.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "hnRNA undergoes additional processing called as capping and tailing. In", "t": "text"}, {"s": "capping", "t": "text"}, {"s": "an unusual nucleotide (methyl guanosine triphosphate) is added to the 5\'-end of hnRNA. In tailing, adenylate residues (200-300) are added at 3\'-end in a template independent manner.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "It is the fully processed hnRNA, now called mRNA, that is transported out of the nucleus for translation (Figure 6.11).", "t": "hl"}]','marked',NULL,NULL),
