(3344,29,25,'paragraph',NULL,'The fructose 1, 6-bisphosphate is split into dihydroxyacetone phosphate and 3-phosphoglyceraldehyde (PGAL). We find that there is one step where NADH + H­­ + is formed from NAD­­ + ; this is when 3-phosphoglyceraldehyde (PGAL) is converted to 1, 3-bisphosphoglycerate (BPGA). Two redox-equivalents are removed (in the form of two hydrogen atoms) from PGAL and transferred to a molecule of NAD­­ + . PGAL is oxidised and with inorganic phosphate to get converted into BPGA. The conversion of BPGA to 3-phosphoglyceric acid (PGA), is also an energy yielding process; this energy is trapped by the formation of ATP. Another ATP is synthesised during the conversion of PEP to pyruvic acid.','[{"s": "The fructose 1, 6-bisphosphate is split into dihydroxyacetone phosphate and 3-phosphoglyceraldehyde (PGAL).", "t": "text"}, {"s": "We find that there is one step where NADH + H­­", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "+", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "is formed from NAD­­", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "+", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "; this is when 3-phosphoglyceraldehyde (PGAL) is converted to 1, 3-bisphosphoglycerate (BPGA). Two redox-equivalents are removed (in the form of two hydrogen atoms) from PGAL and transferred to a molecule of NAD­­", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "+", "t": "hl"}, {"s": ".", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "PGAL is oxidised and with inorganic phosphate to get converted into BPGA. The conversion of BPGA to 3-phosphoglyceric acid (PGA), is also an energy yielding process; this energy is trapped by the formation of ATP. Another ATP is synthesised during the conversion of PEP to pyruvic acid.", "t": "text"}]','marked',NULL,NULL),
(22879,58,135,'paragraph',NULL,'where m is the mass of the particle and v its speed. Equation (11.5) is known as the de Broglie relation and the wavelength λ of the matter wave is called de Broglie wavelength . The dual aspect of matter is evident in the de Broglie relation. On the left hand side of Eq. (11.5), λ is the attribute of a wave while on the right hand side the momentum p is a typical attribute of a particle. Planck’s constant h relates the two attributes.','[{"s": "where", "t": "text"}, {"s": "m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is the mass of the particle and", "t": "text"}, {"s": "v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "its speed. Equation (11.5) is known as the", "t": "text"}, {"s": "de Broglie relation", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and the wavelength λ of the", "t": "text"}, {"s": "matter wave", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is called", "t": "text"}, {"s": "de Broglie wavelength", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}, {"s": "The dual aspect of matter is evident in the de Broglie relation.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "On the left hand side of Eq. (11.5), λ is the attribute of a wave while on the right hand side the momentum", "t": "text"}, {"s": "p", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is a typical attribute of a particle. Planck’s constant", "t": "text"}, {"s": "h", "t": "text"}, {"s": "relates the two attributes.", "t": "text"}]','marked',NULL,NULL),
(3725,32,49,'paragraph',NULL,'Taxonomic studies consider a group of individual organisms with fundamental similarities as a species. One should be able to distinguish one species from the other closely related species based on the distinct morphological differences. Let us consider Mangifera indica, Solanum tuberosum (potato) and Panthera leo (lion). All the three names, indica, tuberosum and leo, represent the specific epithets, while the first words Mangifera, Solanum and Panthera are genera and represents another higher level of taxon or category. Each genus may have one or more than one specific epithets representing different organisms, but having morphological similarities. For example, Panthera has another specific epithet called tigris and Solanum includes species like nigrum and melongena. Human beings belong to the species sapiens which is grouped in the genus Homo. The scientific name thus, for human being, is written as Homo sapiens.','[{"s": "Taxonomic studies consider a group of individual organisms with fundamental similarities as a species.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "One should be able to distinguish one species from the other closely related species based on the distinct morphological differences. Let us consider Mangifera indica, Solanum tuberosum (potato) and Panthera leo (lion). All the three names, indica, tuberosum and leo, represent the specific epithets, while the first words Mangifera, Solanum and Panthera are genera and represents another higher level of taxon or category. Each genus may have one or more than one specific epithets representing different organisms, but having morphological similarities.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "For example, Panthera has another specific epithet called tigris and Solanum includes species like nigrum and melongena.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "Human beings belong to the species sapiens which is grouped in the genus Homo. The scientific name thus, for human being, is written as Homo sapiens.", "t": "text"}]','marked','["10526"]',NULL),
