(30463,73,521,'paragraph',NULL,'9.16: A small pin fixed on a tabletop is viewed from above from a distance of 50 cm. By what distance would the pin appear to be raised if it is viewed from the same point through a 15 cm thick glass slab held parallel to the table? Refractive index of glass. Does the answer depend on the location of the slab?','[{"s": "9.16: A small pin fixed on a tabletop is viewed from above from a distance of 50 cm.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "By what distance would the pin appear to be raised if it is viewed from the same point through a 15 cm thick glass slab held parallel to the table? Refractive index of glass. Does the answer depend on the location of the slab?", "t": "text"}]','marked',NULL,NULL),
(2829,25,82,'paragraph',NULL,'Auxins (from Greek ‘auxein’ : to grow) was first isolated from human urine. The term ‘auxin’ is applied to the indole-3-acetic acid (IAA), and to other natural and synthetic compounds having certain growth regulating properties. They are generally produced by the growing apices of the stems and roots, from where they migrate to the regions of their action. Auxins like IAA and indole butyric acid (IBA) have been isolated from plants. NAA (naphthalene acetic acid) and 2, 4-D (2, 4-dichlorophenoxyacetic) are synthetic auxins. All these auxins have been used extensively in agricultural and horticultural practices.','[{"s": "Auxins (from Greek ‘auxein’ : to grow) was first isolated from human urine.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "The term ‘auxin’ is applied to the indole-3-acetic acid (IAA), and to other natural and synthetic compounds having certain growth regulating properties.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "They are generally produced by the growing apices of the stems and roots, from where they migrate to the regions of their action.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "Auxins like IAA and indole butyric acid (IBA) have been isolated from plants.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "NAA (naphthalene acetic acid) and 2, 4-D (2, 4-dichlorophenoxyacetic) are synthetic auxins. All these auxins have been used extensively in agricultural and horticultural practices.", "t": "hl"}]','marked','["151808", "151815"]',NULL),
(1712,17,74,'paragraph',NULL,'The mammary glands of the female undergo differentiation during pregnancy and starts producing milk towards the end of pregnancy by the process called lactation . This helps the mother in feeding the new-born . The milk produced during the initial few days of lactation is called colostrum which contains several antibodies absolutely essential to develop resistance for the new-born babies. Breast-feeding during the initial period of infant growth is recommended by doctors for bringing up a healthy baby.','[{"s": "The mammary glands of the female undergo differentiation during pregnancy and starts producing milk towards the end of pregnancy by the process called", "t": "text"}, {"s": "lactation", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". This helps the mother in feeding the new-born", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "The milk produced during the initial few days of lactation is called", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "colostrum", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "which contains several antibodies absolutely essential to develop resistance for the new-born babies. Breast-feeding during the initial period of infant growth is recommended by doctors for bringing up a healthy baby.", "t": "hl"}]','marked',NULL,NULL),
