(1896,20,27,'paragraph',NULL,'(iv) The two chains are coiled in a right-handed fashion. The pitch of the helix is 3.4 nm (a nanometre is one billionth of a metre, that is 10 -9 m) and there are roughly 10 bp in each turn. Consequently, the distance between a bp in a helix is approximately 0.34 nm.','[{"s": "(iv) The two chains are coiled in a right-handed fashion.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "The pitch of the helix is 3.4 nm (a nanometre is one billionth of a metre, that is 10", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "-9", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "m) and there are roughly 10 bp in each turn. Consequently, the distance between a bp in a helix is approximately 0.34 nm.", "t": "hl"}]','marked',NULL,NULL),
