(22394,57,278,'paragraph',NULL,'Example 3.5 A network of resistors is connected to a 16 V battery with internal resistance of 1Ω, as shown in Fig. 3.19: (a) Compute the equivalent resistance of the network. (b) Obtain the current in each resistor. (c) Obtain the voltage drops V AB , V BC and V CD .','[{"s": "Example 3.5", "t": "text"}, {"s": "A network of resistors is connected to a 16 V battery with internal resistance of 1Ω, as shown", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "in Fig.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3.19: (a) Compute the equivalent resistance of the network. (b) Obtain the current in each resistor. (c) Obtain the voltage drops V", "t": "text"}, {"s": "AB", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", V", "t": "text"}, {"s": "BC", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and V", "t": "text"}, {"s": "CD", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}]','marked','["2000041646", "2000042826"]',NULL),
(22449,57,333,'paragraph',NULL,'Next, consider a parallel combination of the cells (Fig . 3.21). I 1 and I 2 are the currents leaving the positive electrodes of the cells. At the point B 1 , I 1 and I 2 flow in whereas the current I flows out. Since as much charge flows in as out, we have','[{"s": "Next, consider a parallel combination of the cells", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "(Fig", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3.21). I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "are the currents leaving the positive electrodes of the cells. At the point B", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "flow in whereas the current I flows out. Since as much charge flows in as out, we have", "t": "text"}]','marked','["2000041654", "2000042896"]',NULL),
