(23547,59,369,'paragraph',NULL,'The quantity M12 is called mutual inductance of coil 1 with respect to coil 2. One can similarly define M21. There exists a general equality,','[{"s": "The quantity M12 is called mutual inductance of coil 1 with respect to coil 2.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "One can similarly define M21. There exists a general equality,", "t": "text"}]','marked','["2000043502", "2000112275", "2000112360"]',NULL),
(22481,57,365,'paragraph',NULL,'Figure 3.22 At junction a the current leaving is I 1 + I 2 and current entering is I 3 . The junction rule says I 3 = I 1 + I 2 . At point h current entering is I 1 . There is only one current leaving h and by junction rule that will also be I 1 . For the loops ‘ahdcba’ and ‘ahdefga’, the loop rules give –30I 1 – 41 I 3 + 45 = 0 and –30I 1 + 21 I 2 – 80 = 0.','[{"s": "Figure 3.22 At junction a the current leaving is I", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "1", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "+ I", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "2", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "and current entering is I", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "3", "t": "hl"}, {"s": ".", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "The junction rule says I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+ I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". At point h current entering is I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". There is only one current leaving h and by junction rule that will also be I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". For the loops ‘ahdcba’ and ‘ahdefga’, the loop rules give –30I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "– 41 I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+ 45 = 0 and –30I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+ 21 I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "– 80 = 0.", "t": "text"}]','marked','["2000041677", "2000042928"]',NULL),
(22484,57,368,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) Loop rule: The algebraic sum of changes in potential around any closed loop involving resistors and cells in the loop is zero (Fig. 3.22).','[{"s": "(b) Loop rule: The algebraic sum of changes in potential around any closed loop involving resistors and cells in the loop is zero (Fig. 3.22).", "t": "hl"}]','marked','["2000041702", "2000043854"]',NULL),
