(22558,57,442,'paragraph',NULL,'Example 3.9 In a meter bridge (Fig . 3.27), the null point is found at a distance of 33.7 cm from A. If now a resistance of 12Ω is connected in parallel with S, the null point occurs at 51.9 cm. Determine the values of R and S.','[{"s": "Example 3.9", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "In a meter bridge (Fig", "t": "hl"}, {"s": ".", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "3.27), the null point is found at a distance of 33.7 cm from A. If now a resistance of 12Ω is connected in parallel with S, the null point occurs at 51.9 cm. Determine the values of R and S.", "t": "text"}]','marked','["2000041738", "2000043941"]',NULL),
(22569,57,453,'paragraph',NULL,'A current I flows through the wire which can be varied by a variable resistance (rheostat, R) in the circuit. Since the wire is uniform, the potential difference between A and any point at a distance l from A is','[{"s": "A current I flows through the wire which can be varied by a variable resistance (rheostat, R) in the circuit.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Since the wire is uniform, the potential difference between A and any point at a distance l from A", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "is", "t": "text"}]','marked','["2000041742", "2000043961"]',NULL);
