(23407,59,229,'paragraph',NULL,'In the previous sub-section, we considered the flux in one solenoid due to the current in the other. It is also possible that emf is induced in a single isolated coil due to change of flux through the coil by means of varying the current through the same coil. This phenomenon is called self-induction. In this case, flux linkage through a coil of N turns is proportional to the current through the coil and is expressed as','[{"s": "In the previous sub-section, we considered the flux in one solenoid due to the current in the other. It is also possible that emf is induced in a single isolated coil due to change of flux through the coil by means of varying the current through the same coil. This phenomenon is called self-induction.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "In this case, flux linkage through a coil of N turns is proportional to the current through the coil and is expressed as", "t": "hl"}]','marked','["2000043216", "2000044219", "2000112294"]',NULL),
