(34922,80,355,'paragraph',NULL,'Let us choose the convention to take the direction from the observer to the source as the positive direction of velocity. 1 , located at a distance L from the observer, and emits a crest. This reaches the observer at time t 1 = L/v. At time t = T o the source has moved a distance v s T o and is at point S 2 , located at a distance (L + v s T o ) from the observer. At S 2 , the source emits a second crest. This reaches the observer at','[{"s": "Let us choose the convention to take the direction from the observer to the source as the positive direction of velocity.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "", "t": "br"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", located at a distance L from the observer, and emits a crest. This reaches the observer at time t", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= L/v. At time t = T", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "the source has moved a distance v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "T", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and is at point S", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", located at a distance (L + v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "T", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") from the observer. At S", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", the source emits a second crest. This reaches the observer at", "t": "text"}]','marked','["2000040616", "2000109309"]',NULL),
(34944,80,377,'paragraph',NULL,'The observer thus, measures the period of the wave to be','[{"s": "The observer thus, measures the period of the wave to be", "t": "hl"}]','marked','["2000040620", "2000109308"]',NULL),
(34951,80,384,'paragraph',NULL,'We will now derive a general expression for Doppler shift when both the source and the observer are moving . As before, let us take the direction from the observer to the source as the positive direction. Let the source and the observer be moving with velocities v s and v o respectively as shown in Fig.15.18. Suppose at time t = 0, the observer is at O 1 and the source is at S 1 , O 1 being to the left of S 1 . The source emits a wave of velocity v, of frequency v and period T 0 all measured by an observer at rest with respect to the medium. Let L be the distance between O 1 and S 1 at t = 0, when the source emits the first crest. Now, since the observer is moving, the velocity of the wave relative to the observer is v+v 0 . Therefore, the first crest reaches the observer at time t 1 = L/(v+v o ). At time t = T 0 , both the observer and the source have moved to their new positions O 2 and S 2 respectively. The new distance between the observer and the source, O 2 S 2 , would be L+(v s –v o ) T 0 ]. At S 2 , the source emits a second crest.','[{"s": "We will now derive a general expression for Doppler shift when both the source and the observer are moving", "t": "hl"}, {"s": ".", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "As before, let us take the direction from the observer to the source as the positive direction. Let the source and the observer be moving with velocities v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "respectively as shown in Fig.15.18. Suppose at time t = 0, the observer is at O", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and the source is at S", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", O", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "being to the left of S", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". The source emits a wave of velocity v, of frequency v and period T", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": "all measured by an observer at rest with respect to the medium. Let L be the distance between O", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and S", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "at t = 0, when the source emits the first crest. Now, since the observer is moving, the velocity of the wave relative to the observer is v+v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". Therefore, the first crest reaches the observer at time t", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= L/(v+v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": "). At time t = T", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", both the observer and the source have moved to their new positions O", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and S", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "respectively. The new distance between the observer and the source, O", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "S", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", would be L+(v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–v", "t": "text"}, {"s": "o", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") T", "t": "text"}, {"s": "0", "t": "text"}, {"s": "]. At S", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", the source emits a second crest.", "t": "text"}]','marked','["2000040624", "2000109317"]',NULL),
