(200307,'chemistry','Which of the following factors is of no significance for roasting sulphide ores to the oxides and not subjecting the sulphide ores to carbon reduction directly?','CO₂ is more volatile than CS₂','The reduction process depends on the thermodynamic stability of the product and not on their volatility.  (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 156 paragraph 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'2','mcq','CO₂ is more volatile than CS₂','Metal sulphides are thermodynamically more stable than CS₂','CO₂ is thermodynamically more stable than CS₂','Metal sulphides are less stable than the corresponding oxides','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200308,'chemistry','Which of the following statement is correct?','Sphalerite is the ore of Zinc','Sphalerite is an important ore of zinc; around 95% of all primary zinc is extracted from sphalerite ore.  (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 page 152 table 6.1 ).','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'2','mcq','Roasting is extraction because there is no sulphide ore:','In the smelting steps of copper extraction , reduction of the ore take place.','Ores may not be mineral','Sphalerite is the ore of Zinc','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200309,'biology','Skeletal muscles are called striated muscles because they-','Have a striped appearance under the microscope','Skeletal muscles are closely associated with the skeletal components of the body. They have a striped appearance under the microscope and hence are called striated muscles..(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 303;paragraph No.5)','Human Physiology >> Locomotion and Movement >> Muscle 1','Locomotion and Movement','1','mcq','Have a striped appearance under naked eye.','Have a smooth appearance under the microscope','Have a striped appearance under the microscope','Have a rough appearance under the microscope','NEW','11-303','11-218',NULL),
(200310,'chemistry','Fe₂O₃.xH₂O(s) →  Fe₂O₃(s) + xH₂O(g) (heat) This reaction is a type of?','Calcination','Calcination involves heating. It removes the volatile matter which escapes leaving behind the metal oxide. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 155 paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'1','mcq','Roasting','Liquation','Calcination','Digestion','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200311,'chemistry','What\'s the ideal temperature in Roasting used?','Below the melting point','In roasting, the ore is heated in a regular supply of air in a furnace at a temperature below the melting point of the metal. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 155 paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'2','mcq','Above the boiling point','Below the boiling point','Above the melting point','Below the melting point','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200312,'chemistry','Which gas is primarily released in Calcination?','CO₂','ZnCO₃ (s) →  ZnO(s) + CO₂(g) This is the reaction of calcination. Carbon dioxide is released. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 155 paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'1','mcq','SO₂','O₂','CO₂','H₂','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200313,'chemistry','Which gas is primarily released in roasting ?','SO₂','2ZnS + 3O₂ → 2ZnO + 2SO₂ . This is the reaction of roasting . Sulphur dioxide is released. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 156 paragraph 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'1','mcq','CO₂','O₂','H₂','SO₂','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200314,'biology','Visceral muscles are also called-','Non-striated muscles','Visceral muscles are located in the inner walls of hollow visceral organs of the body like the alimentary canal, reproductive tract, etc. They do not\nexhibit any striation and are smooth in appearance. Hence, they are called smooth muscles (nonstriated muscle). ..(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 303;paragraph No.6)','Human Physiology >> Locomotion and Movement >> Muscle 1','Locomotion and Movement','1','mcq','Striated muscles','Non-striated muscles','Skeletal muscles','Cardiac muscles','NEW','11-303','11-218',NULL),
(200315,'chemistry','2PbS + 3O₂ →  A + SO₂ . The name of A is :','Litharge','PbO is commonly known as Litharge. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 156 paragraph 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'1','mcq','Galena','Litharge','Sesquioxide','None of the above','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200316,'chemistry','Partial roasting of Chalcopyrite produces:','Cu₂S and FeO','During partial roasting, CuFeS₂ is first converted to Cu2S and FeS. Further as iron is more reactive than copper FeS is preferentially oxidized to FeO. CuFeS2 + O₂ → Cu2S + 2FeS + SO₂ (heat) , 2FeS + O₂ → Cu2S + 2FeS + SO₂ (heat). (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 156 paragraph 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'3','mcq','Cu₂S and FeO','Cu₂O and FeO','Cu²O and Fe₂O₃','CuS and Fe₂O₃','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200317,'chemistry','Iron is removed from Chalcopyrite (ore of copper) as:','FeSiO₃','Iron oxide ‘slags of’ as iron silicate . FeO + SiO₂ → FeSiO₃ (slag) .  (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 156 paragraph 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'1','mcq','FeO','FeS','Fe₂O₃','FeSiO₃','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
