(200321,'chemistry','How is SO₂ used , which is produced in Roasting?','Production of H₂SO₄','The SO₂ produced is utilised for manufacturing H₂SO₄ . (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 156 paragraph 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'2','mcq','Production of H₂S','Production of H₂SO₄','Production of SF₃','production of SOCl₂','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200526,'chemistry','What impurities found in pig iron?','Mn','The iron obtained from Blast furnace contains about 4% carbon and many impurities in smaller amount (e.g., S, P, Si, Mn). This is known as pig iron. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 161 paragraph 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Applications',NULL,'2','mcq','Ca','Mg','Mn','N','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200527,'chemistry','What impurities are found in Wrought iron?','Si','Limestone is added as a flux and sulphur, silicon and phosphorus are oxidised and passed into the slag. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 161 paragraph 3)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Applications',NULL,'2','mcq','Mn','Ca','Mg','Si','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200322,'chemistry','Select the correct statement:\na. The release of SO₂ in roasting process has been a serious air pollution problem.\nb. Roasting removes easily oxidizable volatile impurities like arsenic as As₂O₃ and antimony as Sb₂O₃ and Sulphur as SO₂\nc. In roasting process If temperature is fairly low about 500 degree Celsius and the concentration of SO₂ in the gaseous environment is more .sulphate may be produced and tighter stable and high temperature is needed to decompose it.','All of them','The release of SO₂ in roasting process has been a serious air pollution problem. Roasting removes easily oxidizable volatile impurities like arsenic as As₂O₃ and antimony as Sb₂O₃ and Sulphur as SO₂. In roasting process If temperature is fairly low about 500 degree Celsius and the concentration of SO₂ in the gaseous environment is more sulphate may be produced and tighter stable and high temperature is needed to decompose it. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 155 paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'3','mcq','Only a and b','Only a and c','Only b and c','All of them','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200323,'chemistry','Cinnabar(HgS) and Galena(PbS) on roasting often gives their respective metals , but Zinc blend(ZnS) does not , give reason:','Because ZnO is highly stable','On roasting all the sulfide ores are converted into the respective oxides since the oxides of Mercury and lead are unstable while that of zinc is stable . Oxides of Mercury and lead bring about reduction in of their respective sulphides to the corresponding metals but zinc oxide does not reduce ZnS to Zn.  (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 156 paragraph 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'2','mcq','Because Zn is highly unstable','Because ZnO is highly stable','Because Zn is highly unstable','None of the above','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200324,'chemistry','Which of the following metal oxides is/are not reduced by self reduction method?','CaO','These metals are the examples of self reducing metals. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 159 paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'3','mcq','Cu₂O','PbO','HgO','CaO','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200325,'chemistry','Disadvantages of using carbon as a reducing agent are:','High temperature is needed,many metals combine with carbon to form carbides','Disadvantages of using carbon as a reducing agent are; high temperature is needed and many metals combine with carbon to form carbides. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 156 paragraph 3)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'2','mcq','High temperature is needed,many metals combine with carbon to form carbides','Low temperature is needed,many metals combine with carbon and do not form carbides','Many metals combine with carbon and do not form carbides','None of the Above','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200326,'chemistry','In iron extraction the roasting is carried out as:','All the FeO converted to Fe₂O₃','After concentration, mixture of oxide ores of iron (Fe₂O₃, Fe₃O₄) is subjected to calcination/roasting to remove water, to decompose carbonates and to oxidise sulphides. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 159 paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'3','mcq','All the FeO converted to Fe₂O₃','The formation of slag is prevented','Fe₂O₃ does not react with SiO₂ fo form slag','The formation of slag is enhanced','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200327,'chemistry','In the commercial extraction of iron roasting is adopted as:','it removes impurities of sulphur arsenic etc in the form of the elemental vapours','In the commercial extraction of iron roasting is adopted because it removes impurities of sulphur arsenic etc in the form of the elemental vapours. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 156 paragraph 3)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'3','mcq','It removes impurities of sulphur arsenic etc in the form of the elemental vapours','It prevents slag formation by Fe₂O₃','It prevents slag formation by FeO oxidisable volatile impurities are removed by calcination process','Limonite is converter into it anhydrous form only calcination occurs for carbonate Ore oxide ore','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200328,'chemistry','Select the correct statements for calcination:','Carbonate ore is converted into its oxide ore','Calcination involves heating. It removes the volatile matter which escapes leaving behind the metal oxide. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 155 paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'3','mcq','Carbonate ore is converted into its oxide ore','Hydrated oxide ore is converted into its oxide ore','Oxidisable volatile impurities are removed by calcination process','Only calcination occurs for carbonate or oxide ores','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200329,'chemistry','Impurities collectively associated with the ore after mining are called?','Gangue','During metallurgy, ‘flux’ is added which combines with ‘gangue’ to form ‘slag’. Slag separates more easily from the ore than the gangue. This way, removal of gangue becomes easier. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 155 Footnote )','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'1','mcq','Flux','Slag','Minerals','Gangue','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200330,'chemistry','Heating of ore in the presence of air to remove impurity of sulphur is called as?','Roasting','S is oxidized to SO₂. This is the process of roasting. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 155 paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'1','mcq','Calcination','Roasting','Smelting','Sintering','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200331,'chemistry','By which process Lead and Tin are extracted, respectively:','Self reduction , carbon reduction','PbS + 2PbO → 3Pb + SO₂ (self reduction) SnO + C → Sn + CO ( carbon reduction). (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 156 paragraph 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'3','mcq','Electrolytic reduction , self reduction','Self reduction , carbon reduction','Electrolytic reduction , cyanide process','Cyanide process , electrolytic reduction','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200332,'chemistry','In the reverberatory furnace:','Only hot gases come in contact with the charge','The sulphide ores of copper are heated in reverberatory furnace. If the ore contains iron, it is mixed with silica before heating. As shown in diagram (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 155 Paragraph 2 )\ndiagram(e0602)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'3','mcq','The flames are in contact with the charge','The flames do not come in contact with the charge','Only hot gases come in contact with the charge','The flames are not at all there','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200333,'chemistry','During smelting an additional substance is added which combines with impurities to form a fusible mass the additional substances called as?','Flux','Limestone is also decomposes to CaO which removes silicate impurity of the ore as slag. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 156 paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'1','mcq','Slag','Ore','Flux','Gangue','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200334,'chemistry','Reduction can be done by:','CO','Reduction of the metal oxide usually involves heating it with a reducing agent, for example C, or CO or even another metal.(Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 156 paragraph 3)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'1','mcq','CO₂','CN','CH₄','CO','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/match/200334q.png'),
(200335,'chemistry','To extract metal from concentrated ore, it must be converted to a form which is suitable for _________ to metal.','Reduction','To extract metal from concentrated ore, it must be converted to a form which is suitable for reduction to metal. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 155 Paragraph 3 )','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'1','mcq','Oxidation','Reduction','Non-metal','Metalloids','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200336,'chemistry','Choose the incorrect statement:\na. Sulphide ores are converted to oxide before reduction because oxides are easier to reduce.\nb. Isolation of metals from concentrated ore involves three major steps.\nc. To extract metal from concentrated ore, it must be converted to a form which is suitable for reduction to metal.','Only b','To extract metal from concentrated ore, it must be converted to a form which is suitable for reduction to metal. Usually sulphide ores are converted to oxide before reduction because oxides are easier to reduce. Thus isolation of metals from concentrated ore involves two major steps viz., (a) conversion to oxide, and (b) reduction of the oxide to metal. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 155 Paragraph 3 )','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'1','mcq','Only a','Only b','Only b and c','Only a and c','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200337,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion(A) and reason(R):\nAssertion: Calcination removes the volatile matter which escapes leaving behind the metal oxide.\nReason: The ore is heated in a regular supply of air in a furnace at a temperature below the melting point of the metal in a roasting.','Both assertion and reason are true but reason is not a correct explanation of assertion','Calcination removes the volatile matter which escapes leaving behind the metal oxide. In roasting, the ore is heated in a regular supply of air in a furnace at a temperature below the melting point of the metal. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 155 paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'3','mcq','Both assertion and reason are true and reason is a correct explanation of assertion','Both assertion and reason are true but reason is not a correct explanation of assertion','Assertion is true but the reason is false','Both assertion and reason are false','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200338,'chemistry','Choose the incorrect statement:\na. Calcination and roasting involves heating.\nb. If the ore contains iron, it is mixed with silica before heating. \nc. The sulphide ores of copper are heated in blast furnace.','Only c','Calcination involves heating.Calcination removes the volatile matter which escapes leaving behind the metal oxide. In roasting, the ore is heated in a regular supply of air in a furnace at a temperature below the melting point of the metal.The sulphide ores of copper are heated in reverberatory furnace. If the ore contains iron, it is mixed with silica before heating. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 155 Paragraph 3 )','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'1','mcq','Only a','Only a and b','Only c','Only b and c','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200339,'chemistry','Choose the correct statement:\na. Reduction of the metal oxide usually involves heating it with a oxidizing agent.\nb. The reducing agent combines with the oxygen of the metal oxide.\nc. Some metal oxides get reduced easily while others are very difficult to be reduced. In any case, heating is required.','Only b and c','Reduction of the metal oxide usually involves heating it with a reducing agent, for example C, or CO or even another metal. The reducing agent (e.g., carbon) combines with the oxygen of the metal oxide. Some metal oxides get reduced easily while others are very difficult to be reduced (reduction means electron gain by the metal ion). In any case, heating is required. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 155 Paragraph 3 )','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'1','mcq','Only a','Only a and b','Only c','Only b and c','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200340,'chemistry','Choose the correct equation according to the given statement: "The reducing agent combines with the oxygen of the metal oxide."','MxOy + yC → xM + y CO','The reducing agent (e.g., carbon) combines with the oxygen of the metal oxide. MxOy + yC → xM + y CO  (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 155 Paragraph 3 )','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Extraction of crude metals from concentrated ore',NULL,'3','mcq','MxOy + yC → xM + y CO','MxCy + yO →  xM + y CO','CxOy + yM →  xC + y MO','MxOy + yC →  xC + y MO','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200341,'biology','________ in the ‘A’ band are held together by a thin fibrous membrane called the M line.','Thick filaments','The thick filaments in the ‘A’ band are also held together in the middle of this band by a thin fibrous membrane called ‘M’ line..(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 305;paragraph No.1)','Human Physiology >> Locomotion and Movement >> Muscle 2','Locomotion and Movement','1','mcq','Thin filaments','Thick filaments','Both','None','NEW','11-305','11-220',NULL),
(200342,'biology','The functional unit of contraction is called____________','Sarcomere','The portion of the myofibril between two successive ‘Z’ lines is considered as the functional unit of contraction and is called a sarcomere.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 305;paragraph No.1).','Human Physiology >> Locomotion and Movement >> Muscle 2','Locomotion and Movement','1','mcq','Sarcomere','Sarcolemma','M line','None','NEW','11-305','11-220',NULL),
(200343,'biology','The central part of thick filament, not overlapped by thin filaments is called the_________','H zone','This central part of thick filament, not overlapped by thin filaments is called the ‘H’ zone.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 305;paragraph No.1).','Human Physiology >> Locomotion and Movement >> Muscle 2','Locomotion and Movement','1','mcq','N zone','L zone','H zone','P zone','NEW','11-305','11-220',NULL),
