(200512,'chemistry','At what temperature ranges, Iron oxides converted to Fe ?','900 K to 1500 K','At 900 – 1500 K (higher temperature range in the blast furnace) C + CO₂ → 2CO   ...  FeO + CO → Fe + CO₂ (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 160 paragraph 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Applications',NULL,'3','mcq','500 K to 800 K','1500 K to 2100 K','900 K to 1500 K','2100 K','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
