(200514,'chemistry','What\'s the role of adding limestone along with the ore in the blast furnace?','Help removing impurities','Limestone is also decomposes to CaO which removes silicate impurity of the ore as slag. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 160 paragraph 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Applications',NULL,'2','mcq','Helps in further increasing the temperature','Help removing impurities','Help in reducing Iron','None of these','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200515,'chemistry','Coke is added during smelting to:','Check the oxidation of FeO to Fe₂O₃','In upper part, the temperature is lower and the iron oxides (Fe2O3 and Fe3O4) coming from the top are reduced in steps to FeO. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 160 paragraph 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Applications',NULL,'1','mcq','Reduce FeO to Fe','Reduce Cu₂O to Cu','Check the oxidation of FeO to Fe₂O₃','Check the oxidation of Cu₂O to CuO','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200516,'chemistry','Which of the following statements are correct regarding metallurgy of iron?','Coke reduces FeO to Fe above 1073 k ,CO reduces Fe₂O₃ to FeO below 1073 K','Thermodynamics helps us to understand how coke reduces the oxide and why this furnace is chosen. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 160 paragraph 3)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Applications',NULL,'3','mcq','Coke reduces FeO to Fe above 1073 k','CO reduces Fe₂O₃ to FeO below 1073 K','Coke reduces FeO to Fe above 1073 k ,CO reduces Fe₂O₃ to FeO below 1073 K','Coke reduces Fe₂O₃ to FeO above 1073 K','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200517,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding following Assertion and Reason:\nAssertion : Reduction of Fe₂O₃ with CO is done below 710°c.\nReason : ∆rG is negative at this temperature ; this process is spontaneous .','Both assertion and reason are true and reason is a correct explanation of assertion','In ∆rG vs T plot representing the change Fe→ FeO goes upward and that representing the change C→ CO (C,CO) goes downward. They cross each other at about 1073. At temperatures above 1073K (approx.), the C, CO line is below the Fe, FeO line ∆rG(C,CO)<∆rG(Fe,FeO) .So above 1073 K in the range of temperature 900–1500 K coke will reduce FeO and will itself be oxidised to CO. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 161 paragraph 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Applications',NULL,'3','mcq','Both assertion and reason are true and reason is a correct explanation of assertion','Both assertion and reason are true but reason is not a correct explanation of assertion','Assertion is true but the reason is false','Both assertion and reason are false','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
