(200624,'chemistry','The low grade ore of copper is reduced by :','H₂','Copper is extracted by hydrometallurgy from low grade ores. It is leached out using acid or bacteria. The solution containing Cu²⁺ is treated with scrap iron or H2. (Reference: NCERT  , class 12 , unit 6 , page 163 paragraph 3)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Electrochemical principles of metallurgy',NULL,'1','mcq','C','CO','H₂','O₂','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/200624q.png'),
