(200626,'chemistry','H₂ is not widely used as a reducing agent in metallurgical process because:','Many metals react with hydrogen at elevated temperature was forming hydrides ,there is a risk of explosion from H₂ and O₂ present in the air , the reducing power of H₂ does not increase with temperature','H₂ is not widely used as a reducing agent in metallurgical process because many metals react with hydrogen at elevated temperature was forming hydrides ,there is a risk of explosion from H₂ and O₂ present in the air , the reducing power of H₂ does not increase with temperature. (Reference: NCERT  , class 12 , unit 6 , page 163 paragraph 3)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Electrochemical principles of metallurgy',NULL,'3','mcq','Many metals react with hydrogen at elevated temperature was forming hydrides ,there is a risk of explosion from H₂ and O₂ present in the air , the reducing power of H₂ does not increase with temperature','There is a risk of explosion from H₂ and O₂ present in the air','The reducing power of H₂ does not increase with temperature','Reducing power of H₂ increases with temperature','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/200626q.png'),
(200627,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding following Assertion and Reason:\nAssertion : Graphite is used as anode but diamond is not. \nReason : There exist free electrons between two parallel sheets of Graphite hence it helps in electrode conduction.','Both assertion and reason are true and reason is a correct explanation of assertion','There exist free electrons between two parallel sheets of Graphite hence it helps in electrode conduction.Graphite is used as anode instead of diamond.  (Reference: NCERT  , class 12 , unit 6 , page 163 paragraph first)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Electrochemical principles of metallurgy',NULL,'3','mcq','Both assertion and reason are true and reason is a correct explanation of assertion','Both assertion and reason are true but reason is not a correct explanation of assertion','Assertion is true but the reason is false','Both assertion and reason are false','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/200627q.png'),
(200628,'chemistry','The major role of fluorspar CaF₂ which is added in small quantities in electrolytic reduction of Alumina dissolved in fused cryolite Na3AlF6 is :','To make the used mixture very conducting','The electrolysis of pure Alumina faces some difficulties pure Alumina is a bad conductor of electricity the fusion temperature of pure Alumina is about 2000 degree Celsius at this temperature when electrolysis is carried out on the fused mass of the metal formed vaporizes as the boiling point of Aluminium is 1800 degree Celsius these difficulties are overcome by using a mixture of Alumina cryolite and fluorspar.  (Reference: NCERT  , class 12 , unit 6 , page 163 paragraph first)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Electrochemical principles of metallurgy',NULL,'1','mcq','As a catalyst','To make the used mixture very conducting','To increase the temperature of the melt','To decrease the rate of oxidation of carbon at anode','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/200628q.png'),
(200629,'chemistry','Reduction of oxides to elements with carbon generally takes place at high temperatures hence aluminium is used in alumino thermite process it is because:','Al is more electropositive than the other metals , Al has maximum affinity for oxygen','In the metallurgy of aluminium, purified Al₂O₃ is mixed with Na₃AlF₆ or CaF₂ which lowers the melting point of the mixture and brings conductivity. The fused matrix is electrolysed. Steel vessel with lining of carbon acts as cathode and graphite anode is used. The overall reaction may be written as: 2Al2₂O₃ + 3C  → 4Al + 3CO₂ (Reference: NCERT  , class 12 , unit 6 , page 162 paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Electrochemical principles of metallurgy',NULL,'3','mcq','Al is more electropositive than the other metals , Al has maximum affinity for oxygen','Al has maximum affinity for oxygen','Reduction is highly exothermic and the heat liberated makes the process spontaneous','Reduction is highly endothermic and the heat absorbed makes the process spontaneous','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/match/200629q.png'),
(200630,'chemistry','In the metallurgy of aluminium:','Graphite anode is oxidised to carbon monoxide and carbon dioxide','At anode     2C + O₂ —> 2CO ;  C + O₂ —> CO₂  (Reference: NCERT  , class 12 , unit 6 , page 162 paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Electrochemical principles of metallurgy',NULL,'3','mcq','Al3+ positive is oxidised to Al(s)','Graphite anode is oxidised to carbon monoxide and carbon dioxide','Oxidation state of oxygen changes in the reaction at anode','Oxidation state of oxygen changes in the overall reaction involved in the process','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/200630q.png'),
