(200646,'biology','Bones and cartilage are','Specialised connective tissue','Bone and cartilage are specialised connective tissues. NCERT Class 11th pg. 309.','Human Physiology >> Locomotion and Movement >> Skeletal system 1','Locomotion and Movement','1','mcq','Simple dense tissue','Specialised tissue','Dense areolar tissue','Specialised connective tissue','NEW','11-309','11-224',NULL),
(200647,'biology','Choose the correct option concerning to the matrix of cartilage','Matrix contain chondroitin salts','The matrix of cartilage is slightly pliable due to the presence of chondroitin salts and the matrix of bone is non-pliable due to calcium salts. (Reference: class 11 NCERT page 309, para 1)','Human Physiology >> Locomotion and Movement >> Skeletal system 1','Locomotion and Movement','1','mcq','Matrix is non-pliable','Matrix contain chondroitin salts','Matrix is slightly pliable due to calcium salts','Both B and C','NEW','11-309','11-224',NULL),
(200648,'biology','Choose the false statement','Axial skeleton of a human body contains 26 bones','Axial skeleton do not have 206 bones. Axial skeleton of human body has 80 bones constituted by ribs, sternum, vertebrae and skull. all other statements are true. (Reference: class 11 NCERT page 309, para 1)','Human Physiology >> Locomotion and Movement >> Skeletal system 1','Locomotion and Movement','1','mcq','Axial skeleton of a human body contains 26 bones','Hyoid is a U-shaped bone.','Ribs are bicephalic','Vertebrochondral ribs are false ribs','NEW','11-309','11-224',NULL),
(200649,'biology','Human skull is','Dicondylic','The skull region articulates with the superior region of the vertebral column with the help of two occipital condyles (dicondylic skull).  NCERT Class 11th pg. 309 and 310.','Human Physiology >> Locomotion and Movement >> Skeletal system 1','Locomotion and Movement','1','mcq','Monocondylic','Dicondylic','Tricondylic','non-condylic','NEW','11-309','11-224',NULL),
(200650,'biology','Parts of scapula includes','Spine, Acromion and cavity','Scapula is a large triangular flat bone situated in the dorsal part of the thorax between the second and the seventh ribs. The dorsal, flat, triangular body of scapula has a slightly elevated ridge called the spine which projects as a flat, expanded process called the acromion.  NCERT Class 11th pg. 311','Human Physiology >> Locomotion and Movement >> Skeletal system 1','Locomotion and Movement','1','mcq','Acromion only','Cavity and Atlas','Atlas only','Spine, Acromion and cavity','NEW','11-311','11-226',NULL),
(200651,'biology','Assertion: The 8th, 9th and 10th pairs of ribs are called false ribs. \nReason: They are not connected ventrally.','Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.','The 8th, 9th and 10th pairs of ribs do not articulate directly with the sternum but join the seventh rib with the help of hyaline cartilage. These are called vertebrochondral (false) ribs. Last 2 pairs (11th and 12th) of ribs are not connected ventrally and are therefore, called floating ribs. NCERT class 11th, pg 310','Human Physiology >> Locomotion and Movement >> Skeletal system 1','Locomotion and Movement','1','mcq','Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.','Assertion and Reason are correct, but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.','Assertion and Reason are incorrect.','NEW','11-311','11-226',NULL),
(200652,'biology','The clavicle articulates with','Acromion of scapula','The dorsal, flat, triangular body of scapula has a slightly elevated ridge called the spine which projects as a flat, expanded process called the acromion. The clavicle articulates with this. NCERT class 11th, pg 311','Human Physiology >> Locomotion and Movement >> Skeletal system 1','Locomotion and Movement','1','mcq','Spine of scapula','Acromion of scapula','Cavity of scapula','Head of scapula','NEW','11-311','11-226',NULL),
(200653,'biology','Choose the correct option about pelvic girdle','Acetabulum is formed at the point of fusion of 3 bones','Pelvic girdle consists of two coxal bones. Each coxal bone is formed by the fusion of three bones – ilium, ischium and pubis. At the point of fusion of the above bones is a cavity called acetabulum to which the thigh bone articulates. The two halves of the pelvic girdle meet ventrally to form the pubic symphysis containing fibrous cartilage. (Reference: NCERT class 11th, pg 311 para 2)','Human Physiology >> Locomotion and Movement >> Skeletal system 1','Locomotion and Movement','2','mcq','Pelvic girdle is formed of three coaxal bones-ilium, ischium, pubis','Halves of pelvic girdle meet dorsally to form symphysis','Pubic symphysis contains collagenous cartilage','Acetabulum is formed at the point of fusion of 3 bones','NEW','11-311','11-226',NULL),
(200654,'biology','The number of cervical vertebrae are seven in almost all mammals.','TRUE','The number of cervical vertebrae are seven in almost all mammals including human beings.  (Reference: NCERT class 11th, pg 310 para 2)','Human Physiology >> Locomotion and Movement >> Skeletal system 1','Locomotion and Movement','1','mcq','TRUE','FALSE',NULL,NULL,'NEW','11-310','11-225',NULL),
(200655,'biology','Which of the following is not the function of the vertebral column?','Protect the heart','protecting the heart is the function of ribcage (Reference: NCERT class 11th, pg 310 para 2)','Human Physiology >> Locomotion and Movement >> Skeletal system 1','Locomotion and Movement','1','mcq','Protects the spinal cord','Supports the head','Serves as points of attachment for the ribs and musculature of the back','Protect the heart','NEW','11-310','11-225',NULL),
(200656,'biology','Public symphysis contains','Fibrous cartilage','Public symphysis contains Fibrous cartilage (Reference: NCERT class 11th, pg 311 para 2)','Human Physiology >> Locomotion and Movement >> Skeletal system 1','Locomotion and Movement','1','mcq','Calcium','Elastic cartilage','Fibrous cartilage','Muscle','NEW','11-311','11-226',NULL),
(200701,'chemistry','The extraction of gold and silver involves leaching of the metals present in the core with:','CN','Extraction of gold and silver involves leaching the metal with CN–. This is also an oxidation reaction (Ag → Ag+ or Au → Au+).The metal is later recovered by displacement method. (Reference: NCERT  , class 12 , unit 6 , page 163 paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Oxidation reduction',NULL,'1','mcq','C','O₂','CN','H₂','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200702,'chemistry','Oxidation reduction method is generally employed for :','Both of the above','The oxidation-reduction or redox reactions involve the transfer of electrons between an electron donor (that becomes oxidized) and an electron acceptor is generally employed for metals and non metals. (Reference: NCERT  , class 12 , unit 6 , page 163 paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Oxidation reduction',NULL,'2','mcq','Metals','Non metals','Both of the above','None of the above','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200703,'chemistry','In the extraction of chlorine by electrolysis of Brine :','Oxidation of Cl ion to chlorine gas occurs','In the extraction of chlorine by electrolysis of brine, oxidation of Cl− ion to chlorine gas occurs. (Reference: NCERT  , class 12 , unit 6 , page 163 paragraph last).','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Oxidation reduction',NULL,'3','mcq','Oxidation of Cl ion to chlorine gas occurs','The reduction of Cl ion to chlorine gas occurs','For overall reaction ∆G has negative value','A displacement reaction takes place','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/match/200703q.png'),
(200704,'chemistry','In the extraction of chlorine from Brine :','∆G for the overall reaction is positive ,E for overall reaction has negative value','∆G is positive , E is negative. The ∆G for this reaction is + 422 kJ. When it is converted to E(using ∆G= – nE0F), we get E0= – 2.2 V.  (Reference: NCERT  , class 12 , unit 6 , page 163 paragraph last).','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Oxidation reduction',NULL,'3','mcq','∆G for the overall reaction is negative','∆G for the overall reaction is positive ,E for overall reaction has negative value','E for overall reaction has negative value','E for overall reaction has positive value','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/200704q.png'),
(200705,'chemistry','Which non-metal is extracted from the sea:','Cl','A very common example of extraction based on oxidation is the extraction of chlorine from brine (chlorine is abundant in sea water as common salt) . (Reference: NCERT  , class 12 , unit 6 , page 163 paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Oxidation reduction',NULL,'2','mcq','Cl','Br','Na','P','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/200705q.png'),
(200706,'chemistry','Brine is electrolysed by using inert electrodes. The reaction at anode is:','Cl⁻(aq) —> 1/2 Cl₂(g) + e⁻ ;        Ecell =1.36V','For oxidation at anode, two possible reactions are oxidation of chlorine and of oxygen. (Reference: NCERT  , class 12 , unit 6 , page 163 paragraph last).','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Oxidation reduction',NULL,'3','mcq','Cl⁻(aq) —> 1/2 Cl₂(g) + e⁻ ;        Ecell =1.36V','2H₂O(l) —> O₂(g) + 4H⁺ + 4e⁻ ;        Ecell= 1.23V','Na⁺ (aq)  + e⁻ —> Na(s);       Ecell = 2.71V','H⁺ (aq)  + e⁻ —> 1/2H₂(g);     Ecell=0.00V','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/200706q.png'),
(200707,'chemistry','Native silver metal forms a water soluble complex with a dilute aqueous solution of sodium cyanide in the presence of:','Oxygen','Native silver metal forms a water soluble complex with a dilute aqueous solution of sodium cyanide in the presence of oxygen. (Reference: NCERT  , class 12 , unit 6 , page 164 paragraph first)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Oxidation reduction',NULL,'1','mcq','Nitrogen','Oxygen','Carbon dioxide','Argon','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/match/200707q.png'),
(200708,'chemistry','Extraction of gold and silver involves leaching the metal with cyanide ion the metal is recovered by :','Displacement of metal by some other metal from the complex ion','Displacement of gold or silver from the solution is made by addition of electropositive metal like zinc.  (Reference: NCERT  , class 12 , unit 6 , page 164 paragraph first)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Oxidation reduction',NULL,'2','mcq','Displacement of metal by some other metal from the complex ion','Roasting of metal complex','Calcination followed by roasting','Thermal decomposition of metal complex','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/200708q.png'),
(200709,'chemistry','Gold is extracted by hydrometallurgy process based on its property:','Of being electropositive','Gold is extracted by hydrometallurgical process, based on its property of being electropositive. of being less reactive, to form complexes which are water soluble. (Reference: NCERT  , class 12 , unit 6 , page 164 paragraph first).','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Oxidation reduction',NULL,'1','mcq','Of being electropositive','To form complexes which are water soluble','Of being less reactive','To form salts which are water soluble','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/200709q.png');
INSERT INTO `ncert_book_pyq` (`unique_id`, `subject`, `question`, `answer`, `explanation`, `topic_name`, `chapter_name`, `difficulty`, `quiz_type`, `option_a`, `option_b`, `option_c`, `option_d`, `syllabus_update`, `ncert22_page`, `ncert23_page`, `image_url`) VALUES
(200710,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding following Assertion and Reason:\nAssertion : Ag and Au are extracted by leaching the ore with dilute solution of NaCN.    \nReason : impurities associated with these ores dissolved in NaCN','Assertion is true but the reason is false','The correct reason is silver and gold dissolve in sodium cyanide forming a soluble complex. 4Au + 8NaCN + 2H₂O + O₂ —> 4Na[Au(CN)₂] + 4NaOH .','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Oxidation reduction',NULL,'3','mcq','Both assertion and reason are true and reason is a correct explanation of assertion','Both assertion and reason are true but reason is not a correct explanation of assertion','Assertion is true but the reason is false','Both assertion and reason are false','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/match/200710q.png'),
(200711,'chemistry','How the metals are recovered in the case of gold and silver reduction?','Displacement reaction','Extraction of gold and silver involves leaching the metal with CN–. This is also an oxidation reaction (Ag → Ag⁺ or Au → Au⁺).The metal is later recovered by displacement method..(Reference: NCERT  , class 12 , unit 6 , page 164 paragraph first)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Oxidation reduction',NULL,'1','mcq','Redox reaction','Replacement reaction','Displacement reaction','Double displacement reaction','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/200711q.png'),
(200712,'chemistry','What are the reducing agent in the gold and silver reduction method?','Zn','2[Au(CN)₂]–(aq) + Zn(s) → 2Au(s) + [Zn(CN)₄]₂– (aq) In this reaction zinc acts as a reducing agent. (Reference: NCERT  , class 12 , unit 6 , page 164 paragraph first)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Oxidation reduction',NULL,'2','mcq','NaCN','Zn','Ag,Au','H₂O','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/200712q.png'),
(200713,'chemistry','In the process of Extraction of Gold:\n1) Roasted gold ore + CN + H₂O → X + OH⁻\n2) X + Zn → Y + Au\nIdentify X and Y','X = [Au(CN)₂]⁻ , Y = [Zn(CN)₄]²⁻','4Au(s) + 8CN– (aq) + 2H₂O(aq) + O₂ (g) → 4[Au(CN)₂]⁻(aq) + 4OH⁻(aq) 2[Au(CN)₂](aq) + Zn(s) → 2Au(s) + [Zn(CN)₄]²⁻(aq) (Reference: NCERT  , class 12 , unit 6 , page 164 paragraph first)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Oxidation reduction',NULL,'3','mcq','X = [Au(CN)₂]⁻ , Y = [Zn(CN)₄]²⁻','X = [Au(CN)₄]²⁻ , Y = [Zn(CN)₄]²⁻','X = [Au(CN)₂]⁻ , Y = [Zn(CN)₆]⁴⁻','X = [Au(CN)₂]⁻ , Y = [Zn(CN)₆]⁴⁻','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/200713q.png'),
(200714,'chemistry','Which gas is released along with chlorine gas during extraction of chlorine from Brine ?','H₂','The production of chlorine results in the co-products caustic soda (sodium hydroxide, NaOH) and hydrogen gas (H2). (Reference: NCERT  , class 12 , unit 6 , page 163 paragraph last).','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Oxidation reduction',NULL,'2','mcq','O₂','H₂','CO₂','Cl₂','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200715,'chemistry','Why is external EMF of more than 2.2 V is required for the extraction of chlorine from Brine?','Because E° comes out to be-2.2 volt','The reaction of extraction of chlorine from the brine the value of ∆G comes out to +422 kJ using the equation E° comes out to be -2.2 v therefore the extraction of Cl2 from brine will require an external EMF of more than 2.2. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 165 , paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Oxidation reduction',NULL,'3','mcq','Because the reaction is exothermic','Because E° comes out to be-2.2 volt','Because the reaction is extremely slow','Because E° comes out to be + 2.2 volt','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200716,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion(A) and reason(R):\nAssertion: Cl₂ is obtained by electrolysis giving out H₂ and aqueous NaOH as by-products. Electrolysis of molten NaCl is also carried out.\nReason:  But in aforementioned case, NaOH is produced and not Na metal.','Assertion is true but the reason is false','Cl₂ is obtained by electrolysis giving out H₂ and aqueous NaOH as by-products. Electrolysis of molten NaCl is also carried out. But in that case, Na metal is produced and not NaOH. (Reference: NCERT  , class 12 , unit 6 , page 163 paragraph 3)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Oxidation reduction',NULL,'2','mcq','Both assertion and reason are true and reason is a correct explanation of assertion','Both assertion and reason are true but reason is not a correct explanation of assertion','Assertion is true but the reason is false','Both assertion and reason are false','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200717,'biology','How many carpals are there?','8','The bones of the hand (fore limb) are humerus, radius andulna, carpals (wrist bones – 8 in number),metacarpals (palm bones – 5 in number) and phalanges (digits – 14 in number).(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 311;paragraph No.1)','Human Physiology >> Locomotion and Movement >> Skeletal system 2','Locomotion and Movement','1','mcq','5','8','14','15','NEW','11-311','11-226',NULL),
(200718,'biology','How many metacarpals are there?','5','The bones of the hand (fore limb) are humerus, radius andulna, carpals (wrist bones – 8 in number),metacarpals (palm bones – 5 in number) and phalanges (digits – 14 in number).(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 311;paragraph No.1)','Human Physiology >> Locomotion and Movement >> Skeletal system 2','Locomotion and Movement','1','mcq','5','8','14','15','NEW','11-311','11-226',NULL),
(200719,'biology','How many phalanges are there?','14','The bones of the hand (fore limb) are humerus, radius andulna, carpals (wrist bones – 8 in number),metacarpals (palm bones – 5 in number) and phalanges (digits – 14 in number).(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 311;paragraph No.1)','Human Physiology >> Locomotion and Movement >> Skeletal system 2','Locomotion and Movement','1','mcq','5','8','14','15','NEW','11-311','11-226',NULL),
(200720,'biology','Which of the following are ALL bones of the lower limb?','Femur,Tibia,Fibula,Tarsals,Metatarsals,Phalanges','Femur (thigh bone – the longest bone), tibia and fibula, tarsals (ankle bones – 7 in number), metatarsals (5 in number) and phalanges (digits – 14 in number) are the bones of the legs (hind limb).(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 311;paragraph No.1)','Human Physiology >> Locomotion and Movement >> Skeletal system 2','Locomotion and Movement','2','mcq','Humerus,Tibia,Fibula,Tarsals,Metatarsals,Phalanges','Femur,Tibia,Fibula,Carpals,Metatarsals,Phalanges','Femur,Tibia,Fibula,Tarsals,Metacarpals,Phalanges','Femur,Tibia,Fibula,Tarsals,Metatarsals,Phalanges','NEW','11-311','11-226',NULL),
(200801,'biology','______is the longest bone.','Femur','Femur is the longest bone. (Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 311;paragraph No.1)','Human Physiology >> Locomotion and Movement >> Skeletal system 3','Locomotion and Movement','1','mcq','Humerus','Tibia','Femur','Hip','NEW','11-311','11-226',NULL),
(200802,'chemistry','Distillation is employed for metals :','With low boiling point','This is very useful for low boiling metals like zinc and mercury. The impure metal is evaporated to obtain the pure metal as distillate. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 165 , paragraph 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Refining',NULL,'2','mcq','With high melting point','With high boiling point','With low melting point','With low boiling point','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200803,'chemistry','Distillation is used for which of the following metals?','Hg','Metals with low boiling point are purified using this method. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 165 , paragraph 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Refining',NULL,'1','mcq','Na','Fe','Ag','Hg','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200804,'chemistry','Liquation process may be applied for purification of :','Tin','In this method a low melting metal like tin can be made to flow on a sloping surface. In this way it is separated from higher melting impurities. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 165 , paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Refining',NULL,'2','mcq','Copper','Tin','Iron','Lead','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200805,'chemistry','Silver containing containing lead as impurity is not purified by:','Levigation','Silver containing lead as impurity is removed by cupellation. Levigation is not involved in this process. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 165 , paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Refining',NULL,'2','mcq','Poling','Levigation','Cupellation','Distillation','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200806,'chemistry','Which is the not correct process-mineral group in Metallurgy extraction?','Zone refining : Sn','Refining of impure Sn Sn cannot be done by zone-refining process. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 165 , paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Refining',NULL,'3','mcq','Leaching: silver','Van arkel : Zr','Liquation: Sn','Zone refining : Sn','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200807,'chemistry','In liquidation the metal is separated by which impurities?','Higher melting','In this method a low melting metal like tin can be made to flow on a sloping surface. In this way it is separated from higher melting impurities.  (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 165 , paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Refining',NULL,'1','mcq','Higher melting','Lower melting','Higher boiling','Lower boiling','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200808,'chemistry','During the process of Electrorefining of copper some metals present as impurity settle down as anode mud, these are:','Ag , Au','More electropositive metals associated with copper pass in solution whereas less electropositive metals collect below the anode as anode mud. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 165 , paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Refining',NULL,'3','mcq','Sn , Ag','Pb , Zn','Ag , Au','Fe , Ni','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200809,'chemistry','When the sample of copper with zinc impurity is to be purified by electrolysis the appropriate electrodes are:','Cathode: Pure Cu ; Anode: Impure sample','In this method impure sample is taken as anode as zinc impurity goes into solution and pure copper is taken as cathode, as pure metal from sample deposits on cathode. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 164, paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Refining',NULL,'3','mcq','Cathode: pure Zn ; Anode: pure Cu','Cathode: Impure sample ; Anode:pure Cu','Cathode: Impure Zn ; Anode:Impure sample','Cathode: Pure Cu ; Anode: Impure sample','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200810,'chemistry','Electrolytic refining may be used for which of the following:','Zn','Copper and Zinc are two metals which are generally purified by using electrolyte refining. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 165 , paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Refining',NULL,'1','mcq','Ni','Zn','Al','Ag','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200811,'chemistry','Which element is purified by zone refining?','Germanium,silicon','This method is very useful for producing semiconductor and other metals of very high purity, e.g., germanium, silicon, boron, gallium and indium. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 165 , paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Refining',NULL,'1','mcq','Germanium,silicon','Gold','Tin','Nickel','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200812,'chemistry','Zone refining is based on the principle of:','Impurities are more soluble in molten metal than in solid metal','This method is based on the principle that the impurities are more soluble in the melt than in the solid state of the metal.(Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 165 , paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Refining',NULL,'3','mcq','Impurities of low boiling metals can be separated by distillation','Impurities are more soluble in molten metal than in solid metal','Different components of a mixture are differently absorbed on adsorbent','Vapours of volatile compounds can be decomposed in pure metal','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200813,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding following Assertion and Reason:\nAssertion: Zone refining method is very useful for producing semiconductors. \nReason : Semiconductors are of high purity','Both assertion and reason are true but reason is not a correct explanation of assertion','Van Arkel Method for Refining Zirconium or Titanium. This method is very useful. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 165 , paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Refining',NULL,'3','mcq','Both assertion and reason are true and reason is a correct explanation of assertion','Both assertion and reason are true but reason is not a correct explanation of assertion','Assertion is true but the reason is false','Both assertion and reason are false','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200814,'chemistry','Zone refining is a method to obtain:','Ultra Pure metals','This method is very useful for producing semiconductor and other metals of very high purity .(Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 165 , paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Refining',NULL,'2','mcq','Very high temperature','Ultra Pure aluminium','Ultra Pure oxides','Ultra Pure metals','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200815,'chemistry','The method not used in Metallurgy to refine impure metal is:','All are used','Amalgamation process is not used for refining impure metal, while other methods are used to refine the impure metal. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 165 , paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Refining',NULL,'1','mcq','Mond\'s process','Van arkel process','Liquation','All are used','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200816,'chemistry','Copper is purified by electrolytic refining of blister copper, the correct statements about this process is/are :','Impurity settle as anode mud','In this method, the impure metal is made to act as anode. A strip of the same metal in pure form is used as cathode. They are put in a suitable electrolytic bath containing soluble salt of the same metal. The more basic metal remains in the solution and the less basic ones go to the anode mud.(Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 165 , paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Refining',NULL,'3','mcq','A copper strip is used as cathode','Acidified Aqua CuSO₄ is used as electrolyte','Pure copper is deposited at cathode','Impurity settle as anode mud','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200817,'chemistry','Vapour phase refining involves the removal of impurities from the crude metal by:','converting the metal into its volatile compound','Vapour phase refining involves the removal of impurities from the crude metal by converting the metal into its volatile compound. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 165 , paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Refining',NULL,'2','mcq','by turning the materials into non volatile compounds','converting the metal into its volatile compound','both of the above','none of the above','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200818,'chemistry','Which method is not correct for refining of crude metals','Mond\'s process : aluminium','Mond Process for Refining Nickel .(Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 165 , paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Refining',NULL,'2','mcq','Liquation: tin','Zone refining: silicon','Electrolytic refining: blister copper','Mond\'s process : aluminium','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200819,'chemistry','Van arkel method of purification of metals involves converting the metal to a :','Volatile enough stable compound','Van-Arkel method of purification of metals involves conversion of an impure metal to a volatile stable compound. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 164 , paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Refining',NULL,'2','mcq','Volatile enough stable compound','Volatile unstable compound','Non volatile stable compound','None of these','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200820,'chemistry','The process of isolation of metals by dissolving the ore in a suitable chemical reagent followed by precipitation of the metal by a more electropositive metal is','Hydrometallurgy','Hydrometallurgy involves dissolving the ore in a suitable reagent (like water, dilute acids or sodium cyanide solution) followed by precipitation by a more electropositive metal. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 164 , paragraph last)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Refining',NULL,'1','mcq','Electro metallurgy','Hydrometallurgy','Electrorefining','Zone refining','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(200901,'chemistry','Justify the  statement: "Copper can be extracted by hydrometallurgy but not zinc"','To extract zinc more reactive metals are required','The metal that cannot be extracted by hydrometallurgy is zinc. This is because to extract zinc more reactive metals are required. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 168 , Exercise 6.1)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Exercise',NULL,'1','mcq','To extract zinc less reactive metals are required','To extract zinc more reactive metals are required','Zinc can also be extract by hydrometallurgy','None of these','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/match/200901q.png'),
(200902,'chemistry','Which of the following is a better reducing agent at 673 K?','CO','Carbon monoxide (CO) is a better reducing agent at 673 K than coke (C ). (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 168 , Exercise 6.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Exercise',NULL,'1','mcq','CO','C','CO₂','CH₄','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/200902q.png'),
(200903,'chemistry','Choose the common elements present in the anode mud in electrolytic refining of copper:\na. Gold & Silver\nb. Platinum\nc. Selenium & Tellurium\nd. Antimony','All of these','In the electrolytic refining of copper, the anode mud contains antimony, selenium, tellurium, silver gold and platinum. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 168 , Exercise 6.6)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Exercise',NULL,'1','mcq','Only a and d','Only b and c','Only d','All of these','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/200903q.png'),
(200904,'chemistry','Which chemical reactions taking place in the extraction of zinc from zinc blende?','Roasting & Reduction','(a) Roasting: The concentrated ore is heated with oxygen at 900°C in reverberatory furnace to convert zinc sulphide to zinc oxide. At 900°C zinc sulphate which is formed due to the oxidation of zinc sulphide also decomposes to zinc oxide. (b) Reduction: Zinc oxide is reduced to zinc with the help of carbon. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 168 , Exercise 6.8)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Exercise',NULL,'1','mcq','Roasting & Reduction','Elimination & Addition','Leaching','All of these','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/200904q.png'),
(200905,'chemistry','State the role of silica in the metallurgy of copper.','Slag','The role of silica in the metallurgy of copper is to remove the iron oxide obtained during the process of roasting as \'slag\'. If the sulphide ore of copper contains iron, then silica SiO2 is added as flux before roasting. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 168 , Exercise 6.9)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Exercise',NULL,'1','mcq','Slag','Flux','Catalyst','Mud','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/200905q.png'),
(200906,'chemistry','Which method of refining may be more suitable if element is obtained in minute quantity?','Column chromatography','Column chromatography is the refining technique that is more suitable if element is obtained in minute quantity. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 168 , Exercise 6.10)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Exercise',NULL,'1','mcq','Distillation','Zone refining','Electrolysis','Column chromatography','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/match/200906q.png'),
(250702,'chemistry','Today, most of the methanol is produced by catalytic hydrogenation of?','Carbon Monoxide','Today, most of the methanol is produced by catalytic hydrogenation of carbon monoxide.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 344; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Some Commercially Important Alcohols',NULL,'1','mcq','Glucose','Benzene','Carbon Monoxide','None of them','NEW','12-344','12-214',NULL),
(200907,'chemistry','Which method of refining will be best for an element in which impurities present have chemical properties close to the properties of that elements?','Zone refining','Zone refining is the method for an element in which impurities present have chemical properties close to the properties of those elements. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 168 , Exercise 6.11)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Exercise',NULL,'1','mcq','Distillation','Zone refining','Electrolysis','Column chromatography','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/200907q.png'),
(200908,'chemistry','Choose equation for the statement: "Separation of alumina from silica in a bauxite ore associated with silica"','Al₂O₃. xH₂O(s)1470K → Al₂O₃(s)+xH₂O(g)','To separate alumina from silica in bauxite ore associated with silica, first the powdered ore is digested with a concentrated NaOH solution at 473 - 523 K and 35 - 36 bar pressure. This results in the leaching out of alumina (Al₂O₃) as sodium aluminate and silica (SiO₂) as sodium silicate leaving the impurities behind. Al₂O₃. xH₂O(s)1470K →Al₂O₃(s)+xH₂O(g) (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 168 , Exercise 6.13)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Exercise',NULL,'2','mcq','Al₂O₃. xH₂O(s)1470K → Al₂O₃(s)+xH₂O(g)','Al₂O₃. xOH(s) 470K → Al₂O₃(s)+xH₂O(g)','Al₂O₃. xH₂O(s)470K →Al₂O₃(s)+xH₂O(g)','Al₂O₃. xOH(s) 1470K →Al₂O₃(s)+xH₂O(g)','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/200908q.png'),
(200909,'chemistry','Why copper matte is put in silica lined converter?','To remove the remaining slag','Copper matte is put in a silica-lined converter to remove the remaining FeO and FeS present in the matte as slag (FeSiO₃). Also, some silica is added to the silica-lined converter. Then, a hot air blast is blown. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 168 , Exercise 6.17)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Exercise',NULL,'1','mcq','To remove the remaining slag','Additional slag is lined','To dilute','None of these','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/200909q.png'),
(200910,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion(A) and reason(R):\nAssertion: By adding the cryolite to the pure Alumina,the melting point of pure Alumina is lowered (Which is very high 2324K).\nReason: Cryolite increases the electrical conductivity of the mixture.','Both assertion and reason are true but reason is not a correct explanation of assertion','By adding the cryolite to the pure Alumina,the melting point of pure Alumina is lowered (Which is very high 2324K) and electrical conductivity of pure alumina is increased. (Reference: NCERT class 12 , unit 6 , page 168 , Exercise 6.18)','Inorganic chemistry >> General principles and processes of isolation of Elements >> Exercise',NULL,'2','mcq','Both assertion and reason are true and reason is a correct explanation of assertion','Both assertion and reason are true but reason is not a correct explanation of assertion','Assertion is true but the reason is false','Both assertion and reason are false','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/200910q.png'),
