(210901,'chemistry','Which of the following correctly describe Ammonia?','Colourless and pungent odour','Ammonia is a colourless gas with a pungent odour.\n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 176, Paragraph No.2)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Ammonia - Properties',NULL,'1','mcq','Colourless and pleasant odour','Pale yellow and pungent odour','Pale yellow and pleasent odour','Colourless and pungent odour','NEW','12-176',NULL,NULL),
(210902,'chemistry','Consider the following:\n\n(a) Ammonia\'s freezing and boiling points are 198.4 K and 239.7 K respectively.\n(b) The ammonia molecule is trigonal pyramidal with the nitrogen atom at the apex.\n(c) Ammonia is a colourless gas with a sweet odour. \n(d) Ammonia gas is sparigly soluble in water.\n\nWhich of the following options are correct?','(a), (b)','Ammonia is a colourless gas with a pungent odour. Its freezing and boiling points are 198.4 and 239.7 K respectively. In the solid and liquid states.  The ammonia molecule is trigonal pyramidal with the nitrogen atom at the apex. Ammonia gas is highly soluble in water. Its aqueous solution is weakly basic due to the formation of OH⁻ ions.\n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 176, Paragraph No.2)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Ammonia - Properties',NULL,'3','mcq','(a), (c)','(b), (d)','(b), (c)','(a), (b)','NEW','12-176',NULL,NULL),
(210903,'chemistry','Which among the following doesn\'t describe NH₃ molecule?','Lewis acid','Ammonia is a colourless gas with a pungent odour. In the solid and liquid states, it is associated through hydrogen bonds. mass. The ammonia molecule\nis trigonal pyramidal with the nitrogen atom at the apex. It has three bond pairs and one lone pair of electrons. The presence of a lone pair of electrons on the nitrogen atom of the ammonia molecule makes it a Lewis base.\n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 176, Paragraph No.2)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Ammonia - Properties',NULL,'3','mcq','Associated through hydrogen bond','Trigonal pyramidal geometry','Three hydrogen bonds','Lewis acid','NEW','12-176',NULL,NULL),
(210904,'chemistry','What is the H-N-H bond angle in ammonia?','107.8⁰','The H-N-H bond angle in ammonia is 107.8⁰\n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 176, Paragraph No.2)\nRefer diagram(ne2102)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Ammonia - Properties',NULL,'1','mcq','109.5⁰','107.8⁰','104.5⁰','101.7⁰','NEW','12-176',NULL,NULL),
(210905,'chemistry','Ammonia\'s aqueous solution is weakly basic due to the formation of which ions?','OH⁻','Ammonia gas is highly soluble in water. Its aqueous solution is weakly basic due to the formation of OH⁻ ions.\nNH₃(g) + H₂O(l)   ⇋   NH⁴⁺ (aq) + OH⁻ (aq)\n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 176, Paragraph No.2)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Ammonia - Properties',NULL,'2','mcq','H⁺','OH⁻','N⁻','H⁻','NEW','12-176',NULL,NULL),
