(211006,'chemistry','Why does NO₂ dimerize?','Because of having odd electron in valence shell','NO₂ contains odd number of valence electrons. It behaves as a typical odd molecule. On dimerisation, it is converted to stable N₂O₄ molecule with even number of electrons.\n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 179, Example 7.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Oxides of Nitrogen',NULL,'2','mcq','Because of having odd electron in valence shell','Because of having even electron in valence shell','Because of having two electron in valence shell','Because of having seven electron in valence shell','NEW','12-179',NULL,NULL),
