(211101,'chemistry','Which among the following is not the oxoacid of Nitrogen?','Hypophosphorous acid','Nitrogen forms oxoacids such as H₂N₂O₂ (hyponitrous acid), HNO₂ (nitrous acid) and HNO₃ (nitric acid). Amongst them HNO₃  is the most important. \n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 179)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Nitric acid - Preparation',NULL,'1','mcq','Hyponitrous acid','Nitrous acid','Nitric acid','Hypophosphorous acid','NEW','12-179',NULL,NULL);
