(211102,'chemistry','In the laboratory, nitric acid is prepared by heating _________ or _________ and concentrated H₂SO₄ in a glass retort.','KNO₃, NaNO₃','In the laboratory, nitric acid is prepared by heating _________ or _________ and concentrated H₂SO₄ in a glass retort.\nNaNO₃ + H₂SO₄ → NaHSO₄ + HNO₃ \n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 179)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Nitric acid - Preparation',NULL,'2','mcq','KNO₃, NaNO₃','Ca(NO₃)₂, Mg(NO₃)₂','KNO₂, NaNO₂','CaNO₂, MgNO₂','NEW','12-179',NULL,NULL),
(211103,'chemistry','Nitric acid is prepared by _________ process.','Ostwald’s process.','On a large scale Nitric acid is prepared mainly by Ostwald’s process.\n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 179)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Nitric acid - Preparation',NULL,'2','mcq','Oxidation','Nitrification','Haber’s Process','Ostwald’s process.','NEW','12-179',NULL,NULL),
(211104,'chemistry','Complete the equation: \nNaNO₃ + H₂SO₄  → _________ + HNO₃.','NaHSO₄','In the laboratory, nitric acid is prepared by heating _________ or _________ and concentrated H₂SO₄ in a glass retort.\nNaNO₃ + H₂SO₄ → NaHSO₄ + HNO₃ \n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 179)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Nitric acid - Preparation',NULL,'3','mcq','NaHSO₄','Na₂SO₃','NaSO₄','SO₂','NEW','12-179',NULL,NULL),
(211105,'chemistry','What is the purity of Nitric acid produced by Ostwald\'s process?','98%','NO thus formed is recycled and the aqueous HNO₃ can be concentrated by distillation upto ~ 68% by mass. Further concentration to 98% can be achieved by dehydration with concentrated H₂SO₄. \n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 179)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Nitric acid - Preparation',NULL,'1','mcq','90%','95%','98%','92%','NEW','12-179',NULL,NULL),
(211106,'biology','Lateral to the blind spot, there is a yellowish pigmented spot called ______.','Macula lutea','Lateral to the blind spot, there is a yellowish pigmented spot called macula lutea with a central pit called the fovea..(Reference  : NCERT biology class 11; page 324;paragraph no.3)','Human Physiology >> Neural Control and Coordination >> The Eye 2','Neural Control and Coordination','2','mcq','Corpus lutea','Macula callosum','Macula lutea','Fovea','OLD','11-324',NULL,NULL),
(211107,'biology','Macula lutea has a central pit called the _______.','Fovea','Lateral to the blind spot, there is a yellowish pigmented spot called macula lutea with a central pit called the fovea. .(Reference  : NCERT biology class 11; page 324;paragraph no.3)','Human Physiology >> Neural Control and Coordination >> The Eye 2','Neural Control and Coordination','2','mcq','Macula fossa','Fovea','Ganglion cells','Carotid','OLD','11-324',NULL,NULL),
(211108,'biology','The fovea is a thinned-out portion of the retina where only _____ are densely packed.','Cones','The fovea is a thinned-out portion of the retina where only the cones are densely packed. .(Reference  : NCERT biology class 11; page 324;paragraph no.3)','Human Physiology >> Neural Control and Coordination >> The Eye 2','Neural Control and Coordination','1','mcq','Cones','Rods','Arteries','Veins','OLD','11-324',NULL,NULL),
(211109,'biology','The ______ is the point where the visual acuity (resolution) is the greatest.','Fovea','Fovea is the point where the visual acuity (resolution) is the greatest..(Reference  : NCERT biology class 11; page 324;paragraph no.3)','Human Physiology >> Neural Control and Coordination >> The Eye 2','Neural Control and Coordination','2','mcq','Macula Lutea','Fovea','Macula fossa','Optic disc','OLD','11-324',NULL,NULL),
