(211117,'biology','The photosensitive compounds (photopigments) in the human eyes is composed of- \n\n1. Opsin \n2. Retinoid \n3. Aldehyde form of Vitamin A \n4. Alkaline form of Vitamin A','Both 1,3 are correct','The photosensitive compounds (photopigments) in the human eyes is composed of opsin (a protein) and retinal (an aldehyde of Vitamin A). .(Reference  : NCERT biology class 11; page 324;paragraph no.6)','Human Physiology >> Neural Control and Coordination >> The Eye 2','Neural Control and Coordination','2','mcq','Both 3,4 are correct','Both 1,4 are correct','Both 1,3 are correct','Both 2,4 are correct','OLD','11-324',NULL,NULL),
(211118,'biology','Retinal is an aldehyde of ______.','Vitamin A','The photosensitive compounds (photopigments) in the human eyes is composed of opsin (a protein) and retinal (an aldehyde of Vitamin A). .(Reference  : NCERT biology class 11; page 324;paragraph no.6)','Human Physiology >> Neural Control and Coordination >> The Eye 2','Neural Control and Coordination','3','mcq','Vitamin B','Vitamin A','Vitamin C','Vitamin D','OLD','11-324',NULL,NULL),
(211119,'biology','Changes in photoreceptor cells result in action in _______ cells.','Ganglion','Potential differences are generated in the photoreceptor cells. This produces a signal that generates action potentials in the ganglion cells through the bipolar cells..(Reference  : NCERT biology class 11; page 324;paragraph no.6)','Human Physiology >> Neural Control and Coordination >> The Eye 2','Neural Control and Coordination','2','mcq','Ganglion','Photoreceptor','Bipolar','Unipolar','OLD','11-324',NULL,NULL),
(211120,'biology','Changes in photoreceptor cells result in action in ganglion cells through ______ cells.','Bipolar','Potential differences are generated in the photoreceptor cells. This produces a signal that generates action potentials in the ganglion cells through the bipolar cells..(Reference  : NCERT biology class 11; page 324;paragraph no.6)','Human Physiology >> Neural Control and Coordination >> The Eye 2','Neural Control and Coordination','2','mcq','Photoreceptor','Bipolar','Ganglion','Unipolar','OLD','11-324',NULL,NULL),
(211121,'biology','Impulses are transmitted by the optic nerves to the ________ area of the brain.','Visual cortex','Impulses are transmitted by the optic nerves to the visual cortex area of the brain..(Reference  : NCERT biology class 11; page 324;paragraph no.6)','Human Physiology >> Neural Control and Coordination >> The Eye 2','Neural Control and Coordination','3','mcq','Visual cortex','Auditory cortex','Cerebellum','Pons','OLD','11-324',NULL,NULL),
