(211133,'biology','What is abnormal curvature of the cornea called','Astigmatism','Astigmatism is a kind of defect of vision in which the image of an object is distorted. It is because all the light rays do not come to focus on retina. It is due to abnormal curvature of the lens . It can be corrected by wearing cylindrical lenses.','Human Physiology >> Neural Control and Coordination >> The Eye 2','Neural Control and Coordination','2','mcq','Glaucoma','Presbyopia','Myopia','Astigmatism','OLD',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(211134,'biology','The thin watery fluid in the eye in the anterior chamber of the eye is called?','Aqueous humor','The space between the cornea and the lens is called the aqueous chamber and contains a thin watery fluid called aqueous humor. The space between the lens and the retina is called the vitreous chamber and is filled with a transparent gel called vitreous humor','Human Physiology >> Neural Control and Coordination >> The Eye 2','Neural Control and Coordination','3','mcq','Aqueous humor','Tears','Mucus','Vitreous humor','OLD','11-324',NULL,NULL),
(211135,'biology','The transparent gel in posterior chamber of the eye is called?','Vitreous humor','The space between the cornea and the lens is called the aqueous chamber and contains a thin watery fluid called aqueous humor. The space between the lens and the retina is called the vitreous chamber and is filled with a transparent gel called vitreous humor.','Human Physiology >> Neural Control and Coordination >> The Eye 2','Neural Control and Coordination','2','mcq','Aqueous chamber','Tears','Mucus','Vitreous humor','OLD','11-324',NULL,NULL),
(211201,'chemistry','Match the following','Specific gravity of HNO₃-1.504, Boiling point of HNO₃-355.6K, Freezing point of HNO₃-231.4K, Analytical grade of HNO₃-68% by mass','The correct match is Specific gravity of HNO₃-1.504, Boiling point of HNO₃-355.6K, Freezing point of HNO₃-231.4K, Analytical grade of HNO₃-68% by mass\n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 179)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Nitric acid - Properties',NULL,'3','match','Specific gravity of HNO₃,1.504','Boiling point of HNO₃,355.6K','Freezing point of HNO₃,231.4K','Analytical grade of HNO₃,68% by mass','NEW','12-179',NULL,NULL),
