(211203,'chemistry','In aqueous solution, nitric acid acts as strong acid and what does it give?','H₃O⁺ ,NO₃⁻','In aqueous solution, nitric acid behaves as a strong acid giving hydronium and nitrate ions.\nHNO₃(aq) + H₂O(l) → H₃O⁺(aq) + NO₃⁻ (aq)\n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 179)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Nitric acid - Properties',NULL,'1','mcq','OH⁻ ,NO₃⁺','H₃O⁺ ,NO₃⁻','H₃O⁺ ,NO⁻','H₃O ,NO₃⁻','NEW','12-179',NULL,NULL),
(211204,'chemistry','Concentrated nitric acid is a strong _________.','oxidising agent','Concentrated nitric acid is a strong oxidising agent.\n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 179)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Nitric acid - Properties',NULL,'1','mcq','base','pollutant','reducing agent','oxidising agent','NEW','12-179',NULL,NULL),
(211205,'chemistry','What does dilute HNO₃ upon reaction with copper give?','NO','Copper reacts with dilute nitric acid to release NO.\n3Cu + 8 HNO₃(dilute) → 3Cu(NO₃)₂ + 2NO + 4H₂O\n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 180)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Nitric acid - Properties',NULL,'1','mcq','NO','NO₂','N₂O','NH₄NO₃','NEW','12-180',NULL,NULL),
(211206,'chemistry','Concentrated HNO₃ upon reaction with metals gives-','NO₂','Metals, on reaction with Conc. Nitric acid, release NO₂\n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 180)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Nitric acid - Properties',NULL,'1','mcq','NO','NO₂','N₂O','NH₄NO₃','NEW','12-180',NULL,NULL),
(211207,'chemistry','Complete the reaction;\nP₄ + 20HNO₃ → 4H₃PO4 + X + 4H₂O','NO₂','HNO₃ converts Phosphorous to Phosphoric acid.\nP₄ + 20HNO₃ → 4H₃PO4 + 2NO₂ + 4H₂O\n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 180 Paragraph 3)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Nitric acid - Properties',NULL,'1','mcq','NO','NO₂','N₂O','NH₄NO₃','NEW','12-180',NULL,NULL),
(211208,'chemistry','Zinc reacts with dilute nitric acid to give N₂O and with concentrated acid to give _________ .','NO₂','Zinc reacts with dilute nitric acid to give N₂O and with concentrated acid to give NO₂..\n4Zn + 10HNO₃ (dilute) → 4Zn(NO₃)₂ + 5H₂O + N₂O\nZn + 4HNO₃ (conc.) → Zn(NO₃)₂ + 2H₂O + 2NO₂\n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 180)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Nitric acid - Properties',NULL,'2','mcq','NO','NO₂','N₂O','N₂O₅','NEW','12-180',NULL,NULL),
(211209,'chemistry','What is formed at the interface between the solution and sulphuric acid layers indicates the presence of nitrate ion in solution?','Brown ring','A brown ring at the interface between the solution and sulphuric acid layers indicates the presence of nitrate ion in solution.\nNO³⁻ + 3Fe²⁺ + 4H⁺ → NO + 3Fe³⁺ + 2H₂O\n[Fe(H₂O)₆]²⁺ + NO → [Fe (H2O)₅(NO)]²⁺ + H₂O\n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 180)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Nitric acid - Properties',NULL,'2','mcq','Brown ring','Blue ring','Black ring','Yellow ring','NEW','12-180',NULL,NULL),
(211210,'chemistry','Which among the following cannot be dissolved in concentrated HNO₃?','Cr','Cr cannot be dissoved in concentrated HNO₃ due to formation of passive film on the surface of Cr \n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 180)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Nitric acid - Properties',NULL,'1','mcq','Cr','Cu','Zn','Mg','NEW','12-180',NULL,NULL),
(211211,'chemistry','What does concentrated HNO₃ oxidises I₂ to?','HIO₃','Concentrated HNO₃ oxidises I₂ to HIO₃\nI₂ + 10HNO₃ → 2HIO₃ + 10NO₂ + 4H₂O\n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 180)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Nitric acid - Properties',NULL,'1','mcq','HIO₃','CO₂','H₂SO₄','H₃PO₄','NEW','12-180',NULL,NULL),
(211212,'chemistry','What does concentrated HNO₃ oxidises C to?','CO₂','Concentrated HNO₃ oxidises C to CO₂.\nC + 4HNO₃ → CO₂ + 2H₂O + 4NO₂\n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 180)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Nitric acid - Properties',NULL,'1','mcq','CO₂','HIO₃','CO','H₃PO₄','NEW','12-180',NULL,NULL),
(211213,'chemistry','What does concentrated HNO₃ oxidises S₈ to?','H₂SO₄','Concentrated HNO₃ oxidises S₈ to H₂SO₄.\nS₈ + 48HNO₃ → 8H₂SO₄ + 48NO₂ + 16H₂O\n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 180)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Nitric acid - Properties',NULL,'1','mcq','H₂SO₄','SO₂','HIO₃','H₃PO₄','NEW','12-180',NULL,NULL),
(211214,'chemistry','What does concentrated HNO₃ oxidises P₄ to?','H₃PO₄','Concentrated HNO₃ oxidises P₄ to H₃PO₄.\nP₄ + 20HNO₃ → 4H₃PO₄ + 20NO₂ + 4H₂O\n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 180)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Nitric acid - Properties',NULL,'1','mcq','H₃PO₄','H₂SO₄','P₂O₅','HIO₃','NEW','12-180',NULL,NULL),
(211215,'chemistry','What can be detected using brown ring test?','Nitrates','Brown ring test is used for the detection of Nitrates.\nNO³⁻ + 3Fe²⁺ + 4H⁺ → NO + 3Fe³⁺ + 2H₂O\n[Fe(H₂O)₆]²⁺ + NO → [Fe (H2O)₅(NO)]²⁺ + H₂O\n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 180)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Nitric acid - Properties',NULL,'1','mcq','Nitrates','Nitrites','Nitrides','Nitriles','NEW','12-180',NULL,NULL),
(211216,'chemistry','Addition of what to a solution containing nitrate ion with careful addition of H₂SO₄ gives brown layer between junction of solution and H₂SO₄?','dilute FeSO₄','Addition of dilute FeSO₄ to a solution containing nitrate ion with careful addition of H₂SO₄ gives brown layer between junction of solution and H₂SO₄\nNO³⁻ + 3Fe²⁺ + 4H⁺ → NO + 3Fe³⁺ + 2H₂O\n[Fe(H₂O)₆]²⁺ + NO → [Fe (H2O)₅(NO)]²⁺ + H₂O\n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 180)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Nitric acid - Properties',NULL,'1','mcq','conc. FeSO₄','dilute FeSO₄','conc. H₂SO₄','dilute H₂SO₄','NEW','12-180',NULL,NULL),
(211217,'chemistry','In ring test, what does Fe²⁺ reduces nitrate to?','Nitric oxide','In ring test ,Fe²⁺ reduces nitrate to Nitric Oxide.\nNO³⁻ + 3Fe²⁺ + 4H⁺ → NO + 3Fe³⁺ + 2H₂O\n[Fe(H₂O)₆]²⁺ + NO → [Fe (H2O)₅(NO)]²⁺ + H₂O\n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 180)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Nitric acid - Properties',NULL,'1','mcq','Nitrogen dioxide','Nitric oxide','Nitrides','Nitrites','NEW','12-180',NULL,NULL),
(211218,'chemistry','Consider the following:\n\n(a) The major use of nitric acid is in the manufacture of ammonium nitrate for fertilisers and other nitrates for use in explosives and pyrotechnics.\n(b) In the gaseous state, HNO₃ does not exist as a planar molecule with the structure. \n(c) In brown ring test precipitate occur as blue.\n(d) In Haber\'s process 89% pure nitric acid is obtained. \n\nWhich of the following options are correct?','only (a)','In the gaseous state, HNO₃ exists as a planar molecule with the structure. The precipitate in brown ring test is brown in colour. In Haber\'s process 98% pure nitric acid is obtained.   \n(Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page No. 180)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Nitric acid - Properties',NULL,'3','mcq','only (a)','only (b)','only (a) and (b)','only (d)','NEW','12-180',NULL,NULL),
(211219,'biology','The space within cochlea called-','Scala media','The space within cochlea called scala media is filled with endolymph.(Reference  : NCERT biology class 11; page 326;paragraph no.1)','Human Physiology >> Neural Control and Coordination >> The Ear 1','Neural Control and Coordination','2','mcq','Scala tympani','Scala media','Scala vestibuli','Scala tubuli','OLD','11-326',NULL,NULL),
(211220,'biology','Scala vestibuli ends at-','Oval window','At the base of the cochlea, the scala vestibuli ends at the oval window, while the scala tympani terminates at the round window which opens to the middle ear..(Reference  : NCERT biology class 11; page 326;paragraph no.1)','Human Physiology >> Neural Control and Coordination >> The Ear 1','Neural Control and Coordination','2','mcq','Oval window','Round window','Eustachian tube','Membranous labyrinth','OLD','11-326',NULL,NULL),
(211221,'biology','Scala tympani ends at-','Round window','At the base of the cochlea, the scala vestibuli ends at the oval window, while the scala tympani terminates at the round window which opens to the middle ear. (Reference  : NCERT biology class 11; page 326;paragraph no.1)','Human Physiology >> Neural Control and Coordination >> The Ear 1','Neural Control and Coordination','2','mcq','Oval window','Round window','Eustachian tube','Membranous labyrinth','OLD','11-326',NULL,NULL),
(211222,'biology','The _______ is a structure located on the basilar membrane which contains hair cells that act as auditory receptors.','Organ of corti','The organ of corti is a structure located on the basilar membrane which contains hair cells that act as auditory receptor.(Reference  : NCERT biology class 11; page 326;paragraph no.2)','Human Physiology >> Neural Control and Coordination >> The Ear 1','Neural Control and Coordination','2','mcq','Eustachian tube','Oval window','Organ of corti','Membranous labyrinth','OLD','11-326',NULL,NULL),
(211223,'biology','The organ of corti contains ________ that act as auditory receptors.','Hair cells','The organ of corti is a structure located on the basilar membrane which contains hair cells that act as auditory receptors.(Reference  : NCERT biology class 11; page 326;paragraph no.2).','Human Physiology >> Neural Control and Coordination >> The Ear 1','Neural Control and Coordination','2','mcq','Hair cells','Rod cells','Cone cells','Bipolar cells','OLD','11-326',NULL,NULL),
(211224,'biology','The _______ end of the hair cell is in close contact with the afferent nerve fibres.','Basal','The basal end of the hair cell is in close contact with the afferent nerve fibres. A large number of processes called stereocilia are projected from the apical part of each hair cell. Above the rows of the hair cells is a thin elastic membrane called tectorial membrane..(Reference  : NCERT biology class 11; page 326;paragraph no.2)','Human Physiology >> Neural Control and Coordination >> The Ear 1','Neural Control and Coordination','2','mcq','Apical','Basal','Lateral','Ventral','OLD','11-326',NULL,NULL),
(211225,'biology','A large number of processes called __________ are projected from the apical part of each hair cell.','Stereocilia','The basal end of the hair cell is in close contact with the afferent nerve fibres. A large number of processes called stereocilia are projected from the apical part of each hair cell. Above the rows of the hair cells is a thin elastic membrane called tectorial membrane..(Reference  : NCERT biology class 11; page 326;paragraph no.2)','Human Physiology >> Neural Control and Coordination >> The Ear 1','Neural Control and Coordination','2','mcq','Basal cilia','Pseudo cilia','Stereocilia','Change','OLD','11-326',NULL,NULL),
