(180302,'chemistry','Rate of reaction in terms of concentration of reactants is known as','All of the above','Rate of reaction in terms of concentration of reactants is known as rate law, rate equation and rate expression.(Reference:  NCERT 12th chemistry ; Page 100 ; Paragraph 2)','Physical chemistry >> Chemical kinetics >> Factors influencing rate of a reaction',NULL,'1','mcq','Rate law','Rate equation','Rate expression','All of the above','NEW','12-100','12-066',NULL),
(180303,'chemistry','The rate of a chemical reaction at a given temperature may depend on the concentration of one or more.','Reactants an products','Rate of reaction depends upon concentration of both reactants and products(Reference:  NCERT 12th chemistry ; Page 100 ; Paragraph 2)','Physical chemistry >> Chemical kinetics >> Factors influencing rate of a reaction',NULL,'1','mcq','Reactants an products','Only reactants','Only products','None of the above','NEW','12-100','12-066',NULL),
(180304,'chemistry','Rate of reaction ____with the passage of time as the concentration of reactants decreases.','Decreases','Rate of reaction depends upon the concentration of reactants.(Reference:  NCERT 12th chemistry ; Page 100 ; Paragraph 3)','Physical chemistry >> Chemical kinetics >> Factors influencing rate of a reaction',NULL,'1','fillup','De,cre,as,es,in,cr,ea,se,s,hh',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-100','12-066',NULL),
(180305,'chemistry','Assertion: Rate law is the expression in which reaction rate is given in terms of molar concentration of reactants with each term raised to some power.                                                                                                                                                                                                     Reason: Powers may or may not be same as the stoichiometric coefficient of the reacting species in a balanced chemical equation.','Both assertion and reason are true but reason is not a correct explanation of the assertion.','(Reference:  NCERT 12th ; Page 101 ; Paragraph 3)','Physical chemistry >> Chemical kinetics >> Factors influencing rate of a reaction',NULL,'3','mcq','Both assertion and reason are true and reason is a correct explanation of the assertion.','Both assertion and reason are true but reason is not a correct explanation of the assertion.','Assertion is true. Reason is false.','Both assertion and reason are false.','NEW','12-101','12-067',NULL),
(180306,'chemistry','For the balanced chemical equation, write the correct rate equation.  2NO(g) + O₂(g)→2NO₂(g) diagram(1801)','Rate =k[NO]² [O₂]','After looking at the results, that when the concentration of NO is doubled and that of O₂ is kept constant then initial rate increases by factor of four.                                                                      \nThis indicates that the rate depends upon the square of the concentration of NO. When NO kept constant , O₂ concentration is doubled the rate also gets doubled.                                                                      Hence, Rate =k[NO]² [O₂](Reference:  NCERT 12th ; Page 101 ; Paragraph 5)','Physical chemistry >> Chemical kinetics >> Factors influencing rate of a reaction',NULL,'3','mcq','Rate =k[NO]² [O₂]','Rate =k[NO] [O₂]²','Rate =k[NO]²[O₂]²','Rate =k[NO] [O₂]','NEW','12-101','12-067','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/180306q.png'),
