(180308,'biology','What is the lifespan of RBCs?','120 days','RBCs have an average life span of 120 days after which they are destroyed in the spleen (graveyard of RBCs).(Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 279; Paragraph No. 3)','Human Physiology >> Body Fluids and circulation >> Formed elements','Body fluids and circulation','2','mcq','100 days','115 days','120 days','125 days','NEW','11-279','11-194',NULL),
(180309,'biology','RBCs are destroyed in the kidneys.','FALSE','RBCs have an average life span of 120 days after which they are destroyed in the spleen (graveyard of RBCs).(Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 279; Paragraph No. 3)','Human Physiology >> Body Fluids and circulation >> Formed elements','Body fluids and circulation','2','mcq','TRUE','FALSE',NULL,NULL,'NEW','11-279','11-194',NULL),
(180310,'biology','Leukocytes are colourless due to-','Lack of hemoglobin','Leukocytes are also known as white blood cells (WBC) as they are colourless due to the lack of haemoglobin. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 279; Paragraph No. 4)','Human Physiology >> Body Fluids and circulation >> Formed elements','Body fluids and circulation','2','mcq','Lack of oxygen','Presence of nucleus','Presence of white coloured pigment','Lack of hemoglobin','NEW','11-279','11-194',NULL),
(180311,'biology','WBCs are lesser in number than RBCs.','TRUE','They are nucleated and are relatively lesser in number which averages 6000-8000 ᵐᵐ³ of blood. Leukocytes are generally short lived. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 279; Paragraph No. 4)','Human Physiology >> Body Fluids and circulation >> Formed elements','Body fluids and circulation','2','mcq','TRUE','FALSE',NULL,NULL,'NEW','11-279','11-194',NULL),
(180312,'biology','What is the average number of WBCs per mm⁻ ³ of blood in an adult man ?','6000-8000','They are nucleated and are relatively lesser in number which averages 6000-8000 ᵐᵐ³ of blood. Leukocytes are generally short lived. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 279; Paragraph No. 4)','Human Physiology >> Body Fluids and circulation >> Formed elements','Body fluids and circulation','2','mcq','6000-8000','15000-20000','2000-6000','20000-25000','NEW','11-279','11-194',NULL),
(180313,'biology','The two main categories of WBCs are-','Agranulocytes and granulocytes','We have two main categories of WBCs – granulocytes and agranulocytes. Neutrophils, eosinophils and basophils are different types of granulocytes, while lymphocytes and monocytes are the agranulocytes. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 279; Paragraph No. 4)','Human Physiology >> Body Fluids and circulation >> Formed elements','Body fluids and circulation','2','mcq','Agranulocytes and granulocytes','Granulocytes and neutrophils','Agranulocytes and Leucocytes','Leucocytes and erythrocytes','NEW','11-279','11-194',NULL),
(180314,'biology','Pick the odd one out.','Lymphocytes','We have two main categories of WBCs – granulocytes and agranulocytes. Neutrophils, eosinophils and basophils are different types of granulocytes, while lymphocytes and monocytes are the agranulocytes.(Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 279; Paragraph No. 4)','Human Physiology >> Body Fluids and circulation >> Formed elements','Body fluids and circulation','2','mcq','Basophils','Eosinophils','Lymphocytes','Neutrophils','NEW','11-279','11-194',NULL),
(180315,'biology','Which of the following is an agranulocyte?','Monocyte','We have two main categories of WBCs – granulocytes and agranulocytes. Neutrophils, eosinophils and basophils are different types of granulocytes, while lymphocytes and monocytes are the agranulocytes. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 279; Paragraph No. 4)','Human Physiology >> Body Fluids and circulation >> Formed elements','Body fluids and circulation','2','mcq','Monocyte','Eosinophils','Neutrophils','Basophils','NEW','11-279','11-194',NULL),
(180316,'biology','Which of the following are phagocytic cells?','Neutrophils and monocytes','Neutrophils and monocytes (6-8 %) are phagocytic cells which destroy foreign organisms entering the body. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 279; Paragraph No. 4)','Human Physiology >> Body Fluids and circulation >> Formed elements','Body fluids and circulation','2','mcq','Monocytes and basophils','Neutrophils and lymphocytes','Eosinophils and basophils','Neutrophils and monocytes','NEW','11-279','11-194',NULL),
(180317,'biology','Which of the following is the most abundant WBC?','Neutrophils','Neutrophils are the most abundant cells (60-65 %) of the total WBCs and basophils are the least (0.5-1 percent) among them. Neutrophils and monocytes (6-8 %) are phagocytic cells which destroy foreign organisms entering the body. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 279; Paragraph No. 4)','Human Physiology >> Body Fluids and circulation >> Formed elements','Body fluids and circulation','2','mcq','Neutrophils','Eosinophils','Lymphocytes','Basophils','NEW','11-279','11-194',NULL),
(180318,'biology','Which of the following is the least abundant WBC?','Basophils','Neutrophils are the most abundant cells (60-65 %) of the total WBCs and basophils are the least (0.5-1 percent) among them. Neutrophils and monocytes (6-8 % ) are phagocytic cells which destroy foreign organisms entering the body. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 279; Paragraph No. 4)','Human Physiology >> Body Fluids and circulation >> Formed elements','Body fluids and circulation','2','mcq','Neutrophils','Eosinophils','Lymphocytes','Basophils','NEW','11-279','11-194',NULL),
(180319,'biology','Which of the following is not secreted by basophils?','Steroids','Basophils secrete histamine, serotonin, heparin, etc., and are involved in inflammatory reactions. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 279; Paragraph No. 4)','Human Physiology >> Body Fluids and circulation >> Formed elements','Body fluids and circulation','2','mcq','Steroids','Histamine','Serotonin','Heparin','NEW','11-279','11-194',NULL),
