(180702,'chemistry','Assertion: The temperature dependence of the rate of a chemical reaction can be explained by Arrhenius equation.                                               Reason: k = Ae ⁻ᴱᵃ/ᴿᵀ , A is the Arrhenius factor.','Both assertion and reason are true and reason is a correct explanation of the assertion.','(Reference NCERT Class 12; page 112; Paragraph 4)','Physical chemistry >> Chemical kinetics >> Temperature dependence of the rate of a reaction',NULL,'3','mcq','Both assertion and reason are true and reason is a correct explanation of the assertion.','Both assertion and reason are true but reason is not a correct explanation of the assertion.','Assertion is true. Reason is false.','Both assertion and reason are false.','NEW','12-112','12-078',NULL),
