(180704,'chemistry','The energy required to form activated complex is known as','Activation energy','The energy required to form activated complex is known as activation energy.','Physical chemistry >> Chemical kinetics >> Temperature dependence of the rate of a reaction',NULL,'1','mcq','Activation energy','Most probable kinetic energy','Kinetic energy','Potential energy','NEW','12-113','12-079','/ncert/pyq/physics/mcq/180704q.png'),
(180705,'chemistry','Assertion: All the molecules in the reacting species do not have the same kinetic energy.                                                                           Reason: The final enthalpy of the reaction depends upon the nature of reactants and products.','Both assertion and reason are true but reason is not a correct explanation of the assertion.','Both the statements are correct but  not related to each other.','Physical chemistry >> Chemical kinetics >> Temperature dependence of the rate of a reaction',NULL,'3','mcq','Both assertion and reason are true but reason is a correct explanation of the assertion.','Both assertion and reason are true but reason is not a correct explanation of the assertion.','Assertion is true. Reason is false.','Both assertion and reason are false.','NEW','12-113','12-079',NULL),
(180706,'chemistry','Which one of the following doesn\'t represent Arrhenius equation.','k = AE⁻ᴿᵀ','All other are different forms of Arrhenius equation.','Physical chemistry >> Chemical kinetics >> Temperature dependence of the rate of a reaction',NULL,'2','mcq','k = Ae⁻ᴱ/ᴿᵀ','logₑk = logₑA - E/RT','log₁₀k = log₁₀A - E/2.303RT','k = AE⁻ᴿᵀ','NEW','12-114','12-080',NULL),
(180707,'chemistry','Energy of activation of a reactant is reduced by','Increased temperature','Energy of activation of a reactant is reduced by increasing temperature.','Physical chemistry >> Chemical kinetics >> Temperature dependence of the rate of a reaction',NULL,'1','mcq','Increased temperature','Reduced temperature','Reduced pressure','Increased pressure','NEW','12-113','12-079',NULL),
