(181216,'chemistry','Calculate the half-life of the first order reaction from their rate constants given below: 200 /s','3.46 × 10⁻³ s','Half life period of a first order reaction is given by t₁/₂ = 0.693/k , hence t₁/₂ = 0.693/200 = 3.46 × 10⁻³ s','Physical chemistry >> Chemical kinetics >> NCERT Exercises',NULL,'1','mcq','3.46 × 10⁻³ s','3.46 × 10³ s','1.73 × 10³ s','3.46 × 10⁻⁴ s','NEW','12-111','12-077',NULL),
