(181304,'chemistry','Consider the following figure and mark the correct option.','Activation energy of forward reaction is E1 + E2 and product is more stable than reactant.','Ea(forward) = E1 + E2\nSince energy of reactants is less than products and the product is less stable than the reactant.','Physical chemistry >> Chemical kinetics >> NCERT Examplar',NULL,'1','mcq','Activation energy of forward reaction is E1 + E2  and product is less stable than reactant','Activation energy of forward reaction is E1 + E2 and product is more stable than reactant.','Activation energy of both forward and backward reactions is E1 + E2 and reactant is more stable than product.','Activation energy of backward reaction is E, and product is more stable than reactant.','NEW','12-113','12-079','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/181304q.png'),
