(250102,'chemistry','Alcohols and phenols are formed when a hydrogen atom in a hydrocarbon is replaced by ____ group.','OH','Alcohols and phenols are formed when a hydrogen atom in a hydrocarbon, aliphatic and aromatic respectively, is replaced by –OH group. \n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 323; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Introduction',NULL,'1','mcq','RO','CH₃','OH','ArO','NEW','12-323','12-193',NULL),
