(250104,'chemistry','The sugar we eat, the cotton used for fabrics, the paper we use for writing, are all made up of compounds containing ___________.','OH','The sugar we eat, the cotton used for fabrics, the paper we use for writing, are all made up of compounds containing –OH groups.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 323; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Introduction',NULL,'1','mcq','OH','OR','ArO','COOR','NEW','12-323','12-193',NULL),
(250105,'chemistry','An alcohol contains one or more hydroxyl group(s) directly attached to carbon atom(s) of a/an _______________ system.','Aliphatic','An alcohol contains one or more hydroxyl (OH) group(s) directly attached to carbon atom(s), of an aliphatic system (CH₃OH).\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 323; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Introduction',NULL,'1','mcq','Aromatic','Aliphatic','Benzoic','Carbonyl system','NEW','12-323','12-193',NULL),
(250106,'chemistry','Which of the following statement is correct?','An alcohol contains one or more hydroxyl (OH) group(s) directly attached to carbon atom(s), of an aliphatic system','An alcohol contains one or more hydroxyl (OH) group(s) directly attached to carbon atom(s), of an aliphatic system (CH₃OH). \n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 323; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Introduction',NULL,'2','mcq','An alcohol contains one or more hydroxyl (OH) group(s) directly attached to carbon atom(s), of an aromatic system.','An alcohol contains one or more hydroxyl (OH) group(s) directly attached to carbon atom(s), of an aliphatic system','A phenol contains one or more hydroxyl (OH) group(s) directly attached to carbon atom(s), of an aliphatic system','All of the above','NEW','12-323','12-193',NULL),
