(250108,'chemistry','A phenol contains __________','–OH group(s) directly attached to carbon atom(s) of an aromatic system.','A phenol contains –OH group(s) directly attached to carbon atom(s) of an aromatic system (C₆H₅OH).\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 323; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Introduction',NULL,'2','mcq','–RO group(s) directly attached to carbon atom(s) of an aromatic system.','–OH group(s) directly attached to carbon atom(s) of an aliphatic system.','–RO group(s) directly attached to carbon atom(s) of an aliphatic system.','–OH group(s) directly attached to carbon atom(s) of an aromatic system.','NEW','12-323','12-193',NULL),
(250109,'chemistry','_____________ are formed when hydrogen atom in a hydrocarbon is substituted with an alkoxy or aryloxy group.','Ethers','The substitution of a hydrogen atom in a hydrocarbon by an alkoxy or aryloxy group (R–O/Ar–O) yields another class of compounds known as ‘ethers.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 323; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Introduction',NULL,'1','mcq','Alcohols','Phenol','Ketones','Ethers','NEW','12-323','12-193',NULL),
(250110,'chemistry','Consider the following statements.\nWhich of the above statements are false?','Both alcohols and phenols contain π bond in their structure.','An alcohol contains one or more hydroxyl (OH) group(s) directly attached to carbon atom(s), of an aliphatic system (CH₃OH) while a phenol contains –OH group(s) directly attached to carbon atom(s) of an aromatic system (C₆H₅OH). The substitution of a hydrogen atom in a hydrocarbon by an alkoxy or aryloxy group (R–O/Ar–O) yields another class of compounds known as ‘ethers’.\n (Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 323; Paragraph No. 2 and 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Introduction',NULL,'2','mcq','An alcohol contains one or more hydroxyl (OH) group(s) directly attached to carbon atom(s), of an aliphatic system','A phenol contains –OH group(s) directly attached to carbon atom(s) of an aromatic system.','The substitution of a hydrogen atom in a hydrocarbon by an alkoxy or aryloxy group yields ethers','Both alcohols and phenols contain π bond in their structure.','NEW','12-323','12-193',NULL),
(250111,'chemistry','CH₃OCH₃  is the example of?','Ether','In ethers O-atom is attached to two alkyl groups for example CH₃OCH₃ (dimethyl ether).\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 323; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Introduction',NULL,'1','mcq','Aromatic System','Alcohols','Ether','Phenols','NEW','12-323','12-193',NULL),
