(250113,'chemistry','Match the following?','Alcohol-CH₃OH,Phenol-C₆H₅OH,Ether-CH₃OCH₃,Alkoxy-RO','An alcohol contains one or more hydroxyl (OH) group(s) directly attached to carbon atom(s), of an aliphatic system (CH₃OH) while a phenol contains –OH group(s) directly attached to carbon atom(s) of an aromatic system (C₆H₅OH). The substitution of a hydrogen atom in a hydrocarbon by an alkoxy or aryloxy group (R–O/Ar–O) yields another class of compounds known as ‘ethers’, for example, CH₃OCH₃ (dimethyl ether).\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 323; Paragraph No. 2 and 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Introduction',NULL,'3','match','Alcohol,CH₃OH','Phenol,C₆H₅OH','Ether,CH₃OCH₃','Alkoxy,RO','NEW','12-323','12-193',NULL),
(250114,'biology','Interstitial spaces do not contain-','Epididymis','The regions outside the seminiferous tubules called interstitial spaces, contain small blood vessels and interstitial cells or Leydig cells. \nREF: NCERT PAGE 43','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 1',NULL,'3','mcq','Small blood vessels','Interstitial cells','Leydig cells','Epididymis','NEW','12-043','12-027',NULL),
(250115,'biology','Which cells synthesise and secrete testicular hormones called androgens?','Leydig cells','The regions outside the seminiferous tubules called interstitial spaces, contain small blood vessels and interstitial cells or Leydig cells. Leydig cells synthesise and secrete testicular hormones called androgens. REF: NCERT PAGE 43','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 1',NULL,'2','mcq','Leydig cells','Sertoli cells','Urethral cells','Prostate cells','NEW','12-043','12-027',NULL),
(250116,'biology','The male sex accessory ducts do not include-','Bartholin Glands','The male sex accessory ducts include rete testis, vasa efferentia, epididymis and vas deferens. REF: NCERT PAGE 44','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 1',NULL,'2','mcq','Rete testis','Vasa efferentia','Epididymis','Bartholin Glands','NEW','12-044','12-028',NULL),
(250117,'biology','The seminiferous tubules of the testis open into the vasa efferentia through-','Rete testis','The seminiferous tubules of the testis open into the vasa efferentia through rete testis. REF: NCERT PAGE 43','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 1',NULL,'1','mcq','Rete testis','Vas deferens','Leydig cells','Sertoli cells','NEW','12-043','12-027',NULL),
(250118,'biology','The vasa efferentia leave the testis and open into__________located along the posterior surface of each testis.','Epididymis','The vasa efferentia Leave the testis and open into epididymis located along the posterior surface of each testis REF: NCERT PAGE 43','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 1',NULL,'3','fillup','E,p,i,di,d,y,m,is',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-043','12-027',NULL),
(250119,'biology','The epididymis leads to _______ that ascends to the abdomen and loops over the urinary bladder.','Vas deferens','The epididymis leads to vas deferens that ascends to the abdomen and loops over the urinary bladder. REF: NCERT PAGE 43','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 1',NULL,'2','mcq','Vas deferens','Rete testis','Vasa efferentia','Vasa afferentia','NEW','12-043','12-027',NULL),
