(250126,'biology','Humans are :','Sexually reproducing and viviparous','Humans, like most mammals, are viviparous animals. Humans reproduce via internal fertilization. As in all higher mammals, the egg implants in the uterine wall while it develops. REF: NCERT PAGE 42','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 1',NULL,'1','mcq','Sexually reproducing and viviparous','Asexually reproducing and oviparous','Sexually reproducing and oviparous','Asexually reproducing and viviparous','NEW','12-042','12-026',NULL),
(250127,'biology','The primary sex organs in Human male are:','Testis','In human beings, the primary sex organs – the testis in the males and the ovaries in the females – produce gametes, i.e, sperms and ovum, respectively, by the process called gametogenesis. REF: NCERT PAGE 43','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 1',NULL,'1','mcq','Ovaries','Testis','Urethra','Uterus','NEW','12-043','12-027',NULL),
(250128,'biology','What is inseminaion?','Transfer of sperms into the female genital tract','Insemination is the deposition of semen in the female reproductive tract. With sexual intercourse, the deposit is made within the vagina or the cervix.','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 1',NULL,'2','mcq','Transfer of sperms into the female genital tract','Transfer of sperms into the male genital tract','Transfer of ovum into the female genital tract','Transfer of ovum into the male genital tract','NEW','12-042','12-026',NULL),
(250129,'biology','Formation and development of blastocyst and its attachment to the uterine wall is known as ________','implantation','In embryology, implantation refers specifically to the attachment of the fertilized egg to the uterine lining, which occurs approximately 6 or 7 days after conception REF: NCERT PAGE 46','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 1',NULL,'3','fillup','im,pl,an,ta,ti,on',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-046','12-030',NULL),
(250130,'biology','Gestation refers to:','Period of developing inside the womb between conception and birth','Gestation refers to the process or period of developing inside the womb between conception and birth.','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 1',NULL,'2','mcq','Period of developing inside the womb between conception and birth','Development of blastocyst','Period of developing inside the womb between conception and death','Formation of zygote','NEW','12-042','12-026',NULL),
(250131,'biology','Assertion: Delivery of the baby is known as Parturition. \n\nReason: Parturition is one of the reproductive events found in humans.','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Childbirth, the process of delivering the baby and placenta from the uterus to the vagina to the outside world is known as Parturition REF: NCERT PAGE 46','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 1',NULL,'2','mcq','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Assertion is true but reason is fase','Both Assertion and Reason are false','NEW','12-046','12-030',NULL),
(250132,'biology','In Human beings reproductive changes begin after __________','puberty','Puberty is the stage when the reproductive organs have developed and attained maturity.Hence In Human beings reproductive events occur after puberty.','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 1',NULL,'1','fillup','p,u,b,e,r,ty',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-042','12-026',NULL),
(250133,'biology','The correct sequence of reproductive events in humans include:','Gametogenesis-insemination-fertilisation-implantation-gestation-parturition','The reproductive events in humans include formation of gametes (gametogenesis), i.e., sperms in males and ovum in females, transfer of sperms into the female genital tract (insemination) and fusion of male and female gametes (fertilisation) leading to formation of zygote. This is followed by formation and development of blastocyst and its attachment to the uterine wall (implantation), embryonic development (gestation) and delivery of the baby (parturition). Reference  : NCERT Page 42','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 1',NULL,'3','mcq','Gametogenesis-insemination-implantation-fertilisation-gestation-parturition','Gametogenesis-insemination-fertilisation-implantation-gestation-parturition','Fertilisation-insemination-gametogenesis-implantation-gestation-parturition','Gametogenesis-insemination-fertilisation-implantation-parturition-gestation','NEW','12-042','12-026',NULL),
(250134,'biology','Assertion:There are remarkable differences between the reproductive events in the male and in the female. \n\nReason: Sperm formation continues even in old men, but formation of ovum ceases in women around the age of fifty years.','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','There are remarkable differences between the reproductive events in the male and in the female, for example, sperm formation continues even in old men, but formation of ovum ceases in women around the age of fifty years, because after birth no more oogonia are added after birth but in males spermatogonia keep dividing constantly.','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 1',NULL,'2','mcq','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Assertion is true but reason is fase','Both Assertion and Reason are false','NEW','12-042','12-026',NULL),
(250135,'biology','Formation of ovum ceases in women around the age of:','50 to 55 years','Formation of ovum ceases in women around the age of 50 years because the ovaries no longer make estrogen and progesterone. Reference  : NCERT Page 46','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 1',NULL,'2','mcq','20 to 30 years','12 to 15 years','50 to 55 years','60 to 70 years','NEW','12-046','12-030',NULL),
(250136,'biology','The scrotum helps in maintaining the low temperature of the testes (2–2.5°C) lower than the normal internal body temperature) necessary for spermatogenesis.','TRUE','The scrotum hangs outside the body because it needs to maintain a slightly lower temperature than the rest of the body. This lower temperature helps to maintain sperm production. Reference  : NCERT Page 43','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 1',NULL,'2','mcq','TRUE','FALSE',NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-043','12-027',NULL),
(250137,'biology','Shape of the testis in adult human beings is ______','Oval','Shape of the testis in adult human beings is oval Reference  : NCERT Page 43','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 1',NULL,'1','mcq','Oval','Round','Globular','Rhomboid','NEW','12-043','12-027',NULL),
(250138,'biology','Choose the correct length and width of the testis respectively:','4 to 5 cm,2 to 3 cm','In adults, each testis is oval in shape, with a length of about 4 to 5 cm and a width of about 2 to 3 cm. Reference  : NCERT Page 43','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 1',NULL,'3','mcq','4 to 5 cm,2 to 3 cm','2 to 3 cm,4 to 5 cm','3 to 5 cm,1 to 3 cm','1 to 3cm,3 to 5 cm','NEW','12-043','12-027',NULL),
