(250201,'chemistry','________alcohols and phenols contain many hydroxyl group(s) in their structures.','Polyhydric','Alcohols and phenols may be classified as mono–, di–, tri- or polyhydric compounds depending on whether they contain one, two, three or many hydroxyl groups respectively in their structures.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 324; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Classification',NULL,'1','mcq','Polyhydric','Monohydric','Aromatic','Oligohydric','NEW','12-324','12-195',NULL),
(250202,'chemistry','Monohydric alcohols may be further classified according to the _____________ of the carbon atom to which the hydroxyl group is attached.','Hybridisation','Monohydric alcohols may be further classified according to the hybridisation of the carbon atom to which the hydroxyl group is attached.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 324; Paragraph No. 4)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Classification',NULL,'1','mcq','Hybridisation','Isotope','Charge','Position','NEW','12-324','12-195',NULL),
(250203,'chemistry','______________ may be further classified according to the hybridisation of the carbon atom to which the hydroxyl group is attached.','Monohydric Alcohols','Monohydric alcohols may be further classified according to the hybridisation of the carbon atom to which the hydroxyl group is attached.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 324; Paragraph No. 4)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Classification',NULL,'1','mcq','Tertiary Alcohols','Monohydric Alcohols','Primary Ketones','Primary Alcohols','NEW','12-324','12-195',NULL),
(250204,'chemistry','Consider the following statements.Which of the above statements are correct?\n\n i. Primary, secondary and tertiary alcohols are those in which one, two or three OH groups are attached to the carbon atom respectively. \nii. Primary, secondary and tertiary alcohols are those in which the OH group is attached to primary, secondary and tertiary carbon atom, respectively. \niii. Primary, secondary and tertiary alcohols are those in which the OH group is attached to primary, secondary and tertiary hydrogen atom, respectively.\niv. Primary, secondary and tertiary alcohols are also called as 1°, 2° and 3° alcohols.','ii and iv','Primary, secondary and tertiary alcohols: In these three types of alcohols, the –OH group is attached to primary, secondary and tertiary carbon atom, respectively.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 324; Paragraph No. 5)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Classification',NULL,'2','mcq','i and iii','ii and iv','i, ii and iv','Only iv','NEW','12-324','12-195',NULL),
(250205,'chemistry','In these alcohols, the —OH group is attached to a sp³ hybridised carbon adjacent to the carbon-carbon double bond?','Allylic','Allylic alcohols: In these alcohols, the —OH group is attached to a sp³ hybridised carbon adjacent to the carbon-carbon double bond.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 324; Paragraph No. 6)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Classification',NULL,'1','mcq','Dihydric','Polyhydric','Allylic','Benzylic','NEW','12-324','12-195',NULL),
(250206,'chemistry','In these alcohols, the —OH group is attached to a sp³ hybridised carbon atom next to an aromatic ring?','Benzylic','Benzylic alcohols: In these alcohols, the —OH group is attached to a sp³ hybridised carbon atom next to an aromatic ring.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 324; Paragraph No. 7)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Classification',NULL,'1','mcq','Allylic','Benzylic','Vinylic','Polyhydric','NEW','12-324','12-195','/ncert/pyq/biology/match/250206q.png'),
(250207,'chemistry','Which of the following statement is false?\n\ni. Monohydric alcohols may be further classified according to the hybridisation of the carbon atom to which the hydroxyl group is attached.\nii. In benzylic alcohols, the —OH group is attached to a sp³ hybridised carbon atom next to an aromatic ring.\niii. Allylic and benzylic alcohols may be primary, secondary or tertiary.\niv. None of the above','iv','Monohydric alcohols may be further classified according to the hybridisation of the carbon atom to which the hydroxyl group is attached. \nBenzylic alcohols: In these alcohols, the —OH group is attached to a sp³ hybridised carbon atom next to an aromatic ring. \nAllylic and benzylic alcohols may be primary, secondary or tertiary.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 324; Paragraph No. 4,7; Page 325; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Classification',NULL,'2','mcq','i and iii','ii','ii and iii','iv','NEW','12-324','12-195','/ncert/pyq/biology/match/250207q.png'),
(250208,'chemistry','Alcohols contain —OH group bonded to a carbon-carbon double bond are known as _____________ alcohols.','Vinylic','Alcohols contain —OH group bonded to a carbon-carbon double bond, i.e., to a vinylic carbon or to an aryl carbon. These alcohols are also known as vinylic alcohols.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 325; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Classification',NULL,'1','mcq','Tertiary','Secondary','Vinylic','Primary','NEW','12-325','12-196','/ncert/pyq/biology/match/250208q.png'),
(250209,'chemistry','Carbon which makes double bond with another carbon atom is called ________ carbon.','Vinylic','These alcohols contain —OH group bonded to a carbon-carbon double bond, i.e., to a vinylic carbon or to an aryl carbon.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 325; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Classification',NULL,'1','mcq','Vinylic','Primary','Secondary','Tertiary','NEW','12-325','12-196','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/250209q.png'),
(250210,'chemistry','Phenols are divided into __________ types.','3','Phenols— Mono, Di and trihydric phenols.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 325; Topic No. 11.1.2)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Classification',NULL,'1','mcq','2','3','4','5','NEW','12-325','12-196','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/250210q.png'),
(250211,'chemistry','Ethers are classified into __________ types.','2','Ethers are classified as simple or symmetrical. (Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 325; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Classification',NULL,'1','mcq','2','3','5','4','NEW','12-325','12-196','/ncert/pyq/biology/match/250211q.png'),
(250212,'chemistry','Ethers are classified as?','Symmetrical and Unsymmetrical','Ethers are classified as simple or symmetrical, if the alkyl or aryl groups attached to the oxygen atom are the same, and mixed or unsymmetrical.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 325; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Classification',NULL,'1','mcq','Mono and Diethers','Di and Triethers','Symmetrical and Unsymmetrical','Polyethers and Monoethers','NEW','12-325','12-196','/ncert/pyq/biology/match/250212q.png'),
(250213,'chemistry','Name of this compound (C₂H₅OC₂H₅) is?','Diethyl ether','Diethyl ether, C₂H₅OC₂H₅.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 325; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Classification',NULL,'1','mcq','Ethanol','Dimethyl ether','Diethyl ether','Ethylmethyl ether','NEW','12-325','12-196','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/250213q.png'),
(250214,'chemistry','C₂H₅OC₆H₅ is the example of?','Unsymmetrical ether','C₂H₅OC₆H₅ is unsymmetrical ether.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 325; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Classification',NULL,'1','mcq','Vinylic alcohol','Symmetrical ether','Dihydric alcohol','Unsymmetrical ether','NEW','12-325','12-196','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/250214q.png'),
