(250217,'biology','The seminiferous tubules of the testis are lined by the germinal epithelium consisting of','Spermatogonia and Sertoli cells','Each seminiferous tubule is lined on its inside by two types of cells called male germ cells (spermatogonia) and Sertoli cells Reference  : NCERT Page 43','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Prostate cells','Cells of Sertoli only','Spermatogonium only','Spermatogonia and Sertoli cells','NEW','12-043','12-027',NULL),
(250218,'biology','Which of these is an accessory reproductive gland in human males ?','Prostate gland','The male accessory glands (Figure 3.1a, b) include paired seminal vesicles, a prostate and paired bulbourethral glands. Reference  : NCERT Page 43','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 2',NULL,'3','mcq','Cervical gland','Endometrial gland','Mammary glands','Prostate gland','NEW','12-043','12-027',NULL),
(250219,'biology','Which one of the following is not a male accessory gland ?','Ampulla','The male accessory glands (Figure 3.1a, b) include paired seminal vesicles, a prostate and paired bulbourethral glands. Reference  : NCERT Page 43','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Prostate','Seminal vesicle','Ampulla','Bulbourethral gland','NEW','12-043','12-027',NULL),
(250220,'biology','The vas deferens receives duct from the seminal vesicle and opens into urethra as','Ejaculatory duct','The vas deferens receives duct from the seminal vesicle and opens into urethra as ejaculatory duct. Reference  : NCERT Page 43','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 2',NULL,'3','mcq','Epididymis','Ejaculatory duct','Efferent ductule','Ureter','NEW','12-043','12-027',NULL),
(250221,'biology','Temperature of the scrotum which is necessary for the functioning of testis is always around ________ below body temperature.','2°C','Temperature of the scrotum which is necessary for the functioning of testis is always 2C around below body temperature. Reference  : NCERT Page 43','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 2',NULL,'3','mcq','2°C','4°C','6°C','8°C','NEW','12-043','12-027',NULL),
(250222,'biology','The nutritive cells found in seminiferous tubules are','Sertoli cells','The nutritive cells found in seminiferous tubules are Sertoli cells Reference  : NCERT Page 43','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 2',NULL,'3','mcq','Sertoli cells','Leydig’s cells','Atretic follicular cells','Chromaffin cells','NEW','12-043','12-027',NULL),
(250223,'biology','Prostate glands are located below','Seminal vesicles','Prostate glands are located below Seminal vesicles Reference  : NCERT Page 44','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Gubernaculum','Seminal vesicles','Epididymis','Bulbourethral glands','NEW','12-044','12-028',NULL),
(250224,'biology','The ___________ leads to vas deferens that ascends to the abdomen and loops over the urinary bladder.','Epididymis','The epididymis leads to vas deferens that ascends to the abdomen and loops over the urinary bladder. Reference  : NCERT Page 44','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Sertoli cells','Rete testis','Vasa efferentia','Epididymis','NEW','12-044','12-028',NULL),
(250225,'biology','Which of the following receives a duct from seminal vesicle and opens into urethra as the ejaculatory duct ?','Vas deferens','Vas deferens, rete testes, vasa efferentia and epididymis are male accessory ducts. Vas deferens receives a duct from seminal vesicle and opens into urethra as the ejaculatory duct Reference  : NCERT Page 44','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Epididymis','Vas deferens','Rete testis','Sertoli cells','NEW','12-044','12-028',NULL),
(250226,'biology','________ store and transport the sperms from the testis to the outside through _________','Ejaculatory duct,urethra','Ejaculatory ducts store and transport the sperms from the testis to the outside through urethra. Reference  : NCERT Page 44','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Urethra,ejaculatory duct','Rete testis,ejaculatory duct','Ejaculatory duct,urethra','Ejaculatory duct,vas deferens','NEW','12-044','12-028',NULL),
(250227,'biology','The urethra originates from the urinary bladder and extends through the penis to its external opening called','Urethral meatus','The urethra originates from the urinary bladder and extends through the penis to its external opening called urethral meatus. Reference  : NCERT Page 45','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Urethral meatus','Vaginal opening','Cervix','Urinary opening','NEW','12-045','12-029',NULL),
(250228,'biology','Which carbohydrate is rich in Seminal Plasma?','Fructose','Seminal plasma which is rich in fructose, calcium and certain enzymes. Reference  : NCERT Page 44','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Glucose','Fructose','Lactose','Glycogen','NEW','12-044','12-028',NULL),
(250229,'biology','The enlarged end of penis called the glans penis is covered by a loose fold of skin called','Foreskin','The enlarged end of penis called the glans penis is covered by a loose fold of skin called foreskin Reference  : NCERT Page 43','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 2',NULL,'1','mcq','Elastic tissue','Foreskin','Collagenous tissue','Loose skin','NEW','12-043','12-027',NULL),
(250230,'biology','Assertion: Secretions of male accessory glands constitute the seminal plasma. \n\nReason: The seminal plasma is rich in fructose, calcium and certain enzymes.','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Seminal plasma is a complex fluid comprised of secretions from all organs or tubules of the seminal tract and from the seminiferous tubules in the testicles. Reference  : NCERT Page 45','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Assertion is true but reason is fase','Both Assertion and Reason are false','NEW','12-045','12-029',NULL),
(250231,'biology','Other name for the insterstitial cells is?','Leyding cells','The regions outside the seminiferous tubules called interstitial spaces, contain small blood vessels and interstitial cells or Leydig cells. Reference  : NCERT Page 43','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Cowpers cells','Leyding cells','Sertoli cells','Germinal cells','NEW','12-043','12-027',NULL),
(250232,'biology','The seminiferous tubules of the testis open into the vasa efferentia through','Rete testis','The seminiferous tubules of the testis open into the vasa efferentia through rete testis.','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 2',NULL,'1','mcq','Urethral meatus','Epididymis','Vasa efferentia','Rete testis','NEW','12-043','12-027',NULL),
(250233,'biology','Leydig cells are found in','Seminiferous tubule','Leydig cells are found in Seminiferous tubule.','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Liver','Ovary','Seminiferous tubule','kidney','NEW','12-043','12-027',NULL),
(250234,'biology','What are the primary sex organs in male and female are respectively ?','Testis and ovaries','The primary sex organs in male and female are respectively-Testis and ovaries.  Reference  : NCERT Page 47','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Ovaries and testis','Testis and uterus','Testis and ovaries','Testis and vagina','NEW','12-047','12-031',NULL),
(250235,'biology','Which of the following is not a constitiuent of Seminal Plasma?','Glucose','Secretions of these glands constitute the seminal plasma which is rich in fructose, calcium and certain enzymes. Reference  : NCERT Page 44','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Male Reproductive System 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Fructose','Calcium','Glucose','Enzymes','NEW','12-044','12-028',NULL),
(250301,'chemistry','The common name of an alcohol is derived from the common name of the _________ group and adding the word alcohol to it.','Alkyl','The common name of an alcohol is derived from the common name of the alkyl group and adding the word alcohol to it.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 325; Paragraph No. 4)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Nomenclature',NULL,'1','mcq','Aryl','Alkoxy','Alkyl','Vinyl','NEW','11-325','11-195',NULL),
(250302,'chemistry','What is the formula of methyl alcohol?','CH₃OH','CH₃OHis methyl alcohol.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 325; Paragraph No. 4)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Nomenclature',NULL,'1','mcq','CH₃OCH₃','C₂H₅OC₆H₅','C₂H₅OH','CH₃OH','NEW','11-325','11-195',NULL),
(250303,'chemistry','According to IUPAC system the name of alcohol is derived by substituting \'e\' of an alkane with ______.','ol','The name of an alcohol is derived from the name of the alkane from which the alcohol is derived, by substituting ‘e’ of alkane with the suffix ‘ol’.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 326; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Nomenclature',NULL,'1','mcq','ol','yl','al','el','NEW','11-326','12-196',NULL),
(250304,'chemistry','In alcohols that do not contain any other substituent , the parent chain is numbered starting at the end nearest to which atom or group?','Hydroxyl Group','The longest carbon chain (parent chain) is numbered starting at the end nearest to the hydroxyl group.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 326; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Nomenclature',NULL,'1','mcq','Alkyl Group','Carbon Atom','Hydroxyl Group','Oxygen Atom','NEW','12-326','12-196',NULL),
(250305,'chemistry','For naming ____________ alcohols, the ‘e’ of alkane is retained and the ending ‘ol’ is added.','polyhydric','For naming polyhydric alcohols, the ‘e’ of alkane is retained and the ending ‘ol’ is added.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 326; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Nomenclature',NULL,'1','mcq','polyhydric','monohydric','dihydric','trihydric','NEW','12-326','12-196',NULL),
(250306,'chemistry','Consider the following statements. Which of the above statement(s) is/are false?\n\ni. According to IUPAC system the name of alcohol is derived by substituting \'e\' of an alkane with \'ol\'. \nii. For naming polyhydric alcohols, the ‘e’ of alkane is retained and the ending ‘ol’ is added. \niii. The positions of the –OH group and other substituents are indicated by using the numbers of carbon atoms to which these are attached. \niv. For naming monohydric alcohols, the ‘e’ of alkane is retained and the ending ‘ol’ is added.','iv','The name of an alcohol is derived from the name of the alkane from which the alcohol is derived, by substituting ‘e’ of alkane with the suffix ‘ol’. The positions of the –OH group and other substituents are indicated by using the numbers of carbon atoms to which these are attached. For naming polyhydric alcohols, the ‘e’ of alkane is retained and the ending ‘ol’ is added.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 326; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Nomenclature',NULL,'2','mcq','ii','iv','i,ii,iii','ii,iv','NEW','12-326','12-196',NULL),
(250307,'chemistry','In polyhydric alcohols, the number of –OH groups is indicated by adding the multiplicative prefix, di, tri, etc. at which position?','Before ‘ol’','The number of –OH groups is indicated by adding the multiplicative prefix, di, tri, etc., before ‘ol’.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 326; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Nomenclature',NULL,'1','mcq','After \'ol\'','Before ‘ol’','At start of the name','Anywhere in between','NEW','12-326','12-196',NULL),
(250308,'chemistry','HO–CH₂–CH₂–OH is named as?','ethane–1,2-diol','HO–CH₂–CH₂–OH is named as ethane–1, 2-diol.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 326; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Nomenclature',NULL,'1','mcq','ethane–1,2-diol','ethene–1,2-diol','ethyne–1,2-diol','methyl alcohol','NEW','12-326','12-196',NULL),
(250309,'chemistry','IUPAC name for CH₃–CH₂–CH₂–CH₂–OH is?','butan-1-ol','CH₃–CH₂–CH₂–CH₂–OH, butan-1-ol.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 326; Table No. 11.1)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Nomenclature',NULL,'1','mcq','propan-1-ol','butan-2-ol','butan-1-ol','ethan-1-ol','NEW','12-326','12-196',NULL),
(250310,'chemistry','Common name for 2-methylpropan-2-ol is?','tert-butyl alcohol','tert-Butyl alcohol, 2-methylpropan-2-ol.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 326; Table No. 11.1)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Nomenclature',NULL,'1','mcq','isobutyl alcohol','tert-butyl alcohol','2-methylpropan-1-ol','glycerol','NEW','12-326','12-196',NULL),
(250311,'chemistry','IUPAC name of Glycerol is?','propane -1, 2, 3-triol','Glycerol, propane -1, 2, 3-triol.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 326; Table No. 11.1)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Nomenclature',NULL,'1','mcq','2-methylpropan-2-ol','butan-2-ol','propane -1, 2, 3-triol','propan-2-ol','NEW','12-326','12-196',NULL);
