(250314,'chemistry','Name the following compound.\ndiagram(n2502)','Cyclohexanol','Cyclic alcohols are named using the prefix cyclo and considering the —OH group attached to C–1. \nThe compound is not derivative of phenol as it does not contain aromatic ring.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 326; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Nomenclature',NULL,'1','mcq','Cresol','Hydroquinone','Cyclohexanol','Benzene','NEW','12-326','12-196','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250314q.png'),
