(250316,'chemistry','The structure of phenol involves?','Both a and b','Structure of phenol involves a benzene ring.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 326; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Nomenclature',NULL,'1','mcq','Hydroxyl Group','Benzene Ring','Straight Chain','Both a and b','NEW','12-326','12-196',NULL),
(250317,'chemistry','The terms "ortho, meta and para" when two hydroxyl groups are attached to a benzene ring are used in the common names in the naming  of ____________.','Phenols','Structure of phenol involves a benzene ring, in its substituted compounds the terms ortho (1,2- disubstituted), meta (1,3-disubstituted) and para (1,4-disubstituted) are often used in the common names.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 326; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Nomenclature',NULL,'1','mcq','Phenols','Cyclic','both a and b','Aliphatic','NEW','12-326','12-196',NULL),
