(250326,'biology','The female reproductive system consists of :','Pair of ovaries ,a pair of oviducts, uterus, cervix, vagina, external genitalia,mammary glands','The female reproductive system consists of a pair of ovaries alongwith a pair of oviducts, uterus, cervix, vagina and the external genitalia. Reference  : NCERT Page 44','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Female Reproductive System 1',NULL,'2','mcq','Pair of ovaries ,a pair of oviducts, uterus, cervix, vagina, external genitalia,mammary glands,seminal vesicles','Pair of ovaries ,a pair of oviducts, uterus, cervix, vagina, external genitalia,mammary glands','Pair of testis ,a pair of oviducts, uterus, cervix, vagina, external genitalia,mammary glands','Pair of ovaries ,a pair of oviducts, prostate gland,uterus, cervix, vagina, external genitalia,mammary glands','NEW','12-044','12-028',NULL),
(250327,'biology','The female reproductive system is located in the:','pelvic region and lower abdomen','The female reproductive organs are located in the pelvic region, except ovaries whuch are situated in the lower abdomen.','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Female Reproductive System 1',NULL,'1','mcq','Cervical region','pelvic region and lower abdomen','Abdominal region','Scrotal region','NEW','12-044','12-028',NULL),
(250328,'biology','All the organs of female reproductive system are integrated structurally and functionally to support the processes of  \n\ni.Ovulation        \nii.Pregnancy,birth        \niii.fertilisation   \niv.Spermatogenesis','i, ii and iii','All organs of female reproductive system are integrated structurally and functionally to support the processes of ovulation, fertilisation, pregnancy, birth and child Reference  : NCERT Page 47','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Female Reproductive System 1',NULL,'2','mcq','ii and iv','i, ii and iii','i and iii','iii and iv','NEW','12-047','12-031',NULL),
(250329,'biology','Ovaries produce:  \n\ni.The female gamete (ovum)   \nii.Several steroid hormones (ovarian hormones)    \niii.Sperms   \niv.Androgens','i and ii','Ovaries are the primary female sex organs that produce the female gamete (ovum) and several steroid hormones (ovarian hormones) Reference  : NCERT Page 48','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Female Reproductive System 1',NULL,'1','mcq','ii and iv','i and ii','iii and iv','i and iii','NEW','12-048','12-032',NULL),
(250330,'biology','The ovaries are located one on each side of the ________ abdomen','Lower','The ovaries are located one on each side of the lower abdomen. Reference  : NCERT Page 48','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Female Reproductive System 1',NULL,'1','mcq','Lower','Upper','Lateral','Medial','NEW','12-048','12-032',NULL),
(250331,'biology','Each ovary is connected to _________ and __________ by ligaments.','pelvic wall,uterus','Each ovary is about 2 to 4 cm in length and is connected to the pelvic wall and uterus by ligaments. Reference  : NCERT Page 49','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Female Reproductive System 1',NULL,'2','mcq','pelvic wall,uterus','pelvic wall,vagina','uterus,vagina','urehthra,vagina','NEW','12-049','12-033',NULL),
(250332,'biology','The ovarian epithelium encloses the _______________','ovarian stroma','Each ovary is covered by, a thin epithelium which encloses the ovarian stroma. Reference  : NCERT XII Page 44','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Female Reproductive System 1',NULL,'2','fillup','ov,ari,an str,o,ma',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-044','12-028',NULL),
(250333,'biology','The ovarian stroma is divided into:','A peripheral cortex and an inner medulla','The ovarian stroma is divided into two zones – a peripheral cortex and an inner medulla. Reference  : NCERT Page 48','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Female Reproductive System 1',NULL,'2','mcq','A peripheral medulla and an inner cortex','A peripheral cortex and an inner mucosa','A peripheral mucosa and an inner medulla','A peripheral cortex and an inner medulla','NEW','12-048','12-032',NULL),
(250334,'biology','Each fallopian tube extends from the periphery of _______ to _______','each ovary,uterus','Each fallopian tube is about 10-12 cm long and extends from the periphery of each ovary to the uterus Reference  : NCERT Page 48','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Female Reproductive System 1',NULL,'2','mcq','each ovary,uterus','uterus,each ovary','each ovary,urethra','each ovary,vagina','NEW','12-048','12-032',NULL),
(250335,'biology','Which of the following is the last part of the oviduct?','Isthmus','The part of the fallopian tube closer to the ovary is the funnel-shaped infundibulum.The infundibulum leads to a wider part of the oviduct called ampulla. The last part of the oviduct, isthmus has a narrow lumen and it joins the uterus.','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Female Reproductive System 1',NULL,'3','mcq','Isthmus','Ampulla','Infundibulum','Fimbriae','NEW','12-046','12-030',NULL),
(250336,'biology','Uterus is a paired organ of the female reproductive system.','FALSE','The uterus is single and it is also called womb. Reference  : NCERT Page 46','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Female Reproductive System 1',NULL,'1','mcq','TRUE','FALSE',NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-046','12-030',NULL),
(250337,'biology','Shape of the uterus is like an:','Inverted pear','The shape of the uterus is like an inverted pear Reference  : NCERT Page 46','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Female Reproductive System 1',NULL,'2','mcq','Inverted cone','Inverted pear','Inverted pyramidal','Oval','NEW','12-046','12-030',NULL),
(250338,'biology','Uterus is supported by _______ attached to the pelvic wall.','ligaments','Uterus is supported by ligaments attached to the pelvic wall Reference  : NCERT Page 46','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Female Reproductive System 1',NULL,'1','fillup','l,i,ga,m,en,t,s',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-046','12-030',NULL),
(250339,'biology','Birth canal is formed by which of the following:','Cervical canal,vagina','The uterus opens into vagina through a narrow cervix. The cavity of the cervix is called cervical canal which alongwith vagina forms the birth canal. Reference  : NCERT Page 46','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Female Reproductive System 1',NULL,'2','mcq','Vagina,uterus','Cervical canal,vagina','Cervical canal,uterus','Cervical canal,urethra','NEW','12-046','12-030',NULL),
