(250401,'chemistry','In alcohols, the oxygen of the –OH group is attached to carbon by a __________ bond.','Sigma','In alcohols, the oxygen of the –OH group is attached to carbon by a sigma (σ ) bond.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 328; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Structures of Functional Groups',NULL,'1','mcq','Sigma','Double','Pi','Triple','NEW','12-328','12-198',NULL),
(250402,'chemistry','The bond angle in alcohols is slightly less than the __________ angle.','Tetrahedral','The bond angle in alcohols is slightly less than the tetrahedral angle (109°-28′).\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 329; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Structures of Functional Groups',NULL,'1','mcq','Tetrahedral','Octahedral','Hexagonal','Pyramidal','NEW','12-329','12-199',NULL),
(250403,'chemistry','The bond angle in alcohols is slightly less than the tetrahedral angle. It is due to the repulsion between the unshared electron pairs of?','Oxygen','The bond angle in alcohols is slightly less than the tetrahedral angle (109°-28′). It is due to the repulsion between the unshared electron pairs of oxygen.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 329; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Structures of Functional Groups',NULL,'1','mcq','Hydrogen','Carbon','Oxygen','Nitrogen','NEW','12-329','12-199',NULL),
(250404,'chemistry','In phenols, the –OH group is attached to __________ hybridized carbon of an aromatic ring.','sp²','In phenols, the –OH group is attached to sp² hybridised carbon of an aromatic ring.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 329; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Structures of Functional Groups',NULL,'1','mcq','sp²','sp','sp³','sp³d','NEW','12-329','12-199',NULL),
