(250406,'chemistry','In ethers, the four electron pairs are arranged approximately in a ______________ arrangement.','Tetrahedral','In ethers, the four electron pairs, i.e., the two bond pairs and two lone pairs of electrons on oxygen are arranged approximately in a tetrahedral arrangement.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 329; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Structures of Functional Groups',NULL,'1','mcq','Tetrahedral','Octahedral','Hexagonal','Pyramidal','NEW','12-329','12-199',NULL),
