(250427,'biology','Choose the correct statement with regards to labia majora:','The labia majora are fleshy folds of tissue','The labia majora are fleshy folds of tissue, which extend down from the mons pubis and surround the vaginal opening REF: NCERT PAGE 46','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Female Reproductive System 2',NULL,'2','mcq','The labia majora are multiple folds of tissue','The labia majora is a cushion of fatty tissue covered by skin and pubic hair','The labia majora are fleshy folds of tissue','The labia majora are ligamentous folds of tissue','NEW','12-046','12-030',NULL),
(250428,'biology','The _______ is often torn during the first coitus?','hymen','The opening of the vagina is often covered partially by a membrane called hymen. The hymen is often torn during the first coitus (intercourse). REF: NCERT PAGE 46','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Female Reproductive System 2',NULL,'2','fillup','h,y,m,e,n',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-046','12-030',NULL),
(250429,'biology','All regarding external female genitalia are true , except:','Hymen can never be torn, except during first intercourse','The hymen is often torn during the first coitus (intercourse). However, it can also be broken by a sudden fall or jolt, insertion of a vaginal tampon, active participation in some sports like horseback riding, cycling, etc. In some women the hymen persists even after coitus.\n(Reference  : NCERT 12th, page 46, paragraph 3)','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Female Reproductive System 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Hymen can be broken by a sudden fall or jolt','Hymen can be torn by insertion of a vaginal tampon','Hymen can be torn by active participation in some sports like horseback riding, cycling, etc','Hymen can never be torn, except during first intercourse','NEW','12-046','12-030',NULL),
(250430,'biology','Assertion: The presence or absence of hymen is not a reliable indicator of virginity or sexual experience. \n\nReason: In some women the hymen persists even after coitus','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','In some women the hymen persists even after coitus. In fact, the presence or absence of hymen is not a reliable indicator of virginity or sexual activity, it can also be torn by other physically sternous activity.  REF: NCERT PAGE 46','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Female Reproductive System 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Assertion is true but reason is fase','Both Assertion and Reason are false','NEW','12-046','12-030',NULL),
(250431,'biology','The mammary glands are paired structures.','TRUE','The mammary glands are paired structures (breasts) that contain glandular tissue and variable amount of fat. REF: NCERT PAGE 46','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> The Female Reproductive System 2',NULL,'1','mcq','TRUE','FALSE',NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-046','12-030',NULL),
