(250720,'biology','Choose the incorrect statement regarding gonadotropins, LH and FSH','The secretion of gonadotropins (LH and FSH) decreases gradually during the follicular phase','The secretion of gonadotropins (LH and FSH) increases gradually during the follicular phase, and stimulates follicular development as well as secretion of estrogens by the growing follicles. Reference  : NCERT Page 50 and 51','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Menstrual Cycle',NULL,'3','mcq','The secretion of gonadotropins (LH and FSH) decreases gradually during the follicular phase','FSH and LH stimulates secretion of estrogens by the growing follicles','Both LH and FSH attain a peak level in the middle of cycle (about 14th day).','FSH and LH stimulates follicular development','NEW','12-051','12-035',NULL),
(250721,'biology','What is LH surge?','Rapid secretion of LH leading to its maximum level during the mid-cycle is called LH Surge','Rapid secretion of LH leading to its maximum level during the mid-cycle called LH surge induces rupture of Graafian follicle and thereby the release of ovum. Reference  : NCERT Page 50','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Menstrual Cycle',NULL,'2','mcq','Rapid secretion of FSH leading to its maximum level during the mid-cycle is called LH Surge','Rapid secretion of LH leading to its maximum level during the end of the cycle is called LH Surge','Rapid secretion of LH leading to its minimum level during the mid-cycle is called LH Surge','Rapid secretion of LH leading to its maximum level during the mid-cycle is called LH Surge','NEW','12-050','12-034',NULL),
(250722,'biology','Rapid secretion of ______ induces rupture of Graafian follicle and thereby the release of ovum (ovulation)','LH','Rapid secretion of LH leading to its maximum level during the mid-cycle called LH surge induces rupture of Graafian follicle and thereby the release of ovum. Reference  : NCERT Page 50','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Menstrual Cycle',NULL,'2','mcq','FSH','LH','GnRH','Estrogen','NEW','12-050','12-034',NULL),
