(250838,'biology','Cleavage occurs at which part of female reproductive system?','Isthumus','The mitotic division starts as the zygote moves through the isthmus of the oviduct called cleavage towards the uterus. Reference  : NCERT Page 52','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Fertilisation and Implantation',NULL,'2','mcq','Vagina','Fundus','Cervix','Isthumus','NEW','12-052','12-036',NULL),
(250901,'chemistry','The structure of intermediate A in the following reaction is \ndiagram(n2520)','c','Cumene (isopropylbenzene) is oxidised in the presence of air to cumene hydroperoxide. \nIt is converted to phenol and acetone by treating it with dilute acid.\nNEET 2019','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','a','b','c','d','NEW','12-332','12-202','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250901q.png'),
(250902,'chemistry','When vapours of a secondary alcohol is passed over heated copper at 573 K, the product formed is','a ketone','This reaction involves the dehydration of secondary alcohols.\nOdisha NEET 2019','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','a carboxylic acid','an aldehyde','a ketone','an alkene.','NEW','12-339','12-209','/ncert/pyq/physics/mcq/250902q.png'),
(250903,'chemistry','In the reaction, the electrophile involved is:\ndiagram(n2521)','dichlorocarbene (:CCl₂)','This reaction is an example of Reimer-Tiemann reaction. The electrophile formed when chloroform react with OH⁻ ion from sodium hydroxide.\nNEET 2018','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'3','mcq','chloromethyl cation  (C⁺HCl₂)','formyl cation (C⁺HO)','dichloromethyl anion(C⁻HCl₂ )','dichlorocarbene (:CCl₂)','NEW','12-343','12-213','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250903q.png'),
(250904,'chemistry','Compound A, C₈H₁₀O, is found to react with NaOI (produced by reacting Y with NaOH) and yields a yellow precipitate with characteristic smell. A and Y are respectively.\n diagram(n2522)','c','It is an example of Haloform reaction because compound is forming yellow ppts. with NaOI. NaOI is produed by reating I₂ with NaOH and this test is given by those Alochols which contain methyl group adjacent to the carbon atom that is attached with OH group.\nNEET 2018','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','a','b','c','d','NEW','12-343','12-213','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250904q.png'),
(250905,'chemistry','Which one is the most acidic compound? \ndiagram(n2523)','c','As NO₂ is electron withdrawin group it will increase the acidity of phenol while CH₃ is electron donating group so it will decrease the acidity of phenol.\nNEET 2017','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','a','b','c','d','NEW','12-337','12-207','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250905q.png'),
(250906,'chemistry','Reaction of phenol with chloroform in presence of dilute sodium hydroxide finally introduces which one of the following functional group?','–CHO','On treating phenol with chloroform in the presence of sodium hydroxide, a –CHO group is introduced at ortho position of benzene ring. This reaction is known as Reimer - Tiemann reaction. \nNEET 2015','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','–COOH','–CHCl₂','–CHO','–CH₂Cl','NEW','12-343','12-213',NULL);
INSERT INTO `ncert_book_pyq` (`unique_id`, `subject`, `question`, `answer`, `explanation`, `topic_name`, `chapter_name`, `difficulty`, `quiz_type`, `option_a`, `option_b`, `option_c`, `option_d`, `syllabus_update`, `ncert22_page`, `ncert23_page`, `image_url`) VALUES
(250907,'chemistry','Which of the following will not be soluble in sodium hydrogen carbonate?','o-nitrophenol','o-nitrophenol is a weak acid than carbonic acid hence it will not react with NaHCO₃.\nNEET 2014','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'2','mcq','2,4,6-trinitrophenol','benzoic acid','o-nitrophenol','benzenesulphonic acid','NEW','12-341','12-211','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/250907q.png'),
(250908,'chemistry','Number of isomeric alcohols of molecular formula C₆H₆₁₄O which give positive iodoform test is','4','Alcohols with formula R — CHOH — CH₃ give iodoform test positive and only 4 isomers of C₆H₁₄O has this type of formula.\nKarnataka NEET 2013','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','3','4','5','2','NEW','12-343','12-213','/ncert/pyq/biology/match/250908q.png'),
(250909,'chemistry','Anisole on cleavage with HI gives \ndiagram(n2524)','a','Anisole on cleavage with HI gives phenol and methyl iodide. Bond between phenyl ring and oxygen is not cleaved because of partial double bond character. \nNEET 2020','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','a','b','c','d','NEW','12-350','12-220','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250909q.png'),
(250910,'chemistry','The compound that is most difficult to protonate is \ndiagram(n2525)','a','Lone pair on Oxygen atom in phenol is in conjugation with the ring so it will be difficult to protonate.\nNEET 2019','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'2','mcq','a','b','c','d','NEW','12-333','12-203','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250910q.png'),
(250911,'chemistry','The major products C and D formed in the following reactions respectively are \ndiagram(n2526)','a','Ethers react with HI to form alkyl halide and alcohol. if there is excess HI then alcohol formed will react further to give alhyl iodide.\nNEET 2019','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'2','mcq','a','b','c','d','NEW','12-347','12-217','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250911q.png'),
(250912,'chemistry','The heating of phenyl methyl ether with HI produces','phenol','In the first step HI will attack phenyl methyl ether to give oxonium ion and iodide ion. \nIn the second step iodide ion attack on methyl group of oxonium ion and produce phenol and methyl iodide as final product.\nNEET 2019\ndiagram(ne2503)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','iodobenzene','phenol','benzene','ethyl chloride','NEW','12-347','12-217',NULL),
(250913,'chemistry','The reaction depicted in the diagram is an example of: diagram(n2527)','Williamson ether synthesis reaction','This reaction is an example of  Williamson’s ether synthesis reaction. In this reaction sodium alkoxide react with alkyl halide to form ether.\nNEET 2017','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'2','mcq','dehydration reaction','Williamson alcohol synthesis reaction','Williamson ether synthesis reaction','alcohol formation reaction.','NEW','12-345','12-215','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250913q.png'),
(250914,'chemistry','The reaction is an example of:\ndiagram(n2528)','Williamson synthesis','This reaction is an example of  Williamson’s ether synthesis reaction.\nNEET 2015','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','Etard reaction','Gattermann-Koch reaction','Williamson synthesis','Williamson continuous etherification process.','NEW','12-345','12-215','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250914q.png'),
(250915,'chemistry','Identify Z in the sequence of reactions \ndiagram(n2529)','a','1-butene will react with HBr to give 1-bromobutane which will react with C₂H₅ONa to form CH₃—(CH₂)₃ — O — CH₂CH₃\nNEET 2014\ndiagram(ne2504)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','a','b','c','d','NEW','12-347','12-217','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250915q.png'),
(250916,'chemistry','Among the following ethers, which one will produce methyl alcohol on treatment with hot concentrated HI \ndiagram(n2530)','a','This is an example of Nucleophilic substituion reaction of ether. Primary and secondary ethers react with HX through Sɴ2 mechanism and produce alcohol with most substituted carbon atom, but tertiary ethers react with HX through Sɴ1 and produce alcohol with less substituted carbon.\nNEET 2013\ndiagram(ne2505)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','a','b','c','d','NEW',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250916q.png'),
(250917,'chemistry','The general molecular formula, which represents the homologous series of alkanols is:','CₙH₂ₙ+2O','Alcohols have general formula CₙH₂ₙ+₂.\nONEET 2006','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','CₙH₂ₙ+2O','CnH₂ₙO₂','CₙH₂ₙO','CₙH₂ₙ + 3O','NEW','12-323','12-193',NULL),
(250918,'chemistry','Reaction between acetone and methyl magnesium chloride followed by hydrolysis will give. ( NEET 2020)','tert-butyl alcohol','Reaction between acetone and methyl magnesium chloride followed by hydrolysis will give tert-butyl alcohol.\nNEET 2020','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','iso-propyl alcohol','sec-butyl alcohol','tert-butyl alcohol','iso-butyl alcohol','NEW',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250918q.png'),
(250919,'chemistry','Identify the major products P, Q and R in the following sequence of reactions:\ndiagram(n2531)','d','In the first step cumene is formed by the reaction of benzene and propyl chloride. cumene furhter oxidise in the presence of to cumene hydroperoxide. It is converted to phenol and acetone by treating it with dilute acid.\nNEET 2018\ndiagram(ne2532)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'3','mcq','a','b','c','d','NEW','12-332','12-202','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250919q.png'),
(250920,'chemistry','Which of the following reaction(s) can be used for the preparation of alkyl halides?\ndiagram(n2533)','d','Primary and Secondary alcohols produce alkyl halide on reaction with HCl in the presence of Anh. ZnCl₂. While tertiary alcohol don\'t need Anh. ZnCl₂ for this reaction.\nNEET 2015','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','a','b','c','d','NEW','12-338','12-208','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250920q.png'),
(250921,'chemistry','In the following sequence of reactions, the end product (C) is \ndiagram(n2534)','ethyl alcohol','The first step will produce methyl cyanide (CH₃CN) which react with an acid to form acetic acid (CH₃COOH). In final step acetic acid will react with LiAlH₄ in the presence of ether to form ethyl alcohol (C₂H₅OH).\nNEET 2012','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','acetone','methane','acetaldehyde','ethyl alcohol','NEW','12-330','12-200','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250921q.png'),
(250922,'chemistry','Given are cyclohexanol \n(I), acetic acid\n(II), 2,4,6-trinitrophenol \n(III) and phenol \n(IV) In these the order of decreasing acidic character will be','III > II > IV > I','cyclohexanol is an aliphatic alcohol and aliphatic alcohols are less acidic than phenols and carboxylic acid. 2,4,6-trinitrophenol is most acidic among all because of three electron withdrawing group. Acetic acid is more acidic than phenol due to presence of electron withdrawing group C=O.\nNEET 2010','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'2','mcq','III > II > IV > I','II > III > I > IV','II > III > IV > I','III > IV > II > I','NEW','12-337','12-207',NULL),
(250923,'chemistry','Which of the following compounds has the most acidic nature?\ndiagram(n2535)','b','Phenol has the highest acidic character due to presence of phenyl ring in (a) the OH is separated from phenyl ring due to the presence of CH₂ group so it\'s acidity decreases. (c) and (d) are aliphatic alcohols and they are less acidic then phenol .\nNEET 2010','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'2','mcq','a','b','c','d','NEW','12-345','12-215','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250923q.png'),
(250924,'chemistry','Among the following four compounds, arrange in descending order of acidity order \n(i) Phenol \n(ii) Methyl phenol\n(iii)Meta-nitrophenol \n(iv) Para-nitrophenol\nThe acidity order is','(iv) > (iii) > (i) > (ii)','If NO₂ group is attached with phenol its acidity will increase. because it is electron withdrawing group. If NO₂ is attached at para position, phenol acidity will increase more than at mata position because of greater stability of phenoxide ion. \nNEET 2010','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'2','mcq','(iv) > (iii) > (i) > (ii)','(iii) > (iv) > (i) > (ii)','(i) > (iv) > (iii) > (ii)','(ii) > (i) > (iii) > (iv)','NEW','12-337','12-207',NULL),
(250925,'chemistry','When glycerol is treated with excess of HI, it Produces.','2-iodopropane','Glycerol react with excess HI to give 2-iodopropane.\nNEET 2010\ndiagram(ne2536)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'3','mcq','2-iodopropane','allyl iodide','propene','glycerol triiodide','NEW','12-347','12-217',NULL),
(250926,'chemistry','Ethylene oxide when treated with Grignard reagent yields.','primary alcohol','Ethylene oxide on reaction with Grignard reagent  primary alcohol.\nNEET 2006','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','primary alcohol','secondary alcohol','tertiary alcohol','cyclopropyl alcohol','NEW','12-331','12-201',NULL),
(250927,'chemistry','Which one of the following compounds is most acidic?\ndiagram(n2537)','c','Aliphatic alcohols are very less acidic than phenol. If NO₂ group is attached with phenol its acidity will increase. because it is electron withdrawing group. similarly CH₃ is electron donating group it makes phenol less acidic.\nNEET 2005','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'2','mcq','a','b','c','d','NEW','12-337','12-207','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250927q.png'),
(250928,'chemistry','Which one of the following will not form a yellow precipitate on heating with an alkaline solution of iodine?','CH₃OH','It is an example of iodoform test and this test is given by those alcohols which have CH₃CH(OH)– group. methyl alcohol do not give this test.\nNEET 2004','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','CH₃CH(OH)CH₃','CH₃CH₂CH(OH)CH₃','CH₃OH','CH₃CH₂OH','NEW','12-343','12-213','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/250928q.png'),
(250929,'chemistry','n-propyl alcohol and isopropyl alcohol  can be chemically distinguished by which reagent?','Oxidation with potassium dichromate','n-propyl alcohol and Isopropyl alcohol both oxidise by potassium dichromate but former give aldehyde and latter give ketone upon reaction.\nNEET 2002','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','PCl₅','Reduction','Oxidation with potassium dichromate','Ozonolysis','NEW','12-339','12-209','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/250929q.png'),
(250930,'chemistry','When phenol is treated with CHCl₃ and NaOH, the product formed is','salicylaldehyde','It is an example of Reimer-Tiemann reaction.\nNEET 2002\ndiagram(ne2538)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','benzaldehyde','salicylaldehyde','salicylic acid','benzoic acid','NEW','12-343','12-213',NULL),
(250931,'chemistry','Which of the following is correct?','Alcoholic iodine with NaOH gives iodoform.','On reduction, any aldehyde gives primary alcohol. Glycerine is produced by saponification. Glucose and NaCl do not react.\nNEET 2001','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','On reduction, any aldehyde gives secondary alcohol.','Reaction of vegetable oil with H2SO4 gives glycerine.','Alcoholic iodine with NaOH gives iodoform.','Sucrose on reaction with NaCl gives invert sugar.','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(250932,'chemistry','When 3,3-dimethyl-2-butanol is heated with H₂SO₄, the major product obtained is','2,3-dimethyl-2-butene','In the first step protonation of alcohol takes place which followed by formation of tertiary carbocation through dehydration. In the final step dehydrogenation of tertiary carbocation produces 2,3-dimethyl-2-butene.\nNEET 1995','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'2','mcq','2,3-dimethyl-2-butene','cis and trans isomers of 2,3-dimethyl-2-butene','2,3-dimethyl-1-butene','3,3-dimethyl-1-butene','NEW','12-340','12-210',NULL),
(251001,'chemistry','Which of the following is an appropriate set of reactants for the preparation of 1-methoxy-4-nitrobenzene?\ndiagram(n2562)','b',NULL,'Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Examplar Based Advanced Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','a','b','c','d','NEW','12-345','12-215','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/251001q.png'),
(251002,'chemistry','The cleavage of C-O bond in ethers takes place under drastic conditions with excess of__________.','hydrogen halides','The reaction of phenol with Br2 depends on the solvent system. If the polar solvent is used then bromination occurs at all the ortho and para positions.','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Examplar Based Advanced Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','sulfuric acid','alkyl halides','hydrogen halides','aluminium chloride','NEW','12-347','12-217',NULL),
(251003,'chemistry','Cleavage of C-O bond in ethers takes place with HBr and HI because these reagents are sufficiently______','acidic',NULL,'Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Examplar Based Advanced Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','basic','acidic','neutral','amphoteric','NEW','12-347','12-217',NULL),
(251004,'chemistry','What product will form when ethyl methyl ether react with HI at room temperature?','methyl iodide and ethyl alcohol','If a solvent is non-polar like CS2 or CHCl3 (CHCl3 has a dipole moment of 1.08 D)then bromination at only at the ortho or para position.','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Examplar Based Advanced Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','ethyl iodide and methyl alcohol','water and ethyl iodide','water and methyl iodide','methyl iodide and ethyl alcohol','NEW','12-347','12-217',NULL),
(251005,'chemistry','Select the correct option(s) regarding  following statements which explain about " Ethers reaction with hydrogen halides",Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:\n\na) Ethers react with excess HI at high temperature yield two molecule of alkyl iodide.\nb) Reactivity of hydrogen halides towards ethers is in order of HCl> HBr> HI.\nc) When one of the alkyl group of ether is tertiary then reaction with hydrogen halide follows Sɴ1 mechanism.\nd) The reaction of an ether with concentrated HI starts with protonation of ether molecule.','a,c and d','When HI is in excess and the reaction is carried out at high temperature, ethanol reacts with another molecule of HI and is converted to ethyl iodide. \nWhen one of the alkyl group of ether is tertiary then reaction with hydrogen halide follows Sɴ1 mechanism. \nThe reaction of an ether with concentrated HI starts with protonation of ether molecule.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 347; Paragraph No. 3, Page 348; Paragraph No. 1,2)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Examplar Based Advanced Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','Both a and b','Both c and d','a,c and d','only a','NEW','12-347','12-217',NULL),
(251006,'chemistry','The solubility of ethers resembles that of______.:','Alcohols','The miscibility of ethers with water resembles those of alcohols of the same molecular mass\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 347; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Examplar Based Advanced Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','Phenols','Alcohols','Ketones','Aldehyde','NEW','12-347','12-217',NULL),
(151404,'chemistry','A : In Schottky defect, density of crystal decreases.\n\nR : Equal number of cations and anions are missing in Schottky defect.','Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A.','In Schottky defect density decreases because equal number of cations and equal number of anions are missing\n i.e., A & R → true and correct explanation.','Physical chemistry >> Solid state >> Assertion and Reason Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A.','Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A.','A is true but R is false.','Both A and R are false.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(251007,'chemistry','Given Below are two statements: one is labelled as Assertion (A) and other is labelled as Reason (R).\nAssertion (A):Both ethoxyethane and butan-1-ol are miscible to almost the same extent.\nReason (R): The solubility of alcohols and ethers is same because both can form hydrogen bonding with water.','Both (A) and (R) are correct and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).','Both ethoxyethane and butan-1-ol are miscible to almost the same extent i.e., 7.5 and 9 g per 100 mL water, respectively. This is due to the fact that just like alcohols, oxygen of ether can also form hydrogen bonds with water molecule.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 347; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Examplar Based Advanced Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Both (A) and (R) are correct but (R) is not the correct explanation of (A).','(A) is correct but (R) is not correct.','Both (A) and (R) are correct and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).','(A) is not correct but (R) is correct.','NEW','12-347','12-217',NULL),
(251008,'chemistry','The major products that are formed by heating following with HI.\ndiagram(n2563)','d','In this reaction the attack by I⁻ ion breaks O–CH₃  bond to form CH₃I. Phenols do not react further to give halides because the sp² hybridised carbon of phenol cannot undergo nucleophilic substitution reaction needed for conversion to the halide.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 348; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Examplar Based Advanced Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','a','b','c','d','NEW','12-348','12-218','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/251008q.png'),
(251009,'chemistry','The major product of bromination of anisole','p-bromoanisole','The major product of bromination of anisole is p-bromoanisole,\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 349; Paragraph No. 4)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Examplar Based Advanced Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','p-bromoanisole','o-bromoanisole','m-bromoanisole','p-bromophenol','NEW','12-349','12-219',NULL),
(251010,'chemistry','Anisole undergoes bromination with bromine in ethanoic acid even in the absence of_________.','iron (III) bromide','anisole undergoes bromination with bromine in ethanoic acid even in the absence of iron (III) bromide catalyst. It is due to the activation of benzene ring by the methoxy group. \n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 349; Paragraph No. 4)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Examplar Based Advanced Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','iron (III) bromide','iron (II) bromide','aluminium (III) bromide','both a and b','NEW','12-349','12-219',NULL),
(251011,'chemistry','The percentage yield of p-bromoanisole in the following reaction is.\ndiagram(n2564)','0.9','Phenylalkyl ethers undergo usual halogenation in the benzene ring, e.g., anisole undergoes bromination with bromine in ethanoic acid even in the absence of iron (III) bromide catalyst. It is due to the activation of benzene ring by the methoxy group. Para isomer is obtained in 90% yield.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 349; Paragraph No. 4)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Examplar Based Advanced Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','0.8','0.85','0.9','0.95','NEW','12-349','12-219','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/251011q.png'),
(251012,'chemistry','In anisole during Friedel-Crafts reaction alkyl and acyl group are introduce at_______','ortho and para','Anisole undergoes Friedel-Crafts reaction, i.e., the alkyl and acyl groups are introduced at ortho and para positions. \n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 350; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Examplar Based Advanced Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','para and meta','ortho and para','meta and ortho','only at para','NEW','12-350','12-220',NULL),
(251013,'chemistry','What will be the major product in following reaction.\ndiagram(n2565)','4-methoxytoluene','Anisole undergoes Friedel-Crafts reaction, i.e., the alkyl and acyl groups are introduced at ortho and para positions by reaction with alkyl halide and acyl halide in the presence of anhydrous aluminium chloride (a Lewis acid) as catalyst.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 350; Paragraph No. 1)\ndiagram(ne2501)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Examplar Based Advanced Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','4-methoxytoluene','2-methoxytoluene','2-methoxyacetophenon','4-methoxyacetophenon','NEW','12-350','12-220','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/251013q.png'),
(251014,'chemistry','select the correct option(s) from the following statements which explain about " Anisole",\n\na) Anisole undergoes bromination with bromine in ethanoic acid even in the absence of iron (III) bromide catalyst.\nb) In anisole bond between O-CH₃ is stronger than O-C₆H₅.\nc) The -OCH₃ group in anisole is ortho and para directing.\nd) Anisole undergo halogination through electrophilic substitution reaction.\nChoose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:','a, c and d','Anisole undergoes bromination with bromine in ethanoic acid even in the absence of iron (III) bromide catalyst.\nThe bond between O–CH3  is weaker than the bond between O–C6H5 because the carbon of phenyl group is sp2 hybridised and there is a partial double bond character.\nThe alkoxy group (-OR) is ortho, para directing and activates the aromatic ring towards electrophilic substitution in the same way as in phenol.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 348; Paragraph No. 6, page 349; Paragrapgh No.3, 4 )','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Examplar Based Advanced Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','Both a and b','Both c and d','a, c and d','a, b and d','NEW','12-349','12-219',NULL),
(251101,'chemistry','Which of them will not be formed during the Hydroboration-oxidation of CH₃CH=CH₂ ?','CH₃CH₂CH₃','Diborane (BH₃)₂ reacts with alkenes to give trialkyl boranes as addition product. This is oxidised to alcohol to hydrogen peroxide in the presence of aqueous sodium hydroxide.\n\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 330; Paragraph No. 1). Refer diagram(ne2578)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Named Reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','CH₃CH₂CH₂BH₂','(CH₃CH₂CH₂)₂BH','CH₃CH₂CH₃','(CH₃CH₂CH₂)₃B','NEW','12-330','12-200',NULL),
(251102,'chemistry','The given reaction diagram(n2595) will undergo?','Kolbe reaction','Kolbe’s Reaction – Treating phenol with sodium hydroxide generates phenoxide ion. The mechanism of Kolbe reaction proceeds through the nucleophilic addition of phenoxide to carbon dioxide, yielding the salicylate. (Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 342; Paragraph No. 3).Refer diagram(ne2579)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Named Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','Schimdt reaction','Kolbe reaction','Riemer Tieman reaction','Claisen reaction','NEW','12-343','12-213','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/251102q.png'),
(251103,'chemistry','The intermediate formed during Reimer - Tieman reaction is:','Benzal chloride','On treating phenol with chloroform in the presence of sodium hydroxide, a –CHO group is introduced at ortho position of benzene ring. This reaction is known as Reimer - Tiemann reaction.\n\nThe intermediate substituted benzal chloride is hydrolysed in the presence of alkali to produce salicylaldehyde.\n\n (Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 343; Paragraph No. 1). Refer diagram(ne2580)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Named Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','Benzal chloride','Benzyl chloride','Benzochloride','Salicylaldehyde','NEW','12-343','12-213',NULL),
(251104,'chemistry','The given reaction diagram(n2596) will undergo?','Riemer Tieman reaction','On treating phenol with chloroform in the presence of sodium hydroxide, a –CHO group is introduced at ortho position of benzene ring. This reaction is known as Reimer - Tiemann reaction.\n\nThe intermediate substituted benzal chloride is hydrolysed in the presence of alkali to produce salicylaldehyde.\n\n (Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 343; Paragraph No. 1). Refer diagram(ne2580)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Named Reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','Schimdt reaction','Kolbe reaction','Riemer Tieman reaction','Claisen reaction','NEW','12-343','12-213','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/251104q.png'),
(251105,'chemistry','Which of them is not true for Williamson synthesis?','Alkyl halide reacts with sodium alkali','Williamson synthesis, It is an important laboratory method for the preparation of symmetrical and unsymmetrical ethers. In this method, an alkyl halide is allowed to react with sodium alkoxide.\n\nIn case of seconday and tertiary alkali halides, elimation competes over substitution. If a tertiary alkyl halide is used, an alkene is the only reaction product and no ether is formed.\n\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 345; Paragraph No. 6)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Named Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','Lab method for preparation of symmetrical ether','Lab method for preparation of unsymmetrical ether','Alkyl halide reacts with sodium alkali','In case of seconday and tertiary alkali halides, elimation competes over substitution.','NEW','12-345','12-215',NULL),
(251106,'chemistry','Which of the following is not an appropriate reaction for the preparation of t-butyl ethyl ether ? Refer diagram(n2597)','b','The major product of (a) will be 2-methylpropene because sodium ethoxide is a strong nucleophile as well as base. Thus elimination reaction predominates over substitution.\n\n(b) will form form t-butyl ethyl ether as shown in the diagram(ne2581)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Named Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','a','b','both a and b','neither a nor b','NEW','12-340','12-210','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/251106q.png'),
(251107,'biology','The difference between spermiogenesis and spermiation is [NEET 2018]','In spermiogenesis spermatozoa are formed, while in spermiation spermatozoa are released from Sertoli cells into the cavity of seminiferous tubules.','Formation of spermatozoa from spermatids is called spermiogenesis. After spermiogenesis, sperm heads become embedded in the Sertoli cells and are finally released from the seminiferous tubules by the process called spermiation. Reference  : NCERT Page46','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 1',NULL,'3','mcq','In spermiogenesis spermatids are formed, while in spermiation spermatozoa are formed','In spermiogenesis spermatozoa are formed, while in spermiation spermatids are formed','In spermiogenesis spermatozoa from Sertoli cells are released into the cavity of seminiferous tubules, while in spermiation spermatozoa are formed','In spermiogenesis spermatozoa are formed, while in spermiation spermatozoa are released from Sertoli cells into the cavity of seminiferous tubules.','NEW','12-046','12-030',NULL),
(251108,'biology','Which of the following layers in an antral follicle is acellular? [AIPMT 2015]','Zona pellucida','Zona pellucida in an antral follicle is acellular, meaning it is not made of cells. The zona pellucida is a glycoprotein layer surrounding the plasma membrane of mammalian oocytes. It is a vital constitutive part of the oocyte.\nThe granulosa, theca interna and stroma layers are all made of cells and hence are cellular in nature.','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 1',NULL,'3','mcq','Stroma','Zona pellucida','Granulosa','Theca interna','NEW','12-051','12-035',NULL),
(251109,'biology','Which of the following cells during gametogenesis is normally diploid? [AIPMT 2015 Cancelled]','Spermatogonia','Spermatogonia are diploid germ cells of seminiferous tubules that undergo mitosis to form the primary spermatocytes. These primary spermatocytes are coverted to haploid sperms by meiotic division. \n Reference  : NCERT Page 49','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 1',NULL,'3','mcq','Spermatogonia','Secondary polar body','Primary polar body','Spermatid','NEW','12-049','12-033',NULL),
(251110,'biology','What is the correct sequence of sperm formation? [AIPMT 2013]','Spermatogonia, spermatocytes, spermatids, spermatozoa','Spermatogenesis is the process of formation of haploid spermatozoa (sperms) from diploid spermatogonia inside the testes of the male. At sexual maturity, the undifferentiated primordial germ cells divide several times by mitosis to produce a large number of spermatogonia or sperm mother cells. Each spermatogonium actively grows to a larger primary spermatocyte by obtaining nourishment from the nursing cells. The phenomenon of formation of primary spermatocytes from spermatogonia, is called spermatocytogenesis. Each primary spermatocyte undergoes two successive divisions, called maturation divisions. The first maturation division is reductional or meiotic. Hence, the primary spermatocyte divides into two haploid daughter cells called secondary spermatocytes. Both secondary spermatocytes now undergo second maturation division which is called second meiotic division (meiosis II) to form four haploid spermatids, by each primary spermatocyte. The transformation of spermatids into spermatozoa is called spermiogenesis or spermateleosis or differentiation phase. Referencde: NCERT Page 50','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 1',NULL,'3','mcq','Spermatogonia, spermatozoa, spermatocytes, spermatids','Spermatogonia, spermatocytes, spermatids, spermatozoa','Spermatids, spermatocytes, spermatogonia, spermatozoa','Spermatogonia, spermatocytes, spermatozoa, spermatids','NEW','12-050','12-034',NULL),
(251111,'biology','Which of the following hormone levels will cause release of ovum (ovulation) from the Graffian follicle? [NEET 2020]','High concentration of Estrogen','FSH, LH and estrogen are at peak during ovulation (release of ovum).Reference  : NCERT Page50','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 1',NULL,'3','mcq','High concentration of Estrogen','High concentration of Progesterone','Low concentration of LH','Low concentration of FSH','NEW','12-050','12-034',NULL),
(251112,'biology','No new follicles develop in the luteal phase of the menstrual cycle because [NEET 2019]','Both FSH and LH levels are low in the luteal phase.','Both FSH and LH levels are low in the luteal phase. Reference  : NCERT Page 50','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 1',NULL,'3','mcq','Follicles do not remain in the ovary after ovulation','FSH levels are high in the luteal phase','LH levels are high in the luteal phase','Both FSH and LH levels are low in the luteal phase.','NEW','12-050','12-034',NULL),
(251113,'biology','Changes in GnRH pulse frequency in females is controlled by circulating levels of [NEET-I 2016]','Estrogen and progesterone','GnRH is secreted by the hypothalamus which stimulates the anterior lobe of pituitary gland to secrete luteinising hormone (LH) and follicle stimulating hormone (FSH). FSH stimulates the growth of the ovarian follicles and stimulates the formation of estrogens. LH stimulates the corpus luteum to secrete progesterone. Rising levels of progesterone and estrogen inhibits the release of GnRH, which in turn, inhibits the production of FSH and LH','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 1',NULL,'3','mcq','Progesterone only','Progesterone and inhibin','Estrogen and progesterone','Estrogen and inhibin','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(251114,'biology','Select the incorrect statement [NEET-I 2016]','LH and FSH decrease gradually during the follicular phase.','During follicular phase, FSH secretion increases. Follicular phase (proliferative phase) usually includes cycle days 6-13 or 14 in a 28 days cycle. The follicle stimulating hormone (FSH) secreted by the anterior lobe of the pituitary gland stimulates the ovarian follicle to secrete estrogen. Reference  : NCERT Page 50','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 1',NULL,'3','mcq','LH and FSH decrease gradually during the follicular phase.','LH triggers secretion of androgens from the Leydig cells.','FSH stimulates the Sertoli cells which help in spermiogenesis.','LH triggers ovulation in ovary.','NEW','12-050','12-034',NULL),
(251115,'biology','Identify the correct statement on ‘inhibin’. [NEET-I 2016]','Is produced by granulosa cells in ovary and inhibits the secretion of FSH','FSH acts on the Sertoli cells and stimulates secretion of some factors which help in the process of spermiogenesis.FSH and LH act on specific membrane receptors in granulosa cells and theca cells of the ovary, stimulating follicular growth and hormone synthesis. The peptide hormone inhibin is synthesized and secreted by granulosa cells and specifically inhibits FSH synthesis and secretion by the pituitary. So, the correct option is "is produced by granulosa cells in ovary and inhibits the secretion of FSH". Reference  : NCERT Page 47','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 1',NULL,'3','mcq','Is produced by granulosa cells in ovary and inhibits the secretion of LH','Is produced by nurse cells in testes and inhibits the secretion of LH','Inhibits the secretion of LH, FSH and prolactin','Is produced by granulosa cells in ovary and inhibits the secretion of FSH','NEW','12-047','12-031',NULL),
(251116,'biology','Which of the following events is not associated with ovulation in human female? [AIPMT 2015]','Decrease in estradiol','In human females, ovulation is the release of secondary oocyte from the ovary at about 14th day of the menstrual cycle. Both LH and FSH attain a peak level during this period. Rapid secretion of LH induces rupturing of fully developed Graafian follicle and thereby release of ovum. LH surge is actually responsible for ovulation. Reference  : NCERT Page 51','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 1',NULL,'3','mcq','Release of secondary oocyte','LH surge','Decrease in estradiol','Full development of Graafian follicle','NEW','12-051','12-035',NULL),
(251117,'biology','The main function of mammalian corpus luteum is to produce [AIPMT 2014]','Progesterone','Corpus luteum secretes progesterone to make uterus suitable for implantation (in case fertilisation occurs) and its maintenance (mainly endometrium).  Reference  : NCERT Page 51','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 1',NULL,'3','mcq','Estrogen only','Progesterone','Human chorionic gonadotropin','Relaxin only.','NEW','12-051','12-035',NULL),
(251118,'biology','Menstrual flow occurs due to lack of [AIPMT 2013]','Progesterone','The corpus luteum secretes large amount of progesterone which is essential for maintenance of the endometrium necessary for implantation of the fertilized ovum and other events of pregnancy. In the absence of fertilization, the corpus luteum degenerates. This causes disintegration of the endometrium leading to menstruation. The menstrual flow results due to breakdown of endometrial lining of the uterus and its blood vessels which forms liquid that comes out through vagina. Reference  : NCERT Page 51','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 1',NULL,'3','mcq','Oxytocin','Vasopressin','Progesterone','FSH.','NEW','12-051','12-035',NULL),
(251201,'chemistry','Which of the following reaction will not form primary alcohol? Refer diagram(n2598)','b','Ketones on reduction will form secondary alcohols. Refer diagram(ne2582)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','a','b','c','d','NEW','12-339','12-209','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/251201q.png'),
(251202,'chemistry','The product formed on acidification of sodium phenoxide will be?','Phenol','Chlorobenzene is fused with NaOH at 623K and 320 atmospheric pressure. Phenol is obtained by acidificationof sodium phenoxide so produced.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 332; Paragraph No. 1). Refer diagram(ne2583)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','Benzene diazonium chloride','Phenol','Benzene','Bezaldehyde','NEW','12-332','12-202',NULL),
(251203,'chemistry','Which of them will not be formed in the reaction ? Refer diagram(n25100)','H₂O','Diazonium salts are hydrolysed to phenols by warming with water or by treating with dilute acids.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 332; Paragraph No. 2). Refer diagram(ne2584)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','Phenol','N₂','HCl','H₂O','NEW','12-332','12-202','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/251203q.png'),
(251204,'chemistry','The product formed on oxidation of isopropylbenzene in the presence of air is?','Cumene hydroperoxide','Phenol is manufactured from the hydrocarbon, cumene(isopropyl benzene).\nCumene is oxidised in the presence of air to cumene hydroperoxide. It is converted to phenol and acetone by treating it with dilute acid.\n\nAcetone, a by-product of this reaction, is also obtained in large quanitities by this method.\n\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 332; Paragraph No. 4). Refer diagram(ne2585)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','Acetone','Phenol','Cumene','Cumene hydroperoxide','NEW','12-332','12-202',NULL),
(251205,'chemistry','Select the incorrect statement with respect to production of Phenol from cumene','Cumene is oxidised to cumene peroxide in the presence of air','Phenol is manufactured from the hydrocarbon, cumene(isopropyl benzene).\nCumene is oxidised in the presence of air to cumene hydroperoxide. It is converted to phenol and acetone by treating it with dilute acid.\n\nAcetone, a by-product of this reaction, is also obtained in large quanitities by this method.\n\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 332; Paragraph No. 4). Refer diagram(ne2585)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','Most of the worldwide production of phenol is from cumene.','Cumene is oxidised to cumene peroxide in the presence of air','Acetone is obtained in large quantities','Cumene is a hydrocarbon','NEW','12-332','12-202',NULL),
(251206,'chemistry','ROH + RCOCl in the presence of pyridine will form','ROCOR +  HCl','The reaction with acid chloride is carried out in the presence of a base (pyridine) so as to neutralise HCl which is formed during the reaction.\n\nIt shifts the equillibrium to the right hand side..\n\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 338; Paragraph No. 4)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','ROCOR +  HCl','ROH + HCl','RCOCl + HCl','ROCOR +  H₂O','NEW','12-338','12-208',NULL),
(251207,'chemistry','Which of them is not formed during the reaction? Refer diagram(n25101)\n\na. CH₃COOH\nb. Acetylsalicylic acid\nc. CH₃OH\nd. CH₃CHO','c,d','Acetylation of salicylic acid produces aspirin.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 338; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','CH₃COOH, Acetylsalycilic acid','Acetylsalycilicacid,  CH₃OH','CH₃OH, CH₃CHO','CH₃COOH,CH₃CHO','NEW','12-338','12-208','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/251207q.png'),
(251208,'chemistry','The product formed in the given reaction diagram(n25102)','Propene','Secondary and tertiary alcohols are dehyrated under milder conditions\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 339; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','Propene','Propanoic acid','Propanal','Propane','NEW','12-339','12-209','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/251208q.png'),
(251209,'chemistry','The product formed in the given reaction diagram(n25103)','CH₃-CH=CH-CHO','A better reagent for oxidation of primary alcohols to aldehydes in good yield is pyridinium chlorochromate (PCC).\n\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 340; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','CH₃-CH=CH-CHO','CH₃-CH=CH-CH₂OH','CH₃-CH₂CH₂-CHO','CH₃-CH=CH-COOH','NEW','12-340','12-210','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/251209q.png'),
(251210,'chemistry','Which of the following reaction will form an alkene? Refer diagram(n25104)','c','When the vapours of primary or  secondary alcohol are passed over heated copper at 573 K, dehydrogenation takes place and aldehyde or ketone is formed.\n\nTertiary alcohols undergo dehydration forming alkenes\n\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 340; Paragraph No. 5). Refer diagram(ne2586)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','a','b','c','both b and c','NEW','12-340','12-210','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/251210q.png'),
(251211,'chemistry','Which of the following reaction will form picric acid? Refer diagram(n25105)','b','With concentrated nitric acid, phenol is converted to 2,4,6-trinitrophenol. The product is commonly known as picric acid.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 341; Paragraph No. 5) Refer diagram(ne2587)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','a','b','c','both a and b','NEW','12-341','12-211','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/251211q.png'),
(251212,'chemistry','The product in the given reaction diagram(n25106) will be:','Benzoquinone','Oxidation of phenol with chromic acid produces a conjugated diketone known as benzoquinone.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 343; Paragraph No. 4). Refer diagram(ne2588)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','Benzene diazonium chloride','Benzene','Benzaldehyde','Benzoquinone','NEW','12-343','12-213','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/251212q.png'),
(251213,'chemistry','Which of the following reaction will not form alcohol? Refer diagram(n25107)','b','The sugar in molasses, sugarcane or fruits such as grapes is converted to glucose and fructose in the presence of an enzyme invertase.\n\nGlucose and fructose undergo fermentation in the presence of another enzyme, zymase, which is found in yeast.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 344; Paragraph No. 3). Refer diagram(ne2589)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','a','b','c','both b and c','NEW','12-344','12-214','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/251213q.png'),
(251214,'chemistry','Which of them will not be formed in the reaction ? Refer diagram(n25108)\n\na. p-Bromoanisole\nb. 2-Methoxytoluene\nc. 2-Nitroanisole','b,c','Anisole undergoes bromination with bromine in ethanoic acid even in the absence of iron (III) bromide catalyst. It is due to the activation of benzene ring by the methoxy group. \n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 349; Paragraph No. 4) Refer diagram(ne2590)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','a','b','b,c','c only','NEW','12-349','12-219','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/251214q.png'),
(251215,'chemistry','The product in the given reaction diagram(n25109) will be:\n\na. 4-Methoxy acetophenone\nb. 4-Methoxy toluene\nc. 4-Bromoanisole\nd.2-Methoxy toluene','a only','Anisole undergoes Friedel-Crafts reaction, i.e., the alkyl and acyl groups are introduced at ortho and para positions. \n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 350; Paragraph No. 1) . Refer diagram(ne2591)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','a only','a,b','b,c','b,c,d','NEW','12-350','12-220','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/251215q.png'),
(251216,'biology','Which of the following are the layers wall of Uterus? \n\ni. Endometrium \nii.Myometrium \niii.Perimetrium \niv.Epimeterium','i, ii and iii','The wall of the uterus has three layers of tissue. The external thin membranous perimetrium, middle thick layer of smooth muscle, myometrium and inner glandular layer called endometrium that\nlines the uterine cavity. Reference  : NCERT Page 46','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 2',NULL,'2','mcq','i, ii and iv','i, ii and iii','ii and iv','iii and iv','NEW','12-046','12-030',NULL),
(251217,'biology','Which part of mammary glands secrete Milk?','Alveoli','Alveoli of the mammary gland secretes milk and it passes through the alveolar ducts, mammary ducts, lactiferous ducts and passes through the nipple','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Alveoli','Nipple','Lactiferous duct','Mammary duct','NEW','12-047','12-031',NULL),
(251218,'biology','Which of the following hormone levels will cause release of ovum (ovulation) from the Graffian follicle? [NEET 2020]','High concentration of Estrogen','FSH, LH and estrogen are at peak during ovulation (release of ovum). Reference  : NCERT Page 47','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 2',NULL,'1','mcq','High concentration of Estrogen','High concentration of Progesterone','Low concentration of LH','Low concentration of FSH','NEW','12-050','12-034',NULL),
(251219,'biology','Match the items given in column I with those in column II','Proliferative phase-Follicular phase,Secretory phase-Luteal phase,Menstruation-Breakdown of endometrial lining','Proliferative phase-Follicular phase,\nSecretory phase-Luteal phase,\nMenstruation-Breakdown of endometrial lining','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 2',NULL,'2','match','Proliferative phase,Follicular phase','Secretory phase,Luteal phase','Menstruation,Breakdown of endometrial lining',NULL,'NEW','12-050','12-034',NULL),
(251220,'biology','Find the correct match:','Bulbourethral glands - Lubrication of penis','Placenta-hCG,\nZona pellucida-Layer of ovum,\nBulbourethral glands-Lubrication of penis,\nLeydig cells-Androgens','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 2',NULL,'1','mcq','Placenta - testosterone','Zona pellucida - Layer of sperm','Bulbourethral glands - Lubrication of penis','Leydig cells - Estrogen','NEW','12-044','12-028',NULL),
(251221,'biology','Hormones secreted by the placenta to maintain pregnancy are [NEET 2018]','hCG, hPL, progestogens, estrogens','Placenta is temporary organ that helps in exchange of gases, nutrients and waste materials between mother and fetus. During pregnancy, placenta acts as an endocrine gland and secretes some hormones such as estrogen, progestogens, human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG), human placental lactogen (hPL), chorionic thyrotropin, chorionic corticotropin and relaxin. Reference  : NCERT Page 50','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 2',NULL,'2','mcq','hCG, hPL, progestogens, prolactin','hCG, hPL, estrogens, relaxin, oxytocin','hCG, hPL, progestogens, estrogens','hCG, progestogens, estrogens, glucocorticoids','NEW','12-050','12-034',NULL),
(100308,'chemistry','Which of the following is the correct magnetic property of superoxides?','Paramagnetic','The superoxides are paramagnetic because of one unpaired electron in π*2p molecular orbital. \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 303; Paragraph 10.2.1)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 1 elements- General Characteristics of Compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Diamagnetic','Paramagnetic','Ferromagnetic','Antiferromagnetic','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(251222,'biology','The amnion of mammalian embryo is derived from [NEET 2018]','Ectoderm and mesoderm','Amnion, in reptiles, birds and mammals is a membrane forming a fluid-filled cavity (the amniotic sac) that encloses the embryo. During development, the amnion arises by a folding of a mass of extra-embryonic tissue called the somatopleure. Lined with ectoderm and covered with mesoderm, the amnion contains a thin transparent fluid in which the embryo is suspended, thus providing a cushion against mechanical injury. Reference  : NCERT Page 54','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Ectoderm and mesoderm','Endoderm and mesoderm','Mesoderm and trophoblast','Ectoderm and endoderm','NEW','12-054','12-038',NULL),
(251223,'biology','Receptors for sperm binding in mammals are present on [NEET 2021]','Zona pellucida','During mammalian fertilization, sperm are believed undergo the acrosome reaction when coming into contact with the extracellular matrix—the zona pellucida—of egg cells. This exposes the Izumo1 receptor on sperm, which is essential for recognition of the egg. Reference  : NCERT Page 53','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 2',NULL,'3','mcq','Zona pellucida','Corona radiata','Vitelline membrane','Perivitelline space','NEW','12-053','12-037',NULL),
(251224,'biology','Which of these is not an important component of initiation of parturition in humans ? [NEET 2021]','Release of Prolactin','Foetal ejection reflex. This triggers release of oxytocin from the maternal pituitary. Oxytocin acts on the uterine muscle and causes stronger uterine contractions, which in turn stimulates further secretion of oxytocin. The stimulatory reflex between the uterine contraction and oxytocin secretion continues resulting in stronger and stronger contractions. Reference  : NCERT Page 54','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 2',NULL,'3','mcq','Release of Prolactin','Increase in estrogen and progesterone ratio','Synthesis of prostaglandins','Release of Oxytocin','NEW','12-054','12-038',NULL),
(251225,'biology','Which of the following secrets the hormone, relaxin, during the later phase of pregnancy?[NEET 2021]','ovary','In the later phase of pregnancy, a hormone called relaxin is also secreted by the ovary. Reference  : NCERT Page 54','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 2',NULL,'3','mcq','Uterus','Graafian follicle','ovary','Foetus','NEW','12-054','12-038',NULL),
(251226,'biology','Which part of sperm contains numerous Mitochondria?','Middle piece','The middle piece possesses numerous mitochondria, which produce energy for the movement of tail that facilitate sperm motility essential for fertilisation. Reference  : NCERT Page 46','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 2',NULL,'3','mcq','Head','Neck','Middle piece','Tail','NEW','12-046','12-030',NULL),
(251227,'biology','All of the following statements concerning pregnancy are accurate EXCEPT [AIPMT 2015]','The cyclic release of pituitary gonadotropins and ovarian steroids is continued during pregnancy','The cyclical changes in the ovary and the uterus during menstrual cycle are induced by changes in the levels of pituitary and ovarian hormones. Reference  : NCERT Page 55','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 2',NULL,'3','mcq','The detection of human chorionic gonadotropin in the urine forms the basis for pregnancy tests.','The cyclic release of pituitary gonadotropins and ovarian steroids is continued during pregnancy','The mammary gland tissue of the pregnant woman is stimulated to develop by placental hormones.','The corpus luteum of pregnancy maintains the uterus until the placenta is well established','NEW','12-055','12-039',NULL),
(251228,'biology','Ejaculation of human male contains about 200 – 300 million sperms, of which for normal fertility ____ % sperms must have normal shape and size and at least ____% must show energetic motility. [AIPMT 2016]','60, 40','Ejaculation of human male contains about 200 – 300 million sperms, of which for normal fertility 60 % sperms must have normal shape and size and at least 40 % must show energetic motility.  Reference  : NCERT Page 44','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 2',NULL,'3','mcq','40, 60','50, 50','60, 40','30, 70','NEW','12-044','12-028',NULL),
(251229,'biology','Which of the following statements are true for spermatogenesis but do not hold true for Oogenesis?\n\n (1) It results in the formation of haploid gametes \n\n(2) Differentiation of gamete occurs after the completion of meiosis \n\n(3) Meiosis occurs continuously in a mitotically dividing stem cell population \n\n(4) It is controlled by the Luteinising hormone (LH) and Follicle Stimulating Hormone (FSH) secreted by the anterior pituitary \n\n(5) It is initiated at puberty\n[NEET 2022]','(2), (3) and (5) only','In both, spermatogenesis and oogenesis haploid gametes are formed. So (1) is true for both.\nThe spermatids are transformed into spermatozoa (sperms) by the process called spermiogenesis. \nHence, (2) is true for spermatogenesis only. Meiosis occurs continuously in a mitotically dividing stem cell population in males but in females, no new oocytes are added till Reproductive age in females, so (3) is true for spermatogenesis only.\nSpermatogenesis and oogenesis both are controlled by LH and FSH secreted by the anterior pituitary. \nHence (4) is true for both.\nSpermatogenesis is a continuous process that begins at puberty. So (5) is true for spermatogenesis. \nOogenesis on the other hand begins during embryonic development of the female.\n\nReference  : NCERT Page 48','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 2',NULL,'3','mcq','(3) and (5) only','(2), (4) and (5) only','(2) and (3) only','(2), (3) and (5) only','NEW','12-048','12-032',NULL),
(251230,'biology','Given below are two statements:\n\nStatement I :\nThe release of sperms into the seminiferous tubules is called spermiation.\n\nStatement II :\nSpermiogenesis is the process of formation of sperms from spermatogonia.\n\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :\n[NEET 2022]','Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect','Statement II is incorrect as the transformation of spermatids into spermatozoa (sperms) are called spermiogenesis. After this, sperm head becomes embedded in \nthe Sertoli cells and are finally released from the seminiferous tubules by the process called spermiation. Hence, Statement I is a correct statement.\nSpermatogenesis is the process of formation of sperms from spermatogonia.\nReference  : NCERT 12th biology, Page 47, paragraph 2','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 2',NULL,'3','mcq','Both Statement I and Statement II are correct','Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect','Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect','Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct','NEW','12-047','12-031',NULL),
(251231,'biology','At which stage of life the oogenesis process is initiated?\n[NEET 2022]','Embryonic development stage','oogenesis is initiated during the embryonic development stage when a couple of million gamete mother cells (oogonia) are formed within each foetal ovary. No more oogonia are formed and added after birth in a human female. At puberty only 60,000 to 80,000 primary follicles are left in each ovary, rest degenerate during the phase from birth to puberty.\nReference  : NCERT 12th biology, Page 48, paragraph no. 3','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 2',NULL,'3','mcq','Puberty','Embryonic development stage','Birth','Adult','NEW','12-048','12-032',NULL),
(251232,'biology','Lippe’s loop is a type of contraceptive used as:\n[NEET 2022]','Non-Medicated IUD','intrauterine device (IUD) presently available as the non medicated IUDs, is Lippe’s loop.\ncopper releasing IUDs are CuT, Cu7 and multiload 375.\ndiaphragms, cervical caps and vaults are included in barrier method \nof contraception.','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 2',NULL,'3','mcq','Cervical barrier','Vault barrier','Copper releasing IUD','Non-Medicated IUD','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(251233,'biology','Given below are two statements regarding \noogenesis: \n Statement I :-\n The primary follicles get surrounded by more layers of granulosa cells, a theca and shows fluid filled \ncavity antrum. Now it is called secondary follicle. \nStatement II :-\n Graffian follicle ruptures to release the secondary oocyte from the ovary by the process called \novulation. \n In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below: [ NEET 2023(Phase 2)]','(2) Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is true','Statement I: The primary follicles get surrounded by more layers of granulosa cells, a theca, and show a fluid-filled cavity called antrum. Now it is called a secondary follicle. Statement II: The Graafian follicle ruptures to release the secondary oocyte from the ovary by the process called ovulation.\n\nStatement I is incorrect because the primary follicle does not develop into a secondary follicle by acquiring more layers of granulosa cells, a theca, and an antrum. Instead, the primary follicle develops into a secondary follicle by growing and maturing, but it does not acquire these additional structures. The development of an antrum and the surrounding layers occur in later stages of follicular development.\n\nStatement II is true. The Graafian follicle, which is a mature follicle, undergoes ovulation, where it ruptures to release the secondary oocyte from the ovary. Ovulation is an important event in oogenesis and is responsible for the release of the egg for potential fertilization.\n\nTherefore, statement I is incorrect, but statement II is true.','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 2',NULL,'1','mcq','(1) Statement I is correct but Statement II is false.','(2) Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is true','(3) Both Statement I and Statement II are true','(4) Both Statement I and Statement II are false.','NEW','12-048','12-032',NULL),
(251234,'biology','Given below are two statements: one is labelled as Assertion A and the other is labelled as Reason R.\nAssertion A: Endometrium is necessary for implantation of blastocyst.\nReason R: In the absence of fertilization, the corpus luteum degenerates that causes disintegration of\nendometrium.\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below: [ NEET 2023]','(1) Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A.','Assertion A is true: The endometrium is indeed necessary for the implantation of the blastocyst, which is the early stage of embryo development. Reason R is also true: In the absence of fertilization, the corpus luteum, which forms from the ovarian follicle after ovulation, degenerates.','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 2',NULL,'1','mcq','(1) Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A.','(2) A is true but R is false.','(3) A is false but R is true.','(4) Both A and R are true and R is the correct expiation of A.','NEW','12-046','12-030',NULL),
(251235,'biology','Given below are two statements:\nStatement I: Vas deferens receives a duct from seminal vesicle and opens into urethra as the ejaculatory\nduct.\nStatement Il: The cavity of the cervix is called cervical canal which along with vagina forms birth canal.\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below: [ NEET 2023]','(4) Both Statement I and Statement II are true.','Vas deferens receives a duct from seminal vesicle and opens into urethra as the ejaculatory duct. Cervical canal + vagina = Birth canal.','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 2',NULL,'1','mcq','(1) Both Statement I and Statement II are false.','(2) Statement I is correct but Statement II is false.','(3) Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is true.','(4) Both Statement I and Statement II are true.','NEW','12-043','12-027',NULL),
(251236,'biology','Given below are two statements : one is labelled as Assertion (A) and the other is labelled as Reason (R). \nAssertion (A) : \n During pregnancy the level of thyroxine is increased in the maternal blood. \nReason (R) : \n Pregnancy is characterised by metabolic changes in the mother. \n In the light of the above statements, choose themost appropriate answer from the options given below :','(1) Both (A) and (R) are correct and (R) is the \ncorrect explanation of (A)','Option (a) is the correct answer because thyroxine is the main hormone that increases the basal metabolic rate in our body. A high metabolic rate is required during pregnancy, so levels of thyroxine increase in pregnant females along with other hormones such as cortisol, progesterone, etc.','Reproduction >> Human Reproduction >> Previous year questions 2',NULL,'1','mcq','(1) Both (A) and (R) are correct and (R) is the \ncorrect explanation of (A)','(2) Both (A) and (R) are correct but (R) is not the correct explanation of (A)','(3) (A) is correct but (R) is not correct','(4) (A) is not correct but (R) is correct','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
