(380212,'biology','Identify the given diagram ? (3801)','Electrostatic Precipitator','An electrostatic precipitator (ESP) is a filtration device that removes fine particles, like dust and smoke, from a flowing gas using the force of an induced electrostatic charge minimally impeding the flow of gases through the unit.','Ecology >> Environmental Issues >> Air Pollution and Control',NULL,'2','mcq','Scrubber','Purifier','Electrostatic Precipitator','Catalytic converter','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/380212q.png'),
(380213,'biology','A brief exposure to _____ dB sound level may damage ear drums thus permanently impairing hearing ability.?','150','A brief exposure to extremely high sound level, 150 dB or more generated by take off of a jet plane or rocket, may damage ear drums thus permanently impairing hearing ability.','Ecology >> Environmental Issues >> Air Pollution and Control',NULL,'2','mcq','50','100','150','200','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(380214,'biology','Some of the Stringent following of laws laid down in relation to noise are ?\n \n i.delimitation of horn-free zones around hospitals and schools\n\n ii. permissible sound-levels of crackers and of loudspeakers\n\n iii.Unlimited timings for playing loudspeakers','ii and i','Stringent following of laws laid down in relation to noise like delimitation of horn-free zones around hospitals and schools, permissible sound-levels of crackers and of loud\\u0002speakers, timings after which loudspeakers cannot be played, etc., need to be enforced to protect ourselves from noise pollution.','Ecology >> Environmental Issues >> Air Pollution and Control',NULL,'2','mcq','i only','ii and  iii','ii and i','i, ii and iii','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(380215,'biology','All the buses in Delhi were converted to run on ______  by the end of 2002?','Compressed natural gas','All the buses of Delhi were converted to run on CNG by the end of 2002.','Ecology >> Environmental Issues >> Air Pollution and Control',NULL,'2','mcq','Diesel','Petrol','Compressed natural gas','Liquified Petroleum Gas','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(380216,'biology','What is not a benefit of CNG?','Distribution points/pumps need to be setup to ensure uninterrupted supply.','CNG burns(combustion) most efficiently, unlike petrol or diesel, in automobiles and very little of it is left unburnt. Moreover, CNG is cheaper than petrol or diesel, cannot be siphoned off by thieves and adulterated like petrol or diesel. The main problem with switching over to CNG is the difficulty of laying down pipelines to deliver CNG through distribution points/ pumps and ensuring uninterrupted supply.','Ecology >> Environmental Issues >> Air Pollution and Control',NULL,'2','mcq','Low chances of adulteration','High combustion efficiency','Cheaper than petrol/deisel','Distribution points/pumps need to be setup to ensure uninterrupted supply.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(380217,'biology','Euro III norms stipulate controlling of which of the following air pollutant?','Sulphur','Euro III norms,stipulate that sulphur be controlled at 350parts-per-million (ppm) in diesel and 150 ppm in petrol','Ecology >> Environmental Issues >> Air Pollution and Control',NULL,'2','mcq','Sulphur','CO₂','Carbon monoxide','Nitrogen','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
