(380309,'biology','Thermal waste water eliminates or reduces the number of organisms sensitive to?','High temperature','Thermal wastewater eliminates or reduces the number of organisms sensitive to high temperature, and may enhance the growth of plants and fish in extremely cold areas but, only after causing damage to the indigenous flora and fauna.','Ecology >> Environmental Issues >> Water pollution and its control',NULL,'3','mcq','High temperature','Low temperature','Moderate temperature','Specific temperature','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(380310,'biology','Presence of large amounts of nutrients in waters also causes excessive growth of _______ (free floating) algae.','Planktonic','Presence of large amounts of nutrients in waters also causes excessive growth of planktonic (free floating) algae, called algal bloom.','Ecology >> Environmental Issues >> Water pollution and its control',NULL,'2','mcq','Planktonic','Diatoms','Zooplankton','Blue green','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(380311,'biology','Micro-organisms involved in the biodegradation of organic matter in the receiving water body consumes a lot of _________?','Oxygen','Micro-organisms involved in biodegradation of organic matter in the receiving water body consume a lot of oxygen, and as a result there is a sharp decline in dissolved O₂ downstream from the point of sewage discharge.','Ecology >> Environmental Issues >> Water pollution and its control',NULL,'1','mcq','Nitrogen','CO₂','Hydrogen','Oxygen','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(380312,'biology','Pollutants from man’s activities like effluents from the industries and homes can radically accelerate the aging process. This phenomenon has been called?','Accelerated Eutrophication','Pollutants from man’s activities like effluents from the industries and homes can radically accelerate the aging process. This phenomenon has been called Cultural or Accelerated Eutrophication','Ecology >> Environmental Issues >> Water pollution and its control',NULL,'1','mcq','Step Euphotrication','Accelerated Eutrophication','Deccelerated Eutrophication','Cryopathic Eutrophication','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(380313,'biology','In the past century, lakes in many parts of the earth have been severely eutrophied by? \n\ni.sewage \n\nii.agricultural wastes \n\niii. industrial wastes','i, ii  and iii','During the past century, lakes in many parts of the earth have been severely eutrophied by sewage and agricultural and industrial wastes','Ecology >> Environmental Issues >> Water pollution and its control',NULL,'1','mcq','i only','i and ii','ii only','i, ii  and iii','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(380314,'biology','Find the incorrect statements about contaminants like nitrates and phosphates?','They cause enrichment of aquatic plantys and in turn improve aquatic life','The prime contaminants are nitrates and phosphates, which act as plant nutrients. They overstimulate the growth of algae, causing unsightly scum and unpleasant odours, and robbing the water of dissolved O₂ vital to other aquatic life. At the same time, other pollutants flowing into a lake may poison whole populations of fish, whose decomposing remains further deplete the water’s dissolved O₂ content. In such fashion, a lake can literally choke to death.','Ecology >> Environmental Issues >> Water pollution and its control',NULL,'1','mcq','They act as plant nutrients and robbing the water of dissolved O₂ vital to other aquatic life','They overstimulate the growth of algae','They causing unsightly scum and unpleasant odours','They cause enrichment of aquatic plantys and in turn improve aquatic life','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(380315,'biology','Arcata Marsh is located at ________, and is an integrated project with _____________. Select the options respectively','Northern coast of California, Humboldt State University','Wastewater including sewage can be treated in an integrated manner, by utilising a mix of artificial and natural processes. An example of such an initiative is the town of Arcata, situated along the northern coast of California. Collaborating with biologists from the Humboldt State University, the townspeople created an integrated waste water treatment process within a natural system.','Ecology >> Environmental Issues >> Water pollution and its control',NULL,'1','mcq','Northern coast of California, Humboldt State University','Southern coast of California, Humboldt State University','Northern coast of California, Harvard University','Southern coast of California, Oxford University','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(380316,'biology','Friends of the Arcata Marsh (FOAM) are associated with','Integrated Waste Water Treatment','A citizens group called Friends of the Arcata Marsh (FOAM) are responsible for the upkeep and safeguarding Integrated Waste Water Treatment of arcata','Ecology >> Environmental Issues >> Water pollution and its control',NULL,'1','mcq','Integrated Waste Water Treatment','Air Pollution Clearance','Radioactive waste Clearance','Hospital waste management','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
