(380508,'biology','A lake which is rich in organic waste may result in (NEET 2016)','Mortality of fish due to lack of oxygen','High amount of organic waste in a lake will trigger and activate decomposer microbes which will decompose organic waste. Biochemical O₂ Demand (BOD) of this lake will shoot up and decomposers will utilise the most of dissolved O₂ present in lake. Consequently the level of dissolved O₂ will go down to alarming extent. Aquatic animals like fish which totally depend on the O₂ dissolved in the water will ultimately die.','Ecology >> Environmental Issues >> Agro-chemicals and their Effects',NULL,'2','mcq','Increased population of aquatic organisms due to minerals','Drying of lake due to algal bloom','Increased population of fishes due to lots of nutrients','Mortality of fish due to lack of oxygen','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
