(380602,'biology','What are the inherent problems caused by nuclear energy ?\n \ni. accidental leakage\n\nii. increased secondary pollution\n\niii. absence of safe disposal methods','i and iii','Initially, nuclear energy was hailed as a non-polluting way for generating electricity. Later on, it was realised that the use of nuclear energy has two very serious inherent problems. The first is accidental leakage, as occurred in the Three Mile Island and Chernobyl incidents and the second is safe disposal of radioactive wastes.','Ecology >> Environmental Issues >> Radioactive Wastes, Greenhouse effect and Global Warming',NULL,'3','mcq','i and iii','ii only','i, ii, iii','ii  and  iii','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
