(380805,'biology','Fertile top soil erosion can be prevented by ?','By planting cover crops off-season','Fertile top-soil takes centuries. But, it can be removed very easily due to human activities like over-cultivation, unrestricted grazing, deforestation and poor irrigation practices, resulting in arid patches of land. But by planting cover crops during off season instead of leaving the land barren, we can reduce and stop soil erosion.','Ecology >> Environmental Issues >> Degradation by Improper Resource Utilisation and Maintenance',NULL,'1','mcq','Deforestation following Aforestation','Over-cultivation of crops in crop seasons','Unrestricted grazing','By planting cover crops off-season','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(380806,'biology','When large barren patches extend and meet over time, a ____  is created.','Desert','When large barren patches extend and meet over time, a desert is created, as the dry patches come together and cover large stretches of land','Ecology >> Environmental Issues >> Degradation by Improper Resource Utilisation and Maintenance',NULL,'1','mcq','Desert','Pond','Hill','River','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
