(260617,'biology','Which of the following is one of the safest method of birth control?','Sterilisation Techniques','Sterilisation Technique is the safest method of contraception as it prevents the occurance of any further pregnancies.','Reproduction >> Reproductive Health >> Birth control and Surgical Methods',NULL,'1','mcq','The Rhythm Method','Sterilisation Techniques','Use of Physical Barriers','Termination of unwanted pregnancy','NEW','12-062','12-046',NULL),
(260701,'chemistry','Give the IUPAC names of the following compound given in diagram(n26044)','3-phenyl propanoic acid','In the IUPAC system, aliphatic carboxylic acids are named by replacing the ending –e in the name of the corresponding alkane with – oic acid. \n\nIn numbering the carbon chain, the carboxylic carbon is numbered one. \n\nFor naming compounds containing more than one carboxyl group, the alkyl chain leaving carboxyl groups is numbered and the number of carboxyl groups is indicated by adding the multiplicative prefix, dicarboxylic acid, tricarboxylic acid, etc. to the name of parent alkyl chain.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-374 Paragraph -3)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Nomenclature and Structure of Carboxyl Group',NULL,'3','mcq','3-phenyl propanoic acid','3-methyl but-2-en-1-oic acid','2-methyl cyclopentane carboxylic acid','2, 4, 6-trinitrobenzoic acid','NEW','12-374','12-244','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/260701q.png'),
(260702,'chemistry','Give the IUPAC names of the following compound given in diagram(n26045)','3-methyl but-2-en-1-oic acid','In the IUPAC system, aliphatic carboxylic acids are named by replacing the ending –e in the name of the corresponding alkane with – oic acid.\n \nIn numbering the carbon chain, the carboxylic carbon is numbered one. \n\nFor naming compounds containing more than one carboxyl group, the alkyl chain leaving carboxyl groups is numbered and the number of carboxyl groups is indicated by adding the multiplicative prefix, dicarboxylic acid, tricarboxylic acid, etc. to the name of parent alkyl chain.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-374 Paragraph -3)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Nomenclature and Structure of Carboxyl Group',NULL,'3','mcq','3-phenyl propanoic acid','3-methyl but-2-en-1-oic acid','2-methyl cyclopentane carboxylic acid','2, 4, 6-trinitrobenzoic acid','NEW','12-373','12-243','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/260702q.png'),
(260703,'chemistry','Give the IUPAC names of the following compound given in diagram(n26046)','2-methyl cyclopentane carboxylic acid','In the IUPAC system, aliphatic carboxylic acids are named by replacing the ending –e in the name of the corresponding alkane with – oic acid. \n\nIn numbering the carbon chain, the carboxylic carbon is numbered one. \n\nFor naming compounds containing more than one carboxyl group, the alkyl chain leaving carboxyl groups is numbered and the number of carboxyl groups is indicated by adding the multiplicative prefix, dicarboxylic acid, tricarboxylic acid, etc. to the name of parent alkyl chain.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-374 Paragraph -3)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Nomenclature and Structure of Carboxyl Group',NULL,'3','mcq','3-phenyl propanoic acid','3-methyl but-2-en-1-oic acid','2-methyl cyclopentane carboxylic acid','2, 4, 6-trinitrobenzoic acid','NEW','12-374','12-244','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/260703q.png'),
(260704,'chemistry','Give the IUPAC names of the following compound given in diagram(n26047)','2, 4, 6-trinitrobenzoic acid','In the IUPAC system, aliphatic carboxylic acids are named by replacing the ending –e in the name of the corresponding alkane with – oic acid. \n\nIn numbering the carbon chain, the carboxylic carbon is numbered one. \n\nFor naming compounds containing more than one carboxyl group, the alkyl chain leaving carboxyl groups is numbered and the number of carboxyl groups is indicated by adding the multiplicative prefix, dicarboxylic acid, tricarboxylic acid, etc. to the name of parent alkyl chain.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-374 Paragraph -3)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Nomenclature and Structure of Carboxyl Group',NULL,'3','mcq','3-phenyl propanoic acid','3-methyl but-2-en-1-oic acid','2-methyl cyclopentane carboxylic acid','2, 4, 6-trinitrobenzoic acid','NEW','12-374','12-244','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/260704q.png'),
(260705,'chemistry','IUPAC name of a-acetyl succinic acid is?','2-(1-oxoethyl) butan-1,4-dioic acid','In the IUPAC system, aliphatic carboxylic acids are named by replacing the ending –e in the name of the corresponding alkane with – oic acid. \n\nIn numbering the carbon chain, the carboxylic carbon is numbered one. \n\nFor naming compounds containing more than one carboxyl group, the alkyl chain leaving carboxyl groups is numbered and the number of carboxyl groups is indicated by adding the multiplicative prefix, dicarboxylic acid, tricarboxylic acid, etc. to the name of parent alkyl chain.\n\n--COOH  is priority functional group according to IUPAC .\n \nSo, in main chain both −COOH must be there. \n\nso , assign 1 & 4 to acid group. alpha position is next carbon from main functional group. \n\nSo second position goes to the oxoethyl subgroup.In ethyl group, oxo group is present at position 1 from main chain.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-374 Paragraph -3)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Nomenclature and Structure of Carboxyl Group',NULL,'1','mcq','3-(2-oxoethyl) butan-1,4-dioic acid','2-(1-oxoethyl) butan-1,4-dioic acid','Hexan-1,6-dioic acid','Butan-1,4-dicarboxylic acid','NEW','12-374','12-244',NULL),
(260706,'chemistry','What is the common name of 2-hydroxypropanoic acid?','Lactic acid','In the IUPAC system, aliphatic carboxylic acids are named by replacing the ending –e in the name of the corresponding alkane with – oic acid. \n\nIn numbering the carbon chain, the carboxylic carbon is numbered one. \n\nFor naming compounds containing more than one carboxyl group, the alkyl chain leaving carboxyl groups is numbered and the number of carboxyl groups is indicated by adding the multiplicative prefix, dicarboxylic acid, tricarboxylic acid, etc. to the name of parent alkyl chain.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-374 Paragraph -3)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Nomenclature and Structure of Carboxyl Group',NULL,'1','mcq','Adipic acid','Crotonic acid','Lactic acid','Acrylic acid','NEW','12-374','12-244',NULL),
(151411,'chemistry','A : Silicon is insulator at 0 K but semiconductor at room temperature.\n\nR : Conductivity of silicon at room temperature is due to electronic defect.','Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A.','Silicon is semiconductor → true.\nAt room temperature due to electronic defect (doping).','Physical chemistry >> Solid state >> Assertion and Reason Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A.','Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A.','A is true but R is false.','Both A and R are false.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(260707,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following. \n\nAssertion (A): IUPAC nameofCH₃CH₂CH₂COOH is butyric acid. \n\nReason (R):In the IUPAC system, aliphatic carboxylic acids are named by replacing the ending -e in the name of the corresponding alkane with -oic acid.','R is correct; but A is incorrect','In the IUPAC system, aliphatic carboxylic acids are named by replacing the ending –e in the name of the corresponding alkane with – oic acid. \n\nIn numbering the carbon chain, the carboxylic carbon is numbered one. \n\nFor naming compounds containing more than one carboxyl group, the alkyl chain leaving carboxyl groups is numbered and the number of carboxyl groups is indicated by adding the multiplicative prefix, dicarboxylic acid, tricarboxylic acid, etc. to the name of parent alkyl chain.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-374 Paragraph -3)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Nomenclature and Structure of Carboxyl Group',NULL,'3','mcq','Both A and R are correct; and R is the correct explanation of A','Both A and R are correct; but R is not the correct explanation of A','A is correct; but R is incorrect','R is correct; but A is incorrect','NEW','12-374','12-244',NULL),
(260708,'chemistry','In carboxylic acids, the bonds to the carboxyl carbon lie in _____ plane.','one','In carboxylic acids, the bonds to the carboxyl carbon lie in one plane and are separated by about 120°. \n\nThe carboxylic carbon is less electrophilic than carbonyl carbon because of the possible resonance structure.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-375 Paragraph -1)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Nomenclature and Structure of Carboxyl Group',NULL,'1','mcq','one','different','all the plane','any of the above','NEW','12-375','12-245',NULL),
(260709,'chemistry','In carboxylic acids, the bonds to the carboxyl carbon are seperated by about ____.','120°','In carboxylic acids, the bonds to the carboxyl carbon lie in one plane and are separated by about 120°. \n\nThe carboxylic carbon is less electrophilic than carbonyl carbon because of the possible resonance structure.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-375 Paragraph -1)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Nomenclature and Structure of Carboxyl Group',NULL,'1','mcq','90°','60°','180°','120°','NEW','12-375','12-245',NULL),
(260710,'chemistry','The carboxylic carbon is______  than carbonyl carbon.','less electrophilic','In carboxylic acids, the bonds to the carboxyl carbon lie in one plane and are separated by about 120°. \n\n\\The carboxylic carbon is less electrophilic than carbonyl carbon because of the possible resonance structure.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-375 Paragraph -1)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Nomenclature and Structure of Carboxyl Group',NULL,'1','mcq','less electrophilic','more electrophilic','less nucleophillic','none of the above','NEW','12-375','12-245',NULL),
(260711,'chemistry','The carboxylic carbon is less electrophilic than carbonyl carbon because of the','resonance','In carboxylic acids, the bonds to the carboxyl carbon lie in one plane and are separated by about 120°. \n\nThe carboxylic carbon is less electrophilic than carbonyl carbon because of the possible resonance structure.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-375 Paragraph -1)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Nomenclature and Structure of Carboxyl Group',NULL,'1','mcq','ionic  nature','electronegativity','resonance','All of the above','NEW','12-375','12-245',NULL),
(260712,'chemistry','Which one is the correct IUPAC name of the compound?\ndiagram(n26125)','4-Choloro-5-phenylpentanoic acid','In the IUPAC system, aliphatic carboxylic acids are named by replacing the ending –e in the name of the corresponding alkane with –oic acid. \n\nIn numbering the carbon chain, the carboxylic carbon is numbered one. \n\nFor naming compounds containing more than one carboxyl group, the alkyl chain leaving carboxyl groups is numbered and the number of carboxyl groups is indicated by adding the multiplicative prefix, dicarboxylic acid, tricarboxylic acid, etc. to the name of parent alkyl chain. \n\nThe position of –COOH groups are indicated by the arabic numeral before the multiplicative prefix.\n\nReference: (NCERT - Class 12 Page-374 Paragraph -2)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Nomenclature and Structure of Carboxyl Group',NULL,'3','mcq','3-Chloro-1-phenyl-5-pentanoic acid','4-Choloro-5-phenylpentanoic acid','5-Phenyl-2-chloropentanoic acid','4-Chloro butylbenzene methanoic acid','NEW','12-374','12-244','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/260712q.png'),
(260713,'chemistry','Write the IUPAC name of the compound given below?\ndiagram(n26126)','2-Hydroxy-5-methyl-3-hexenoic acid','In the IUPAC system, aliphatic carboxylic acids are named by replacing the ending –e in the name of the corresponding alkane with –oic acid. \n\nIn numbering the carbon chain, the carboxylic carbon is numbered one. \n\nFor naming compounds containing more than one carboxyl group, the alkyl chain leaving carboxyl groups is numbered and the number of carboxyl groups is indicated by adding the multiplicative prefix, dicarboxylic acid, tricarboxylic acid, etc. to the name of parent alkyl chain. \n\nThe position of –COOH groups are indicated by the arabic numeral before the multiplicative prefix.\n\nReference: (NCERT - Class 12 Page-374 Paragraph -2)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Nomenclature and Structure of Carboxyl Group',NULL,'3','mcq','2-Hydroxy-1-isopropyl-1-butenoic acid','2-Hydroxy-3-heptenoic acid','2-Hydroxy-5-methyl-3-hexenoic acid','2-hydroxy-5-methyl hexanoic acid','NEW','12-375','12-245','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/260713q.png'),
(260714,'chemistry','IUPAC name of the given compound?\ndiagram(n26131)','5-Hydroxy hexan-3-one','The IUPAC names of open chain aliphatic aldehydes and ketones are derived from the names of the corresponding alkanes by replacing the ending –e with –al and –one respectively. \n\nIn case of aldehydes the longest carbon chain is numbered starting from the carbon of the aldehyde group while in case of ketones the numbering begins from the end nearer to the carbonyl group.\n\nReference: (NCERT - Class 12 Page-359 Paragraph -2)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Nomenclature and Structure of Carboxyl Group',NULL,'3','mcq','2-Hydroxy hexan-4-one','4-Hydroxy hexan-2-one','5-Hydroxy hexan-3-one','3-Oxo ethyl propanol','NEW','12-374','12-244','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/260714q.png'),
(260715,'biology','The technique which makes use of amniotic fluid for the detection of parental disorder that might be present in the developing foetus is known as?','Amniocentesis','In Amniocentesis, the amniotic fluid is used to determined the disorders or the gender of the foetus.','Reproduction >> Reproductive Health >> Medical Termination of Pregnancy (MTP)',NULL,'3','mcq','Amniocentesis','MTP','Endoscopy','IVF','NEW','12-062','12-046',NULL),
(260716,'biology','Illegal abortions including the infamous female foeticides are carried on as a part of which of the following procedures?','Medical Termination of Pregnancy','Medical Termination of Pregnancy is misused by certain people to abort female fetuses, which is an illegal and morally wrong practice.','Reproduction >> Reproductive Health >> Medical Termination of Pregnancy (MTP)',NULL,'1','mcq','Medical Termination of Pregnancy','Amniocentesis','Drug abuse','Physical violence','NEW','12-062','12-046',NULL),
(260717,'biology','Harmful or unwanted pregnancies can be terminated through?','MTP','Unwanted pregnancies which might also be harmful or fatal either to the mother or to the foetus or both can legally be terminated through MTP.','Reproduction >> Reproductive Health >> Medical Termination of Pregnancy (MTP)',NULL,'2','mcq','Amniocentesis','ET','Foeticide','MTP','NEW','12-062','12-046',NULL),
(260801,'chemistry','Which agent will not convert primary alcohols to carboxylic acid?','CrO₃','Primary alcohols are readily oxidised to carboxylic acids with common oxidising agents such as potassium permanganate (KMnO₄) in neutral, acidic or alkaline media or by potassium dichromate (K₂Cr₂O₇) and chromium trioxide (CrO₃) in acidic media (Jones reagent).\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-375 Paragraph -2)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Methods of Preparation of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'1','mcq','Potassium dichromate','Potassium permanganate','Jones reagent','CrO₃','NEW','12-375','12-245',NULL),
(260802,'chemistry','Chromium trioxide (CrO₃ ) in acidic media is known as ______.','jones reagent','Primary alcohols are readily oxidised to carboxylic acids with common oxidising agents such as potassium permanganate (KMnO₄) in neutral, acidic or alkaline media or by potassium dichromate (K₂Cr₂O₇) and chromium trioxide (CrO₃) in acidic media (Jones reagent).\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-375 Paragraph -2)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Methods of Preparation of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'1','mcq','grignard reagent','jones reagent','tollens reagent','millon\'s reagent','NEW','12-375','12-245',NULL),
(260803,'chemistry','Carboxylic acids are also prepared from ______ by the use of mild oxidising agents.','aldehydes','Primary alcohols are readily oxidised to carboxylic acids with common oxidising agents such as potassium permanganate (KMnO₄) in neutral, acidic or alkaline media or by potassium dichromate (K₂Cr₂O₇) and chromium trioxide (CrO₃ ) in acidic media (Jones reagent).\n\nCarboxylic acids are also prepared from aldehydes by the use of mild oxidising agents.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-375 Paragraph -2)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Methods of Preparation of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'1','mcq','ketone','grignard reagent','Jones reagent','aldehydes','NEW','12-375','12-245',NULL),
(260804,'chemistry','Name the substrate given in the diagram(n26048)','toluene','Aromatic carboxylic acids can be prepared by vigorous oxidation of alkyl benzenes with chromic acid or acidic or alkaline potassium permanganate. \n\nThe entire side chain is oxidised to the carboxyl group irrespective of length of the side chain. \n\nPrimary and secondary alkyl groups are oxidised in this manner while tertiary group is not affected. \n\nSuitably substituted alkenes are also oxidised to carboxylic acids with these oxidising reagents.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-376 Paragraph -2)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Methods of Preparation of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'3','mcq','benzene','Ethyl benzene','cresol','toluene','NEW','12-376','12-246','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/260804q.png'),
(260805,'chemistry','Name the catalyst omitted in the given diagram(n26049)','Potassium permanganate + alkali','Aromatic carboxylic acids can be prepared by vigorous oxidation of alkyl benzenes with chromic acid or acidic or alkaline potassium permanganate. \n\nThe entire side chain is oxidised to the carboxyl group irrespective of length of the side chain. \n\nPrimary and secondary alkyl groups are oxidised in this manner while tertiary group is not affected. \n\nSuitably substituted alkenes are also oxidised to carboxylic acids with these oxidising reagents.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-376 Paragraph -2)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Methods of Preparation of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'3','mcq','Jones reagent','alkylbenzene','Potassium permanganate + alkali','toluene','NEW','12-376','12-246','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/260805q.png'),
(260806,'chemistry','Primary and secondary alkyl groups are oxidised in this manner while _______ group is not affected.','tertiary','Aromatic carboxylic acids can be prepared by vigorous oxidation of alkyl benzenes with chromic acid or acidic or alkaline potassium permanganate. \n\nThe entire side chain is oxidised to the carboxyl group irrespective of length of the side chain. \n\nPrimary and secondary alkyl groups are oxidised in this manner while tertiary group is not affected. \n\nSuitably substituted alkenes are also oxidised to carboxylic acids with these oxidising reagents.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-376 Paragraph -2)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Methods of Preparation of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'1','mcq','alcoholic','tertiary','aldehyde','All of the above','NEW','12-376','12-246',NULL),
(260807,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following.\nAssertion (A): IUPAC nameofCH₃CH₂CH₂COOH is butanoic acid. \nReason (R): In the IUPAC system, aliphatic carboxylic acids are named by replacing the ending -e in the name of the corresponding alkane with -oic acid.','Both A and R are correct; and R is the correct explanation of A.','Aromatic carboxylic acids can be prepared by vigorous oxidation of alkyl benzenes with chromic acid or acidic or alkaline potassium permanganate. \n\nThe entire side chain is oxidised to the carboxyl group irrespective of length of the side chain. \n\nPrimary and secondary alkyl groups are oxidised in this manner while tertiary group is not affected. \n\nSuitably substituted alkenes are also oxidised to carboxylic acids with these oxidising reagents.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-376 Paragraph -2)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Methods of Preparation of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'1','mcq','Both A and R are correct; and R is the correct explanation of A.','Both A and R are correct; but R is not the correct explanation of A.','A is correct but R is not correct.','A is not correct but R is correct.','NEW','12-376','12-246',NULL),
(260808,'chemistry','Mild reaction conditions are used to stop the reaction at the _____ stage.','amide','Nitriles are hydrolysed to amides and then to acids in the presence of H + or OH − as catalyst. \n\nMild reaction conditions are used to stop the reaction at the amide stage.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-376 Paragraph -3)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Methods of Preparation of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'1','mcq','alcoholic','nitrile','cyanide','amide','NEW','12-376','12-246',NULL),
