(260811,'chemistry','Guess the catalyst in the given diagram(n26052)','Dry ether','Grignard reagents react with carbon dioxide (dry ice) to form salts of carboxylic acids which in turn give corresponding carboxylic acids after acidification with mineral acid.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-376 Paragraph -4)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Methods of Preparation of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'3','mcq','Dry ether','CO₂','Grignard reagent','none','NEW','12-376','12-246','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/260811q.png'),
