(260813,'chemistry','Acid chlorides when hydrolysed with water give _______.','carboxylic acids','Acid chlorides when hydrolysed with water give carboxylic acids or more readily hydrolysed with aqueous base to give carboxylate ions which on acidification provide corresponding carboxylic acids. \n\nAnhydrides on the other hand are hydrolysed to corresponding acid(s) with water.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-377 Paragraph -2)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Methods of Preparation of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'1','mcq','alcohol','carboxylic acids','aldehyde','ketone','NEW','12-377','12-247',NULL),
(260814,'chemistry','_______ ions which on acidification provide corresponding carboxylic acids.','Carboxylate','Acid chlorides when hydrolysed with water give carboxylic acids or more readily hydrolysed with aqueous base to give carboxylate ions which on acidification provide corresponding carboxylic acids. \n\nAnhydrides on the other hand are hydrolysed to corresponding acid(s) with water.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-377 Paragraph -2)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Methods of Preparation of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'2','mcq','alcoholic','aldehydic','ketonic','Carboxylate','NEW','12-377','12-247',NULL),
(260815,'chemistry','Anhydrides  are hydrolysed to corresponding acid with ______.','water','Acid chlorides when hydrolysed with water give carboxylic acids or more readily hydrolysed with aqueous base to give carboxylate ions which on acidification provide corresponding carboxylic acids.\n\nAnhydrides on the other hand are hydrolysed to corresponding acid(s) with water.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-377 Paragraph -2)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Methods of Preparation of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'1','mcq','mineral acids','dilute alkali','dilute acid','water','NEW','12-377','12-247',NULL),
(260816,'chemistry','Guess the reagent in the given diagram(n26053)','water','Acid chlorides when hydrolysed with water give carboxylic acids or more readily hydrolysed with aqueous base to give carboxylate ions which on acidification provide corresponding carboxylic acids. \n\nAnhydrides on the other hand are hydrolysed to corresponding acid(s) with water.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-377 Paragraph -2)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Methods of Preparation of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'3','mcq','hydroxyl ion','dilute alkali','dilute acid','water','NEW','12-377','12-247','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/260816q.png'),
(260817,'chemistry','Guess the reagent in the given diagram(n26054)','H₃O⁺','Acidic hydrolysis of esters gives directly carboxylic acids while basic hydrolysis gives carboxylates, which on acidification give corresponding carboxylic acids.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-377 Paragraph -3)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Methods of Preparation of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'3','mcq','H₂O','H₃O⁺','H₃O⁻','NaOH','NEW','12-377','12-247','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/260817q.png'),
(260901,'chemistry','Aliphatic carboxylic acids upto _______ carbon atoms are colourless liquids at room temperature.','nine','Aliphatic carboxylic acids upto nine carbon atoms are colourless liquids at room temperature with unpleasant odours. \n\nThe higher acids are wax like solids and are practically odourless due to their low volatility. \n\nCarboxylic acids are higher boiling liquids than aldehydes, ketones and even alcohols of comparable molecular masses. \n\nThis is due to more extensive association of carboxylic acid molecules through intermolecular hydrogen bonding. \n\nThe hydrogen bonds are not broken completely even in the vapour phase. \n\nIn fact, most carboxylic acids exist as dimer in the vapour phase or in the aprotic solvents.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-379 Paragraph -1)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Physical Properties of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'1','mcq','five','ten','nine','three','NEW','12-378','12-248',NULL),
(260902,'chemistry','The higher acids are wax like solids and are practically ______.','odourless','Aliphatic carboxylic acids upto nine carbon atoms are colourless liquids at room temperature with unpleasant odours. \n\nThe higher acids are wax like solids and are practically odourless due to their low volatility. \n\nCarboxylic acids are higher boiling liquids than aldehydes, ketones and even alcohols of comparable molecular masses. \n\nThis is due to more extensive association of carboxylic acid molecules through intermolecular hydrogen bonding. \n\nThe hydrogen bonds are not broken completely even in the vapour phase. \n\nIn fact, most carboxylic acids exist as dimer in the vapour phase or in the aprotic solvents.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-379 Paragraph -1)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Physical Properties of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'1','mcq','fishy odour','pleasant odour','odourless','waxy odour','NEW','12-378','12-248',NULL),
(260903,'chemistry','Carboxylic acids are ______ boiling liquids than aldehydes, ketones and even alcohols.','higher','Aliphatic carboxylic acids upto nine carbon atoms are colourless liquids at room temperature with unpleasant odours. \n\nThe higher acids are wax like solids and are practically odourless due to their low volatility. \n\nCarboxylic acids are higher boiling liquids than aldehydes, ketones and even alcohols of comparable molecular masses. \n\nThis is due to more extensive association of carboxylic acid molecules through intermolecular hydrogen bonding. \n\nThe hydrogen bonds are not broken completely even in the vapour phase. \n\nIn fact, most carboxylic acids exist as dimer in the vapour phase or in the aprotic solvents.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-379 Paragraph -1)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Physical Properties of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'1','mcq','lower','higher','same','none of the above','NEW','12-378','12-248',NULL),
(260904,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following:\n\nAssertion (A): Carboxylic acids are higher boiling liquids than aldehydes, ketones and even alcohols of comparable molecular masses.\n \nReason (R): More extensive association of carboxylic acid molecules through intermolecular hydrogen bonding.','Both A and R are correct; and R is the correct explanation of A.','Aliphatic carboxylic acids upto nine carbon atoms are colourless liquids at room temperature with unpleasant odours. \n\nThe higher acids are wax like solids and are practically odourless due to their low volatility. \n\nCarboxylic acids are higher boiling liquids than aldehydes, ketones and even alcohols of comparable molecular masses. \n\nThis is due to more extensive association of carboxylic acid molecules through intermolecular hydrogen bonding. \n\nThe hydrogen bonds are not broken completely even in the vapour phase. \n\nIn fact, most carboxylic acids exist as dimer in the vapour phase or in the aprotic solvents.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-379 Paragraph -1)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Physical Properties of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'3','mcq','Both A and R are correct; and R is the correct explanation of A.','Both A and R are correct; but R is not the correct explanation of A.','A is correct; but R is incorrect.','R is correct; but A is incorrect.','NEW','12-378','12-248',NULL),
(260905,'chemistry','Choose the incorrect option regarding the physical properties of carboxylic acid.','Aliphatic carboxylic acids upto four C-atoms are coloured','Simple aliphatic carboxylic acids having up to four carbon atoms are miscible in water due to the formation of hydrogen bonds with water.\n \nThe solubility decreases with increasing number of carbon atoms. \n\nHigher carboxylic acids are practically insoluble in water due to the increased hydrophobic interaction of hydrocarbon part. \n\nBenzoic acid, the simplest aromatic carboxylic acid is nearly insoluble in cold water. \n\nCarboxylic acids are also soluble in less polar organic solvents like benzene, ether, alcohol, chloroform.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-379 Paragraph -2)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Physical Properties of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'2','mcq','Higher carboxylic acids are insoluble in water','Benzoic acid is soluble in cold water','Carboxylic acids have higher boiling point than aldehydes of comparable masses','Aliphatic carboxylic acids upto four C-atoms are coloured','NEW','12-378','12-248',NULL),
(260906,'chemistry','In the vapour phase or in the aprotic solvents carboxylic acids exist as?','dimer','Aliphatic carboxylic acids upto nine carbon atoms are colourless liquids at room temperature with unpleasant odours. \n\nThe higher acids are wax like solids and are practically odourless due to their low volatility.\n \nCarboxylic acids are higher boiling liquids than aldehydes, ketones and even alcohols of comparable molecular masses. \n\nThis is due to more extensive association of carboxylic acid molecules through intermolecular hydrogen bonding. \n\nThe hydrogen bonds are not broken completely even in the vapour phase. \n\nIn fact, most carboxylic acids exist as dimer in the vapour phase or in the aprotic solvents.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-379 Paragraph -1)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Physical Properties of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'1','mcq','dimer','trimer','tetramer','All of the above','NEW','12-378','12-248',NULL),
(260907,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following: \n\nAssertion (A):The molecular mass of acetic acid in benzene is 120 instead of 60.\n \nReason (R): The carboxylic acids exist as cyclic dimers.','Both A and R are correct; and R is the correct explanation of A','Aliphatic carboxylic acids upto nine carbon atoms are colourless liquids at room temperature with unpleasant odours. \n\nThe higher acids are wax like solids and are practically odourless due to their low volatility. \n\nCarboxylic acids are higher boiling liquids than aldehydes, ketones and even alcohols of comparable molecular masses.\n \nThis is due to more extensive association of carboxylic acid molecules through intermolecular hydrogen bonding.\n\nThe hydrogen bonds are not broken completely even in the vapour phase. \n\nIn fact, most carboxylic acids exist as dimer in the vapour phase or in the aprotic solvents.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-379 Paragraph -1)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Physical Properties of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'3','mcq','Both A and R are correct; and R is the correct explanation of A','Both A and R are correct; but R is not the correct explanation of A','A is correct; but R is incorrect','R is correct; but A is incorrect','NEW','12-378','12-248',NULL),
(260908,'chemistry','______ acid is insoluble in cold water.','Benzoic acid','Simple aliphatic carboxylic acids having up to four carbon atoms are miscible in water due to the formation of hydrogen bonds with water. \n\nThe solubility decreases with increasing number of carbon atoms. \n\nHigher carboxylic acids are practically insoluble in water due to the increased hydrophobic interaction of hydrocarbon part. \n\nBenzoic acid, the simplest aromatic carboxylic acid is nearly insoluble in cold water.\n \nCarboxylic acids are also soluble in less polar organic solvents like benzene, ether, alcohol, chloroform.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-379 Paragraph -2)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Physical Properties of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'1','mcq','Higher carboxylic','Valeric','Benzoic acid','p-methylbenzoic acid','NEW','12-378','12-248',NULL),
(260909,'chemistry','Higher carboxylic acids are ______ in water.','insoluble','Simple aliphatic carboxylic acids having up to four carbon atoms are miscible in water due to the formation of hydrogen bonds with water. \n\nThe solubility decreases with increasing number of carbon atoms. \n\nHigher carboxylic acids are practically insoluble in water due to the increased hydrophobic interaction of hydrocarbon part. \n\nBenzoic acid, the simplest aromatic carboxylic acid is nearly insoluble in cold water. \n\nCarboxylic acids are also soluble in less polar organic solvents like benzene, ether, alcohol, chloroform.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-379 Paragraph -2)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Physical Properties of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'1','mcq','soluble','insoluble','sparingly soluble','none of the above','NEW','12-378','12-248',NULL),
(260910,'chemistry','Carboxylic acids is soluble in','chloroform','Simple aliphatic carboxylic acids having up to four carbon atoms are miscible in water due to the formation of hydrogen bonds with water. \n\nThe solubility decreases with increasing number of carbon atoms. \n\nHigher carboxylic acids are practically insoluble in water due to the increased hydrophobic interaction of hydrocarbon part. \n\nBenzoic acid, the simplest aromatic carboxylic acid is nearly insoluble in cold water. \n\nCarboxylic acids are also soluble in less polar organic solvents like benzene, ether, alcohol, chloroform.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-379 Paragraph -2)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Physical Properties of Carboxylic Acids',NULL,'1','mcq','methanol','ethanol','water','chloroform','NEW','12-378','12-248',NULL),
(260911,'biology','The stage at which the zygote is transferred into the Fallopian Tube is ?','8 blastomeres','The zygote or early embryos (with upto 8 blastomeres) can be transferred into the Fallopian Tube.','Reproduction >> Reproductive Health >> Infertility',NULL,'3','mcq','8 metameres','16 blastomeres','8 blastomeres','8 blastocyst','NEW','12-064','12-048',NULL),
(260912,'biology','The technique of transferring a zygote into the Fallopian Tube is known as?','ZIFT','Zygote  or early embryo (with upto 8 blastomeres) are transferred into the Fallopian Tube through ZIFT–Zygote Intra Fallopian Transfer.','Reproduction >> Reproductive Health >> Infertility',NULL,'2','mcq','ZIFT','GIFT','IUT','ICSI','NEW','12-064','12-048',NULL),
