(230104,'chemistry','Where are coordination compounds used?','All of these','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 244; Paragraph No. 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Introduction',NULL,'1','mcq','Metallurgical processes','Industrial catalysts','Analytical reagents','All of these','NEW','12-244','12-118',NULL),
(230105,'chemistry','What are the applications of coordination compounds?','All of these','Coordination compounds also find many applications\nin electroplating, textile dyeing and medicinal chemistry.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 244; Paragraph No. 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Introduction',NULL,'1','mcq','Electroplating','Textile dyeing','Medicinal chemistry','All of these','NEW','12-244','12-118',NULL),
(230106,'chemistry','____ compounds in which the metal atoms are bound to a number of anions or\nneutral molecules by sharing of electrons.','Complex','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 244; Paragraph No. 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Introduction',NULL,'1','fillup','Com,pl,ex,Si,mp,le,Mi,xed',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-244','12-118',NULL),
(230107,'biology','When offspring is produced by a single parent with or without the involvement of gamete formation, the reproduction is said to be','Asexual','Based on whether there is participation of one organism or two in the process of reproduction, it is of two types. When offspring is produced by a single parent with or without the involvement of gamete formation, the reproduction is asexual.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:5, paragraph no:2)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Life Span',NULL,'1','mcq','Asexual','Sexual','Heterosexual','Bisexual','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230108,'biology','When two parents (opposite sex) participate in the reproductive process and there is involvement of  fusion of male and female gametes, it is','Sexual reproduction','Based on whether there is participation of one organism or two in the process of reproduction, it is of two types. When offspring is produced by a single parent with or without the involvement of gamete formation, the reproduction is asexual. When two parents (opposite sex) participate in the reproductive process and also involve fusion of male and female gametes, it is called sexual reproduction.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:5, paragraph no:2)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Life Span',NULL,'2','mcq','Sexual reproduction','Asexual reproduction','Unisexual production','Bisexual production','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230122,'biology','Peepal tree has a much shorter life span than a mango tree.','FALSE','Mango tree has a much shorter life span (300 years) than peepal tree (900-1500 years).(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:3, paragraph no:1)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Life Span',NULL,'1','mcq','TRUE','FALSE',NULL,NULL,'DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230123,'biology','Assertion: Sizes of crows and parrots are not very different yet their life spans show a wide range of difference. \nReason: Life spans of organisms are not necessarily correlated with their Sizes','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Life spans of organisms are not necessarily correlated with their Sizes.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:3, paragraph no:1)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Life Span',NULL,'3','mcq','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Assertion is true but Reason is false','Both Assertion and Reason are false','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230124,'biology','Choose the correct life cycle of a living organism','Grow-mature-produce new offspring-death','Grow-mature-produce new offspring-death. The offspring grow mature and in turn produce new offspring. Thus there is a cycle of birth,growth and death.\n(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:5, paragraph no:1)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Life Span',NULL,'2','mcq','Mature-produce new offspring-death-grow','Grow-mature-produce new offspring-death','Produce new offspring-death-grow-mature','Death-mature-grow-produce new offspring','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230125,'biology','Which of the following factors are not responsible for reproduction?\ni) Organism’s habitat\nii) Organism’s life span\niii) Organism’s internal physiology\niv) Organism’s skin color','ii and iv','The organism’s habitat, its internal physiology and several other factors are collectively responsible for how it reproduces.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:5, paragraph no:2)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Life Span',NULL,'3','mcq','ii and iv','i and iii','i and ii','iii and iv','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230126,'biology','Find out the correct statement -','Reproduction is essential for continuity of species on the earth','Life spans of organisms are not necessarily correlated with their sizes, e.g. The sizes of crows and parrots are not very different, but their life spans are very different. A peepal tree has a much longer life span as compared to a mango tree. Reproduction is essential for the continuity of species on the earth.','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Life Span',NULL,'2','mcq','Life spans of organisms are necessarily correlated with their sizes','The sizes crows and parrots are not very different, so their life spans are almost similar','A peepal tree has much shorter life span as compared to a mango tree','Reproduction is essential for continuity of species on the earth','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL);
