(230127,'biology','Find out the organism with highest life span -','Tortoise','Lifespan of - \n                      Tortoise - 80-150 yrs\n                      Horse - 25-30 yrs\n                      Fruit fly - 40 to 50 days\n                      Dog - 20-30 yrs','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Life Span',NULL,'3','mcq','Tortoise','Horse','Fruit fly','Dog','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230128,'biology','No individual is immortal except -','Single celled Organisms','Because they don\'t die as they grow old. They usually undergo Mitosis (asexual reproduction) to reproduce, in which the organism itself gets divided into two (cell division).(Reference :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:3, paragraph no:1)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Life Span',NULL,'1','mcq','Single celled Organisms','Green plants','Sponges','Drones','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230201,'chemistry','Which scientist was first to formulate ideas about structure of coordination compounds?','Werner','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 244; Paragraph No. 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Werner\'s Theory of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Werner','Fleming','Pauling','Feynmann','NEW','12-244','12-118',NULL),
(230202,'chemistry','Who proposed the idea of primary and secondary valency for metal ion?','Werner','Werner proposed the concept of a primary valence and\na secondary valence for a metal ion.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 244; Paragraph No. 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Werner\'s Theory of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Werner','Maxwell','Pauling','SN Bose','NEW','12-244','12-118',NULL),
(230203,'chemistry','What is the primary valency of PdCl₂?','2','Binary compounds such as\nCrCl₃, CoCl₂ or PdCl₂ have primary valence of 3, 2 and 2 respectively.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 244; Paragraph No. 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Werner\'s Theory of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','2','3','1','4','NEW','12-244','12-118',NULL),
(230204,'chemistry','Which compound has primary valency as 3?','CoCl₃','Binary compounds such as CrCl₃, CoCl₂ or PdCl₂ have primary valence of 3, 2 and 2 respectively.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 244; Paragraph No. 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Werner\'s Theory of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','NaCl','CoCl₃','PdCl₂','NiCl₂','NEW','12-244','12-118','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/230204q.png'),
(230205,'chemistry','How many moles of AgCl would be precipitated when CoCl₃•6NH₃ is treated with excess silver nitrate?','3','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 245; Paragraph No. 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Werner\'s Theory of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','1','2','3','0','NEW','12-245','12-119','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/230205q.png'),
(230207,'chemistry','___ valence is the number of groups bound directly to metal ion.','secondary','Werner proposed the term secondary valence for the\nnumber of groups bound directly to the metal ion(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 245; Paragraph No. 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Werner\'s Theory of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'1','fillup','se,con,da,ry',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-245','12-119','/ncert/pyq/biology/match/230207q.png'),
(230208,'chemistry','The atoms within the square brackets form a single entity which ____dissociate under the reaction\nconditions.','does not','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 245; Paragraph No. 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Werner\'s Theory of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'1','fillup','do,es, not',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-245','12-119',NULL),
(230209,'chemistry','What is the color of CoCl₃•5NH₃?','Purple','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 245; Paragraph No. 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Werner\'s Theory of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Yellow','Purple','Green','Violet','NEW','12-245','12-119',NULL),
(230210,'chemistry','For which of the following compounds solution conductivity corresponds to 1:2 electrolyte?','[CoCl₂(NH₃)₅]⁺Cl⁻','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 245; Table 9.1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Werner\'s Theory of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','[CoCl₂(NH₃)₄]⁺²2Cl⁻','[CoCl₂(NH₃)₅]⁺Cl⁻','[CoCl₂(NH₃)₆]⁺³3Cl⁻','All of these','NEW','12-245','12-119',NULL),
(230211,'chemistry','What is the secondary valence of the [CoCl₂(NH₃)₆]⁺³3Cl⁻?','6','Werner proposed the term secondary valence for the\nnumber of groups bound directly to the metal ion(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 245; Paragraph No. 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Werner\'s Theory of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','3','4','6','8','NEW','12-245','12-119',NULL),
(230212,'chemistry','How many of the postulates of Werner\'s theory correctly stated?\nA. In coordination compounds metals show two types of linkages.\nB. The secondary valency are normally ionisable are satisfied by negative ions.\nC. The primary valency are non-ionisable.\nD. The ions/groups bound by the secondary linkages to the metal have\ncharacteristic spatial arrangements corresponding to different\ncoordination numbers.','2','Werner in 1898, propounded his theory of coordination compounds. The main postulates are:\n1. In coordination compounds metals show two types of linkages\n(valences)-primary and secondary.\n2. The primary valences are normally ionisable and are satisfied by\nnegative ions.\n3. The secondary valences are non ionisable. These are satisfied by\nneutral molecules or negative ions. The secondary valence is equal to\nthe coordination number and is fixed for a metal.\n4. The ions/groups bound by the secondary linkages to the metal have\ncharacteristic spatial arrangements corresponding to different\ncoordination numbers.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 245; Paragraph No. 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Werner\'s Theory of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','2','1','3','4','NEW','12-245','12-119',NULL),
(230213,'chemistry','The ___ valence is equal to\nthe coordination number and is fixed for a metal.','secondary','The secondary valence is equal to the coordination number and is fixed for a metal.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 245; Paragraph No. 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Werner\'s Theory of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'1','fillup','se,con,da,ry,pri,ma',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-245','12-119',NULL),
(230214,'chemistry','The ions/groups bound by the secondary linkages to the metal have\ncharacteristic spatial arrangements called as','Coordination polyhedra','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 245; Paragraph No. 3)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Werner\'s Theory of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Coordination polyhedra','Coordination entities','Ligands','Coordination complex','NEW','12-245','12-119',NULL),
(230215,'chemistry','Choose the odd one with respect to common geometrical shapes in coordination compounds of transition metals.','Trigonal bipyramidal','Werner further postulated that octahedral, tetrahedral and square planar\ngeometrical shapes are more common in coordination compounds of\ntransition metals.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 245; Paragraph No. 4)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Werner\'s Theory of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Tetrahedral','Trigonal bipyramidal','Octahedral','Square Planar','NEW','12-245','12-119',NULL),
(230216,'chemistry','What is the shape of [Ni(CO)₄]?','Tetrahedral','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 245; Paragraph No. 4)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Werner\'s Theory of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Tetrahedral','Trigonal Planar','Linear','Square Planar','NEW','12-245','12-119',NULL),
(230217,'chemistry','What is the secondary valence of the CoCl₃•4NH₃, if one mole of this compound gives 1 mole of AgCl as precipitate upon with excess silver nitrate?','6','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 246; Example 9.1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Werner\'s Theory of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','2','4','6','8','NEW','12-246','12-120',NULL),
(230301,'chemistry','A ______ constitutes a central metal atom or ion bonded\nto a fixed number of ions or molecules.','Coordination entity','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 247; Paragraph 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Definition of terms pertaining to Coordination Compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Coordination entity','Ligands','Coordination polyhedra','Coordination number','NEW','12-247','12-121',NULL),
(230302,'chemistry','Which of the following are also referred as Lewis acids?','Central atom','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 247; Paragraph 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Definition of terms pertaining to Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Coordination entity','Ligands','Central atom','Coordination polyhedra','NEW','12-247','12-121',NULL),
(230303,'chemistry','In a coordination entity, the atom to which a fixed number\nof groups are bound in a definite geometrical arrangement\naround it, is called the ____.','Central atom','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 247; Paragraph 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Definition of terms pertaining to Coordination Compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Coordination entity','Ligands','Central atom','Coordination polyhedra','NEW','12-247','12-121',NULL),
(230304,'chemistry','Which of the following can be ligands?','All of these','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 247; Paragraph 3)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Definition of terms pertaining to Coordination Compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Proteins','Cl⁻','H₂O','All of these','NEW','12-247','12-121',NULL),
(230305,'chemistry','The ions or molecules bound to the central atom/ion in the\ncoordination entity are called ____.','ligands','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 247; Paragraph 3)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Definition of terms pertaining to Coordination Compounds',NULL,'1','fillup','lig,an,ds',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-247','12-121',NULL),
(230306,'chemistry','Which of the following is unidentate ligands?','All of these','When a ligand is bound to a metal ion through a single donor\natom, as with Cl–, H2O or NH3, the ligand is said to be unidentate.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 247; Paragraph 4)\\','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Definition of terms pertaining to Coordination Compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','NH₃','Cl⁻','H₂O','All of these','NEW','12-247','12-121',NULL),
(230307,'chemistry','Which of the following is bidentate ligands?','Oxalate','When a ligand can bind through two donor atoms as in\nH2NCH2CH2NH2 (ethane-1,2-diamine) or C2O4\n2– (oxalate), the ligand is said to be didentate.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 247; Paragraph 4)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Definition of terms pertaining to Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Ammonia','Oxalate','EDTA','Cyanide ion','NEW','12-247','12-121',NULL),
(230308,'chemistry','Which of the following ligand is represented in the diagram(n2301)','NH₃','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 247; Paragraph 4)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Definition of terms pertaining to Coordination Compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','Cl⁻','Co','NH₃','None of them','NEW','12-247','12-121','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/230308q.png'),
(230309,'chemistry','How many carbon atoms are present in Ethylenediaminetetraacetate ion?','10','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 247; Paragraph 4)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Definition of terms pertaining to Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','4','6','8','10','NEW','12-247','12-121',NULL),
(230310,'chemistry','What is false about Ethylenediaminetetraacetate ion?','It can bind through four nitrogen and two oxygen atoms to a central metal ion.','Ethylenediaminetetraacetate ion (EDTA4–) is\nan important hexadentate ligand. It can bind through two\nnitrogen and four oxygen atoms to a central metal ion.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 247; Paragraph 4)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Definition of terms pertaining to Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','It is hexadentate ligand.','It can bind through two nitrogen and four oxygen atoms to a central metal ion.','It can bind through four nitrogen and two oxygen atoms to a central metal ion.','All of these','NEW','12-247','12-121',NULL),
(230311,'chemistry','When a di- or polydentate ligand uses its two or more donor\natoms simultaneously to bind a single metal ion, it is said to be a\n____ ligand','chelate','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 247; Paragraph 5)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Definition of terms pertaining to Coordination Compounds',NULL,'1','fillup','ch,ela,te,mono,den',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-247','12-121',NULL),
(230312,'chemistry','Chelate complexes tend to be ___ stable than similar complexes containing unidentate\nligands.','more','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 247; Paragraph 5)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Definition of terms pertaining to Coordination Compounds',NULL,'1','fillup','mo,re,le,ss',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-247','12-121',NULL),
(230313,'chemistry','Which ligand can have denticity of 6?','EDTA','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 247; Paragraph 4)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Definition of terms pertaining to Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','EDTA','Ethane-1,2 diamine','Oxalate','All of these','NEW','12-247','12-121',NULL),
(230314,'chemistry','Which ligand has two different donor atom and either of\nthe two ligetes in the complex ?','Ambidentate','Ligand which has two different donor atoms and either of\nthe two ligetes in the complex is called ambidentate\nligand.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 247; Paragraph 5)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Definition of terms pertaining to Coordination Compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Ambidentate','Bidentate','Unidentate','Polydentate','NEW','12-247','12-121',NULL),
(230315,'chemistry','Which ion is example of ambidentate ligand?','SCN⁻','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 247; Paragraph 5)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Definition of terms pertaining to Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','SCN⁻','Cl⁻','NH₃','CN⁻','NEW','12-247','12-121',NULL),
(230316,'chemistry','Thiocyanate ion can coordinate through which of the following atoms?','S or N','SCN– ion can coordinate through the\nsulphur or nitrogen atom.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 247; Paragraph 5)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Definition of terms pertaining to Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','S or N','S or C','C or O','C or N','NEW','12-247','12-121',NULL),
(230317,'chemistry','Which term can be defined as the number of ligand donor atoms to which the metal is\ndirectly bonded?','Coordination number','The coordination number (CN) of a metal ion in a complex can be\ndefined as the number of ligand donor atoms to which the metal is\ndirectly bonded.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 247; Paragraph 6)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Definition of terms pertaining to Coordination Compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Coordination polyhedra','Coordination number','Central atom','Coordination entity','NEW','12-247','12-121',NULL),
(230318,'chemistry','What is the coordination of Co in [Co(en)₃]³⁺?','6','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 247; Paragraph 6)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Definition of terms pertaining to Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','6','3','4','8','NEW','12-247','12-121',NULL),
(230319,'chemistry','What determines the coordination number?','Only sigma bonds formed by ligand and central atom.','It is important to note here that coordination number of the central\natom/ion is determined only by the number of sigma bonds formed by\nthe ligand with the central atom/ion.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 248; Paragraph 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Definition of terms pertaining to Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Only sigma bonds formed by ligand and central atom.','Both sigma and pi bonds formed by ligand and the central atom.','Only pi bonds formed by central atom and ligand.','Pi bonds not involved in bonding is included in coordination number.','NEW','12-248','12-122',NULL),
(230320,'chemistry','The central atom/ion and the ligands attached to it are enclosed in\nsquare bracket and is collectively termed as the','Coordination sphere','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 248; Paragraph 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Definition of terms pertaining to Coordination Compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Coordination entity','Coordination sphere','Coordination polyhedra','Ligands','NEW','12-248','12-122',NULL),
(230321,'chemistry','The ionisable groups are written ___ the bracket and are called counter ions.','outside','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 248; Paragraph 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Definition of terms pertaining to Coordination Compounds',NULL,'1','fillup','out,si,de,in',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-248','12-122',NULL),
(230401,'chemistry','Which the following rule is incorrect for writing the formulas of coordination compounds?','The placement of ligand in the list depends on its charge','The central atom is listed first.\n The ligands are then listed in alphabetical order. The placement of\na ligand in the list does not depend on its charge.\n Polydentate ligands are also listed alphabetically. In case of\nabbreviated ligand, the first letter of the abbreviation is used to\ndetermine the position of the ligand in the alphabetical order.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 249; Paragraph 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Formulas of Mononuclear Coordination entities',NULL,'2','mcq','The central atom is listed first.','The placement of ligand in the list depends on its charge','The ligands are listed in alphabetical order.','Polydentate ligands are also listed alphbetically.','NEW','12-249','12-123',NULL),
(230402,'chemistry','Among the following statements, which statement are true with respect to rules for writing formulas of coordination compounds?','All of these','The formula for the entire coordination entity, whether charged or\nnot, is enclosed in square brackets. When ligands are polyatomic,\ntheir formulas are enclosed in parentheses. Ligand abbreviations\nare also enclosed in parentheses. There should be no space between the ligands and the metal\nwithin a coordination sphere.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 249; Paragraph 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Formulas of Mononuclear Coordination entities',NULL,'2','mcq','The formula for the entire coordination entity, whether charged or\nnot, is enclosed in square brackets.','When ligands are polyatomic,\ntheir formulas are enclosed in parentheses.','There should be no space between the ligands and the metal\nwithin a coordination sphere.','All of these','NEW','12-249','12-123',NULL),
(230403,'chemistry','According 2004 IUPAC draft, On basis of what basis ligands are sorted in formula?','Alphabetically','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 249; Paragraph 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Formulas of Mononuclear Coordination entities',NULL,'1','mcq','Charge','Strength','Molecular size','Alphabetically','NEW','12-249','12-123',NULL),
(230404,'chemistry','When the formula of a charged coordination entity is to be written\nwithout that of the counter ion, the charge is indicated outside the\nsquare brackets as a right ____ with the number before the\nsign.','superscript','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 249; Paragraph 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Formulas of Mononuclear Coordination entities',NULL,'1','fillup','sup,er,sc,ri,pt,sub',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-249','12-123',NULL),
(230405,'biology','Small plants emerge from the buds called eyes in?','Potato tuber','Small plants emerge from the buds called eyes in potato tuber. Each tuber or potato has several buds.It\'s from these buds that new potato plants can grow.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:8, paragraph no:3)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Asexual Reproduction 3',NULL,'1','mcq','Ginger','Potato tuber','Sugarcane','Dahlia','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230406,'biology','When the nodes come in contact with the damp soil and water they produce roots and new plants.','TRUE','Site of origin of the new plantlets  is nodes present in modified stems of these plants.The nodes have meristematic cells. Nodes when come in contact with damp soil or water, they produce roots and gives rise to new plants.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:8, paragraph no:3)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Asexual Reproduction 3',NULL,'2','mcq','TRUE','FALSE',NULL,NULL,'DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230407,'biology','Algae and Fungi reproduces through','Both Asexual and Sexual methods of Reproduction','Asexual reproduction is the common method of reproduction in organisms that have a relatively simple organisation like algae and fungi and that they shift to sexual mode of reproduction just before the onset of adverse conditions.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:5, paragraph no:4)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Asexual Reproduction 3',NULL,'2','mcq','Asexual reproduction only','Both Sexual reproduction and fragmentation','Both Asexual and Sexual methods of Reproduction','Sporulation only','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230408,'biology','Identify the diagram (2304)','Zoospores of Chlamydomonas','Figure 1.3a NCERT class 12 page no: 6','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Asexual Reproduction 3',NULL,'3','mcq','Zoospores of Chlamydomonas','Conidia of Penicillium','Buds in Hydra','Gemmules in sponge','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/230408q.png'),
