(230420,'biology','In Protists and Monerans, ____________ is itself a mode of reproduction.','Cell division','In Protists and Monerans, the organism or the parent cell divides by mitosis into two to give rise to new individuals. Thus, in these organisms cell division is itself a mode of reproduction.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:5, paragraph no:4)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Asexual Reproduction 3',NULL,'3','fillup','Ce,ll di,vi,si,on',NULL,NULL,NULL,'DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230421,'biology','The term vegetative reproduction is frequently used in,','Plants','In animals and other simple organisms the term asexual is used unambiguously, in plants, the term vegetative reproduction is frequently used.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:7, paragraph no:3)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Asexual Reproduction 3',NULL,'2','mcq','Animals','Plants','Monera','Protists','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230422,'biology','The formation of vegetative propagules is asexual process because of which of the following reason?','It does not involve two parents','The formation of vegetative propagules does not involve two parents, the process involved is asexual.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:8, paragraph no:1)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Asexual Reproduction 3',NULL,'3','mcq','It involves more than two parents','It does not involve two parents','Because the offsprings are exactly different from the parent','It involves two parents','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
