(230516,'chemistry','What is IUPAC name for[Cr(NH₃)₃(H₂O)₃]Cl₃?','triamminetriaquachromium(III) chloride','The complex ion is inside the square bracket, which is\na cation. The amine ligands are named before the aqua ligands according to alphabetical order. Since there are three chloride ions in\nthe compound, the charge on the complex ion must be +3 (since the compound is electrically neutral). From the charge on the complex\nion and the charge on the ligands, we can calculate the oxidation number of the metal. In this example, all the ligands are neutral molecules. Therefore, the oxidation number of chromium must be\nthe same as the charge of the complex ion, +3.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 250; Paragraph 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Naming of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','triamminetetraaquachromium(II) chlorine','triamminetriaquachromium(III) chloride','hexaaminetriaquachromium(III) chloride','triamminetriaquachromium(IV) chloride','NEW','12-250','12-124',NULL),
(230517,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for [Co(NH₃)₄(H₂O)Cl]Cl₂?','Tetraamineaquachloridocobalt(III) chloride','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 250; Example 9.1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Naming of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Tetraamineaquachloridocobalt(III) chloride','Tetraammineaquachlorocobalt(III)chloride','Tetraamminehydrochloridocobalt(III) chloride','Tetraammineaquachlorylcobalt(III) chloride','NEW','12-250','12-124',NULL),
