(230525,'biology','Process of formation of the two types of gametes – male and female.','Gametogenesis','As you are already aware, gametogenesis refers to the process of formation of the two types of gametes – male and female.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:10, paragraph no:5)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Sexual Reproduction',NULL,'2','mcq','Gametogenesis','Oogenesis','Spermatogenesis','Spermiogenesis','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230526,'biology','Choose the correct option:','In perennial species it is very difficult to define the vegetative, reproductive and senescent phases.','Perennial plants live for many years that is, they have a very long life span. Hence, it becomes very difficult to define and study their vegetative, reproductive and senescent phases.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:9, paragraph no:4)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Sexual Reproduction',NULL,'2','mcq','In perennial species it is very difficult to define the vegetative, reproductive and senescent phases.','In perennial species all the phases are clearly demarcated','In biennial species all the phases are not clearly demarcated','In biennial species it is very difficult to define the vegetative, reproductive and senescent phases.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230527,'biology','Clear cut vegetative, reproductive and senescent phases are exhibited by?','Both annual and biennial plants','Annuals complete their life cycle in one year while biennials complete in two years. Hence, vegetative, reproductive and senescent phases are clearly visible.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:9, paragraph no:4)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Sexual Reproduction',NULL,'1','mcq','Perennial plants','Biennial Plants','Both annual and biennial plants','Annual Plants','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230528,'biology','Unusual flowering phenomenon is exhibited by ?','Bamboo species and Strobilanthus Kunthiana','A few plants exhibit unusual flowering phenomenon; some of them such as bamboo species flower only once in their lifetime, generally after 50-100 years similarlyStrobilanthus kunthiana (neelakuranji), flowers once in 12 years.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:9, paragraph no:4)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Sexual Reproduction',NULL,'2','mcq','Peepal tree and bamboo tree','Bamboo tree and mango tree','Strobilanthus Kunthiana and Peepal tree','Bamboo species and Strobilanthus Kunthiana','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230529,'biology','Choose the incorrect statement regarding strobilanthus kunthiana:','Strobilanthus kunthiana flowered during September - October 2009.','Strobilanthus kunthiana (neelakuranji), flowers once in 12 years. Strobilanthus kunthiana flowered during September - October 2006.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:9, paragraph no:4)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Sexual Reproduction',NULL,'2','mcq','Strobilanthus kunthiana (neelakuranji), flowers once in 12 years','Unusual flowering phenomenon is exhibited by Strobilanthus Kunthiana.','Strobilanthus kunthiana flowered during September - October 2009.','It\'s mass flowering transformed large tracks of hilly areas into blue stretches and attracted a large number of tourists','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230530,'biology','In animals the juvenile phase is followed by _________  and __________ changes prior to active reproductive behavior.','Morphological and physiological','In animals, the juvenile phase is followed by morphological and physiological changes prior to active reproductive behaviour.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:9, paragraph no:4)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Sexual Reproduction',NULL,'2','mcq','Morphological and reproductive','Anatomical and physiological','Morphological and physiological','Anatomical and reproductive','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230531,'biology','Choose the correct option:','Birds living in nature lay eggs only seasonally','Birds living in nature lay eggs only seasonally. However, birds in captivity can be made to lay eggs throughout the year. In this case, laying eggs is not related to reproduction but is a commercial exploitation for human welfare.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:9, paragraph no:6)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Sexual Reproduction',NULL,'3','mcq','Birds living in nature can be made to lay eggs throughout the year','Birds in captivity lay eggs only seasonally','Birds living in nature lay eggs only seasonally','Birds living in nature do not lay eggs only seasonally','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230532,'biology','The females of __________________ exhibit cyclical changes in the activities of ovaries and accessory ducts as well as hormones during the reproductive phase.','Placental mammals','The females of placental mammals exhibit cyclical changes in the activities of ovaries and accessory ducts as well as hormones during reproductive phase.Many mammals are reproductively active only during certain periods in a year. Some other mammals, are reproductively active throughout the year.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:9, paragraph no:6)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Sexual Reproduction',NULL,'2','mcq','Placental mammals','Reptiles','Aquatic mammals','Birds','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230533,'biology','Non primate mammals include:','Rats,dogs,deers,cows','Non-primates are animals which do not include characteristics similar to primates. Birds, reptiles and amphibians belong to this group. Some mammals are also considered as non-primates.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:9, paragraph no:6)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Sexual Reproduction',NULL,'1','mcq','Rats,deers,monkeys,dogs','Tigers,apes,rats,dogs','Rats,deers,humans,dogs','Rats,dogs,deers,cows','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230534,'biology','When it comes to sexual mode of reproduction, plants, animals, and fungi share a ___________ pattern','Similar','A study of diverse organisms–plants, animals or fungi–show that though they differ so greatly in external morphology, internal structure and physiology, when it comes to sexual mode of reproduction, surprisingly, they share a similar pattern.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:8, paragraph no:6)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Sexual Reproduction',NULL,'2','mcq','Different','Similar','Non parallel','Non significant','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230535,'biology','Choose the correct statements regarding old age.\n\ni) Old age ultimately leads to death\n\nii) There are concomitant changes during this last phase of life such as speeding of metabolism\n\niii) The end of reproductive phase can be considered as one of the parameters of senescence or old age.\n\niv) There are concomitant changes during this last phase of life such as slowing of metabolism','i, iii, and iv','Old age, also called senescence, in human beings, the final stage of the normal life span.The end of reproductive phase can be considered as one of the parameters of senescence or old age.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:10, paragraph no:2)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Sexual Reproduction',NULL,'2','mcq','i, ii, and iii','ii, ii, and iv','i, ii, and iv','i, iii, and iv','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230536,'biology','Assertion:The end of reproductive phase can be considered as one of the parameters of senescence or old age\n. \nReason:There are other progressive changes during this last phase of life such as slowing of metabolism','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Old age, also called senescence, in human beings, the final stage of the normal life span.The end of reproductive phase can be considered as one of the parameters of senescence or old age.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:10, paragraph no:2)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Sexual Reproduction',NULL,'2','mcq','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Assertion is true but Reason is false','Both Assertion and Reason are false','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230537,'biology','What regulates the reproductive processes and the associated behavioral expressions of organisms ?','Interaction between hormones and certain environmental factors','In both plants and animals, hormones are responsible for the transitions between the three phases. Interaction between hormones and certain environmental factors regulate the reproductive processes and the associated behavioural expressions of organisms.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:10, paragraph no:3)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Sexual Reproduction',NULL,'2','mcq','Interaction between hormones and certain physical factors','Interaction between hormones and certain environmental factors','Interaction between chemicals and certain environmental factors','Interaction between physiological and certain environmental factors','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230538,'biology','Structures associated with sexual reproduction are same in all living organisms','FALSE','After attainment of maturity, all sexually reproducing organisms exhibit events and processes that have remarkable fundamental similarity, even though the structures associated with sexual reproduction are indeed very different.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:10, paragraph no:4)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Sexual Reproduction',NULL,'1','mcq','TRUE','FALSE',NULL,NULL,'DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230539,'biology','Events of sexual reproduction are','Elaborated and Complex','The events of sexual reproduction though elaborate and complex, follow a regular sequence. Sexual reproduction is characterised by the fusion of the male and female gametes, the formation of zygote and embryogenesis.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:10, paragraph no:4)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Sexual Reproduction',NULL,'1','mcq','Elaborated and Complex','Short and Complex','Elaborated and Simple','Complex','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230540,'biology','Assertion:Events of sexual reproduction are Elaborated and Complex \nReason: Events of Sexual reproduction follow irregular pattern.','Assertion is true but Reason is false','The events of sexual reproduction though elaborate and complex, follow a regular sequence. For convenience these sequential events may be grouped into three distinct stages namely, the pre-fertilisation, fertilisation and the post-fertilisation events.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:10, paragraph no:4)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Sexual Reproduction',NULL,'2','mcq','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Assertion is true but Reason is false','Both Assertion and Reason are false','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230541,'biology','Events of sexual reproduction are grouped into three stages namely:','Pre-Fertilization,Fertilization And Post Fertilization','For convenience events of sexual reproduction may be grouped into three distinct stages namely, the pre-fertilisation, fertilisation and the post-fertilisation events.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:10, paragraph no:4)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Sexual Reproduction',NULL,'1','mcq','Pre-Fertilization,Fertilization And Post Fertilization','Mitosis,Fertilization And Meiosis','Mitosis,Fertilization And Post Fertilization','Pre-Fertilization,Fertilization And Meiosis','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
