(230602,'chemistry','Assertion: Isomers differ in one or more physical or chemical properties.\nReason: Isomers have different arrangement of atoms.','Both assertion and reason are true and reason is a correct explanation of the assertion.','Isomers are two or more compounds that have the same chemical\nformula but a different arrangement of atoms. Because of the different\narrangement of atoms, they differ in one or more physical or chemical\nproperties.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 251; Paragraph 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Isomerism in Coordination Compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','Both assertion and reason are true but reason is not a correct explanation of the assertion.','Both assertion and reason are true and reason is a correct explanation of the assertion.','Both assertion and reason are false.','Assertion is true and reason is false.','NEW','12-251','12-125',NULL),
