(230621,'chemistry','Which ligand in complex will be capable of showing Linkage isomerism?','NCS⁻','Linkage isomerism arises in a coordination compound containing\nambidentate ligand. A simple example is provided by complexes\ncontaining the thiocyanate ligand, NCS–, which may bind through the\nnitrogen to give M–NCS or through sulphur to give M–SCN.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 253; Paragraph 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Isomerism in Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Cl⁻','CN⁻','NCS⁻','All of these','NEW','12-253','12-127',NULL),
