(230901,'chemistry','The crystal field theory (CFT) is an ___ model.','electrostatic','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 257; Paragraph 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Crystal Field Theory',NULL,'1','fillup','el,ec,tr,os,tat,ic',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-257','12-131',NULL),
(230902,'chemistry','What are the assumption made in CFT?','Neutral ligands are treated as point dipoles.','Ligands are treated\nas point charges in case of anions or point dipoles in case of neutral\nmolecules. The five d orbitals in an isolated gaseous metal atom/ion\nhave same energy, i.e., they are degenerate. This degeneracy is\nmaintained if a spherically symmetrical field of negative charges\nsurrounds the metal atom/ion.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 257; Paragraph 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Crystal Field Theory',NULL,'2','mcq','Neutral ligands are treated as point dipoles.','The five d orbitals in an isolated gaseous metal atom/ion\nhave different energies.','Crystal Field theory is based on electrodynamic model.','All of these','NEW','12-257','12-131',NULL),
(230903,'chemistry','Assertion: The degeneracy of d-orbitals in gaseous state is maintained if a spherically symmetrical field of negative charges surround them.\nReason: When negative field is due to ligands, it becomes asymmetrical and the degeneracy of the d orbitals is lifted.','Both assertion and reason are true but reason is not a correct explanation of the assertion.','Ligands are treated\nas point charges in case of anions or point dipoles in case of neutral molecules. The five d orbitals in an isolated gaseous metal atom/ion\nhave same energy, i.e., they are degenerate. This degeneracy is maintained if a spherically symmetrical field of negative charges\nsurrounds the metal atom/ion.However, when this negative field is due to ligands (either anions or the negative ends of dipolar molecules\nlike NH3 and H2O) in a complex, it becomes asymmetrical and the degeneracy of the d orbitals is lifted. It results in splitting of the d orbitals. The pattern of splitting depends upon the nature of the crystal\nfield.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 257; Paragraph 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Crystal Field Theory',NULL,'3','mcq','Both assertion and reason are true but reason is not a correct explanation of the assertion.','Both assertion and reason are true and reason is a correct explanation of the assertion.','Both assertion and reason are false.','Assertion is true and reason is false.','NEW','12-257','12-131',NULL),
(230904,'chemistry','Along which of the following orbitals ligand will experience more repulsion in octahedral coordination entities?','dₓ²-dᵧ²','In an octahedral coordination entity with six ligands surrounding\nthe metal atom/ion, there will be repulsion between the electrons in\nmetal d orbitals and the electrons (or negative charges) of the ligands.\nSuch a repulsion is more when the metal d orbital is directed towards\nthe ligand than when it is away from the ligand. Thus, the dₓ²-dᵧ²\nand d𝓏² orbitals which point towards the axes along the direction of\nthe ligand will experience more repulsion and will be raised in\nenergy;(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 257; Paragraph 3)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Crystal Field Theory',NULL,'2','mcq','dₓ²-dᵧ²','dₓᵧ','dᵧ𝓏','d𝓏ₓ','NEW','12-257','12-131',NULL),
(230905,'chemistry','Which of the following orbital will be lowered in energy as compared to average energy of octahedral entity in spherical field?','dₓᵧ','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 257; Paragraph 3)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Crystal Field Theory',NULL,'2','mcq','dₓ²-dᵧ²','dₓᵧ','d𝓏²','All of these','NEW','12-257','12-131',NULL),
(230906,'chemistry','What is meant by e𝓰 set in octahedral crystal field splitting?','Two orbitals of higher energy as compared to average energy.','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 257; Paragraph 3)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Crystal Field Theory',NULL,'1','mcq','Three orbitals of lower energy as compared to average energy.','Two orbitals of higher energy as compared to average energy.','Three orbitals of higher energy as compared to average energy.','Two orbitals of lower energy as compared to average energy.','NEW','12-257','12-131',NULL),
(230907,'chemistry','Splitting of the degenerate levels due to the presence of ____ in a definite geometry is termed as crystal field splitting.','ligands','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 258; Paragraph 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Crystal Field Theory',NULL,'1','fillup','li,gan,ds',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-258','12-132',NULL),
(230908,'chemistry','What will energy gap between e𝓰 orbitals and barycentre is crystal field splitting energy is X.','0.6X','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 258; Figure 9.8)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Crystal Field Theory',NULL,'3','mcq','0.4X','0.6X','0.8X','X','NEW','12-258','12-132',NULL),
(230909,'chemistry','On what factors does crystal field splitting energy depends upon?','All of these','The crystal field splitting, Do, depends upon the field\nproduced by the ligand and\ncharge on the metal ion.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 258; Paragraph 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Crystal Field Theory',NULL,'2','mcq','Ligands','Charge','Size of metal','All of these','NEW','12-258','12-132',NULL),
