(230919,'chemistry','For same metal, same ligands and metal-ligands distances, if crystal field splitting energy for octaheral field is 4500 X then what will be value for tetrahedral crystal field energy? (X is arbitary unit)','2000X','Which of the following statements about "Geometry of Coordination compounds" are true?\n\na. [Co(NH₃)₆]⁺³ has a spin paired complex.\n\nb. In tetrahedral complexes one s and 3 p orbitals are hybridised to form four equivalent orbitals oriented tetrahedrally.\n\nc.  [Ni(CO)₄] is has tetrahedral geometry but is paramagnetic','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Crystal Field Theory',NULL,'3','mcq','2000X','10125X','1000X','3423X','NEW','12-259','12-133',NULL),
(230920,'chemistry','Which of the following is true for tetraheral complexes?\nA. They lack centre of symmetry.\nB. Low spin configurations are rarely seen.\nC. Orbital splitting energy are very large.\nD. \'g\' subscript is not used with energy levels.','A, B, D','In tetrahedral geometry the orbital splitting energies are not\nsufficiently large for forcing pairing and,\ntherefore, low spin configurations are rarely\nobserved. The ‘g’ subscript is used for the\noctahedral and square planar complexes\nwhich have centre of symmetry. Since\ntetrahedral complexes lack symmetry, ‘g’\nsubscript is not used with energy levels.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 259; Paragraph 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Crystal Field Theory',NULL,'2','mcq','A, B, D','Only A','B and C only','All A, B, C and D','NEW','12-259','12-133',NULL),
(230921,'biology','In oviparous animals, after a period of _________ young ones hatch out','Incubation','The animals which give birth to their young ones through eggs are called oviparous animal.Eg,Birds, fishes and frogs. Adult birds sit on the eggs for a few days to keep them warm till they hatch. This is called as Incubation.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:16, paragraph no:1)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Post-fertilisation Events',NULL,'2','fillup','Inc,uba,tion,inf',NULL,NULL,NULL,'DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230922,'biology','In viviparous animals the developed zygote, after attaining a certain age of _________ the young ones are delivered out of the female organism.','Growth','In viviparous animals (majority of mammals including human beings), the zygote develops into a young one inside the body of the female organism. After attaining a certain stage of growth, the young ones are delivered out of the body of the female organism.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:16, paragraph no:1)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Post-fertilisation Events',NULL,'1','mcq','Maturity','Puberty','Growth','Senescence','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230923,'biology','In flowering plants, after fertilisation, the sepals,petals and stamens ______________.','Wither and fall off','After fertilization or pollination, the ovary of the flower develops into fruit. During this process, certain hormones are released by the plant which initiates the development of fruit. This leads to withering of the other parts such as petals, sepals and stamens.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:16, paragraph no:2)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Post-fertilisation Events',NULL,'2','mcq','Remain attached','Wither and fall off','Gets separated','Split into half','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230924,'biology','In flowering plants, pistil remains attached  to the plant','TRUE','Pistil remains attached to plant after fertilisation because it contains fertilised zygotes inside the ovules.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:16, paragraph no:2)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Post-fertilisation Events',NULL,'2','mcq','TRUE','FALSE',NULL,NULL,'DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230925,'biology','After dispersal, seeds germinate under _________  conditions to produce new plants.','Favourable','After dispersal, seeds germinate under favourable conditions to produce new plants.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:16, paragraph no:2)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Post-fertilisation Events',NULL,'2','mcq','Favourable','Unfavourable','Extreme','Harsh','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230926,'biology','Inside the mature ________ is the progenitor of next generation, the embryo.','Seed','In flowering plants, after fertilisation, ovary develops into fruit and ovules mature into seeds. Inside the mature seed is the progenitor of the next generation, the embryo. (Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:17, paragraph no:7)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Post-fertilisation Events',NULL,'2','fillup','Se,ed,we',NULL,NULL,NULL,'DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230927,'biology','Post Fertilization Events involve:','Formation of zygote,Embryogenesis','Post-fertilization is a series of events that takes place after fertilization to develop a seed from an ovule and a fruit from an ovary. (Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:15, paragraph no:2)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Post-fertilisation Events',NULL,'1','mcq','Formation of zygote,Embryogenesis','Gamete transfer,Gametogenesis','Formation of zygote,Gametogenesis',NULL,'DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(230928,'biology','In animals the zygote starts developing soon after it\'s formation.','TRUE','In animals the zygote starts developing soon after it\'s formation.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:17, paragraph no:6)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Post-fertilisation Events',NULL,'2','mcq','TRUE','FALSE',NULL,NULL,'DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(231102,'chemistry','What is the shape of Hexacarbonyl chromium(0) ?','Octahedral','Tetracarbonylnickel(0) is tetrahedral, pentacarbonyliron(0) is trigonalbipyramidal while\nhexacarbonyl chromium(0) is octahedral.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 261; Paragraph 3)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Bonding in Metal Carbonyls',NULL,'1','mcq','trigonal bipyramidal','square pyramidal','Octahedral','Tetrahedral','NEW','12-261','12-135',NULL),
(231103,'chemistry','How many bridge CO are present in Decacarbonyldimanganese(0)?','0','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 262; Figure 9.13)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Bonding in Metal Carbonyls',NULL,'2','mcq','0','2','5','10','NEW','12-262','12-136',NULL),
(231104,'chemistry','In Decacarbonyldimanganese(0), what is the shape of each Mn(CO)₅ unit?','square pyramidal','Decacarbonyldimanganese(0) is made up of two square pyramidal\nMn(CO)5 units joined by a Mn – Mn bond.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 261; Paragraph 4)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Bonding in Metal Carbonyls',NULL,'1','mcq','trigonal bipyramidal','square pyramidal','tetrahedral','square planar','NEW','12-261','12-135',NULL),
(231105,'chemistry','How many bridging CO are present in Octacarbonyldicobalt(0)?','2','Octacarbonyldicobalt(0)\nhas a Co – Co bond bridged by two CO groups.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 261; Paragraph 4)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Bonding in Metal Carbonyls',NULL,'2','mcq','2','0','4','1','NEW','12-262','12-136',NULL),
(231114,'biology','In some plants, the female gamete develops into embryo without fertilisation. This phenomenon is known as (2019)','Parthenogenesis','Parthenogenesis is the spontaneous development of an embryo from an unfertilised egg cell. It naturally occurs in variety of plants, where parthenogenesis usually is found in combination with apomeiosis (the omission of meiosis) and pseudogamous (with or without central cell fertilisation), endosperm formation, together known as apomixis (clonal seed production). Parthenocarpy is development of fruit without fertilisation.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:4, paragraph no:3)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','Parthenogenesis','Autogamy','Parthenocarpy','Syngamy','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(231115,'biology','Which of the following flowers only once in its lifetime?(2018)','Bamboo species','Certain bamboo species are monocarpic, i.e., flower generally only once in their lifetime (after 50-100 years). Other plants (jackfruit, mango and papaya) are polycarpic, i.e., produce flowers and fruits many times during their lifetime.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:9, paragraph no:4)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','Bamboo species','Jackfruit','Mango','Papaya','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(231116,'biology','Which one of the following generates new genetic combinations leading to variation? (2016)','Sexual reproduction','Sexual reproduction involves formation and fusion of male and female gametes. Gamete formation is accomplished through meiotic cell division which involves crossing over between non-sister chromatids of homologous chromosomes leading to new genetic recombination in gametes. Random fusion of these male and female gametes lead to the genetic variability in the offspring which although resemble their parents but also exhibit new traits of their own.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:8, paragraph no:5)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','Vegetative reproduction','Parthenogenesis','Sexual reproduction','Nucellar polyembryony','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(231117,'biology','Match column I with column II and select the correct option using the codes given below.','Pistils fused together-Syncarpous,Formation of gametes-Gametogenesis,Hyphae of higher ascomycetes-Dikaryotic,Unisexual female-Pistillate','Pistils fused together-Syncarpous,Formation of gametes-Gametogenesis,Hyphae of higher ascomycetes-Dikaryotic,Unisexual female-Pistillate.','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'3','match','Pistils fused together,Syncarpous','Formation of gametes,Gametogenesis','Hyphae of higher ascomycetes,Dikaryotic','Unisexual female,Pistillate','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(231118,'biology','Flowers are unisexual in [2015]','Cucumber','In cucumber, unisexual flower, separate male and female flowers are present on the same plant (monoecious plant)Note, Monecious plant  but dioecious flower.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:11, paragraph no:3)','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','China rose','Onion','Pea','Cucumber','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(231119,'biology','Product of sexual reproduction generally generates (2013)','New genetic combination leading to variation','Sexual reproduction always involves meiosis (zygotic in case of haploid individuals and gametic in case of diploid individuals). Meiosis results in crossing over between chromosomes during prophase I generating new recombinations. Besides, sexual reproduction generally involves combination of genes from two different organisms. Thus, sexual reproduction generates new genetic combinations leading to variations.','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','New genetic combination leading to variation','Large biomass','Longer viability of seeds','Prolonged dormancy','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(231120,'biology','Meiosis takes place in (2013)','Meiocyte','Gemmule and conidia are asexual propagules thus, no meiosis takes place in them. Megaspores are haploid which are formed as a result of meiosis of diploid megaspore mother cell. Meiocyte is any cell that undergoes meiosis.','Reproduction >> Reproduction in Organisms >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','Gemmule','Megaspore','Meiocyte','Conidia','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(231201,'chemistry','Which of the following ccordination compounds find use in many qualitative and quantitative chemical analysis?','All of these','Coordination compounds find use in many qualitative and\nquantitative chemical analysis. The familiar colour reactions given by metal ions with a number of ligands (especially chelating ligands),\nas a result of formation of coordination entities, form the basis for their detection and estimation by classical and instrumental methods of analysis. Examples of such reagents include EDTA, DMG (dimethylglyoxime), a–nitroso–b–naphthol, cupron, etc.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 262; Paragraph 3)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Importance and Application of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','EDTA','Cupron','DMG','All of these','NEW','12-262','12-136',NULL),
