(231206,'chemistry','Anti-pernicious anaemia factor is coordination compound of','Co','Haemoglobin, the red\npigment of blood which acts as oxygen carrier is a coordination\ncompound of iron. Vitamin B12, cyanocobalamine, the anti–\npernicious anaemia factor, is a coordination compound of cobalt.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 263; Paragraph 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Importance and Application of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Cu','Co','Cr','Rh','NEW','12-263','12-137',NULL),
