(151020,'biology','Which is synthetic auxin','NAA','Auxins like IAA and indole butyric acid (IBA) have been isolated from plants. NAA (naphthalene acetic acid) and 2, 4-D (2, 4-dichlorophenoxyacetic) are synthetic auxins.','Plant Physiology >> Plant Growth and Development >> Auxins',NULL,'1','mcq','IAA','IBA','NAA','Florigen','NEW','11-248','11-175',NULL),
(151021,'biology','Leaf fall occurs when the content of','Auxin decreases','Auxins promote flowering e.g. in pineapples. They help to prevent fruit and leaf drop at early stages','Plant Physiology >> Plant Growth and Development >> Auxins',NULL,'1','mcq','Auxin increases','Gibberellic acid decreases','Auxin decreases','Abscisic acid decreases','NEW','11-248','11-175','/ncert/pyq/physics/mcq/151021q.png'),
(151022,'biology','Which is not a part of plant hormone','Phytochrome','All others are plant hormones that regulate certain plant activities, their growth and developement but phytochrome is not a hormone.','Plant Physiology >> Plant Growth and Development >> Auxins',NULL,'2','mcq','IAA','Phytochrome','Florigen','Cytokinin','NEW','11-248','11-175','/ncert/pyq/physics/mcq/151022q.png'),
(151023,'biology','The phytohormones ,isolated from human urine showed which of the following properties- \nA) Bolting effect. \nB) Apical dominance. \nC) Control of xylem differentiation. \nD) Promote leaf senescence.','Both B and C','Auxins (from Greek ‘auxein’ : to grow) was first isolated from human urine. Kogl and Haagen Smith discovered the first naturally occurring Auxin in human urine. Auxin is responsible for regulating cell division, plant growth, differentiation, and other physiological processes. Indole -3- acetic acid (auxin class) was the first plant hormone isolated from human urine. This hormone helps in the growth of the plant in the tip regions.\nUsing this hormone, the growth of the shoot in the callus culture can be promoted. As u know like any other ,Auxin it promoted apical dominance and controlled differentiation of xylem.','Plant Physiology >> Plant Growth and Development >> Auxins',NULL,'2','mcq','Both A and D','Both B and D','Both B and C','Both A and C','NEW','11-248','11-175',NULL),
(151024,'biology','Which hormone is used to produce parthenocarpic or seedless Banana and tomatoes','Auxin','Auxins also induce parthenocarpy, e.g., in tomatoes. They are widely used as herbicides. 2, 4-D, widely used to kill dicotyledonous weeds, does not affect mature monocotyledonous plants. It is used to prepare weed-free lawns by gardeners.','Plant Physiology >> Plant Growth and Development >> Auxins',NULL,'2','mcq','Auxin','Kinetin','GA','ABA','NEW','11-248','11-175',NULL),
