(191004,'chemistry','A : Starch and gelatin are lyophillic colloid.\nR : They have strong interaction with the dispersion medium.','Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A','Assertion:\nProteins, starch, and rubber are lyophilic colloids.\nReason:\nThey have a strong interaction with the dispersion medium.Other examples of lyophilic colloids include gum and gelatin. These are solvent loving colloids which are stable and not easily coagulated by electrolytes. Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation for Assertion','Physical chemistry >> Surface chemistry >> Assertion & reason',NULL,'1','mcq','Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A','Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A.','A is true but R is false.','Both A and R are false.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
