(70308,'chemistry','Choose the correct statement --> \nI. We can write equilibrium relation for the reaction which involve solid or liquid reactants or products.\nII. Molar concentration of solid or liquid is taken as constant.','Both are true','We can simplify equilibrium expressions for the heterogeneous equilibria involving a pure liquid or a pure solid, as the molar concentration of a pure solid or liquid is constant (i.e., independent of the amount present). In other words if a substance ‘X’ is involved, then [X(s)] and [X(l)] are constant, whatever the amount of ‘X’ is taken.(NCERT chemistry class 11; page 203 ; paragraph 3)','Physical Chemistry >> Equilibrium >> Chemical processes',NULL,'2','mcq','Both are false','I is true but II is false','I is false but II is true','Both are true','NEW','11-203','11-179',NULL),
(70309,'chemistry','The value of Kₚ for the reaction, CO₂ (g) + C (s) ⇌ 2CO (g) is 3.0 at 1000 K. If initially P = 0.48 bar CO₂ and P = 0 bar and pure graphite is CO present, calculate the equilibrium partial pressures of CO and CO₂.','Pr. of CO₂ = 0.15 bar; Pr. of CO = 0.66 bar','(NCERT chemistry class 11; page 204 ; Problem 7.6) diagram(ne0705)','Physical Chemistry >> Equilibrium >> Chemical processes',NULL,'3','mcq','Pr. of CO₂ = 0.15 bar; Pr. of CO = 0.66 bar','Pr. of CO₂ = 0.015 bar; Pr. of CO = 0.66 bar','Pr. of CO₂ = 0.15 bar; Pr. of CO = 0.066 bar','Pr. of CO₂ = 0.015 bar; Pr. of CO = 0.066 bar','NEW','11-204','11-180',NULL),
(2000034241,'physics','A particle moves from a point $(-2 \\hat{i}+5 \\hat{j})$ to $(4 \\hat{j}+3 \\hat{k})$ when a force of $(4 \\hat{i}+3 \\hat{j}) N$ is applied. How much work has been done by the force ?','C','$\\vec{S}=$ Displacement $=(4 \\hat{j}+3 \\hat{k})-(-2 \\hat{i}+5 \\hat{j})$<br>$=2 \\hat{i}-\\hat{j}+3 \\hat{k}$<br>Work $=\\vec{F} \\cdot \\vec{S}=(4 \\hat{i}+3 \\hat{j}) \\cdot(2 \\hat{i}-\\hat{j}+3 \\hat{k})=5 \\mathrm{j}$','Work','Work, Energy and Power','Medium',NULL,'8 $J$','11 $J$','5 $J$','2 $J$',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(70310,'biology','_________ make up more than onehalf the volume of neural tissue in our body','Neuroglia','The neuroglial cell which constitute the rest of the neural system protect and support neurons. Neuroglia make up more than onehalf the volume of neural tissue in our body (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:105, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Muscle And Neural Tissue',NULL,'2','mcq','Neurons','Neuroglia','Neurolemma','both a and b','NEW','11-105',NULL,NULL),
