(70401,'chemistry','Choose the correct stament/s \n(i)Equilibrium constant is temperature dependent \n(ii)Equilibrium constant remains the same whether or not the reaction is balanced','only (i) is correct','Equilibrium constant is temperature dependent having one unique value for a particular reaction represented by a balanced equation at a given temperature.\n(NCERT chemistry class 11; page 205 ; paragraph 1)','Physical Chemistry >> Equilibrium >> Application of equilibrium constants',NULL,'1','mcq','only (i) is correct','both statements are incorrect','only (ii) is correct','both the statements are correct','NEW','11-205','11-181',NULL),
(70402,'chemistry','H₂(g) + Cl₂ (g) ⇌ 2HCl(g) at 300K has K꜀ = 4.0 × 10³¹. The equilibrium conc. for all of the species are','[HCl] >>> [H₂], [Cl₂]','If Kc > 10³, products predominate over reactants, i.e., if Kc is very large, the reaction proceeds nearly to completion. Consider the following examples:(NCERT chemistry class 11; page 205 ; paragraph 3)','Physical Chemistry >> Equilibrium >> Application of equilibrium constants',NULL,'2','mcq','[HCl] > [H₂] > [Cl₂]','[HCl] >>> [H₂], [Cl₂]','[HCl] = [H₂] =[Cl₂]','[HCl] <<< [H₂], [Cl₂]','NEW','11-205','11-181',NULL),
(70403,'chemistry','Choose the correct statements \n\n(i)The expression of equilibrium constant involves equilibrium concentration only.\n\n(ii)The expression of reaction quotient may or may not involve equilibrium concentration.\n\n(iii)Numerical value of Equilibrium constant and reaction helps to determine the extent of a reaction.','(iii) is false (i) and (ii) are correct','The reaction quotient, Q (Q with molar concentrations and Q with partial pressures) P is defined in the same way as the equilibrium constant Kc except that the concentrations in Q are not necessarily equilibrium values.(NCERT chemistry class 11; page 206 ; paragraph 2)\n\nLet us consider applications of equilibrium constant to:\n• predict the extent of a reaction on the basis of its magnitude\n• predict the direction of the reaction, and\n• calculate equilibrium concentrations.(NCERT chemistry class 11; page 205 ; paragraph 3)\n\nThe numerical value of the equilibrium constant for a reaction indicates the extent of the reaction.\nthe reaction.(NCERT chemistry class 11; page 205 ; paragraph 3)','Physical Chemistry >> Equilibrium >> Application of equilibrium constants',NULL,'1','mcq','(i) (iii) are correct (ii) is false','(i) is correct (ii) and (iii) are false','(iii) is false (i) and (ii) are correct','(i) (ii) and (iii) are correct','NEW','11-206','11-182',NULL),
(70404,'chemistry','A particular net chemical reaction goes right to left. What does it mean?','Q꜀ > K꜀','If Q꜀ < K꜀, net reaction goes from left to right\nIf Q꜀ > K꜀ net reaction goes from right to left.\nIf Q꜀ = K꜀, no net reaction occurs.(NCERT chemistry class 11; page 206 ; paragraph 12)','Physical Chemistry >> Equilibrium >> Application of equilibrium constants',NULL,'2','mcq','Q꜀ > K꜀','Q꜀ < K꜀','Q꜀ = K꜀','Can any of the above','NEW','11-206','11-182',NULL),
(70405,'chemistry','The value of K꜀ for the reaction 2A ⇌ B + C is 2 × 10⁻³. At a given time, the composition of reaction mixture is [A] = [B] = [C] = 3 × 10⁻⁴ M. In which direction reaction will proceed ?','Backward','(NCERT chemistry class 11; page 206 ; Problem 7.7) diagram(ne0706)','Physical Chemistry >> Equilibrium >> Application of equilibrium constants',NULL,'2','mcq','Forward','Backward','In dynamic equilibrium state','Can\'t be determined','NEW','11-206','11-182',NULL),
(70406,'chemistry','13.8g of N₂O₄ was placed in a 1L reaction vessel at 400K and allowed to attain equilibrium, N₂O₄ (g) = 2NO₂ (g) ,the total pressure at equilbrium was found to be 9.15 bar. Calculate Kp , K꜀ and partial pressures at equilibrium.','Kₚ = 85.87; K꜀ = 2.6; p(N₂O₄) = 0.81 bar ; p(NO₂) = 8.34 bar','(NCERT chemistry class 11; page 207 ; Problem 7.8) diagram(ne0707)','Physical Chemistry >> Equilibrium >> Application of equilibrium constants',NULL,'3','mcq','Kₚ = 85.87; K꜀ = 2.6; p(N₂O₄) = 0.81 bar ; p(NO₂) = 8.34 bar','Kₚ = 8.587; K꜀ = 2.6; p(N₂O₄) = 0.81 bar ; p(NO₂) = 8.34 bar','Kₚ = 85.87; K꜀ = 2.6; p(N₂O₄) = 8.1 bar ; p(NO₂) = 8.34 bar','Kₚ = 85.87; K꜀ = 0.26; p(N₂O₄) = 0.81 bar ; p(NO₂) = 8.34 bar','NEW','11-207','11-183',NULL),
(70407,'biology','Segment of earthworm bearing mouth is -','Peristomium','The first body segment is called the peristomium (buccal segment) which contains the mouth (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:106, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','Clitellar','Prostomium','Peristomium','Deuterostomium','NEW','11-106',NULL,NULL),
(70408,'biology','Regarding prostomium in earthworm, which statement is false -','It is the final segment that aids locomotion and brings about and helps in defecation .','Anterior end consists of the mouth and the prostomium, a lobe which serves as a covering for the mouth and as a wedge to force open cracks in the soil into which the earthworm may crawl. The prostomium is sensory in function. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:106, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'3','mcq','Is sensory in function','Is a fleshy lobefold overhanging the mouth','Serves to open cracks in the soil during crawling','It is the final segment that aids locomotion and brings about and helps in defecation .','NEW','11-106',NULL,NULL),
