(70413,'biology','In earthworm, genital papillae occur in segments-','17 and 19th','Two pairs of accessory glands are present one pair each in the 17th and 19th segments.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:110, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','16 and 17th','16 and 18th','17 and 18th','17 and 19th','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70414,'biology','Segments having no setae in earthworm are -','First, last and clitellum','In each body segment, except the first, last andclitellum, there are rows of S-shaped setae, embedded in the epidermal pits in the middle of each segment.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:107, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','First','Last','Clitellar','First, last and clitellum','NEW','11-107',NULL,NULL),
(70415,'biology','Setae in earthworm -','All are correct','All are correct (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:107, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','Are s-shaped and can be extended and retracted','Have principal role in locomotion','Cuticle, epidermis, coelomic epithelium, circular muscle, longitudinal muscle are seen in cross sectional structure of a single segment','All are correct','NEW','11-107',NULL,NULL),
(70416,'biology','Which of the following layers you will find in the body wall of earthworm (from outside to inside)','Noncellular cuticle, epidermis, circular muscles, longitudinal muscle, coelomic epithelium','The body wall of the earthworm is covered externally by a thin non-cellular cuticle below which is the epidermis, two muscle layers (circular and longitudinal) and an innermost coelomic epithelium (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:107, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'3','mcq','Noncellular cuticle, epidermis, circular muscles, longitudinal muscle, coelomic epithelium','Cuticle, epidermis, longitudinal muscles, circular muscles, coelomic epithelium','Cuticle, epidermis,thoracic muscles','Cuticle, epidermis, peritoneum muscles','NEW','11-107',NULL,NULL),
(70417,'biology','The alimentary canal in earthworm is a straight tube extending from ____ segment to ___ - segment','1st, last','The alimentary canal is a straight tube and runs between first to last segment of the body.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:108, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','3rd, last','3rd, 46th','4th, 46th','1st, last','NEW','11-108',NULL,NULL),
(70418,'biology','In pheretima, lymph glands lie in the segments –','26th and behind','The characteristic feature of the intestine after 26th segment except the last 23rd-25th segments is the presence of internal median fold of dorsal wall called typhlosole.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:108, paragraph no:1) The lymph glands are whitish fluffy  glands present on the dorsal blood vessel from 26th segment to the last segment. They secrete phagocytes and destroys harmful bacteria. The earthworm contains the accessory glands whose secretions basically helps in attachment during copulation','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','4, 5 and 6','7, 8 and 9','14, 15 and 16','26th and behind','NEW','11-108',NULL,NULL),
(70419,'biology','How many lymph glands are present in pheretima?','From 26th segment onwards','The characteristic feature of the intestine after 26th segment except the last 23rd-25th segments is the presence of internal median fold of dorsal wall called typhlosole.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:108, paragraph no:1) The lymph glands are whitish fluffy  glands present on the dorsal blood vessel from 26th segment to the last segment. They secrete phagocytes and destroys harmful bacteria. The earthworm contains the accessory glands whose secretions basically helps in attachment during copulation','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','From 26th segment onwards','From 3rd segment onwards','4 pairs','No glands','NEW','11-108',NULL,NULL),
(70420,'biology','The role of typhlosole in earthworm is to –','Increase absorptive area','The characteristic feature of the intestine after 26th segment except the last 23rd-25th segments is the presence of internal median fold of dorsal wall called typhlosole. This increases the effective area of absorption in the intestine.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:108, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','Emulsify fat','Control blood flow','Increase absorptive area','Release digestive juice','NEW','11-108',NULL,NULL),
(70421,'biology','Gizzard in earthworm serves for-','Grinding the soil particles and decaying leaves','A small narrow tube, oesophagus (5-7 segments), continues into a muscular gizzard (8-9 segments). It helps in grinding the soil particles and decaying leaves, (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:108, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','Excretion','Grinding the soil particles and decaying leaves','Secreting slime','Food absorption','NEW','11-108',NULL,NULL),
(70422,'biology','Calciferous glands in stomach of Earthworm  -','Neutralize the humic acid present in humus','Calciferous glands, present in the stomach, neutralise the humic acid present in humus. Intestine starts from the 15th segment onwards and continues till the last segment.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:108, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','Secrete enzymes','Secrete hormone','Neutralize the humic acid present in humus','Purifies blood','NEW','11-108',NULL,NULL),
(70423,'biology','Intestinal caecae (one pair) project from the intestine of Earthworm on which segment?','26','A pair of short and conical intestinal caecae project from the intestine on the 26th segment.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:108, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','26','18','30','40','NEW','11-108',NULL,NULL),
