(70440,'biology','Pharyngeal nephridia are present as three pairs of tufts in the segments -','4,5, 6th','Pharyngeal nephridia, present as three paired tufts in the 4th, 5th and 6th segments (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:109, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','6, 7, 8th','5, 6, 7th','4,5, 6th','1, 2, 3rd','NEW','11-109',NULL,NULL),
(70441,'biology','Chemoreceptors in earthworms','React to chemical stimuli, located at the anterior part','Worms have specialised chemoreceptors (taste receptors) which react to chemical stimuli. These sense organs are located on the anterior part of the worm. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:110, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'3','mcq','React to chemical stimuli, located at the anterior part','React to sensory stimuli, located at the anterior part','React to chemical stimuli, located at the posterior part','React to sensory stimuli, located at the posterior part','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70442,'biology','One earthworm has to find another worm and they mate by','Juxtaposing opposite gonadal openings and Exchanging packets of sperms called spermatophores.','A mutual exchange of sperm occurs between two worms during mating. One worm has to find another worm and they mate juxtaposing opposite gonadal openings exchanging packets of sperms called spermatophores. Mature sperm and egg cells and nutritive fluid are deposited in cocoons produced by the gland cells of clitellum. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:110, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'3','mcq','Juxtaposing opposite gonadal openings and Exchanging packets of sperms called spermatophores.','Superimposing gonadal openings and Exchanging packets of sperms called ooganophores.','Superimposing gonadal openings and Exchanging packets of sperms called spermatophores.','Self fertilisation without requiring a partner','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70443,'biology','Which of the following segments in Earthworm are called "forest of nephridia"','Clitellar segments','Clitellar region has a group of nephridium (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:109, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','Clitellar segments','Preclitellar segments','Postclitellar segments','Rostellum','NEW','11-109',NULL,NULL),
(70444,'biology','Nerve ring of earthworm is formed surrounding -','Pharynx','The nerve cord in the anterior region (3rd and 4th segments) bifurcates, laterally encircling the pharynx and joins the cerebral ganglia dorsally to form a nerve ring. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:109, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','Pharynx','Gizzard','Stomach','None','NEW','11-109',NULL,NULL),
(70445,'biology','Nerve cord of pheretima is -','Paired, solid and ventral','Nervous system is basically represented by ganglia arranged segmentwise on the ventral paired nerve cord.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:109, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','Paired, solid and ventral','Paired, solid and dorsal','Single, solid and dorsal','Single, hollow and dorsal','NEW','11-109',NULL,NULL),
(70446,'biology','Earthworm has -','No eyes','Earthworm do not have eyes (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:110, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'1','mcq','No eyes','2 eyes','Many eyes','1 eye','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70447,'biology','Earthworm has no special sense organs, still they are sensitive to -','Touch, taste, light and vibration','Sensory system does not have eyes but does possess light and touch sensitive organs (receptor cells) to distinguish the light intensities and to feel the vibrations in the ground. Worms have specialised chemoreceptors (taste receptors) which react to chemical stimuli. These sense organs are located on the anterior part of the worm. Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:110, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'1','mcq','Light and sound only','Touch and sound only','Touch, taste and light only','Touch, taste, light and vibration','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70448,'biology','Pheretima is -','Hermaphrodite','Both male and female sex organs are present in the same organism that is why Earthworm is bisexual,or Hermaphrodite (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:110, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','Sterile','Unisexual','Hermaphrodite','Dioecious','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70449,'biology','In earthworm, two pair of testes are located in segments -','10 and 11th','There are two pairs of testes present in the 10th and 11th segments. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:110, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','10 and 11th','12 and 13th','14 and 15th','17 and 18th','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70450,'biology','In earthworm, testis sacs are present in segments -','10 and 11th','There are two pairs of testes present in the 10th and 11th segments. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:110, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','10 and 11th','11 and 12th','12 and 13th','13 and 14th','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70451,'biology','Vasa deferentia of testis in earthworm run upto ____ segment where they join the _____ duct -','18th, prostatic','Their vasa deferentia run up to the 18th segment where they join the prostatic duct. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:110, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','17th, accessory','18th, prostatic','17th, prostatic','18th, accessory','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70452,'biology','2 pairs of accessory glands in earthworm are found in segments -','17,19th','Two pairs of accessory glands are present one pair each in the 17th and 19th segments. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:110, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','17, 18th','17,19th','19, 20th','18, 19th','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70453,'biology','Spermathecae in earthworm are found in –','6, 7, 8, 9th','Four pairs of spermathecae are located in 6th-9th segments (one pair in each segment). (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:110, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','6, 7, 8, 9th','4, 5, 6, 7th','11, 12, 13, 14th','15, 16, 17, 18th','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70454,'biology','Seminal vesicles in earthworm lie in the segments -','11,12th','Seminal vesicles in Earthworm lie at the 11th,12th position (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:110, Figure 7.13)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','11,12th','12,13th','10,11th','13,14th','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70455,'biology','Prostate glands in earthworm are present in segments -','17 to 20th','Prostate glands are present in segments 17 to 20 in Earthworm(Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:110, Figure 7.13)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','16 to 25th','17 to 20th','20-25th','25 – 30th','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70456,'biology','In earthworm, the prostatic secretion is helpful for-','Activation of sperms','Prostatic secretion helps in activation of sperms and helps in fertilization (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:110, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','Formation of eggs','Activation of sperms','Formation of sperms','Formation of spermatophore','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70457,'biology','Mature sperm and egg cells of earthworm with nutritive fluid are deposited in cocoons produced by the gland cells of _______','Clitellum','Spermatophores. Mature sperm and egg cells and nutritive fluid are deposited in cocoons produced by the gland cells of clitellum. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:110, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','Clitellum','Blood cells','Accessory glands','Septal nephridia','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70458,'biology','Which among the following is incorrect regarding reproductions in Earthworm ?','Larva is formed and baby earthworms come out','The ova (eggs) are fertilised by the sperm cells within the cocoon which then slips off the worm and is deposited in or on the soil. The cocoon holds the worm embryos. After about 3 weeks, each cocoon produces two to twenty baby worms with an average of four. Development of earthworms is direct, i.e., there is no larval stage or in other words no larva is formed (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:110, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','Cocoon holds the worm embryos','After about 3 weeks, each cocoon produces two to twenty baby worms with an average of four','Development of earthworms is direct','Larva is formed and baby earthworms come out','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70459,'biology','Function of spermathecae in earthworm is to -','Receive sperms during copulation for storage','Spermathecae helps in collecting the sperms  for storage (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:110, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','Receive spermatogonia for maturation','Secrete substances that form the cocoons','Receive sperms during copulation for storage','Receive fertilized ova for embryonic development','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70460,'biology','In earthworm ovaries are attached at the inter-segmental septum of -','12th  and  13th segments','One pair of ovaries is attached at the inter-segmental septum of the 12th and 13th segments. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:110, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','12th  and  14th segments','12th  and  13th segments','13th  and  14th segments','14th  and  15th segment','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70461,'biology','Ovarian funnels of Earthworm are present beneath the ovaries which continue into oviduct, join together and open on the ventral side as a single median female genital pore on the segment','14th','Ovarian funnels are present beneath the ovaries which continue into oviduct, join together and open on the ventral side as a single median female genital pore on the 14th segment. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:110, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','13th','14th','15th','16th','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70462,'biology','In a copulating pair of earthworms, which of the two processes take place?','Cross fertilization and modified external fertilization','Though earthworm is a hermaphrodite cross fertilization takes place involving two individuals, it can also be known as juxtposing copulation. and the Gametes fuse in the slime tube outside the body which later dries and falls off to form the cocoon , considered as modified external fertilization(Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:110, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','Internal fertilization and cross fertilization','Cross fertilization and modified external fertilization','External fertilization and internal fertilization','Reciprocal fertilization and modified  internal fertilization','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70463,'biology','Pheretima is not useful in making -','Specimen for testing drugs','Earthworm is used in all the following and mice is commonly used in drug trials (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:111, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','Bait for fishing','Soil porous  and  fertile','Laboratory use','Specimen for testing drugs','NEW','11-111',NULL,NULL),
(70464,'biology','Which one is known as a "friend of farmers"?','Pheretima','Earthworm helps in breaking the soil particles and hence it is called as friend of farmers (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:111, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'1','mcq','Rana','Cockroach','Pheretima','Rattus','NEW','11-111',NULL,NULL),
(70465,'biology','The process of increasing fertility of soil by the earthworm is called -','Vermicomposting','The process of increasing fertility of soil by the earthworms is called vermicomposting. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:111, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'1','mcq','Vermicomposting','Chemicomposting','Chemimanuring','Percolation','NEW','11-111',NULL,NULL),
