(70472,'biology','_________ present in the stomach of Earthworm, neutralise the humic acid present in humus.','Calciferous glands','Calciferous glands, present in the stomach of Earthworm, neutralise the humic acid present in humus.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'2','mcq','Calciferous glands','Gastric Glands','Salivary Glands','Intestinal glands','NEW','11-108',NULL,NULL),
(70473,'biology','Which of the following statement is incorrect regarding an Earthworm','Earthworms contain specialised breathing devices','They produce blood cells and haemoglobin which is dissolved in plasma. Earthworms lack specialised breathing devices. Respiratory exchange occurs through moist body surface into their blood stream. Blood cells are phagocytic in nature.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Earthworm',NULL,'1','mcq','They produce blood cells and haemoglobin which is dissolved in blood plasma.','Blood cells are phagocytic in nature','Earthworms contain specialised breathing devices','Respiratory exchange occurs through moist body surface into their blood stream','NEW','11-108',NULL,NULL),
(70501,'chemistry','I. ∆G = -ve , forward reaction is spontaneous. \nII. ∆G = +ve , backward reaction is spontaneous.','Both are true','• ∆G is negative, then the reaction is spontaneous and proceeds in the forwarddirection.\n• ∆G is positive, then reaction is considered non-spontaneous. Instead, as reverse reaction would have a negative ∆G, the products of the forward reaction shall be converted to the reactants. (NCERT chemistry class 11; page 208 ; paragraph 1)','Physical Chemistry >> Equilibrium >> Realationship between Equilibrium Constant K, Reaction Quotient Q and Gibbs Engergy G',NULL,'1','mcq','Both are true','I is true but II is false','II is true but I is false','Both are false','NEW','11-208','11-184',NULL),
(70502,'chemistry','The value of ∆G⁰ for the phosphorylation of glucose in glycolysis is 13.8 kJ/mol. What is the value of Kc at 298 K.?','3.81 × 10⁻³','(NCERT chemistry class 11; page 208 ; Problem 7.10) diagram(ne0708)','Physical Chemistry >> Equilibrium >> Realationship between Equilibrium Constant K, Reaction Quotient Q and Gibbs Engergy G',NULL,'2','mcq','3.81 × 10⁻²','3.81 × 10⁻³','3.81 × 10⁻¹','3.81 × 10⁻⁴','NEW','11-208','11-184',NULL),
(70503,'chemistry','Le Chatelier’s principle. It states that a change in any of the factors that determine the equilibrium conditions of a system will cause the system to change in such a manner so as to reduce or to\n_________ the effect of the change.','Counteract','Le Chatelier’s principle. It states that a change in any of the factors that determine the equilibrium conditions of a system will cause the system to change in such a manner so as to reduce or to\ncounteract the effect of the change.(NCERT chemistry class 11; page 209, paragraph 2)','Physical Chemistry >> Equilibrium >> Realationship between Equilibrium Constant K, Reaction Quotient Q and Gibbs Engergy G',NULL,'1','mcq','Increase','Counteract','Intensify','None of the above','NEW','11-209','11-185',NULL),
(70504,'biology','In each segment of cockroach, the exoskeleton has hardened plates called -','Sclerites','In each segment, exoskeleton has hardened plates called sclerites\n(tergites dorsally and sternites ventrally) that are joined to each other by\na thin and flexible articular membrane (arthrodial membrane). (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:111, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Sclerites','Arthrodites','Ossicles','Chitinites','NEW','11-111',NULL,NULL),
(70505,'biology','The dorsal sclerites and ventral sclerites are called (respectively)-','Tergites and sternites','In each segment, exoskeleton has hardened plates called sclerites (tergites dorsally and sternites ventrally) that are joined to each other by a thin and flexible articular membrane (arthrodial membrane). (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:111, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Sternites and tergites','Tergites and sternites','Sternites and pleurites','Tergites and pleurites','NEW','11-111',NULL,NULL),
(70506,'biology','The head of cockroach consists of fusion of segments -','Six','The head is a fusion of 6 segments (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:112, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Six','Ten','Fourteen','Eighteen','NEW','11-112',NULL,NULL),
(70507,'biology','In cockroach, head can move in all directions due to-','Flexible neck','Head is triangular in shape and lies anteriorly at right angles to the\nlongitudinal body axis. It is formed by the fusion of six segments and\nshows great mobility in all directions due to flexible neck (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:112, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Absence of neck','Fusion of all 6 segments of head','Flexible neck','Head is small and light in weight','NEW','11-112',NULL,NULL),
(70508,'biology','In cockroach, a pair of antennae arises from membranous socket. antennae are -','Filiform and sensory in function','A pair of thread like antennae arise from membranous sockets lying in front of eyes. Antennae have sensory receptors that help in monitoring the environment.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:112, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Without any sensory receptors','Filiform and sensory in function','Motor receptors that help in locomotion.','Filiform and motor in function','NEW','11-112',NULL,NULL),
(70509,'biology','Mouth parts of cockroach are -','Biting and chewing type','Anterior end of the head bears appendages forming biting and chewing type of mouth parts. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:112, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Sponging type','Biting and sucking type','Biting and chewing type','Piercing and sucking type','NEW','11-112',NULL,NULL),
(70510,'biology','Tongue of cockroach is -','Hypopharynx','A median flexible\nlobe, acting as tongue (hypopharynx), lies within the cavity enclosed by\nthe mouthparts (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:112, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Labrum','Mandibles','Labium','Hypopharynx','NEW','11-112',NULL,NULL),
(70511,'biology','In cockroach, wings are absent in -','Prothorax','Wings are present only in metathorax and mesothorax segments (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:112, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Prothorax','Mesothorax','Metathorax','Wings are present in all segments','NEW','11-112',NULL,NULL),
(70512,'biology','_________ is the type of photoreceptor other than compound eye present in some animals like cockroach','Ocellus','Ocelli (singular Ocellus) are simple photo-receptors (light detecting organs) .refer NCERT 1 pgno.112 Figure 7.15 Head region of cockroach : (a) parts of head region','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Ocellus','Omphalus','Octavius','Oneccus','NEW','11-112',NULL,NULL),
(70513,'biology','Forewings of cockroach are articulated to -','Mesothorax','Forewings (mesothoracic) called\ntegmina are opmcque dark and leathery and cover the hind wings when at\nrest. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:112, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Prothorax','Metathorax','Mesothorax','Amnothorax','NEW','11-112',NULL,NULL),
(70514,'biology','Forewings wings in cockroaches are -','Tegmina','The first pair of wings arises from mesothorax and the second pair from metathorax. Forewings are called as tegmina.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:112, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Halteres','Tegmina','Hemielytra','Forawings','NEW','11-112',NULL,NULL),
(70515,'biology','Which of the following statements are false about the forewings in cockroach?','They are metathoracic and used in flight','All are correct (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:112, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','They are mesothoracic','They are opmcque, dark and leathery and cover hindwing when at rest','They are not used in flight','They are metathoracic and used in flight','NEW','11-112',NULL,NULL),
(70516,'biology','In cockroach, thorax is divided into how many segments?','Three','Prothorax,Mesothorax and Metathorax (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:112, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Three','Four','Five','Six','NEW','11-112',NULL,NULL),
(70517,'biology','At the junction of midgut and hindgut of cockroach, is present another ring of 100-150 yellow coloured thin filamentous called_________','Malpighian tubules','At the junction of midgut and hindgut is present another ring of 100-150 yellow coloured thin filamentous Malpighian tubules. They help in removal of excretory products from haemolymph. The hindgut is broader than midgut and is differentiated into ileum, colon and rectum. The rectum opens out through anus. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:113, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'1','mcq','Salivary glands','Spermatheca','Gastric caeca','Malpighian tubules','NEW','11-113',NULL,NULL),
(70518,'biology','The abdomen in both male and female cockroach consists of -','10 segments','The abdomen in both males and females consists of 10 segments. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:112, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','10 segments','8 segments','12 segments','18 segments','NEW','11-112',NULL,NULL),
(70519,'biology','In female cockroach, 7th sternum is -','Boat shaped','In females, the 7th sternum is boat shaped and together with the 8th and 9th sterna forms a brood or genital pouch whose anterior part contains female gonopore, spermathecal pores and collateral glands. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:112, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Annular','Filamentous','Boat shaped','Spiral','NEW','11-112',NULL,NULL),
(70520,'biology','Match the following regarding the structure of cockroach','labrum-upper lip,labium-lower lip,tergites-dorsal,sternites-ventral','(Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:112, paragraph no:1-2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'3','match','labrum,upper lip','labium,lower lip','tergites,dorsal','sternites,ventral','NEW','11-112',NULL,NULL),
(70521,'biology','Which of the following is NOT correct about cockroach?','Cockroach is a hermaphrodite','Hermaphrodite means presence of both male and female sex organs in the same individual. cockroach has wee distinct male and females (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:112, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Sexual dimorphism is distinct','The anal styles are present on 9th sternite of male only','In both sexes the 10th segment bears a pair of jointed filamentous structures called anal cerci','Cockroach is a hermaphrodite','NEW','11-112',NULL,NULL),
(70522,'biology','Genital pouch of Male cockroach has -','Dorsal anus, ventral genital pore and gonapophysis','In males, genital pouch or chamber lies at the hind end of abdomen bounded dorsally by 9th and 10th terga and ventrally by the 9th sternum. It contains dorsal anus, ventral male genital pore and gonapophysis.(Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:112, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Dorsal anus, ventral genital pore and gonapophysis','Ventral anus, dorsal genital pore and gonapophysis','Dorsal anus, ventral genital pore but no gonapophysis','Dorsal anus, ventral genital pore, gonapophysis but no anal styles','NEW','11-112',NULL,NULL),
(70523,'biology','The largest part of the alimentary canal of cockroach is -','Crop','Crop used for storing of food in cockroach (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:113, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Crop','Rectum','Gizzard','Ileum','NEW','11-113',NULL,NULL),
(70524,'biology','Which part of alimentary canal of cockroach contributes to crushing food?','Gizzard','Gizzard helps in grinding the food particles. The entire foregut is lined by cuticle. A ring of 6-8 blind tubules called hepatic or gastric caeca is present at the junction of foregut and midgut, which secrete digestive juice.(Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:113, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Crop','Rectum','Gizzard','Ileum','NEW','11-113',NULL,NULL),
(2000036211,'physics','A block of mass $100\\,kg$ slides over a distance of $10 \\,m$ on a horizontal surface. If the coefficient of friction between the surfaces is 0.4 then the work done against friction (in $J$ ) is','B','Work done against friction $=-$ Work done by friction<br>$\\therefore \\,\\,\\,\\,W = {f_k}s = {\\mu _k}Ns$<br>$ = {\\mu _k}mgs$<br>$ = 0.4 \\times 100 \\times 10 \\times 10 = 4000\\,J$','Work','Work, Energy and Power','Medium',NULL,'4200','4000','4500','3900',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(70525,'biology','The gizzard or proventriculus of a cockroach has an outer layer of thick muscles and thick inner cuticle forming  how many highly,chitinous plates called teeth -','Six','The crop is followed by gizzard or proventriculus. It has an outer layer of thick circular muscles and thick inner cuticle forming six highly chitinous plate called teeth. Gizzard helps in grinding the food particles (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:113, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Three','Six','Nine','Twelve','NEW','11-113',NULL,NULL),
(70526,'biology','In female cockroach Genital pouch is divided in','Genital chamber and Vestibulum','Genital pouch consists of Genital Chamber and vestibulum, (Reference : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:112, paragraph no:2 and Figure 7.18)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Genital chamber and Vestibulum','Vestibulum and Collaterial glands','Spermatheca and oviduct','Malphigian tubules and Spermatheca','NEW','11-112',NULL,NULL),
(70527,'biology','In Cockroach, a ring of 6 - 8 blind tubules called hepatic ie gastric caecae are present at -','Junction of foregut and midgut','Hepatic cecae is present at the junction of foregut and midgut (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:113, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Junction of foregut and hindgut','Junction of midgut and hindgut','Junction of hindgut and foregut','Junction of foregut and midgut','NEW','11-113',NULL,NULL),
(70528,'biology','Which of the following is INCORRECT about the alimentary canal of cockroach?','Midgut is differentiated into ileum,cecum and jejunum','The alimentary canal is divided into three regions foregut,midgut and hindgut . The entire foregut is lined by cuticle. The hindgut is broader than mudgut.Hindgut is differentiated into ileum, colon and rectum (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:113, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','The entire fore gut is lined by cuticle','Hindgut is broader than midgut','Hindgut is differentiated into ileum, colon and rectum','Midgut is differentiated into ileum,cecum and jejunum','NEW','11-113',NULL,NULL),
(70529,'biology','Open blood vascular system without haemoglobin is found in -','Cockroach','Arthropods have open circulatory system (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:113, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Earthworm','Frog','Rat','Cockroach','NEW','11-113',NULL,NULL),
(70530,'biology','Which of the following is a character of cockroach?','13-chambered heart','(Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:113, figure 7.17)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'1','mcq','Reduced wing','Cocoon formation','13-chambered heart','Absence of salivary gland','NEW','11-113',NULL,NULL),
(70531,'biology','Common oviduct and single median oviduct refer to which part in the reproductive tract of a female cockroach','Vagina','Each ovary is formed of a group of eight ovarian tubules or ovarioles, containing a chain of developing ova. Oviducts of each ovary unite into a single median oviduct or common oviduct (also called vagina) which opens into the genital chamber (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:114, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'1','mcq','Vagina','lateral oviduct','Fallopian canal','Ovarian tubules','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70532,'biology','Which of the following is false about the heart of cockroach?','It is myogenic','It is neurogenic,meaning does not pump unless stimulated by nervous system needs continuous nerve supply to keep pumping. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:113 paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','It is differentiated into funnel shaped chambers with ostia on either side','It is myogenic','Blood from sinuses enter the heart through ostia and is pumped anteriorly to sinuses again','Alary muscles are related to heart','NEW','11-113',NULL,NULL),
(70533,'biology','Which of the following is wrong?','In Cockroach, there is presence of Cu containing respiratory pigment.','In cockroach, blood vessels are poorly developed and open into haemocoel. In cockroach, visceral organs located in haemocoel are bathed in blood (haemolymph). The haemolymph consists of colourless plasma and haemocytes.Aquatic molluscs and Arthropods contain blue coloured Cu containing respiratory pigment','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','In cockroach, blood vessels are poorly developed and open into haemocoel','In cockroach, visceral organs located in haemocoel are bathed in blood (haemolymph)','The haemolymph consists of colourless plasma and haemocytes','In Cockroach, there is presence of Cu containing respiratory pigment.','NEW','11-118',NULL,NULL),
(70534,'biology','The respiratory system in the body of cockroach consists of -','Network of trachea','The respiratory system consists of a\nnetwork of trachea, that open through 10 pairs\nof small holes called spiracles present on the\nlateral side of the body. Thin branching tubes\n(tracheal tubes subdivided into tracheoles)\ncarry O₂ from the air to all the parts. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:113, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'1','mcq','Bronchi','Bronchioles','Network of trachea','Haemocyanin','NEW','11-113',NULL,NULL),
(70535,'biology','Spiracles in cockroach are small holes present on _____ side of body.','Lateral','The respiratory system consists of a\nnetwork of trachea, that open through 10 pairs\nof small holes called spiracles present on the\nlateral side of the body. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:113, paragraph no:))','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Dorsal','Ventral','Lateral','Medial','NEW','11-113',NULL,NULL),
(70536,'biology','The excretory organs in cockroach are-','Malpighian tubules','Excretion is performed by Malpighian tubules. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:113, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Green glands','Hepatic caecae','Malpighian tubules','Malpighian corpuscles','NEW','11-113',NULL,NULL),
(70537,'biology','Cockroach is -','Uricotelic','Each tubule is lined\nby glandular and ciliated cells. They absorb nitrogenous waste products\nand convert them into uric acid which is excreted out through the hindgut.\nTherefore, this insect is called uricotelic. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:114, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'1','mcq','Uricotelic','Ureotelic','Ammonotelic','Guanotelic','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70538,'biology','Malpighian tubules remove excretory products from -','Haemolymph','Malpighian\ntubules help in removal of excretory\nproducts from haemolymph.. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:113, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Haemolymph','Gut','Both a and b','Kidney','NEW','11-113',NULL,NULL),
(70539,'biology','Malpighian tubules in cockroach open at the junction of –','Midgut and ileum','At the junction of midgut and\nhindgut is present another ring of 100-150\nyellow coloured thin filamentous Malpighian\ntubules. They help in removal of excretory\nproducts from haemolymph. The hindgut is\nbroader than midgut and is differentiated into\nileum, colon and rectum. The rectum opens\nout through anus. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:113, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Gizzard and midgut','Midgut and ileum','Ileum and colon','Colon and rectum','NEW','11-113',NULL,NULL),
(70540,'biology','The main excretory product in cockroach is -','Uric acid','Each tubule is lined\nby glandular and ciliated cells. They absorb nitrogenous waste products\nand convert them into uric acid which is excreted out through the hindgut.\nTherefore, this insect is called uricotelic. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:114, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'1','mcq','Urea','Ammonia','Guanine','Uric acid','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70541,'biology','In addition to malpighian tubules, which of the following does not help in excretion in cockroach -','Kidney','All helps in excretion (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:114, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'1','mcq','Nephrocytes','Urecose glands','Fat body','Kidney','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70542,'biology','Go through the paragraph - "it is lined by glandular and ciliated cell, it absorbs nitrogenous waste products from haemocoel and convert them into uric acid which is excreted out through the hindgut". Above functions are related to which of the following structures in cockroach?','Malpighian tubules','At the junction of midgut and\nhindgut is present another ring of 100-150\nyellow coloured thin filamentous Malpighian\ntubules. They help in removal of excretory\nproducts from haemolymph. The hindgut is\nbroader than midgut and is differentiated into\nileum, colon and rectum. The rectum opens\nout through anus. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:113, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Kidney','Hepatic caecae','Liver','Malpighian tubules','NEW','11-113',NULL,NULL),
(70543,'biology','Common feature of earthworm and cockroach is -','Ventral nerve cord','Non chordates have ventral nerve cord (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:114, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Hermaphrodism','Ventral nerve cord','Moulting of cuticle','Excretion by nephridia','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70544,'biology','Number of thoracic and abdominal ganglia in cockroach are(respectively) -','3 and 6','Three ganglia lie in the thorax, and six in the abdomen. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:114, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','3 and 6','3 and 3','6 and 6','6 and 3','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70545,'biology','The nervous system in cockroach is represented by -','Segmentally arranged ganglia and ventral nerve cord, spread throughout the body','The nervous system of cockroach consists of a series of fused,\nsegmentally arranged ganglia joined by paired longitudinal connectives\non the ventral side. Three ganglia lie in the thorax, and six in the abdomen.\nThe nervous system of cockroach is spread throughout the body. The\nhead holds a bit of a nervous system while the rest is situated along the\nventral (belly-side) part of its body. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:114, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Nervous plexus in the head and not throughout the body','Segmentally arranged ganglia and ventral nerve cord','Segmentally arranged ganglia and ventral nerve cord, spread throughout the body','Supra-oesopharyngeal ganglia in head and dorsal nerve cord','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70546,'biology','In cockroach, supra-oesopharyngeal ganglion supplies nerves to -','Compound eyes and antenna','In\nthe head region, the brain is represented by supra-oesophageal ganglion\nwhich supplies nerves to antennae and compound eyes. In cockroach,\nthe sense organs are antennae, eyes, maxillary palps, labial palps, anal\ncerci, etc. The compound eyes are situated at the dorsal surface of the\nhead.It is present in the head region (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:114, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Compound eyes and antenna','Antennae and simple eyes','Spikes and compound eyes','Abdomen area','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70547,'biology','The visual unit of cockroach are -','Ommatidia','Each eye consists of about 2000 hexagonal ommatidia (sing.: ommatidium). With the help of several ommatidia, a cockroach can receive several images of an object (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:114, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Ocelli','Ctenidia','Ommatidia','Rhabdatida','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70548,'biology','Which of the following is wrong about vision in cockroach?','Cockroach has binocular vision','With the help of several ommatidia, a cockroach receives several images of an object. It is with more sensitivity but has less resolution. It has Mosaic vision.Being common during night, it is called nocturnal vision   (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:114, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','With the help of several ommatidia, a cockroach receives several images of an object','It is with more sensitivity but has less resolution','Being common during night, it is called nocturnal vision.','Cockroach has binocular vision','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70549,'biology','Besides eyes and antenna which of the following is not a sense organ in cockroach?','Tegmina','All the given options help in sensing the environment except Tegmina  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:114, paragraph no:2)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Maxillary palps','Labial palps','Anal cerci','Tegmina','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70550,'biology','In male cockroach, from each testis arises a thin vas deferens, which open into_______ through seminal vesicle','Ejaculatory duct','From each testis arises a thin vas deferens, which opens into\nejaculatory duct through seminal vesicle. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:114, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Anal cercus','Caudal style','Collateral gland','Ejaculatory duct','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70551,'biology','In male cockroach, the ejaculatory duct opens into a pore situated ventral to anus. this pore is -','Gonopore','Male reproductive system consists of a pair of testes one lying on each lateral side in the 4th -6th abdominal segments. From each testis arises a thin vas deferens, which opens into ejaculatory duct through seminal vesicle. The ejaculatory duct opens (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:114, paragraph no:3) into male gonopore situated ventral to anus','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Gonopore','Genital papilla','Nephridiopore','Peristomium','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70552,'biology','Chitinous asymmetrical structures, called male gonapophyses or phallomere represent external genitalia. they surround male gonopore. the male cockroach has -','3 phallomeres','3 phallomeres are Left phallomere, Right phallomere and Ventral phallomere (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:114, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','2 phallomeres','3 phallomeres','4 phallomeres','5 phallomeres','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70553,'biology','During copulation, cockroach transfers male gametes in the form of-','Spermatophore','The sperms are stored in the seminal\nvesicles and are glued together in the form of bundles called\nspermatophores which are discharged during copulation. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:114, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Sperms','Spermatophore','Seminal vesicles','Spermatid','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70554,'biology','In male cockroach, the sperms are stored in the seminal vesicles and are glued together in the form of bundles called-','Spermatophores','The sperms are stored in the seminal\nvesicles and are glued together in the form of bundles called\nspermatophores which are discharged during copulation. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:114, paragraph no:4)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Semen','Spermatophores','Spermathecae','Spermatogonia','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70555,'biology','In female cockroach, two oviducts from each side open into a common oviduct i vagina which opens into the genital chamber. a pair of which structures located in the 6th segment opens in the genital chamber?','Spermathecae','The female\nreproductive sysytem consists of two large ovaries, lying laterally in the\n2\nnd – 6th abdominal segments. Each ovary is formed of a group of eight\novarian tubules or ovarioles, containing a chain of developing ova.\nOviducts of each ovary unite into a single median oviduct (also called\nvagina) which opens into the genital chamber. A pair of spermatheca is\npresent in the 6th segment which opens into the genital chamber. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:114, paragraph no:4)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Spermathecae','Gonapophyses','Ejaculatory duct','Pseudopenis','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70556,'biology','Collaterial glands are present in -','Female cockroach','(Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:115, Figure no:7.18)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Male cockroach','Female cockroach','In both Male and female cockroaches.','Absent in cockroach','NEW','11-115',NULL,NULL),
(70557,'biology','Eggs of cockroach are fertilized in -','Genital pouch of female','A pair of spermatheca is\npresent in the 6th segment which opens into the genital chamber.\nSperms are transferred through spermatophores. Their fertilised eggs\nare encased in capsules called oothecae. Ootheca is a dark reddish to\nblackish brown capsule, about 3/8" (8 mm) long. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:114, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Cocoon','Oomatida of Cockroach','Fallopian tube','Genital pouch of female','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70558,'biology','Collateral glands of cockroach help in -','Formation  of ootheca','(Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:114, Fig no. 7.128)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Fertilization','Formation  of ootheca','Copulation','Formation of oothecal chamber','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70559,'biology','Development of periplanata americana is -','Paurometabolous','Nymphal stage is similar to the adult (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:115,  paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Ametabolous','Paurometabolous','Hemimetabolous','Holometabolous','NEW','11-115',NULL,NULL),
(70560,'biology','In cockroach life cycle, the nymph looks very much similar like adult. The nymph -','Lacks wing and has wing pads','(Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:115, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Lacks wing and has wing pads','Has wing and lacks wing pads','Lacks wing and lacks wing pads','Has wing and has wing pads','NEW','11-115',NULL,NULL),
(70561,'biology','Match the correct names of a,b,c and d parts in the given diagram (0723)','a-Filiform antennae,b-Tegmina,c-Pronotum,d-Anal cerci','NCERT class 11 Figure 7.14 page.no-111','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','match','a,Filiform antennae','b,Tegmina','c,Pronotum','d,Anal cerci','NEW','11-111',NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/match/70561q.png'),
(70562,'biology','Match the correct names of a,b,c and d parts in the given diagram (0724)','a-Ocellus,b-Compound eye,c-Labrum,d-Labium','NCERT class 11 Figure 7.15 (a) page.no-112','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'3','match','a,Ocellus','b,Compound eye','c,Labrum','d,Labium','NEW','11-112',NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/match/70562q.png'),
(70563,'biology','Identify the given diagram (0725)','Mandible','NCERT class 11 Figure 7.15 (b) page.no-112','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'3','mcq','Labrum','Hypopharynx','Maxilla','Mandible','NEW','11-112',NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/70563q.png'),
(70564,'biology','Match the correct names of a,b,c and d parts in the given diagram (0726)','a-Labrum,b-Hypopharynx,c-Labium,d-Maxilla','NCERT class 11 Figure 7.15 (b) page.no-112','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'3','match','a,Labrum','b,Hypopharynx','c,Labium','d,Maxilla','NEW','11-112',NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/match/70564q.png');
INSERT INTO `ncert_book_pyq` (`unique_id`, `subject`, `question`, `answer`, `explanation`, `topic_name`, `chapter_name`, `difficulty`, `quiz_type`, `option_a`, `option_b`, `option_c`, `option_d`, `syllabus_update`, `ncert22_page`, `ncert23_page`, `image_url`) VALUES
(70565,'biology','Match the correct names of a,b,c and d parts in the given diagram (0727)','a-Salivary reservoir,b-Crop,c-Hepatic caeca,d-Malpighian tubules','NCERT class 11 Figure 7.16 (b) page.no-113','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'3','match','a,Salivary reservoir','b,Crop','c,Hepatic caeca','d,Malpighian tubules','NEW','11-113',NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/match/70565q.png'),
(70566,'biology','Match the correct names of a,b,c and d parts in the given diagram (0728)','a-Anterior aorta,b-Alary muscles,c-Chambers of heart','NCERT class 11 Figure 7.17 page.no-113','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'3','match','a,Anterior aorta','b,Alary muscles','c,Chambers of heart',NULL,'NEW','11-113',NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/match/70566q.png'),
(70567,'biology','Match the correct names of a,b,c and d parts in the given diagram (0729)','a-Phallic gland,b-Caudal style,c-Pseudopenis,d-Titillator','NCERT class 11 Figure 7.18 (a) page.no-115','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'3','match','a,Phallic gland','b,Caudal style','c,Pseudopenis','d,Titillator','NEW','11-115',NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/match/70567q.png'),
(70568,'biology','Match the correct names of a,b,c and d parts in the given diagram (0730)','a-Collaterial glands,b-Vestibulum,c-gonapophyses,d-Spermatheca','NCERTclass 11 Figure 7.18 (b) page.no-115','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','match','a,Collaterial glands','b,Vestibulum','c,gonapophyses','d,Spermatheca','NEW','11-115',NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/match/70568q.png'),
(70569,'biology','Which of the following statement is incorrect regarding Cockroaches','They are insect carnivores that live in damp places throughout the world.','Bright yellow, red and green coloured cockroaches have also been reported in tropical regions. Their size ranges from ¼ inches to 3 inches (0.6-7.6 cm) and have long antenna, legs and flat extension of the upper body wall that conceals head. They are nocturnal omnivores that live in damp places throughout the world. They have become residents of human homes and thus are serious pests and vectors of several diseases.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Bright yellow, red and green coloured cockroaches have also been reported in tropical regions','Their size ranges from ¼ inches to 3 inches (0.6-7.6 cm) and have long antenna, legs and flat extension of the upper body wall that conceals head.','They are insect carnivores that live in damp places throughout the world.','They have become residents of human homes and thus are serious pests and vectors of several diseases.','NEW','11-111',NULL,NULL),
(70570,'biology','Which of the following is correct regarding cockroaches','The respiratory system consists of a network of trachea, that open through 10 pairs of small holes called spiracles present on the lateral side of the body','Blood vascular system of cockroach is an open type  Blood vessels are poorly developed and open into space (haemocoel). Visceral organs located in the haemocoel are bathed in blood (haemolymph). The haemolymph is composed of colourless plasma and haemocytes. Heart of cockroach consists of elongated muscular tube lying along mid dorsal line of thorax and abdomen. It is differentiated into funnel shaped chambers with ostia on either side. Blood from sinuses enter heart through ostia and is pumped anteriorly to sinuses again. The respiratory system consists of a network of trachea, that open through 10 pairs of small holes called spiracles present on the lateral side of the body. Thin branching tubes (tracheal tubes subdivided into tracheoles) carry O₂ from the air to all the parts.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Blood vascular system of cockroach is a closed type, where blood vessels are well developed and open into space (hematocele).','The haemocoel is composed of colourless plasma and haemocytes and bathes the organs located in the hematocele.','Heart of cockroach consists of elongated muscular tube lying along mid ventral line of abdomen and is differentiated into funnel shaped chambers with sinuses on either side','The respiratory system consists of a network of trachea, that open through 10 pairs of small holes called spiracles present on the lateral side of the body','NEW','11-113',NULL,NULL),
(70571,'biology','In the respiratory system of cockroach, the opening of the spiracles is regulated by the _______','Sphincters','In th respiratory system of cockroach, the opening of the spiracles is regulated by the sphincters.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Sphincters','Alveolar Ducts','Ostia','Tracheolar valves','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70572,'biology','Which of the following is incorrect regarding cockroach\'s nervous system','The nervous system of cockroach is spread throughout the body. The head holds a bit of a nervous system while the rest is situated along the dorsal (spinal-side) part of its body','The nervous system of cockroach consists of a series of fused, segmentally arranged ganglia joined by paired longitudinal connectives on the ventral side.The nervous system of cockroach is spread throughout the body. The\nhead holds a bit of a nervous system while the rest is situated along the\nventral (belly-side) part of its body. "If the\nhead of a cockroach is cut off, it will still live for as long as one week.In cockroach,\nthe sense organs are antennae, eyes, maxillary palps, labial palps, anal\ncerci,','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','The nervous system of cockroach consists of a series of fused, segmentally arranged ganglia joined by paired longitudinal connectives on the ventral side.','The nervous system of cockroach is spread throughout the body. The head holds a bit of a nervous system while the rest is situated along the dorsal (spinal-side) part of its body','If the head of a cockroach is cut off, it will still live for as long as one week','In cockroach, the sense organs are antennae, eyes, maxillary palps, labial palps, anal cerci,','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70573,'biology','In Cockroaches,The sperms are stored in the _______ and are glued together in the form of bundles called ______ which are discharged during copulation(respectively)','Seminal vesicles, spermatophores','The sperms are stored in the seminal\nvesicles and are glued together in the form of bundles called\nspermatophores which are discharged during copulation','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Seminal vesicles, spermatophores','Uretric duct, semen','Uretric duct, spermatophores','Seminal vesicles, semen','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70574,'biology','The development of P. americana is ________, meaning there is development through ________stage.','Paurometabolous, nymphal','The development of P. americana is paurometabolous, meaning there is development through nymphal stage.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Cockroach',NULL,'2','mcq','Paurometabolous, nymphal','Ametabolous,no stages','Hemimetabolous,nymph','Holometabolous, larva','NEW','11-115',NULL,NULL),
(70601,'chemistry','Consider the reaction, H₂(g) + I₂(g) ⇌ 2HI (g). If we increase partial pressure of H₂, what will happen to the partial pressure of I₂(g) ?','Decrease','(NCERT chemistry class 11; page 209, Fig- 7.8)Fig-7.8 diagram(ne0709)','Physical Chemistry >> Equilibrium >> Factors Affecting Equilibria',NULL,'3','mcq','Increase','Decrease','Remain same','Can\'t be determined','NEW','11-209','11-185',NULL),
(70602,'chemistry','Choose the correct answer --> \nI. Addition of aq. HgCl₂ to [Fe(SCN)]²⁺ also decreases red colour.\nII.Addition of potassium thiocyanate on the other hand increases the red colour.','Both are true','Addition of aq. HgCl₂ also decreases red colour because Hg²⁺ reacts with SCN⁻ ions to form stable complex ion [Hg(SCN)₄]²⁻. Removal of free SCN⁻ (aq) shifts the equilibrium in equation (7.24) from right to left to replenish SCN⁻ ions. Addition of potassium thiocyanate on the other hand increases the colour intensity of the solution as it shift theequilibrium to right.\n(NCERT chemistry class 11; page 210, paragraph 3)','Physical Chemistry >> Equilibrium >> Factors Affecting Equilibria',NULL,'2','mcq','Both are false','Both are true','I is true but II is false','II is true but I is false','NEW','11-210','11-186',NULL),
(70603,'chemistry','The relation between equilibrium constant for an exothermic reaction and temperature is as','Decreases as temperature increases','The equilibrium constant for an exothermic reaction (negative ∆H) decreases as the temperature increases.(NCERT chemistry class 11; page 211 ; paragraph 5)','Physical Chemistry >> Equilibrium >> Factors Affecting Equilibria',NULL,'1','mcq','Decreases as temperature increases','Increases as temperature increases','They are inversly proportional to each other','Both a and c','NEW','11-211','11-187',NULL),
(70604,'chemistry','Choose the correct one --->\nI. Catalyst lowers the activation energy for the forward and reverse reactions by exactly the same amount.\nII. Catalyst does not affect the equilibrium composition of a reaction mixture.','Both are true','Catalyst lowers the activation energy for the forward and reverse reactions by exactly the same amount. Catalyst does no affect the equilibrium composition of a reaction mixture.\n(NCERT chemistry class 11; page 212 ; paragraph 3)','Physical Chemistry >> Equilibrium >> Factors Affecting Equilibria',NULL,'1','mcq','Both are false','Both are true','I is true but II is false','II is true but I is false','NEW','11-212','11-188',NULL),
(70605,'biology','The adult frog is -','Carnivorous','The alimentary canal is short because frogs are carnivores and hence the\nlength of intestine is reduced. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:116, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'1','mcq','Herbivorous','Carnivorous','Omnivorous','None of these','NEW','11-116','11-81',NULL),
(70606,'biology','The structure present in man but absent in frog is -','Salivary gland','(Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:117, Fig no. 7.20','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'2','mcq','Pancreas','Salivary gland','Thyroid gland','Adrenal gland','NEW','11-117','11-82',NULL),
(70607,'biology','In frog, digestion of fats occurs mostly in -','Small intestine','Partially digested food called chyme is passed from stomach to the first part of the small intestine, the duodenum. The duodenum receives bile from gall bladder and pancreatic juices from the pancreas through a common bile duct. Bile emulsifies fat and pancreatic juices digest carbohydrates and proteins. Final digestion takes place in the intestine. Digested food is absorbed by the numerous finger-like folds in the inner wall of intestine called villi and microvilli. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:117, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'2','mcq','Rectum','Stomach','Duodenum','Small intestine','NEW','11-117','11-82',NULL),
(70608,'biology','Frog is-','Ureotelic','The frog\nexcretes urea and thus is a ureotelic animal. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:118, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'2','mcq','Ammonotelic','Uricotelic','Ureotelic','Guanotelic','NEW','11-118','11-83',NULL),
(70609,'biology','Chief nitrogenous waste product in frog is -','Urea','The frog excretes urea and thus is a ureotelic animals (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:118, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'2','mcq','Ammonia','Urea','Uric acid','Allantoin','NEW','11-118','11-83',NULL),
(70610,'biology','In frog, the ureter acts as urinogenital duct in -','Male','Frogs have well organised male and female\nreproductive systems. Male reproductive organs\nconsist of a pair of yellowish ovoid testes (Figure\n7.21), which are found adhered to the upper part\nof kidneys by a double fold of peritoneum called\nmesorchium. Vasa efferentia are 10-12 in\nnumber that arise from testes. They enter the\nkidneys on their side and open into Bidder’s\ncanal. Finally it communicates with the\nurinogenital duct that comes out of the kidneys\nand opens into the cloaca. The cloaca is a small,\nmedian chamber that is used to pass faecal\nmatter, urine and sperms to the exterior. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:118, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'2','mcq','Male','Female','Male and  female','Neither sexes','NEW','11-118','11-82',NULL),
(70611,'biology','In male frog, 10 - 12 vasa efferentia (arising from testis) enter the kidney and open into-','Bidder\'s canal','Frogs have well organised male and female\nreproductive systems. Male reproductive organs\nconsist of a pair of yellowish ovoid testes, which are found adhered to the upper part\nof kidneys by a double fold of peritoneum called\nmesorchium. Vasa efferentia are 10-12 in\nnumber that arise from testes. They enter the\nkidneys on their side and open into Bidder’s\ncanal. Finally it communicates with the\nurinogenital duct that comes out of the kidneys\nand opens into the cloaca. The cloaca is a small,\nmedian chamber that is used to pass faecal\nmatter, urine and sperms to the exterior. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:119, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'2','mcq','Urinogenital duct','Seminal vesicle','Bidder\'s canal','Spermatophore','NEW','11-119','11-83',NULL),
(70612,'biology','Bidder\'s canal is meant for passage of-','Sperms','Frogs have well organised male and female\nreproductive systems. Male reproductive organs\nconsist of a pair of yellowish ovoid testes (Figure\n7.21), which are found adhered to the upper part\nof kidneys by a double fold of peritoneum called\nmesorchium. Vasa efferentia are 10-12 in\nnumber that arise from testes. They enter the\nkidneys on their side and open into Bidder’s\ncanal. Finally it communicates with the\nurinogenital duct that comes out of the kidneys\nand opens into the cloaca. The cloaca is a small,\nmedian chamber that is used to pass faecal\nmatter, urine and sperms to the exterior. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:119, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'2','mcq','Ova','Urine','Sperms','All of these','NEW','11-119','11-84',NULL),
(70613,'biology','Bidder\'s canal in frog is found in -','Kidney','Frogs have well organised male and female reproductive systems. Male reproductive organs consist of a pair of yellowish ovoid testes , which are found adhered to the upper part of kidneys by a double fold of peritoneum called mesorchium. Vasa efferentia are 10-12 in number that arise from testes. They enter the kidneys on their side and open into Bidder’s canal. Finally it communicates with the urinogenital duct that comes out of the kidneys and opens into the cloaca. The cloaca is a small, median chamber that is used to pass faecal matter, urine and sperms to the exterior. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:119, paragraph no:3)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'2','mcq','Liver','Testis','Ovary','Kidney','NEW','11-119','11-83',NULL),
(70614,'biology','Which of the following is not an use of frog?','Frogs are used for drug testing','Frogs are beneficial for mankind because they eat insects and protect\nthe crop. Frogs maintain ecological balance because these serve as an\nimportant link of food chain and food web in the ecosystem. In some\ncountries the muscular legs of frog are used as food by man.         (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11: page no:120, paragraph no:1)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'2','mcq','Legs of frog are used as food','Frog is suitable for classroom studies','Frogs maintain ecological balance because they serve as an important link of food chain and food web','Frogs are used for drug testing','NEW','11-120','11-84',NULL),
(70615,'biology','Match the correct names of a,b,c and d parts in the given diagram (0731)','a-Rectum,b-Cloacal Aperture,c-Urinary bladder,d-Lung','NCERT class 11 Figure 7.20 page.no-117','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'2','match','a,Rectum','b,Cloacal Aperture','c,Urinary bladder','d,Lung','NEW','11-117','11-83','/ncert/pyq/biology/match/70615q.png'),
