(70617,'biology','Identify the given diagram (0733)','Female reproductive system of frog','NCERT class 11 Figure 7.22 page.no-119','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'2','mcq','Female reproductive system of Human','Male reproductive system of Human','Male reproductive system of frog','Female reproductive system of frog','NEW','11-119','11-83','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/70617q.png'),
(70618,'biology','Which of the following regarding frogs is incorrect','Eyes are bulged and covered by a nictitating membrane that protects them while outside water and prevent them from drying.','The hind limbs end\nin five digits and they are larger and muscular than\nfore limbs that end in four digits. Feet have webbed\ndigits that help in swimming. Frogs exhibit sexual\ndimorphism. Male frogs can be distinguished by the\npresence of sound producing vocal sacs and also a\ncopulatory pad on the first digit of the fore limbs\nwhich are absent in female frogs. Eyes\nare bulged and covered by a nictitating membrane that protects them\nwhile in water.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'2','mcq','The hind limbs end in five digits and they are larger and muscular than fore limbs that end in four digits.','Male frogs can be distinguished by the presence of sound producing vocal sacs and also a copulatory pad on the first digit of the fore limbs which are absent in female frogs.','Frogs exhibit sexual dimorphism.','Eyes are bulged and covered by a nictitating membrane that protects them while outside water and prevent them from drying.','NEW','11-116','11-80',NULL),
(70619,'biology','Which of the following regarding digestive system in frogs is incorrect','The undigested solid waste moves into the rectum and passes out through anus.','Food is captured by the bilobed tongue.\nDigestion of food takes place by the action of HCl and gastric juices secreted\nfrom the walls of the stomach.Liver secretes bile that is stored in\nthe gall bladder. Pancreas, a digestive gland produces pancreatic juice\ncontaining digestive enzymes.duct. Bile emulsifies fat and pancreatic\njuices digest carbohydrates and proteins. Final digestion takes place in the\nintestine.The undigested solid\nwaste moves into the rectum and passes out through cloaca.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'2','mcq','The undigested solid waste moves into the rectum and passes out through anus.','Liver secretes bile that is stored in the gall bladder. Pancreas, a digestive gland produces pancreatic juice containing digestive enzymes.','Food is captured by the bilobed tongue. Digestion of food takes place by the action of HCl and gastric juices secreted from the walls of the stomach.','Bile emulsifies fat and pancreatic juices digest carbohydrates and proteins and final digestion takes place in the intestine.','NEW','11-117','11-82',NULL),
(70620,'biology','Which of the following regarding nervous system in frogs is incorrect','Hind-brain consists of cerebellum, pons and medulla oblongata.','There are ten\npairs of cranial nerves arising from the brain. Brain\nis enclosed in a bony structure called brain box\n(cranium).The brain is divided into fore-brain,\nmid-brain and hind-brain."Hind-brain\nconsists of cerebellum,and medulla oblongata. not pons;"','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'2','mcq','There are ten pairs of cranial nerves arising from the brain. Brain is enclosed in a bony structure called brain box (cranium).','The brain is divided into fore-brain, mid-brain and hind-brain.','Forebrain includes olfactory lobes, paired cerebral hemispheres and unpaired diencephalon. The midbrain is characterised by a pair of optic lobes.','Hind-brain consists of cerebellum, pons and medulla oblongata.','NEW','11-119','11-83',NULL),
(70621,'biology','In Frogs,Forebrain includes________., paired cerebral hemispheres and unpaired diencephalon. The midbrain is characterised by a pair of ________.(respectively)','Olfactory lobes,optic lobes','In Frogs,Forebrain includes\nolfactory lobes, paired cerebral hemispheres and\nunpaired diencephalon. The midbrain is\ncharacterised by a pair of optic lobes.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'2','mcq','Olfactory lobes,optic lobes','Auditory lobes, olfactory lobes','Auditory lobes,optic lobes','Olfactory lobes, auditory lobes','NEW','11-119','11-83',NULL),
(70622,'biology','Which of the following regarding sense organs in frogs is incorrect','Smell (oral epithelium),','Frog has different types of sense organs, namely\norgans of touch (sensory papillae), taste (taste\nbuds), smell (nasal epithelium), vision (eyes) and\nhearing (tympanum with internal ears).','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'2','mcq','Organs of touch (sensory papillae),','Taste (taste buds),','Smell (oral epithelium),','Vision (eyes)','NEW','11-119','11-83',NULL),
(70623,'biology','Which of the following regarding sense organs in frogs is incorrect','Internal ear is absent in frogs and only tympanum can be seen externally.','The medulla oblongata passes out through the foramen magnum and continues into spinal cord, which is enclosed in the vertebral column.Eyes in a frog are a pair of spherical structures situated in the orbit in skull. These are simple eyes (possessing only one unit). External ear is absent in frogs and only tympanum can be seen externally. The ear is an organ of hearing as well as balancing (equilibrium). Out of these, eyes and internal ears are well-organised structures and the rest are cellular aggregations around nerve endings.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'2','mcq','Simple eyes, possesing only unit in a frog are a pair of spherical structures situated in the orbit in skull.','Internal ear is absent in frogs and only tympanum can be seen externally.','Out of these, eyes and internal ears are well-organised structures and the rest are cellular aggregations around nerve endings.','The medulla oblongata passes out through the foramen magnum and continues into spinal cord, which is enclosed in the vertebral column.','NEW','11-119','11-83',NULL),
(350302,'biology','The average temperature on land varies depending on what factors?\n \n i) Seasonally\n \n ii) From plains to the mountain tops.\n \n iii) Decreases progressively from the equator towards the poles\n \n iv) Decreases progressively from the poles towards the equator','i, ii, and iii','The average temperature on land varies seasonally, decreases progressively from the equator towards the poles and from plains to the mountain tops.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:221, paragraph no:3)','Ecology >> Organisms And Populations >> Major Abiotic factors(Temperature  and  Water)',NULL,'2','mcq','i, ii, and iii','i and iv','ii and iii','i and iii','NEW','12-221',NULL,NULL),
(70624,'biology','Which of the following regarding reproduction in frogs is correct','Indirect development through larval stage called tadpole.','A pair of oviduct arising from the ovaries opens into the cloaca separately.A mature female can\nlay 2500 to 3000 ova at a time. Fertilisation is external and takes place in water. Development involves a larval stage called tadpole. Tadpole\nundergoes metamorphosis to form the adult.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'1','mcq','A pair of oviduct arising from the ovaries opens into the vagina separately.','A mature male frog can lay 2500 to 3000 ova at a time.','Fertilisation is internal and takes place in the female genital tract.','Indirect development through larval stage called tadpole.','NEW','11-120','11-84',NULL),
(70625,'biology','Frog’s heart when taken out of the body continues to beat for sometime. select the best option from the following statements.\n\n(1) Frog is a poikilotherm.\n\n(2) Frog does not have any coronary circulation.\n\n(3) Heart is “myogenic” in nature.\n\n(4) Heart is autoexcitable.','(3) and (4)','Frog’s heart is myogenic, i.e., heartbeat originates from muscles of heart. Hence, it is autorythmic. Wave of contraction originates from sinus venosus and spreads to wall of sinus venosus and both auricles. This compels the heart to beat. Due to this reason, frog’s heart will continue to beat as long as it gets supply of ATP.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'2','mcq','Only (4)','(1) and (2)','(3) and (4)','Only 3)','NEW','11-116','11-80',NULL),
(70626,'biology','Find the incorrect match','Rana- Common toad','Rana- Common toad','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'1','mcq','Bufo- Toad','Rana- Frog','Hyla- Tree frog','Rana- Common toad','NEW','11-116','11-80',NULL),
(70627,'biology','The biological adaptation that allows frogs to obtain water for their survival during conditions of water scarcity is the','Presence of water channels in the skin by which they absorb water from their surroundings.','Presence of water channels in the skin by which they absorb water from their surroundings.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'1','mcq','Presence of a modified tongue that acts like a sponge to suck water from damp soils.','Presence of water channels in the skin by which they absorb water from their surroundings.','Presence of ciliated esophagus that helps in separating water from ingested particulate matter.','Selective feeding on plants with a large amount of water that would fulfill the water requirement.','NEW','11-117',NULL,NULL),
(70628,'biology','Statement I: They have the ability to change the colour to hide them from their enemies (camouflage). \nStatement II: They undergo summer sleep called as hibernation as well as winter sleep called as aestivation.','Only Statement I is correct','Only Statement I is correct','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'1','mcq','Only Statement II is correct','Only Statement I is correct','Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect.','Both Statement I and Statement II are correct.','NEW','11-116','11-80',NULL),
(70629,'biology','Frogs belonging to class phylum chordata are animals and show hibernation in and aestivation in of','Amphibia, poikilothermic, winter, summer','Amphibia, poikilothermic, winter, summer','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'1','mcq','Hemichordata, poikilothermic, winter, summer','Amphibia, poikilothermic, summer, rainy season','Amphibia, poikilothermic, winter, summer','Amphibia, warmblooded, winter, summer','NEW','11-116','11-80',NULL),
(70630,'biology','The frogs have the ability to change to hide them from enemies (camouflage).This protective coloration is called -','Mimicry','Mimicry','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'1','mcq','Mimicry','Antagonism','Burrowing','Symbiosis','NEW','11-116','11-80',NULL),
(70631,'biology','Assertion (A): Hibernation during winter and aestivation during summer is seen in frogs.\n\nReason (R): Frogs are poikilotherms.','(1) Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation for A.','(1) Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation for A.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'2','mcq','(1) Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation for A.','(2) Both A and R are true both R is not the correct explanation for A.','(3) A is true and R is false.','(4) A is false and R is true.','NEW','11-116','11-80',NULL),
