(70640,'biology','The undigested solid waste moves into the rectum and passes out through ______.','Cloaca','Digested food is absorbed by the numerous finger-like folds in the inner wall of intestine called villi and microvilli. The undigested solid waste moves into the rectum and passes out through cloaca.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'2','mcq','Cloaca','Small intestine','Large intestine','Duodenum','NEW','11-117','11-82',NULL),
(70641,'biology','What is the correct pathway of digestion of food particles in frog ?','Mouth → buccal cavity → pharynx → oesophagus → stomach → intestine → rectum → cloaca','The mouth opens into the buccal cavity that leads to the oesophagus through pharynx. Oesophagus is a short tube that opens into the stomach which in turn continues as the intestine, rectum and finally opens outside by the cloaca.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'1','mcq','Mouth → buccal cavity → pharynx → oesophagus → stomach → intestine → rectum → cloaca','Mouth → buccal cavity → pharynx → oesophagus → stomach → intestine →   cloaca → rectum','Mouth → buccal cavity → pharynx → oesophagus → intestine → stomach  → rectum → cloaca','Mouth → buccal cavity  → oesophagus → pharynx → stomach → intestine → rectum → cloaca','NEW','11-117','11-82',NULL),
(70642,'biology','Digestion of food takes place by the action of ____ and gastric juices secreted from the ______.','HCl & walls of stomach','Digestion of food takes place by the action of HCl and gastric juices secreted from the walls of the stomach.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'2','mcq','HCl & walls of stomach','NaCl & walls of stomach','HCl & Duodenum','NaCl & walls of Duodenum','NEW','11-117','11-82',NULL),
(70643,'biology','What is mode of respiration when frog is under the water?','Cutaneous Respiration','Cutaneous Respiration','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'1','mcq','Cutaneous Respiration','Lung','Vascular skin & Buccal cavity','None of them','NEW','11-117','11-82',NULL),
(70645,'biology','Which organ helpful in respiration, when frog is partially under water & partially in air?','Vascular skin & Buccal cavity','Vascular skin & Buccal cavity','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'1','mcq','Cutaneous Respiration only','Vascular skin & Buccal cavity','Lung','None of them','NEW','11-118','11-82',NULL),
(70646,'biology','Which organ helpful in respiration, when frog is in land surface?','Lung','Lung','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'1','mcq','Cutaneous Respiration only','Vascular skin & Buccal cavity','Lung','None of them','NEW','11-118','11-82',NULL),
(70647,'biology','What is the function of blood in Frog ?','All of them','Transport of oxygen, transport of nutrients & removal of waste products','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'1','mcq','Transport of oxygen','Transport of nutrients','Removal of waste Products','All of them','NEW','11-118','11-82',NULL),
(70648,'biology','What type of blood circulation present in frog ?','Incomplete double circulation','Incomplete double circulation','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'1','mcq','Incomplete double circulation','Double circulation','Single circulation','Incomplete single circulation','NEW','11-118','11-82',NULL),
(70649,'biology','Frog has 1 atria & 2 ventricles.','FALSE','Frog has 2 atria & 1 ventricle','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'2','mcq','TRUE','FALSE',NULL,NULL,'NEW','11-118','11-82',NULL),
(70650,'biology','What is the nature of frogs tongue ?','Bilobed','Frog has bilobed tongue.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'1','mcq','Unilobed','Bilobed','Trilobed','Tetralobed','NEW','11-117','11-82',NULL),
(70651,'biology','Gall bladder stores _____','Bile','Liver secretes bile that is stored in gall bladder. Gall bladder stores bile juice. The duodenum receives bile from gall bladder. (NCERT class 11, structural organization in animals , Frog, pg.117)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Frog',NULL,'1','mcq','Bile','Pancreatic juice','Intestinal juice','None of them','NEW','11-117','11-81',NULL),
(70701,'chemistry','Which of the following facts are true ?\n(i)Lemon has citric acid as well as ascorbic acid\n(ii)Washing soda can turn red litmus blue.\n(iii)Acids on reaction with metals liberate dinitrogen gas.','(i) and (ii) are true , (iii) is false','Lemon and orange juices contain citric and ascorbic acids, and tartaric acid is found in tamarind paste.\nAs most of the acids taste sour, the word “acid” has been derived from a latin word “acidus” meaning sour. Acids are known to turn blue litmus paper into red and liberate dihydrogenon reacting with some metals. Similarly, bases are known to turn red litmus paper blue, taste bitter and feel soapy. A common example of abase is washing soda used for washing purposes.\n(NCERT chemistry class 11; page 213 ; paragraph 2)','Physical Chemistry >> Equilibrium >> Acids, Bases and Salts',NULL,'1','mcq','All are true','(i) is true ,(ii) and (iii) are false','(i) and (ii) are true , (iii) is false','(i) and (iii) are true ,(ii) is false','NEW','11-213','11-189',NULL),
(70702,'chemistry','NaCl salt completely dissolves within water. One of the main reasons of this phenomenon is','Water has high dielectric constant','The electrostatic forces between two charges are inversely proportional to dielectric constant of the medium. Water, a universal solvent, possesses a very high dielectric constant of 80. Thus, when sodium chloride is dissolved in water, the electrostatic interactions are reduced by a factor of 80 and this facilitates the ions to move freely in the solution.\n(NCERT chemistry class 11; page 213 ; paragraph 2)','Physical Chemistry >> Equilibrium >> Acids, Bases and Salts',NULL,'3','mcq','NaCl is unstable','NaCl is stable','Water has high dielectric constant','None of the above','NEW','11-213','11-189',NULL),
(70703,'chemistry','(i)According to Arrhenius theory, acids are substances that dissociates in water to give H⁺ ions.\n(ii)According to  Brönsted-Lowry theory bases are substance that produce OH⁻ ions.\n(iii)According to Brönsted-Lowry theory, acid is a substance that is capable of donating an H⁺ ion.\n(iv)According to Arrhenius theory, bases are substances that accepts  H⁺ ions.','(i) and (iii) are true , (ii) and (iv) are false','According to Arrhenius theory, acids are substances that dissociates in water to give hydrogen ions H⁺ (aq) and bases are substances that produce hydroxyl ionsOH⁻ (aq).\n(NCERT chemistry class 11; page 214; paragraph 2)\nAccording to Brönsted-Lowry theory, acid is a substance that is capable of donating a hydrogen ion H+ and bases are substances capable of accepting a hydrogen ion, H+.\n(NCERT chemistry class 11; page 214; paragraph 6).','Physical Chemistry >> Equilibrium >> Acids, Bases and Salts',NULL,'1','mcq','(i) and (ii) are correct ,(iii) and (iv) are false','(i)  and (iv) are true ,(ii) and (iii) are false','(i) and (iii) are true , (ii) and (iv) are false','(i) and (iii) are false , (ii) and (iv) are true','NEW','11-214','11-190',NULL),
(70715,'biology','One very special feature in the earthworm (pheretima) is that [NEET 2011]','The typhlosole greatly increases the effective absorption area of the digested food in the intestine','The characteristic feature of the\n\nintestine after 26th segment except the last 23rd-25th segments is the presence of internal median fold of dorsal wall called typhlosole. This\n\nincreases the effective area of absorption in the intestine. \n\n (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:108, paragraph no:2)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Fertilization of eggs occurs inside the body','The typhlosole greatly increases the effective absorption area of the digested food in the intestine','The s shaped setae embedded in the integument are the defensive weapons used against the enemies','It has a long dorsal tubular heart','NEW','11-108',NULL,NULL),
(70716,'biology','Which of the following happens in the common cockroach? [NEET 2011]','The food is ground by mandibles and gizzard','Mouth part of cockroach contain two mandibles, which bears teeth. When both the mandibles work simultaneously in a horizontal plane, the food matter is cut and masticated into fine and smaller pieces. Gizzard is a part of alimentary canal. It bears six muscular folds which are covered by chitinous conical plates, the teeth, used for grinding the food (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:113, paragraph no:1)...','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Malpighian tubules are excretory organs projecting out from the colon.','O₂ is transported by haemoglobin in blood.','Nitrogenous excretory product is urea.','The food is ground by mandibles and gizzard','NEW','11-113',NULL,NULL),
(70717,'biology','Frogs differ from humans in possessing [MAINS 2011]','Nucleated red blood cells','Human erythrocytes are enucleated, discoidal while in frogs erythrocytes are large, oval and biconvex nucleated cells. Erythrocytes are the carriers of haemoglobin.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Paired cerebral hemispheres','Hepatic portal system','Nucleated red blood cells','Thyroid as well as parathyroid','NEW','11-118',NULL,NULL),
(70718,'biology','The cells lining the blood vessels belong to the category of [MAINS  2011, 2010]','Squamous epithelium','Simple squamous epithelium is composed of large flat cells whose edges fit closely together like the tiles in a floor, hence it is also called pavement epithelium. The nuclei of the cells are flattened and often lie at the centre of the cells and cause bulgings of cells surface. The epithelium lines the blood vessels, lymph vessels, heart, terminal bronchioles, alveoli of the lungs, walls of the Bowman’s capsules, descending limbs of loop of Henle. In the blood vessels and heart it is called endothelium.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:101, paragraph no:2)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Smooth muscle tissue','Squamous epithelium','Columnar epithelium','Connective tissue','NEW','11-101',NULL,NULL),
(70719,'biology','Which one of the following structures in pheretima is correctly matched with its function? [MAINS 2011]','Clitellum secretes cocoon','In a mature earthworm, segments of clitellum secretes cocoon (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:110, paragraph no:3)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Clitellum secretes cocoon','Gizzard absorbs digested food','Setae defence against predators','Typhlosole storage of extra nutrients','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70720,'biology','Which one of the following correctly describes the location of some body parts in the earthworm pheretima? [AIPMT 2009]','Two pairs of testes in 10 th and 11 th segments','In Pheretima two pairs of testis sac are situated in the tenth and eleventh segments. Each testis sac of the tenth segment encloses a testis and a seminal funnel. Each testis sac of the eleventh segment encloses a testis, a seminal vesicle and a seminal funnel.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:110, paragraph no:4)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Four pairs of spermathecae in 4 th 7 th segments','One pair of ovaries attached at intersegmental septum of 14 th and 15 th segments','Two pairs of testes in 10 th and 11 th segments','Two pairs of accessory glands in 16 th 18 th segments','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70721,'biology','Which one of the following is correct pairing of a body part and the kind of muscle tissue that moves it? [AIPMT 2009]','Iris – involuntary smooth muscle','Smooth muscles are called as involuntary muscles as action of these muscles is controlled by autonomic nervous system i.e. not under the control of animal’s will. Iris of eyes consist of smooth involuntary muscles. Abdominal wall also have smooth muscles. Biceps of upper arm is made of skeletal muscles while heart wall consists of cardiac muscles.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:105, paragraph no:1)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Biceps of upper arm – smooth muscle fibres','Abdominal wall – voluntary smooth muscle','Iris – involuntary smooth muscle','Heart wall – involuntary unstriated muscle','NEW','11-105',NULL,NULL),
(70722,'biology','The epithelial tissue present on the inner surface of bronchioles and fallopian tubes is [AIPMT 2009]','Ciliated','(Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:101, paragraph no:3)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Glandular','Ciliated','Squamous','Cuboidal','NEW','11-101',NULL,NULL),
(70723,'biology','The cell junctions called tight, adhering and gap junctions are found in [AIPMT 2009]','Epithelial tissue','Epithelial tissues consist of variously shaped cells closely arranged in one or more layers. The cells are held together by intercellular junctions like tight, adhering and gap junctions.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:101, paragraph no:1)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Connective tissue','Epithelial tissue','Neural tissue','Muscular tissue','NEW','11-101',NULL,NULL),
(70724,'biology','The kind of tissue that forms the supportive structure in our pinna (external ears) is also found in [AIPMT 2009]','Tip of the nose','Yellow elastic fibrocartilage, a type of skeletal tissue, is found in the pinna, Eustachian tubes, epiglottis and tip of the nose. It is a type of cartilage and due to presence of yellow fibres, it becomes more flexible.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:104, paragraph no:1)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Nails','Ear ossicles','Tip of the nose','Vertebrae','NEW','11-104',NULL,NULL),
(350303,'biology','Temperature ranges from sub zero levels in polar areas and high altitudes to _______ in tropical deserts in summer.','> 50 °C','It ranges from sub zero levels in polar areas and high altitudes to >50C in tropical deserts in summer.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:221, paragraph no:3)','Ecology >> Organisms And Populations >> Major Abiotic factors(Temperature  and  Water)',NULL,'1','mcq','> 20 °C','> 50 °C','> 40 °C','none of the above','NEW','12-221',NULL,NULL),
(70725,'biology','Earthworms have no skeleton but during burrowing, the anterior end becomes turgid and acts as a hydraulic skeleton. it is due to [AIPMT 2008]','Coelomic fluid','Hydraulic skeleton is the system of support found in soft bodied invertebrates, which relies on the incompressibility of fluids contained within the body cavity. In earthworms the coelomic fluid is under pressure within the coelom and therefore provides support for internal organs. Due to hydraulic skeleton, during burrowing, the anterior end becomes turgid and aids in relaxation of longitudinal muscles.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:107, paragraph no:2)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Gut peristalsis','Setae','Coelomic fluid','Blood','NEW','11-107',NULL,NULL),
(70726,'biology','Which one of the following is the true description about an animal concerned? [AIPMT 2008]','Cockroach 10 pairs of spiracles (2 pairs on thorax and 8 pairs on abdomen)','The respiratory system consists of a network of trachea, that open through 10 pairs of small holes called spiracles present on the lateral side of the body. Thin branching tubes\n(tracheal tubes subdivided into tracheoles) carry O₂ from the air to all the parts. NCERT Class 11, chapter 7 Page 113.\nthe divison of spiracles is such that, there are 2 pairs in the thorax and remaining 8 pairs in the abdomen.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Rat left kidney is slightly higher in position than the right one','Cockroach 10 pairs of spiracles (2 pairs on thorax and 8 pairs on abdomen)','Earthworm the alimentary canal consists of a sequence of pharynx, oesophagus, stomach, gizzard and intestine','Frog body divisible into three regions head, neck and trunk','NEW','11-113',NULL,NULL),
(70727,'biology','Which one of the following pairs of structures distinguishes a nerve cell from other types of cell? [AIPMT 2007]','Perikaryon and dendrites','Neuron (nerve cell) is one of the basic functional units of the nervous system. Neuron is a cell specialized to transmit electrical nerve impulse and so carry information from one part of the body to another. Each neuron has an enlarged portion, the cell body (perikaryon), containing the nucleus; from the body extend several processes (dendrites) through which impulses enter from their branches. A longer process, the nerve fibre, extends outward and carries impulses away from the cell body. This is normally unbranched except at the nerve ending. The point of contact of one neuron with another is known as a synapse.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Vacuoles and fibres','Flagellum and medullary sheath','Nucleus and mitochondria','Perikaryon and dendrites','NEW','11-105',NULL,NULL),
(70728,'biology','In which one of the following preparations are you likely to come across cell junctions most frequently? [AIPMT 2007]','Ciliated epithelium','From the given four options cell junctions come across most frequently in the preparation of ciliated epithelium. A cell junction is a structure within a tissue of a multicellular organism. Cell junctions are especially abundant in epithelial tissues. They consist of protein complexes and provide contact between neighbouring cells, between a cell and the extracellular matrix, or they built up the paracellular barrier of epithelia and control the paracellular transport. Ciliated epithelium is a region of epithelium consisting of columnar or cuboidal cells bearing hairlike appendages that are capable of beating rapidly. Ciliated epithelium performs the function of moving particles or fluid over the epithelial surface in such structures as the trachea, bronchial tubes, and nasal cavities. It often occurs in the vicinity of mucus secreting goblet cells. The other three (thrombocytes, tendon and hyaline cartilage) belongs to connective tissue. Connective tissue is widely distributed and has many functions including support, packing, defence and repair. Thrombocytes or platelets aid the formation of blood clots by releasing various protein substances. Tendon attaches a muscle to a bone and hyaline cartilage consists largely of glycosaminoglycan, giving a shiny glass like appearance and gives flexibility and support at the joints.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:101, paragraph no:2)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Thrombocytes','Tendon','Hyaline cartilage','Ciliated epithelium','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(70729,'biology','Areolar connective tissue joins [AIPMT 2006]','Integument with muscles','Areolar tissue is a loose connective tissue comprised of a semifluid ground substance containing several kinds of loosely arranged fibres. Its function is to attach the skin to the underlying tissues, to fill the spaces between various organs and thus holds them in place, and surrounds and supports the blood vessels. Tendons connect muscles with bone while ligaments connect bone with bone.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Bones with bones','Fat body with muscles','Integument with muscles','Bones with muscles','NEW','11-103',NULL,NULL),
(70730,'biology','Mast cells secrete [AIPMT 2006]','Histamine','Mast cells are granulated wandering cells that are found in connective tissue. Their granules contain histamine which is a vasodilator. It causes running nose, sneezing and itching; and narrows the airways in the lungs. Haemoglobin and myoglobin are the pigments present in the blood and muscles respectively.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Haemoglobin','Hippurin','Myoglobin','Histamine','NEW','11-103',NULL,NULL),
(70731,'biology','Earthworms are [AIPMT 2006]','Ammonotelic when plenty of water is available','Earthworm has excretory organ called nephridia. Ammonia is the chief excretory waste when water is available and hence it is ammonotelic in water and terrestrial earthworm is ureotelic.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:106, paragraph no:2)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Ammonotelic when plenty of water is available','Ureotelic when plenty of water is available','Uricotelic when plenty of water is available','Uricotelic under conditions of water scarcity','NEW','11-106',NULL,NULL),
(70732,'biology','Four healthy people in their twenties got involved in injuries resulting in damage and death of few cells of the following. which of the cells are least likely to be replaced by new cells? [AIPMT 2005]','Neurons','Neurons are least likely to be replaced by new cells as they have least regeneration power. Osteocytes are the bone forming cells. Liver cells and Malpighian layer of the skin have regeneration power.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Liver cells','Neurons','Malpighian layer of the skin','Osteocytes','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(350304,'biology','In which of following habitats, the average temperatures exceed 100 °C?\n \n i) Thermal springs\n \n ii) Polar ice caps in summer\n \n iii) Deep-sea hydrothermal vents.','i and iii','There are, however, unique habitats such as thermal springs and deep-sea hydrothermal vents where average temperatures exceed 100 °C.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:221, paragraph no:3)','Ecology >> Organisms And Populations >> Major Abiotic factors(Temperature  and  Water)',NULL,'2','mcq','i, ii, and iii','i and ii','ii and iii','i and iii','NEW','12-221',NULL,NULL),
(70733,'biology','Mast cells of connective tissue contain [ AIPMT 2004]','Heparin and histamine','Mast cells are the large cells with densely granular cytoplasm that is found in connective tissues. Their granules contain histamine which is a vasodilator, heparin which is an anticoagulant and serotonin which acts as a mediator of inflammation and allergic reactions. Vasopressin is a hormone secreted by posterior pituitary gland. Calcitonin is a hormone secreted by thyroid gland. Melanin is a pigment produced by specialized epidermal cells called melanocytes. Relaxin is a hormone produced by the corpus luteum and placenta during the terminal stages of pregnancy.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Vasopressin and relaxin','Heparin and histamine','Heparin and calcitonin','Serotonin and melanin','NEW','11-103',NULL,NULL),
(70734,'biology','Which one of the following contains the largest quantity of extracellular material ? [AIPMT 2003]','Areolar tissue','In areolar tissue, there is more intercellular space, so largest quantity of extracellular material is present in this tissue. It contains all cell types and fibres of connective tissue. There is a thin layer of extracellular fluid in stratified epithelium whereas striated muscle is attached with tendons and there is very less amount of extracellular fluid in myelinated nerve fibre.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Striated muscle','Areolar tissue','Stratified epithelium','Myelinated nerve fibres','NEW','11-103',NULL,NULL),
(70735,'biology','Collagen is [AIPMT 2002]','Fibrous protein','Collagen is an insoluble fibrous protein found extensively in the connective tissue of skin, tendons and bone. Collagen accounts for over  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:104, paragraph no:2)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Fibrous protein','Globular protein','Lipid','Carbohydrate','NEW','11-104',NULL,NULL),
(70736,'biology','Melanin protects from [AIPMT 2002]','UV rays','Melanin is produced by specialized epidermal cells called melanophores (or melanocytes). Their dispersion in these cells is controlled by melanocyte stimulating hormone and melatonin. Melanin, a pigment present in skin, protects it from harmful effects of UV rays. People living in tropics have more melanin in their skin which is an adaptation to protect themselves from harmful UV rays. Melanin cannot protect from infrared rays and Xrays.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','UV rays','Visible rays','Infrared rays','X rays','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(70737,'biology','During an injury nasal septum gets damaged and for its recovery which cartilage is preferred? [AIPMT 2001]','Hyaline cartilage','Nasal septum consists of hyaline cartilage. It is bluishgreen and translucent in appearance. It has fewer very fine white fibres in the matrix. This type of cartilage gives flexibility and support at the joints. Elastic, calcified and fibrous cartilages occur in other parts of body.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','Elastic cartilage','Hyaline cartilage','Calcified cartilage','Fibrous cartilage','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(70738,'biology','Which cells do not form layer and remains structurally separate? [AIPMT 2001]','Nerve cells','Nerve cells are the highly excitable cells, specialized for impulse conduction. They originate from neural plate of embryonic ectoderm and serve as structural and functional units of nervous tissue.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:105, paragraph no:3)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Epithelial cells','Muscle cells','Nerve cells','Gland cells','NEW','11-105',NULL,NULL),
(70739,'biology','Proteoglycan in cartilages which is a part of polysaccharide is [AIPMT 2000]','Chondroitin','Proteoglycans consist of polysaccharide attached with a protein chondroitin. It is present in cartilage as well as in extracellular material. Ossein is a protein present in matrix of bone. Casein is a milk protein.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Chondroitin','Ossein','Casein','Cartilagin','NEW','11-104',NULL,NULL),
(70740,'biology','Characteristic of simple epithelium is that they [AIPMT 2000]','Make a definite layer','Simple epithelium consists of a single layer of cells resting on a basement membrane. This makes a definite layer. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:101, paragraph no:1)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Are arranged indiscriminately','Make a definite layer','Continue to divide and help in organ function','None of the above','NEW','11-101',NULL,NULL),
(70741,'biology','Which pair is correct? [AIPMT 2000]','Sweat – temperature regulation','Sweat is secreted by sweat glands of skin and helps in regulating body temperature. Saliva is secreted by salivary glands and helps in digestion (carbohydrate digestion). Sebum is the waxy secretion secreted by sebaceous glands. Sebum is a fatty mildly antiseptic material that protects, lubricates, and waterproofs the skin and hair and helps prevent desiccation. Humerus is the long bone of the upper arm. It articulates with the scapula at the glenoid cavity and with the ulna and radius at the elbow.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','Sweat – temperature regulation','Saliva – sense of food taste','Sebum – sexual attraction','Humerus – hindleg','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(70742,'biology','Primary function of enteronephric nephridia of pheretima is [AIPMT 2000]','Osmoregulation','Pharyngeal nephridia and septal nephridia are enteronephric as they discharge excretory matter into the gut. Discharge of waste matter via gut is an adaptation to conserve water by its reabsorption in the gut. Integumentary nephridra are exonephric, as they discharge waste matter to the exterior.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:109, paragraph no:1)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Osmoregulation','Excretion of nitrogenous wastes','Respiration','Locomotion','NEW','11-109',NULL,NULL),
(70743,'biology','Ligament is a/an [AIPMT 1999]','Modified yellow elastic fibrous tissue','Ligament occurs in the form of cords in a modified yellow elastic fibrous tissue and connects bone with a bone. Modified white fibrous tissue is present in the tendons. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:103, paragraph no:3)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Inelastic white fibrous tissue','Modified white fibrous tissue','Modified yellow elastic fibrous tissue','None of the above','NEW','11-103',NULL,NULL),
(350305,'biology','Snow leopards are not found in Kerala forests. Which factor is responsible for it?','Temperature','Snow leopards are not found in Kerala forests. Temperature factor is responsible for it.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:222, paragraph no:1)','Ecology >> Organisms And Populations >> Major Abiotic factors(Temperature  and  Water)',NULL,'2','mcq','Temperature','Soil','Water','Light','NEW','12-222',NULL,NULL),
(70744,'biology','Tendon is made up of [AIPMT 1999]','Modified white fibrous tissue','White fibrous tissue has two forms : cords and sheets. The white fibres run parallel to form cords, called tendons. Tendon attaches a muscle to a bone. It consists of collagen fibres and are therefore inelastic. They ensure that the force exerted by muscular contraction is transmitted to the relevant part of the body to be moved. Yellow elastic tissue also has two forms : cords and sheets. Here, cords are called ligaments. Adipose tissue is a fat storing loose connective tissue. Areolar tissue is the most widely distributed connective tissue in the body.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:103, paragraph no:3)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Yellow fibrous connective tissue','Modified white fibrous tissue','Areolar tissue','Adipose tissue','NEW','11-103',NULL,NULL),
(70745,'biology','In mammals, histamine is secreted by [AIPMT 1998]','Mast cells','Mast cells are found in the matrix of areolar connective tissue and secrete histamine (vasodilator), serotonin (vasoconstrictor) and heparin (anticoagulant). These take part in allergic reactions and also help in a body defence. Fibroblasts and histiocytes are also found in the matrix of areolar tissue. Fibroblasts secrete ground substance while histiocytes engulf the microbes, foreign particles and damaged cells. Lymphocytes are the type of leucocytes present in blood and secrete antibodies.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Lymphocytes','Mast cells','Fibroblasts','Histiocytes','NEW','11-103',NULL,NULL),
(70746,'biology','Protein present in cartilage is [AIPMT 1997]','Chondrin','Chondrin is a protein present in the matrix of cartilage. It forms a constituent of a compound called chondrin sulphate. Chondrin sulphate consists of proteoglycans, that is protein chains bonded to long chains of disaccharide hyaluronic acid. Matrix of bone is made up of a protein called ossein.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Cartilagin','Ossein','Chondrin','None of these','NEW','11-104',NULL,NULL),
(70747,'biology','Basement membrane is made up of [AIPMT 1997]','No cell product of epithelial cell','Basement membrane (basal lamina) is a thin sheet of fibrous proteins that underlies and supports the cells of an epithelium, separating this from underlying tissue. Basement membranes are components of the extracellular matrix (= the viscous watery fluid that surrounds cells in animal tissue) and help to regulate passage of materials between epithelial cells and adjacent blood vessels. Each consists of a framework of collagen fibrils within which are glycosaminoglycans (mucopolysacc harides) and laminins, which are proteins that bind the basement membrane to neighbouring cells via cell adhesion molecules.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','No cell product of epithelial cell','Epidermal cell only','Endodermal cell','Both b and c','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(70748,'biology','Stratum germinativum is an example of which kind of epithelium? [AIPMT 1997]','Columnar','Stratum germinativum (also stratum basale or basal cell layer) is the layer of keratinocytes that lies at the base of the epidermis immediately above the dermis. It consists of a single layer of tall, simple columnar epithelial cells lying on a basement membrane. These cells undergo rapid cell division, mitosis to replenish the regular loss of skin by shedding from the surface. About  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:101, paragraph no:1)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','Columnar','Squamous','Cuboidal','Ciliated','NEW','11-101',NULL,NULL),
(70749,'biology','The roof of the cranium of frog is formed by [AIPMT 1997]','Frontoparietal','Frontoparietals are a pair of long, broad, flattened and membranous bones. They are united along the middorsal line and form the whole roof of cranium. In larval frog, each frontoparietal occurs into separate frontal and parietal parts, but in adult frog, they become fused to form a single frontoparietal. The entire floor of cranium is covered and strengthened by a large parasphenoid bone.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Frontoparietal','Orbitosphenoid','Parasphenoid','Alisphenoid','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(70750,'biology','In frog, the surface of attachment of tongue is [AIPMT 1997]','Hyoid apparatus','In adult frog, gills disappear and their skeletal framework is also reduced to form hyoid apparatus. It lies below tongue in the floor of mouth and provides surface of attachment to the tongue. Pterygoid contributes to the posteroventral margin of orbit of its side. Palatine connects the anterior side of cranium with the middle of maxilla. Parasphenoid forms floor of the cranium. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:116, paragraph no:3)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Pterygoid','Hyoid apparatus','Parasphenoid','Palatine','NEW','11-116',NULL,NULL),
(70751,'biology','In frog, “fenestra ovalis” is [AIPMT 1997]','The air filled cavity of the middle ear','The bony partition between tympanic cavity (cavity of middle ear) and auditory capsule (internal ear) is perforated by a small windowlike oval aperture, the fenestra ovalis, which remains closed by a membrane and a cartilaginous nodule, the stapedial plate.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','The communication between the pharynx and the tympanic cavity','The external opening of the tympanic cavity which is covered by the tympanic membrane','The air filled cavity of the middle ear','The opening in the auditory capsule which separates the middle ear from the internal ear','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(70752,'biology','The kidney of an adult frog is [AIPMT 1997]','Mesonephros','Mesonephros kidney is present in both adult as well as embryo of frog. A mesonephros develops from the middle part of intermediate mesoderm, posterior to each pronephros soon after its degeneration.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Metanephros','Opisthonephros','Pronephros','Mesonephros','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(70753,'biology','An epithelial tissue which has thin flat cells, arranged edge to edge so as to appear like closely packed tiles, is found to be present at [AIPMT 1994]','Inner lining of cheeks','An epithelial tissue which has thin flat cells, arranged edge to edge so as to appear like closely packed tiles is known as pseudostratified epithelium. It covers moist surfaces where there is little wear and tear by friction such as inner lining of cheeks.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Outer surface of ovary','Inner lining of fallopian tube','Inner lining of stomach','Inner lining of cheeks','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(121321,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name of the compound in the given diagram(12123)','3-amino-5-heptenoic acid','Carbon of priority functional group is given first number and that is also included in the chain. (NEET 1995)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Previous years questions',NULL,'3','mcq','3-amino-5-heptenoic acid','β-amino-δ-heptenoic acid','5-amino-2-heptenoic acid','5-amino-hex-2-enecarboxylic acid','NEW','11-341','11-263','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/121321q.png'),
(70754,'biology','Hair present in the skin are [AIPMT 1993]','Epidermal in origin and made of dead cells','Each hair is present in a tubular pit called hair follicle which is made up by sinking of epidermis. Living cells are present only at the base of hair i.e. in hair papilla, rest of the hair is dead and is divisible into outer cuticle, middle cortex and inner medulla.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Epidermal in origin and made of dead cells','Epidermal in origin and made of living cells','Dermal in origin and made of living cells','Dermal in origin and made of dead cells','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(70755,'biology','The layer of actively dividing cells of skin is termed as [AIPMT 1993]','Stratum malpighii/stratum germinativum','Stratum malpighii/stratum germinativum is the innermost layer of the skin consisting of one celled thick columnar epithelial cells. It lies on the basement layer. Its cells are active and continuously produce new cells by mitotic division that is why called germinative layer.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','Stratum compactum','Stratum corneum','Stratum malpighii/stratum germinativum','Stratum lucidum','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(70756,'biology','Formation of cartilage bones involves [AIPMT 1993]','Deposition of bony matter by osteoblasts and resorption by chondroclasts','Bone is an unusual tissue in that it is continually being reconstructed. The osteoblasts secrete bone matrix, whereas the large, much branched, motile, lysosomerich, multinucleate cells, called osteoclasts, destroy bone matrix. The twin process of resorption and resconstruction enables a particular bone to remodel its structure to meet any change in the mechanical requirements of the animal during its development.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:104, paragraph no:2)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Deposition of bony matter by osteoblasts and resorption by chondroclasts','Deposition of bony matter by osteoclasts','Deposition of bony matter by osteoclasts only','Deposition of bony matter by osteoblasts only','NEW','11-104',NULL,NULL),
(70757,'biology','Mucus helps frog in forming [AIPMT 1993]','Moist skin','Mucus helps frog in forming moist skin as skin is its respiratory organ.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:116, paragraph no:2)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','Thick skin','Dry skin','Smooth skin','Moist skin','NEW','11-116',NULL,NULL),
(70758,'biology','Characteristics of smooth muscle fibres are [AIPMT 1992]','Spindleshaped, unbranched, nonstriated, uninucleate and involuntary','The smooth muscle consists of long, narrow unbranched spindleshaped fibres. Each fibre contains a single oval nucleus in its thick middle part. The crossstriations are absent so that the fibres look smooth, hence the name nonstriated. Its contraction is not under the control of the animal, therefore, also called involuntary muscle (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:105, paragraph no:1)...','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Spindleshaped, unbranched, nonstriated, uninucleate and involuntary','Spindleshaped, unbranched, unstriped, multinucleate and involuntary','Cylindrical, unbranched, unstriped, multinucleate and involuntary','Cylindrical, unbranched, striated, multinucleate and voluntary','NEW','11-105',NULL,NULL),
(70759,'biology','Male and female cockroaches can be distinguished externally through [AIPMT 1991]','Anal styles in male','The abdomen in both males and females consists of 10 segments. In females, the 7th sternum is boat shaped and together with the 8th and 9th sterna forms a brood or genital pouch whose anterior part contains female gonopore, spermathecal pores and collateral glands. In males, genital pouch or chamber lies at the hind end of abdomen bounded dorsally by 9th and 10th terga and ventrally by the 9th sternum. It contains dorsal anus, ventral male genital pore and gonapophysis. Males bear a pair of short, thread- like anal styles which are absent in females. In both sexes, the 10th segment bears a pair of jointed filamentous structures called anal cerci.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:112, paragraph no:2)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Anal styles in male','Anal cerci in female','Anal style and antennae in females','Both b and c','NEW','11-112',NULL,NULL),
(70760,'biology','Earthworm possesses hearts [AIPMT 1991]','4 pairs','If you look at the diagram given below, you will see that 2 pairs of lateral hearts and lateral oesophageal hearts have been marked, making it a total of 4 pairs of hearts, (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:109, fig 7.11). (0720) Lateral hearts and lateral esophageal hearts is marked by (d).','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','6 pairs','4 pairs','2 pairs','1 pair','NEW','11-109',NULL,NULL),
(70761,'biology','Blood of pheretima is [AIPMT 1990]','Red with haemoglobin in plasma','Circulatory or blood vascular system of earthworm is a closed system consisting of blood vessels and capillaries which ramify to all parts of the body. Blood is composed of a fluid plasma and colourless corpuscles, physiologically comparable to the leucocytes of the vertebrates. The red respiratory pigment, haemoglobin (or erythrocruorin) occurs dissolved in plasma. It gives a red colour to blood and aids in the transportation of O₂ for respiration.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:108, paragraph no:2)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Blue with haemocyanin in corpuscles','Blue with haemocyanin in plasma','Red with haemoglobin in corpuscles','Red with haemoglobin in plasma','NEW','11-108',NULL,NULL),
(70762,'biology','Pheretima posthuma is highly useful as [AIPMT 1990]','They make the soil porous, leave their castings and take organic debris in the soil','Pheretima posthuma is highly useful and beneficial in agriculture. Its habit of burrowing and swallowing earth makes it porous and increases the soil fertility in many ways. Their burrows permit penetration of air and moisture in porous soil and their excretory wastes and other secretions also enrich soil by adding nitrogenous matters to the soil. Pheretima posthuma is not used as fish meal. Whereas a small white earthworm (Enchytraeus albidus) is often grown in soil and used to feed mcquarium fish.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:111 paragraph no:1)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Their burrows make the soil loose','They make the soil porous, leave their castings and take organic debris in the soil','They are used as fish meal','They kill the birds due to biomagnification of chlorinated hydrocarbons','NEW','11-111',NULL,NULL),
(70763,'biology','Haversian canals occur in [AIPMT 1989]','Humerus','Small bones are solid. Long bones, such as the humerus and femur, have a cavity, the marrow cavity, at the centre. The substance of the bone is distinguishable into','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Humerus','Pubis','Scapula','Clavicle','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(70764,'biology','Histamine secreting cells are found in [AIPMT 1989]','Connective tissues','Blood contains Blood components which includes cells that secrete Histamine, like mast cells and eosinophils, Blood is a type of specialised connective tissue','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Connective tissues','Lungs','Muscular tissue','Nervous tissue','NEW','11-103',NULL,NULL),
(70765,'biology','Mineral found in red pigment of vertebrate blood is [AIPMT 1989]','Iron','Red pigment of vertebrate blood is haemoglobin. Haemoglobin is a conjugated protein. It consists of a basic protein globin joined to a nonprotein group heme, hence the name haemoglobin. Heme is an ironporphyrin ring. A mammalian haemoglobin molecule is a complex of  iron.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Magnesium','Iron','Calcium','Copper','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(70766,'biology','Photoreceptors of earthworm occur on [AIPMT 1989]','Dorsal surface','Photoreceptors restricted only to dorsal surface, are more numerous on prostomium and peristomium of earthworm and gradually reduce in number towards posterior end of body. They are totally absent in clitellum. Each photoreceptor consists of a single ovoid cell, with a nucleus and clear cytoplasm containing a network of neurofibrillae and a small transparent Lshaped lens or optic organelle or phaosome, made up of a hyaline substance. Photoreceptors enable worms to judge the intensity and duration of light.  (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:110, paragraph no:1)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Clitellum','Many eyes','Dorsal surface','Lateral sides','NEW','11-110',NULL,NULL),
(70767,'biology','Which of the following characteristics is incorrect with respect to cockroach?[NEET 2021]','A ring of gastric caeca is present at the junction of midgut and hind gut','The entire foregut is lined by cuticle. A ring of 6-8 blind tubules called hepatic or gastric caeca is present at the junction of foregut and midgut, which secrete digestive juice. At the junction of midgut and hindgut is present another ring of 100-150 yellow coloured thin filamentous Malpighian tubules. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Chapter 7 page no:113, paragraph no.1','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','10th abdominal segment in both sexes, bears a pair of anal cerci','A ring of gastric caeca is present at the junction of midgut and hind gut','Hypopharynx lies within the cavity enclosed by the mouth parts','In females, 7th-9th sterna together form a genital pouch','NEW','11-113',NULL,NULL),
(70768,'biology','Identify the types of cell junctions that help to stop the leakage of the substances across a tissue and facilitation of communication with neighbouring cells via rapid transfer of ions and molecules [NEET 2021]','Tight junctions and Gap junctions, respectively','Tight junctions help to stop substances from leaking across a tissue. Adhering junctions perform cementing to keep neighbouring cells together. Gap junctions facilitate the cells to communicate with each other by connecting the cytoplasm of adjoining cells, for rapid transfer of ions, small molecules and sometimes big molecules.(Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11;Chapter 7; page no:102, paragraph no:3)..','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Adhering junctions and Gap junctions, respectively','Gap junctions and Adhering junctions, respectively','Tight junctions and Gap junctions, respectively','Adhering junctions and Tight junctions, respectively.','NEW','11-102',NULL,NULL),
(70769,'biology','Following are the statements about prostomium of earthworm.  [NEET 2021]\n\n(a) It serves as a covering for mouth. \n\n(b) It helps to open cracks in the soil into which it can crawl. \n\n(c) It is one of the sensory structures. \n\n(d) It is the first body segment Choose the correct answer from the options given below','(a), (b) and (c) are correct','Anterior end consists of the mouth and the prostomium, a lobe which serves as a covering for the mouth and as a wedge to force open cracks in the soil into which the earthworm may crawl. The prostomium is sensory in function. The first body segment is called the peristomium (buccal segment) which contains the mouth.\nReference   NCERT Chapter 7, Page 106, Last Paragraph','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','(b) and (c) are correct','(a), (b) and (c) are correct','(a), (b) and (d) are correct','(a), (b), (c) and (d) are correct','NEW','11-106',NULL,NULL),
(70770,'biology','Exoskeleton of arthropods is composed of :[NEET 2022]','Chitin','Exoskeleton of Arthropods are made up of chitin,The body of arthropods is covered by chitinous exoskeleton.\nReference   : NCERT Class 1 Chapter 4, Page 53, 1st Paragraph','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','Cutin','Cellulose','Chitin','Glucosamine','NEW','11-53',NULL,NULL),
(70771,'biology','Match List-I with List-II\n[NEET 2022]','Bronchioles-Ciliated epithelium,Goblet Cell-Glandular Tissue,Tendons-Dense Regular Connective tissue,Adipose Tissue-Loose Connective tissue','Bronchioles-Ciliated epithelium,\nGoblet Cell-Glandular Tissue,\nTendons-Dense Regular Connective tissue,\nAdipose Tissue-Loose Connective tissue\nReference   NCERT Class 11, Chapter 7, Pages 101-103;','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','match','Bronchioles,Ciliated epithelium','Goblet Cell,Glandular Tissue','Tendons,Dense Regular Connective tissue','Adipose Tissue,Loose Connective tissue','NEW','11-103',NULL,NULL),
(70772,'biology','Given below are two statements : \n Statement I :\n In cockroach, the forewings are transparent and \nprothoracic in origin. \nStatement II :\n In cockroach, the hind wings are opaque, leathery \nand mesothoracic in origin. \n In the light of the above statements, choose the \ncorrect answer from the options given below : [ NEET 2023(Phase 2)]','(4) Both Statement I and Statement II are false','Two pairs of wings are present, of which one pair is attached to the mesothoracic and the other pair to the metathoracic segments. Both pairs of the wings together cover the entire body segments starting from mesothorax. The fore wings are mesothoracic and are called wing covers or tegmina or elytra. They cover the hindwings and are protective in function. These are dark stiff opaque and leathery. The hind wings are large, thin, membranous and transparent. They are kept folded below the tegmina and are used for flying.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','(4) Both Statement I and Statement II are false','(1) Statement I is correct but Statement II is \nfalse','(2) Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is \ntrue','(3) Both Statement I and Statement II are true','NEW','11-112',NULL,NULL),
(70773,'biology','In cockroach, excretion is brought about by-\nA. Phallic gland\nB. Uricose gland\nC. Nephrocytes\nD. Fat body\nE. Collaterial glands [ NEET 2023]','(2) B, C and D only','Fat body, Urecose glands and Nephrocytes helps in excretion in cockroach.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','(1) A, B and E only','(2) B, C and D only','(3) B and D only','(4) A and E only','NEW','11-114',NULL,NULL),
(70774,'biology','Which of the following is characteristic feature of cockroach regarding sexual dimorphism? [ NEET 2023]','(1) Presence of anal styles','Cockroach males have a pair of short, thread-like anal styles that females do not have.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','(1) Presence of anal styles','(2) Presence of sclerites','(3) Presence of anal cerci','(4) Dark brown body colour and anal cerci','NEW','11-112',NULL,NULL),
(70775,'biology','Given below are two statements:\nStatement I: Ligaments are dense irregular tissue.\nStatement II: Cartilage is dense regular tissue.\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below: [ NEET 2023]','(1) Both Statement I and Statement II are false','Statement I is false - Ligaments are not dense irregular tissue. Ligaments are dense regular connective tissue that connects bone to bone and provides strength and stability to joints.\nStatement II is false - Cartilage is not dense regular tissue. Cartilage is a type of connective tissue that is more flexible than bone and provides structural support to various body parts.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','(1) Both Statement I and Statement II are false','(2) Statement I is true but Statement II is false','(3) Statement I is false but Statement II is true','(4) Both Statement I and Statement II are true','NEW','11-103',NULL,NULL),
(70776,'biology','Match List I with List II.\nA. Mast cells - I. Ciliated epithelium\nB. Inner surface of bronchiole -II. Areolar connective tissue\nC. Blood - III. Cuboidal epithelium\nD. Tubular parts of nephron - IV. Specialised connective tissue\nChoose the correct answer from the options give below: [ NEET 2023]','(2) A-II, B-I, C-IV, D-III','A-II, B-I, C-IV, D-III','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','(1) A-II, B-III, C-I, D-IV','(2) A-II, B-I, C-IV, D-III','(3) A-III, B-IV, C-II, D-I','(4) A-I, B-II, C-IV, D-III','NEW','11-103',NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/70776q.png'),
(70779,'biology','Which cartilage is present on the end of long bones:','2. Hyaline cartilage','Class 11 pg 104','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','1. Calcified cartilage','2. Hyaline cartilage','3. Elastic cartilage','4. Fibrous cartilage','NEW','11-104',NULL,NULL),
(70777,'biology','Choose the correct statements : \n (a) Bones support and protect softer tissues and organs \n (b) Weight bearing function is served by limb bones \n (c) Ligament is the site of production of blood cells. \n (d) Adipose tissue is specialised to store fats. \n (e) Tendons attach one bone to another. \n Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below : [ RE NEET 2022]','(1) (a), (b) and (d) only','Bones are the hardest tissue of our body that support and protect softer tissues and organs.\n\n Limb bones serve weight bearing function.\n\n Adipose tissue is a type of loose connective tissue specialised to store fats.\n\n Option (a) is incorrect because statement (e) is false as tendons attach bones to muscles.\n\n Option (c) is incorrect because statement (c) is false as bone marrow in some bones is the site of production of blood cells.\n\n Option (d) is incorrect because this option includes statement (c) which is false.','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','(1) (a), (b) and (d) only','(2) (b), (c) and (e) only','(3) (a), (c) and (d) only','(4) (a), (b) and (e) only','NEW','11-104',NULL,NULL),
(70778,'biology','Match List-I with List-II. \n List-I List-II \n (A) Columnar epithelium (I) Ducts of glands\n (B) Ciliated epithelium (II) Inner lining of \n stomach and \nintestine \n (C) Squamous epithelium (III) Inner lining of \n bronchioles \n (D) Cuboidal epithelium (IV) Endothelium \n Choose the correct answer from the options given \nbelow : [ NEET 2023(Phase 2)]','(A)-(II), (B)-(III), (C)-(IV), (D)-(I)','(A)-(II), (B)-(III), (C)-(IV), (D)-(I)','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','(A)-(III), (B)-(II), (C)-(I), (D)-(IV)','(A)-(III), (B)-(II), (C)-(IV), (D)-(I)','(A)-(II), (B)-(III), (C)-(I), (D)-(IV)','(A)-(II), (B)-(III), (C)-(IV), (D)-(I)','NEW','11-101',NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/70778q.png'),
(70780,'biology','Identify the tissue shown in the diagram(70780Q) and match with its characteristics and its location:','Skeletal muscle, shows striations and is closely attached to the bones of the limbs','Class 11 pg 104','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Smooth muscles, show branching, found in the walls of the heart','Cardiac muscles, unbranched 2. muscles, found in the walls of the heart','Striated muscles, tapering at 3. both ends attached to the bones of the ribs','Skeletal muscle, shows striations and is closely attached to the bones of the limbs','NEW','11-104',NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/70780q.png'),
