(71036,'biology','Assertion: Alimentary canal of frog is short\nReason: Because frogs are carnivores','If both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.','The alimentary canal is short because frogs are carnivores and hence the length of intestine is reduced','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Structural Organisation In Animals >> Indepth questions (syllabus reduction)',NULL,'1','mcq','If both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.','If both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.','If Assertion is true but Reason is false','If both Assertion and Reason are false','NEW','11-116','11-81',NULL),
(270102,'chemistry','Amines constitute an important class of organic compounds derived by replacing one or more hydrogen atoms of ___________ molecule by alkyl/aryl group(s).','ammonia','Amines constitute an important class of organic compounds derived by replacing one or more hydrogen atoms of ammonia molecule by alkyl/aryl group(s).\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No.389; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','aniline','ammonia','amide','anhydride','NEW','12-389','12-259',NULL),
(270103,'chemistry','What is the chief commercial use of amines?','Intermediates in the synthesis of medicines and fibres','Amines are widly used as intermediates in the synthesis of medicines and fibres.\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No.389; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Amines',NULL,'2','mcq','Proteins and vitamins','Intermediates in the synthesis of medicines and fibres','Alkaloids\nand hormones','Polymers,\ndye stuffs and drugs','NEW','12-389','12-259',NULL),
(270104,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement respectively: \nAdrenaline and epinephrine both containing _______ amino group, are used to _______ blood pressure.','secondary, increase','Two biologically active compounds, namely adrenaline and epinephrine, both containing secondary amino group, are used to increase blood pressure.\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No.389; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Amines',NULL,'2','mcq','primary, increases','tertiary, decrease','secondary, increase','quaternary, decrease','NEW','12-389','12-259',NULL),
(270105,'chemistry','Which one of the following is used as anaesthetic in dentistry?','Novocain','Novocain, a synthetic amino compound, is used as an anaesthetic in dentistry.\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No.389; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Amines',NULL,'2','mcq','Novocain','Naloxone','Both a and d','Streptomycin','NEW','12-389','12-259',NULL),
(270106,'chemistry','Which of the following is/are antihistaminic drugs?','All of these','Synthetic drugs, brompheniramine (Dimetapp) and terfenadine (Seldane), act as antihistamines. Benadryl, a well known antihistaminic drug, also contains tertiary amino group. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No.389; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','Benadryl','Brompheniramine','Terfenadine','All of these','NEW','12-389','12-259',NULL),
(270107,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for the given statement:     ________ammonium salts are used as surfactants.','Quaternary','Quaternary ammonium salts are used as surfactants.\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No.389; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','Primary','Secondary','Tertiary','Quaternary','NEW','12-389','12-259',NULL),
(270108,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion (A) and reason (R):                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Assertion (A): Nitrogen atom in amines possesses sp³ hybirdisation and therefore has pyramidal geometry.                                                                                                                                                                                                         Reason(R): Nitrogen atom of amines is trivalent and carries an unshared pair of electrons.','Both the assertion and reason are correct.','Nitrogen atom of amines is trivalent and carries an unshared pair of electrons. Nitrogen orbitals in amines are therefore, sp³ hybridised and the geometry of amines is pyramidal. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No.389; Paragraph No. 3)\ndiagram(ne27119)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Structure of amines',NULL,'3','mcq','Both the assertion and reason are correct.','Assertion is correct and reason is wrong.','Assertion is wrong and reason is correct.','Both assertion and reason is wrong.','NEW','12-389','12-259',NULL),
(270109,'chemistry','What is the geometry of amines?','Pyramidal','Nitrogen orbitals in amines are sp³ hybridised and the geometry of amines is pyramidal.\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No.389; Paragraph No. 3)\ndiagram(ne27119)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Structure of amines',NULL,'3','mcq','Pyramidal','Tetrahedral','Trigonal bipyramidal','Square planar','NEW','12-389','12-259',NULL),
(270110,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         The _________ orbital of nitrogen in all amines contains an unshared pair of electrons.','fourth','The fourth orbital of nitrogen in all amines contains an unshared pair of electrons. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No.389; Paragraph No. 3)\ndiagram(ne27119)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Structure of amines',NULL,'1','mcq','first','second','third','fourth','NEW','12-389','12-259',NULL),
(270111,'chemistry','The chief commercial use of amine is :\na. intermediate in medicine synthesis\nb. constituent of medicines\nc. intermediates in fiber synthesis','a,c','The chief commercial use of amines is as intermediates in the synthesis of medicines and fibers\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 389; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','a,b','b,c','a,c','c only','NEW','12-389','12-259',NULL),
(270112,'chemistry','In nature, the amines occur in all except:\na. proteins\nb. vitamins\nc. alkaloids\nd. glycosides','d only','In nature, amines occur among proteins, vitamins, alkaloids and hormones.\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 389; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','a,b','a,b,d','b,c,d','d only','NEW','12-389','12-259',NULL),
(270201,'chemistry','Match the following amines according to diagram(n2701).','(A)-(iii), (B)-(iv), (C)-(i), (D)-(ii)','Primary amines are the ones in which one hydrogen in ammonia is replaced by alkyl or aryl group. \nIn secondary amines two hydrogens in ammonia get replaced by alkyl or aryl groups. \nIn tertiary amines three hydrogens in ammonia get replaced by alkyl or aryl groups. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No.390; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Classification of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','(A)-(iii), (B)-(iv), (C)-(i), (D)-(ii)','(A)-(i), (B)-(iv), (C)-(ii), (D)-(iii)','(A)-(iii), (B)-(iv), (C)-(ii), (D)-(i)','(A)-(ii), (B)-(iv), (C)-(i), (D)-(iii)','NEW','12-390','12-260','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270201q.png'),
(270202,'chemistry','Match the following  diagram(n2702).','(A)-(iv), (B)-(iii), (C)-(ii), (D)-(i)','Ethylmethylamine is a common name of compound (A). Common names of the compounds (B), (C), and (D) are allylamine, hexamethylendiamine, and trimethylamine respectively. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No.391; Table 13.1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Amines Nomenclature',NULL,'3','mcq','(A)-(iv), (B)-(iii), (C)-(ii), (D)-(i)','(A)-(iv), (B)-(i), (C)-(iii), (D)-(ii)','(A)-(iv), (B)-(ii), (C)-(iii), (D)-(i)','(A)-(iv), (B)-(iii), (C)-(i), (D)-(ii)','NEW','12-391','12-261','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270202q.png'),
(270203,'chemistry','Match the following  diagram(n2703).','(A)-(iv), (B)-(iii), (C)-(ii), (D)-(i)','N-Methylethanamine is the IUPAC name of compound (A).\nThe IUPAC names of the compounds (B), (C), and (D) are prop-2-en-1-amine, hexane-1,6-diamine, and N,N-dimethylmethanamine respectively.\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 391; Table 13.1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Amines Nomenclature',NULL,'3','mcq','(A)-(iv), (B)-(iii), (C)-(ii), (D)-(i)','(A)-(iv), (B)-(i), (C)-(iii), (D)-(ii)','(A)-(iv), (B)-(ii), (C)-(iii), (D)-(i)','(A)-(iv), (B)-(iii), (C)-(i), (D)-(ii)','NEW','12-391','12-261','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270203q.png'),
