(271423,'biology','How is thalassemia transmitted from parents to offspring','When both the partners/parents are unaffected carrier for the gene','Thalassemia  is also an autosome-linked recessive blood disease transmitted from parents to the offspring when both the partners are unaffected carrier for the gene (or heterozygous). Reference   :NCERT PAGE 91','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Thalassemia and Chromosomal Disorders',NULL,'2','mcq','When a mother is a carrier and father is Thalassemic','When both parents/partner are affected with Thalassemia','When both the partners/parents are unaffected carrier for the gene','When both the partners are unaffected homozgous for the gene','NEW','12-091','12-075',NULL),
(271424,'biology','Thalassemia is caused due to?','Reduced rate of synthesis of one of the globin chains (α and β chains) of haemoglobin','The defect could be due to either mutation or deletion which ultimately results in reduced rate of synthesis of one of the globin chains (α and β chains) that make up haemoglobin. This causes the formation of abnormal haemoglobin molecules. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 91','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Thalassemia and Chromosomal Disorders',NULL,'3','mcq','Variation in haemoglobin molecule','Reduced rate of synthesis of one of the globin chains (α and β chains) of haemoglobin','Linkage in globin gene chain','Reduce synthesis of haemoglobin','NEW','12-091','12-075',NULL),
