(270302,'chemistry','Classify the following amine diagram(n2716).','Tertiary','If three hydrogen atoms of ammonia or two hydrogen atom of R-NH₂ are replaced by another alkyl/aryl (R’) group, it will give tertiary amine.\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 390; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Classification of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','Primary','Secondary','Tertiary','Quaternary','NEW','12-390','12-260','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270302q.png'),
