(270406,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion (A) and reason (R):                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 Assertion Assertion (A): Reduction with iron scrap and hydrochloric acid is preferred for reduction of nitro compounds to form amines.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                Reason (R): Large amount of hydrochloric acid is required to initiate the reaction.','Assertion is correct and reason is wrong','Reduction with iron scrap and hydrochloric acid is preferred because FeCl₂ formed gets hydrolysed to release hydrochloric acid during the reaction. Thus, only a small amount of hydrochloric acid is required to initiate the reaction. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 392; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','Both assertion and reason are correct','Both assertion and reason are wrong','Reason is correct and assertion is wrong','Assertion is correct and reason is wrong','NEW','12-392','12-262',NULL),
(270407,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             Ammonolysis of alkyl halide is','Substitution reaction','An alkyl or benzyl halide on reaction with an ethanolic solution of ammonia undergoes nucleophilic substitution reaction in which the halogen atom is replaced by an amino group. \nThis process of cleavage of the C–X bond by ammonia molecule is known as ammonolysis. \nReference: NCERT class-12; Page No. 392; Paragraph No. 3)\ndiagram(ne27118)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','Elimination reaction','Substitution reaction','Addition reaction','Elimination reaction','NEW','12-392','12-262',NULL),
(270408,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     Condition for ammonolysis of alkyl halide','Sealed tube at 373K','Ammonolysis reaction is carried out in a sealed tube at 373 K. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 392; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','Open tube at 373K','Sealed tube at 373K','Sealed tube at 273K','Open tube at 273K','NEW','12-392','12-262',NULL),
(270409,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion (A) and reason (R):                                                                                                                                                                                                                                Assertion Assertion (A): Ammonolysis has the disadvantage of yielding a mixture of primary, secondary and tertiary amines and also a quaternary ammonium salt.                                                                                                                                                                                                                               Reason (R): The reaction is carried out in an open tube at 373 K.','assertion is correct and reason is wrong','Ammonolysis has the disadvantage of yielding a mixture of primary, secondary and tertiary amines and also a quaternary ammonium salt. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 392; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','assertion is correct and reason is wrong','assertion and reason both are correct','assertion is wrong and reason is wrong','assertion and reason are wrong','NEW','12-392','12-262',NULL),
(270410,'chemistry','Which amine is formed as major product on ammonolysis of alkyl halides with excess ammonia?','Primary amine','Primary amine is obtained as a major product by taking large excess of ammonia in ammonolysis. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 392; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','Primary amine','Secondary amine','Tertiary amine','Quaternary amine','NEW','12-392','12-262',NULL),
(270411,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        Primary amine obtained by ammonolysis of alkyl halide behaves as __________ for further procedure of reaction.','nucleophile','The primary amine obtained by ammonolysis of alkyl halide behaves as a nucleophile and further react with alkyl halide till quaternary salt as that is the point when it gets devoid of electrons for donation. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 392; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','electrophile','nucleophile','acid','base','NEW','12-392','12-262',NULL),
(270412,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               An alkyl or benzyl halide on reaction with an ethanolic solution of ammonia undergoes nucleophilic substitution reaction in which the halogen atom is replaced by an amino group. This process is known as ________.','ammonolysis','An alkyl or benzyl halide on reaction with an ethanolic solution of ammonia undergoes nucleophilic substitution reaction in which the halogen atom is replaced by an amino group.This process of cleavage of the C–X bond by ammonia molecule is known as ammonolysis. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 392; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','nitrification','ammonification','ammonolysis','denitrification','NEW','12-392','12-262',NULL),
(270413,'chemistry','Complete the following reaction diagram(n2728).','R-NH₃⁺-X⁻','The primary amine obtained by nucleophilic substitution of halogen in alkyl halide by ammonolysis, behaves as a nucleophile and can further react with alkyl halide to form secondary and tertiary amines, and finally quaternary ammonium salt. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 392 ; Paragraph No. 3). diagram(ne2730)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','R-NH₃⁺-X⁻','R₂NH','R₃N','RNH₂','NEW','12-392','12-262','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270413q.png'),
(2000044893,'physics','The $L - C$ parallel resonant circuit','A','In case of parallel resonance $L - C$ circuit the capacitive and inductive reactance equal to each other, the total impedance of the circuit increase to infinity meaning the circuit draws no current from the $AC$ power source','Alternating Voltage Across Different Elements','Alternating Current','Easy',NULL,'Has a very high impedance','Has a very high current','Acts as resistance of very low value','Has zero impedance',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(270414,'chemistry','Complete the following reaction diagram(n2738).','(C₂H₅)₃-N⁺Cl⁻','The primary amine obtained by nucleophilic substitution of halogen in alkyl halide by ammonolysis, behaves as a nucleophile and can further react with alkyl halide to form secondary and tertiary amines, and finally quaternary ammonium salt.\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 392; Paragraph No. 3). diagram(ne2739)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','C₂H₅-NH₂','(C₂H₅)₃-N','(C₂H₅)₃-N⁺Cl⁻','(C₂H₅)₂-NH','NEW','12-392','12-262','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270414q.png'),
(270415,'chemistry','Complete the following reaction diagram(n2740).','a = C₆H₅-CH₂NH₂ and b = C₂H₅-CH₂-N-(CH₃)₂','The primary amine obtained by nucleophilic substitution of halogen in alkyl halide by ammonolysis, behaves as a nucleophile and can further react with alkyl halide to form secondary and tertiary amines, and finally quaternary ammonium salt. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No.392; Paragraph No.3). diagram(ne2743)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','a = C₆H₅-CH₂NH₂ and b = C₂H₅-CH₂-N-(CH₃)₂','a = C₂H₅-NH₂ and b = (C₂H5)₃-N','a = (C₂H₅)₃-N+Cl- and b = R₃N','a = C₂H₅-NH₂ and b = (C₂H₅)₂-NH','NEW','12-392','12-262','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270415q.png'),
(270416,'chemistry','Free amine can be prepared from ammonium salt----------','by treatment with strong base.','The free amine can be obtained from the ammonium salt by treatment with a strong base. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 393; Paragraph No.1). diagram(ne2727)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','by treatment with strong acid.','by treatment with strong base.','by treatment with week base.','by treatment with week acid.','NEW','12-393','12-263',NULL),
(270417,'chemistry','Choose the correct order of reactivity of halides with amine.','RI > RBr >RCl','The order of reactivity of halides with amines is RI > RBr > RCl. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 393; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','RI > RBr >RCl','RI < RBr >RCl','RI > RBr < RCl','RI < RBr < RCl','NEW','12-393','12-263',NULL),
(270418,'chemistry','Which of the following amine is formed on ammonolysis of alkyl halide?','All of these','Ammonolysis has the disadvantage of yielding a mixture of primary, secondary and tertiary amines and also a quaternary ammonium salt. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 393; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','Primary and secondary','Tertiary and quaternary','None of these','All of these','NEW','12-393','12-263',NULL),
(270419,'chemistry','Complete the following reaction diagram(n2744).','RCH₂NH₂','Nitriles on reduction with lithium aluminium hydride or catalytic hydrogenation produce primary amines. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 393; Paragraph No. 4). diagram(ne2745)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','RCH₂NH₂','C₆H₅-CH₂NH₂','(C₂H₅)₃-N⁺Cl⁻','C₂H₅-NH₂','NEW','12-393','12-263','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270419q.png'),
(270420,'chemistry','Choose suitable reagent for the following conversion. diagram(n2751).','Both of these','Nitriles on reduction with lithium aluminium hydride or catalytic hydrogenation produce primary amines. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 393; Paragraph No. 4). diagram(ne2745)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','H₂/Ni, Na(Hg)/C₂H₅OH','(i)-LiAlH₄ and (ii) -H₂0','Both of these','None of these','NEW','12-393','12-263','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270420q.png'),
(270421,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      Reduction of nitriles reaction is used for ________ of amine series.','ascent','Nitriles on reduction with lithium aluminium hydride or catalytic hydrogenation produce primary amines. This reaction is used for ascent of amine series, i.e., for preparation of amines containing one carbon atom more than the starting amine. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 393; Paragraph No.4)\ndiagram(ne2745)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','ascent','descent','same','none','NEW','12-393','12-263',NULL),
(270422,'chemistry','Select the suitable reagent for the following conversion diagram(n2752).','(i) LiAlH₄ and (ii) H₂0','The amides on reduction with lithium aluminium hydride yield amines. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 393; Paragraph No. 5). \ndiagram(ne2749)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','H₂/Ni, Na(Hg)/C₂H₅OH','(i) LiAlH₄ and (ii) H₂0','Both of these','None of these','NEW','12-393','12-263','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270422q.png'),
(270423,'chemistry','Complete the following reaction diagram(n2747).','RCH₂NH₂','The amides on reduction with lithium aluminium hydride yield amines. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 393; Paragraph No. 5) \ndiagram(ne2749)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','RCH₂NH₂','C₆H₅-CH₂NH₂','(C₂H₅)₃-N⁺Cl⁻','C₂H₅-NH₂','NEW','12-393','12-263','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270423q.png'),
(270424,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         Gabriel synthesis is used for the preparation of ________ amines.','primary','Gabriel synthesis is used for the preparation of primary amines. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 394; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','primary','secondary amine','tertiary','quaternary','NEW','12-394','12-264',NULL),
(270425,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion (A) and reason (R):                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 Assertion Assertion (A): Aromatic primary amines can be prepared by gabriel phthalimide synthesis.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                Reason (R): Aryl halides undergo nucleophilic substitution with the anion formed by phthalimide.','Both assertion and reason are wrong','Aromatic primary amines cannot be prepared by this method because aryl halides do not undergo nucleophilic substitution with the anion formed by phthalimide. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 394; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','Assertion is correct and reason is wrong','assertion and reason both are correct','Both assertion and reason are wrong','Assertion is wrong and reason is correct','NEW','12-394','12-264',NULL),
(270426,'chemistry','Choose the correct statement:','Phthalimide on treatment with ethanolic potassium hydroxide forms potassium salt of phthalimide which on heating with alkyl halide followed by alkaline hydrolysis produces the corresponding primary amine.','Phthalimide on treatment with ethanolic potassium hydroxide forms potassium salt of phthalimide which on heating with alkyl halide followed by alkaline hydrolysis produces the corresponding primary amine. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 394; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'2','mcq','Phthalimide on treatment with alkaline potassium hydroxide forms salt of phthalimide.','Phthalimide on treatment with ethanolic potassium hydroxide forms potassium salt of phthalimide which on heating with alkyl halide followed by alkaline hydrolysis produces the corresponding primary amine.','Phthalimide on treatment with alkaline potassium hydroxide forms\nsodium salt of phthalimide.','Phthalimide on treatment with ethanolic potassium hydroxide forms\npotassium salt of phthalimide.','NEW','12-394','12-264',NULL),
(270427,'chemistry','Choose the correct name of the following structure diagram(n2753).','Phthalimide','The given compound is commonly known as phthalimide. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 394; Paragraph No. 1)\ndiagram(ne2754)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','Phthalimide','Pthalimide','Pthalimine','Phthalimine','NEW','12-394','12-264','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270427q.png'),
(270428,'chemistry','Complete the reaction diagram(n2757).','a = Ar(CO)₂N⁻K⁺ and b = Ar(CO)₂NR','It is a well known reaction named as Gabriel synthesis of pthalimide. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 394; Paragraph No. 1)\ndiagram(ne2758)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','a = Ar(CO)₂N⁻K⁺ and b = Ar(CO)₂NR','a=Ar(CO)₂N⁻K⁺&b=Ar(CO)₂N⁻K⁺','a = Ar(CO)₂NR and b = Ar(CO)₂N⁻K⁺','a = Ar(CO)₂NR and b = Ar(CO)₂NR','NEW','12-394','12-264','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270428q.png'),
(270429,'chemistry','Balance the givem equation diagram(n2759).','a = 1, b = 1, c = 4, d = 1, e = 1, f = 2, g = 2','Hoffmann synthesis of primary amine by the reaction of amide and bromine in the presence of NaOH. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 394; Paragraph No. 2)\ndiagram(ne2760)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','a = 1, b = 2, c = 4, d = 1, e = 1, f = 2, g = 2','a = 1, b = 1, c = 4, d = 1, e = 1, f = 2, g = 2','a = 1, b = 1, c = 4, d = 1, e = 1, f = 4, g = 2','a = 1, b = 1, c = 4, d = 1, e = 1, f = 2, g = 4','NEW','12-394','12-264','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270429q.png'),
(270430,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            The amine formed by hoffman bromamide reaction contains _____ carbon _____ than that present in the amide.','one, less','The amine formed by Hoffman bromamide contains one carbon less than that present in the amide. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 394; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','one, less','two, less','one, more','two, more','NEW','12-394','12-264',NULL),
(270431,'chemistry','Complete the given reaction diagram(n2764).','a = CH₃-CH₂-CN and b = CH₃CH₂CH₂NH₂','First step is the nucleophilic substitution reaction in which CN⁻ attacks on the alkylehalide to substitute the halide (-Cl). Further reduction of the nitrile group gives the primary amine. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 393; Paragraph No. 2; Example 13.2)\ndiagram(ne2763)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','a = Ar(CO)₂N⁻K⁺ and b = CH₃CH₂CH₂NH₂','a = CH₃-CH₂-CN and b = CH₃CH₂CH₂NH₂','a = CH₃-CH₂-CN and b = Ar(CO)₂N⁻K⁺','a = CH₃-CH₂-CN and b = CH₃CH₂CH₂NH₂','NEW','12-393','12-263','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270431q.png'),
(270432,'chemistry','Name the amine produced by the Hoffmann degradation of benzamide.','Aniline','Benzamide is an aromatic amide containing seven carbon atoms. Hence, the amine formed from benzamide is aromatic primary amine containing six carbon atoms. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 395; Example 13.3).','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','Aniline','Toulene','Toulidine','Phthalimide','NEW','12-395','12-265',NULL),
(270433,'chemistry','Which amide gives propanamine by Hoffmann bromamide reaction?','Butanamide','Propanamine contains three carbons. Hence, the amide molecule must contain four carbon atoms. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 395; Example 13.3).','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','Butanamide','Allylamine','Prop-2-en-1-amine','Aniline','NEW','12-395','12-265',NULL),
(270434,'chemistry','Complete the given reaction diagram(n2765).','a = Ph-NO₂ and b = Ph-NH₃','Nitration of benzene gives nitrobenzene by electrophilic substitution reaction. Which on further reduction shows nucleophilic substitution reaction and gives aniline.   \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 395; intext question 13.3)\ndiagram(ne2766)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','a = m-nitrophenylsulfonic acid and b = C₆H₆','a = benzenesulfonic acid and b = C₆H₆','a = m-nitrophenylsulfonic acid and b = Ph-NH₃','a = Ph-NO₂ and b = Ph-NH₃','NEW','12-395','12-265','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270434q.png'),
(270435,'chemistry','Nitro compounds can be reduced to amines by all, except','Metals in strongly basic medium','Nitro compounds are reduced to amines by passing hydrogen gas in the presence of finely divided nickel, palladium or platinum and also by reduction with metals in acidic medium. Nitroalkanes can also be similarly reduced to the corresponding alkanamines.\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 392; Paragraph No. 1)\ndiagram(ne2720)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Preparation of Amines',NULL,'2','mcq','Passing hydrogen gas in the presence of finely divided nickel','Passing hydrogen gas in the presence of Pd and ethanol','Metals in acidic medium','Metals in strongly basic medium','NEW','12-392','12-262',NULL),
(270501,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        The lower aliphatic amines are ______ with _____ odour.','gases, fishy','The lower aliphatic amines are gases with fishy odour.  \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 395; Paragraph No.1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Physical properties of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','gases, fishy','liquid,fishy','gases, fruity','liquid, fruity','NEW','12-395','12-265',NULL),
(270502,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        Primary amines with ________ or more carbon atoms are ______ and still higher ones are ______.','three, liquid, solid','Primary amines with three or more carbon atoms are liquid and still higher ones are solid.  \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 395; Paragraph No.1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Physical properties of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','two, liquids, liquids','three, liquid, solid','four, liquid, solid','four, liquid, liquid','NEW','12-395','12-265',NULL),
(270503,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           Aniline and other arylamines are usually ________ and get _________on storage due to atmospheric oxidation.','colourless, coloured','Aniline and other arylamines are usually colourless but get coloured on storage due to atmospheric oxidation.   \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 395; Paragraph No.1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Physical properties of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','colourless, coloured','coloured, colourless','colourless, purple','purple, colourless','NEW','12-395','12-265',NULL),
(270504,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion (A) and reason (R):                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               Assertion (A): Lower aliphatic amines are insoluble in water.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        Reason (R): They can not form hydrogen bonds with water molecules.','Both assertion and reason are wrong.','Lower aliphatic amines are soluble in water because they can form hydrogen bonds with water molecules .  \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 395; Paragraph No.2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Physical properties of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','Assertion is correct and reason is wrong.','Both assertion and reason are correct.','Both assertion and reason are wrong.','Assertion is wrong and reason is correct.','NEW','12-395','12-265',NULL),
(270505,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion (A) and reason (R):                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            Assertion (A): Solubility of aliphatic amines decreases with increase in molar mass of amines.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              Reason (R): Size of the hydrophobic alkyl part increases in aliphatic amines as molar mass increase.','Both assertion and reason are correct.','Solubility of aliphatic amines decreases with increase in molar mass of amines due to increase in size of the hydrophobic alkyl part.  \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 395; Paragraph No.2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Physical properties of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','Both assertion and reason are correct.','Assertion is correct and reason is wrong.','Both assertion and reason are wrong.','Assertion is wrong and reason is correct.','NEW','12-395','12-265',NULL),
(270506,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       Solubility of aliphatic amines _______ with increase in molar mass.','decrease','Solubility of aliphatic amines decreases with increase in molar mass of amines due to increase in size of the hydrophobic alkyl part.  \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 395; Paragraph No.2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Physical properties of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','increases','decrease','constant','vary','NEW','12-395','12-265',NULL),
(270507,'chemistry','Which will be more soluble in water?','butan-1-ol','Alcohols are more soluble in water than amines because electronegativity of O is greater than that of N and hence, the alcohol molecule is more polar than amine molecule. \nSo, -OH group of alcohol forms more stronger hydrogen bond with water then -NH group of amines.  \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 395; Paragraph No.2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Physical properties of Amines',NULL,'2','mcq','butan-1-ol','butan-1-amine','methanamine','ethan-1-amine','NEW','12-395','12-265',NULL),
(270508,'chemistry','Which forms strong intermolecular hydrogen bonds?','Alcohols','Alcohols are able to form intermolecular hydrogen bonds to greater extent than amines due to their higher electronegativity. Ethers are less soluble than alcohols because alcohols can act both as hydrogen donor and acceptor and possess intermolecular hydrogen bonding.  \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 395; Paragraph No.2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Physical properties of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','Alcohols','Amines','Ethers','Alkanes','NEW','12-395','12-265',NULL),
(270509,'chemistry','Choose the correct order of boiling points of isomeric amines.','Primary > Secondary > Tertiary','Primary and secondary amines are engaged in intermolecular association due to hydrogen bonding between nitrogen of one and hydrogen of another molecule. \nThis intermolecular association is more in primary amines than in secondary amines as there are two hydrogen atoms available for hydrogen bond formation in it.\nTertiary amines do not have intermolecular association due to the absence of hydrogen atom available for hydrogen bond formation. \nTherefore, the order of boiling points of isomeric amines is as follows: Primary > Secondary > Tertiary.  \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 395; Paragraph No.3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Physical properties of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','Primary > Secondary > Tertiary','Primary < Secondary < Tertiary','Primary > Secondary < Tertiary','Primary < Secondary > Tertiary','NEW','12-395','12-265',NULL),
(51039,'chemistry','Which of these statements are true?\n\na) On heating a gas, kinetic energy of the particles increases and they strike the walls of the container more frequently, thus, exerting more pressure.\n\nb) Collisions of gas molecules are perfectly elastic.','both a and b','On heating a gas, kinetic energy of the particles increases and they strike the walls of the container more frequently, thus, exerting more pressure. \n\nCollisions of gas molecules are perfectly elastic.\n\nReference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 149; Paragraph No. 4)','Physical chemistry >> States of matter >> Most Challenging Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','a only','b only','both a and b','none of these','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(270510,'chemistry','Choose the correct order of extent of intermolecular hydrogen bonding.','Primary > Secondary > Tertiary','Primary and secondary amines are engaged in intermolecular association due to hydrogen bonding between nitrogen of one and hydrogen of another molecule. This intermolecular association is more in primary amines than in secondary amines as there are two hydrogen atoms available for hydrogen bond formation in it. Tertiary amines do not have intermolecular association due to the absence of hydrogen atom available for hydrogen bond formation. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 395; Paragraph No.3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Physical properties of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','Primary > Secondary > Tertiary','Primary < Secondary < Tertiary','Primary > Secondary < Tertiary','Primary < Secondary > Tertiary','NEW','12-395','12-265',NULL),
(270511,'chemistry','Amines are soluble in :\na. alcohol\nb. ether\nc. benzene','a,b,c','Alcohols are more soluble in water than amines because electronegativity of O is greater than that of N and hence, the alcohol molecule is more polar than amine molecule. \nSo, -OH group of alcohol forms more stronger hydrogen bond with water then -NH group of amines.  \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 395; Paragraph No.2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Physical properties of Amines',NULL,'2','mcq','a,b','b,c','a,c','a,b,c','NEW','12-395','12-265',NULL),
(270512,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion (A) and reason (R):                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              Assertion (A): Amines behave as nucleophiles.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     Reason (R): Unshared pair of electrons are present over the nitrogen atom.','Both assertion and reason are correct.','Amines behave as nucleophiles due to the presence of unshared electron pair. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 396; Paragraph No.2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','Both assertion and reason are correct.','Assertion is correct and reason is wrong.','Both assertion and reason are wrong.','Assertion is wrong and reason is correct.','NEW','12-396','12-266',NULL),
(270513,'biology','A Gene is said to be Dominant if','It expresses Its effects both in Heterozygous and Homozygous Conditions','A Dominant gene is expressed both in F1 and F2 Hybrid in heterozygous and homozygous state. Reference   : NCERT Page No 76','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'2','mcq','It expresses Its effects only in Heterozygous condition','It expresses Its effects only in homozygous stage','Expression Its effect only in F2 hybrid','It expresses Its effects both in Heterozygous and Homozygous Conditions','NEW','12-076','12-060',NULL),
(270514,'biology','Sometimes the F1 had a phenotype that did not resemble either of the two parents,but In between two parents such condition is called as?','Incomplete Dominance','It is the case when the Dominant character is not completely Dominant due to some changes. such times the F1 had a phenotype that did not resemble either of the two parents and was in between the two. Reference   : NCERT Page No 76','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'2','mcq','Codominance','Incomplete Dominance','Back cross','Linkage between two parental trait','NEW','12-076','12-060',NULL),
(270515,'biology','Incomplete Dominance can be best understood by which of the following:  \n\ni.Snapdragon        \nii.Dog Flower        \niii.Antirrhinum sp.        \niv.Sheep','i, ii and iii','The inheritance of flower colour in the dog flower (snapdragon or Antirrhinum sp.) is a good example for Incomplete Dominance. Reference   : NCERT Page No 76','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'3','mcq','ii and iii','i, ii and iii','iii and iv','i and iv','NEW','12-076','12-060',NULL),
(270516,'biology','The Given diagram is an example of (2704)','Incomplete Dominance','Reference  : Figure 5.6 NCERT 12 Page.no 76','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'2','mcq','Test Cross','Back cross','Incomplete Dominance','Codominance','NEW','12-076','12-060','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/270516q.png'),
(270517,'biology','Pick up the what is true in F1 Hybrid of given diagram (2705)','All pink (Rr)','Reference   :Figure 5.6 NCERT 12 Page.no 76','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'2','mcq','All pink (Rr)','All Red(Rr)','All Red(RR)','All White(rr)','NEW','12-076','12-060','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/270517q.png'),
(270518,'biology','Incomplete Dominance of a Monohybrid cross between True breeding Red flower (RR) and True breeding white flowers (rr) of dog flower the Resulting genotype and phenotype was?','Genotype : Rr,Phenotype : Pink','The Cross pollination between RR×rr gives the zygote Rr in F1 Generation whose phenotype is Pink,Instead of Red.The Reason for this is that not Always a dominant trait can be Dominant over Recessive. Because of some modifications change occurs.such conditions are called Incomplete Dominance Reference   : NCERT Page No 76','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'3','mcq','Genotype : Rr,Phenotype : Red','Genotype : RR,Phenotype : Red','Genotype : Rr,Phenotype : Pink','Genotype : rr,Phenotype : Pink','NEW','12-076','12-060',NULL),
(270519,'biology','The Genotypic ratio of dog flower in Incomplete Dominance is?','1 : 2 : 1','The ratio of Genotype and phenotype in Incomplete Dominance is same. Reference   : NCERT Page No 76','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'3','mcq','1 : 2 : 1','1 : 3','1 : 2 : 3','2 : 1','NEW','12-076','12-060',NULL),
(270520,'biology','The phenotypic ratio of dog flower in Incomplete Dominance is?','1 : 2 : 1','F2 Generation consist of 1/4th Red flowers, 1/2th Pink flowers and 1/4th White flowers. Reference   : NCERT Page No 76','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'2','mcq','3 : 1','2 : 3 : 1','1 : 2 : 1','1 : 1','NEW','12-076','12-060',NULL),
(270521,'biology','Which among the following is true regarding to change in phenotype of dog flower in Incomplete Dominance?','Red flower isn\'t completely Dominant over Recessive white flower','Red flower isn\'t completely Dominant over Recessive white flower;The change in phenotype is due to modifications or changes in one gene on different allele,Incomplete Dominance is seen Both F1 and F2 Generation of dog flower.\nReference   : NCERT Page No 76','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'2','mcq','Red flower is completely Dominant over Recessive white flower','The change in phenotype is due to modifications or changes in one gene on different chromosomes','Red flower isn\'t completely Dominant over Recessive white flower','Only F2 shows Incomplete Dominance of Red flower resulting in some pink flowers','NEW','12-076','12-060',NULL),
(270522,'biology','Unmodified and modified alleles which produce enzymes theoretically, the modified allele could be responsible for production of: \n\ni. The normal/less efficient enzyme \n\nii. A non-functional enzyme  \n\niii. No enzyme at all','i, ii and iii','Modified allele is Recessive compared to unmodified allele.Theoretically, the modified allele could be responsible for production of (i) the normal/less efficient enzyme, or (ii) a non-functional enzyme, or (iii) no enzyme at allReference   : NCERT Page No 76','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'2','mcq','i, ii and iii','ii and iii','i and iii','Only ii','NEW','12-076','12-060',NULL),
(270523,'biology','Which among the following is false','None of the Above','In cross hybrid of dog flower production of Pink colour is the reason for the presence of less efficient or no enzyme(low or absence of thing that is  responsible for synthesis of complete Dominant Trait) production by modified allele. So any change in the form of allele, if it becomes less functional or non functional will directly have change on the phenotype\nReference  :NCERT Page 77','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'2','mcq','In modified and unmodified alleles if the allele produces a non-functional enzyme or no enzyme, the phenotype may be effected.','The modified allele can be  equivalent to the unmodified allele,i.e it will produce the same phenotype/trait.','In cross hybrid of dog flower the recessive trait is seen due to non-functional enzyme or because no enzyme is produced','None of the Above','NEW','12-077','12-061',NULL),
(270524,'biology','The phenotype of F1 Hybrid didn\'t resemble either of the two parents in?','Incomplete Dominance','In Incomplete Dominance the phenotype of F1 Hybrid is different from either of the parental trait as seen in Dog flower experiment as there is incomplete expression in heterozygous state and complete expression in homozygous state. Reference   : NCERT Page No 76','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'1','mcq','Monohybrid Dominance','Incomplete Dominance','Test Cross','Complete Dominance','NEW','12-076','12-060',NULL),
(270525,'biology','The case in which  F1 generation resembles both parents is _____?','Codominance','Codominance is the case in which F1 resembles both parents.A good example is different types of red blood cells that determine ABO blood grouping in humans, where both the forms of a gene are equally dominant and can co exist and get expressed. Reference   : NCERT Page No 77','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'2','mcq','Dihybrid Cross','Codominance','Incomplete Dominance','Dominance','NEW','12-077','12-061',NULL),
(270526,'biology','ABO blood grouping in the Human can be best understood by____?','Codominance','ABO blood grouping is based on Codominance. In this the chances of F1 to resemble either of the parent are equal. Reference   : NCERT Page No 77','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'2','mcq','Test Cross','Back Cross','Dominance','Codominance','NEW','12-077','12-061',NULL),
(270527,'biology','The plasma membrane of the red blood cells has sugar polymers that protrude from Its surface and the kind of sugar is controlled by the gene ___?','Gene I','The plasma membrane of the red blood cells has sugar polymers that protrude from Its surface and the kind of sugar is controlled by the gene. The gene (I). Reference   : NCERT Page No 77','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'1','mcq','Gene I','Gene A','Gene B','Gene ABO','NEW','12-077','12-061',NULL),
(270528,'biology','The alleles of Gene I are: \n\ni. IA  \n\nii.IB        \n\niii. i     \n   \niv.Ib,Ic','i ii and iii','The gene (I) has three alleles IA, IB and i Reference   : NCERT Page No 77','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'2','mcq','ii and iii','i and iii','i ii and iii','iii and iv','NEW','12-077','12-061',NULL),
(270529,'biology','Which of the following is the most common form of allele?','The normal/less efficient enzyme','In the first case, the modified allele is equivalent to the unmodified allele,\ni.e., it will produce the same phenotype/trait, i.e., result in the transformation\nof substrate S. Such equivalent allele pairs are very common.','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'1','mcq','The normal/less efficient enzyme','a non-functional enzyme','no enzyme at all','all of the above','NEW','12-077','12-061',NULL),
(270530,'biology','Which of the following is false?','In a\ndiploid organism, there are two copies of each\ngene, i.e., as a pair of chromosomes','Every gene, as you know by now, contains the\ninformation to express a particular trait. In a\ndiploid organism, there are two copies of each\ngene, i.e., as a pair of alleles. Now, these two alleles\nneed not always be identical, as in a heterozygote.\nOne of them may be different due to some changes\nthat it has undergone (about which you will read\nfurther on, and in the next chapter) which modifies\nthe information that particular allele contains','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'2','mcq','Every gene contains the\ninformation to express a particular trait.','In a\ndiploid organism, there are two copies of each\ngene, i.e., as a pair of chromosomes','two alleles\nneed not always be identical, as in a heterozygote.','None of the above','NEW','12-077','12-061',NULL),
(270531,'biology','The plasma membrane of the red blood cells has ______ polymers\nthat protrude from its surface and determine the blood group','Sugar','The plasma membrane of the red blood cells has sugar polymers\nthat protrude from its surface and the kind of sugar is controlled by the\ngene.','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'2','mcq','Sugar','Protein','Lipid','Nucleic acid','NEW','12-077','12-061',NULL),
(270532,'biology','How many alleles are present for Gene I?','3','The gene (I) has three alleles','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'1','mcq','1','4','3','7','NEW','12-077','12-061',NULL),
(270533,'biology','How many of the following is true about blood grouping in humans? \n(i) The alleles IA and IB produce a slightly different form of the sugar while allele i does not      produce any sugar\n(ii)  each person possesses any  of the three I gene alleles \n(iii) IA and IB are completely dominant over i, in other words when IA and i are present only IA expresses.\n(iv) i produces a recessive sugar \n(v) when IA and IB are present together they both express their own types\nOf sugar , this is because of incomplete co-dominance.','2','The gene (I) has three alleles IA, IB and i. The alleles IA and IB produce\na slightly different form of the sugar while allele i does not produce any\nsugar. Because humans are diploid organisms, each person possesses\nany two of the three I gene alleles. IA and IB are completely dominant over\ni, in other words when IA and i are present only IA expresses (because i\ndoes not produce any sugar), and when IB and i are present IB expresses.\nBut when IA and IB are present together they both express their own types\nof sugars: this is because of co-dominance. Hence red blood cells have\nboth A and B types of sugars','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'2','mcq','5','2','3','4','NEW','12-077','12-061',NULL),
(270534,'biology','there are ____ different alleles, there\nare ____ different combinations of these alleles that are possible of the human ABO blood types','3,6','there are three different alleles, there\nare six different combinations of these three alleles that are possible, and\ntherefore, a total of six different genotypes of the human ABO blood types','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'1','mcq','3,6','4,7','2,4','3,4','NEW','12-077','12-061',NULL),
(270535,'biology','How many phenotypes and genotypes of human blood groups are possible?','4,6','Since there are three different alleles, there\nare six different combinations of these three alleles that are possible, and\ntherefore, a total of six different genotypes of the human ABO blood types. Four phenotypes can be found i.e. A, AB, B, O.','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Laws of Inheritance',NULL,'2','mcq','4,7','7,4','4,6','6,4','NEW','12-077','12-061',NULL),
(270601,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        Amines are ______ in nature.','basic','Amines are basic in nature because of their ability to accept hydrogen ion. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 396; Paragraph No.2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','basic','acidic','neutral','electrophilic','NEW','12-396','12-266',NULL),
(270602,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                Amines are _______ in organic solvents and amine salts are _______ in organic solvents.','soluble, insoluble','Amine salts are soluble in water but insoluble in organic solvents like ether. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 397; Paragraph No.1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','soluble, insoluble','soluble, soluble','insoluble, soluble','insoluble, insoluble','NEW','12-397','12-267',NULL),
(270607,'chemistry','Which of the following factor affects basic strength of amine?','All of these','Besides inductive effect, there are other effects like solvation effect, steric hinderance, etc., which affect the basic strength of amines. Inductive effect increases the electron density on nitrogen atom of amine, increasing the electron donor power and hence the basic strength. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 398; Paragraph No.1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'2','mcq','Inductive effect','Solvation effect,','Steric hinderance','All of these','NEW','12-398','12-268',NULL),
(270604,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion (A) and reason (R):                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 Assertion (A): Aliphatic amines are stronger bases than ammonia.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Reason (R): Positive inductive effect of alkyl groups leading to high electron density on the nitrogen atom.','Both assertion and reason are correct.','Aliphatic amines are stronger bases than ammonia due to +I effect of alkyl groups leading to high electron density on the nitrogen atom. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 397; Paragraph No.3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','Both assertion and reason are correct.','Assertion is correct and reason is wrong.','Both assertion and reason are wrong.','Assertion is wrong and reason is correct.','NEW','12-397','12-267',NULL),
(270605,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                pKb values of aliphatic amines lie in the range of _________.','3 to 4.22','pKb value of ammonia is 4.75. Aliphatic amines are stronger bases than ammonia due to positive inductive effect of alkyl groups leading to high electron density on the nitrogen atom. Their pKᵇ values lie in the range of 3 to 4.22.  \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 397; Paragraph No.3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','3 to 4.22','3.5 to 4.5','2.5 to 3.5','3.3 to 4.33','NEW','12-397','12-267',NULL),
(270606,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion (A) and reason (R):                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   Assertion (A): Aromatic amines are weaker bases than ammonia.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Reason (R): The electron withdrawing nature of the aryl group lowers the electron donating tendency.','Both assertion and reason are correct.','Aromatic amines are weaker bases than ammonia due to the electron withdrawing nature of the aryl group. Hence, the electron donating tendency of N reduces, making it a weaker base. Reference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 397; Paragraph No.3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','Both assertion and reason are correct.','Assertion is correct and reason is wrong.','Both assertion and reason are wrong.','Assertion is wrong and reason is correct','NEW','12-397','12-267',NULL),
(270608,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    The order of basicity of amines in the gaseous phase is:','Tertiary amine > Secondary amine > Primary amine > Ammonia','The basic nature of aliphatic amines increase with increase in the number of alkyl groups. This trend is followed in the gaseous phase. Hence, the order of basicity of amines in the gaseous phase is as follows; tertiary amine > secondary amine > primary amine > ammonia. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 398; Paragraph No.3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','Tertiary amine < Secondary amine > Primary amine > Ammonia','Tertiary amine > Secondary amine < Primary amine > Ammonia','Tertiary amine < Secondary amine < Primary amine < Ammonia','Tertiary amine > Secondary amine > Primary amine > Ammonia','NEW','12-398','12-268',NULL),
(270609,'chemistry','Order of extent of H-bonding in water of amine ions by solvation:','Primary amine > Secondary amine > Tertiary amine','In the aqueous phase, the substituted ammonium cations get stabilised not only by electron releasing effect of the alkyl group (+I) but also by solvation with water molecules. The greater the size of the ion, lesser will be the solvation. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 398; Paragraph No.3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','Primary amine < Secondary amine < Tertiary amine','Primary amine < Secondary amine > Tertiary amine','Primary amine > Secondary amine > Tertiary amine','Primary amine > Secondary amine < Tertiary amine','NEW','12-398','12-268',NULL),
(270610,'chemistry','Order of stability of amine ions by solvation:','Primary amine > Secondary amine > Tertiary amine','In the aqueous phase, the substituted ammonium cations get stabilised not only by electron releasing effect of the alkyl group (+I) but also by solvation with water molecules. The greater the size of the ion, lesser will be the solvation. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 398; Paragraph No.3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','Primary amine < Secondary amine < Tertiary amine','Primary amine < Secondary amine > Tertiary amine','Primary amine > Secondary amine > Tertiary amine','Primary amine > Secondary amine < Tertiary amine','NEW','12-398','12-268',NULL),
(270611,'chemistry','The order of basic strength in case of methyl substituted amines in aqueous solution:','Secondary > Primary > Tertiary > Ammonia','There is a subtle interplay of the inductive effect, solvation effect and steric hinderance of the alkyl group which decides the basic strength of alkyl amines in the aqueous state. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 399; Paragraph No.1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','Secondary > Primary > Tertiary > Ammonia','Secondary < Primary < Tertiary < Ammonia','Secondary < Primary > Tertiary > Ammonia','Secondary > Primary < Tertiary > Ammonia','NEW','12-399','12-269',NULL),
(270612,'chemistry','The order of basic strength in case of ethyl substituted amines in aqueous solution:','Secondary > Tertiary > Primary > Ammonia','There is a subtle interplay of the inductive effect, solvation effect and steric hinderance of the alkyl group which decides the basic strength of alkyl amines in the aqueous state . \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 399; Paragraph No.1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','Secondary > Tertiary > Primary < Ammonia','Secondary > Tertiary < Primary > Ammonia','Secondary > Tertiary > Primary > Ammonia','Secondary < Tertiary > Primary > Ammonia','NEW','12-399','12-269',NULL),
(270613,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      Aniline is _______ stable than anilinium ion.','more','Greater the number of resonating structures, greater is the stability. Therefore that aniline (five resonating structures) is more stable than anilinium ion. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 399; Paragraph No.3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','more','less','equal','same','NEW','12-399','12-269',NULL),
(270614,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         _____the resonating structure _______ is the stability.','more, more','Greater the number of resonating structures, greater is the stability. Therefore that aniline (five resonating structures) is more stable than anilinium ion.  \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 399; Paragraph No.3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','more, more','less, more','more, less','less,less','NEW','12-399','12-269',NULL),
(270615,'chemistry','The possible resonating structures of aniline are------------.','five','All the possible resonating structures of aniline are shown in the following diagram. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 399; Paragraph No.1)\ndiagram(ne2774)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','five','four','six','seven','NEW','12-399','12-269',NULL);
INSERT INTO `ncert_book_pyq` (`unique_id`, `subject`, `question`, `answer`, `explanation`, `topic_name`, `chapter_name`, `difficulty`, `quiz_type`, `option_a`, `option_b`, `option_c`, `option_d`, `syllabus_update`, `ncert22_page`, `ncert23_page`, `image_url`) VALUES
(270616,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion (A) and reason (R):                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 Assertion (A): The basic nature of aniline or other aromatic amines would be less than that of ammonia.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Reason (R): Having more number of resonating structures, aniline is more stable than anilinium ion.','Both assertion and reason are correct.','Greater the number of resonating structures, greater is the stability. Thus, aniline having five resonating structures, is more stable than anilinium ion. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 399; Paragraph No.3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','Both assertion and reason are correct.','Assertion is correct and reason is wrong.','Both assertion and reason are wrong.','Assertion is wrong and reason is correct.','NEW','12-399','12-269',NULL),
(270617,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  In case of substituted aniline, it is observed that electron releasing groups _______ basic strength whereas electron withdrawing groups ________ it.','increases, decreases','In case of substituted aniline, it is observed that electron releasing groups like –OCH₃, –CH₃ increase basic strength whereas electron withdrawing groups like –NO₂, –SO₃H, –COOH, –X decrease it. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 399; Paragraph No.3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','increases, decreases','increases, increases','decreases, decreases','decreases, increases','NEW','12-399','12-269',NULL),
(41421,'chemistry','The molecular geometry of AB₂E type molecules:','Bent','Theoretically the shape should have been triangular planar but actually it is found to be bent or V-shaped, this is due to lp-bp repulsion which is more than bp-bp repulsion so the angle is reduced from 119 from 120. \n\nAs shown in diagram\n\nReference: (NCERT chemistry Class 11; page 116; Table 4.8) diagram(ne0412)','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> VSEPR theory',NULL,'2','mcq','Bent','See-saw','Trigonal pyramidal','T-shaped','NEW','11-114','11-114',NULL),
(270618,'chemistry','Arrange the following in decreasing order of their basic strength. diagram(n2776).','(C₂H₅)₂NH > C₂H₅NH₂ > NH₃ > C₆H₅NH₂','Aliphatic amines are more basic than aniline as aniline is resonance stabilised. Among the two aliphatic amines, secondary amine due to +I effect have greater electron donating ability making it more basic. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 400; Example 13.4)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','(C₂H₅)₂NH > C₂H₅NH₂ > NH₃ > C₆H₅NH₂','(C₂H₅)₂NH < C₂H₅NH₂ > NH₃ > C₆H₅NH₂','(C₂H₅)₂NH > C₂H₅NH₂ < NH₃ > C₆H₅NH₂','(C₂H₅)₂NH < C₂H₅NH₂ < NH₃ < C₆H₅NH₂','NEW','12-400','12-270','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270618q.png'),
(270619,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        Acylation of amines is ________.','NSR','Aliphatic and aromatic primary and secondary amines react with acid chlorides, anhydrides and esters by nucleophilic substitution reaction. This reaction is known as acylation. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 400; Paragraph No.2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','NSR','ESR','NAR','EAR','NEW','12-400','12-270',NULL),
(270620,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          The products obtained by acylation reaction of amines are known as_____________.','amides','In acylation of amines the replacement of hydrogen atom of –NH₂ or >N–H group by the acyl group. The products obtained by acylation reaction are known as amides. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 400; Paragraph No.2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','amides','imides','amines','imines','NEW','12-400','12-270','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/270620q.png'),
(270621,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion (A) and reason (R):                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 Assertion (A): The acylation reaction of amines is carried out in the presence of a base stronger than the amine, like pyridine.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  Reason (R): Pyridine, removes HCl formed and shifts the equilibrium to the left hand side.','Assertion is correct and reason is wrong.','The reaction is carried out in the presence of a base stronger than the amine, like pyridine, which removes HCl so formed and shifts the equilibrium to the right hand side. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 400; Paragraph No.2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','Assertion is correct and reason is wrong.','Both assertion and reason are correct.','Both assertion and reason are wrong.','Assertion is wrong and reason is correct.','NEW','12-400','12-270','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/270621q.png'),
(270622,'chemistry','Complete the given reaction diagram(n2781).','C₆H₅-NH-CO-CH₃ + CH₃COOH','Aliphatic and aromatic primary and secondary amines react with acid chlorides, anhydrides and esters by nucleophilic substitution\nreaction. This reaction is known as acylation. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 400; Paragraph No.2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','C₆H₅-NH-CO-CH₃ + CH₃COOH','C₂H₅-NH-CO-CH₃ + HCl','CH₃NHCOC₆H₅ + HCl','(C₂H₅)₂N-CO-CH₃ + HCl','NEW','12-400','12-270','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270622q.png'),
(270623,'chemistry','Complete the given reaction diagram(n2783).','CH₃NHCOC₆H₅ + HCl','Aliphatic and aromatic primary and secondary amines react with acid chlorides, anhydrides and esters by nucleophilic substitution\nreaction. This reaction is known as acylation. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 400; Paragraph No.2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','C₆H₅-NH-CO-CH₃ + CH₃COOH','C₂H₅-NH-CO-CH₃ + HCl','CH₃NHCOC₆H₅ + HCl','(C₂H₅)₂N-CO-CH₃ + HCl','NEW','12-400','12-270','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270623q.png'),
(270624,'chemistry','Complete the given reaction diagram(n2784).','(C₂H₅)₂N-CO-CH₃ + HCl','Aliphatic and aromatic primary and secondary amines react with acid chlorides, anhydrides and esters by nucleophilic substitution\nreaction. This reaction is known as acylation. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 400; Paragraph No.2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','C₆H₅-NH-CO-CH₃ + CH₃COOH','C₂H₅-NH-CO-CH₃ + HCl','CH₃NHCOC₆H₅ + HCl','(C₂H₅)₂N-CO-CH₃ + HCl','NEW','12-400','12-270','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270624q.png'),
(270625,'chemistry','which of the following reaction distinguishes primary amines from secondary and tertiary?','Carbylamine reaction','Aliphatic and aromatic primary amines on heating with chloroform and ethanolic potassium hydroxide form isocyanides or carbylamines which are foul smelling substances. Secondary and tertiary amines do not show this reaction. This reaction is known as carbylamine reaction or isocyanide test and is used as a test for primary amines. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 401; Paragraph No.1). diagram(ne2790)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','Carbylamine reaction','Cyanide test','Both of these','None of these','NEW','12-401','12-271',NULL),
(270626,'chemistry','Carbylamine test show positive results for_____.','both aliphatic and aromatic primary amines','Aliphatic and aromatic primary amines on heating with chloroform and ethanolic potassium hydroxide form isocyanides or carbylamines which are foul smelling substances. Secondary and tertiary amines do not show this reaction. This reaction is known as carbylamine reaction or isocyanide test and is used as a test for primary amines. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 401; Paragraph No.1). diagram(ne2790)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','both aliphatic and aromatic primary amines','aliphatic primary amine','aromatic primary amine','secondary amine','NEW','12-401','12-271',NULL),
(270627,'chemistry','In situ reaction of mineral acid and sodium nitrite gives-----------.','nitrous acid','Three classes of amines react differently with nitrous acid which is prepared in situ from a mineral acid and sodium nitrite. Reference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 401; Paragraph No.2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','nitrous acid','nitric acid','hyponitrous acid','orthonitric acid','NEW','12-401','12-271',NULL),
(270628,'chemistry','Which of the following tests can be used in quantitative estimation of amino acids and proteins?','Primary aliphatic amines reaction with nitrous acid.','Primary aliphatic amines react with nitrous acid to form aliphatic diazonium salts which being unstable, liberate nitrogen gas and alcohols. Quantitative evolution of nitrogen is used in estimation of amino acids and proteins. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 401; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','Primary aliphatic amines reaction with nitrous acid.','Secondary aliphatic amines reaction with nitrous acid.','Tertiary aliphatic amines reaction with nitrous acid.','Carbylamine test.','NEW','12-401','12-271',NULL),
(270629,'chemistry','Complete the given reaction diagram(n2796).','a = R-N₂⁺Cl⁻ and b = ROH + N₂ + HCl','Primary aliphatic amines react with nitrous acid to form aliphatic diazonium salts which being unstable, liberate nitrogen gas quantitatively and alcohols . \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 401; Paragraph No. 3)\ndiagram(ne2793)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'3','mcq','a = ROH + N₂ + HCl and b = R-N₂⁺Cl⁻','a = R-N₂⁺Cl⁻ and b = ROH + N₂ + HCl','a = R-N₂⁺Cl⁻ and b = R-N₂⁺Cl⁻','a = ROH + N₂ + HCl and b = ROH + N₂ + HCl','NEW','12-401','12-271','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270629q.png'),
(270630,'chemistry','Complete the given reaction diagram(n2794).','Benzenediazonium chloride','Aromatic amines react with nitrous acid at low temperatures (273-278 K) to form diazonium salts.\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 401; Paragraph No. 4)\ndiagram(ne2795)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','Benzenediazonium chloride','Chlorobenzene','Benzyl chloride','Aniline','NEW','12-401','12-271','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270630q.png'),
(270631,'chemistry','What is Hinsberg’s reagent?','Benzenesulphonyl chloride','Benzenesulphonyl chloride (C₆H₅SO₂Cl), which is also known as Hinsberg’s reagent, reacts with primary and secondary amines to\nform sulphonamides. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 401; Paragraph No. 8)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','Benzenesulphonyl chloride','Benzenediazonium chloride','N-Ethylbenzenesulphonyl amide.','N,N-Diethylbenzenesulphonamide','NEW','12-401','12-271',NULL),
(270632,'chemistry','Which of the following tests not given by tertiary amines?','Both Hinsberg\'s reaction and carbylamine reaction','Tertiary amines do not react with benzenesulphonyl chloride.\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 402; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'2','mcq','Both Hinsberg\'s reaction and carbylamine reaction','Hnsberg\'s reaction','Carbylamine reaction','None of the above','NEW','12-402','12-272',NULL),
(270633,'chemistry','What product is formed when primary amine reacts with Hinsberg\'s reagent?','N-Ethylbenzenesulphonyl amide','The reaction of benzenesulphonyl chloride with primary amine yields N-ethylbenzenesulphonyl amide. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 401; Paragraph No. 6)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','N-Alkylbenzenesulphonyl amide','N,N-Diethylbenzenesulphonamide','N-Ethylbenzenesulphonyl amide','Benzenediazonium chloride','NEW','12-401','12-271',NULL),
(270634,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           The product formed by the reaction of primary amine with Hinsberg\'s reagent is _________ in alkali.','soluble','The hydrogen attached to nitrogen in sulphonamide is strongly acidic due to the presence of strong electron withdrawing sulphonyl group. Hence, it is soluble in alkali. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 401; Paragraph No. 7)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','soluble','insoluble','precipitated','saturated','NEW','12-401','12-271',NULL),
(270635,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             The product formed by the reaction of secondary amine with Hinsberg\'s reagent is _________ in alkali.','insoluble','In the reaction with secondary amine, N,N-diethylbenzenesulphonamide is formed N, N-diethylbenzene sulphonamide does not contain any\nhydrogen atom attached to nitrogen atom, it is not acidic and hence insoluble in alkali. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 401; Paragraph No. 8)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','soluble','insoluble','precipitated','saturated','NEW','12-401','12-271',NULL),
(270636,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  These days Hinsberg\'s reagent is replaced by _____________.','p-Toluenesulphonyl chloride','These days benzenesulphonyl chloride is replaced by p-toluenesulphonyl chloride. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 401; Paragraph No. 5)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','p-Toluenesulphonyl chloride','N-Alkylbenzenesulphonylamide','Benzylchloride','Benzenediazonium chloride','NEW','12-401','12-271',NULL),
(270637,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              ____________ positions to the –NH₂ group become centres of high electron density.','ortho and para','ortho and para positions to the –NH₂ group become centres of high electron density. Thus –NH₂ group is ortho and para directing and a powerful activating group. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 402; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','ortho','para','meta','ortho and para','NEW','12-402','12-272',NULL),
(270638,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement:    \nAniline reacts with bromine water at room temperature to give a _____ ppt of _________.','white, 2,4,6-tribromoaniline','Aniline reacts with bromine water at room temperature to give a white precipitate of 2,4,6-tribromoaniline. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 402; Paragraph No. 4)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','white, 2,4,6-tribromoaniline','white, 2,4-dibromoaniline','green, 2,4,6-tribromoaniline','green, 2,4-dibromoaniline','NEW','12-402','12-272',NULL),
(270639,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for given statement:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           The main problem encountered during electrophilic substitution reactions of aromatic amines is that of their _______reactivity.','very high','The main problem encountered during electrophilic substitution reactions of aromatic amines is that of their very high reactivity. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 402; Paragraph No. 5)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Chemical reactions of Amines',NULL,'1','mcq','very high','high','low','very low','NEW','12-402','12-272',NULL),
(270701,'chemistry','General formula of diazonium salt is________.','R⁺ N₂⁺X','The diazonium salts have the general formula R⁺ N₂⁺ X, where R stands for an aryl group and X⁻ ion may be Cl⁻ Br₄⁻ HSO₄⁻  BF₄⁻ , etc.\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 404; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Methods of preparation of diazonium salts',NULL,'1','mcq','R⁺ N₂⁻ X','R⁺ N₃⁻ X','R⁺ N₆⁻ X','R⁺ N₂⁺X','NEW','12-404','12-274',NULL),
(270702,'chemistry','The __________ group is called diazonium group.','N₂⁺','The N₂⁺ group is called diazonium group.         \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 404; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Methods of preparation of diazonium salts',NULL,'1','mcq','N₂⁻','N₃⁻','N₂','N₂⁺','NEW','12-404','12-274',NULL),
(270703,'chemistry','Primary aliphatic amines form ________ alkyldiazonium salts.','highly unstable','Primary aliphatic amines form highly unstable alkyldiazonium salts. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 404; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Methods of preparation of diazonium salts',NULL,'1','mcq','highly unstable','unstable','stable','highly stable','NEW','12-404','12-274',NULL),
(270704,'chemistry','Benzenediazonium chloride is prepared by the reaction of aniline with ___________.','nitrous acid at 273-278 K','Benzenediazonium chloride is prepared by the reaction of aniline with nitrous acid at 273-278 K. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 404; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Methods of preparation of diazonium salts',NULL,'1','mcq','nitrous acid at 273-278 K','nitric acid at 273-285 K','nitrous acid at 273-285 K','nitric acid at 273-278 K','NEW','12-404','12-274',NULL),
(270705,'chemistry','The conversion of primary aromatic amines into diazonium salts is known as _____.','diazotisation','The conversion of primary aromatic amines into diazonium salts is known as diazotisation. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 404; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Methods of preparation of diazonium salts',NULL,'1','mcq','diazotisation','derivitization','coupling','salination','NEW','12-404','12-274',NULL),
(270706,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion (A) and reason (R):                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         Assertion (A): The diazonium salt is not generally stored and is used immediately after its preparation.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               Reason (R): Because diazonium salt is very unstable at room temperature.','Both assertion and reason are correct','Primary aromatic amines form arenediazonium salts which are stable for a short time in solution at low temperatures (273-278 K). The stability of arenediazonium ion is explained on the basis of resonance.\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 404; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Methods of preparation of diazonium salts',NULL,'3','mcq','Both assertion and reason are correct','Both assertion and reason are wrong','Assertion is wrong and reason is correct','Assertion is correct and reason is wrong','NEW','12-404','12-274',NULL),
(270707,'chemistry','Benzenediazonium chloride is a __________ crystalline solid.','colourless','Benzenediazonium chloride is a colourless crystalline solid.\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 405; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Methods of preparation of diazonium salts',NULL,'1','mcq','blue','colourless','red','green','NEW','12-405','12-275','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/270707q.png'),
(270708,'chemistry','Benzenediazonium fluoroborate is water __________ and ___________at room temperature.','insoluble, stable','Benzenediazonium fluoroborate is water insoluble and stable at room temperature. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 405; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Methods of preparation of diazonium salts',NULL,'1','mcq','insoluble, stable','soluble, stable','insoluble, unstable','soluble, unstable','NEW','12-405','12-275',NULL),
(270709,'chemistry','The Cl⁻, Br⁻ and CN⁻ nucleophiles can easily be introduced in the benzene ring in the presence of Cu(I) ion. This reaction is called___________.','Sandmeyer reaction','The Cl⁻, Br⁻ and CN⁻ nucleophiles can easily be introduced in the benzene ring in the presence of Cu(I) ion. This reaction is called Sandmeyer reaction. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 405; Paragraph No. 4)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Methods of preparation of diazonium salts',NULL,'1','mcq','Gabriel phthalimide reaction','Gatterman reaction','carbylamine reaction','Sandmeyer reaction','NEW','12-405','12-275','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/270709q.png'),
(270710,'chemistry','Chlorine or bromine can also be introduced in the benzene ring by treating the diazonium salt solution with corresponding halogen acid in the presence of copper powder. This is referred as _____.','Gatterman','Chlorine or bromine can be introduced in the benzene ring by treating the diazonium salt solution with corresponding halogen acid in the presence of copper powder. This is referred as Gatterman reaction. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 405; Paragraph No. 5)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Methods of preparation of diazonium salts',NULL,'1','mcq','Gatterman','Gabriel phthalimide reaction','carbylamine reaction','Sandmeyer reaction','NEW','12-405','12-275',NULL),
(270711,'biology','Experimental verification of the chromosomal theory of Inheritance was done by?','Thomas Hunt Morgan and his colleagues','Following synthesis of ideas, experimental verification of the chromosomal theory of inheritance by Thomas Hunt Morgan and his colleagues. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 81','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Chromosomal Theory of Inheritance',NULL,'2','mcq','Tschermak and Correns','Sutton and baveri','Thomas Hunt Morgan and his colleagues','Bateson','NEW','12-081','12-065',NULL),
(270712,'chemistry','ArN₂⁺X⁻ + Cu₂Cl₂/HCl gives __________.','ArCl','The Cl⁻, Br⁻ and CN⁻ nucleophiles can easily be introduced in the benzene ring in the presence of Cu(I) ion. This reaction is called Sandmeyer reaction. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 405; Paragraph No. 4)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Diazonium salts and their Chemical reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','ArBr','ArI','ArCl','ArF','NEW','12-405','12-275',NULL),
(270713,'chemistry','ArN₂⁺X⁻ + Cu₂Br₂/HBr gives __________.','ArBr','The Cl⁻, Br⁻ and CN⁻ nucleophiles can easily be introduced in the benzene ring in the presence of Cu(I) ion. This reaction is called Sandmeyer reaction. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 405; Paragraph No. 4)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Diazonium salts and their Chemical reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','ArBr','ArI','ArCl','ArF','NEW','12-405','12-275','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/270713q.png'),
(270714,'chemistry','ArN₂⁺X⁻ + CuCN/KCN gives ________.','ArCN','The Cl⁻, Br⁻ and CN⁻ nucleophiles can easily be introduced in the benzene ring in the presence of Cu(I) ion. This reaction is called Sandmeyer reaction. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 405; Paragraph No. 4)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Diazonium salts and their Chemical reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','ArCN','ArI','ArBr','ArF','NEW','12-405','12-275',NULL),
(270715,'chemistry','ArN₂⁺X⁻ + Cu/HCl gives _________.','ArCl','Chlorine or bromine can be introduced in the benzene ring by treating the diazonium salt solution with corresponding halogen acid in the presence of copper powder. This is referred as Gatterman reaction. Reference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 405; Paragraph No. 5)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Diazonium salts and their Chemical reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','ArBr','ArI','ArCl','ArF','NEW','12-405','12-275',NULL),
(270716,'chemistry','ArN₂⁺Cl⁻ + KI gives ___________.','ArI','Iodine is not easily introduced into the benzene ring directly, but, when the diazonium salt solution is treated with potassium iodide, iodobenzene is formed. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 405; Paragraph No. 7)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Diazonium salts and their Chemical reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','ArCN','ArI','ArCl','ArF','NEW','12-405','12-275',NULL),
(270717,'chemistry','ArN₂⁺Cl⁻ + HBF₄⁻ gives ___________.','ArF','When arenediazonium chloride is treated with fluoroboric acid, arene diazonium fluoroborate is precipitated which on heating decomposes to yield aryl fluoride. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 405; Paragraph No. 8)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Diazonium salts and their Chemical reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','ArCN','ArI','ArBr','ArF','NEW','12-405','12-275',NULL),
(270718,'chemistry','If the temperature of the diazonium salt solution is allowed to rise upto 283 K, the salt gets hydrolysed to ______.','phenol','If the temperature of the diazonium salt solution is allowed to rise upto 283 K, the salt gets hydrolysed to phenol. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 405; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Diazonium salts and their Chemical reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','phenol','amine','acid','aniline','NEW','12-405','12-275',NULL),
(270719,'chemistry','Benzene diazonium chloride reacts with phenol in which the phenol molecule at its para position is coupled with the diazonium salt to form __________.','parahydroxyazobenzene','Benzene diazonium chloride reacts with phenol in which the phenol molecule at its para position is coupled with the diazonium salt to form p-hydroxyazobenzene.This\ntype of reaction is known as coupling reaction. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 406; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Diazonium salts and their Chemical reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','parahydroxyazobenzene','parahydroxyphenol','parahydroxyazophenol','parahydroxybenzene','NEW','12-406','12-276',NULL),
(270801,'chemistry','Which of the following reactions is appropriate for converting acetamide to methanamine?','Hoffmann hypobromamide reaction','CH₃CONH₂ + Br₂ + 4KOH → CH₃NH₂ + 2KBr + K₂CO₃ + 2H₂O (Hoffmann bromamide reaction). \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 394; Paragraph No. 2) (NEET2017)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Diazonium salts and their Chemical reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','Hoffmann hypobromamide reaction','Stephen’s reaction','Gabriel phthalimide synthesis','Carbylamine reaction','NEW','12-394','12-264',NULL),
(270802,'chemistry','Method by which aniline cannot be prepared is_________.','potassium salt of phthalimide treated with\nchlorobenzene followed by hydrolysis with\naqueous NaOH solution','Aniline is not  prepared by this method as aryl halides can not undergo nucleophilic substitution reaction with potassium phthalimide under mild conditions. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 394; Paragraph No. 1) (NEET2015)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','degradation of benzamide with bromine in\nalkaline solution','reduction of nitrobenzene with H₂/Pd in ethanol','potassium salt of phthalimide treated with\nchlorobenzene followed by hydrolysis with\naqueous NaOH solution','hydrolysis of phenylisocyanide with acidic\nsolution','NEW','12-394','12-264',NULL),
(270803,'chemistry','The electrolytic reduction of nitrobenzene in strongly acidic medium produces __________.','p-aminophenol','The electrolytic reduction of nitrobenzene in strongly acidic medium gives phenylhydroxyl amine which on rearrangement produces  p-aminophenol. \nReference: (NCERT class-12) (NEET2015)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','azobenzene','aniline','p-aminophenol','azoxybenzene','NEW','12-394','12-264',NULL),
(270804,'chemistry','Acetamide is treated with the following reagents separately. Which one of these would yield methyl amine?','NaOH-Br₂','CH₃CONH₂ + Br₂ + 4NaOH → CH₃NH₂ + 2NaBr + Na₂CO₃ + 2H₂O (Hoffmann bromamide reaction). \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 394; Paragraph No. 2) (NEET2010)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','NaOH-Br₂','Sodalime','Hot conc.H₂SO₄','PCl₅','NEW','12-394','12-264',NULL),
(270805,'chemistry','Which one of the following on reduction with lithium aluminium hydride yields a secondary amine?','Methyl isocyanide','Alkyl isocyanide on reduction with lithium aluminium hydride produces secondary amine which contains methyl as one of the alkyl groups.\nReference: (NCERT class-12) (NEET2007)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Methyl isocyanide','Acetamide','Methyl cyanide','Nitroethane','NEW','12-394','12-264',NULL),
(270806,'chemistry','Which of the following amines will give the carbylamine test?','Ar-NH₂','Only aliphatic and aromatic primary amines give carbylamine test. Secondary and tertiary amines do not show carbylamine test. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 401; Paragraph No. 1 (NEET2020)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Ar-NH₂','ArNH-CH₃','ArN-(CH₃)₂','ArNHC₂H₅','NEW','12-401','12-271',NULL),
(220601,'chemistry','The oxidation number method to balance a redox reaction is based on','change in the oxidation number of reducing agent and the oxidising agent','One of these methods is based on the change in the oxidation number of reducing agent and the oxidising agent and the other method is based on splitting the redox reaction into two half reactions — one involving oxidation and the other involving reduction. Both these methods are in use and the choice of their use rests with the individual using them. (Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 274; 8.3.2)','Inorganic chemistry >> Redox Reactions >> Redox Balancing',NULL,'2','mcq','change in the oxidation number of reducing agent and the oxidising agent','splitting the redox reaction into two half reactions — one involving oxidation and the other involving reduction.','conservation of number of electrons lost by oxidising agent and gained by reducing agent','none of these','NEW','11-274','11-246',NULL),
(270807,'chemistry','The correct order of the basic strength of methyl substituted amines in aqueous solution is _____.','(CH₃)₂NH > CH₃NH₂ > (CH₃)₃N','The basicity of amines in aqueous solution depends on the stability factor of the ammonium cation or conjugate acid which is formed by accepting a proton from water that in turn depends on the + I-effect of alkyl group, extent of hydrogen bonding and stearic factor. \nAll these conditions are favourable for 2° amines. Therefore, 2° amines are the strongest bases.\nIf the alkyl group is small i.e., CH₃ then there is no steric hindrance to H-bonding. \nThus, the stability due to hydrogen bonding predominates over the stability due to + I-effect of —CH₃ group therefore, primary amine is a stronger base than 3° amine, resulting in the order of decreasing basic strength for methylamines in aqueous solution:\n(CH₃)₂NH > CH₃NH₂ > (CH₃)₃N.\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 398; Paragraph No. 3) (NEET2019)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','CH₃NH₂ > (CH₃)₂NH > (CH₃)₃N','(CH₃)₂NH > CH₃NH₂ > (CH₃)₃N','(CH₃)₃N > CH₃NH₂ > (CH₃)₂NH','(CH₃)₃N > (CH₃)₂NH > CH₃NH₂','NEW','12-398','12-268',NULL),
(270808,'chemistry','The amine that reacts with Hinsberg’s reagent to give an alkali insoluble product is _________.','(CH₃)₂—CH—NH—CH—(CH₃)₂','Secondary amines by reactiong with Hinsberg’s reagent gives N, N-dialkylbenzene sulphonamide which does not contain any hydrogen atom attached to N-atom, it is not acidic and therefore, insoluble in alkali. Tertiary amines don\'t show reaction with Hinsberg’s reagent. Primary amines generates products which are soluble in alkali.\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 401; Paragraph No. 4) (ODISHA NEET 2019)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','(CH₃)₂—CH—NH—CH—(CH₃)₂','CH₃—CH₂—N—(CH₂CH₃)₂','(CH₃)₂—C(NH₂)—CH₂CH₂CH₃','(CH₃)₃—C—CH(CH₃)—NH₂','NEW','12-401','12-271',NULL),
(270809,'chemistry','Nitration of aniline in strong acidic medium also gives m-nitroaniline because','in acidic (strong) medium aniline is present as\nanilinium ion.','The reason for formation of an unexpected amount of m-nitroaniline is being , under strongly acidic condition of nitration, most of the aniline gets converted into anilinium ion and since, NH₃⁺ is a meta directing group, producing a large amount of m-nitroaniline. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 403; Paragraph No. 1) Reference: (NEET2018)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','inspite of substituents nitro group always goes to only m-position','in electrophilic substitution reactions amino\ngroup is meta directive','in absence of substituents nitro group always\ngoes to m-position','in acidic (strong) medium aniline is present as\nanilinium ion.','NEW','12-403','12-273',NULL),
(270810,'chemistry','The correct increasing order of basic strength for the following compounds is _______. diagram(n27106).','II < I < III','Positive inductive effect of substituted group increases the basic strength whereas –I effect of substitutent reduces the basic strength of aniline.\nReference: (NCERT class-12) (NEET2017)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','III < I < II','III < II < I','II < I < III','II < III < I','NEW','12-403','12-273','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270810q.png'),
(270811,'chemistry','The correct statement regarding the basicity of arylamines is __________.','arylamines are generally less basic than alkylamines because the nitrogen lone-pair electrons are delocalised by interaction with the aromatic ring p-electron system','In arylamines, lone pair of electrons on nitrogen atom gets delocalised over the benzene ring, making it unavailable for donation. therefore, arylamines are less basic than alkylamines. Reference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 399; Paragraph No. 3) (NEET-1 2016)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','arylamines are generally more basic than alkylamines because of aryl group','arylamines are generally more basic than alkylamines, because the nitrogen atom in arylamines is sp-hybridised','arylamines are generally less basic than alkylamines because the nitrogen lone-pair electrons are delocalised by interaction with the aromatic ring p-electron system','arylamines are generally more basic than alkylamines because the nitrogen lone-pair electrons are not delocalised by interaction with the aromatic ring p-electron system','NEW','12-399','12-269',NULL),
(270812,'chemistry','On hydrolysis of a “compound”, two compounds are obtained. One of which on treatment with sodium nitrite and hydrochloric acid gives a product which does not respond to iodoform test. The second one reduces Tollens’ reagent and Fehling’s solution. The “compound” is __________.','CH₃CH₂CH₂NC','CH₃CH₂CH₂NC + 2 H₂O  →  CH₃CH₂CH₂NH₂ + HCOOH.\nCH₃CH₂CH₂NH₂ + NaNO₂ + HCl → CH₃CH₂CH₂N₂ + Cl + H₂O → CH₃CH₂CH₂OH \n(CH₃CH₂CH₂OH does not give iodoform test). \n(HCOOH reduces Tollens’ reagent and Fehling’s solution).\nReference: (NCERT class-12) (Karnatka NEET 2013)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','CH₃CH₂CH₂NC','CH₃CH₂CH₂CN','CH₃CH₂CH₂ON=O','CH₃CH₂CH₂CON(CH₃)₂','NEW','12-393','12-263',NULL),
(270813,'chemistry','Some reactions of amines are given. Which one is not correct?','(CH₃)₂N-Ar + NaNO₂ + HCl → (CH₃)₂N-Ar-N=NCl','Aromatic tertiary amines show electrophilic substitution with nitrosonium ion at para-position of the phenyl ring which gives a green-coloured para-nitrosoamines. \nReference: (NCERT class-12) (Karnataka NEET 2013)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','(CH₃)₂N-Ar + NaNO₂ + HCl → (CH₃)₂N-Ar-N=NCl','CH₃CH₂NH₂ + HNO₂ → CH₃CH₂OH + N₂','CH₃NH₂ + C₆H₅SO₂Cl → CH₃NHSO₂C₆H₅','(CH₃)₂NH + NaNO₂ + HCl → (CH₃)₂N—N=O','NEW','12-402','12-272',NULL),
(270814,'chemistry','An organic compound (C₃H₉N) (A), when treated with nitrous acid, gave an alcohol and N₂ gas was evolved. (A) on warming with CHCl₃ and caustic potash gave (C) which on reduction gave isopropylmethylamine. Predict the structure of (A).','(CH₃)₂ CH NH₂','As A gives alcohol on reacting with nitrous acid it means that it should be a primary amine. C₃H₉N has two possible structures containing –NH₂ group. CH₃ — CH₂ — CH₂ — NH₂ or (CH₃)₂ — CH — NH₂ As it gives isopropylmethylamine therefore, it should be isopropyl amine and not n-propyl amine. \nReference: (NCERT class-12) (NEET 2012)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','(CH₃)₂ CH NH₂','CH₃CH₂ – NH – CH₃','(CH₃)₃-N','CH₃CH₂CH₂ – NH₂','NEW','12-404','12-274',NULL),
(270815,'chemistry','Which of the following will be most stable diazonium salt RN₂⁺X⁻?','C₆H₅N₂⁺X⁻','Aromatic diazonium salts are more stable because of the dispersal of the positive charge in benzene ring.\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 404; Paragraph No. 2) (NEET 2014)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','CH₃N₂⁺X⁻','C₆H₅N₂⁺X⁻','CH₃CH₂N₂⁺X⁻','C₆H₅CH₂N₂⁺X⁻','NEW','12-404','12-274',NULL),
(270816,'chemistry','A given nitrogen containing aromatic compound ‘A’ reacts with Sn/HCl, followed by HNO₂ to give an unstable compound ‘B’. ‘B’, on treatment with phenol, forms a beautiful coloured compound ‘C’ with the molecular formula C₁₂H₁₀N₂₀. The structure of compound ‘A’ is','Ar-NO₂','In the presence of Sn/HCl, Nitrogen containing aromatic compound can be reduced to primary aromatic amine that can be diazotised easily.\nThe diazonium salt produced when reacts with phenol, gives the azo dye as mentioned in the given diagram.\nReference: (NCERT class-12) (NEET-II 2016)\ndiagram(ne27109)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','Ar-NH₂','Ar-NO₂','Ar-CN','Ar-CONH₂','NEW','12-404','12-274',NULL),
(270817,'chemistry','In the following reaction, the product (A) is _______. diagram(n27107)','p-Aminobenzene','An example of azo-coupling reaction.\nReference: (NCERT class-12) (NEET 2014). diagram(ne27110)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','Ar-N=N-NH-Ar','o-Aminobenzene','m-Aminobenzene','p-Aminobenzene','NEW','12-408','12-278','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270817q.png'),
(270818,'chemistry','In the reaction diagram(n27108)','H₃PO₂ and H₂O','H₃PO₂ and H₂O can reduces the N₂⁺Cl⁻ of diazonium salt to –H. Reference: (NEET 2013)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','H₃PO₂ and H₂O','H+/H₂O','HgSO₄/H₂SO₄','Cu₂Cl₂','NEW','12-404','12-274','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270818q.png'),
(270901,'chemistry','Choose the most stable diazonium salt among the following:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                diagram(n27113)','1','Benzene ring stabilizes the diazonium salt through conjugation effect. \nHence the most stable diazonium salt is 1. \nOptions 2 and 3, and 4 are aliphatic in nature so, less stable than aromatic diazonium salts. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 404; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Exemplar based Advanced Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','1','2','3','4','NEW','12-404','12-274','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/270901q.png'),
(270902,'chemistry','Phenylamine is mainly used in the synthesis of _______.','dyes','Phenylamine forms the stable diazonium salt that further undergoes coupling reaction to give dye molecule. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 408; Summary)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Exemplar based Advanced Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','fertilizers','medicines','dyes','azide','NEW','12-408','12-278',NULL),
(270903,'chemistry','Which of the following does not give diazotisaion-coupling reaction?','Phenylmethylamine','Phenylmethylamine is an aliphatic amine.\nIt forms highly unstable diazonium salt that decomposes immediately at room temperature to form alcohol and N₂ gas.\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 404; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Exemplar based Advanced Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','p-Nitroaniline','Phenylmethylamine','Phenylamine','ortho-Aminophenol','NEW','12-404','12-274',NULL),
(270904,'chemistry','Name the reaction for the preparation of primary amine from RX and pthalimide in the presence of an acidic solution.','None of the above','Gabriel phthalimide reaction for the synthesis of primary amine from alkylhalide and phthalimide in the presence of alkali. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 394; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Exemplar based Advanced Questions',NULL,'0','mcq','Hoffmann degradation reaction','Gattermann reaction','Sandermeyer reaction','None of the above','NEW','12-394','12-264',NULL),
(271001,'chemistry','Which of the following is a tertiary amine?','Triethylamine','If three hydrogen atoms of ammonia or two hydrogen atom of R-NH₂ are replaced by another alkyl/aryl (R’) group, it will give tertiary amine.\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 390; Paragraph No. 1). Refer diagram()','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Exemplar based Advanced Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','1-methylcyclohexylamine','Triethylamine','tert-butylamine','N-methylaniline','NEW','12-390','12-260',NULL),
(271002,'chemistry','The correct IUPAC name for CH₂=CHCH₂NHCH₃ is','N-methylprop-2-en-1-amine','The correct IUPAC name will be N-methylprop-2-en-1-amine. It is a secondary amine.','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Exemplar based Advanced Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','allyl methylamine','2-amino-4-pentene','4-aminopentene','N-methylprop-2-en-1-amine','NEW','12-390','12-260',NULL),
(271003,'chemistry','Amongst the following the most basic compound in aqueous medium is','(CH₃)₂NH','Here,+I effect increases the basic character while -I and resonance effect decreases the basic character.','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Exemplar based Advanced Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','CH₃NH₂','NCCH₂NH₂','(CH₃)₂NH','Ph-NH-CH₃','NEW','12-398','12-268',NULL),
(271004,'chemistry','Which of the following is the weakest Bronsted base?Refer diagram(n27141)','a','Due to resonance in aniline the lone pair of electron are not available for donation. Thus it is the weakest Bronsted base among the given compounds.','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Exemplar based Advanced Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','a','b','c','d','NEW','12-398','12-268','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/271004q.png'),
(271005,'chemistry','Which of the following alkyl halides is best suited for this reaction through SN1 mechanism?','Ph-CH₂Br','"The reaction proceeds through nucleophillic substitution , so it depends on the stability of carbocation.\n\n Benzyl carbocation has even more stability than tertiary carbocation.\n\nThe tertiary carbocation is more stable than secondary or primary . Higher the stability of intermediate, higher is the reactivity of the reactant molecule. (Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 338; Paragraph No. 4)"','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Exemplar based Advanced Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','CH₃Br','Ph-Br','Ph-CH₂Br','C₂H₅Br','NEW','12-402','12-272',NULL),
(271006,'chemistry','Which of the following reagents would not be a good choice for reducing an aryl nitro compound into an amine?','LiAlH4 in ether','LiAlH4 in ether will not reduce nitro group to amine . All the other reagents can will convert aryl nitro compound to an amine','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Exemplar based Advanced Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','H2/Pt','LiAlH4 in ether','Fe and HCl','Sn and HCl','NEW','12-392','12-262',NULL),
(271007,'chemistry','The source of nitrogen in Gabriel synthesis of amines is','potassium phthalimide','Gabriel synthesis: "Phthalimide on treatment with ethanolic potassium hydroxide forms potassium salt of phthalimide which on heating with alkyl halide followed by alkaline hydrolysis produces the corresponding primary amine. Reference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 394; Paragraph No. 1)"','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Exemplar based Advanced Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','sodium azide','sodium nitrite','potassium cyanide','potassium phthalimide','NEW','12-394','12-264',NULL),
(271008,'chemistry','The best reagent for converting 2-phenylpropanamide into 1-phenylethanamine is','NaOH/Br2','"Hoffmann synthesis of primary amine by the reaction of amide and bromine in the presence of NaOH. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 394; Paragraph No. 2)\ndiagram(ne2760)"','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Exemplar based Advanced Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','H2/Pt','NaOH/Br2','NaBH₄/ethanol','LiAlH₄/ether','NEW','12-394','12-264',NULL),
(271009,'chemistry','Hoffman bromamide degradation reaction is shown by','ArCONH₂','Hoffmann synthesis of primary amine by the reaction of amide and bromine in the presence of NaOH. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 394; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Exemplar based Advanced Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','ArNH₂','ArCONH₂','ArNO₂','ArCH₂NH₂','NEW','12-394','12-264',NULL),
(271010,'chemistry','Methylamine reacts with HNO₂ to form','CH₃OH','Primary aliphatic amines react with nitrous acid to form aliphatic diazonium salts which being unstable, liberate nitrogen gas and alcohols. Quantitative evolution of nitrogen is used in estimation of amino acids and proteins. Reference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 401; Paragraph No. 3) Refer diagram(ne27142)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Exemplar based Advanced Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','CH₃-O-NO','CH₃-O-CH₃','CH₃OH','CH₃CHO','NEW','12-401','12-271',NULL),
(271011,'chemistry','In the nitration of benzene using a mixture of conc. H2SO4 and conc. nitric acid, the species which initiates the reaction is','NO₂⁺','The reaction will proceed as electrophillic substitution reaction. The electophile generated will be NO₂⁺. Refer diagram(ne27143)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Exemplar based Advanced Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','NO2','NO⁺','NO₂⁺','NO₂⁻','NEW','12-402','12-272',NULL),
(271012,'chemistry','The most reactive amine towards dilute hydrochloric acid is : Refer diagram(n27142)','b','Reactivity towards HCl will increase with the increase in basic strength of amine. Here (CH3)₂NH has highest basic strength, so it will be most reactive.','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Exemplar based Advanced Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','a','b','c','d','NEW','12-398','12-268','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/271012q.png'),
(271013,'chemistry','Acid anhydrides on reaction with primary amines give','amide','Acid anhydrides on reaction with primary amines will give amides.\n\n(RCO)₂O + RNH₂ → RCONH₂ + RCOOH','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Exemplar based Advanced Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','amide','imide','secondary amine','imine','NEW','12-402','12-272',NULL),
(271101,'chemistry','Which of them is not true for Gabriel phthalimide synthesis?\n\na. It is used for preparation of primary amines.\n\nb. Aromatic primary amines can\'t be prepared by this method.\n\nc. Aryl halides undergo nucleophilic substitution with the anion formed by phthalimide.','c only','Gabriel synthesis is used for the preparation of primary amines. Phthalimide on treatment with ethanolic potassium hydroxide forms potassium salt of phthalimide which on heating with alkyl halide followed by alkaline hydrolysis produces the corresponding primary amine.\n\nAromatic primary amines cannot be prepared by this method because aryl halides do not undergo nucleophilic substitution with the anion formed by phthalimide.','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Named Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','a,b','b,c','c only','b only','NEW','12-394','12-264',NULL),
(271102,'chemistry','Which of them is not true for Hoffman bromamide degradation reaction:\n\na. It is used for preparation of primary amines by treating an amide with bromine in aqueous or ethanolic solution of sodium hydroxide.\n\nb. In this degradation reaction, migration of alkyl or aryl group takes places from carbonyl carbon to alkyl group.\n\nc. the amine so formed containes one carbon more than that present in the amide.','b,c','CH₃CONH₂ + Br₂ + 4KOH → CH₃NH₂ + 2KBr + K₂CO₃ + 2H₂O (Hoffmann bromamide reaction). \n"Hoffmann synthesis of primary amine by the reaction of amide and bromine in the presence of NaOH. \n\nIn this degradation reaction, migration of an alkyl or aryl group takes place from carbonyl carbon of the amide to the nitrogen atom. The amine so formed contains one carbon less than that present in the amide.\n\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 394; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Named Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','a,b','b,c','b only','c only','NEW','12-394','12-264',NULL),
(271103,'chemistry','Which of them is not true for Carbylamine reaction?\n\na. Aliphatic primary amines on heating with chloroform and ethanolic potassium hydroxide form carbylamines which are foul smelling substance.\n\nb. Aromatic primary and secondary amines on heating with chloroform and ethanolic potassium hydroxide form isocyanides which are fould smelling substance.\n\nc. Isocyanide test is used as test for tertiary amines.','b,c','Aliphatic and aromatic primary amines on heating with chloroform and ethanolic potassium hydroxide form isocyanides or carbylamines which are foul smelling substances. Secondary and tertiary amines do not show this reaction. This reaction is known as carbylamine reaction or isocyanide test and is used as a test for primary amines. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 401; Paragraph No.1). diagram(ne2790)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Named Reactions',NULL,'3','mcq','a,b','b,c','b only','c only','NEW','12-401','12-271',NULL),
(271104,'chemistry','Which of them are true:\n\na. Sandmeyer reaction occurs in the presence of copper powder.\n\nb. Gatterman reaction occurs in the presence of Cu(I) ion.\n\nc. The yield in Sandmeyer reaction is better than Gatterman reaction.','c only','Sandmeyer reaction:\n"The Cl⁻, Br⁻ and CN⁻ nucleophiles can easily be introduced in the benzene ring in the presence of Cu(I) ion. This reaction is called Sandmeyer reaction.\n\nGatterman reaction:\nChlorine or bromine can be introduced in the benzene ring by treating the diazonium salt solution with corresponding halogen acid in the presence of copper powder.\n\n The yield in Sandmeyer reaction is better than Gatterman reaction.\n\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 405; Paragraph No. 5)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Named Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','a,b','a only','b only','c only','NEW','12-405','12-275',NULL),
(271105,'chemistry','Which of them is not true for Coupling reaction:\n\na. The reaction of diazonium salt with aniline yields p-aminoazobenzene\n\nb. p-hydroxyazobenze is an orange dye, while p-aminoazobenzene is yellow dye.\n\nc. It is an example of electrophillic addition reaction\n\nd. The azo products obtained have an extended conjugate system having both the aromatic rings joined through N-N bond.','c,d','a. The reaction of diazonium salt with aniline yields p-aminoazobenzene \n\nb. p-hydroxyazobenze is an orange dye, while p-aminoazobenzene is yellow dye.\n\nc. Coupling reaction are example of electrophillic substitution reaction\n\nd. The azo products obtained have an extended conjugate system having both the aromatic rings joined through N=N bond.\n\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 406; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> Named Reactions',NULL,'3','mcq','a,b','b,c','c,d','a,d','NEW','12-406','12-276',NULL),
(271106,'biology','The type of sex determination in other large number of insects,mammals and man is?','XY type','The investigation of a number of species to understand the mechanism of sex determination. In a number of other insects and mammals including man, XY type of sex determination is seen, Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'1','mcq','YO type','XO type','XX type','XY type','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271107,'biology','The males and female have autosomes plus (Human being)','Female-XX,Male-XY','Both males and females bear same number of autosomes, the males have autosomes plus XY, while female have autosomes plus XX. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'2','mcq','Female-XY,Male-XX','Female-XX,Male-XY','Female-XO, Male-XY','Female-XX,Male-XO','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271108,'biology','Which among the following is Incorrect according to XO type and XY type','Both types exhibits male homogametic','In XO type and XY type both the male produce two types of Gametes. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'3','mcq','In both cases males produce two different types of gametes','Gametes either with or without X-chromosome','Some gametes with X-chromosome and some with Y-chromosome','Both types exhibits male homogametic','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271109,'biology','What is male heterogamety?','When a male produce two types of Gametes','Heterogamety is when a male produce two types of Gametes. As in case of human. A male produce gametes with or without X chromosomes. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'3','mcq','When a male produce two types of Gametes','When a female produce two types of Gametes','When both male and female produce dissimilar gametes','When male produces same types of gametes','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271110,'biology','Which of them represents heterogamety?','XO type and ZW type','XO and XY type represents male heterogamety in insects and humans respectively. XO in Humans is a case of Turners syndrome,ZW is a case of Female heterogamety in birds Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'2','mcq','XO type and ZW type','XX type and Zw type','ZW type and XX type','XXY type and ZZ type','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271111,'biology','Female Heterogamety is seen in?','Birds','In Birds Female Heterogamety is seen. In which male produce same gametes but female produce two different gametes. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'1','mcq','Human','Drosophila melanogaster','Birds','Insects','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271112,'biology','What is female heterogamety?','When female produces two types of Gametes','In Birds Female produces two types of Gametes such called female heterogamety. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'2','mcq','When female produces two types of Gametes','When female produces gametes similar to that of male','When gametes of female differs with that of male','When female produces same types of gametes','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271113,'biology','The Given diagram represents (2711)','Drosophila melanogaster,male (XY heterogametic) Female (XX homogametic)','Figure 5.12 (b) NCERT 12 Page.no-86','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'3','mcq','Drosophila melanogaster,male (XX homogametic) Female (XY heterogametic)','Drosophila melanogaster,male (XY heterogametic) Female (XX homogametic)','Musca Domestica ,male (XY heterogametic) Female (XX homogametic)','Musca Domestica,male (XX homogametic) Female (XY heterogametic)','NEW','12-086','12-070','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/271113q.png'),
(271114,'biology','The Given diagram represents (2712)','Birds, Male (ZZ) and female (ZW)','Figure 5.12 (c) NCERT 12 Page. No-86','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'3','mcq','Birds, Male (ZZ) and female (ZW)','Birds, Male (ZW) and female (ZZ)','Cocks,Male (ZZ) and female (ZW)','Birds, Male and female  both (ZZ)','NEW','12-086','12-070','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/271114q.png'),
(271115,'biology','____pairs of chromosomes are same in male and female Humans','22','22 pairs of chromosomes called as autosomes are same in male and female humans. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'2','mcq','24','23','20','22','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271116,'biology','What determines characteristics of female?','A Pair of X-chromosomes','A pair of X-chromosomes are present in the female,determinant of the female characteristic. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'3','mcq','A Pair of X-chromosomes','A Pair of Y-chromosomes','A pair of XY-chromosomes','A pair of XO-chromosomes','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271117,'biology','What determines characteristics of male?','Presence of an X and Y chromosome','Presence of an X and Y chromosome determinant of the male characteristic. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'2','mcq','A Pair of X-chromosomes','A Pair of YY-chromosomes','Presence of an X and Y chromosome','Presence of XX and Y chromosomes in normal male','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271118,'biology','The constituent of one type of gamete of Sperm is','50% with X-chromosome plus autosomes','During spermatogenesis among males, two types of gametes are produced. 50 percent of the total sperm produced carry the X-chromosome and the rest 50 percent has Y-chromosome besides the autosomes. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'2','mcq','50% with X-chromosome plus autosomes','20% with Y-chromosome plus autosomes','80% with X-chromosome plus autosomes','50% X and Y chromosome plus autosomes','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271119,'biology','Ovum fertilises with a sperm carrying X-chromosome the zygote develops into a?','Female (XX)','In case the ovum fertilises with a sperm carrying X-chromosome the zygote develops into a female (XX. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'2','mcq','Female(XY)','Male(XX)','Female (XX)','Male(XY)','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271120,'biology','Fertilisation of ovum with Y-chromosome carrying sperm results into a _____ offspring','Male(XY)','The fertilisation of ovum with Y-chromosome carrying sperm results into a male offspring. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'2','mcq','Male(XY)','Female(XX)','Male(XX)','Female(XY)','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271121,'biology','The constituent of Ovum is ____','X chromosome plus autosomes','Females produce only one type of ovum with an X-chromosome.  Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'2','mcq','X chromosome plus autosomes','Y Chromosome plus allosomes','Pair of X chromosome plus autosomes','Presence of X and Y chromosomes','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271122,'biology','______determines the sex of the child.','Genetic Makeup of Sperm','ovum fertilises with a sperm carrying X-chromosome the zygote develops into a female (XX) and the fertilisation of ovum with Y-chromosome carrying sperm results into a male offspring. Thus, it is evident that it is the genetic makeup of the sperm that determines the sex of the child. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'1','mcq','Presence of X chromosome in ovum','Fertilisation of ovum and sperm','Genetic Makeup of Sperm','Types of Gametes which get fertilized','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271123,'biology','The sex determination in honey bee is based on','The number of sets of chromosomes an individual receives','In Honey bees number of sets of chromosomes a zygote receive determines the sex of individual. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'2','mcq','The type of chromosome the individual receive','The number of sets of chromosomes an individual receives','Based on XY chromosomes','XO type','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271124,'biology','Females in Honey bees are','Either Queen or Worker bee','Females in Honey bee are categorised into Queen bee and worker. Queen bee is fertile bee and Worker bee are sterile one Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'2','mcq','Either Queen or Worker bee','Either Queen or drone','Drones only','Queen only','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271125,'biology','In Honey bee offspring formed from the union of a sperm and an egg develops as a ______','Female','An offspring formed from the union of a sperm and an egg develops as a female (queen or worker). Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'3','mcq','Female','Male','Either male or female','No gender descriminaion','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271126,'biology','In Honey bees unfertilised egg develops as?','Drone','An unfertilised egg develops as a male (drone). Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'2','mcq','Drone','Queen','Worker','Both queen and worker','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271127,'biology','By which process Male in honeybee develops from unfertilised egg','Parthenogenesis','In honey bees an unfertilised egg develops as a male (drone) by means of parthenogenesis. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'3','mcq','Parthenogenesis','Mitosis','Meisosis','Binary fission','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271128,'biology','Which among the following is Incorrect in sex determination of honey bee','Males in honey bee produces sperm through meiosis','Males produce sperms by mitosis they do not have father and thus cannot have sons. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'3','mcq','Females 	are	diploid with 32 chromosomes','Males have half the number of chromosomes than that of female i.e 16','Males in honey bee produces sperm through meiosis','Males in Honey bee don\'t have fathers and Son','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271129,'biology','Identify the given diagram (2724)','Sex Determination in Honey bee','Figure 5.13 NCERT 12 Page. No-87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'2','mcq','Sex Determination in Drosophila Melanogaster','Sex Determination in mucus domestica','Sex Determination in Grasshopper','Sex Determination in Honey bee','NEW','12-087','12-071','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/271129q.png'),
(271130,'biology','Sex Determination in Honey bees is also called as','Haplodiploid sex-determination system','The females  are diploid having 32 chromosomes and males are haploid, i.e having 16 chromosomes.This is called as haplodiploid sex-determination system. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'2','mcq','Diploidtriploid Sex-determination system','Heterogamety','Parthenogenesis','Haplodiploid sex-determination system','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271131,'biology','In birds,the females are','ZW','A female bird has been designated to be with Z and W chromosomes Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'1','mcq','ZZ','ZW','ZY','XX','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271132,'biology','Individuals having homogametic sex chromosomes produces','One type of gametes','Homogametic is the condition in which Individual produce one type similar Gametes. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'2','mcq','One type of gametes','No gametes','Two types of Gametes','Only one gamete in entire life span','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271133,'biology','Mark the Incorrect pair','ZO-ZZ type birds','Sex determination in birds is ZW-ZZ type where female(ZW) is heterogamety and produce two types of Gametes. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 87','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'3','mcq','ZW-ZZ type- Ostrich','XX-XO type-Grasshopper','XX-XY type-Drosophila','ZO-ZZ type birds','NEW','12-087','12-071',NULL),
(271134,'biology','The first scientist who traced a specific nuclear structure all through spermatogenesis in a few insects was','Henking(1891)','Henking (1891) could trace a specific nuclear structure all through spermatogenesis in a few insects Reference   :NCERT PAGE 86','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Sex Determination',NULL,'2','mcq','Sterkling(1852)','Henking(1891)','Morgan(1868)','Alfreton(1754)','NEW','12-086','12-070',NULL),
(271135,'biology','What does Henking named the structures that were present only in 50% of sperms','X-body','Henking trace those structures in 50% sperm and in 50% sperm it was absent. So named it as X-body Reference   :NCERT PAGE 86','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >>Sex Determination',NULL,'3','mcq','Y- body','X-body','Z-body','XY-body','NEW','12-086','12-070',NULL),
(271136,'biology','Scientists led to the conclusion that the ‘X body’ of Henking was in fact a ______','Chromosome','Further investigations by other scientists led to the conclusion that the ‘X body’ of Henking was in fact a chromosome and that is why it was given the name X-chromosome. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 86','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >>Sex Determination',NULL,'2','mcq','Chromosome','Chromatin','Gamete','Gene','NEW','12-086','12-070',NULL),
(271137,'biology','In a large number of insects the mechanism of sex determination is of _____type.','XO type','It was also observed that in a large number of insects the mechanism of sex determination is of the XO type, i.e., all eggs bear an additional X-chromosome besides the other chromosomes. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 86 (autosomes)','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >>Sex Determination',NULL,'2','mcq','XY type','ZW-ZZ type','XO type','ABO type','NEW','12-086','12-070',NULL),
(41422,'chemistry','The molecular geometry of AB₃E type molecules:','Trigonal pyramidal','Theoretically the shape should have been tetrahedal but actually it is found to be trigonal pyramidal, this is due to lp-bp repulsion which is more than bp-bp repulsion so the angle is reduced from 107 from 109.5. \n\nAs shown in diagram\n\nReference: (NCERT chemistry Class 11; page 116; Table 4.8) diagram(ne0412)','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> VSEPR theory',NULL,'2','mcq','Bent','Trigonal pyramidal','See-saw','T-shaped','NEW','11-114','11-114',NULL),
(271201,'chemistry','The product of the following reaction is: Refer diagram(n27146)','Aniline, Aniline','Nitro compounds are reduced to amines by passing hydrogen gas in the presence of finely divided nickel, palladium or platinum and also by reduction with metals in acidic medium. Nitroalkanes can also be similarly, reduced to the corresponding alkanamines. \n\nReduction with iron scrap and HCl is preferred as FeCl2 formed gets hydrolysed to release HCl during reaction\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 392; Paragraph No. 1)\ndiagram(ne2710)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','Aniline, Phenol','Phenol, Phenol','Aniline, acetanalide','Aniline, Aniline','NEW','12-392','12-262','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/271201q.png'),
(271202,'chemistry','The final product of the following reaction is: Ammonolysis of benzyl chloride and reaction of amine so formed with two moles of CH3Cl','N,N-Dimethylphenylmethanamine','The reaction will proceed as given in the diagram(ne27150). \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 393, Example 393)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'3','mcq','Benzylamine','N-Methylphenylmethanamide','N,N-Dimethylphenylmethanamine','Ethylethanamine','NEW','12-393','12-263',NULL),
(271203,'chemistry','The reactant \'A\' can be: Refer diagram(n27147)','RCN','Nitriles on reduction with lithium aluminium hydride or catalytic hydrogenation produce primary amines. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 393; Paragraph No. 4). diagram(ne2745)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','RCN','RCONH2','RCl','Phthalimide','NEW','12-393','12-263','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/271203q.png'),
(271204,'chemistry','The product of the following reaction is: Refer diagram(n27148)','N-ethylbenzenesulphonamide','The reaction of benzenesulphonyl chloride with primary amine yields N-ethylbenzenesulphonyl amide. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 401; Paragraph No. 6)Refer diagram(ne27151)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'3','mcq','N,N-Dimethylphenylmethanamine','N-ethylbenzenesulphonamide','N,N-Dimethylphenylmethanamine','N,N-Diethylbenzenesulphonamide','NEW','12-401','12-271','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/271204q.png'),
(271205,'chemistry','The product of the following reaction is: Refer diagram(n27149)','N,N-Diethylbenzenesulphonamide','In the reaction with secondary amine, N,N-diethylbenzenesulphonamide is formed N, N-diethylbenzene sulphonamide does not contain any\nhydrogen atom attached to nitrogen atom, it is not acidic and hence insoluble in alkali. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 401; Paragraph No. 8) Refer diagram(ne27152)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'3','mcq','N,N-Dimethylphenylmethanamine','N-ethylbenzenesulphonamide','N,N-Dimethylphenylmethanamine','N,N-Diethylbenzenesulphonamide','NEW','12-401','12-271','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/271205q.png'),
(271206,'chemistry','The product of the following reaction is: Refer diagram(n27150)','2,4,6-Tribromoaniline','Aniline reacts with bromine water at room temperature to give a white precipitate of 2,4,6-tribromoaniline. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 402; Paragraph No. 4)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','o-Bromoaniline','p-Bromoaniline','2,4,6-Tribromoaniline','N-Phenylethanamide','NEW','12-402','12-272','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/271206q.png'),
(271207,'chemistry','The product of the following reaction is: Refer diagram(n27151)','N-Phenylethanamide','Aniline is a highly reactive compound due to the presence of NH₂ group that activates it towards aromatic electrophilic substitution reaction. \nIts bromination give trisubstituted product. Hence, the activating effect of NH₂ can be controlled by protecting it by acetylation. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 402; Paragraph No. 3) Refer diagram(ne27153)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','o-Bromoaniline','p-Bromoaniline','2,4,6-Tribromoaniline','N-Phenylethanamide','NEW','12-402','12-272','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/271207q.png'),
(271208,'chemistry','The product of the following reaction is: Refer diagram(n27152)\n\na. o-Nitroaniline\nb. p-Nitroaniline\nc. m-Nitroaniline\nd. p-Nitroacetanilide','a,b,c','Direct nitration of aniline yields tarry oxidation products in addition to the nitro derivatives. Moreover, in the strongly acidic medium, aniline is protonated to form the anilinium ion which is meta directing. That is why besides the ortho and para derivatives, significant amount of meta derivative is also formed. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 403; Paragraph No. 2). Refer diagram(ne27154)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','a,b','b,c','a,b,c','a,c,d','NEW','12-403','12-273','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/271208q.png'),
(271209,'chemistry','The product of the following reaction is: Refer diagram(n27153)\n\na. o-Sulphoaniline\nb. p-Sulphoaniline\nc. Sulphanilic acid\nd. Anilinium hydrogensulphate','d only','Aniline reacts with concentrated sulphuric acid to form anilinium hydrogensulphate which on heating with sulphuric acid at 453-473 K produces p-aminobenzene sulphonic acid, commonly known as sulphanilic acid, as the major product. \nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 403; Paragraph No. 4). Refer diagram(ne27155)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','a','b,c','a,b,c','d only','NEW','12-403','12-273','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/271209q.png'),
(271210,'chemistry','Which of them will not be formed during the reaction. Refer diagram(n27154)','BF₃','When arenediazonium chloride is treated with floruoboric acid and heat , aryl floride is formed.\n\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 405; Paragraph No. 4)" Refer diagram(ne27156)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','Ar-F','BF₃','N₂','F₂','NEW','12-405','12-275','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/271210q.png'),
(271211,'chemistry','The product \'B\' in the given reaction diagram(n27155) will be:','Nitrobenzene','When diazonium flouroborate is heated with aqueous sodium nitrite solution in the presence of Copper, the diazonium goup is replaced by -NO2 group.\n\nReference: (NCERT class-12; Page No. 406; Paragraph No. 3)" Refer diagram(ne27157)','Organic Chemistry >> Organic Compounds Containing Nitrogen >> NCERT Reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','p-Hydroxyazobenzen','Nitrobenzene','p-nitroaniline','Phenol','NEW','12-406','12-276','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/271211q.png'),
