(271218,'biology','Loss (deletions) or gain (insertion/duplication) of a segment of DNA results in','Alteration in chromosomes','One DNA helix runs continuously from one end to the other in each chromatid,in a highly supercoiled form.Therefore loss (deletions) or gain (insertion/duplication) of a segment of DNA,result in alteration in chromosomes. Reference   :NCERT PAGE 88','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Mutation and Pedigree Analysis',NULL,'3','mcq','Alteration in chromatin material','Alteration in chromosomes','Changes in protein coding genes','No change in chromosomes','NEW','12-088','12-072',NULL),
