(271755,'biology','Which one of the following cannot be explained on the basis of Mendel\'s Law of Dominance?','Alleles do not show any blending and both the 3. characters recover as such in the F2 generation.','NCERT XII, Page 75','Genetics and Evolution >> Principles Of Inheritance And Variation >> Previous Year Questions 3',NULL,'2','mcq','The discrete unit controlling a particular character is called a factor.','Out of one pair of factors, one is dominant, and the other recessive.','Alleles do not show any blending and both the 3. characters recover as such in the F2 generation.','Factors occurs in pair','NEW','12-075','12-059',NULL),
