(2000046414,'physics','The angular momentum of an electron in a hydrogen atom is proportional to  (where $r$ is the radius of the orbit of electron)','C','Angular momentum of an electron in a hydrogen atom.<br>$L=\\dfrac{n h}{2 \\pi}$<br>$ \\Rightarrow L \\propto n \\propto \\sqrt r \\left( {\\because r \\propto {n^2} \\Rightarrow n \\propto \\sqrt r } \\right)\\quad \\quad (1)$','Bohr Model of the Hydrogen Atom ','Atoms','Medium',NULL,'$\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{r}}$','$\\dfrac{1}{r}$','$\\sqrt{r}$','$r$',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
