(350801,'biology','Some organisms are able to respond through certain physiological adjustments while others do so behaviourally (migrating temporarily to a less stressful habitat). These responses are also actually, their __________','Adaptations','Some organisms are able to respond through certain physiological adjustments while others do so behaviourally (migrating temporarily to a less stressful habitat). These responses are also actually, their adaptations.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:225, paragraph no:4)','Ecology >> Organisms And Populations >> Adaptations',NULL,'2','fillup','Ad,ap,ta,ti,on,s',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-225',NULL,NULL),
(350802,'biology','What is the attribute of the organism that enables the organism to survive and reproduce in its habitat.','Adaptations','Adaptation is any attribute of the organism (morphological, physiological, behavioural) that enables the organism to survive and reproduce in its habitat.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:225, paragraph no:4)','Ecology >> Organisms And Populations >> Adaptations',NULL,'2','mcq','Responses','Adaptations','Exponential growth','Homeostasis','NEW','12-225',NULL,NULL),
(350803,'biology','Which among the following is type of adaptations?\n \n i) behavioural\n \n ii) physiological\n \n iii) morphological\n \n iv) genetical','i, ii, and iii','Adaptation is any attribute of the organism (morphological, physiological, behavioural) that enables the organism to survive and reproduce in its habitat.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:225, paragraph no:4)','Ecology >> Organisms And Populations >> Adaptations',NULL,'2','mcq','i and ii','ii and iv','i, ii, and iii','iii only','NEW','12-225',NULL,NULL),
(350804,'biology','Kangaroo rat has a unique adaptation, that is it','Does not need to drink water','One behavior that makes kangaroo rats so unique is that they never drink water. They are able to extract all the water they need from the seeds and grasses that they eat. Their urine is extremely concentrated and they produce very dry feces.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:225, paragraph no:4)','Ecology >> Organisms And Populations >> Adaptations',NULL,'2','mcq','Have a greener cacti diet','Avoids eating fats by selective absorption','Does not need to drink water','Is heat in-sensitive','NEW','12-225',NULL,NULL),
(350805,'biology','Kangaroo rat in North American deserts is capable of meeting all its water requirements through its','Internal fat oxidation','Kangaroo rat in North American deserts is capable of meeting all its water requirements through its internal fat oxidation (in which water is a by product).(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:225, paragraph no:4)','Ecology >> Organisms And Populations >> Adaptations',NULL,'2','fillup','In,ter,nal ,fa,t ox,id,at,io,n',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-225',NULL,NULL),
