(2000110747,'physics','If voltage across a bulb rated $220\\,V,100\\,W$ drops by $2.5 \\%$ of its rated value, the percentage of the rated value by which the power would decrease is','A','<br>$P = \\frac{{{V^2}}}{R}$<br>$ \\Rightarrow \\quad \\frac{{\\Delta P}}{P} = 2\\frac{{\\Delta \\,V}}{{\\,V}} = 2 \\times ( - 2.5\\% ) =  - 5\\% $','Electrical Energy and Power Through a Resistor','Current Electricity','Hard',NULL,'$5 \\%$','$10 \\%$','$20 \\%$','$2.5 \\%$',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
