(350813,'biology','_________ rule states that mammals from colder climates generally have shorter ears and limbs to minimise heat loss.','Allen\'s','Mammals from colder climates generally have shorter ears and limbs to minimise heat loss. This is called the Allen’s Rule.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:226, paragraph no:1)','Ecology >> Organisms And Populations >> Adaptations',NULL,'2','mcq','Berger\'s','Allen\'s','Borg\'s','Powell\'s','NEW','12-226',NULL,NULL),
(350814,'biology','In the polar sea aquatic mammals like seals have a thick layer of fat known as ______________.','Blubber','In the polar seas aquatic mammals like seals have a thick layer of fat ,blubber below their skin that acts as an insulator and reduces loss of body heat.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:226, paragraph no:1)','Ecology >> Organisms And Populations >> Adaptations',NULL,'2','mcq','Adipose','Blubber','Dermis','Brown fat','NEW','12-226',NULL,NULL),
