(350816,'biology','Some organisms possess adaptations that are ________ which allow them to respond quickly to a stressful situation.','Physiological','Some organisms possess adaptations that are physiological which allow them to respond quickly to a stressful situation.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:226, paragraph no:2)','Ecology >> Organisms And Populations >> Adaptations',NULL,'2','mcq','Behavioural','Physiological','Morphological','Ecological','NEW','12-226',NULL,NULL),
(350817,'biology','Altitude sickness is related to?','Low atmospheric pressure','Tourists visiting high altitude areas such as Rohtang Pass or Mansarovar, experience altitude sickness. Its symptoms include nausea, fatigue and heart palpitations. This is because in the low atmospheric pressure of high altitudes, the body does not get enough oxygen. But, gradually we get acclimatized and stop experiencing altitude sickness. The body compensates low O₂ availability by increasing red blood cell production, decreasing the binding affinity of haemoglobin and by increasing breathing rate.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:226, paragraph no:2)','Ecology >> Organisms And Populations >> Adaptations',NULL,'2','mcq','Temperature','Low atmospheric pressure','Concentration','High atmospheric pressure','NEW','12-226',NULL,NULL),
(350818,'biology','Symptoms of altitude sickness include\n \n i) nausea\n \n ii) fatigue\n \n iii) heart palpitations\n \n iv) weight gain','i, ii, and iii','Symptoms of altitude sickness include nausea,fatigue and heart palpitations.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:226, paragraph no:2)','Ecology >> Organisms And Populations >> Adaptations',NULL,'2','mcq','i and ii','ii and iv','i, ii, and iii','i and iv','NEW','12-226',NULL,NULL),
(350819,'biology','People who have migrated from the planes to an area adjoining Rohtang Pass about six months back','Have more RBCs and their haemoglobin has a lower binding affinity to oxygen','Tourists visiting high altitude areas such as Rohtang Pass or Mansarovar, experience altitude sickness. Its symptoms include nausea, fatigue and heart palpitations. This is because in the low atmospheric pressure of high altitudes, the body does not get enough oxygen. But, gradually we get acclimatized and stop experiencing altitude sickness. The body compensates low O₂ availability by increasing red blood cell production, decreasing the binding affinity of haemoglobin and by increasing breathing rate.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:226, paragraph no:2)','Ecology >> Organisms And Populations >> Adaptations',NULL,'2','mcq','Have more RBCs and their haemoglobin has a lower binding affinity to oxygen','Are not physically fit to play games like football','suffer from altitude sickness with symptoms like nausea, fatigue, etc for lifetime','Have the usual RBC count but their haemoglobin has very high binding affinity to oxygen','NEW','12-226',NULL,NULL),
(350820,'biology','How the body compensates low O₂ availability to stop experiencing altitude sickness?','Decreasing the binding affinity of hemoglobin','The body compensates low O₂ availability by increasing red blood cell production, decreasing the binding affinity of hemoglobin and by increasing breathing rate.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:226, paragraph no:2)','Ecology >> Organisms And Populations >> Adaptations',NULL,'2','mcq','By decreasing red blood cell production','Decreasing the binding affinity of hemoglobin','By decreasing breathing rate.','Increasing the binding affinity of hemoglobin','NEW','12-226',NULL,NULL),
