(350822,'biology','A particular type of microbe that can flourish in hot springs and deep sea hydrothermal vents where temperatures far exceed 100 °C?','Archaebacteria','Microbes like archaebacteria, that flourish in hot springs and deep sea hydrothermal vents where temperatures far exceed 100 °C.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:226, paragraph no:3)','Ecology >> Organisms And Populations >> Adaptations',NULL,'2','mcq','Protozoa','Archaebacteria','Cyanobacteria','Diatoms','NEW','12-226',NULL,NULL),
(350823,'biology','Pick up the false one?','Many fish thrive in Antarctic waters where the temperature is always 100 °C.','Many fish thrive in Antarctic waters where the temperature is always below zero. A large variety of marine invertebrates and fish live at great depths in the ocean where the pressure could be >100 times the normal atmospheric pressure that we experience.Organisms living in such extreme environments show a fascinating array of biochemical adaptations. Some organisms show behavioural responses to cope up with variations in their environment.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:226, paragraph no:4,5)','Ecology >> Organisms And Populations >> Adaptations',NULL,'2','mcq','Many fish thrive in Antarctic waters where the temperature is always 100 °C.','A large variety of marine invertebrates and fish live at great depths in the ocean where the pressure could be >100 times the normal atmospheric pressure that we experience.','Organisms living in such extreme environments show a fascinating array of biochemical adaptations.','Some organisms show behavioural responses to cope up with variations in their environment.','NEW','12-226',NULL,NULL),
