(350901,'biology','Majority of individuals live in groups in a well defined geographical area, share or compete for similar resources, potentially interbreed and thus constitute a ___________.','Population','In nature, we rarely find isolated, single individuals of any species; majority of them live in groups in a well defined geographical area, share or compete for similar resources, potentially interbreed and thus constitute a population.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 12: page no:226, paragraph no:7)','Ecology >> Organisms And Populations >> Population Attributes',NULL,'2','fillup','Po,pu,la,ti,on',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-226','12-191',NULL),
