(100801,'chemistry','Which oxidation state is most common for group 2 elements?','2+','The dipositive oxidation state (2+) is the predominant valence of Group 2 elements.\n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 309; Paragraph 10.7)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements - General Characteristics',NULL,'1','mcq','1+','2+','3+','4+','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
