(101013,'chemistry','To which of the following, water is added, to form Calcium hydroxide?','CaO','Calcium hydroxide is prepared by adding water to quick lime, CaO.\n \n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 311; Paragraph 10.9)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements - Some Important Compounds of Calcium',NULL,'1','mcq','CaCO₃','CaHCO₃','CaO','Ca(OCl)','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(101014,'chemistry','What is the aqueous solution of Calcium hydroxide called?','Lime water','The aqueous solution is known as lime water and a suspension of slaked lime in water is known as milk of lime. \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 311; Paragraph 10.9)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements - Some Important Compounds of Calcium',NULL,'1','mcq','Lime water','Milk of lime','Soda lime','Quick lime','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(101015,'chemistry','What is the suspension of Calcium hydroxide called?','Milk of lime','The aqueous solution is known as lime water and a suspension of slaked lime in water is known as milk of lime. \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 311; Paragraph 10.9)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements - Some Important Compounds of Calcium',NULL,'1','mcq','Milk of lime','Soda lime','Lime water','Quick lime','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(101016,'chemistry','Why does lime water turns milky on passing Carbon dioxide through it?','Because of formation of Calcium carbonate.','When carbon dioxide is passed through lime water it turns milky due to the formation of Calcium carbonate. \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 311; Paragraph 10.9)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements - Some Important Compounds of Calcium',NULL,'1','mcq','Because of formation of Calcium bicarbonate.','Because of precipitation of Calcium hydroxide','Because of formation of Calcium oxide','Because of formation of Calcium carbonate.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(101017,'chemistry','What happens on passing excess of Carbon dioxide through lime water?','The precipitate dissolves to form Calcium hydrogencarbonate.','On passing excess of carbon dioxide, the precipitate dissolves to form Calcium hydrogencarbonate. \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 311; Paragraph 10.9)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements - Some Important Compounds of Calcium',NULL,'1','mcq','The precipitate dissolves to form Calcium carbonate.','The precipitate dissolves to form Calcium hydroxide.','The precipitate dissolves to form Calcium hydrogencarbonate.','Gas bubbles of Carbon dioxide are observed.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
