(101019,'chemistry','2Ca(OH)₂ + Cl₂  →  CaCl₂ + ______ + 2H₂O','Ca(OCl)₂','2Ca(OH)₂ + Cl₂  →  CaCl₂ + Ca(OCl)₂ + 2H₂O \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 311; Paragraph 10.9)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements - Some Important Compounds of Calcium',NULL,'1','mcq','Ca(OCl)₂','Ca(OCl)','Ca(OCl)₃','Ca(OCl)₄','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(101020,'chemistry','How many from the given are not the uses of Ca(OH)₂?\n\n1) manufacture of sodium carbonate from caustic soda.\n\n2) purifies sugar.\n\n3) preparation of mortar.\n\n4) used in tanning industries.\n\n5) used in preparation of bleaching powder. \n\n6) manufacture of dyestuffs.\n\n7) important primary material for manufacturing cement.','3','The following arethe uses of Ca(OH)₂ \n\n(i) It is used in the preparation of mortar, a building material. \n\n(ii) It is used in white wash due to its disinfectant nature. \n\n(iii) It is used in glass making, in tanning industry, for the preparation of bleaching powder and for purification of sugar. \n\nRest are the uses of CaO\n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 311; Paragraph 10.9)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements - Some Important Compounds of Calcium',NULL,'3','mcq','4','5','6','3','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(101021,'chemistry','How many from the given are the uses of Ca(OH)₂ ?\n\n1) manufacture of sodium carbonate from caustic soda.\n\n2) purifies sugar.\n\n3) preparation of mortar.\n\n4) used in tanning industries.\n\n5) used in preparation of bleaching powder.\n\n6) manufacture of dyestuffs.\n\n7) important primary material for manufacturing cement.','4','The following arethe uses of Ca(OH)₂ \n\n(i) It is used in the preparation of mortar, a building material. \n\n(ii) It is used in white wash due to its disinfectant nature. \n\n(iii) It is used in glass making, in tanning industry, for the preparation of bleaching powder and for purification of sugar. \n\nRest are the uses of CaO\n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 311; Paragraph 10.9)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements - Some Important Compounds of Calcium',NULL,'3','mcq','4','5','6','7','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
