(101025,'chemistry','CaCO₃ reacts with ______ to liberate carbon dioxide.','dilute acid','CaCO₃ reacts with dilute acid to liberate carbon dioxide. \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 311; Paragraph 10.9)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements - Some Important Compounds of Calcium',NULL,'2','mcq','strong acid','strong base','dilute acid','dilute base','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(101026,'chemistry','How many among following are not the uses of CaCO₃?\n1) manufacture of sodium carbonate from caustic soda.\n2) purifies sugar\n3) preparation of mortar.\n4) used in tanning industries.\n5) constituent of chewing gum.\n6) filler in cosmetics.\n7) manufacturing of high quality paper .\n8) flux in extraction of iron','4','The following are the uses of CaCO₃ -\nIt is used as a building material in the form of marble and in the manufacture of quick lime. Calcium carbonate along with magnesium carbonate is used as a flux in the extraction of metals such as iron. Specially precipitated CaCO3 is extensively used in the manufacture of high quality paper. It is also used as an antacid, mild abrasive in tooth paste, a constituent of chewing gum, and a filler in cosmetics.\n1 and 2 are the uses of Calcium oxide.\n2, 3 and 4 are the uses of Calcium hydroxide.\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 311; Paragraph 10.9)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements - Some Important Compounds of Calcium',NULL,'3','mcq','4','5','6','7','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(101027,'chemistry','How many among following are the uses of CaCO₃?\n\n1) manufacture of sodium carbonate from caustic soda.\n\n2) purifies sugar.\n\n3) preparation of mortar.\n\n4) used in tanning industries.\n\n5) constituent of chewing gum.\n\n6) filler in cosmetics.\n\n7) manufacturing of high quality paper.\n\n8) flux in extraction of iron','4','The following are the uses of CaCO₃ -\n\nIt is used as a building material in the form of marble and in the manufacture of quick lime. \n\nCalcium carbonate along with magnesium carbonate is used as a flux in the extraction of metals such as iron. \n\nSpecially precipitated CaCO3 is extensively used in the manufacture of high quality paper. \n\nIt is also used as an antacid, mild abrasive in tooth paste, a constituent of chewing gum, and a filler in cosmetics.\n\n1 and 2 are the uses of Calcium oxide.\n\n2, 3 and 4 are the uses of Calcium hydroxide.\n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 311; Paragraph 10.9)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements - Some Important Compounds of Calcium',NULL,'3','mcq','4','5','6','7','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
