(101032,'chemistry','How many among following are not the uses of plaster of paris? \n\n1) manufacture of sodium carbonate from caustic soda.\n\n2) purifies sugar.\n\n3) preparation of mortar.\n\n4) used in tanning industries.\n\n5) constituent of chewing gum.\n\n6) filler in cosmetics.\n\n7) manufacturing of high quality paper.\n\n8) flux in extraction of iron.\n\n9) immobilising organ.\n\n10) dentistry.\n\n11) ornamental work','8','The following are the uses of plaster of paris -\n\nThe largest use of Plaster of Paris is in the building industry as well as plasters. \n\nIt is used for immoblising the affected part of organ where there is a bone fracture or sprain. \n\nIt is also employed in dentistry, in ornamental work and for making casts of statues and busts. \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 312; Paragraph 10.9)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements - Some Important Compounds of Calcium',NULL,'3','mcq','6','7','8','9','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
