(101049,'chemistry','Assertion : When mixed with water, the setting of cement takes place to give a hard mass.\n \nReason : The hydration of the molecules of the constituents and their rearrangement occurs.\n\nChoose the correct option.','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','When mixed with water, the setting of cement takes place to give a hard mass. \n\nThis is due to the hydration of the molecules of the constituents and their rearrangement. \n\nThus, both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion. \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 312; Paragraph 10.9)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements - Some Important Compounds of Calcium',NULL,'3','mcq','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','The Assertion and the Reason are correct but the Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion','The statement of the Reason is false but the Assertion is true','Both the statements are false','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(101050,'chemistry','What is the purpose of adding Gypsum to Cement?','To slow down the process of setting of the cement so that it gets sufficiently hardened.','The purpose of adding gypsum is only to slow down the process of setting of the cement so that it gets sufficiently hardened. \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 312; Paragraph 10.9)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements - Some Important Compounds of Calcium',NULL,'1','mcq','To slow down the process of setting of the cement so that it gets sufficiently soft.','To slow down the process of setting of the cement so that it gets sufficiently hardened.','To make the process of setting of the cement fast so that it gets sufficiently hardened.','To make the process of setting of the cement fast so that it gets sufficiently soft.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
