(130217,'biology','How many carbons are present in the glucose formed at the end of photosynthesis','Six','Glucose formed at the end of photosynthesis contains a six carbon skeleton. (Reference  : NCERT Class 11th, Pg. 208)','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'1','mcq','Seven','Six','Five','Eight','NEW','11-208','11-135',NULL),
(130218,'biology','On which organism Cornelius van Niel based his study of photosynthesis','Purple and green bacteria','Cornelius van Niel (1897-1985) based his study of photosynthesis on purple and green bacteria. (Reference  : NCERT Class 11th, Pg. 208)','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'1','mcq','Blue and green bacteria','Purple and green bacteria','Blue and purple bacteria','Green and yellow bacteria','NEW','11-208','11-135',NULL),
(130219,'biology','According to Cornelius van Niel photosynthesis is a','Light dependent reaction','According to Cornelius van Niel photosynthesis is light dependent reaction in which hydrogen forms an oxidisable compound that reduces  CO₂  to form carbohydrates. (Reference  : NCERT Class 11th, Pg. 208)','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'1','mcq','Light independent reaction','Light dependent reaction','Dark dependent reaction','Dark independent reaction','NEW','11-208','11-135',NULL),
(130220,'biology','In green plants during photosynthesis which compound is hydrogen donor','H₂O','In green plants H₂O acts as hydrogen donor which is later oxidised to O₂. (Reference  : NCERT Class 11th, Pg. 208)','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'1','mcq','H₃O⁺','H₂O','H⁺','OH⁻','NEW','11-208','11-135',NULL),
(130221,'biology','In purple and green sulphur bacteria which of the following is hydrogen donor','H₂S','In purple and green sulphur bacteria H₂S is the hydrogen donor and sulphur is the oxidation product. (Reference  : NCERT Class 11th, Pg. 208)\n\nPurple and green sulfur bacteria are photosynthetic bacteria that use bacteriochlorophyll pigments to capture light energy and transfer it to reaction centers, where electron transfer reactions occur. During these reactions, H2S (hydrogen sulfide) acts as the hydrogen donor and is oxidized to elemental sulfur or sulfate, depending on the specific type of bacteria.','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'1','mcq','H₂O','H₂O₂','H₂S','HCl','NEW','11-208','11-135',NULL),
(130222,'biology','In case of H₂S as hydrogen donor which compound acts as the product of oxidation','Either Sulphur or Sulphate','When H₂S is used as hydrogen donor the oxidized product is either sulphur or sulphate instead of O₂ depending upon the species. (Reference  : NCERT Class 11th, Pg. 208)','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'1','mcq','Sulphur','Sulphur ion','Sulphate','Either Sulphur or Sulphate','NEW','11-208','11-135',NULL),
(130223,'biology','From Cornelius van Niel findings it was inferred that O₂ comes from','H₂O','It was concluded through his findings that O₂ is evolved by green plants and comes from H₂O and not CO₂. (Reference  : NCERT Class 11th, Pg. 208)','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'1','mcq','H₂O','CO₂','H₂O₂','OH⁻','NEW','11-208','11-135',NULL),
(130224,'biology','O₂ is released from water was found through ___________ techniques','Radio isotope','The radio isotope techniques were used to find that O₂ comes from water. (Reference  : NCERT Class 11th, Pg. 208)','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'1','mcq','Radiometry','Spectroscopy','Radio isotope','Isotone','NEW','11-208','11-135',NULL),
(130225,'biology','Which cells have large number of chloroplasts','Mesophyll cells','Mesophyll cells present within the leaves have large number of chloroplasts. (Reference  : NCERT Class 11th, Pg. 209)','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'1','mcq','Parenchyma cells','Mesophyll cells','Sclerenchyma cells','Palisade','NEW','11-209','11-136',NULL),
(130226,'biology','______ are aligned along the walls of mesophyll cells','Chloroplast','The pigment containing cell organelles called chloroplasts are aligned across the walls of mesophyll cells of leaves','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'1','mcq','Chloroplast','Mitochondria','Lysosomes','Mesosomes','NEW','11-209','11-136',NULL),
(130227,'biology','Chloroplasts are aligned with the walls of mesophyll cells provide them with optimum quality of','Incident light','The incident light directly reaches the chloroplasts aligned along the walls of mesophyll. (Reference  : NCERT Class 11th, Pg. 209)','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'1','mcq','Watering the plants','Soil','Incident light','Air','NEW','11-209','11-136',NULL),
(130228,'biology','The membranous system within the chloroplast consists of','Grana and stroma lamellae','Within the chloroplast there is membranous system consisting of grana, the stroma lamellae, and the matrix stroma. \nWhat the NCERT states is, in the chloroplast there are 2 systems, the membranous system and the matrix, The membranous system is made up of grana and stroma lamellae, while the matrix is the stroma\n(Reference : NCERT Class 11, Pg. 209)','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'1','mcq','Grana and stroma lamellae','Stroma lamellae only','Matrix and stroma','Grana, stroma and Matrix','NEW','11-209','11-136',NULL),
(130229,'biology','What is the function membranous system in chloroplast','Synthesizes NADPH, Traps light, Synthesize ATP','The membranous system in chloroplast traps light, synthesizes ATP and NADPH. (Reference  : NCERT Class 11th, Pg. 209)','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'2','mcq','Traps light and synthesize glucose','Synthesizes ATP, NADP','Synthesizes NADPH, Traps light, Synthesize ATP','Synthesizes ATP, NADPH','NEW','11-209','11-136',NULL),
(130230,'biology','In stroma the enzymatic reactions synthesize sugar as the building block of','Starch','Enzymatic reactions occur in the stroma of chloroplast to produce sugar which in turn forms starch. (Reference  : NCERT Class 11th, Pg. 209)','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'1','mcq','Cellulose','Sugar','Starch','Glucose','NEW','11-209','11-136',NULL),
(130231,'biology','The light driven set of reactions in photosynthesis are called','Light reactions','The former set of reactions driven by light are called light reactions. (Reference  : NCERT Class 11th, Pg. 209)','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'1','mcq','Dark reactions','Light reactions','Photosynthesis-I','Both a and b','NEW','11-209','11-136',NULL),
(130232,'biology','Dark reactions are dependent on','ATP and NADPH','Dark reactions do not depend upon direct light but on the products of light reactions which are ATP and NADPH. (Reference  : NCERT Class 11th, Pg. 209)','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'1','mcq','ATP and NADPH','Light','ADP and NADH','Water and ATP','NEW','11-209','11-136',NULL),
(130233,'biology','Cornelius van Niel was a','Microbiologist','A milestone contribution to the understanding of photosynthesis was that made by a microbiologist, Cornelius van Niel (Reference  : NCERT Class 11th Pg. 208)','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'1','mcq','Microbiologist','Zoologist','Pathologist','Botanist','NEW','11-209','11-136',NULL),
(130234,'biology','What does chloroplast do to receive the optimum light during photosynthesis','Change their alignment with respect to mesophyll wall','Usually the chloroplasts align themselves along the walls of the mesophyll cells, such that they get the optimum quantity of the incident light. (Reference  : NCERT Class 11th Pg. 209)','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'2','mcq','Increase their number','Absorb the light to store it','Change their alignment with respect to mesophyll wall','Change the alignment of mesophylls','NEW','11-209','11-136',NULL),
(130235,'biology','First action spectrum was described by','Engelman','T.W Engelmann (1843 – 1909) using a prism he split light into its spectral components and then illuminated a green alga, Cladophora, placed in a suspension of aerobic bacteria.','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'1','mcq','Julius Von Sachs','Ingenhousz','Engelman','Englishman','NEW','11-208','11-135',NULL),
(130236,'biology','Organism used in describing first action spectra','Green Algae','T.W Engelmann (1843 – 1909) using a prism he split light into its spectral components and then illuminated a green alga, Cladophora, placed in a suspension of aerobic bacteria.','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'1','mcq','Sulphur bacteria','Green Algae','Bacteria','Aquatic plant','NEW','11-208','11-135',NULL),
(130237,'biology','Photosynthesis is essentially a light dependent reaction as demonstrated by using','Purple and green bacteria','Cornelius van Niel (1897-1985), who, based on his studies of purple and green bacteria, demonstrated that photosynthesis is essentially a light-dependent reaction in which hydrogen from a suitable oxidisable compound reduces  CO₂  to carbohydrates.','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'1','mcq','Purple bacteria','Green Algae','Purple and green bacteria','Phosphate solubilizing bacteria','NEW','11-208','11-135',NULL),
(130238,'biology','Choose the correct option regarding the experiment of Julius von Sachs-\n\n i) Chlorophyll is located in special bodies. \n\nii) Photosynthesis is light independent. \n\niii) Glucose is produced in green plants when they grow.','i and iii','Julius von Sachs provided evidence for production of glucose when plants grow. Glucose is usually stored as starch. His later studies showed that the green substance in plants (chlorophyll as we know it now) is located in special bodies (later called chloroplasts) within plant cells. He found that the green parts in plants is where glucose is made, and that the glucose is usually stored as starch','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'2','mcq','i and ii','ii only','iii only','i and iii','NEW','11-208','11-135',NULL),
(130239,'biology','Choose the correct statement regarding photosynthesis','H₂O is oxidized to oxygen','CO₂  + H₂O = [CH₂O] +oxygen, H₂O Is oxidized to oxygen. NCERT Class 11th, Pg. 208.','Plant Physiology >> Photosynthesis in higher plants >> Early Experiments',NULL,'2','mcq','CO₂  is oxidised to sugar','H₂O is oxidized to oxygen','CO₂  reduces H₂O','H₂O is reduced','NEW','11-208','11-135',NULL),
