(220402,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion(A) and reason(R)\nAssertion : All combustion reactions, which make use of elemental dioxygen, as well as other reactions involving elements other than dioxygen, are redox reactions. Reason : C(s) + O₂ (g) CO₂(g) is a redox reaction','The Assertion and the Reason are correct but the Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion','All combustion reactions, which make use of elemental dioxygen, as well as other reactions involving elements other than dioxygen, are redox reactions. (Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 270; Paragraph 8.3.1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Redox Reactions >> Types of Redox Reactions',NULL,'3','mcq','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','The Assertion and the Reason are correct but the Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion','The statement of the Assertion is false but the Reason is true','Both the statements are false','NEW','11-270','11-242',NULL),
(241810,'biology','Assertion: The vegetative cell of the pollen grain is small in size.\n\nReason: It is spindle shaped and floats around.','Both the Assertion and Reason are incorrect','The vegetative cell is bigger, has abundant food reserve and a large irregularly shaped nucleus. The generative cell is small and floats in the cytoplasm of the vegetative cell. It is spindle shaped with dense cytoplasm and a nucleus. (Reference  : NCERT, page 23, paragraph 2).','Reproduction >> Sexual Reproduction in Flowering Plants >> Assertion Reason and Multiple statement questions part 1',NULL,'3','mcq','Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Both Assertion and Reason are correct, but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect','Both the Assertion and Reason are incorrect','NEW','12-023',NULL,NULL),
