(220408,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion(A) and reason(R)\nAssertion : CaCO3 (s) CaO(s) + CO2(g) Reason : All decomposition reactions are not redox reactions','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','In a displacement reaction, an ion (or an atom) in a compound is replaced by an ion (or an atom) of another element. (Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 270; Paragraph 8.3.1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Redox Reactions >> Types of Redox Reactions',NULL,'3','mcq','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','The Assertion and the Reason are correct but the Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion','The statement of the Assertion is false but the Reason is true','Both the statements are false','NEW','11-270','11-242',NULL),
(220409,'chemistry','Assertion : A metal in a compound can be displaced by another metal in the uncombined state. Reason : Metal displacement reactions find many applications in metallurgical processes in which pure metals are obtained from their compounds in ores.','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','In a displacement reaction, an ion (or an atom) in a compound is replaced by an ion (or an atom) of another element. (Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 270; Paragraph 8.3.1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Redox Reactions >> Types of Redox Reactions',NULL,'3','mcq','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','The Assertion and the Reason are correct but the Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion','The statement of the Assertion is false but the Reason is true','Both the statements are false','NEW','11-270','11-242',NULL),
