(220505,'chemistry','Mark the correct statement.','Idea of fractional oxidation number is unconvincing, because electrons are never shared/transferred in fraction.','Idea of fractional oxidation number is unconvincing to us, because electrons are never shared/transferred in fraction. Actually this fractional oxidation state is the average oxidation state of the element under examination and the structural parameters reveal that the element for whom fractional oxidation state is realised is present in different oxidation states. (Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 273; The Paradox of Fractional Oxidation Number)','Inorganic chemistry >> Redox Reactions >> Paradox of Fractional Oxidation number',NULL,'2','mcq','Idea of fractional oxidation number is obvious, because electrons can be shared/transferred in fraction.','Idea of fractional oxidation number is unconvincing, because electrons are never shared/transferred in fraction.','Idea of fractional oxidation number is unconvincing, because electrons can be shared/transferred in fraction.','Idea of fractional oxidation number is obvious, because electrons can never be shared/transferred in fraction.','NEW','11-273','11-245',NULL),
(220506,'chemistry','Mark the incorrect statement.','Oxidation state of O in O₂⁺ is 0.','We may thus, in general, conclude that the idea of fractional oxidation state should be taken with care and the reality is revealed by the structures only. Further, whenever we come across with fractional oxidation state of any particular element in any species, we must understand that this is the average oxidation number only. In reality (revealed by structures only), the element in that particular species is present in more than one whole number oxidation states.\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 273; The Paradox of Fractional Oxidation Number)','Inorganic chemistry >> Redox Reactions >> Paradox of Fractional Oxidation number',NULL,'2','mcq','Idea of fractional oxidation number is unconvincing to us, because electrons are never shared/transferred in fraction.','Actually the fractional oxidation state is the average oxidation state of the element under examination.','structural parameters reveal that the element for whom fractional oxidation state is realised is present in different oxidation states.','Oxidation state of O in O₂⁺ is 0.','NEW','11-273','11-245',NULL),
