(220540,'biology','ADH _______loss of water through urine.','Reduces','Vasopressin acts mainly at the kidney and stimulates resorption of water and electrolytes by the distal tubules and thereby reduces loss of water through urine (diuresis). Hence, it is also called as anti-diuretic hormone (ADH).(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 334;paragraph No.1)..','Human Physiology >> Chemical Coordination and Integration >> The Pituitary Gland',NULL,'3','mcq','Increases','Reduces','No effect','Have a miscellanous effect','NEW','11-334','11-242',NULL),
(220541,'biology','An impairment affecting synthesis or release of___________causes Diabetes Insipidus.','ADH','Vasopressin acts mainly at the kidney and stimulates resorption of water and electrolytes by the distal tubules and thereby reduces loss of water through urine (diuresis). Hence, it is also called as anti-diuretic hormone (ADH)..(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 334;paragraph No.1).','Human Physiology >> Chemical Coordination and Integration >> The Pituitary Gland',NULL,'2','mcq','GH','ADH','LH','FSH','NEW','11-334','11-242',NULL),
(220542,'biology','An impairment affecting synthesis or release of ADH results in-','Diabetes insipidus','An impairment affecting synthesis or release of ADH results in a diminished ability of the kidney to conserve water leading to water loss and dehydration. This condition is known as Diabetes Insipidus..(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 334;paragraph No.1).','Human Physiology >> Chemical Coordination and Integration >> The Pituitary Gland',NULL,'2','mcq','Diabetes mellitus','Diabetes insipidus','Dwarfism','Acromegaly','NEW','11-334','11-242',NULL),
