(220802,'chemistry','The standard electrode potential values of Al³⁺/Al, Ag⁺/Ag, K⁺/K and Cr³⁺/Cr are −1.66 V, 0.80 V, −2.93 V and −0.74 V, respectively. The correct decreasing order of reducing power of the metal is','K>Al>Cr>Ag','[NEET-2019 (Odisha)]','Inorganic chemistry >> Redox Reactions >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'3','order','1,K','2,Al','3,Cr','4,Ag','NEW','11-278','11-250',NULL),
(220803,'chemistry','Which of the following reactions are disproportionation reaction? \n a) 2Cu⁺→Cu²⁺ + Cu\nb) 3MnO₄²⁻→ 2MnO₄⁻ + MnO₂ + 2H₂O\nc) 2KMnO₄→K₂MnO₄ + MnO₂ + O₂\nd) 2MnO₄⁻+3Mn²⁺+2H₂O→5MnO₂ + 4H⁺\n Select the correct option from the following','a and b only','[NEET-2019]','Inorganic chemistry >> Redox Reactions >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','a and b only','a,b and c','a,c and d','a and d only','NEW','11-272','11-244',NULL),
(220804,'chemistry','The correct order of N-compounds in its decreasing order of oxidation states is','HNO₃>NO>N₂>NH₄Cl','[NEET-2018]','Inorganic chemistry >> Redox Reactions >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'3','order','1,HNO₃','2,NO','3,N₂','4,NH₄Cl','NEW','11-272','11-244',NULL),
(220805,'chemistry','For the redox reaction \nMnO₄⁻ + C₂O₄²⁻+H⁺ → Mn²⁺ + CO₂ + H₂O\nGive coefficient of MnO₄⁻, C₂O₄²⁻,H⁺ respectively.','2,5,16','[NEET-2018]','Inorganic chemistry >> Redox Reactions >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','16,5,2','2,5,16','5,16,2','2,16,5','NEW','11-275','11-247',NULL),
