(221029,'biology','Aldosterone stimulates excretion of-','K+ and Phosphate','Aldosterone acts mainly at the renal tubules and stimulates the reabsorption of Na+ and water and excretion of K+ and phosphate ions..(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 337;paragraph No.2).','Human Physiology >> Chemical Coordination and Integration >> Adrenal Gland',NULL,'3','mcq','K+ and Phosphate','K+ and Ca+2','Na+ and Phosphate','Na+ and water','NEW','11-337','11-245',NULL),
