(221031,'biology','Androgenic steroids secreted by Adrenal cortex play a role in growth of_______________during puberty. \ni.Axial hair \nii. Pubic hair \niii. Facial hair \niv.Not involved in Hair growth','i, ii and iii only','Small amounts of androgenic steroids are also secreted by the adrenal cortex which play a role in the growth of axial hair, pubic hair and facial hair during puberty..(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 337;paragraph No.2).','Human Physiology >> Chemical Coordination and Integration >> Adrenal Gland',NULL,'3','mcq','i and ii only','i, ii and iii only','iii only','iv only','NEW','11-337','11-245',NULL),
