(221101,'chemistry','Which of the following is a redox reaction?','Zn +2AgCN -> 2Ag +Zn(CN)₂','there is a change in oxidation state only in option d . In all others ions like Na⁺,Cl⁻, C₂O₄²⁻,NH₄⁺,Mg₂⁺ all maintain the same oxidation states(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 265;Paragraph 8.2) JEE-mains 2002','Inorganic chemistry >> Redox Reactions >> JEE Mains',NULL,'2','mcq','NaCI+ KNO₃  ->Na NO₃+KCI','CaC₂O₄ +2HCI ->CaCl₂ +H₂C₂O₄','Mg(OH)₂ +2NH₄ CI ->. MgCl₂ +2NH₄OH','Zn +2AgCN -> 2Ag +Zn(CN)₂','NEW','11-262','11-234',NULL),
