(110907,'chemistry','The oxides of In and Tl are','Basic','down the group metallic character increase, among all members of B-\n family In and Tl are most metallic, the oxides of metals are basic in \n nature as when dissolve in water give bases.\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 319; Paragraph No.5)','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 13-Reactivity towards air',NULL,'1','mcq','Neutral','Acidic','Basic','Amphoteric','NEW','11-319',NULL,NULL),
(221103,'chemistry','Which of the following chemical reactions depict the oxidizing beahviour of H₂SO₄','2HI + H₂SO₄ ->I₂ +SO₂ +2H₂O','2HI + H₂SO₄ ->I₂ +SO₂ +2H₂O        In this reaction the oxidation number of sulphur is decreasing from +6 to +4 hence undergoing reduction and for HI oxidation state of Iodine is increasing from -1 to 0 hence undergoing oxidation .Therefore H₂SO₄ acts as a oxidising agent (Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 269;Paragraph 8.3) JEE mains - 2006','Inorganic chemistry >> Redox Reactions >> JEE Mains',NULL,'1','mcq','NaCl + H₂SO₄  -> NaHSO₄ + HCI','2PCls + H₂SO₄ ->2POCI₃   + 2HCI+SO₂Cl₂','2HI + H₂SO₄ ->I₂ +SO₂ +2H₂O','Ca(OH)₂  + H₂SO₄ ->CaSO₄ + 2H₂O','NEW','11-269','11-241',NULL),
(221104,'chemistry','XMnO₄⁻ +YC₂ O₄²⁻ +ZH⁺ -> XMn²⁺ + 2YCO₂ +Z/2 H₂O values of X, Y and Z respectively are','2, 5, 16','first half of reaction is MnO₄⁻ -> Mn²⁺ on balancing becomes.              MnO₄⁻  +8H⁺ +5e⁻ ->Mn⁺² +4H₂ O       Second half of the reaction is.        C₂ O₄²⁻ -> 2CO₂ on multiplying equation 2  by five and equation 1 by two and then adding we can get the answers(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 274;Paragraph 8.3.2) JEE mains - 2012','Inorganic chemistry >> Redox Reactions >> JEE Mains',NULL,'1','mcq','2, 5, 16','8,2,5','5,2, 16','5,8,4','NEW','11-274','11-246',NULL),
(221105,'chemistry','The molecular formula of a commercial resin used for exchanging ions in water softening is C₈H₇SO₃Na⁺ (Mol. wt. 206. What would be the maximum uptake of Ca²⁺ ions by the resin when expressed in mole per gram resin?','1/412','The ion exchange resin with the molecular formula C₈H₇SO₃Na⁺ has a sulfonate functional group (-SO₃Na⁺) which can exchange ions with other cations, such as Ca²⁺.\n\nThe maximum uptake of Ca²⁺ ions by the resin can be calculated using the equivalent weight of the resin, which is the molecular weight divided by the number of equivalents of sulfonate groups in the resin.\n\nThe molecular weight of the resin is given as 206 g/mol. The sulfonate functional group (-SO₃Na⁺) has one equivalent of negative charge, so the number of equivalents of sulfonate groups in the resin is equal to the number of Na⁺ ions, which is 1.\n\nTherefore, the equivalent weight of the resin is:\n\nEquivalent weight = Molecular weight / Number of equivalents = 206 g/mol / 1 = 206 g/equivalent\n\nThe maximum uptake of Ca²⁺ ions can be calculated using the formula:\n\nMaximum uptake of Ca²⁺ ions = (Exchange capacity of resin / Equivalent weight of resin) * (Molecular weight of Ca²⁺ / Valency of Ca²⁺)\n\nThe exchange capacity of the resin is the maximum number of equivalents of Ca²⁺ ions that can be exchanged per gram of resin. Since the resin has one equivalent of sulfonate groups, the exchange capacity is equal to the number of equivalents of Ca²⁺ ions that can be exchanged per equivalent weight of the resin.\nJEE mains - 2015','Inorganic chemistry >> Redox Reactions >> JEE Mains',NULL,'2','mcq','0','1/412','1/103','1/206','NEW','11-274','11-246',NULL),
(221106,'chemistry','Which of the following reactions is an example of a redox reaction?','XeF₄  +O₂F₂ ->  XeF₆  + O₂','In the above reaction Xe is oxidised and oxygen is reduced .Xe is oxidised from +4 to +6 while oxygen is reduced from +1 to 0 hence it is a redox reaction (Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 270;Paragraph 8.3.1)JEE mains -2017','Inorganic chemistry >> Redox Reactions >> JEE Mains',NULL,'2','mcq','XeF₄  +O₂F₂ ->  XeF₆  + O₂','XeF₂ +PF₅  ->[XeF]⁺ +   PF₆⁻','XeF₆  +H₂O  -> XeOF₄ +2HF','XeF₆ +2 H₂O-> Xe O₂F₂ + 4HF','NEW','11-270','11-242',NULL),
(221107,'biology','The β-cells secrete a hormone called ______.','Insulin','While the β-cells secrete insulin..(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 337;paragraph No.3).','Human Physiology >> Chemical Coordination and Integration >> Pancreas',NULL,'2','mcq','Thyroid','Glucagon','Insulin','Oxytosin','NEW','11-337','11-245',NULL),
(221108,'biology','Glucagon is a ______ hormone.','Peptide','Glucagon is a peptide hormone, and plays an important role in maintaining the normal blood glucose levels.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 337;paragraph No.4).','Human Physiology >> Chemical Coordination and Integration >> Pancreas',NULL,'1','mcq','Amino acid derivative','Peptide','Steroid','Carbohydrate moiety','NEW','11-337','11-245',NULL),
(221109,'biology','Glucagon\'s main role is _______.','Maintaining the normal blood glucose levels.','Glucagon is a peptide hormone, and plays an important role in maintaining the normal blood glucose levels.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 337;paragraph No.4).','Human Physiology >> Chemical Coordination and Integration >> Pancreas',NULL,'2','mcq','Maintaining the normal blood glucose levels.','Maintaining the normal O₂ levels.','Maintaining the normal water levels.','Maintaining the normal Albumin levels.','NEW','11-337','11-245',NULL),
(221110,'biology','Glucagon acts mainly on ______ cells.','Liver','Glucagon acts mainly on the liver cells (hepatocytes) and stimulates glycogenolysis resulting in an increased blood sugar (hyperglycemia)..(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 337;paragraph No.4).','Human Physiology >> Chemical Coordination and Integration >> Pancreas',NULL,'2','mcq','Pancreas','Liver','Heart','Intestines','NEW','11-337','11-245',NULL),
(221111,'biology','Liver cells are also called ____.','Hepatocytes','Glucagon acts mainly on the liver cells (hepatocytes) and stimulates glycogenolysis resulting in an increased blood sugar (hyperglycemia)..(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 337;paragraph No.4).','Human Physiology >> Chemical Coordination and Integration >> Pancreas',NULL,'3','mcq','Hepatocytes','Metamyelocytes','Tubular cells','Oateocytes','NEW','11-337','11-245',NULL),
