(221113,'biology','An increased blood sugar is also called ______.','Hyperglycemia','Glucagon acts mainly on the liver cells (hepatocytes) and stimulates glycogenolysis resulting in an increased blood sugar (hyperglycemia). In addition this hormone stimulate the process of gluconeogenesis i.e., new glucose formation. It also promotes lipolysis to provide glycerol which serve as substarte for gluconeogenesis.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 337;paragraph No.4).','Human Physiology >> Chemical Coordination and Integration >> Pancreas',NULL,'3','mcq','Hyperglycemia','Hypoglycemia','Hypernatremia','Hyperkalemia','NEW','11-337','11-245',NULL),
(221114,'biology','Glucagon reduces the cellular glucose uptake and utilisation.','TRUE','Glucagon reduces the cellular glucose uptake and utilisation..(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 334;paragraph No.1). It is a hyperglycemia hormone its effect is just opposite of insulin.  it acts on liver cells and stimulate glycogenolysis releasing glucose from stored glycogen from liver','Human Physiology >> Chemical Coordination and Integration >> Pancreas',NULL,'1','mcq','TRUE','FALSE',NULL,NULL,'NEW','11-337','11-245',NULL),
(221115,'biology','Glucagon is a ________ hormone.','Hyperglycemic','Glucagon is a hyperglycemic hormone..(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 337;paragraph No.4).','Human Physiology >> Chemical Coordination and Integration >> Pancreas',NULL,'2','mcq','Hypoglycemic','Steroid','Hyperglycemic','Hyperkalemic','NEW','11-337','11-245',NULL);
