(221120,'biology','A decreased blood glucose level is termed _______.','Hypoglycemia','There is a rapid movement of glucose from blood to hepatocytes and adipocytes resulting in decreased blood glucose levels (hypoglycemia)..(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 338;paragraph No.1).','Human Physiology >> Chemical Coordination and Integration >> Pancreas',NULL,'3','mcq','Glycogenolysis','Hyperglycemia','Hypoglycemia','Hepatocytis','NEW','11-338','11-246',NULL),
