(221507,'biology','Cortisol, testosterone, estradiol and progesterone are all examples of-','Steroids','Steroids (e.g., cortisol, testosterone, estradiol and progesterone).(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 340;paragraph No.1).','Human Physiology >> Chemical Coordination and Integration >> Mechanism of Hormone Action',NULL,'2','mcq','Protein hormones','Steroids','Iodothyronines','Amino-acid derivatives','NEW','11-340','11-248',NULL),
(221508,'biology','Thyroid hormones are-','Iodothyronines','Iodothyronines (thyroid hormones).(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 340;paragraph No.1).','Human Physiology >> Chemical Coordination and Integration >> Mechanism of Hormone Action',NULL,'2','mcq','Protein hormones','Steroids','Iodothyronines','Amino-acid derivatives','NEW','11-340','11-248',NULL),
(221509,'biology','Epinephrine is-','Amino-acid derivatives','Amino-acid derivatives (e.g., epinephrine) (Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 340;paragraph No.1).','Human Physiology >> Chemical Coordination and Integration >> Mechanism of Hormone Action',NULL,'2','mcq','Protein hormones','Steroids','Iodothyronines','Amino-acid derivatives','NEW','11-340','11-248',NULL),
(221510,'biology','Which of the following hormones interact with intra-cellular receptors?','Cortisol and estradiol','Hormones which interact with intracellular receptors (e.g., steroid\nhormones, iodothyronines, etc.) mostly regulate gene expression or\nchromosome function by the interaction of hormone-receptor complex\nwith the genome.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 340;paragraph No.2).','Human Physiology >> Chemical Coordination and Integration >> Mechanism of Hormone Action',NULL,'3','mcq','Aldosterone','Cortisol only','Estradiol only','Cortisol and estradiol','NEW','11-340','11-248',NULL),
(221511,'biology','Which of the following hormones interact with intra-cellular receptors?','Steroids','Hormones which interact with intracellular receptors (e.g., steroid hormones, iodothyronines, etc.) mostly regulate gene expression or chromosome function by the interaction of hormone-receptor complex with the genome..(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 340;paragraph No.2).','Human Physiology >> Chemical Coordination and Integration >> Mechanism of Hormone Action',NULL,'2','mcq','Protein hormones','Steroids','Polypeptides','Amino-acid derivatives','NEW','11-340','11-248',NULL),
(221512,'biology','Hormones which interact with intracellular receptors mostly regulate- \nClue: Answer With Reference to the diagram (2209)','Gene expression and Chromosome functions','Hormones which interact with intracellular receptors (e.g., steroid hormones, iodothyronines, etc.) mostly regulate gene expression or chromosome function by the interaction of hormone-receptor complex with the genome..(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11;page 340;paragraph No.2).','Human Physiology >> Chemical Coordination and Integration >> Mechanism of Hormone Action',NULL,'2','mcq','Gene expression only','Chromosome function only','Gene expression and Chromosome functions','Enzyme activation in cytosol','NEW','11-340','11-248','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/221512q.png'),
(221513,'biology','What type of hormone is seen interacting with a receptor in the diagram ?(2208)','Protein hormones','Figure 22.5 NCERT Class 11 page no: 341 diagrammatic representation of the mechanism of hormone action : (a) Protein hormone (b) Steroid hormone','Human Physiology >> Chemical Coordination and Integration >> Mechanism of Hormone Action',NULL,'2','mcq','Protein hormones','Steroids','Iodothyronines','Amino-acid derivatives','NEW','11-341','11-249','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/221513q.png'),
