(240301,'chemistry','The IUPAC name of isopropyl chloride is','2-chloropropane','The common names of alkyl halides are derived by naming the alkyl group followed by the name of halide. In the IUPAC system of nomenclature, alkyl halides are named as halo substituted hydrocarbons.\n\nThere are several sets of rules for IUPAC nomenclature. \n\n1. The longest continuous carbon chain should be found and named.\n2. List the names of the organisations that make up this chain.\n3. Starting at the end of the chain closest to a substituent group, sequentially number the chain.\n4. Indicate each substituent group\'s location with the relevant number and name.\n\n5. Put the name together by listing the groups alphabetically using the whole name. (e.g., cyclopropyl before isobutyl). The chlorine is attached to the secondary carbon atom in propane which is the middle or the second one.\n\n(Reference  :NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 291; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Haloalkanes and Haloarenes >> Nomenclature',NULL,'1','mcq','2-chloropropane','1-chloropropane','3-chloropropane','2-chlorobutane','NEW','12-291','12-161',NULL),
(240302,'chemistry','Compounds in which the halogen atom is directly bonded to the sp²-hybridised carbon atom of an aromatic ring is called','Aryl halide','These are the compounds in which the halogen atom is directly bonded to the sp²-hybridised carbon atom of an aromatic ring.\n\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 291; Paragraph 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Haloalkanes and Haloarenes >> Nomenclature',NULL,'1','mcq','Aryl halide','Aryl nitrile','Alkyl halide','Vinyl halide','NEW','12-292','12-162',NULL),
(240303,'chemistry','IUPAC name of this compound is__________ .diagram(n2454)','trichloromethane','There are several sets of rules for IUPAC nomenclature. \n\n1. The longest continuous carbon chain should be found and named.\n\n2. List the names of the organisations that make up this chain.\n\n3. Starting at the end of the chain closest to a substituent group, sequentially number the chain.\n\n4. Indicate each substituent group\'s location with the relevant number and name.\n\n5. Put the name together by listing the groups alphabetically using the whole name. (e.g., cyclopropyl before isobutyl).\n\nThe IUPAC name of chloroform is trichloromethane.\n\n(Reference: NCERT Table 10.1  Class 12 Chemistry NCERT Page 292 )','Organic Chemistry >> Haloalkanes and Haloarenes >> Nomenclature',NULL,'3','mcq','chloroform','trichloromethane','bromoform','tribromomethane','NEW','12-292','12-162','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/240303q.png'),
(240304,'chemistry','Common name of this compound is__________. diagram(n2452)','benzyl chloride','The common name of the given compound is benzyl chloride.\n\n(Reference: NCERT Table 10.1  Class 12 Chemistry NCERT Page 292)','Organic Chemistry >> Haloalkanes and Haloarenes >> Nomenclature',NULL,'3','mcq','benzyl chloride','chlorophenylmethane','methylene chloride','dichloromethane','NEW','12-293','12-163','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/240304q.png'),
(260332,'chemistry','Catalyst of Gatterman – Koch reaction?','CuCl','Gatterman – Koch reaction \n\nWhen benzene or its derivative is treated with carbon monoxide and hydrogen chloride in the presence of anhydrous aluminium chloride or cuprous chloride, it gives benzaldehyde or substituted benzaldehyde.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-363 Paragraph -3)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Preparation of Aldehydes and Ketones',NULL,'2','mcq','AgCl','CuCl','Both (a) and (b)','FeCl₃','NEW','12-363','12-233',NULL),
(240305,'chemistry','IUPAC name of this compound is__________. diagram(n2452)','chlorophenylmethane','There are several sets of rules for IUPAC nomenclature. \n\n1. The longest continuous carbon chain should be found and named.\n\n2. List the names of the organisations that make up this chain.\n\n3. Starting at the end of the chain closest to a substituent group, sequentially number the chain.\n\n4. Indicate each substituent group\'s location with the relevant number and name.\n\n5. Put the name together by listing the groups alphabetically using the whole name. (e.g., cyclopropyl before isobutyl).\n\nThe IUPAC name of given compound is chlorophenylmethane.\n\n(Reference: NCERT Table 10.1  Class 12 Chemistry NCERT Page 292 )','Organic Chemistry >> Haloalkanes and Haloarenes >> Nomenclature',NULL,'3','mcq','benzyl chloride','chlorophenylmethane','methylene chloride','dichloromethane','NEW','12-293','12-163','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/240305q.png'),
(240306,'chemistry','Which of the following IUPAC name represents which structure? diagram(n2466)','4-tert-butyl-3-iodoheptane','There are several sets of rules for IUPAC nomenclature. \n\n1. The longest continuous carbon chain should be found and named.\n\n2. List the names of the organisations that make up this chain.\n\n3. Starting at the end of the chain closest to a substituent group, sequentially number the chain.\n\n4. Indicate each substituent group\'s location with the relevant number and name.\n\n5. Put the name together by listing the groups alphabetically using the whole name. (e.g., cyclopropyl before isobutyl).\n\nThe IUPAC name of the given compound 4-tert-butyl-3-iodoheptane.\n\n(Reference: Intext Question 10.1 Class 12 Chemistry NCERT Page 293)','Organic Chemistry >> Haloalkanes and Haloarenes >> Nomenclature',NULL,'3','mcq','2-chloro-3-methylpentane','1-chloro-4-ethylcyclohexane','4-tert-butyl-3-iodoheptane','1,4-dibromobut-2-ene','NEW','12-293','12-163','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/240306q.png'),
