(240322,'chemistry','Which name correctly represents diagram(n2465)','1-chloro-4-ethylcyclohexane','There are several sets of rules for IUPAC nomenclature. \n\n1. The longest continuous carbon chain should be found and named.\n\n2. List the names of the organisations that make up this chain.\n\n3. Starting at the end of the chain closest to a substituent group, sequentially number the chain.\n\n4. Indicate each substituent group\'s location with the relevant number and name.\n\n5. Put the name together by listing the groups alphabetically using the whole name. (e.g., cyclopropyl before isobutyl).\n\n(Reference : Intext Question 10.1 Class 12 Chemistry NCERT Page 293)','Organic Chemistry >> Haloalkanes and Haloarenes >> Nomenclature',NULL,'3','mcq','2-chloro-3-methylpentane','1-chloro-4-ethylcyclohexane','4-tert-butyl-3-iodoheptane','1,4-dibromobut-2-ene','NEW','12-293','12-163','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/240322q.png'),
