(121404,'chemistry','Electronegativity of carbon atoms depends upon their state of hybridisation. In which of the following compounds, the carbon marked with asterisk is most electronegative? Refer diagram(12144)','c','The greater the s character of the hybrid orbitals, the greater is the electronegativity. Relative electronegativity is reflected in several physical and chemical properties of the molecules.The sp hybrid orbital contains more s character and hence it is closer to its nucleus.\n\nReference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 335; Paragraph No.2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> NCERT Exemplar Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','a','b','c','d','NEW','11-335','11-257','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/121404q.png'),
(240324,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name of the compound _________ given in the diagram?(n2463)','3-bromo-2-methylpropene','There are several sets of rules for IUPAC nomenclature. \n\n1. The longest continuous carbon chain should be found and named.\n\n2. List the names of the organisations that make up this chain.\n\n3. Starting at the end of the chain closest to a substituent group, sequentially number the chain.\n\n4. Indicate each substituent group\'s location with the relevant number and name.\n\n5. Put the name together by listing the groups alphabetically using the whole name. (e.g., cyclopropyl before isobutyl).\n\nThe IUPAC name of the given compound is 3-bromo-2methylpropene.\n\n(Reference: NCERT Table 10.1  Class 12 Chemistry NCERT Page 292)','Organic Chemistry >> Haloalkanes and Haloarenes >> Nomenclature',NULL,'3','mcq','4-bromopent-2-ene','1-bromobut-2-ene','3-bromo-2-methylpropene','1-bromo-2-methylbut-2-ene','NEW','12-293','12-163','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/240324q.png'),
(240325,'chemistry','Which name correctly represents diagram(n2467)','1,4-dibromobut-2-ene','There are several sets of rules for IUPAC nomenclature. \n\n1. The longest continuous carbon chain should be found and named.\n\n2. List the names of the organisations that make up this chain.\n\n3. Starting at the end of the chain closest to a substituent group, sequentially number the chain.\n\n4. Indicate each substituent group\'s location with the relevant number and name.\n\n5. Put the name together by listing the groups alphabetically using the whole name. (e.g., cyclopropyl before isobutyl).\n\n(Reference: Intext Question 10.1 Class 12 Chemistry NCERT Page 293)','Organic Chemistry >> Haloalkanes and Haloarenes >> Nomenclature',NULL,'3','mcq','2-chloro-3-methylpentane','1-chloro-4-ethylcyclohexane','4-tert-butyl-3-iodoheptane','1,4-dibromobut-2-ene','NEW','12-293','12-163','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/240325q.png'),
