(240337,'chemistry','IUPAC name of this compound is________. diagram(n2461)','1-bromo-2-methylbut-2-ene','There are several sets of rules for IUPAC nomenclature. \n\n1. The longest continuous carbon chain should be found and named.\n\n2. List the names of the organisations that make up this chain.\n\n3. Starting at the end of the chain closest to a substituent group, sequentially number the chain.\n\n4. Indicate each substituent group\'s location with the relevant number and name.\n\n5. Put the name together by listing the groups alphabetically using the whole name. (e.g., cyclopropyl before isobutyl)\n\n(Reference: NCERT Table 10.1  Class 12 Chemistry NCERT Page 292 )','Organic Chemistry >> Haloalkanes and Haloarenes >> Nomenclature',NULL,'3','mcq','4-bromopent-2-ene','3-bromo-2-methylbut-1-ene','4-bromo-3-methylpent-2-ene','1-bromo-2-methylbut-2-ene','NEW','12-293','12-163','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/240337q.png'),
(240401,'chemistry','The reason for the polarized nature of carbon halogen bond is ?','Due to large electronegativity difference of carbon and halogen atom','Halogen atoms are more electronegative than carbon, therefore, carbon-halogen bond of alkyl halide is polarised; the carbon atom bears a partial positive charge whereas the halogen atom bears a partial negative charge. \n\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12, page 293; Paragraph 10.1)','Organic Chemistry >> Haloalkanes and Haloarenes >> Nature of C-X bond',NULL,'1','mcq','Due to large electronegativity difference of carbon and halogen atom','As both atoms are having charges','As the overall compound is charged and polarized','Due to paramagnetic nature of compound','NEW','12-293','12-163',NULL),
(240402,'chemistry','Select the correct order of carbon halogen bond length?','C-I>C-Br>C-Cl>C-F','As we go down the group in the periodic table, the size of halogen atom increases. \n\nFluorine atom is the smallest and iodine atom is the largest. \n\nConsequently the carbon-halogen bond length also increases from C—F to C—I.  \n\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 293; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Haloalkanes and Haloarenes >> Nature of C-X bond',NULL,'1','order','1,C-I','2,C-Br','3,C-Cl','4,C-F','NEW','12-293','12-163',NULL),
(240403,'chemistry','Which is the best substrate for the production of alkyl halides?','Alcohols','Alkyl halides are best prepared from alcohols, which are easily accessible.\n\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 293; Paragraph No.2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Haloalkanes and Haloarenes >> Nature of C-X bond',NULL,'1','mcq','Alcohols','Alkanes','Alkenes','Carboxylic acids','NEW','12-293','12-163',NULL),
(240404,'chemistry','Which of the following has the shortest carbon halogen bond length?','CH₃F','As we go down the group in the periodic table, the size of halogen atom increases. \n\nFluorine atom is the smallest and iodine atom is the largest. \n\nConsequently the carbon-halogen bond length also increases from C—F to C—I.\n\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 293; Paragraph No.3)','Organic Chemistry >> Haloalkanes and Haloarenes >> Nature of C-X bond',NULL,'1','mcq','CH₃F','CH₃I','CH₃Br','CH₃Cl','NEW','12-293','12-163',NULL),
