(300210,'chemistry','Assertion: Excessive hydrogencarbonate can make the stomach alkaline and trigger the production of even more acid.\nReason: Metal hydroxides are better alternatives because of being insoluble, these do not increase the pH above neutrality.','The Assertion and the Reason are correct but the Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 451; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs',NULL,'3','mcq','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','The Assertion and the Reason are correct but the Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion','Assertion is True  but the Reason is false','Both the Assertion and Reason are false.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300211,'chemistry','_____________ only control symptoms not cause of over production of HCL.','Metal hydroxides(Al,Mg)','Over production of acid in the stomach causes irritation and pain. In severe cases, ulcers are developed in the stomach. Until 1970, only treatment  for  acidity was administration of antacids, such as sodium hydrogencarbonate or a mixture of aluminium and magnesium hydroxide. However, excessive hydrogencarbonate can make the stomach alkaline and trigger the production of even more acid. Metal hydroxides are better alternatives because of being insoluble, these do not increase the pH above neutrality. These treatments control only symptoms, and not the cause. Therefore,  with these metal salts, the patients cannot be treated easily. In advanced stages, ulcers become life threatening and its only treatment is removal of the affected part of the stomach.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 451; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs',NULL,'1','mcq','Ranitidine','Cimetidine','Metal hydroxides(Al,Mg)','Nardil','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300212,'chemistry','_____________  control cause of over production of HCL.','Cimetidine','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 451; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs',NULL,'1','mcq','Cimetidine','Metal hydroxides(Al,Mg)','Nardil','Antacid','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300213,'chemistry','In the treatment of hyperacidity _______chemical stimulates the secretion of pepsin and hydrochloric acid in the stomach.','Histamine','A major breakthrough in the treatment of hyperacidity came through the discovery according  to which a chemical, histamine, stimulates the secretion of pepsin and hydrochloric acid in the stomach. (Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 451; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs',NULL,'1','mcq','Antihistamine','Histamine','Cimetidine','HCl','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300214,'chemistry','The drug cimetidine (Tegamet), was designed to prevent the interaction of histamine with the receptors present in -','Stomach wall','The drug cimetidine (Tegamet), was designed to prevent the interaction of histamine with the receptors present in the stomach wall.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 451; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs',NULL,'1','mcq','Gut wall','Intestinal wall','Stomach wall','Mast cell','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300215,'chemistry','The largest selling drug(antihistamine ) in the world until another drug ranitidine (Zantac) was discovered.','Cimetidine','The drug cimetidine (Tegamet), was designed to prevent the interaction of histamine with the receptors present in the stomach wall. This resulted in release of lesser amount of acid.  The importance of the drug was so much that it remained the largest selling drug in the world until another drug, ranitidine (Zantac), was discovered.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 451; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs',NULL,'2','mcq','Cimetidine','Seldane','Metal hydroxides(Al,Mg)','brompheniramine','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
