(300220,'chemistry','How Histamines affects Blood Vessel?','Vasodilator','Histamine is a potent vasodilator. (Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 451; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs',NULL,'1','mcq','Vasoconstrictor','Vasodilator','It depends on site of action','There no affect on Blood vessels','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300221,'chemistry','Which is true for Histamine:\n1. It Relaxes other muscles except Gut and bronchi. \n2. It contracts the smooth muscles in the bronchi and gut.\n3. It Relaxes the smooth muscles in Bronchi.\n4. Vasodilator \n5. Vasoconstrictor\n6. Allergic response to pollen.\n7. Nasal congestion associated with common cold.','1,2,4,6,7','Histamine is a potent vasodilator. It has various functions. It contracts the smooth muscles in the bronchi and gut and relaxes other muscles, such as those in the walls of fine blood vessels. Histamine is also responsible for the nasal congestion associated with common cold and allergic response to pollen.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 451; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs',NULL,'3','mcq','1,2,4,6,7','1,2,5,6,7','1,3,4,6,7','1,3,4,5,7','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
