(300301,'chemistry','Which of the following analgesics are called opiates','Morphine','Morphine narcotics are sometimes referred to\nas opiates, since they are obtained from the opium poppy.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 453 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'1','mcq','Aspirin','Paracetamol','Morphine','Both a and c','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/300301q.png'),
(300302,'chemistry','Assertion: Morphine narcotics are sometimes referred to as opiates \nReason: Because they are obtained from the Atropa Beladona','Assertion is True  but the Reason is false','Morphine narcotics are sometimes referred to\nas opiates, since they are obtained from the opium poppy.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 453 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'3','mcq','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','The Assertion and the Reason are correct but the Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion','Assertion is True  but the Reason is false','Both the Assertion and Reason are false.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/300302q.png'),
(300303,'chemistry','Consider the following:\n1. Aspirin is both analgesic and antipyretic.\n2. Ampicillin is a semisynthetic antibiotic.\n3.Salvarsan is toxic to human being.\n4. Some disinfectants are used as antiseptic at Higher concentration.\nWhich of the following are true?','1 ,2 and 3','Salvarsan is antibacterial earlier used in the treatment of syphilis and is no longer used as it was found to be toxic to humans,\n Some disinfectants are used as antiseptic at lower concentration.','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'2','mcq','1 and 3','3 and 4','2 and 3','1 ,2 and 3','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/300303q.png'),
(300304,'chemistry','Barbiturates acts as','Hypnotics','Barbiturates are hypnotic, i.e.,\nsleep producing agents. (Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 453 Para 1 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'1','mcq','Analgesic','Hypnotics','Antipyretic','Stimulants','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/300304q.png'),
(300305,'chemistry','Seretonin and Valium  are Example of','Tranquilizers','Derivatives of barbituric acid viz., veronal, amytal, nembutal, luminal\nand seconal constitute an important class of tranquilizers. These\nderivatives are called barbiturates. Barbiturates are hypnotic, i.e.,\nsleep producing agents. Some other substances used as tranquilizers\nare valium and serotonin.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 453 Para 1 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'1','mcq','Tranquilizers','Analgesic','Antihistamines','Stimulants','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/match/300305q.png'),
(300306,'chemistry','Aspirin use to Reduce-','Pain as well as Fever','Aspirin is the most familiar example. Aspirin inhibits the synthesis\nof chemicals known as prostaglandins which stimulate\ninflammation in the tissue and cause pain. These drugs are effective\nin relieving skeletal pain such as that due to arthritis. These drugs\nhave many other effects such as reducing fever (antipyretic). (Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 453 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'1','mcq','Stomach Acid','Fever only','Pain as well as Fever','Pain as well as act as Sedative','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/300306q.png'),
(300307,'chemistry','Drug act as antipyretic as well as analgesic','Paracetamol','Paracetamol belong to the class of non-narcotic analgesics. Aspirin  is the most familiar example. Aspirin inhibits the synthesis of chemicals known as prostaglandins which stimulate inflammation in the tissue and cause pain. These drugs are effective in relieving skeletal pain such as that due to arthritis. These drugs have many other effects such as reducing fever (antipyretic)  and preventing platelet coagulation. Because of its anti blood clotting action, aspirin finds use in prevention of heart attacks.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 453 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'1','mcq','Pentaprazole','Paracetamol','Acetylmorphine','Narcotics','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/300307q.png'),
(300308,'chemistry','Which of the following drug inherit the synthesis of prostaglandin-','Aspirin','Aspirin inhibits the synthesis of chemicals known as prostaglandins which stimulate inflammation in the tissue and cause pain. These drugs are effective in relieving skeletal pain such as that due to arthritis. These drugs have many other effects such as reducing fever (antipyretic) and preventing platelet coagulation. Because of its anti blood clotting action, aspirin finds use in prevention of heart attacks.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 453 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'1','mcq','Paracetamol','Aspirin','Serotonin','Cimitidine','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/300308q.png'),
(300309,'chemistry','Which of the following is a narcotic analgesic-','Morphine','Morphine narcotics are sometimes referred to as opiates, since they are obtained from the opium poppy. These analgesics are chiefly used for the relief of postoperative pain, cardiac pain and pains of terminal cancer, and in child birth.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 453 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'1','mcq','Paracetamol','Morphine','Valium','Aspirin','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300310,'chemistry','Which of the following can be used as analgesic without causing addiction','Aspirin','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 453 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'1','mcq','Morphine','Aspirin','Codein','Valium','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300311,'chemistry','Analgesic reduces pain without causing impairment of-','All of these','Analgesics  reduce or abolish pain without causing impairment of consciousness, mental confusion, incoordination or paralysis or some other disturbances of nervous system.','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'2','mcq','paralysis','consciousness','mental confusion','All of these','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300312,'chemistry','Presence of high amount of prostaglandin in blood leads to-','Induce pain','Aspirin inhibits the synthesis of chemicals known as prostaglandins which stimulate inflammation in the tissue and cause pain.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 453 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'1','mcq','reduce pain','Induce pain','Increase RBC','Increase WBC','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300313,'chemistry','Among the following which are narcotic analgesic-','Morphine, Heroine, Codeine','Morphine, Heroine, Codeine','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Morphine, Heroine, Seretonin','Morphine, Heroine, Codeine','Salvarsan, Heroine, Codeine','Aspirin, Heroine, Valium','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300314,'chemistry','Morphine and many of its homeo logis administrator in medicinal dose. then they produce-','Relieve pain and induce sleep','Morphine and many of its homologues, when administered in medicinal doses, relieve pain and produce sleep. In poisonous doses, these produce stupor, coma, convulsions and ultimately death. Morphine narcotics are sometimes referred to as opiates, since they are obtained from the opium poppy.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 453 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Relieve pain and induce sleep','Relieve pain only','Can Cause Poisonous effect','lower the body temperature','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300315,'chemistry','Which class of drug used in sleeping pills-','Sedative','Sedative','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'1','mcq','Analgesic','Antihistamines','Sedative','Stimulants','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300316,'chemistry','The term opiates stands  for','Narcotic analgesics obtained from the  Opium poppy','Narcotic analgesics obtained from the  Opium poppy. (Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 453 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'1','mcq','Non Narcotic analgesics obtained from the Opium poppy','Narcotic analgesics obtained from the  Opium poppy','Tranquilizers use to reduce tension','Narcotics having Sedative Effect','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300317,'chemistry','High dose of morphine produce-','All of these','Morphine and many of its homologues, when administered in medicinal doses, relieve pain and produce sleep. In poisonous doses, these produce stupor, coma, convulsions and ultimately death. Morphine narcotics are sometimes referred to as opiates, since they are obtained from the opium poppy.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 453 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Stupor','Coma','Convulsions','All of these','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300318,'chemistry','Characteristic of Aspirin responsible for prevention of heart attack','Anticogulative action','Preventing platelet coagulation. Because of its anti blood clotting action, aspirin finds use in prevention of heart attacks.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 453 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'1','mcq','Cogulative action','Anticogulative action','Analgesic','Antipyretic','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300319,'chemistry','Which of the following statements are true for Barbiturates?\n1. These are class of tranquilizers\n2. Barbituates are hypnotic\n3. They are used as sleeping pills.','1,2 and 3','Derivatives of barbituric acid viz., veronal, amytal, nembutal, luminal \nand seconal constitute an important class of tranquilizers. These \nderivatives are called barbiturates. Barbiturates are hypnotic, i.e., \nsleep producing agents. Some other substances used as tranquilizers \nare valium and serotonin.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 453 Para 1 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'3','mcq','2 and 3','1 and 3','1,2 and 3','1 and 2','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300320,'chemistry','Which of the following drug suggested by doctor to relieve pain due to arthritis?','Aspirin','Aspirin is the most familiar example. Aspirin inhibits the synthesis\nof chemicals known as prostaglandins which stimulate\ninflammation in the tissue and cause pain. These drugs are effective\nin relieving skeletal pain such as that due to arthritis. These drugs\nhave many other effects such as reducing fever (antipyretic). (Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 453 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'1','mcq','Valium','Cimitidine','Aspirin','Equanil','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300321,'chemistry','Aspirin and paracetamol belong to the class of-','non-narcotic analgesics.','Aspirin and paracetamol belong to the class of non-narcotic analgesics.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 453 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'1','mcq','non-narcotic antihistamines','narcotic analgesics.','non-narcotic analgesics.','narcotic Sedative','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300322,'chemistry','Assertion: Aspirin inhibits the synthesis of chemicals known as prostaglandins which stimulate inflammation in the tissue and cause pain.\nReason: Because of its anti blood clotting action, aspirin finds use in prevention of Dengue.','Assertion is True  but the Reason is false','Aspirin inhibits the synthesis of chemicals known as prostaglandins which stimulate inflammation in the tissue and cause pain. These drugs are effective in relieving skeletal pain such as that due to arthritis. These drugs have many other effects such as reducing fever (antipyretic)  and preventing platelet coagulation. Because of its anti blood clotting action, aspirin finds use in prevention of heart attacks.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 453 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'3','mcq','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','The Assertion and the Reason are correct but the Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion','Assertion is True  but the Reason is false','Both the Assertion and Reason are false.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/300322q.png'),
(300323,'chemistry','Assertion: Aspirin act a non narcotic analgesic.\nReason: Aspirin induce the synthesis of chemicals known as prostaglandins which stimulate inflammation in the tissue and reduce pain.','Assertion is True  but the Reason is false','Aspirin inhibits the synthesis of chemicals known as prostaglandins which stimulate inflammation in the tissue and cause pain. These drugs are effective in relieving skeletal pain such as that due to arthritis. These drugs have many other effects such as reducing fever (antipyretic)  and preventing platelet coagulation. Because of its anti blood clotting action, aspirin finds use in prevention of heart attacks.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 453 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'3','mcq','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','The Assertion and the Reason are correct but the Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion','Assertion is True  but the Reason is false','Both the Assertion and Reason are false.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300324,'chemistry','Assertion: Aspirin not recommended to Dengue patient to relieve from fever.\n\nReason: Because of its anti blood clotting action aspirin.','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','Assertion: Aspirin not recommended to Dengue patient to relieve from fever.\n\nReason: Because of its anti blood clotting action aspirin','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'3','mcq','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','The Assertion and the Reason are correct but the Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion','Assertion is True  but the Reason is false','Both the Assertion and Reason are false.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300325,'chemistry','Assertion: Aspirin has found use in prevention of heart attack.\nReason : Because of its blood clotting action.','Assertion is True  but the Reason is false','Because of its anti-blood clotting action as it prevents platelet aggregation, aspirin finds use in prevention of heart attacks.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 453 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'3','mcq','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','The Assertion and the Reason are correct but the Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion','Assertion is True  but the Reason is false','Both the Assertion and Reason are false.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
