(300327,'chemistry','Match the following -','Anti biotic-effective against bacteria, Anti viral-effective against virus, Anti fungal-restrict or kill Fungus, Anti histamine-effective against allergies','Diseases in human beings and animals may be caused by a variety of microorganisms such as bacteria, virus, fungi and other pathogens. An antimicrobial tends to destroy/prevent development or inhibit the pathogenic action of microbes such as bacteria (antibacterial drugs), fungi (antifungal agents), virus (antiviral agents), or other parasites (antiparasitic drugs) selectively. Antibiotics, antiseptics and disinfectants are antimicrobial drugs.','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'3','match','Anti biotic,effective against bacteria','Anti viral,effective against virus','Anti fungal,restrict or kill Fungus','Anti histamine,effective against allergies','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/300327q.png'),
(300328,'chemistry','Salvarsan is arsenic containing drug which was first used for curing-','Syphilis','Arsphenamine, known as salvarsan. Paul Ehrlich got Nobel prize for  Medicine in 1908 for this discovery. It was the first effective treatment discovered for syphilis. (Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 454 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'1','mcq','Typhoid','Syphilis','HIV AIDS','Tuberculosis','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300329,'chemistry','Assertion: Antibiotics are used as drugs to treat infections over Arsphenamine(Salvarsan).\nReason: Because of its low toxicity.','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 454 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'3','mcq','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','The Assertion and the Reason are correct but the Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion','Assertion is True  but the Reason is false','Both the Assertion and Reason are false.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300330,'chemistry','An antibiotic now refers to a substance produced-','Wholly or partly by chemical synthesis,','An antibiotic now refers to a substance produced wholly or partly by chemical synthesis, which in low concentrations  inhibits the growth or destroys microorganisms by intervening in their metabolic processes.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 454 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'1','mcq','Natural origin from microorganisms','Completely Synthetic','Wholly or partly by chemical synthesis,','Completely natural','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300331,'chemistry','Which of the following is arsenic based structure -','Both A and C','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 454 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'1','mcq','Arsphenamine','Protonsil','Salvarsan','Both A and C','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300332,'chemistry','Protonsil have _________linkage.','-N=N-','The –As = As– linkage present in arsphenamine resembles the –N = N – linkage present in azodyes in the sense that arsenic atom is present in place of nitrogen. (Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 455 Para 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'1','mcq','-As=As-','-N=N-','-O=O-','-As=N-','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300333,'chemistry','Azodye contains which of the following linkage ?','-N=N-','The –As = As– linkage present in arsphenamine resembles the –N = N – linkage present in azodyes in the sense that arsenic atom is present in place of nitrogen. (Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 455 Para 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'1','mcq','-As=As-','-N=N-','-O=O-','-As=N-','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300334,'chemistry','Salvarsan contain which of the following linkage?','-As=As-','The –As = As– linkage present in arsphenamine resembles the –N = N – linkage present in azodyes in the sense that arsenic atom is present in place of nitrogen. (Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 455 Para 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'1','mcq','-As=As-','-N=N-','-O=O-','-As=N-','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300335,'chemistry','first effective antibacterial agent-','Protonsil','In 1932, he succeeded in preparing the first effective antibacterial agent, prontosil, which resembles in structure to the compound, salvarsan. Soon it was discovered that in the body prontosil H.W. Florey and Alexander Fleming shared the Nobel prize for Medicine in 1945 for their independent contributions to the development of penicillin. is converted to a compound called sulphanilamide, which is the real active compound. Thus the sulpha drugs were discovered.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 455 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Antibiotic','Salvarsan','Protonsil','All of these','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300401,'chemistry','Vancomycin and ofloxacin are important _____spectrum antibiotics.','Broad','Vancomycin and ofloxacin are the other important broad spectrum antibiotics.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 455 Para 3 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 3',NULL,'1','fillup','Br,oa,d,Na,rr,ow',NULL,NULL,NULL,'DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
