(300501,'chemistry','Chemicals are added to food for-','All of these','Chemicals are added to food for (i) their preservation, (ii) enhancing their appeal, and (iii) adding  nutritive value in them.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 457 Para 1 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Chemicals in food',NULL,'1','mcq','Adding nutritive values','Preservation','Enhancing their appeal','All of these','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300502,'chemistry','Many People prefer Artificial sweetener over Natural','Calorie intake is less in former then the latter','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 457 Para 1 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Chemicals in food',NULL,'2','mcq','No role of Calorie Intake','Calorie intake is more in former then the latter','Calorie intake is less in former then the latter','This role has no practical significance','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300503,'chemistry','Which of the following increase Nutritive value-','None of these','(i) Food colours (ii) Flavours and sweeteners (iii) Fat emulsifiers and stabilising agents (iv) Flour improvers - antistaling agents and bleaches (v) Antioxidants (vi) Preservatives (vii) Nutritional supplements such as minerals, vitamins and amino acids. Except for chemicals of category (vii), none of the above additives have nutritive value. These are added either to increase the shelf life of stored food or for cosmetic purposes. In this Section we will discuss only sweeteners and food preservatives.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 457 Para 1 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Chemicals in food',NULL,'1','mcq','Antioxidants','Preservatives','Food colour','None of these','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300504,'chemistry','The additive having nutritive value-','Nutritional Supplements','(i) Food colours (ii) Flavours and sweeteners (iii) Fat emulsifiers and stabilising agents (iv) Flour improvers - antistaling agents and bleaches (v) Antioxidants (vi) Preservatives (vii) Nutritional supplements such as minerals, vitamins and amino acids. Except for chemicals of category (vii), none of the above additives have nutritive value. These are added either to increase the shelf life of stored food or for cosmetic purposes. In this Section we will discuss only sweeteners and food preservatives.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 457 Para 1 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Chemicals in food',NULL,'1','mcq','Preservatives','Antioxidants','Nutritional Supplements','Food colour','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
