(300513,'chemistry','Assertion: Aspartame is the most successful and widely used artificial sweetener. It is roughly 100 times as sweet as cane sugar. \nReason: It is methyl ester of dipeptide formed from Glutamic acid and phenylalanine.','Assertion is True  but the Reason is false','Aspartame is the most successful and widely used artificial sweetener. It is roughly 100 times as sweet as cane sugar. It is methyl ester of dipeptide formed from aspartic acid and phenylalanine. (Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 458 Para 1 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Chemicals in food',NULL,'3','mcq','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','The Assertion and the Reason are correct but the Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion','Assertion is True  but the Reason is false','Both the Assertion and Reason are false.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300514,'chemistry','Assertion: Use of aspartame is limited to cold foods and soft drinks.\nReason: it is unstable at cooking temperature.','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','Use of aspartame is limited to cold foods and soft drinks because it is unstable at cooking temperature.','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Chemicals in food',NULL,'3','mcq','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','The Assertion and the Reason are correct but the Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion','Assertion is True  but the Reason is false','Both the Assertion and Reason are false.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300515,'chemistry','Which of the following is true for Aspartame -','It is Less stable than sucralose.','Aspartame is the most successful and widely used artificial sweetener. It is roughly 100 times as sweet as cane sugar. It is methyl ester of dipeptide formed from aspartic acid and phenylalanine. Use of aspartame is limited to cold foods and soft drinks because it is unstable at cooking temperature.','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Chemicals in food',NULL,'2','mcq','It is more stable than alitame','The control of sweetness of food is easy while using it.','It is Less stable than sucralose.','It is a combination of phenylalanine and Tryptophan','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300516,'chemistry','_______  is trichloro derivative of sucrose.','Sucralose','Sucralose  is trichloro derivative of sucrose. Its appearance and taste are like sugar. It is stable at cooking temperature. It does not provide calories.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 458 Para 1 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Chemicals in food',NULL,'1','fillup','Sucr,al,Sucr,ose,aspa,rtame,sac,cha,rin',NULL,NULL,NULL,'DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300601,'chemistry','Soaps used for cleaning purpose are__________ salts of long chain fatty acids','sodium or potassium','Soaps used for cleaning purpose are sodium or potassium salts of long chain fatty acids.Saponification reaction, esters of fatty acids are hydrolysed and the soap obtained remains in colloidal form. It is precipitated from the solution by adding sodium chloride.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 459 Para 1 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Cleansing agents',NULL,'2','mcq','sodium or calcium','sodium or potassium','magnesium or potassium','calcium and magnesium','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300602,'chemistry','Soaps containing sodium salts are formed by heating fat (i.e., glyceryl ester of fatty acid) with aqueous sodium hydroxide solution. This reaction is known as -','saponification','Soaps containing sodium salts are formed by heating fat (i.e., glyceryl ester of fatty acid) with aqueous sodium hydroxide solution. This reaction is known as saponification.Saponification reaction, esters of fatty acids are hydrolysed and the soap obtained remains in colloidal form. It is precipitated from the solution by adding sodium chloride.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 459 Para 1 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Cleansing agents',NULL,'1','fillup','sap,oni,fication,hyd,rog,enat,ion',NULL,NULL,NULL,'DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300603,'chemistry','Saponification reaction, esters of fatty acids are hydrolysed and the soap obtained remains in ________ form.','colloidal','Saponification reaction, esters of fatty acids are hydrolysed and the soap obtained remains in colloidal form. It is precipitated from the solution by adding sodium chloride.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 459 Para 1 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Cleansing agents',NULL,'1','mcq','Suspension','Solution','colloidal','precipitation','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300604,'chemistry','During saponification precipitation of colloidal soap is done by adding-','Sodium Chloride','Saponification reaction, esters of fatty acids are hydrolysed and the soap obtained remains in colloidal form. It is precipitated from the solution by adding sodium chloride.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 459 Para 1 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Cleansing agents',NULL,'1','mcq','Sodium hydroxide','Hydrogen peroxide','Sodium Chloride','Sodium Benzoate','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300605,'chemistry','During saponification after removing soap from solution then remaining solution contains -','Glycerol','saponification. In this reaction, esters of fatty acids are hydrolysed and the soap obtained remains in colloidal form. It is precipitated from the solution by adding sodium chloride. The solution left after removing the soap contains glycerol, which can be recovered by fractional distillation. Only sodium and potassium soaps are soluble in water and are used for cleaning purposes. Generally potassium soaps are soft to the skin than sodium soaps. These can be prepared by using potassium hydroxide solution in place of sodium hydroxide.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 459 Para 1 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Cleansing agents',NULL,'1','mcq','Ester','Glycerine','Glycerol','Fatty acid','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300606,'chemistry','Glycerine can be recovered after formation of Soap by process of -','fractional distillation','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 459 Para 1 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Cleansing agents',NULL,'1','mcq','Through Ultra filtration','Through Filter paper','fractional distillation','Simple Boiling','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300607,'chemistry','Sodium and potassium soaps are ________ in water and are used for cleaning purposes.','soluble','Sodium and potassium soaps are soluble in water and are used for cleaning purposes. (Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 459 Para 1 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Cleansing agents',NULL,'1','fillup','solu,bile,In,solu,ble',NULL,NULL,NULL,'DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300608,'chemistry','Which of the following soap are soft for skin-','Potassium soap','Generally potassium soaps are soft to the skin than sodium soaps. These can be prepared by using potassium hydroxide solution in place of sodium hydroxide.','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Cleansing agents',NULL,'1','mcq','Fatty soap','Sodium soap','Potassium soap','Soap with Glycerine','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300701,'chemistry','Among the following, the narrow spectrum \nantibiotic is-','penicillin G','Penicillin G has a narrow spectrum. \nChloramphenicol is a broad spectrum antibiotic. \nAmpicillin and amoxycillin are synthetic modifications \nof penicillins. These have broad spectrum.(Reference NCERT class 12 page 447 paragraph 3 NEET 2019)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Previous Year question',NULL,'1','mcq','chloramphenicol','penicillin G','ampicillin','amoxycillin','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
