(300704,'chemistry','Bithional is generally added to the soaps as an \nadditive to function as a/an','antiseptic','Bithionol (the compound is also called bithional) is added to soaps to impart antiseptic properties. Iodine is a powerful antiseptic. Its 2-3 per cent solution in alcohol- water mixture is known as tincture of iodine. It is applied on wounds. (Reference NCERT class 12 page 448 paragraph 1 NEET 2015)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Previous Year question',NULL,'1','mcq','buffering agent','antiseptic','softener','dryer','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300705,'chemistry','Antiseptics and disinfectants either kill or prevent \ngrowth of microrganisms. Identify which of the \nfollowing statements is not true.','Dilute solutions of boric acid and hydrogen \nperoxide are strong antiseptics.','Dilute solutions of boric acid and hydrogen peroxide is weak antiseptic (Reference NCERT class 12 page 448 paragraph 1 NEET 2013)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Previous Year question',NULL,'2','mcq','Dilute solutions of boric acid and hydrogen \nperoxide are strong antiseptics.','A 0.2% solution of phenol is an antiseptic while \n1% solution acts as a disinfectant.','Disinfectants harm the living tissues.','Chlorine and iodine are used as strong \ndisinfectants.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
