(300801,'chemistry','Which of the following macromolecules exist and perform some role in the cell membrane\n \n a)carrier proteins\n \n b)lipids \n \n c)carbohydrates\n \n d)nucleic acids','a,b,c','Carrier proteins-carry polar molecules across the cell membrane\n \n Lipids and carbohydrates are structural part of membrane\n \n (Reference: NCERT class 12 page 440 paragraph last)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Advanced questions',NULL,'3','mcq','a,b,c','d,b,a','b,c,d','a,c,d','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300802,'chemistry','Function of which macromolecule involves the storage and expression of the genetic informatons?\n \n a)carrier proteins\n \n b)receptors\n \n c)ribonucleic acid\n \n d)deoxyribonucleic acid','c,d','Nucleic acids coded genetic information for the cell\n \n (Reference NCERT class 12 page 440 paragraph 5)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Advanced questions',NULL,'2','mcq','a,b','c,d','a,c','b,d','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300803,'chemistry','Catalytic function of enzymes are based on:\n \n a)Active Site holding a substance molecule in a suitable position ,so it can be attacked by reagent\n \n b)enzyme provides functional groups that will attack the substrate\n \n c) Functional groups hold a molecule in a suitable position , so it can be attacked by reagent\n \n d)Active site attacks the substrate','a,b','First function of an enzyme is based on active sites of enzyme holds a substance molecule in a suitable position so that it can be attacked by the reagent effectivelly. The second function - enzyme provides functional groups that will attack the substrate and carry out the chemical reaction.\n \n (Reference NCERT class 12 page 440 paragraph last)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Advanced questions',NULL,'2','mcq','a,b','c,d','a,c','b,d','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300804,'chemistry','What sort of bonding is substrate bind to the active site:\n \n a)dipole-dipole\n \n b)van der Waals\n \n c)strong covalent bonding\n \n d)ionic bonding','a,b,d','Substrate bind to the active site of the enzyme could be ionic bonding,hydrogen bonding,van der Waals , dipole dipole interaction\n \n (Reference NCERT class 12 page 440 paragraph last)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Advanced questions',NULL,'2','mcq','a,b,d','a,b,c','d,c,a','c,b,d','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300805,'chemistry','Activity of enzymes:\n \n a)can be inhibited by enzyme inhibitors\n \n b)can be blocked by enzyme inhibitors\n \n c)can\'t be permanently blocked\n \n d)can only be only blocked but not inhibited','a,b','Enzyme inhibitors can block or inhibit the catalytic activity of enzymes\n \n If the enzyme-inhibitor bond is strong covalent bond the enzyme is blocked permanently\n \n (Reference NCERT class 12 page 441 paragraph 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Advanced questions',NULL,'2','mcq','a,b','b,c','c,d','a,c','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300806,'chemistry','Given below are two statements : one is labelled assertation (A) and the other is labeled reason (R)\n \n A:Binding of inhibitor at allosteric site changes the shape of allosteric site.\n \n R:Substrate can\'t recognise allosteric site that is changed by the substrate and can\'t bind to the site.','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','Some drugs bind to the allosteric site . That binding changes the shape of allosteric site in such way that substrate can\'t recognise it .\n \n (Reference NCERT class 12 page 441 paragraph 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Advanced questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','A is correct but R is not correct','R is correct but A is not correct','Both A and R are correct but R is not explanation of A','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300807,'chemistry','Given bellow are two statements : one is labelled assertation (A) and the other is labeled reason (R)\n \n A:The enzyme can be blocked permanently , than body degrades enzyme-inhibitor complex and synthesizes the new enzyme\n \n R:The enzyme-inhibitor can be strong covalent bond that can\'t be broken easily','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','If the enzyme-inhibitor bond is strong covalent bond that cannot be broken easily than the enzyme is blocked permanently . The body degrades enzyme-inhibitor complex and synthesises the new enzyme.\n \n (Reference NCERT class 12 page 441 paragraph 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Advanced questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','A is correct but R is not correct','R is correct but A is not correct','Both A and R are correct but R is not explanation of A','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300808,'chemistry','Difference between allosteric and active site is:\n \n a)allosteric site is active site with changed shape\n \n b)Allosteric site is the site that inhibitor occupies\n \n c)Active site is the site that inhibitor occupies\n \n d)active site is changing when inhibitor occupies the allosteric site','b,c','Active sites of enzyme hold a substance molecule in a suitable position so that it can be attacked by reagent\n \n Allosteric site is the site that inhibitor occupies ,after that active site is changing so that substrate can\'t recognise it.\n \n (Reference NCERT class 12 page 441 paragraph 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Advanced questions',NULL,'2','mcq','a,c','b,c','a,d','b,d','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300809,'chemistry','Which statements is true \n \n a)drugs that compete for their attachment on the active sites are called competitive inhibitors\n \n b)enzymes that compete for their attachment on the allosteric sites are called competitive inhibitors\n \n c)competitive inhibitors are enzymes\n \n d)competitive inhibitors are drugs','a,d','Drugs compete for their attachment on the active sites of enzymes are competitive inhibitors\n \n (Reference NCERT class 12 page 441 paragraph 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Advanced questions',NULL,'2','mcq','a,c','b,c','a,d','b,d','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300901,'chemistry','Which of the following statements is not correct?','Antiseptic medicines can be ingested','Antiseptics  are applied to the living tissues such as wounds, cuts, ulcers and diseased skin surfaces. \n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 448 Para 1 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Exemplar Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Some antiseptics can be added to soaps','Dilute solutions of some disinfectants can be used as antiseptic','Disinfectants are antimicrobial drugs','Antiseptic medicines can be ingested','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300902,'chemistry','Which is the correct statement about birth control pills?','contain a mixture of estrogen and progesterone derivatives','Birth control pills essentially contain a mixture of synthetic estrogen and progesterone derivatives(Reference NCERT class 12 page 448 paragraph last).','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Exemplar Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','contain estrogen only','contain progesterone only','contain a mixture of estrogen and progesterone derivatives','progesterone enhances ovulation','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300903,'chemistry','Which statement about aspirin is not true?','Aspirin belongs to narcotic analgesics','"Aspirin are effective in relieving skeletal pain such as that due to arthritis. These drugs have many other effects such as reducing fever (antipyretic) and preventing platelet coagulation. Because of its anti blood clotting action, aspirin finds use in prevention of heart attacks.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 453 Para 2 )"','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Exemplar Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Aspirin belongs to narcotic analgesics','It is effective in relieving pain','It has antiblood clotting action','It is neurologically active drug','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(2000037771,'physics','Which one of the following statement is correct?','B','Surface tension is the force applied per unit length or work done (or energy) per unit area of a liquid surface. While surface energy is the amount of work done per unit area by the force.','Surface Tension','Mechanical Properties of Fluids','Easy',NULL,'surface energy is potential energy per unit length','surface tension is work done per unit area','surface tension is work done per unit length','surface energy is work done per unit force',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(301001,'chemistry','Which one of the following types of drugs reduces fever?','Anitpyretic','Aspirin is effective in relieving skeletal pain such as that due to arthritis. These drugs have many other effects such as reducing fever (antipyretic) and preventing platelet coagulation. Because of its anti blood clotting action, aspirin finds use in prevention of heart attacks.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 453 Para 2 ) [AIEEE 2005]','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> JEE Mains',NULL,'1','mcq','Tranquiliser','Antibiotic','Anitpyretic','Analgesic','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(301002,'chemistry','Which of the following compounds  is not an antacid?','Phenelzine','Phenelzine is not an antacid. It is a medication used as an antidepressant and anxiolytic agent.\n\nAluminium hydroxide and ranitidine are commonly used as antacids to neutralize stomach acid, while cimetidine is an H2 receptor antagonist used to reduce the secretion of stomach acid.\n[JEE Mains 2015]','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> JEE Mains',NULL,'1','mcq','Aluminium hydroxide','Cimetidine','Phenelzine','Ranitidine','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(301003,'chemistry','Which of the following is an anionic detergent?','Sodium lauryl sulphate','Cetyltrimethylammoniumbromide is a popular cationic detergent and is used in hair conditioners.\n \n Liquid dishwashing detergents are non-ionic type of detergent.\n \n Anionic detergents are sodium salts of sulphonated long chain alcohols or hydrocarbons. Alkyl hydrogensulphates formed by treating long chain alcohols with concentrated sulphuric acid are neutralised with alkali to form anionic detergents.\n \n (Reference NCERT class 12 page 452 1,3,last) [JEE Mains 2016]','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> JEE Mains',NULL,'1','mcq','Sodium lauryl sulphate','Cetyltrimethyl ammonium bromide','Glyceryl oleate','Sodium stearate','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(301004,'chemistry','If a person is suffering from the deficiency of nor adrenaline, what kind of drug can be suggested?','Antidepressant','Antidepressant drugs inhibit the enzymes which catalyse the degradation of noradrenaline.Iproniazid and phenelzine are\nantidepressants.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 444 Para last)[JEE Mains 2020]','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> JEE Mains',NULL,'2','mcq','Antihistamine','Analgesic','Antidepressant','Anti-inflmammatory','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
