(301107,'biology','Which of the following is not a mode of transfer of HIV?','Consuming contaminated food','Transmission of HIV-infection generally occurs by (a) sexual contact with infected person, (b) by transfusion of contaminated blood and blood products, (c) by sharing infected needles as in the case of intravenous drug abusers and (d) from infected mother to her child through placenta.','Biology In Human Welfare >> Human Health and Disease >> AIDS',NULL,'2','mcq','By sharing IV needles','By coming in contact with contaminated blood','Consuming contaminated food','From infected mother to child through the placenta','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(301108,'biology','Which of the following is not a high risk group for contracting HIV?','People eating off from sidewalks','People who are at high risk of getting AIDS includes - individuals who have multiple sexual partners, drug addicts who take drugs intravenously, individuals who require repeated blood transfusions and children born to an HIV infected mother.','Biology In Human Welfare >> Human Health and Disease >> AIDS',NULL,'2','mcq','People requiring repeated transfusions','Drug addicts','People eating off from sidewalks','Children born to affected mothers','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(301109,'biology','Label the stages correctly in the given diagram . (3007)','Viral DNA produced by reverse transcriptase-a,viral DNA incorporated within host genome-b,new viral RNA produced by infected cells-c','Figure 8.6 NCERT Class 12 page no;155 Replication of retrovirus','Biology In Human Welfare >> Human Health and Disease >> AIDS',NULL,'2','match','Viral DNA produced by reverse transcriptase,a','Viral DNA incorporated within host genome,b','New viral RNA produced by infected cells,c',NULL,'NEW',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/match/301109q.png'),
