(301327,'biology','Cocaine is usually ________.','Snorted','Cocaine, commonly called coke or crack is usually snorted.','Biology In Human Welfare >> Human Health and Disease >> Drugs and Alcohol Abuse',NULL,'1','mcq','Orally ingested','Injected','Inhaled','Snorted','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(301328,'biology','Cocaine has a potent stimulating action on ____________.','Central nervous system','It has a potent stimulating action on central nervous system, producing a sense of euphoria and increased energy.','Biology In Human Welfare >> Human Health and Disease >> Drugs and Alcohol Abuse',NULL,'2','mcq','Peripheral nervous system, gastrointestinal tract','Central nervous system','Central nervous system, gastrointestinal tract','Peripheral nervous system, spinal cord','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(301329,'biology','Cocaine produces a sense of  ____________.','Increased energy','It has a potent stimulating action on central nervous system, producing a sense of euphoria and increased energy.','Biology In Human Welfare >> Human Health and Disease >> Drugs and Alcohol Abuse',NULL,'1','mcq','Increased energy','Low energy','Depression','Dullness','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(301330,'biology','Excessive dosage of cocaine causes ___________.','Hallucinations','Excessive dosage of cocaine causes hallucinations.','Biology In Human Welfare >> Human Health and Disease >> Drugs and Alcohol Abuse',NULL,'2','mcq','Vomiting','Shaking','Anxiety','Hallucinations','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(301331,'biology','Which of these plants has hallucinogenic properties?','Atropa belladonna','Other well-known plants with hallucinogenic properties are atropa belladonna and datura.','Biology In Human Welfare >> Human Health and Disease >> Drugs and Alcohol Abuse',NULL,'2','mcq','Allium cepa','Atropa belladonna','Musa paradisiaca','None of them','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(301332,'biology','Drugs like barbiturates and amphetamines help patients cope with diseases like _________.','Depression','Drugs like barbiturates, amphetamines, benzodiazepines, and other similar drugs, that are normally used as medicines to help patients cope with mental illnesses like depression and insomnia, are often abused.','Biology In Human Welfare >> Human Health and Disease >> Drugs and Alcohol Abuse',NULL,'2','mcq','Depression','Amnesia','ADHD','OCD','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
