(330807,'biology','Repeated amplification is achieved by the use of a','Thermostable DNA polymerase','If the process of replication of DNA is repeated many times, the segment of DNA can be amplified to approximately billion times, i.e., 1 billion copies are made. Such repeated amplification is achieved by the use of a thermostable DNA polymerase','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology : Principles And Processes >> Biotechnology : Amplification of Gene of Interest using PCR','Biotechnology: Principles and Processes','2','mcq','Unstable RNA polymerase','Thermostable DNA polymerase','Reactive DNAase','Protease','NEW','12-203','12-173',NULL),
(330808,'biology','In PCR, thermostable DNA polymerase is isolated from','Thermus aquaticus','Thermostable DNA polymerase is isolated from a bacterium called Thermus aquaticus','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology : Principles And Processes >> Biotechnology : Amplification of Gene of Interest using PCR','Biotechnology: Principles and Processes','2','mcq','Thermus aquaticus','Escherichia coli','Agrobacterium tumefaciens','Hemophilus influenzae','NEW','12-203','12-173',NULL),
(330809,'biology','DNA polymerase used in PCR is active during','High temperature','Thermostable DNA polymerase which is isolated from a bacterium called Thermus aquaticus,remains active during the high temperature induced denaturation of double stranded DNA','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology : Principles And Processes >> Biotechnology : Amplification of Gene of Interest using PCR','Biotechnology: Principles and Processes','2','mcq','High pressure','Low temperature','High temperature','High potential','NEW','12-203','12-173',NULL),
(330810,'biology','DNA polymerase which remain active during the high temperature induce','denaturation of double stranded DNA.','Thermostable DNA polymerase which is isolated from a bacterium called Thermus aquaticus,remains active during the high temperature induced denaturation of double stranded DNA','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology : Principles And Processes >> Biotechnology : Amplification of Gene of Interest using PCR','Biotechnology: Principles and Processes','2','mcq','denaturation of single stranded DNA','denaturation of double stranded DNA.','denaturation of\ndouble stranded RNA','denaturation of single stranded RNA','NEW','12-203','12-173',NULL),
(330811,'biology','Which of the following is the correct sequence of PCR or polymerase chain reaction?','Denaturation -> Annealing -> Extension','Polymerase chain reaction or PCR consists of the following three steps: Denaturation- The two DNA strands of template DNA separate from each other when heated to 92℃. Annealing- The primers anneal to the 3’ end of single strands of DNA. Extension- The primers are extended by DNA polymerase by the addition of nucleotides to form complete strands of DNA. Hence the sequence of steps is denaturation, annealing, extension. So, the correct answer is option C.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology : Principles And Processes >> Biotechnology : Amplification of Gene of Interest using PCR','Biotechnology: Principles and Processes','3','mcq','Denaturation -> Annealing -> Extension','Extension -> Denaturation -»annealing','Annealing -> Extension -> Denaturation','Denaturation -> Extension -> Annealing','NEW','12-202','12-172',NULL),
(330812,'biology','Match a b and c in the given diagram (3307)','a-denaturation,b-annealing,c-extension','Figure 11.6 pageno-202 NCERT 12th class"','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology : Principles And Processes >> Biotechnology : Amplification of Gene of Interest using PCR','Biotechnology: Principles and Processes','3','match','a,denaturation','b,annealing','c,extension',NULL,'NEW','12-202','12-172','/ncert/pyq/biology/match/330812q.png'),
