(330901,'biology','Recipient cells need to be _____ before taking up foriegn DNA','Competent','There are several methods of introducing the ligated DNA into recipient cells. Recipient cells after making them ‘competent’ to receive, take up DNA present in its surrounding.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology : Principles And Processes >> Insertion of Recombinant DNA','Biotechnology: Principles and Processes','3','mcq','Competent','Slow','Inactive','Damaged','NEW','12-203','12-173',NULL),
(330902,'biology','In PCR, recombinant DNA bearing gene for resistance to an antibiotic Ampicllin is transferred into cells of','E. coli','So, if a recombinant DNA bearing gene for resistance to an antibiotic (e.g., ampicillin) is transferred into E. coli cells, the host cells become transformed into ampicillin-resistant cells','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology : Principles And Processes >> Insertion of Recombinant DNA','Biotechnology: Principles and Processes','3','mcq','Salmonella typhyi','E. coli','Yeast','Bacillus','NEW','12-203','12-173',NULL),
(330903,'biology','If a recombinant DNA bearing gene for resistance to an antibiotic like Ampicillin is transferred into E. coli cells, the host cells become transformed into','Ampicillin-resistant cells','If a recombinant DNA bearing gene for resistance to an antibiotic (e.g., ampicillin) is transferred into E. coli cells, the host cells become transformed into ampicillin-resistant cells','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology : Principles And Processes >> Insertion of Recombinant DNA','Biotechnology: Principles and Processes','3','mcq','Ampicillin-promoting cells','Ampicillin-resistant cells','Ampicillin-modifying cells','Ampicillin- deleting cells','NEW','12-203','12-173',NULL),
(110909,'biology','When the guard cells lose turgor, due to water loss (or water stress) the elastic inner walls regain their original shape, the guard cells become','Flaccid and the stoma closes','When the guard cells lose turgor, due to water loss (or water stress) the elastic inner walls regain their original shape, the guard cells become flaccid and the stoma closes\nReference  :NCERT Class 11th Pg., 187','Plant Physiology >> Transport in plants >> Transpiration',NULL,'3','mcq','Flaccid and the stoma opens','Flaccid and the stoma closes','Turgid and the stoma closes','Turgid and the opens','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(330904,'biology','If we spread the transformed cells on agar plates containing ampicillin,','Transformants recipient cells-grow,untransformed recipient cells-die','If a recombinant DNA bearing gene for resistance to an antibiotic (e.g., ampicillin) is transferred into E. coli cells, the host cells become transformed into ampicillin-resistant cells. If we spread the transformed cells on agar plates containing ampicillin, only transformants will grow, untransformed recipient cells will die.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology : Principles And Processes >> Insertion of Recombinant DNA','Biotechnology: Principles and Processes','3','match','Transformants recipient cells,grow','Untransformed recipient cells,die',NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-203','12-173',NULL),
(330905,'biology','Due to ampicillin resistance gene, one is able to select a transformed cell in the\npresence of ampicillin. The ampicillin resistance gene in this case is called','Selectable marker','Due\nto ampicillin resistance gene, one is able to select a transformed cell in the\npresence of ampicillin. The ampicillin resistance gene in this case is called\na selectable marker.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology : Principles And Processes >> Insertion of Recombinant DNA','Biotechnology: Principles and Processes','3','mcq','Selectable marker','Tandem Repeat','Origin of Replication','Promoter region','NEW','12-203','12-173',NULL),
(331001,'biology','In almost all recombinant technologies, the ultimate aim is to produce a desirable','Protein','In almost all recombinant technologies, the ultimate aim is to produce a desirable protein. Hence, there is a need for the recombinant DNA to be expressed','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology : Principles And Processes >> Obtaining the Foreign Gene Product','Biotechnology: Principles and Processes','2','mcq','Atoms','Protein','Nutrients','Carbohydrate','NEW','12-203','12-173',NULL),
(331002,'biology','Any protein encoding gene is expressed in a heterologous host, it is called a _____','Recombinant protein','If any protein encoding gene is expressed in a heterologous host, it is called a recombinant protein','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology : Principles And Processes >> Obtaining the Foreign Gene Product','Biotechnology: Principles and Processes','2','mcq','RNA complex','Recombinant protein','Rh proteins','mRNA','NEW','12-203','12-173',NULL),
(331003,'biology','Recombinant protein is expressed in','Heterologous host','Protein encoding gene is expressed in a heterologous host, it is called a recombinant protein. The cells harbouring cloned genes of interest may be grown on a small scale in the laboratory','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology : Principles And Processes >> Obtaining the Foreign Gene Product','Biotechnology: Principles and Processes','2','mcq','Heterologous host','Homozygous vector','Homologous vector','Homologous host','NEW','12-203','12-173',NULL),
(331004,'biology','The cells harbouring cloned genes of interest may be grown on a small scale in?','Laboratory','Protein encoding gene is expressed in a heterologous host, it is called a recombinant protein. The cells harbouring cloned genes of interest may be grown on a small scale in the laboratory','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology : Principles And Processes >> Obtaining the Foreign Gene Product','Biotechnology: Principles and Processes','2','mcq','Kitchen','Factories','Laboratory','Bioreactors','NEW','12-203','12-173',NULL),
(331005,'biology','What happens in a continuous culture system?','Used medium is drained out from one side while fresh medium is added','In a continuous culture system wherein\nthe used medium is drained out from one side while fresh medium is\nadded from the other to maintain the cells in their physiologically most active log/exponential phase.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology : Principles And Processes >> Obtaining the Foreign Gene Product','Biotechnology: Principles and Processes','2','mcq','Used medium is drained out from one side while fresh medium is added','Fresh medium is drained out from one side while used medium is added','Fresh medium is added only once','Partition of fresh and drain medium don\'t occur','NEW','12-203','12-173',NULL),
(331006,'biology','The purpose of a continuous culture system is to maintain','Cells in their physiologically most active log/exponential phase','The cells can also be multiplied in a continuous culture system wherein the used medium is drained out from one side while fresh medium is added from the other to maintain the cells in their physiologically most active log/exponential phase. This type of culturing method produces a larger biomass leading to higher yields of desired protein','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology : Principles And Processes >> Obtaining the Foreign Gene Product','Biotechnology: Principles and Processes','2','mcq','Cells in their hormonal stage','Cells in their physiologically most active log/exponential phase','Cells to under to growth','Cells in their physiologically most active lag phase','NEW','12-203','12-173',NULL),
(331007,'biology','Which type of culturing method produces a larger biomass leading to higher yields of desired proteins?','Continuous culture system','Culturing method produces a larger biomass leading to higher yields of desired protein','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology : Principles And Processes >> Obtaining the Foreign Gene Product','Biotechnology: Principles and Processes','2','mcq','Conventional culture system','Continuous culture system','Synthetic system','Unsynthetic system','NEW','12-204','12-174',NULL),
(331009,'biology','Small volume cultures cannot yield appreciable quantities of products','TRUE','Small volume cultures cannot yield appreciable quantities of products.\nTo produce in large quantities, the development of bioreactors, where\nlarge volumes (100-1000 litres) of culture can be processed, was required.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology : Principles And Processes >> Obtaining the Foreign Gene Product','Biotechnology: Principles and Processes','2','mcq','TRUE','FALSE',NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-204','12-174',NULL),
(331010,'biology','Which of the following is required to process and obtain large quantities of products from culture?','Bioreactors','Small volume cultures cannot yield appreciable quantities of products. To produce in large quantities, the development of bioreactors, where large volumes (100-1000 litres) of culture can be processed, was required','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology : Principles And Processes >> Obtaining the Foreign Gene Product','Biotechnology: Principles and Processes','2','mcq','Biovessels','Biofermentors','Bioreactors','Bioactivators','NEW','12-204','12-174',NULL),
(331011,'biology','Vessels in which raw materials are biologically converted into specific products, individual enzymes, etc., using microbial plant, animal or human cells','Bioreactors','Bioreactors can be thought of as vessels in which raw materials are biologically converted into specific products, individual enzymes, etc., using microbial plant, animal or human cells. A bioreactor provides the optimal conditions for achieving the desired product by providing optimum growth conditions (temperature, pH, substrate, salts, vitamins, oxygen).','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology : Principles And Processes >> Obtaining the Foreign Gene Product','Biotechnology: Principles and Processes','2','mcq','Bioreactors','Biofermentors','Biocultors','Biovessels','NEW','12-204','12-174',NULL),
